e R2 オブジェクトストレージは、効率的なデータストレージと管理ソリューションを提供し、クイックスタートと最新バージョンをサポート","ko":"Cloudflare R2 객체 저장소는 효율적인 데이터 저장소 및 관리 솔루션을 제공하며 빠른 시작 및 최신 버전을 지원","es":"Cloudflare R2 es un almacenamiento de objetos escalable y seguro. Crea buckets y gestiona tus datos con facilidad.","fr":"Cloudflare R2 est un stockage d''objets évolutif et sécurisé. Créez des buckets et gérez vos données avec facilité.","de":"Cloudflare R2 ist ein skalierbarer und sicherer Objekt-Speicher. Erstellen Sie Buckets und verwalten Sie Ihre Daten mit Leichtigkeit.","pt":"O Cloudflare R2 é um serviço de armazenamento de objetos em nuvem que oferece uma solução escalável e segura para armazenar e gerenciar dados","ru":"Cloudflare R2 - это облачный сервис хранения объектов, который предлагает масштабируемое и безопасное решение для хранения и управления данными","ar":"Cloudflare R2 هو خدمة تخزين كائنات سحابية تقدم حلًا متسلسلًا وآمنًا لتخزين وإدارة البيانات","en":"Comprehensive collection of 100+ custom Droids & 300+ Skills for FactoryAI Droid system"},"definition":{"en":"Comprehensive collection of 100+ custom Droids & 300+ Skills for FactoryAI Droid system"},"features":{"zh":["快速入门","最新版本支持","依赖项管理","高效的数据存储","对象存储服务"],"ja":["クイックスタート","最新バージョンのサポート","依存関係の管理","効率的なデータストレージ","オブジェクトストレージサービス"],"ko":["빠른 시작","최신 버전 지원","종속 항목 관리","효율적인 데이터 저장소","객체 저장소 서비스"],"es":["Almacenamiento de objetos escalable","Crea buckets con facilidad","Gestiona tus datos con seguridad","Integración con Cloudflare Worker","Compatibilidad con wrangler y workers-types"],"fr":["Stockage d''objets évolutif","Créez des buckets avec facilité","Gérez vos données avec sécurité","Intégration avec Cloudflare Worker","Compatibilité avec wrangler et workers-types"],"de":["Skalierbarer Objekt-Speicher","Erstellen Sie Buckets mit Leichtigkeit","Verwalten Sie Ihre Daten mit Sicherheit","Integration mit Cloudflare Worker","Kompatibilität mit wrangler und workers-types"],"pt":["Armazenamento de objetos em nuvem escalável","Segurança de dados avançada","Integração com o Cloudflare Worker","Suporte a wrangler e workers-types","Compatibilidade com aws4fetch"],"ru":["Масштабируемое облачное хранение объектов","Продвинутая безопасность данных","Интеграция с Cloudflare Worker","Поддержка wrangler и workers-types","Совместимость с aws4fetch"],"ar":["تخزين كائنات سحابية متسلسل","أمان بيانات متقدم","إدماج مع Cloudflare Worker","دعم wrangler و workers-types","توافق مع aws4fetch"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare R2","对象存储","数据存储","云计算","效率管理","快速入门","最新版本"],"ja":["Cloudflare R2","オブジェクトストレージ","データストレージ","クラウドコンピューティング","効率管理","クイックスタート","最新バージョン"],"ko":["Cloudflare R2","객체 저장소","데이터 저장소","클라우드 컴퓨팅","효율 관리","빠른 시작","최신 버전"],"es":["Cloudflare R2","almacenamiento de objetos","buckets","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","desarrollo de aplicaciones","infraestructura en la nube"],"fr":["Cloudflare R2","stockage d''objets","buckets","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","développement d''applications","infrastructure cloud"],"de":["Cloudflare R2","Objekt-Speicher","Buckets","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Cloud-Infrastruktur"],"pt":["armazenamento de objetos em nuvem","Cloudflare R2","serviço de armazenamento de objetos","nuvem","segurança de dados","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","aws4fetch"],"ru":["облачное хранение объектов","Cloudflare R2","сервис хранения объектов","облако","безопасность данных","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","aws4fetch"],"ar":["تخزين كائنات سحابية","Cloudflare R2","خدمة تخزين كائنات","السحابة","أمان البيانات","Cloudflare Worker","wrangler","workers-types","aws4fetch"]}},"owner":"ovachiever","repo":"droid-tings","repoPath":"ovachiever/droid-tings","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloudflare-r2","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Cloudflare R2 Object Storage\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2025-10-21\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.43.0, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20251014.0, aws4fetch@1.0.20\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n### 1. Create R2 Bucket\n\n```bash\n# Via Wrangler CLI (recommended)\nnpx wrangler r2 bucket create my-bucket\n\n# Or via Cloudflare Dashboard\n# https://dash.cloudflare.com → R2 Object Storage → Create bucket\n```\n\n**Bucket Na","body":"# Cloudflare R2 Object Storage\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2025-10-21\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.43.0, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20251014.0, aws4fetch@1.0.20\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n### 1. Create R2 Bucket\n\n```bash\n# Via Wrangler CLI (recommended)\nnpx wrangler r2 bucket create my-bucket\n\n# Or via Cloudflare Dashboard\n# https://dash.cloudflare.com → R2 Object Storage → Create bucket\n```\n\n**Bucket Naming Rules:**\n- 3-63 characters\n- Lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens only\n- Must start/end with letter or number\n- Globally unique within your account\n\n### 2. Configure R2 Binding\n\nAdd to your `wrangler.jsonc`:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-worker\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2025-10-11\",\n  \"r2_buckets\": [\n    {\n      \"binding\": \"MY_BUCKET\",          // Available as env.MY_BUCKET in your Worker\n      \"bucket_name\": \"my-bucket\",      // Name from wrangler r2 bucket create\n      \"preview_bucket_name\": \"my-bucket-preview\"  // Optional: separate bucket for dev\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**CRITICAL:**\n- `binding` is how you access the bucket in code (`env.MY_BUCKET`)\n- `bucket_name` is the actual R2 bucket name\n- `preview_bucket_name` is optional but recommended for separate dev/prod data\n\n### 3. Basic Upload/Download\n\n```typescript\n// src/index.ts\nimport { Hono } from ''hono'';\n\ntype Bindings = {\n  MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket;\n};\n\nconst app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Bindings }>();\n\n// Upload file\napp.put(''/upload/:filename'', async (c) => {\n  const filename = c.req.param(''filename'');\n  const body = await c.req.arrayBuffer();\n\n  try {\n    const object = await c.env.MY_BUCKET.put(filename, body, {\n      httpMetadata: {\n        contentType: c.req.header(''content-type'') || ''application/octet-stream'',\n      },\n    });\n\n    return c.json({\n      success: true,\n      key: object.key,\n      size: object.size,\n      etag: object.etag,\n    });\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    console.error(''R2 Upload Error:'', error.message);\n    return c.json({ error: ''Upload failed'' }, 500);\n  }\n});\n\n// Download file\napp.get(''/download/:filename'', async (c) => {\n  const filename = c.req.param(''filename'');\n\n  try {\n    const object = await c.env.MY_BUCKET.get(filename);\n\n    if (!object) {\n      return c.json({ error: ''File not found'' }, 404);\n    }\n\n    return new Response(object.body, {\n      headers: {\n        ''Content-Type'': object.httpMetadata?.contentType || ''application/octet-stream'',\n        ''ETag'': object.httpEtag,\n        ''Cache-Control'': object.httpMetadata?.cacheControl || ''public, max-age=3600'',\n      },\n    });\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    console.error(''R2 Download Error:'', error.message);\n    return c.json({ error: ''Download failed'' }, 500);\n  }\n});\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\n### 4. Deploy and Test\n\n```bash\n# Deploy\nnpx wrangler deploy\n\n# Test upload\ncurl -X PUT https://my-worker.workers.dev/upload/test.txt \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d \"Hello, R2!\"\n\n# Test download\ncurl https://my-worker.workers.dev/download/test.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n## R2 Workers API\n\n### Type Definitions\n\n```typescript\n// Add to env.d.ts or worker-configuration.d.ts\ninterface Env {\n  MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket;\n  // ... other bindings\n}\n\n// For Hono\ntype Bindings = {\n  MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket;\n};\n\nconst app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Bindings }>();\n```\n\n### put() - Upload Objects\n\n**Signature:**\n```typescript\nput(key: string, value: ReadableStream | ArrayBuffer | ArrayBufferView | string | Blob, options?: R2PutOptions): Promise<R2Object | null>\n```\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n\n```typescript\n// Upload from request body\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''path/to/file.txt'', request.body);\n\n// Upload string\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''config.json'', JSON.stringify({ foo: ''bar'' }));\n\n// Upload ArrayBuffer\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''image.png'', await file.arrayBuffer());\n```\n\n**With Metadata:**\n\n```typescript\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.put(''document.pdf'', fileData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/pdf'',\n    contentLanguage: ''en-US'',\n    contentDisposition: ''attachment; filename=\"report.pdf\"'',\n    contentEncoding: ''gzip'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=86400'',\n  },\n  customMetadata: {\n    userId: ''12345'',\n    uploadDate: new Date().toISOString(),\n    version: ''1.0'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Conditional Uploads (Prevent Overwrites):**\n\n```typescript\n// Only upload if file doesn''t exist\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', data, {\n  onlyIf: {\n    uploadedBefore: new Date(''2020-01-01''), // Any date before R2 existed\n  },\n});\n\nif (!object) {\n  // File already exists, upload prevented\n  return c.json({ error: ''File already exists'' }, 409);\n}\n\n// Only upload if etag matches (update specific version)\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', data, {\n  onlyIf: {\n    etagMatches: existingEtag,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**With Checksums:**\n\n```typescript\n// R2 will verify the checksum\nconst md5Hash = await crypto.subtle.digest(''MD5'', fileData);\n\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', fileData, {\n  md5: md5Hash,\n});\n```\n\n### get() - Download Objects\n\n**Signature:**\n```typescript\nget(key: string, options?: R2GetOptions): Promise<R2ObjectBody | null>\n```\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n\n```typescript\n// Get full object\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.txt'');\n\nif (!object) {\n  return c.json({ error: ''Not found'' }, 404);\n}\n\n// Return as response\nreturn new Response(object.body, {\n  headers: {\n    ''Content-Type'': object.httpMetadata?.contentType || ''application/octet-stream'',\n    ''ETag'': object.httpEtag,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Read as Different Formats:**\n\n```typescript\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''data.json'');\n\nif (object) {\n  const text = await object.text();           // As string\n  const json = await object.json();           // As JSON object\n  const buffer = await object.arrayBuffer();  // As ArrayBuffer\n  const blob = await object.blob();           // As Blob\n}\n```\n\n**Range Requests (Partial Downloads):**\n\n```typescript\n// Get first 1MB of file\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''large-file.mp4'', {\n  range: { offset: 0, length: 1024 * 1024 },\n});\n\n// Get bytes 100-200\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.bin'', {\n  range: { offset: 100, length: 100 },\n});\n\n// Get from offset to end\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.bin'', {\n  range: { offset: 1000 },\n});\n```\n\n**Conditional Downloads:**\n\n```typescript\n// Only download if etag matches\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.txt'', {\n  onlyIf: {\n    etagMatches: cachedEtag,\n  },\n});\n\nif (!object) {\n  // Etag didn''t match, file was modified\n  return c.json({ error: ''File changed'' }, 412);\n}\n```\n\n### head() - Get Metadata Only\n\n**Signature:**\n```typescript\nhead(key: string): Promise<R2Object | null>\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```typescript\n// Get object metadata without downloading body\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.head(''file.txt'');\n\nif (object) {\n  console.log({\n    key: object.key,\n    size: object.size,\n    etag: object.etag,\n    uploaded: object.uploaded,\n    contentType: object.httpMetadata?.contentType,\n    customMetadata: object.customMetadata,\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Check if file exists\n- Get file size before downloading\n- Check last modified date\n- Validate etag for caching\n\n### delete() - Delete Objects\n\n**Signature:**\n```typescript\ndelete(key: string | string[]): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Single Delete:**\n\n```typescript\n// Delete single object\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete(''file.txt'');\n\n// No error if file doesn''t exist (idempotent)\n```\n\n**Bulk Delete (Up to 1000 keys):**\n\n```typescript\n// Delete multiple objects at once\nconst keysToDelete = [\n  ''old-file-1.txt'',\n  ''old-file-2.txt'',\n  ''temp/cache-data.json'',\n];\n\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete(keysToDelete);\n\n// Much faster than individual deletes\n```\n\n**Delete with Confirmation:**\n\n```typescript\napp.delete(''/files/:filename'', async (c) => {\n  const filename = c.req.param(''filename'');\n\n  // Check if exists first\n  const exists = await c.env.MY_BUCKET.head(filename);\n\n  if (!exists) {\n    return c.json({ error: ''File not found'' }, 404);\n  }\n\n  await c.env.MY_BUCKET.delete(filename);\n\n  return c.json({ success: true, deleted: filename });\n});\n```\n\n### list() - List Objects\n\n**Signature:**\n```typescript\nlist(options?: R2ListOptions): Promise<R2Objects>\n```\n\n**Basic Listing:**\n\n```typescript\n// List all objects (up to 1000)\nconst listed = await env.MY_BUCKET.list();\n\nconsole.log({\n  objects: listed.objects,      // Array of R2Object\n  truncated: listed.truncated,  // true if more results exist\n  cursor: listed.cursor,        // For pagination\n});\n\n// Process objects\nfor (const object of listed.objects) {\n  console.log(`${object.key}: ${object.size} bytes`);\n}\n```\n\n**Pagination:**\n\n```typescript\napp.get(''/api/files'', async (c) => {\n  const cursor = c.req.query(''cursor'');\n\n  const listed = await c.env.MY_BUCKET.list({\n    limit: 100,\n    cursor: cursor || undefined,\n  });\n\n  return c.json({\n    files: listed.objects.map(obj => ({\n      name: obj.key,\n      size: obj.size,\n      uploaded: obj.uploaded,\n      etag: obj.etag,\n    })),\n    hasMore: listed.truncated,\n    nextCursor: listed.cursor,\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Prefix Filtering (List by Directory):**\n\n```typescript\n// List all files in ''images/'' folder\nconst images = await env.MY_BUCKET.list({\n  prefix: ''images/'',\n});\n\n// List all user files\nconst userFiles = await env.MY_BUCKET.list({\n  prefix: `users/${userId}/`,\n});\n```\n\n**Delimiter (Folder-like Listing):**\n\n```typescript\n// List only top-level items in ''uploads/''\nconst listed = await env.MY_BUCKET.list({\n  prefix: ''uploads/'',\n  delimiter: ''/'',\n});\n\nconsole.log(''Files:'', listed.objects);          // Files directly in uploads/\nconsole.log(''Folders:'', listed.delimitedPrefixes); // Sub-folders like uploads/2024/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Multipart Uploads\n\nFor files larger than 100MB or for resumable uploads, use multipart upload API.\n\n### When to Use Multipart Upload\n\n✅ **Use multipart when:**\n- File size > 100MB\n- Need resumable uploads\n- Want to parallelize upload\n- Uploading from browser/client\n\n❌ **Don''t use multipart when:**\n- File size < 5MB (overhead not worth it)\n- Uploading within Worker (use direct put())\n\n### Basic Multipart Upload Flow\n\n```typescript\napp.post(''/api/upload/start'', async (c) => {\n  const { filename } = await c.req.json();\n\n  // Create multipart upload\n  const multipart = await c.env.MY_BUCKET.createMultipartUpload(filename, {\n    httpMetadata: {\n      contentType: ''application/octet-stream'',\n    },\n  });\n\n  return c.json({\n    key: multipart.key,\n    uploadId: multipart.uploadId,\n  });\n});\n\napp.put(''/api/upload/part'', async (c) => {\n  const { key, uploadId, partNumber } = await c.req.json();\n  const body = await c.req.arrayBuffer();\n\n  // Resume the multipart upload\n  const multipart = c.env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n\n  // Upload a part\n  const uploadedPart = await multipart.uploadPart(partNumber, body);\n\n  return c.json({\n    partNumber: uploadedPart.partNumber,\n    etag: uploadedPart.etag,\n  });\n});\n\napp.post(''/api/upload/complete'', async (c) => {\n  const { key, uploadId, parts } = await c.req.json();\n\n  // Resume the multipart upload\n  const multipart = c.env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n\n  // Complete the upload\n  const object = await multipart.complete(parts);\n\n  return c.json({\n    success: true,\n    key: object.key,\n    size: object.size,\n    etag: object.etag,\n  });\n});\n\napp.post(''/api/upload/abort'', async (c) => {\n  const { key, uploadId } = await c.req.json();\n\n  const multipart = c.env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n  await multipart.abort();\n\n  return c.json({ success: true });\n});\n```\n\n### Complete Multipart Upload Example\n\n```typescript\n// Full Worker implementing multipart upload API\ninterface Env {\n  MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket;\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<Response> {\n    const url = new URL(request.url);\n    const key = url.pathname.slice(1);\n    const action = url.searchParams.get(''action'');\n\n    switch (request.method) {\n      case ''POST'': {\n        switch (action) {\n          case ''mpu-create'': {\n            // Create multipart upload\n            const multipart = await env.MY_BUCKET.createMultipartUpload(key);\n            return Response.json({\n              key: multipart.key,\n              uploadId: multipart.uploadId,\n            });\n          }\n          case ''mpu-complete'': {\n            // Complete multipart upload\n            const uploadId = url.searchParams.get(''uploadId'')!;\n            const multipart = env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n            const parts = await request.json();\n            const object = await multipart.complete(parts);\n            return Response.json({\n              key: object.key,\n              etag: object.etag,\n              size: object.size,\n            });\n          }\n          default:\n            return new Response(`Unknown action: ${action}`, { status: 400 });\n        }\n      }\n      case ''PUT'': {\n        switch (action) {\n          case ''mpu-uploadpart'': {\n            // Upload a part\n            const uploadId = url.searchParams.get(''uploadId'')!;\n            const partNumber = parseInt(url.searchParams.get(''partNumber'')!);\n            const multipart = env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n            const uploadedPart = await multipart.uploadPart(partNumber, request.body!);\n            return Response.json({\n              partNumber: uploadedPart.partNumber,\n              etag: uploadedPart.etag,\n            });\n          }\n          default:\n            return new Response(`Unknown action: ${action}`, { status: 400 });\n        }\n      }\n      case ''DELETE'': {\n        switch (action) {\n          case ''mpu-abort'': {\n            // Abort multipart upload\n            const uploadId = url.searchParams.get(''uploadId'')!;\n            const multipart = env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\n            await multipart.abort();\n            return new Response(null, { status: 204 });\n          }\n          default:\n            return new Response(`Unknown action: ${action}`, { status: 400 });\n        }\n      }\n      default:\n        return new Response(''Method Not Allowed'', { status: 405 });\n    }\n  },\n} satisfies ExportedHandler<Env>;\n```\n\n---\n\n## Presigned URLs\n\nPresigned URLs allow clients to upload/download objects directly to/from R2 without going through your Worker.\n\n### When to Use Presigned URLs\n\n✅ **Use presigned URLs when:**\n- Client uploads directly to R2 (saves Worker bandwidth)\n- Temporary access to private objects\n- Sharing download links with expiry\n- Avoiding Worker request size limits\n\n❌ **Don''t use presigned URLs when:**\n- You need to process/validate uploads\n- Files are already public\n- Using custom domains (presigned URLs only work with R2 endpoint)\n\n### Generate Presigned URLs with aws4fetch\n\n```bash\nnpm install aws4fetch\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { AwsClient } from ''aws4fetch'';\n\ninterface Env {\n  R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID: string;\n  R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: string;\n  ACCOUNT_ID: string;\n  MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket;\n}\n\nconst app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Env }>();\n\napp.post(''/api/presigned-upload'', async (c) => {\n  const { filename } = await c.req.json();\n\n  // Create AWS client for R2\n  const r2Client = new AwsClient({\n    accessKeyId: c.env.R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID,\n    secretAccessKey: c.env.R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,\n  });\n\n  const bucketName = ''my-bucket'';\n  const accountId = c.env.ACCOUNT_ID;\n\n  const url = new URL(\n    `https://${bucketName}.${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${filename}`\n  );\n\n  // Set expiry (1 hour)\n  url.searchParams.set(''X-Amz-Expires'', ''3600'');\n\n  // Sign the URL for PUT\n  const signed = await r2Client.sign(\n    new Request(url, { method: ''PUT'' }),\n    { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n  );\n\n  return c.json({\n    uploadUrl: signed.url,\n    expiresIn: 3600,\n  });\n});\n\napp.post(''/api/presigned-download'', async (c) => {\n  const { filename } = await c.req.json();\n\n  const r2Client = new AwsClient({\n    accessKeyId: c.env.R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID,\n    secretAccessKey: c.env.R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,\n  });\n\n  const bucketName = ''my-bucket'';\n  const accountId = c.env.ACCOUNT_ID;\n\n  const url = new URL(\n    `https://${bucketName}.${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${filename}`\n  );\n\n  url.searchParams.set(''X-Amz-Expires'', ''3600'');\n\n  const signed = await r2Client.sign(\n    new Request(url, { method: ''GET'' }),\n    { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n  );\n\n  return c.json({\n    downloadUrl: signed.url,\n    expiresIn: 3600,\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Client-Side Upload with Presigned URL\n\n```javascript\n// 1. Get presigned URL from your Worker\nconst response = await fetch(''https://my-worker.workers.dev/api/presigned-upload'', {\n  method: ''POST'',\n  headers: { ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'' },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ filename: ''photo.jpg'' }),\n});\n\nconst { uploadUrl } = await response.json();\n\n// 2. Upload file directly to R2\nconst file = document.querySelector(''input[type=\"file\"]'').files[0];\n\nawait fetch(uploadUrl, {\n  method: ''PUT'',\n  body: file,\n  headers: {\n    ''Content-Type'': file.type,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Presigned URL Security\n\n**CRITICAL:**\n- ❌ **NEVER** expose R2 access keys in client-side code\n- ✅ **ALWAYS** generate presigned URLs server-side\n- ✅ **ALWAYS** set appropriate expiry times (1-24 hours typical)\n- ✅ **CONSIDER** adding authentication before generating URLs\n- ✅ **CONSIDER** rate limiting presigned URL generation\n\n```typescript\n// Example with auth check\napp.post(''/api/presigned-upload'', async (c) => {\n  // Verify user is authenticated\n  const authHeader = c.req.header(''Authorization'');\n  if (!authHeader) {\n    return c.json({ error: ''Unauthorized'' }, 401);\n  }\n\n  // Validate user has permission\n  const userId = await verifyToken(authHeader);\n  if (!userId) {\n    return c.json({ error: ''Invalid token'' }, 401);\n  }\n\n  // Only allow uploads to user''s own folder\n  const { filename } = await c.req.json();\n  const key = `users/${userId}/${filename}`;\n\n  // Generate presigned URL...\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## CORS Configuration\n\nConfigure CORS to allow browser requests to your R2 bucket.\n\n### Public Bucket CORS\n\n```json\n{\n  \"CORSRules\": [\n    {\n      \"AllowedOrigins\": [\"https://example.com\"],\n      \"AllowedMethods\": [\"GET\", \"HEAD\"],\n      \"AllowedHeaders\": [\"*\"],\n      \"MaxAgeSeconds\": 3600\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Allow All Origins (Public Assets)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"CORSRules\": [\n    {\n      \"AllowedOrigins\": [\"*\"],\n      \"AllowedMethods\": [\"GET\", \"HEAD\"],\n      \"AllowedHeaders\": [\"Range\"],\n      \"MaxAgeSeconds\": 3600\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Upload with CORS\n\n```json\n{\n  \"CORSRules\": [\n    {\n      \"AllowedOrigins\": [\"https://app.example.com\"],\n      \"AllowedMethods\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\", \"POST\", \"DELETE\", \"HEAD\"],\n      \"AllowedHeaders\": [\n        \"Content-Type\",\n        \"Content-MD5\",\n        \"x-amz-meta-*\"\n      ],\n      \"ExposeHeaders\": [\"ETag\"],\n      \"MaxAgeSeconds\": 3600\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Apply CORS via Dashboard\n\n1. Go to Cloudflare Dashboard → R2\n2. Select your bucket\n3. Go to Settings tab\n4. Under CORS Policy → Add CORS policy\n5. Paste JSON configuration\n6. Save\n\n### CORS for Presigned URLs\n\nWhen using presigned URLs, CORS is handled by R2 directly. Configure CORS on the bucket, not in your Worker.\n\n---\n\n## HTTP Metadata\n\n### Content-Type\n\n```typescript\n// Set content type on upload\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''image.jpg'', imageData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''image/jpeg'',\n  },\n});\n\n// Will be returned in Content-Type header when downloaded\n```\n\n### Cache-Control\n\n```typescript\n// Set caching headers\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''static/logo.png'', logoData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''image/png'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=31536000, immutable'',\n  },\n});\n\n// For frequently updated content\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''api/data.json'', jsonData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/json'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=60, must-revalidate'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Content-Disposition\n\n```typescript\n// Force download with specific filename\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''report.pdf'', pdfData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/pdf'',\n    contentDisposition: ''attachment; filename=\"monthly-report.pdf\"'',\n  },\n});\n\n// Display inline\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''image.jpg'', imageData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''image/jpeg'',\n    contentDisposition: ''inline'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Content-Encoding\n\n```typescript\n// Indicate gzip compression\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''data.json.gz'', gzippedData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/json'',\n    contentEncoding: ''gzip'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Custom Metadata\n\nStore arbitrary key-value metadata with objects.\n\n### Setting Custom Metadata\n\n```typescript\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''document.pdf'', pdfData, {\n  customMetadata: {\n    userId: ''12345'',\n    department: ''engineering'',\n    uploadDate: new Date().toISOString(),\n    version: ''1.0'',\n    approved: ''true'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Reading Custom Metadata\n\n```typescript\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.head(''document.pdf'');\n\nif (object) {\n  console.log(object.customMetadata);\n  // {\n  //   userId: ''12345'',\n  //   department: ''engineering'',\n  //   uploadDate: ''2025-10-21T10:00:00.000Z'',\n  //   version: ''1.0'',\n  //   approved: ''true''\n  // }\n}\n```\n\n### Limitations\n\n- Max 2KB total size for all custom metadata\n- Keys and values must be strings\n- Keys are case-insensitive\n- No limit on number of keys (within 2KB total)\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Common R2 Errors\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  await env.MY_BUCKET.put(key, data);\n} catch (error: any) {\n  const message = error.message;\n\n  if (message.includes(''R2_ERROR'')) {\n    // Generic R2 error\n  } else if (message.includes(''exceeded'')) {\n    // Quota exceeded\n  } else if (message.includes(''precondition'')) {\n    // Conditional operation failed\n  } else if (message.includes(''multipart'')) {\n    // Multipart upload error\n  }\n\n  console.error(''R2 Error:'', message);\n  return c.json({ error: ''Storage operation failed'' }, 500);\n}\n```\n\n### Retry Logic\n\n```typescript\nasync function r2WithRetry<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  maxRetries = 3\n): Promise<T> {\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error: any) {\n      const message = error.message;\n\n      // Retry on transient errors\n      const isRetryable =\n        message.includes(''network'') ||\n        message.includes(''timeout'') ||\n        message.includes(''temporarily unavailable'');\n\n      if (!isRetryable || attempt === maxRetries - 1) {\n        throw error;\n      }\n\n      // Exponential backoff\n      const delay = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt), 5000);\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(''Retry logic failed'');\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst object = await r2WithRetry(() =>\n  env.MY_BUCKET.get(''important-file.txt'')\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\n### Batch Operations\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ DON''T: Delete files one by one\nfor (const file of filesToDelete) {\n  await env.MY_BUCKET.delete(file);\n}\n\n// ✅ DO: Batch delete (up to 1000 keys)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete(filesToDelete);\n```\n\n### Range Requests for Large Files\n\n```typescript\n// Download only the first 10MB of a large video\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''video.mp4'', {\n  range: { offset: 0, length: 10 * 1024 * 1024 },\n});\n\n// Return range to client\nreturn new Response(object.body, {\n  status: 206, // Partial Content\n  headers: {\n    ''Content-Type'': ''video/mp4'',\n    ''Content-Range'': `bytes 0-${10 * 1024 * 1024 - 1}/${object.size}`,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Cache Headers\n\n```typescript\n// Immutable assets (hashed filenames)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''static/app.abc123.js'', jsData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/javascript'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=31536000, immutable'',\n  },\n});\n\n// Dynamic content\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''api/latest.json'', jsonData, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/json'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=300'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Checksums for Data Integrity\n\n```typescript\n// Compute MD5 checksum\nconst md5Hash = await crypto.subtle.digest(''MD5'', fileData);\n\n// R2 will verify checksum on upload\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''important.dat'', fileData, {\n  md5: md5Hash,\n});\n\n// If checksum doesn''t match, upload will fail\n```\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n### ✅ Always Do:\n\n1. **Set appropriate `contentType`** for all uploads\n2. **Use batch delete** for multiple objects (up to 1000)\n3. **Set cache headers** (`cacheControl`) for static assets\n4. **Use presigned URLs** for large client uploads\n5. **Use multipart upload** for files > 100MB\n6. **Set CORS policy** before allowing browser uploads\n7. **Set expiry times** on presigned URLs (1-24 hours)\n8. **Handle errors gracefully** with try/catch\n9. **Use `head()`** instead of `get()` when you only need metadata\n10. **Use conditional operations** to prevent overwrites\n\n### ❌ Never Do:\n\n1. **Never expose R2 access keys** in client-side code\n2. **Never skip `contentType`** (files will download as binary)\n3. **Never delete in loops** (use batch delete)\n4. **Never upload without error handling**\n5. **Never skip CORS** for browser uploads\n6. **Never use multipart** for small files (< 5MB)\n7. **Never delete >1000 keys** in single call (will fail)\n8. **Never assume uploads succeed** (always check response)\n9. **Never skip presigned URL expiry** (security risk)\n10. **Never hardcode bucket names** (use bindings)\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevented\n\n| Issue | Description | How to Avoid |\n|-------|-------------|--------------|\n| **CORS errors in browser** | Browser can''t upload/download due to missing CORS policy | Configure CORS in bucket settings before browser access |\n| **Files download as binary** | Missing content-type causes browsers to download files instead of display | Always set `httpMetadata.contentType` on upload |\n| **Presigned URL expiry** | URLs never expire, posing security risk | Always set `X-Amz-Expires` (1-24 hours typical) |\n| **Multipart upload limits** | Parts exceed 100MB or >10,000 parts | Keep parts 5MB-100MB, max 10,000 parts per upload |\n| **Bulk delete limits** | Trying to delete >1000 keys fails | Chunk deletes into batches of 1000 |\n| **Custom metadata overflow** | Metadata exceeds 2KB limit | Keep custom metadata under 2KB total |\n\n---\n\n## Wrangler Commands Reference\n\n```bash\n# Bucket management\nwrangler r2 bucket create <BUCKET_NAME>\nwrangler r2 bucket list\nwrangler r2 bucket delete <BUCKET_NAME>\n\n# Object management\nwrangler r2 object put <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY> --file=<FILE_PATH>\nwrangler r2 object get <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY> --file=<OUTPUT_PATH>\nwrangler r2 object delete <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY>\n\n# List objects\nwrangler r2 object list <BUCKET_NAME>\nwrangler r2 object list <BUCKET_NAME> --prefix=\"folder/\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Official Documentation\n\n- **R2 Overview**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/\n- **Get Started**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/get-started/\n- **Workers API**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/workers/workers-api-reference/\n- **Multipart Upload**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/workers/workers-multipart-usage/\n- **Presigned URLs**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/presigned-urls/\n- **CORS Configuration**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/cors/\n- **Public Buckets**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/public-buckets/\n\n---\n\n**Ready to store with R2!** 🚀\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:22:14.080Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud-Native Agents needing scalable object storage solutions with Cloudflare R2","zh":"非常适合需要可扩展对象存储解决方案的云原生代理，特别是与Cloudflare R2集成","ja":"Cloudflare R2を使用したスケーラブルなオブジェクトストレージソリューションを必要とするクラウドネイティブエージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드플레어 R2와 통합하여 확장 가능한 객체 저장소 솔루션을 필요로 하는 클라우드 네이티브 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Cloud-Native que necesitan soluciones de almacenamiento de objetos escalables con Cloudflare R2","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud-Native ayant besoin de solutions de stockage d''objets évolutives avec Cloudflare R2","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Native-Agents, die skalierbare Objekt-Speicherlösungen mit Cloudflare R2 benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Nativos em Nuvem que necessitam de soluções de armazenamento de objetos escaláveis com Cloudflare R2","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, которым необходимы масштабируемые решения для хранения объектов с Cloudflare R2","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأصليين في السحابة الذين يحتاجون إلى حلول تخزين كائنات قابلة للتوسيع مع Cloudflare R2"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Cloudflare''s edge network for secure and performant data storage, utilizing wrangler and cloudflare-worker-base for seamless Worker setup and management, with dependencies like aws4fetch for secure authentication","zh":"赋予代理使用Cloudflare的边缘网络进行安全高效的数据存储的能力，使用wrangler和cloudflare-worker-base实现Worker的无缝设置和管理，并利用aws4fetch进行安全认证","ja":"エージェントがCloudflareのエッジネットワークを使用してセキュアでパフォーマンスの高いデータストレージを実現できるようにし、wranglerとcloudflare-worker-baseを使用してWorkerのセットアップと管理を簡素化し、aws4fetchを使用してセキュアな認証を実現","ko":"에이전트가 클라우드플레어의 에지 네트워크를 사용하여 보안이 뛰고 성능이 뛰어난 데이터 저장소를 구현할 수 있도록 하며, wrangler와 cloudflare-worker-base를 사용하여 Worker의 설정과 관리를 간소화하고, aws4fetch를 사용하여 보안 인증을 구현","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar la red de borde de Cloudflare para un almacenamiento de datos seguro y de alto rendimiento, utilizando wrangler y cloudflare-worker-base para una configuración y administración de Workers sin problemas, con dependencias como aws4fetch para una autenticación segura","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser le réseau de bord de Cloudflare pour un stockage de données sécurisé et performant, en utilisant wrangler et cloudflare-worker-base pour une configuration et une gestion de Workers sans problème, avec des dépendances comme aws4fetch pour une authentification sécurisée","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Cloudflares Edge-Netzwerk für sicheres und leistungsfähiges Daten-Speichern zu nutzen, indem wrangler und cloudflare-worker-base für eine nahtlose Worker-Konfiguration und -Verwaltung verwendet werden, mit Abhängigkeiten wie aws4fetch für eine sichere Authentifizierung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar a rede de borda da Cloudflare para armazenamento de dados seguro e de alto desempenho, utilizando wrangler e cloudflare-worker-base para configuração e gerenciamento de Workers sem problemas, com dependências como aws4fetch para autenticação segura","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность использовать сеть Edge от Cloudflare для безопасного и высокопроизводительного хранения данных, используя wrangler и cloudflare-worker-base для бесшовной настройки и управления Workers, с зависимостями, такими как aws4fetch, для безопасной аутентификации","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على الاستفادة من شبكة الحافة من Cloudflare لتخزين البيانات الآمن والسريع، باستخدام wrangler و cloudflare-worker-base لإعداد وتشغيل Workers دون مشاكل، مع التبعيات مثل aws4fetch لتحقق الهوية الآمن"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating R2 buckets for data storage","Configuring Cloudflare Workers for custom storage solutions","Integrating object storage with Cloudflare''s edge network for optimized data delivery"],"zh":["为数据存储创建R2存储桶","配置Cloudflare Workers以实现自定义存储解决方案","将对象存储与Cloudflare的边缘网络集成以优化数据交付"],"ja":["データストレージ用のR2バケットを作成","カスタムストレージソリューション用のCloudflare Workersを構成","オブジェクトストレージをCloudflareのエッジネットワークに統合してデータ配信を最適化"],"ko":["데이터 저장을 위한 R2 버킷 생성","사용자 지정 저장소 솔루션을 위한 클라우드플레어 Workers 설정","객체 저장소를 클라우드플레어의 에지 네트워크와 통합하여 데이터 전송을 최적화"],"es":["Crear cubos R2 para el almacenamiento de datos","Configurar Cloudflare Workers para soluciones de almacenamiento personalizadas","Integrar el almacenamiento de objetos con la red de borde de Cloudflare para una entrega de datos optimizada"],"fr":["Créer des buckets R2 pour le stockage de données","Configurer les Cloudflare Workers pour des solutions de stockage personnalisées","Intégrer le stockage d''objets avec le réseau de bord de Cloudflare pour une livraison de données optimisée"],"de":["R2-Buckets für Datenspeicherung erstellen","Cloudflare-Worker für benutzerdefinierte Speicherlösungen konfigurieren","Objektspeicherung in Cloudflares Edge-Netzwerk für optimierte Datenlieferung integrieren"],"pt":["Criar buckets R2 para armazenamento de dados","Configurar Cloudflare Workers para soluções de armazenamento personalizadas","Integrar armazenamento de objetos com a rede de borda da Cloudflare para entrega de dados otimizada"],"ru":["Создание бакетов R2 для хранения данных","Настройка Cloudflare Workers для индивидуальных решений хранения","Интеграция хранения объектов с сетью Edge от Cloudflare для оптимизированной доставки данных"],"ar":["إنشاء دفق R2 لتخزين البيانات","تكوين Cloudflare Workers لحلول تخزين مخصصة","دمج تخزين الكائنات مع شبكة الحافة من Cloudflare لتسليم البيانات المتقن"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare account and Wrangler CLI setup","Dependent on cloudflare-worker-base and @cloudflare/workers-types libraries"],"zh":["需要Cloudflare账户和Wrangler CLI设置","依赖于cloudflare-worker-base和@cloudflare/workers-types库"],"ja":["CloudflareアカウントとWrangler CLIのセットアップが必要","cloudflare-worker-baseと@cloudflare/workers-typesライブラリに依存"],"ko":["클라우드플레어 계정과 Wrangler CLI 설정이 필요","cloudflare-worker-base와 @cloudflare/workers-types 라이브러리에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una cuenta de Cloudflare y una configuración de Wrangler CLI","Depende de las bibliotecas cloudflare-worker-base y @cloudflare/workers-types"],"fr":["Nécessite un compte Cloudflare et une configuration de Wrangler CLI","Dépend des bibliothèques cloudflare-worker-base et @cloudflare/workers-types"],"de":["Benötigt ein Cloudflare-Konto und eine Wrangler-CLI-Konfiguration","Hängt von den Bibliotheken cloudflare-worker-base und @cloudflare/workers-types ab"],"pt":["Exige conta Cloudflare e configuração do Wrangler CLI","Dependente das bibliotecas cloudflare-worker-base e @cloudflare/workers-types"],"ru":["Требует учетной записи Cloudflare и настройки Wrangler CLI","Зависит от библиотек cloudflare-worker-base и @cloudflare/workers-types"],"ar":["يتطلب حساب Cloudflare وإعداد Wrangler CLI","يعتمد على مكتبات cloudflare-worker-base و @cloudflare/workers-types"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jellydn/my-ai-tools/pickup', 'community', 'jellydn', 'my-ai-tools', 'jellydn/my-ai-tools', 'pickup', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:22:17.343Z', NULL, '{"id":"jellydn/my-ai-tools/pickup","name":"pickup","description":{"zh":"Pickup 技术是用于 AI 编码工具的综合配置管理，支持 Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex 和 Claude Code Switch 的自定义配置","ja":"Pickup 技術は、AI コーディングツールのための包括的な設定管理であり、Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex、Claude Code Switch のカスタム設定をサポート","ko":"Pickup 기술은 AI 코딩 도구를 위한 포괄적인 구성 관리로 Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex, Claude Code Switch의 사용자 지정 구성 관리를 지원","es":"El skill pickup ofrece una gestión de configuración integral para herramientas de codificación AI, permitiendo replicar configuraciones personalizadas","fr":"Le skill pickup offre une gestion de configuration complète pour les outils de codage AI, permettant de répliquer des configurations personnalisées","de":"Der pickup-Skill bietet eine umfassende Konfigurationsverwaltung für AI-Coding-Tools, ermöglicht die Replikation von benutzerdefinierten Konfigurationen","pt":"O Pickup é uma ferramenta de gerenciamento de configuração para ferramentas de codificação AI, permitindo a replicação de configurações personalizadas.","ru":"Pickup - это инструмент управления конфигурацией для инструментов кодирования AI, позволяющий реплицировать пользовательские конфигурации.","ar":"بيك أب هو أداة لإدارة التكوين لأدوات التشفير الإصطناعي، مما يسمح بتكرار التكوينات المخصصة.","en":"Comprehensive configuration management for AI coding tools - Replicate my complete setup for Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex and Claude Code Switch with custom configurations, MCP servers, plugins, and commands."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Pickup 技术：AI 编码工具配置管理","ja":"Pickup 技術：AI コーディングツールの設定管理","ko":"Pickup 기술: AI 코딩 도구 구성 관리","es":"Configuración de pickup para herramientas de codificación AI","fr":"Configuration de pickup pour outils de codage AI","de":"Pickup-Konfiguration für AI-Coding-Tools","pt":"Pickup: Gerenciamento de Configuração para Ferramentas de...","ru":"Pickup: Управление конфигурацией для инструментов кодиров...","ar":"بيك أب: إدارة التكوين لأدوات التشفير الإصطناعي","en":"pickup"},"description":{"zh":"Pickup 技术是用于 AI 编码工具的综合配置管理，支持 Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex 和 Claude Code Switch 的自定义配置","ja":"Pickup 技術は、AI コーディングツールのための包括的な設定管理であり、Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex、Claude Code Switch のカスタム設定をサポート","ko":"Pickup 기술은 AI 코딩 도구를 위한 포괄적인 구성 관리로 Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex, Claude Code Switch의 사용자 지정 구성 관리를 지원","es":"El skill pickup ofrece una gestión de configuración integral para herramientas de codificación AI, permitiendo replicar configuraciones personalizadas","fr":"Le skill pickup offre une gestion de configuration complète pour les outils de codage AI, permettant de répliquer des configurations personnalisées","de":"Der pickup-Skill bietet eine umfassende Konfigurationsverwaltung für AI-Coding-Tools, ermöglicht die Replikation von benutzerdefinierten Konfigurationen","pt":"O Pickup é uma ferramenta de gerenciamento de configuração para ferramentas de codificação AI, permitindo a replicação de configurações personalizadas.","ru":"Pickup - это инструмент управления конфигурацией для инструментов кодирования AI, позволяющий реплицировать пользовательские конфигурации.","ar":"بيك أب هو أداة لإدارة التكوين لأدوات التشفير الإصطناعي، مما يسمح بتكرار التكوينات المخصصة.","en":"Comprehensive configuration management for AI coding tools - Replicate my complete setup for Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex and Claude Code Switch with cu..."},"definition":{"en":"Comprehensive configuration management for AI coding tools - Replicate my complete setup for Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex and Claude Code Switch with custom configurations, MCP servers, plugins, and commands."},"features":{"zh":["支持 Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex 和 Claude Code Switch","自定义配置管理","MCP 服务器和插件支持","命令行支持"],"ja":["Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex、Claude Code Switch をサポート","カスタム設定管理","MCP サーバーとプラグインのサポート","コマンドラインのサポート"],"ko":["Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex, Claude Code Switch 지원","사용자 지정 구성 관리","MCP 서버 및 플러그인 지원","명령줄 지원"],"es":["Gestión de configuración integral","Replicación de configuraciones personalizadas","Compatibilidad con herramientas como Claude Code y OpenCode","Uso de comandos y plugins personalizados","Almacenamiento de sesiones de handoff en `.claude/handoffs/`"],"fr":["Gestion de configuration complète","Réplication de configurations personnalisées","Compatibilité avec des outils tels que Claude Code et OpenCode","Utilisation de commandes et de plugins personnalisés","Stockage de sessions de handoff dans `.claude/handoffs/`"],"de":["Umfassende Konfigurationsverwaltung","Replikation von benutzerdefinierten Konfigurationen","Kompatibilität mit Tools wie Claude Code und OpenCode","Verwendung von benutzerdefinierten Befehlen und Plugins","Speicherung von Handoff-Sitzungen in `.claude/handoffs/`"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de configuração para ferramentas de codificação AI","Replicação de configurações personalizadas","Suporte a Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex e Claude Code Switch","Gerenciamento de servidores MCP e plugins","Comandos personalizados"],"ru":["Управление конфигурацией для инструментов кодирования AI","Репликация пользовательских конфигураций","Поддержка Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex и Claude Code Switch","Управление серверами MCP и плагинами","Пользовательские команды"],"ar":["إدارة التكوين لأدوات التشفير الإصطناعي","تكرار التكوينات المخصصة","دعم Claude Code و OpenCode و Amp و Codex و Claude Code Switch","إدارة خوادم MCP والملحقات","الأوامر المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 编码工具","配置管理","Pickup 技术","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"],"ja":["AI コーディングツール","設定管理","Pickup 技術","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"],"ko":["AI 코딩 도구","구성 관리","Pickup 기술","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"],"es":["pickup","configuración de codificación AI","herramientas de desarrollo","replicación de configuraciones","Claude Code","OpenCode","codificación AI","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["pickup","configuration de codage AI","outils de développement","réplication de configurations","Claude Code","OpenCode","codage AI","développement de logiciels"],"de":["pickup","AI-Coding-Konfiguration","Entwicklungstools","Replikation von Konfigurationen","Claude Code","OpenCode","AI-Coding","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["Pickup","gerenciamento de configuração","ferramentas de codificação AI","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"],"ru":["Pickup","управление конфигурацией","инструменты кодирования AI","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"],"ar":["بيك أب","إدارة التكوين","أدوات التشفير الإصطناعي","Claude Code","OpenCode","Amp","Codex","Claude Code Switch"]}},"owner":"jellydn","repo":"my-ai-tools","repoPath":"jellydn/my-ai-tools","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pickup","description":"Resumes work from a previous handoff session which are stored in `.claude/handoffs/`","bodyPreview":"# Pickup Handoff\n\nResumes work from a previous handoff session which are stored in `.claude/handoffs/`.\n\n## Usage\n\n`/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`\n\nIf no handoff file is specified, will show available handoffs and prompt for selection.\n\n## Process\n\n1. Find available handoffs in `.claude/handoffs/`\n2. Read the selected handoff file\n3. Present the handoff summary to the user\n4. Ask the user to confirm they want to continue\n5. If confirmed, proceed with the next step described in the handoff\n\n## Available","body":"# Pickup Handoff\n\nResumes work from a previous handoff session which are stored in `.claude/handoffs/`.\n\n## Usage\n\n`/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`\n\nIf no handoff file is specified, will show available handoffs and prompt for selection.\n\n## Process\n\n1. Find available handoffs in `.claude/handoffs/`\n2. Read the selected handoff file\n3. Present the handoff summary to the user\n4. Ask the user to confirm they want to continue\n5. If confirmed, proceed with the next step described in the handoff\n\n## Available Handoffs\n\nTo see available handoffs:\n\n```bash\nls -la .claude/handoffs/\n```\n\nHandoffs are named in format: `[YYYY-MM-DD]-[slug].md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:22:17.343Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Coding Agents requiring seamless configuration management and handoff capabilities for tools like Claude Code and OpenCode.","zh":"适用于需要无缝配置管理和工具交接的AI编码代理，例如Claude Code和OpenCode。","ja":"Claude CodeやOpenCodeなどのツールでシームレスな設定管理とハンドオフ機能を必要とするAIコーディングエージェントに最適。","ko":"클라우드 코드 및 오픈 코드와 같은 도구에서 무결점 구성 관리 및 인도 기능을 필요로 하는 AI 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de codificación de IA que requieren una gestión de configuración y capacidad de entrega sin problemas para herramientas como Claude Code y OpenCode.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de codage IA nécessitant une gestion de configuration et des capacités de passage en main sans problème pour des outils tels que Claude Code et OpenCode.","de":"Ideal für AI-Coding-Agenten, die eine nahtlose Konfigurationsverwaltung und Übernahmefähigkeiten für Tools wie Claude Code und OpenCode erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Codificação de IA que exigem gerenciamento de configuração sem interrupções e capacidades de handoff para ferramentas como Claude Code e OpenCode.","ru":"Идеально для агентов кодирования ИИ, требующих бесшовного управления конфигурацией и возможностей передачи для инструментов như Claude Code и OpenCode.","ar":"مثالية لعميل الترميز الذكي المتطلب لإدارة التكوين الخالية من العيوب وقدرات التخلي عن الأدوات مثل Claude Code و OpenCode."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to replicate complete setups with custom configurations, MCP servers, plugins, and commands, streamlining development workflows with `.claude/handoffs/` file management and `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]` commands.","zh":"赋予代理复制完整设置的能力，包括自定义配置、MCP服务器、插件和命令，并通过`.claude/handoffs/`文件管理和`/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`命令优化开发工作流程。","ja":"エージェントがMCPサーバー、プラグイン、コマンドを含むカスタム構成で完全なセットアップを複製できるようにし、`.claude/handoffs/`ファイルの管理と`/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`コマンドで開発ワークフローを最適化します。","ko":"에이전트가 MCP 서버, 플러그인, 명령어를 포함한 사용자 지정 구성으로 전체 설정을 복제할 수 있도록 하며, `.claude/handoffs/` 파일 관리 및 `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]` 명령어로 개발 워크플로우를 최적화합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes replicar configuraciones completas con configuraciones personalizadas, servidores MCP, plugins y comandos, simplificando los flujos de trabajo de desarrollo con la gestión de archivos `.claude/handoffs/` y comandos `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de répliquer des configurations complètes avec des configurations personnalisées, des serveurs MCP, des plug-ins et des commandes, simplifiant les flux de travail de développement avec la gestion de fichiers `.claude/handoffs/` et des commandes `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplette Konfigurationen mit benutzerdefinierten Konfigurationen, MCP-Servern, Plugins und Befehlen zu replizieren, und strafft so die Entwicklungsworkflows mit der Verwaltung von `.claude/handoffs/`-Dateien und `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`-Befehlen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes repliquem configurações completas com configurações personalizadas, servidores MCP, plug-ins e comandos, otimizando os fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento com gerenciamento de arquivos `.claude/handoffs/` e comandos `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реплицировать полные настройки с настраиваемыми конфигурациями, серверами MCP, плагинами и командами, оптимизируя рабочие процессы разработки с помощью управления файлами `.claude/handoffs/` и команд `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تكرار الإعدادات الكاملة مع التكوينات المخصصة وخادم MCP والإضافات والأوامر، وتبسيط سير عمل التطوير بإدارة ملفات `.claude/handoffs/` وأوامر `/pickup [HANDOFF_FILE]`."},"useCases":{"en":["Resuming work from previous handoff sessions","Managing multiple project configurations with Claude Code Switch","Automating setup replication across different coding tools"],"zh":["恢复上一次交接会话的工作","使用Claude Code Switch管理多个项目配置","自动跨不同编码工具复制设置"],"ja":["前のハンドオフセッションからの作業の再開","Claude Code Switchを使用した複数プロジェクト構成の管理","さまざまなコーディングツール間のセットアップの自動複製"],"ko":["이전 핸드오버 세션에서 작업 재개","클라우드 코드 스위치를 사용한 여러 프로젝트 구성 관리","다양한 코딩 도구 간 설정 자동 복제"],"es":["Reanudar el trabajo desde sesiones de entrega anteriores","Gestionar varias configuraciones de proyecto con Claude Code Switch","Automatizar la replicación de la configuración en diferentes herramientas de codificación"],"fr":["Reprendre le travail à partir de sessions de passage en main précédentes","Gérer plusieurs configurations de projet avec Claude Code Switch","Automatiser la réplication de la configuration sur différents outils de codage"],"de":["Arbeit von vorherigen Übernahmesitzungen fortsetzen","Mehrere ProjektKonfigurationen mit Claude Code Switch verwalten","Konfigurationsreplikation über verschiedene Codierungstools automatisieren"],"pt":["Retomar o trabalho a partir de sessões de handoff anteriores","Gerenciar várias configurações de projeto com Claude Code Switch","Automatizar a replicação de configuração em diferentes ferramentas de codificação"],"ru":["Возобновление работы из предыдущих сессий handoff","Управление несколькими конфигурациями проекта с помощью Claude Code Switch","Автоматизация репликации настроек в разных инструментах кодирования"],"ar":["استئناف العمل من جلسات التخلي السابقة","إدارة عدة تكوينات لمشروع مع Claude Code Switch","تأتمة تكرار الإعدادات عبر أدوات الترميز المختلفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `.claude/handoffs/` directory","Limited to tools like Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex, and Claude Code Switch"],"zh":["需要访问`.claude/handoffs/`目录","仅限于Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex和Claude Code Switch等工具"],"ja":["`.claude/handoffs/`ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","Claude Code、OpenCode、Amp、Codex、Claude Code Switchなどのツールに限定"],"ko":["`.claude/handoffs/` 디렉토리에 액세스해야 함","클라우드 코드, 오픈 코드, 앰프, コデックス 및 클라우드 코드 스위치와 같은 도구로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio `.claude/handoffs/`","Limitado a herramientas como Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex y Claude Code Switch"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au répertoire `.claude/handoffs/`","Limité à des outils tels que Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex et Claude Code Switch"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis `.claude/handoffs/`","Begrenzt auf Tools wie Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex und Claude Code Switch"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao diretório `.claude/handoffs/`","Limitado a ferramentas como Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex e Claude Code Switch"],"ru":["Требует доступа к каталогу `.claude/handoffs/`","Ограничен инструментами seperti Claude Code, OpenCode, Amp, Codex и Claude Code Switch"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الدليل `.claude/handoffs/`","محدود الأدوات مثل Claude Code و OpenCode و Amp و Codex و Claude Code Switch"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('lgbarn/shipyard/shipyard-writing-skills', 'community', 'lgbarn', 'shipyard', 'lgbarn/shipyard', 'shipyard-writing-skills', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:23:05.249Z', NULL, '{"id":"lgbarn/shipyard/shipyard-writing-skills","name":"shipyard-writing-skills","description":{"zh":"写作技能是应用于流程文档的测试驱动开发，用于创建、编辑和验证技能","ja":"書き込みスキルは、プロセス文書に適用されるテスト駆動開発であり、スキルの作成、編集、検証に使用されます","ko":"작성 스킬은 프로세스 문서에 적용되는 테스트 주도 개발이며, 스킬 생성, 편집 및 검증에 사용됩니다","es":"La habilidad de escritura de astillero es un plugin de ciclo de vida de proyecto estructurado para Claude Code","fr":"La compétence d''écriture de chantier naval est un plugin de cycle de vie de projet structuré pour Claude Code","de":"Die Werft-Schreibfähigkeit ist ein strukturiertes Projekt-Lebenszyklus-Plugin für Claude Code","pt":"O shipyard-writing-skills é um plugin de ciclo de vida de projeto estruturado para Claude Code, que ajuda a criar habilidades de escrita de código de alta qualidade","ru":"Shipyard-writing-skills - это структурированный плагин жизненного цикла проекта для Claude Code, который помогает создавать навыки письма кода высокого качества","ar":"shipyard-writing-skills هو مكون إضافي لمحفظة المشاريع المُنظمة لبرنامج Claude Code، الذي يساعد على إنشاء مهارات كتابة الشفرة عالية الجودة","en":"Structured project lifecycle plugin for Claude Code — from idea to production with discipline, parallel agents, and quality gates."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"项目生命周期插件- Claude Code 写作技能","ja":"プロジェクトライフサイクルプラグイン- Claude Code 書き込みスキル","ko":"프로젝트 生命周期 플러그인 - Claude Code 작성 스킬","es":"Habilidad de escritura de astillero para Claude Code","fr":"Compétence d''écriture de chantier naval pour Claude Code","de":"Werft-Schreibfähigkeit für Claude Code","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Habilidades de Escrita de Código","ru":"Навыки письма кода для разработчиков","ar":"مهارات كتابة الشفرة للبرمجيين","en":"shipyard-writing-skills"},"description":{"zh":"写作技能是应用于流程文档的测试驱动开发，用于创建、编辑和验证技能","ja":"書き込みスキルは、プロセス文書に適用されるテスト駆動開発であり、スキルの作成、編集、検証に使用されます","ko":"작성 스킬은 프로세스 문서에 적용되는 테스트 주도 개발이며, 스킬 생성, 편집 및 검증에 사용됩니다","es":"La habilidad de escritura de astillero es un plugin de ciclo de vida de proyecto estructurado para Claude Code","fr":"La compétence d''écriture de chantier naval est un plugin de cycle de vie de projet structuré pour Claude Code","de":"Die Werft-Schreibfähigkeit ist ein strukturiertes Projekt-Lebenszyklus-Plugin für Claude Code","pt":"O shipyard-writing-skills é um plugin de ciclo de vida de projeto estruturado para Claude Code, que ajuda a criar habilidades de escrita de código de alta qu...","ru":"Shipyard-writing-skills - это структурированный плагин жизненного цикла проекта для Claude Code, который помогает создавать навыки письма кода высокого качества","ar":"shipyard-writing-skills هو مكون إضافي لمحفظة المشاريع المُنظمة لبرنامج Claude Code، الذي يساعد على إنشاء مهارات كتابة الشفرة عالية الجودة","en":"Structured project lifecycle plugin for Claude Code — from idea to production with discipline, parallel agents, and quality gates."},"definition":{"en":"Structured project lifecycle plugin for Claude Code — from idea to production with discipline, parallel agents, and quality gates."},"features":{"zh":["结构化项目生命周期","并行代理","质量门","测试驱动开发","流程文档","技能创建和编辑"],"ja":["構造化されたプロジェクトライフサイクル","並行エージェント","品質ゲート","テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書","スキルの作成と編集"],"ko":["구조화된 프로젝트 生命周期","병렬 에이전트","품질 게이트","테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서","스킬 생성 및 편집"],"es":["Ciclo de vida de proyecto estructurado","Desarrollo de habilidades con disciplina y calidad","Compatibilidad con Claude Code","Verificación y revisión de habilidades","Creación y edición de habilidades"],"fr":["Cycle de vie de projet structuré","Développement de compétences avec discipline et qualité","Compatibilité avec Claude Code","Vérification et révision de compétences","Création et édition de compétences"],"de":["Strukturiertes Projekt-Lebenszyklus-Plugin","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten mit Disziplin und Qualität","Kompatibilität mit Claude Code","Überprüfung und Überarbeitung von Fähigkeiten","Erstellung und Bearbeitung von Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Ciclo de vida de projeto estruturado","Desenvolvimento de habilidades de escrita de código","Test-Driven Development aplicado à documentação de processos","Disciplina e qualidade garantidas","Paralelismo e portas de qualidade"],"ru":["Структурированный жизненный цикл проекта","Разработка навыков письма кода","Test-Driven Development, примененный к документации процессов","Дисциплина и качество гарантированы","Параллелизм и ворота качества"],"ar":["دورة حياة مشروع منظم","تطوير مهارات كتابة الشفرة","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار المُطبق على توثيق العمليات","الضبط و الجودة مضمونة","التوازي و أبواب الجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["项目生命周期","测试驱动开发","流程文档","技能创建","Claude Code","写作技能","并行代理","质量门"],"ja":["プロジェクトライフサイクル","テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書","スキルの作成","Claude Code","書き込みスキル","並行エージェント","品質ゲート"],"ko":["프로젝트 生命周期","테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서","스킬 생성","클라우드 코드","작성 스킬","병렬 에이전트","품질 게이트"],"es":["habilidad de escritura de astillero","desarrollo de habilidades","ciclo de vida de proyecto","Claude Code","pruebas de habilidades","documentación de procesos","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["compétence d''écriture de chantier naval","développement de compétences","cycle de vie de projet","Claude Code","tests de compétences","documentation de processus","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["Werft-Schreibfähigkeit","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Projekt-Lebenszyklus","Claude Code","Fähigkeitstests","Prozessdokumentation","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieur"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades de escrita de código","ciclo de vida de projeto","Test-Driven Development","documentação de processos","disciplina e qualidade","paralelismo e portas de qualidade"],"ru":["разработка навыков письма кода","жизненный цикл проекта","Test-Driven Development","документация процессов","дисциплина и качество","параллелизм и ворота качества"],"ar":["تطوير مهارات كتابة الشفرة","دورة حياة مشروع","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","توثيق العمليات","الضبط و الجودة","التوازي و أبواب الجودة"]}},"owner":"lgbarn","repo":"shipyard","repoPath":"lgbarn/shipyard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"shipyard-writing-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment","bodyPreview":"<!-- TOKEN BUDGET: 530 lines / ~1590 tokens -->\n\n# Writing Skills\n\n<activation>\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n\n- Creating a new skill (SKILL.md file)\n- Editing or improving an existing skill\n- Verifying a skill works before deployment\n- Reviewing skill quality or effectiveness\n\n## Natural Language Triggers\n- \"create a skill\", \"write a skill\", \"new skill\", \"improve this skill\"\n\n</activation>\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal","body":"<!-- TOKEN BUDGET: 530 lines / ~1590 tokens -->\n\n# Writing Skills\n\n<activation>\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n\n- Creating a new skill (SKILL.md file)\n- Editing or improving an existing skill\n- Verifying a skill works before deployment\n- Reviewing skill quality or effectiveness\n\n## Natural Language Triggers\n- \"create a skill\", \"write a skill\", \"new skill\", \"improve this skill\"\n\n</activation>\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.codex/skills` for Codex)**\n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skill, you don''t know if the skill teaches the right thing.\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand shipyard:shipyard-tdd before using this skill. That skill defines the fundamental RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle. This skill adapts TDD to documentation.\n\n**Official guidance:** For Anthropic''s official skill authoring best practices, see anthropic-best-practices.md. This document provides additional patterns and guidelines that complement the TDD-focused approach in this skill.\n\n## What is a Skill?\n\nA **skill** is a reference guide for proven techniques, patterns, or tools. Skills help future Claude instances find and apply effective approaches.\n\n**Skills are:** Reusable techniques, patterns, tools, reference guides\n\n**Skills are NOT:** Narratives about how you solved a problem once\n\n<instructions>\n\n## TDD Mapping for Skills\n\n| TDD Concept | Skill Creation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| **Test case** | Pressure scenario with subagent |\n| **Production code** | Skill document (SKILL.md) |\n| **Test fails (RED)** | Agent violates rule without skill (baseline) |\n| **Test passes (GREEN)** | Agent complies with skill present |\n| **Refactor** | Close loopholes while maintaining compliance |\n| **Write test first** | Run baseline scenario BEFORE writing skill |\n| **Watch it fail** | Document exact rationalizations agent uses |\n| **Minimal code** | Write skill addressing those specific violations |\n| **Watch it pass** | Verify agent now complies |\n| **Refactor cycle** | Find new rationalizations -> plug -> re-verify |\n\nThe entire skill creation process follows RED-GREEN-REFACTOR.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\n**Create when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious to you\n- You''d reference this again across projects\n- Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- Others would benefit\n\n**Don''t create for:**\n- One-off solutions\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project-specific conventions (put in CLAUDE.md)\n- Mechanical constraints (if it''s enforceable with regex/validation, automate it -- save documentation for judgment calls)\n\n## Skill Types\n\n### Technique\nConcrete method with steps to follow (condition-based-waiting, root-cause-tracing)\n\n### Pattern\nWay of thinking about problems (flatten-with-flags, test-invariants)\n\n### Reference\nAPI docs, syntax guides, tool documentation (office docs)\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Main reference (required)\n    supporting-file.*     # Only if needed\n```\n\n**Flat namespace** - all skills in one searchable namespace\n\n**Separate files for:**\n1. **Heavy reference** (100+ lines) - API docs, comprehensive syntax\n2. **Reusable tools** - Scripts, utilities, templates\n\n**Keep inline:**\n- Principles and concepts\n- Code patterns (< 50 lines)\n- Everything else\n\n## SKILL.md Structure\n\n**Frontmatter (YAML):**\n- Only two fields supported: `name` and `description`\n- Max 1024 characters total\n- `name`: Use letters, numbers, and hyphens only (no parentheses, special chars)\n- `description`: Third-person, describes ONLY when to use (NOT what it does)\n  - Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n  - Include specific symptoms, situations, and contexts\n  - **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow** (see CSO section for why)\n  - Keep under 500 characters if possible\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: Skill-Name-With-Hyphens\ndescription: Use when [specific triggering conditions and symptoms]\n---\n\n# Skill Name\n\n## Overview\nWhat is this? Core principle in 1-2 sentences.\n\n## When to Use\n[Small inline flowchart IF decision non-obvious]\n\nBullet list with SYMPTOMS and use cases\nWhen NOT to use\n\n## Core Pattern (for techniques/patterns)\nBefore/after code comparison\n\n## Quick Reference\nTable or bullets for scanning common operations\n\n## Implementation\nInline code for simple patterns\nLink to file for heavy reference or reusable tools\n\n## Common Mistakes\nWhat goes wrong + fixes\n\n## Real-World Impact (optional)\nConcrete results\n```\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n**Critical for discovery:** Future Claude needs to FIND your skill\n\n### 1. Rich Description Field\n\n**Purpose:** Claude reads description to decide which skills to load for a given task. Make it answer: \"Should I read this skill right now?\"\n\n**Format:** Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n\n**CRITICAL: Description = When to Use, NOT What the Skill Does**\n\nThe description should ONLY describe triggering conditions. Do NOT summarize the skill''s process or workflow in the description.\n\n**Why this matters:** Testing revealed that when a description summarizes the skill''s workflow, Claude may follow the description instead of reading the full skill content. A description saying \"code review between tasks\" caused Claude to do ONE review, even though the skill''s flowchart clearly showed TWO reviews (spec compliance then code quality).\n\nWhen the description was changed to just \"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks\" (no workflow summary), Claude correctly read the flowchart and followed the two-stage review process.\n\n**The trap:** Descriptions that summarize workflow create a shortcut Claude will take. The skill body becomes documentation Claude skips.\n\n### CSO Continued\n\n**Content:**\n- Use concrete triggers, symptoms, situations -- describe the *problem* not language-specific symptoms\n- Technology-agnostic unless the skill itself is technology-specific\n- Third person (injected into system prompt)\n- **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow**\n\n### 2. Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- Error messages: \"Hook timed out\", \"ENOTEMPTY\", \"race condition\"\n- Symptoms: \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"zombie\", \"pollution\"\n- Synonyms: \"timeout/hang/freeze\", \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\"\n- Tools: Actual commands, library names, file types\n\n### 3. Descriptive Naming\n\n**Use active voice, verb-first:**\n- `creating-skills` not `skill-creation`\n- `condition-based-waiting` not `async-test-helpers`\n\n### 4. Token Efficiency (Critical)\n\n**Targets:** getting-started <150 words, frequently-loaded <200 words, others <500 words.\n\n**Key techniques:** Move details to `--help`, use cross-references instead of repeating content, compress examples to minimal form, eliminate redundancy. See EXAMPLES.md for detailed token efficiency patterns.\n\n**Naming:** Use active verb-first names (`condition-based-waiting` not `async-test-helpers`). Gerunds work well for processes (`creating-skills`, `testing-skills`).\n\n### 5. Cross-Referencing Other Skills\n\n**When writing documentation that references other skills:**\n\nUse skill name only, with explicit requirement markers:\n- Good: `**REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use shipyard:shipyard-tdd`\n- Good: `**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand shipyard:shipyard-debugging`\n- Bad: `See skills/testing/test-driven-development` (unclear if required)\n- Bad: `@skills/testing/test-driven-development/SKILL.md` (force-loads, burns context)\n\n**Why no @ links:** `@` syntax force-loads files immediately, consuming context tokens you may not need yet.\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_flowchart {\n    \"Need to show information?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Use markdown\" [shape=box];\n    \"Small inline flowchart\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Need to show information?\" -> \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Small inline flowchart\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Use markdown\" [label=\"no\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use flowcharts ONLY for:**\n- Non-obvious decision points\n- Process loops where you might stop too early\n- \"When to use A vs B\" decisions\n\n**Never use flowcharts for:**\n- Reference material -- Tables, lists\n- Code examples -- Markdown blocks\n- Linear instructions -- Numbered lists\n- Labels without semantic meaning (step1, helper2)\n\n## Code Examples\n\n**One excellent example beats many mediocre ones**\n\nChoose most relevant language:\n- Testing techniques -- TypeScript/JavaScript\n- System debugging -- Shell/Python\n- Data processing -- Python\n\n**Good example:**\n- Complete and runnable\n- Well-commented explaining WHY\n- From real scenario\n- Shows pattern clearly\n- Ready to adapt (not generic template)\n\n**Don''t:**\n- Implement in 5+ languages\n- Create fill-in-the-blank templates\n- Write contrived examples\n\nYou''re good at porting - one great example is enough.\n\n## File Organization\n\n### Self-Contained Skill\n```\ndefense-in-depth/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\nWhen: All content fits, no heavy reference needed\n\n### Skill with Reusable Tool\n```\ncondition-based-waiting/\n  SKILL.md    # Overview + patterns\n  example.ts  # Working helpers to adapt\n```\nWhen: Tool is reusable code, not just narrative\n\n### Skill with Heavy Reference\n```\npptx/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  pptxgenjs.md   # 600 lines API reference\n  ooxml.md       # 500 lines XML structure\n  scripts/       # Executable tools\n```\nWhen: Reference material too large for inline\n\n</instructions>\n\n<examples>\n\n## CSO Description Examples\n\n<example type=\"good\" title=\"Triggering conditions only, no workflow summary\">\n```yaml\ndescription: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session\n```\nJust triggering conditions -- Claude reads the full skill to learn the workflow.\n</example>\n\n<example type=\"bad\" title=\"Workflow summary in description\">\n```yaml\ndescription: Use when executing plans - dispatches subagent per task with code review between tasks\n```\nSummarizes workflow -- Claude follows description instead of reading skill body, misses two-stage review.\n</example>\n\n## Skill Content Examples\n\n<example type=\"good\" title=\"Well-structured skill with XML tags and clear activation\">\n```markdown\n---\nname: condition-based-waiting\ndescription: Use when tests need to wait for async operations, processes, or state changes instead of using arbitrary sleep/timeouts\n---\n\n<activation>\n## When This Skill Activates\n- Tests using sleep(), setTimeout(), or fixed delays\n- Flaky tests that pass/fail based on timing\n- Waiting for processes, servers, or async state\n</activation>\n\n<instructions>\n## Core Pattern\nPoll for condition instead of sleeping...\n</instructions>\n\n<rules>\n## Never\n- Use fixed sleep() in tests\n- Assume operation completes in N seconds\n</rules>\n```\nClear activation, XML structure, rules separated.\n</example>\n\n<example type=\"bad\" title=\"Missing structure, narrative style\">\n```markdown\n# Waiting in Tests\n\nLast week I was working on a project where tests were flaky. I found that\nusing sleep(5) was unreliable. After some experimentation, I discovered\nthat polling for conditions works better...\n```\nNarrative style, no activation triggers, no XML structure, not reusable.\n</example>\n\n</examples>\n\n<rules>\n\n## The Iron Law (Same as TDD)\n\n```\nNO SKILL WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nThis applies to NEW skills AND EDITS to existing skills.\n\nWrite skill before testing? Delete it. Start over.\nEdit skill without testing? Same violation.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Not for \"simple additions\"\n- Not for \"just adding a section\"\n- Not for \"documentation updates\"\n- Don''t keep untested changes as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" while running tests\n- Delete means delete\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** The shipyard:shipyard-tdd skill explains why this matters. Same principles apply to documentation.\n\n## Testing All Skill Types\n\nDifferent skill types need different test approaches:\n\n### Discipline-Enforcing Skills\nTest with academic questions, pressure scenarios (time + sunk cost + exhaustion combined), and rationalization tracking. **Pass:** Agent follows rule under maximum pressure.\n\n### Technique Skills\nTest with application scenarios, edge-case variations, and gap detection. **Pass:** Agent applies technique correctly to new scenarios.\n\n### Pattern Skills\nTest with recognition scenarios, application tasks, and counter-examples. **Pass:** Agent identifies when/how to apply pattern and when NOT to.\n\n### Reference Skills\nTest with retrieval tasks, application scenarios, and coverage gaps. **Pass:** Agent finds and correctly applies reference information.\n\n## Common Rationalizations for Skipping Testing\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Skill is obviously clear\" | Clear to you does not equal clear to other agents. Test it. |\n| \"Testing is overkill\" | Untested skills have issues. Always. 15 min saves hours. |\n| \"Academic review is enough\" | Reading does not equal using. Test application scenarios. |\n| \"No time to test\" | Deploying untested wastes more time fixing later. |\n\n**All of these mean: Test before deploying. No exceptions.**\n\n## Bulletproofing Skills Against Rationalization\n\nDiscipline skills must resist rationalization. Key strategies:\n\n1. **Close every loophole explicitly** -- don''t just state the rule, forbid specific workarounds with \"No exceptions\" lists\n2. **Address \"Spirit vs Letter\"** -- add early: \"Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules\"\n3. **Build rationalization tables** from baseline testing -- every excuse agents make gets a counter\n4. **Create red flags lists** for agent self-check (e.g., \"Code before test\", \"This is different because...\")\n5. **Update CSO descriptions** with violation symptoms as triggers\n\nSee EXAMPLES.md for detailed good/bad examples of each strategy.\n\n</rules>\n\n## RED-GREEN-REFACTOR for Skills\n\nFollow the TDD cycle:\n\n### RED: Write Failing Test (Baseline)\n\nRun pressure scenario with subagent WITHOUT the skill. Document exact behavior:\n- What choices did they make?\n- What rationalizations did they use (verbatim)?\n- Which pressures triggered violations?\n\nThis is \"watch the test fail\" - you must see what agents naturally do before writing the skill.\n\n### GREEN: Write Minimal Skill\n\nWrite skill that addresses those specific rationalizations. Don''t add extra content for hypothetical cases.\n\nRun same scenarios WITH skill. Agent should now comply.\n\n### REFACTOR: Close Loopholes\n\nAgent found new rationalization? Add explicit counter. Re-test until bulletproof.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- **Narrative Example** -- session-specific stories are not reusable\n- **Multi-Language Dilution** -- one excellent example beats five mediocre translations\n- **Code in Flowcharts** -- can''t copy-paste, hard to read (use markdown blocks)\n- **Generic Labels** -- helper1/step3 have no semantic meaning; use descriptive names\n\nSee EXAMPLES.md for detailed anti-pattern examples.\n\n## STOP: Before Moving to Next Skill\n\n**After writing ANY skill, you MUST STOP and complete the deployment process.**\n\n**Do NOT:**\n- Create multiple skills in batch without testing each\n- Move to next skill before current one is verified\n- Skip testing because \"batching is more efficient\"\n\n**The deployment checklist below is MANDATORY for EACH skill.**\n\nDeploying untested skills = deploying untested code. It''s a violation of quality standards.\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist (TDD Adapted)\n\n**Use TaskCreate to create tasks for EACH item below.**\n\n**RED:** Create pressure scenarios (3+ for discipline skills) -- run WITHOUT skill -- document baseline rationalizations\n\n**GREEN:**\n- [ ] Name: letters/numbers/hyphens only; YAML frontmatter (name + description, max 1024 chars)\n- [ ] Description: \"Use when...\" + triggers/symptoms, third person, no workflow summary\n- [ ] Keywords for search, clear overview, address baseline failures from RED\n- [ ] Code inline or linked; one excellent example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Run WITH skill -- verify compliance\n\n**REFACTOR:** Find new rationalizations -- add counters -- build rationalization table + red flags -- re-test until bulletproof\n\n**Quality:** Flowcharts only for non-obvious decisions; quick reference table; common mistakes; no narrative; supporting files only for tools/heavy reference\n\n**Deploy:** Commit and push; consider contributing via PR if broadly useful\n\n## Discovery Workflow\n\nHow future Claude finds your skill:\n\n1. **Encounters problem** (\"tests are flaky\")\n2. **Finds SKILL** (description matches)\n3. **Scans overview** (is this relevant?)\n4. **Reads patterns** (quick reference table)\n5. **Loads example** (only when implementing)\n\n**Optimize for this flow** - put searchable terms early and often.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:23:05.249Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing structured project lifecycle management with discipline and quality gates.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化项目生命周期管理、严格遵守纪律和质量门槛的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントが構造化されたプロジェクトライフサイクル管理と規律、品質ゲートを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"구조화된 프로젝트 생명주기 관리와 규율 및 품질 게이트가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan una gestión del ciclo de vida del proyecto estructurada con disciplina y puertas de calidad.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement qui ont besoin d''une gestion du cycle de vie du projet structurée avec discipline et portes de qualité.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel benötigende Agenten, die eine strukturierte Projekt-Lebenszyklus-Verwaltung mit Disziplin und Qualitäts-Toren benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de ciclo de vida de projeto estruturado com disciplina e portas de qualidade.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуется структурированное управление жизненным циклом проекта с соблюдением дисциплины и воротами качества.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيين الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة دورة حياة المشروع الهيكلية مع الانضباط وأبواب الجودة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage skills from idea to production using Test-Driven Development principles, parallel agents, and quality gates, leveraging SKILL.md files and natural language triggers.","zh":"赋予代理管理从创意到生产的技能，使用测试驱动开发原则、并行代理和质量门槛，利用SKILL.md文件和自然语言触发器","ja":"アイデアから生産までのスキルをテスト駆動開発の原則、並列エージェント、品質ゲートを使用して管理するエージェントをEmpowerする、SKILL.mdファイルと自然言語トリガーを活用する","ko":"아이디어에서 생산까지의 스킬을 테스트 주도 개발 원칙, 병렬 에이전트 및 품질 게이트를 사용하여 관리하는 에이전트를 강화하는 것, SKILL.md 파일 및 자연어 트리거를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar habilidades desde la idea hasta la producción utilizando principios de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas, agentes paralelos y puertas de calidad, aprovechando archivos SKILL.md y desencadenadores de lenguaje natural.","fr":"Habilite les agents à gérer les compétences de l''idée à la production en utilisant les principes de développement piloté par les tests, les agents parallèles et les portes de qualité, en exploitant les fichiers SKILL.md et les déclencheurs de langage naturel.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Fähigkeiten von der Idee bis zur Produktion zu verwalten, indem sie Testgetriebene-Entwicklungsprinzipien, parallele Agenten und Qualitäts-Tore nutzen und SKILL.md-Dateien sowie natürliche Sprachauslöser ausschöpfen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar habilidades desde a ideia até a produção usando princípios de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes, agentes paralelos e portas de qualidade, aproveitando arquivos SKILL.md e gatilhos de linguagem natural.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять навыками от идеи до производства с использованием принципов разработки, управляемой тестированием, параллельных агентов и ворот качества, используя файлы SKILL.md и триггеры естественного языка.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إدارة المهارات من الفكرة إلى الإنتاج باستخدام مبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار، والوكلاء الموازيين وأبواب الجودة، والاستفادة من ملفات SKILL.md ومحفزات اللغة الطبيعية."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new skills with structured documentation","Improving existing skills through iterative testing and refinement","Verifying skill functionality before deployment to production","Reviewing skill quality and effectiveness through automated gates"],"zh":["创建具有结构化文档的新技能","通过迭代测试和完善改进现有技能","在部署到生产之前验证技能功能","通过自动化门槛审查技能质量和有效性"],"ja":["構造化されたドキュメントを持つ新しいスキルを作成する","反復的なテストと改良を通じて既存のスキルを改善する","生産へのデプロイ前にスキルの機能を検証する","自動化されたゲートを通じてスキルの品質と有効性をレビューする"],"ko":["구조화된 문서를 갖춘 새로운 스킬 생성","반복적인 테스트 및 개선 통해 기존 스킬 개선","생산 환경에 배포하기 전에 스킬 기능을 검증","자동화된 게이트를 통해 스킬 품질 및 효과성 검토"],"es":["Crear nuevas habilidades con documentación estructurada","Mejorar habilidades existentes a través de pruebas y refinamiento iterativos","Verificar la funcionalidad de la habilidad antes de la implementación en producción","Revisar la calidad y eficacia de la habilidad a través de puertas automatizadas"],"fr":["Créer de nouvelles compétences avec une documentation structurée","Améliorer les compétences existantes à travers des tests et un raffinement itératifs","Vérifier la fonctionnalité de la compétence avant le déploiement en production","Réviser la qualité et l''efficacité de la compétence à travers des portes automatisées"],"de":["Erstellen neuer Fähigkeiten mit strukturierter Dokumentation","Verbessern bestehender Fähigkeiten durch iterative Tests und Verfeinerung","Überprüfen der Funktionalität der Fähigkeit vor der Bereitstellung in der Produktion","Überprüfen der Qualität und Effektivität der Fähigkeit durch automatisierte Tore"],"pt":["Criar novas habilidades com documentação estruturada","Melhorar habilidades existentes por meio de testes e refinamento iterativos","Verificar a funcionalidade da habilidade antes do deploy para produção","Revisar a qualidade e eficácia da habilidade por meio de portas automatizadas"],"ru":["Создание новых навыков со структурной документацией","Улучшение существующих навыков посредством итеративного тестирования и совершенствования","Проверка функциональности навыка до развертывания в производство","Просмотр качества и эффективности навыка посредством автоматических ворот"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات جديدة مع توثيق هيكلي","تحسين المهارات الحالية من خلال اختبارات وتحسين متكرر","التحقق من وظيفة المهارة قبل النشر إلى الإنتاج","مراجعة جودة وفعالية المهارة من خلال أبواب تلقائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code integration","Limited to skills with SKILL.md file structure","Token budget of approximately 1590 tokens"],"zh":["需要Claude Code集成","仅限具有SKILL.md文件结构的技能","令牌预算约为1590个令牌"],"ja":["Claude Codeの統合が必要","SKILL.mdファイル構造を持つスキルに限定","トークン予算は約1590トークン"],"ko":["Claude Code 통합이 필요","SKILL.md 파일 구조를 갖춘 스킬에 제한","토큰 예산은 약 1590 토큰"],"es":["Requiere integración con Claude Code","Limitado a habilidades con estructura de archivo SKILL.md","Presupuesto de tokens de aproximadamente 1590 tokens"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Claude Code","Limité aux compétences avec une structure de fichier SKILL.md","Budget de tokens d''environ 1590 tokens"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit Claude Code","Begrenzt auf Fähigkeiten mit SKILL.md-Dateistruktur","Token-Budget von ungefähr 1590 Token"],"pt":["Requer integração com Claude Code","Limitado a habilidades com estrutura de arquivo SKILL.md","Orçamento de tokens de aproximadamente 1590 tokens"],"ru":["Требуется интеграция с Claude Code","Ограничен навыками со структурой файла SKILL.md","Бюджет токенов примерно 1590 токенов"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل مع Claude Code","محدود بالمهارات ذات هيكل ملف SKILL.md","ميزانية رموز تقريبية 1590 رمز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('verekia/r3f-gamedev/reactive-polling', 'community', 'verekia', 'r3f-gamedev', 'verekia/r3f-gamedev', 'reactive-polling', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:22:47.622Z', NULL, '{"id":"verekia/r3f-gamedev/reactive-polling","name":"reactive-polling","description":{"zh":"Reactive Polling是一种实时检测值的变化并触发React重新渲染的技术，通过使用useReactive hook和useFrame实现","ja":"Reactive Pollingはリアクティブな値の変更を検知してReactを再レンダリングする技術で、useReactive hookとuseFrameを使用して実現します","ko":"Reactive Polling은 값의 변경을 실시간으로 감지하고 React를 다시 렌더링 하는 기술로, useReactive hook과 useFrame을 사용하여 구현합니다","es":"Reactive polling es una técnica para detectar cambios en valores y disparar re-renders en React","fr":"Le reactive polling est une technique pour détecter les changements de valeurs et déclencher des re-rendus dans React","de":"Reaktives Polling ist eine Technik, um Änderungen an Werten zu erkennen und Re-Renderings in React auszulösen","en":"⚛️ React Three Fiber Game Dev Recipes"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Reactive Polling - 实时轮询技术","ja":"Reactive Polling - リアクティブなポーリング","ko":"Reactive Polling - 반응형 폴링","es":"Reactive Polling para React","fr":"Reactive Polling pour React","de":"Reaktives Polling für React","en":"reactive-polling"},"description":{"zh":"Reactive Polling是一种实时检测值的变化并触发React重新渲染的技术，通过使用useReactive hook和useFrame实现","ja":"Reactive Pollingはリアクティブな値の変更を検知してReactを再レンダリングする技術で、useReactive hookとuseFrameを使用して実現します","ko":"Reactive Polling은 값의 변경을 실시간으로 감지하고 React를 다시 렌더링 하는 기술로, useReactive hook과 useFrame을 사용하여 구현합니다","es":"Reactive polling es una técnica para detectar cambios en valores y disparar re-renders en React","fr":"Le reactive polling est une technique pour détecter les changements de valeurs et déclencher des re-rendus dans React","de":"Reaktives Polling ist eine Technik, um Änderungen an Werten zu erkennen und Re-Renderings in React auszulösen","en":"⚛️ React Three Fiber Game Dev Recipes"},"definition":{"en":"⚛️ React Three Fiber Game Dev Recipes"},"features":{"zh":["实时检测值的变化","触发React重新渲染","使用useReactive hook和useFrame实现","可配置的FPS","优化性能","简单易用"],"ja":["リアクティブな値の変更を検知","Reactを再レンダリング","useReactive hookとuseFrameを使用","FPSの設定","パフォーマンスの最適化","簡単に使用"],"ko":["값의 변경을 실시간으로 감지","React를 다시 렌더링","useReactive hook과 useFrame을 사용","FPS 설정","성능 최적화","简单한 사용법"],"es":["Detección de cambios en valores","Disparo de re-renders en React","Uso de un hook personalizado","Configuración de la velocidad de polleo","Compatibilidad con React Three Fiber"],"fr":["Détection des changements de valeurs","Déclenchement de re-rendus dans React","Utilisation d''un hook personnalisé","Configuration de la vitesse de pollage","Compatibilité avec React Three Fiber"],"de":["Erkennung von Änderungen an Werten","Auslösen von Re-Renderings in React","Verwendung eines benutzerdefinierten Hooks","Konfiguration der Polling-Geschwindigkeit","Kompatibilität mit React Three Fiber"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Reactive Polling","实时轮询","React","useReactive","useFrame","FPS","性能优化"],"ja":["Reactive Polling","リアクティブなポーリング","React","useReactive","useFrame","FPS","パフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["Reactive Polling","반응형 폴링","React","useReactive","useFrame","FPS","성능 최적화"],"es":["reactive polling","react","detectar cambios","re-render","hook personalizado","react three fiber","desarrollo de juegos","programación reactiva"],"fr":["reactive polling","react","détecter les changements","re-render","hook personnalisé","react three fiber","développement de jeux","programmation réactive"],"de":["reaktives Polling","react","Änderungen erkennen","Re-Rendering","benutzerdefinierter Hook","react three fiber","Spielentwicklung","reaktive Programmierung"]}},"owner":"verekia","repo":"r3f-gamedev","repoPath":"verekia/r3f-gamedev","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"reactive-polling","description":"Poll for changes to any value and trigger React re-renders when it changes.","bodyPreview":"# Reactive Polling\n\nPoll for changes to any value and trigger React re-renders when it changes.\n\n## Technique\n\nCreate a `useReactive` hook that uses `useFrame` to periodically check a selector function. When the value changes, update React state to trigger a re-render. Throttle with a configurable FPS.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n- Selector function returns the value to watch\n- Compare with previous value to detect changes\n- Only update state when value actually changes\n- Throttle polling with `useFrame`''","body":"# Reactive Polling\n\nPoll for changes to any value and trigger React re-renders when it changes.\n\n## Technique\n\nCreate a `useReactive` hook that uses `useFrame` to periodically check a selector function. When the value changes, update React state to trigger a re-render. Throttle with a configurable FPS.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n- Selector function returns the value to watch\n- Compare with previous value to detect changes\n- Only update state when value actually changes\n- Throttle polling with `useFrame`''s `fps` option\n- Use sparingly for values that don''t change frequently\n\n## Usage\n\n```tsx\nconst useReactive = <T,>(selector: () => T, fps = 30): T => {\n  const [reactiveValue, setReactiveValue] = useState<T>(selector())\n  const previousValueRef = useRef(reactiveValue)\n\n  useFrame(\n    () => {\n      const newValue = selector()\n      if (previousValueRef.current !== newValue) {\n        previousValueRef.current = newValue\n        setReactiveValue(newValue)\n      }\n    },\n    { fps }\n  )\n\n  return reactiveValue\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst isAboveZero = useReactive(() => position.y > 0)\n```\n\n---\n\nThis skill is part of [verekia](https://x.com/verekia)''s [**r3f-gamedev**](https://github.com/verekia/r3f-gamedev).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:22:47.622Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents utilizing React and requiring dynamic, real-time updates with reactive-polling capabilities.","zh":"适合使用 React 的前端代理，需要动态、实时更新和响应式轮询功能。","ja":"React を使用し、動的でリアルタイムの更新と反応的なポーリング機能を必要とするフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"React를 사용하고 동적이고 실시간 업데이트와 반응형 폴링 기능을 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes front-end que utilizan React y requieren actualizaciones dinámicas y en tiempo real con capacidades de encuesta reactiva.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents frontend utilisant React et nécessitant des mises à jour dynamiques et en temps réel avec des capacités de polling réactif.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agents, die React verwenden und dynamische, Echtzeit-Updates mit reaktivem Polling benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend que utilizam React e requerem atualizações dinâmicas e em tempo real com capacidades de reactive-polling.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, использующих React и требующих динамических обновлений в реальном времени с возможностями reactive-polling.","ar":"مثالي لعمال الواجهة الأمامية الذين يستخدمون React ويتطلبون تحديثات ديناميكية ووقت حقيقي مع إمكانيات reactive-polling."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to trigger React re-renders when values change by periodically checking a selector function using useFrame, while throttling with a configurable FPS to optimize performance and efficiency with React Three Fiber.","zh":"通过使用 useFrame 周期性地检查选择函数，并使用可配置的 FPS 进行限制以优化性能和效率，赋予代理触发 React 重新渲染的能力，当值发生变化时。","ja":"useFrame を使用して選択関数を周期的にチェックし、可変の FPS で制限してパフォーマンスと効率を最適化することで、エージェントが React の再描画をトリガーする能力を付与し、値が変更されたときに再描画を実行します。","ko":"useFrame를 사용하여 선택 함수를 주기적으로 확인하고, 구성 가능한 FPS로 제한하여 성능과 효율을 최적화함으로써, 에이전트가 값이 변경될 때 React의 재 렌더링을 트리거하는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para desencadenar nuevas renderizaciones de React cuando los valores cambian, comprobando periódicamente una función selector con useFrame, mientras que limita con un FPS configurable para optimizar el rendimiento y la eficiencia con React Three Fiber.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déclencher des nouvelles renderisations de React lorsque les valeurs changent, en vérifiant périodiquement une fonction sélecteur avec useFrame, tout en limitant avec un FPS configurable pour optimiser les performances et l''efficacité avec React Three Fiber.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, React-Neuernderungen auszulösen, wenn Werte geändert werden, indem sie eine Selektor-Funktion mit useFrame periodisch überprüfen, während sie mit einem konfigurierbaren FPS begrenzen, um Leistung und Effizienz mit React Three Fiber zu optimieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a acionar re-renders do React quando os valores mudam, verificando periodicamente uma função seletora usando useFrame, enquanto regula com um FPS configurável para otimizar o desempenho e a eficiência com React Three Fiber.","ru":"Позволяет агентам запускать повторную отрисовку React при изменении значений, периодически проверяя функцию селектора с помощью useFrame, а также регулирует частоту кадров с помощью настраиваемого FPS для оптимизации производительности и эффективности с React Three Fiber.","ar":"يمنح العمال القدرة على تشغيل إعادة عرض React عند تغيير القيم، من خلال التحقق الدوري لوظيفة محددة باستخدام useFrame، بينما يتحكم في معدل الإطار مع FPS قابل للتحديد لتحسين الأداء والكفاءة مع React Three Fiber."},"useCases":{"en":["Polling for changes in 3D game environments to update React state","Triggering re-renders in real-time data visualization applications","Optimizing game development workflows with reactive-polling and useFrame"],"zh":["轮询 3D 游戏环境中的更改以更新 React 状态","在实时数据可视化应用中触发重新渲染","使用响应式轮询和 useFrame 优化游戏开发工作流"],"ja":["3D ゲーム環境の変更をポーリングして React 状態を更新する","リアルタイム データ ビジュアライゼーション アプリケーションで再描画をトリガーする","useFrame と反応的なポーリングを使用してゲーム開発ワークフローを最適化する"],"ko":["3D 게임 환경의 변경 사항을 폴링하여 React 상태를 업데이트함","실시간 데이터 시각화 애플리케이션에서 재 렌더링을 트리거함","useFrame와 반응형 폴링을 사용하여 게임 개발 워크플로를 최적화함"],"es":["Encuesta de cambios en entornos de juegos 3D para actualizar el estado de React","Desencadenar nuevas renderizaciones en aplicaciones de visualización de datos en tiempo real","Optimizar flujos de trabajo de desarrollo de juegos con encuesta reactiva y useFrame"],"fr":["Polling des changements dans les environnements de jeux 3D pour mettre à jour l''état de React","Déclencher des nouvelles renderisations dans les applications de visualisation de données en temps réel","Optimiser les flux de travail de développement de jeux avec un polling réactif et useFrame"],"de":["Überwachung von Änderungen in 3D-Spielumgebungen, um den React-Zustand zu aktualisieren","Auslösen von Neuernderungen in Echtzeit-Datavisualisierungsanwendungen","Optimieren von Spielentwicklungsworkflows mit reaktivem Polling und useFrame"],"pt":["Polling para alterações em ambientes de jogos 3D para atualizar o estado do React","Acionar re-renders em aplicações de visualização de dados em tempo real","Otimizar fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento de jogos com reactive-polling e useFrame"],"ru":["Опрос изменений в 3D-игровых средах для обновления состояния React","Запуск повторной отрисовки в приложениях визуализации данных в реальном времени","Оптимизация рабочих процессов разработки игр с помощью reactive-polling и useFrame"],"ar":["استجواب التغييرات في بيئات الألعاب ثلاثية الأبعاد لتحديث حالة React","تشغيل إعادة العرض في تطبيقات تصور البيانات في الوقت الفعلي","تحسين سير عمل تطوير الألعاب مع reactive-polling و useFrame"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React and React Three Fiber integration","Dependent on useFrame for periodic checking","Configurable FPS throttle may impact performance"],"zh":["需要 React 和 React Three Fiber 集成","依赖 useFrame 进行周期性检查","可配置的 FPS 节流可能会影响性能"],"ja":["React と React Three Fiber の統合が必要","useFrame によって周期的なチェックに依存","可変の FPS 制限はパフォーマンスに影響を与える可能性がある"],"ko":["React와 React Three Fiber 통합이 필요함","useFrame에 의한 주기적인 확인에 의존함","구성 가능한 FPS 제한은 성능에 영향을 줄 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere integración de React y React Three Fiber","Dependiente de useFrame para la comprobación periódica","La limitación de FPS configurable puede afectar el rendimiento"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration de React et de React Three Fiber","Dépendante de useFrame pour la vérification périodique","La limitation de FPS configurable peut avoir un impact sur les performances"],"de":["Erfordert Integration von React und React Three Fiber","Abhängig von useFrame für periodische Überprüfung","Die konfigurierbare FPS-Begrenzung kann sich auf die Leistung auswirken"],"pt":["Exige integração do React e do React Three Fiber","Depende do useFrame para verificação periódica","Limitador de FPS configurável pode impactar o desempenho"],"ru":["Требует интеграции React и React Three Fiber","Зависит от useFrame для периодической проверки","Настройка ограничения FPS может повлиять на производительность"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل React و React Three Fiber","يعتمد على useFrame للتحقق الدوري","محدد FPS قابل للتحديد قد يؤثر على الأداء"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
