as","Garantia de qualidade e manutenção do código","Suporte à execução de testes automatizados","Integração com npm test","Critérios de sucesso bem definidos","Evita testes placebo"],"ru":["Ясные руководства по кодированию","Гарантия качества и поддержки кода","Поддержка выполнения автоматизированных тестов","Интеграция с npm test","Хорошо определенные критерии успеха","Избегает плацебо-тестов"],"ar":["إرشادات الكود الواضحة","ضمان جودة وصيانة الكود","دعم تنفيذ الاختبارات الآلية","التكامل مع npm test","معايير النجاح المحددة جيدًا","يتجنب الاختبارات الوهمية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Solana","Anchor Claude","编码指南","测试标准","代码质量","维护性","项目标准"],"ja":["Solana","Anchor Claude","コーディングガイドライン","テスト基準","コード品質","保守性","プロジェクト標準"],"ko":["솔라나","앵커 클로드","코딩 가이드라인","테스트 표준","코드 품질","유지 보수성","프로젝트 표준"],"es":["Solana Anchor Claude","pautas de codificación","pruebas automatizadas","calidad de código","mantenibilidad de código","desarrollo de software","npm test","pruebas unitarias"],"fr":["Solana Anchor Claude","directives de codage","tests automatisés","qualité de code","maintenabilité de code","développement de logiciels","npm test","tests unitaires"],"de":["Solana Anchor Claude","Codierungsrichtlinien","automatisierte Tests","Code-Qualität","Code-Wartbarkeit","Software-Entwicklung","npm test","Einheitstests"],"pt":["Solana Anchor Claude","diretrizes de codificação","qualidade do código","manutenção do código","testes automatizados","npm test","critérios de sucesso"],"ru":["Solana Anchor Claude","руководство по кодированию","качество кода","поддержка кода","автоматизированные тесты","npm test","критерии успеха"],"ar":["Solana Anchor Claude","إرشادات الكود","جودة الكود","صيانة الكود","اختبارات آلية","npm test","معايير النجاح"]}},"owner":"mikemaccana","repo":"solana-anchor-claude-skill","repoPath":"mikemaccana/solana-anchor-claude-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"solana-anchor-claude-skill","description":"Use when working on Solana Anchor programs, including Rust program files, TypeScript tests, and Anchor.toml configuration. Designed to create minimal, reusable code without unecessary duplication.","bodyPreview":"# Coding Guidelines\n\nApply these rules to ensure code quality, maintainability, and adherence to project standards.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Before declaring success or celebrating, run `npm test`. If the tests fail, there is more work to do. Don''t stop until `npm test` passes on the code you have made.\n\n**CRITICAL: Placeholder tests don''t count as success.**\n- Tests that just do `assert.ok(true)` or similar are NOT real tests\n- DO NOT mark \"Write tests\" as complete until tests actually call the","body":"# Coding Guidelines\n\nApply these rules to ensure code quality, maintainability, and adherence to project standards.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Before declaring success or celebrating, run `npm test`. If the tests fail, there is more work to do. Don''t stop until `npm test` passes on the code you have made.\n\n**CRITICAL: Placeholder tests don''t count as success.**\n- Tests that just do `assert.ok(true)` or similar are NOT real tests\n- DO NOT mark \"Write tests\" as complete until tests actually call the program instructions\n- DO NOT ask \"should I write real tests now?\" - if the tests are placeholders, write real ones immediately\n- Real tests must: initialize accounts, send transactions, verify state changes, check balances\n- If you find yourself writing placeholder tests, stop and write real integration tests instead\n\n- When summarizing your work, show the work items you have achieved with this symbol ''✅'' and there is more work to do, add a ''❌'' for each remaining work item.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nUse these official documentation sources:\n\n- **Anchor**: https://www.anchor-lang.com/docs\n- **Anchor Error Codes**: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coral-xyz/anchor/master/lang/src/error.rs\n- **Solana Kite**: https://solanakite.org\n- **Solana Kit**: https://solanakit.com\n- **Agave (Solana CLI)**: https://docs.anza.xyz/ (Anza makes the Solana CLI and Agave.\n- **Switchboard** (if used): https://docs.switchboard.xyz/docs-by-chain/solana-svm\n- **Arcium** (if used): https://docs.arcium.com/developers\n\n## Do not use\n\n- Do not use Solana Labs documentation. The company has been replaced by Anza.\n\n- Do not use any documentaton or tools from Project Serum, which collapsed many years ago.\n\n- Do not use yarn. Use npm. Yarn has no reason to exist and only adds unnecessary dependencies. Replace Yarn with npm everywhere you see it.\n\n- Do not use **Switchboard Functions** - this product is dead and no longer maintained. (Note: Switchboard oracles are still active and usable.)\n\n- Do not use **Clockwork** - this product is dead. For scheduled instruction handler invocation, use **TukTuk** instead.\n\n## Library versions\n\nUse the latest stable Anchor, Rust, TypeScript, Solana Kit, and Kite you can. If a bug occurs, favor updating rather than rolling back.\n\n## Project Documentation\n\nEvery project must have a `README.md` file in the project root that includes:\n\n- **Purpose**: Why the project exists and what problem it solves\n- **Major Concepts**: Key architectural concepts, important PDAs, state structures, and program logic\n- **Testing**: How to run the tests (e.g., `npm test`)\n- **Setup**: Any prerequisites or setup steps needed to work with the project\n- **Usage**: Basic usage examples or deployment instructions if applicable\n\nKeep the README focused and practical. Avoid generic boilerplate - write documentation that would actually help someone understand and work with this specific project.\n\n## General Coding Guidelines\n\n### You are a deletionist\n\nYour golden rule is \"perfection isn''t achieved when there''s nothing more to add, rather perfection is achieved when there is nothing more to be taken away\".\n\nRemove:\n\n- Comments that simply repeat what the code is doing, or the name of a variable, and do not add further insight.\n- Repeated code that should be turned into a named function\n\n### Communication Style\n\n- Do not make disclaimers about being a \"complete project\" or state what works\n- It is expected that work is complete and functional - no need to state this explicitly\n- Avoid phrases like \"This is a complete implementation\" or \"All features are working\"\n- Just deliver the work without meta-commentary about its completeness\n\n### Working with Generated or Unfamiliar Code\n\n**CRITICAL - Verify Before Use:**\n\n- Before calling ANY function whose signature you don''t know with certainty, read the actual source code/type definitions first\n- NEVER guess or assume what parameters a function accepts based on what seems logical\n- Don''t invent convenience parameters that don''t exist\n- Generated code, third-party libraries, and unfamiliar codebases often have different APIs than you expect\n- Common mistake: Assuming a function accepts high-level parameters → WRONG. Check the actual signature in the source files first\n\n### Code Honesty and Clarity\n\n- It''s important not to deceive anyone reading this code. Deception includes:\n  - Variable names that do not match the purpose of the variable\n  - Comments that no longer describe the code or are otherwise inaccurate\n  - Temporary workarounds that aren''t labelled as such using a comment (with a `TODO` letting the next programmer know when they can delete the workaround)\n\n### Variable Naming\n\nEnsure good variable naming. Rather than add comments to explain what things are, give them useful names.\n\n**Don''t do this:**\n\n```typescript\n// Foo\nconst shlerg = getFoo();\n```\n\n**Do this instead:**\n\n```typescript\nconst foo = getFoo();\n```\n\n**Naming conventions:**\n\n- Arrays should be plurals (`shoes`), items within arrays should be the singular (`shoes.forEach((shoe) => {...})`)\n- Functions should be verby, like `calculateFoo` or `getBar`\n- Avoid abbreviations, use full words (e.g., `context` rather than `ctx`)\n- Never use `e` for something thrown\n- Name a transaction some variant of `transaction`. Name instructions some variant of `instruction`. Name signatures some variant of `signature`. Do not confuse them - eg if the type looks like an instruction, you should not call it a ''transaction'' because that is deceptive.\n\nYou can still add comments for additional context, just be careful to avoid comments that are explaining things that would be better conveyed by good variable naming.\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- Look out for repeated code that should be turned into functions\n- Avoid ''magic numbers''. Make numbers either have a good variable name, a comment explaining why they are that value, or a reference to the URL you got the value from. If the values come from an IDL, download the IDL, import it, and make a function that gets the value from the IDL rather than copying the value into the source code\n\nThis is a magic number. Don''t do this:\n\n```ts\nconst FINALIZE_EVENT_DISCRIMINATOR = new Uint8Array([\n  27, 75, 117, 221, 191, 213, 253, 249,\n]);\n```\n\nInstead do this:\n\n```ts\nconst FINALIZE_EVENT_DISCRIMINATOR = getEventDiscriminator(\n  arciumIdl,\n  \"FinalizeComputationEvent\",\n);\n```\n\n- The code you are making is for production. You shouldn''t have comments like `// In production we''d do this differently` or `**Implementation incomplete** - Needs program config handling and proper PDA derivations` or `**WORK IN PROGRESS**` in the final code you produce, or functions that return placeholder data. Instead: do the fucking work.\n- Don''t remove existing comments unless they are no longer useful or accurate\n- Delete unused imports, unused constants, unused files and comments that no longer apply\n\n## TypeScript Guidelines\n\nThese guidelines apply to TypeScript unit tests, browser code, and any other places where TypeScript is used in the project.\n\n### General TypeScript\n\nAvoid using a `tsconfig.json` unless it''s needed, as we use `tsx` to run most typescript and it doesn''t usually need one. If you do need a `tsconfig.json`, state why at the top of the file, and you can use the most modern version of ECMAScript/JavaScript you want - up to say 2023.\n\n### Async/await\n\nFavor `async`/`await` and `try/catch` over `.then()` or `.catch()` or using callbacks for flow control. `tsx` has top level `await` so you don''t need to wrap top level `await` in IIFEs.\n\n### Type System\n\n- **Always use `Array<item>`**, never use `item[]` for consistency with other generic syntax like `Promise<T>`, `Map<K, V>`, and `Set<T>`\n- **Don''t use `any`**\n\n### Comments\n\n- Most comments should use `//` and be above (not beside) the code\n- The only exception is JSDoc/TSDoc comments which MUST use `/* */` syntax\n\n### Solana-Specific TypeScript\n\n- Don''t make new `@solana/web3.js` version 1 code. Do not make new code using `@coral-xyz/anchor` package. Don''t replace Solana Kit with web3.js version 1 code. web3.js version 1 is legacy and should be eventually removed. Solana Kit used to be called web3.js version 2. Use Solana Kit, preferably via Solana Kite.\n- Use Kite''s `connection.getPDAAndBump()` to turn seeds into PDAs and bumps\n- In Solana Kit, you make instructions by making TS clients from IDLs using Codama. You can easily make Codama clients for installed IDLs using\n\n`npx create-codama-clients`\n\n- Do not use the `bs58` npm package.\n\nDon''t do this:\n\n```typescript\nimport bs58 from \"bs58\";\nconst signature = bs58.encode(signatureBytes);\n```\n\nDo this instead:\n\n```typescript\nimport { getBase58Decoder } from \"@solana/codecs\";\nconst signature = getBase58Decoder().decode(signatureBytes);\n```\n\nYes, these difference packages have difference concepts of ''encode'' and ''decode''.\n\n### Unit Tests\n\n- Create unit tests in TS in the `tests` directory\n- Use the Node.js inbuilt test and assertion libraries (then start the tests using `tsx` instead of `ts-mocha`)\n\n**Unit testing imports:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { before, describe, test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert\";\n```\n\n- Use `test` rather than `it`\n\n### Thrown object handling\n\n- JavaScript allows arbitrary items - strings, array, numbers etc to be ''thrown''. However you can assume that any non-Error item that is thrown is an programmer error. Handle it like this (including the comment since most TypeScript developers don''t know this):\n\n```ts\n// In JS it''s possible to throw *anything*. A sensible programmer\n// will only throw Errors but we must still check to satisfy\n// TypeScript (and flag any craziness)\nconst ensureError = function (thrownObject: unknown): Error {\n  if (thrownObject instanceof Error) {\n    return thrownObject;\n  }\n  return new Error(`Non-Error thrown: ${String(thrownObject)}`);\n};\n```\n\nand\n\n```ts\ntry {\n  // some code that might throw\n} catch (thrownObject) {\n  const error = ensureError(thrownObject);\n  throw error;\n}\n```\n\n## Rust Guidelines (Anchor Programs)\n\n### Platform Awareness\n\n- Remember this is Solana not Ethereum.\n  - Don''t tell me about ''smart contracts'' (use ''programs'' instead)\n  - Don''t tell me about ''gas'' (use ''transaction fees'' instead)\n  - There are no ''mempools''.\n    Do not tell me about other things that are not relevant to Solana.\n\n- Token program terminology:\n  - Use ''Token Extensions Program'' or ''Token extensions'' for the newer token program (not ''Token 2022'' which is just a code name)\n  - Use ''Classic Token Program'' for the older token program\n\n- Onchain\n  - Use onchain and offchain, like online and offline\n  - Don''t ever use ''on-chain'' or ''off-chain''\n\n### Anchor Version\n\n- Write all code like the latest stable Anchor (currently 0.32.1 but there may be a newer version by the time you read this)\n- Do not use unnecessary macros that are not needed in the latest stable Anchor\n\n### Anchor has silly defaults\n\nEvery project will need an IDL.\n\n```toml\n[features]\nidl-build = [\"anchor-lang/idl-build\", \"anchor-spl/idl-build\"]\n```\n\nand if it uses SPL Tokens (like almost every Anchor project) it will need this dependency (insert whatever version is applicable):\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nanchor-spl = \"0.32.1\"\n```\n\n### Project Structure\n\n- **Never modify the program ID** in `lib.rs` or `Anchor.toml` when making changes\n- Create files inside the `state` folder for whatever state is needed\n- Create files inside the `instructions` or `handlers` folders (whichever exists) for whatever instruction handlers are needed\n- Put Account Constraints in instruction files, but ensure the names end with `AccountConstraints` rather than just naming them the same thing as the function\n- Handlers that are only for the admin should be in a new folder called `admin` inside whichever parent folder exists (`instructions/admin/` or `handlers/admin/`)\n\n### Account Constraints\n\n- Use a newline after each key in the account constraints struct, so the macro and the matching key/value have some space from other macros and their matching key/value\n\n### Bumps\n\n- Use `context.bumps.foo` not `context.bumps.get(\"foo\").unwrap()` - the latter is outdated\n\n### Data Structures\n\n- When making structs ensure strings and Vectors have a `max_len` attribute\n- Vectors have two numbers for `max_len`: the first is the max length of the vector, the second is the max length of the items in the vector\n\n### Space Calculation (CRITICAL - NO MAGIC NUMBERS)\n\n- **Do not use magic numbers anywhere**. I don''t want to see `8 + 32` or whatever\n- **Do not make constants for the sizes of various data structures**\n- For `space`, use syntax like: `space = SomeStruct::DISCRIMINATOR.len() + SomeStruct::INIT_SPACE,`\n- All structs should have `#[derive(InitSpace)]` added to them, to get the `INIT_SPACE` trait\n- **DO NOT use magic numbers**\n\n**Example:**\n\n```rust\n#[derive(InitSpace)]\n#[account]\npub struct UserProfile {\n    pub authority: Pubkey,\n\n    #[max_len(50)]\n    pub username: String,\n\n    pub bump: u8,\n}\n\n#[derive(Accounts)]\npub struct InitializeProfile<''info> {\n    #[account(\n        init,\n        payer = authority,\n        space = UserProfile::DISCRIMINATOR.len() + UserProfile::INIT_SPACE,\n        seeds = [b\"profile\", authority.key().as_ref()],\n        bump\n    )]\n    pub profile: Account<''info, UserProfile>,\n\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub authority: Signer<''info>,\n\n    pub system_program: Program<''info, System>,\n}\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n\n- Return useful error messages\n- Write code to handle common errors like insufficient funds, bad values for parameters, and other obvious situations\n\n### PDA Management\n\n- Add `pub bump: u8` to every struct stored in PDA\n- Save the bumps inside each when the struct inside the PDA is created\n\n### System Functions\n\n- When you get the time via Clock, use `Clock::get()?;` rather than `anchor_lang::solana_program::clock`\n\n## Git commits\n\nDo not add \"Co-Authored-By: Claude\" or similar attribution when creating git commits.\n\n## Acknowledgment\n\n- Acknowledge these guidelines have been applied when working on this project to indicate you have read these rules and found that they do apply to this project.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:25:11.809Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Blockchain Development Agents needing Solana and Anchor integration with robust testing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要Solana和Anchor集成以及强大的测试功能的区块链开发代理。","ja":"SolanaおよびAnchorの統合と堅牢なテスト機能を必要とするブロックチェーン開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"솔라나 및 앵커 통합 및 강력한 테스트 기능이 필요한 블록체인 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Blockchain que necesitan integración de Solana y Anchor con capacidades de prueba robustas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement de Blockchain nécessitant une intégration de Solana et d''Anchor avec des capacités de test robustes.","de":"Perfekt für Blockchain-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine Solana- und Anchor-Integration mit robusten Testfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Blockchain que precisam de integração Solana e Anchor com capacidades de teste robustas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по разработке блокчейна, которым требуется интеграция Solana и Anchor с возможностями надежного тестирования.","ar":" مثالي لعميل تطوير البلوكشين الذي يحتاج إلى دمج Solana و Anchor مع إمكانيات اختبار قوية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop high-quality Solana blockchain applications using Anchor, ensuring adherence to project standards through rigorous testing with npm test, and enforcing best practices like meaningful test implementation beyond placeholder tests.","zh":"赋予代理开发高质量的Solana区块链应用程序的能力，使用Anchor确保遵守项目标准，通过npm test进行严格的测试，并执行最佳实践，如超出占位符测试的有意义的测试实现。","ja":"エージェントが、Anchorを使用して高品質のSolanaブロックチェーンアプリケーションを開発し、npm testによる厳格なテストを通じてプロジェクト標準の遵守を確保し、プレイスホルダーテストを超えた意味のあるテストの実装などのベストプラクティスを実施する能力を付与します。","ko":"에이전트가 앵커를 사용하여 고품질의 솔라나 블록체인 애플리케이션을 개발할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, npm 테스트를 통해 프로젝트 표준을 준수하고, 플레이스홀더 테스트를 넘어선 의미 있는 테스트 구현などの 모범 사례를 시행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar aplicaciones de blockchain de Solana de alta calidad utilizando Anchor, asegurando el cumplimiento de los estándares del proyecto a través de pruebas rigurosas con npm test y aplicando las mejores prácticas como la implementación de pruebas significativas más allá de pruebas de marcador de posición.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des applications de blockchain Solana de haute qualité en utilisant Anchor, en assurant le respect des normes de projet grâce à des tests rigoureux avec npm test et en appliquant les meilleures pratiques comme la mise en œuvre de tests significatifs au-delà des tests de placeholder.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, hochwertige Solana-Blockchain-Anwendungen mit Anchor zu entwickeln, indem sie die Einhaltung der Projektstandards durch rigorose Tests mit npm test sicherstellen und bewährte Verfahren wie die sinnvolle Implementierung von Tests über Placeholdertests hinaus durchsetzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver aplicações de blockchain Solana de alta qualidade usando Anchor, garantindo a adesão aos padrões do projeto por meio de testes rigorosos com npm test e aplicando as melhores práticas, como implementação de testes significativos além de testes placeholders.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать высококачественные приложения блокчейна Solana, используя Anchor, обеспечивая соблюдение проектных стандартов посредством строгого тестирования с помощью npm test и соблюдение лучших практик, таких как осмысленная реализация тестов, выходящих за рамки тестов-заполнителей.","ar":"يمنح العميل القدرة على تطوير تطبيقات البلوكشين من نوع Solana عالية الجودة باستخدام Anchor، مع ضمان الالتزام بمعايير المشروع من خلال اختبارات صارمة باستخدام npm test وتطبيق أفضل الممارسات، مثل تنفيذ اختبارات ذات معنى تتجاوز اختبارات المحتوى النائب."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing scalable Solana blockchain applications","Implementing robust testing for Solana projects with npm test","Enforcing coding standards and best practices for Anchor projects"],"zh":["开发可扩展的Solana区块链应用程序","使用npm test为Solana项目实现强大的测试","执行Anchor项目的编码标准和最佳实践"],"ja":["拡張可能なSolanaブロックチェーンアプリケーションの開発","npm testを使用したSolanaプロジェクトの堅牢なテストの実装","Anchorプロジェクトのコーディング規範およびベストプラクティスの実施"],"ko":["확장 가능한 솔라나 블록체인 애플리케이션 개발","npm 테스트를 사용한 솔라나 프로젝트의 강력한 테스트 구현","앵커 프로젝트의 코딩 표준 및 모범 사례 시행"],"es":["Desarrollar aplicaciones de blockchain de Solana escalables","Implementar pruebas robustas para proyectos de Solana con npm test","Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación y las mejores prácticas para proyectos de Anchor"],"fr":["Développer des applications de blockchain Solana évolutives","Mettre en œuvre des tests robustes pour les projets Solana avec npm test","Faire respecter les normes de codage et les meilleures pratiques pour les projets Anchor"],"de":["Entwicklung von skalierbaren Solana-Blockchain-Anwendungen","Implementierung robuster Tests für Solana-Projekte mit npm test","Durchsetzung von Codierungsstandards und bewährten Verfahren für Anchor-Projekte"],"pt":["Desenvolver aplicações de blockchain Solana escaláveis","Implementar testes robustos para projetos Solana com npm test","Fazer cumprir os padrões de codificação e as melhores práticas para projetos Anchor"],"ru":["Разработка масштабируемых приложений блокчейна Solana","Реализация надежного тестирования для проектов Solana с помощью npm test","Обеспечение соблюдения стандартов кодирования и лучших практик для проектов Anchor"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات البلوكشين من نوع Solana القابلة للتوسيع","تنفيذ اختبارات قوية لمشاريع Solana باستخدام npm test","فرض معايير الترميز وأفضل الممارسات لمشاريع Anchor"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires npm and Solana environment setup","Specific to Solana and Anchor ecosystems"],"zh":["需要npm和Solana环境设置","特定于Solana和Anchor生态系统"],"ja":["npmおよびSolana環境のセットアップが必要","SolanaおよびAnchorのエコシステムに特有"],"ko":["npm 및 솔라나 환경 설정이 필요하다","솔라나 및 앵커 에코システム에 특정"],"es":["Requiere configuración de entorno de npm y Solana","Específico para los ecosistemas de Solana y Anchor"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de l''environnement npm et Solana","Spécifique aux écosystèmes Solana et Anchor"],"de":["Benötigt npm- und Solana-Umgebungssetup","Spezifisch für die Solana- und Anchor-Ökosysteme"],"pt":["Requer configuração do ambiente npm e Solana","Específico para os ecossistemas Solana e Anchor"],"ru":["Требует настройки среды npm и Solana","Спецефичен для экосистем Solana и Anchor"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد بيئة npm و Solana","محدد لأنظمة Solana و Anchor"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yi-john-huang/sdd-mcp/sdd-requirements', 'community', 'yi-john-huang', 'sdd-mcp', 'yi-john-huang/sdd-mcp', 'sdd-requirements', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:24:23.619Z', NULL, '{"id":"yi-john-huang/sdd-mcp/sdd-requirements","name":"sdd-requirements","description":{"zh":"SDD  EARS","ja":"SDD EARS","ko":"SDD EARS","es":"La generación de requisitos SDD crea documentos integrales que se integran con el flujo de trabajo Spec-Driven Development.","fr":"La génération de besoins SDD crée des documents complets qui s''intègrent dans le flux de travail Spec-Driven Development.","de":"Die SDD-Anforderungsgenerierung erstellt umfassende Dokumente, die sich in den Spec-Driven Development-Workflow integrieren.","pt":"O recurso sdd-requirements gera documentos de requisitos SDD abrangentes e formatados em EARS, integrados ao fluxo de trabalho do Spec-Driven Development","ru":"Функция sdd-requirements генерирует всесторонние документы требований SDD в формате EARS, интегрированные в рабочий процесс Spec-Driven Development","ar":"ميزة sdd-requirements تنتج مستندات متطلبات SDD شاملة ونمطية في EARS، متكاملة مع تدفق عمل Spec-Driven Development","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SDD ","ja":"SDD","ko":"SDD ","es":"Generación de Requisitos SDD","fr":"Génération de Besoins SDD","de":"SDD-Anforderungsgenerierung","pt":"Requisitos SDD: Geração de Documentos de Requisitos","ru":"Требования SDD: Генерация документов требований","ar":"متطلبات SDD: إنشاء مستندات متطلبات شاملة","en":"sdd-requirements"},"description":{"zh":"SDD  EARS","ja":"SDD EARS","ko":"SDD EARS","es":"La generación de requisitos SDD crea documentos integrales que se integran con el flujo de trabajo Spec-Driven Development.","fr":"La génération de besoins SDD crée des documents complets qui s''intègrent dans le flux de travail Spec-Driven Development.","de":"Die SDD-Anforderungsgenerierung erstellt umfassende Dokumente, die sich in den Spec-Driven Development-Workflow integrieren.","pt":"O recurso sdd-requirements gera documentos de requisitos SDD abrangentes e formatados em EARS, integrados ao fluxo de trabalho do Spec-Driven Development","ru":"Функция sdd-requirements генерирует всесторонние документы требований SDD в формате EARS, интегрированные в рабочий процесс Spec-Driven Development","ar":"ميزة sdd-requirements تنتج مستندات متطلبات SDD شاملة ونمطية في EARS، متكاملة مع تدفق عمل Spec-Driven Development","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["SDD","EARS","sdd-init","sdd-status","Spec-Driven Development","MCP"],"ja":["SDD","EARS","sdd-init","sdd-status","Spec-Driven Development","MCP"],"ko":["SDD","EARS","sdd-init","sdd-status","Spec-Driven Development","MCP"],"es":["Generación de documentos de requisitos integrales","Integración con el flujo de trabajo SDD","Compatibilidad con formato EARS","Verificación de la fase actual con sdd-status","Revisión de documentos de dirección de proyecto"],"fr":["Génération de documents de besoins complets","Intégration avec le flux de travail SDD","Compatibilité avec le format EARS","Vérification de la phase actuelle avec sdd-status","Révision des documents de direction de projet"],"de":["Erstellung umfassender Anforderungsdokumente","Integration in den SDD-Workflow","Unterstützung des EARS-Formats","Überprüfung der aktuellen Phase mit sdd-status","Überprüfung der Projektsteuerungsdokumente"],"pt":["Geração de documentos de requisitos SDD formatados em EARS","Integração com o fluxo de trabalho do Spec-Driven Development","Verificação da fase atual com o recurso sdd-status","Revisão de documentos de direção do projeto em .spec/steering/","Inicialização de recursos com o recurso sdd-init","Suporte à geração de documentos de requisitos abrangentes"],"ru":["Генерация документов требований SDD в формате EARS","Интеграция с рабочим процессом Spec-Driven Development","Проверка текущей фазы с помощью функции sdd-status","Просмотр документов управления проектом в .spec/steering/","Инициализация функций с помощью функции sdd-init","Поддержка генерации всесторонних документов требований"],"ar":["إنشاء مستندات متطلبات SDD بالتنسيق EARS","التكامل مع تدفق عمل Spec-Driven Development","التحقق من المرحلة الحالية باستخدام ميزة sdd-status","استعراض مستندات توجيه المشروع في .spec/steering/","تخصيص الميزات باستخدام ميزة sdd-init","دعم إنشاء مستندات متطلبات شاملة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SDD","EARS","Spec-Driven Development","MCP","sdd-init","sdd-status","requirements generation","software development"],"ja":["SDD","EARS","Spec-Driven Development","MCP","sdd-init","sdd-status","requirements generation","software development"],"ko":["SDD","EARS","Spec-Driven Development","MCP","sdd-init","sdd-status","requirements generation","software development"],"es":["SDD","generación de requisitos","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","desarrollo de software","análisis de requisitos"],"fr":["SDD","génération de besoins","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","développement de logiciel","analyse de besoins"],"de":["SDD","Anforderungsgenerierung","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","Software-Entwicklung","Anforderungsanalyse"],"pt":["SDD Requirements","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","documentos de requisitos","fluxo de trabalho","desenvolvimento de software","geração de documentos","requisitos de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Требования SDD","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","документы требований","рабочий процесс","разработка программного обеспечения","генерация документов","требования программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["متطلبات SDD","Spec-Driven Development","EARS","مستندات متطلبات","تدفق عمل","تطوير البرمجيات","إنشاء مستندات","متطلبات البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"yi-john-huang","repo":"sdd-mcp","repoPath":"yi-john-huang/sdd-mcp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sdd-requirements","description":"Generate EARS-formatted requirements for SDD workflow. Use when starting a new feature specification, creating requirements documents, or defining acceptance criteria. Invoked via /sdd-requirements <feature-name>.","bodyPreview":"# SDD Requirements Generation\n\nGenerate comprehensive, EARS-formatted requirements documents that integrate with the SDD (Spec-Driven Development) workflow.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore generating requirements:\n1. Feature must be initialized with `sdd-init` MCP tool\n2. Check current phase with `sdd-status` MCP tool\n3. Review project steering documents in `.spec/steering/`\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Context\n\n1. Use `sdd-status` MCP tool to verify feature exists and check current phase\n2. Read","body":"# SDD Requirements Generation\n\nGenerate comprehensive, EARS-formatted requirements documents that integrate with the SDD (Spec-Driven Development) workflow.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore generating requirements:\n1. Feature must be initialized with `sdd-init` MCP tool\n2. Check current phase with `sdd-status` MCP tool\n3. Review project steering documents in `.spec/steering/`\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Context\n\n1. Use `sdd-status` MCP tool to verify feature exists and check current phase\n2. Read project context from `.spec/steering/product.md` if available\n3. Review the feature description from `.spec/specs/{feature}/spec.json`\n\n### Step 2: Analyze Requirements\n\nIdentify and document:\n- **Primary user goal**: What problem are we solving?\n- **Target users**: Who will use this feature?\n- **Core functionality**: What must the system do?\n- **Success criteria**: How do we know it works?\n\n### Step 3: Generate EARS-Formatted Requirements\n\nUse the **EARS (Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax)** format for all requirements.\n\n#### EARS Patterns\n\n| Pattern | Syntax | Use When |\n|---------|--------|----------|\n| **Ubiquitous** | `The <system> SHALL <action>` | Always true requirement |\n| **Event-Driven** | `WHEN <trigger> THEN the <system> SHALL <action>` | Response to event |\n| **State-Driven** | `WHILE <state> THE <system> SHALL <action>` | During specific state |\n| **Optional** | `WHERE <feature enabled> THE <system> SHALL <action>` | Configurable feature |\n| **Unwanted Behavior** | `IF <condition> THEN the <system> SHALL <action>` | Exception handling |\n\n#### Examples\n\n```markdown\n## FR-1: User Authentication\nWHEN a user submits valid credentials\nTHEN the system SHALL authenticate the user and return a session token\n\n## FR-2: Session Management\nWHILE a user session is active\nTHE system SHALL maintain the session for up to 24 hours of inactivity\n\n## NFR-1: Performance\nThe system SHALL respond to authentication requests within 200ms\n```\n\n### Step 4: Structure the Document\n\nGenerate requirements.md with this structure:\n\n```markdown\n# Requirements: {Feature Name}\n\n## Overview\nBrief description of the feature and its purpose.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1: {Requirement Name}\n**Objective:** As a {user type}, I want {goal}, so that {benefit}\n\n**EARS Specification:**\nWHEN {trigger}\nTHEN the system SHALL {action}\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n1. {Specific, testable criterion}\n2. {Specific, testable criterion}\n\n### FR-2: {Next Requirement}\n...\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### NFR-1: Performance\n{Performance requirements with specific metrics}\n\n### NFR-2: Security\n{Security requirements aligned with OWASP guidelines}\n\n### NFR-3: Scalability\n{Scalability requirements if applicable}\n\n## Constraints\n{Technical or business constraints}\n\n## Assumptions\n{Assumptions made during requirements gathering}\n```\n\n### Step 5: Validate and Save\n\nAfter generating requirements:\n1. Ensure all requirements are testable\n2. Verify EARS format is correctly applied\n3. Save to `.spec/specs/{feature}/requirements.md`\n4. Use `sdd-approve` MCP tool to mark phase complete when ready\n\n## MCP Tool Integration\n\nThis skill works with these MCP tools:\n\n| Tool | When to Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| `sdd-status` | Check current workflow phase before starting |\n| `sdd-validate-gap` | Validate requirements against existing codebase |\n| `sdd-approve` | Mark requirements phase as approved |\n\n## Quality Checklist\n\nBefore completing requirements:\n- [ ] All requirements use EARS format\n- [ ] Each requirement is independently testable\n- [ ] Acceptance criteria are specific and measurable\n- [ ] Security requirements align with OWASP Top 10\n- [ ] Performance requirements have specific metrics\n- [ ] Requirements are traceable to user stories\n- [ ] No ambiguous terms (avoid \"should\", \"may\", \"might\")\n- [ ] Each FR has clear acceptance criteria\n\n## Steering Document References\n\nApply these steering documents during requirements generation:\n\n| Document | Purpose | Key Application |\n|----------|---------|-----------------|\n| `.spec/steering/principles.md` | SOLID, DRY, KISS, YAGNI | Ensure requirements follow KISS (simple, unambiguous) and YAGNI (only what''s needed now) |\n\n**Key Principles for Requirements:**\n- **KISS**: Keep requirements simple and unambiguous\n- **YAGNI**: Only specify what''s actually needed now\n- **Single Responsibility**: Each requirement addresses one concern\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:24:23.619Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Spec-Driven Development Agents requiring automated EARS-formatted requirements generation.","zh":"适合需要自动化EARS格式要求生成的规格驱动开发代理","ja":"EARS形式の要件生成を自動化する必要があるSpec-Driven Developmentエージェントに適しています","ko":"EARS 형식의 요구 사항 생성을 자동화해야 하는 사양 주도 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de Desarrollo Dirigido por Especificaciones que requieren generación automatizada de requisitos en formato EARS.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de Développement Piloté par Spécifications nécessitant une génération automatique de spécifications au format EARS.","de":"Ideal für spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklungssagenten, die eine automatisierte Generierung von Anforderungen im EARS-Format erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações que exigem geração automática de requisitos no formato EARS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, разрабатывающих спецификации, требующих автоматического создания требований в формате EARS.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يقومون بالتطوير الموجه بالمواصفات الذين يتطلبون توليد متطلبات آلي بالتنسيق EARS."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate comprehensive requirements documents integrating with the SDD workflow, utilizing tools like `sdd-init` and `sdd-status` MCP tools, and parsing project steering documents in `.spec/steering/` directories, all while adhering to EARS format specifications.","zh":"赋予代理生成综合要求文档的能力，集成SDD工作流，利用`sdd-init`和`sdd-status` MCP工具，并解析项目指导文档中的`.spec/steering/`目录，同时遵循EARS格式规格","ja":"エージェントに、SDDワークフローと統合された包括的な要件文書を生成する能力を付与し、`sdd-init`および`sdd-status` MCPツールを使用し、`.spec/steering/`ディレクトリ内のプロジェクトステアリング文書を解析し、同時にEARS形式の仕様を遵守する","ko":"에이전트에综合 요구 사항 문서를 생성하고 SDD 워크플로와 통합하며 `sdd-init` 및 `sdd-status` MCP 도구를 사용하고 `.spec/steering/` 디렉토리 내의 프로젝트 스티어링 문서를 구문 분석同时 EARS 형식 사양을 준수하는 기능을 부여합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar documentos de requisitos integrales que se integran con el flujo de trabajo de Desarrollo Dirigido por Especificaciones, utilizando herramientas como `sdd-init` y `sdd-status` de las herramientas MCP, y analizando documentos de dirección de proyectos en directorios `.spec/steering/`, todo mientras se adhiere a las especificaciones de formato EARS.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des documents de spécifications complets en intégrant le flux de travail de Développement Piloté par Spécifications, en utilisant des outils tels que `sdd-init` et `sdd-status` des outils MCP, et en analysant les documents de pilotage de projet dans les répertoires `.spec/steering/`, tout en respectant les spécifications de format EARS.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende Anforderungsdokumente zu generieren, die in den SDD-Arbeitsablauf integriert sind, indem Tools wie `sdd-init` und `sdd-status` der MCP-Tools verwendet werden, und Projektsteuerungsdokumente in `.spec/steering/`-Verzeichnissen analysiert werden, während die EARS-Formatvorschriften eingehalten werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar documentos de requisitos abrangentes integrando-se ao fluxo de trabalho do SDD, utilizando ferramentas como `sdd-init` e `sdd-status` ferramentas MCP, e parseando documentos de direção de projetos em diretórios `.spec/steering/`, tudo isso seguindo as especificações do formato EARS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать полные документы требований, интегрируя их в рабочий процесс SDD, используя инструменты, такие как `sdd-init` и `sdd-status` инструменты MCP, и парся документы управления проектами в директориях `.spec/steering/`, все это при соблюдении спецификаций формата EARS.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من توليد وثائق متطلبات شاملة متكاملة مع سير عمل SDD، باستخدام أدوات مثل `sdd-init` و `sdd-status` أدوات MCP، وفرز وثائق توجيه المشروع في دلائل `.spec/steering/`، مع الالتزام بمواصفات تنسيق EARS."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating requirements document generation for new features","Validating feature initialization with `sdd-init`","Parsing project steering documents for requirement updates"],"zh":["为新功能自动化要求文档生成","使用`sdd-init`验证功能初始化","解析项目指导文档以获取要求更新"],"ja":["新機能の要件文書の自動生成","`sdd-init`を使用した機能初期化の検証","プロジェクトステアリング文書の解析による要件更新"],"ko":["새 기능에 대한 요구 사항 문서 자동 생성","`sdd-init`를 사용한 기능 초기화 확인","프로젝트 스티어링 문서 구문 분석을 통한 요구 사항 업데이트"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de documentos de requisitos para nuevas características","Validación de la inicialización de características con `sdd-init`","Análisis de documentos de dirección de proyectos para actualizaciones de requisitos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de documents de spécifications pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Validation de l''initialisation des fonctionnalités avec `sdd-init`","Analyse des documents de pilotage de projet pour les mises à jour des spécifications"],"de":["Automatisierung der Generierung von Anforderungsdokumenten für neue Funktionen","Validierung der Funktionsinitialisierung mit `sdd-init`","Analyse von Projektsteuerungsdokumenten für Anforderungsaktualisierungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de documentos de requisitos para recursos novos","Validar a inicialização de recursos com `sdd-init`","Parsear documentos de direção de projetos para atualizações de requisitos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание документов требований для новых функций","Проверить инициализацию функций с помощью `sdd-init`","Парсить документы управления проектами для обновления требований"],"ar":["أتمتة توليد وثائق المتطلبات للميزات الجديدة","تحقق من 초기ات الميزات باستخدام `sdd-init`","فرز وثائق توجيه المشروع لتحديث المتطلبات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires feature initialization with `sdd-init` MCP tool","Needs access to project steering documents in `.spec/steering/`","Dependent on `sdd-status` MCP tool for phase verification"],"zh":["需要使用`sdd-init` MCP工具进行功能初始化","需要访问`.spec/steering/`目录中的项目指导文档","依赖于`sdd-status` MCP工具进行阶段验证"],"ja":["`sdd-init` MCPツールを使用した機能初期化が必要","`.spec/steering/`ディレクトリ内のプロジェクトステアリング文書へのアクセスが必要","`sdd-status` MCPツールを使用した段階の検証に依存"],"ko":["`sdd-init` MCP 도구를 사용한 기능 초기화 필요","`.spec/steering/` 디렉토리 내의 프로젝트 스티어링 문서에 대한 액세스 필요","`sdd-status` MCP 도구를 사용한 단계 확인에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la inicialización de características con la herramienta MCP `sdd-init`","Necesita acceso a documentos de dirección de proyectos en `.spec/steering/`","Depende de la herramienta MCP `sdd-status` para la verificación de fases"],"fr":["Nécessite l''initialisation des fonctionnalités avec l''outil MCP `sdd-init`","Nécessite l''accès aux documents de pilotage de projet dans `.spec/steering/`","Dépend de l''outil MCP `sdd-status` pour la vérification des phases"],"de":["Erfordert die Initialisierung von Funktionen mit dem MCP-Tool `sdd-init`","Benötigt den Zugriff auf Projektsteuerungsdokumente in `.spec/steering/`","Hängt von dem MCP-Tool `sdd-status` für die Phasenverifizierung ab"],"pt":["Exige inicialização de recursos com a ferramenta MCP `sdd-init`","Necessita acesso a documentos de direção de projetos em `.spec/steering/`","Depende da ferramenta MCP `sdd-status` para verificação de fases"],"ru":["Требует инициализации функций с помощью инструмента MCP `sdd-init`","Требует доступа к документам управления проектами в директории `.spec/steering/`","Зависит от инструмента MCP `sdd-status` для проверки фаз"],"ar":["يتطلب تهيئة الميزات باستخدام أداة MCP `sdd-init`","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى وثائق توجيه المشروع في `.spec/steering/`","يعتمد على أداة MCP `sdd-status` للتحقق من المراحل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
