 mit E-Mail und OAuth","MongoDB-Datenbank","Entwicklung von Fullstack-Webanwendungen","Keine Serververwaltung erforderlich","Unterstützung für Magic Links","Integration mit GitHub und Google"],"pt":["Autenticação via e-mail e OAuth","Banco de dados MongoDB","Desenvolvimento de aplicações web fullstack","Suporte a links mágicos","Integração com bkend.ai"],"ru":["Аутентификация через электронную почту и OAuth","База данных MongoDB","Разработка полноценных веб-приложений","Поддержка магических ссылок","Интеграция с bkend.ai"],"ar":["التحقق من خلال البريد الإلكتروني و OAuth","قاعدة بيانات MongoDB","تطوير تطبيقات ويب كاملة","دعم الروابط السحرية","التكامل مع bkend.ai"]},"keywords":{"zh":["全栈开发","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","无服务器管理","身份验证","数据库","MongoDB","SaaS产品","数据驱动应用"],"ja":["フルスタック開発","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","サーバー管理不要","認証","データベース","MongoDB","SaaS製品","データドリブンアプリ"],"ko":["풀스택 개발","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","서버 관리가 필요하지 않음","인증","데이터베이스","몽고DB","SaaS 제품","데이터 주도 애플리케이션"],"es":["desarrollo web fullstack","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","autenticación","base de datos","desarrollo de aplicaciones","sin servidor","Magic Links","OAuth","GitHub"],"fr":["développement web fullstack","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","authentification","base de données","développement d''applications","sans serveur","Magic Links","OAuth","GitHub"],"de":["Fullstack-Webentwicklung","bkend.ai","Backend-as-a-Service","Authentifizierung","Datenbank","Anwendungsentwicklung","serverlos","Magic Links","OAuth","GitHub"],"pt":["desenvolvimento web fullstack","bkend.ai","backend como serviço","autenticação","banco de dados","desenvolvimento de aplicações","técnicas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["полноценное веб-разработка","bkend.ai","бэкэнд как сервис","аутентификация","база данных","разработка приложений","техники разработки"],"ar":["تطوير ويب كامل","bkend.ai","الخلفية كخدمة","التحقق","قاعدة البيانات","تطوير التطبيقات","تقنيات التطوير"]}},"owner":"popup-studio-ai","repo":"bkit-gemini","repoPath":"popup-studio-ai/bkit-gemini","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dynamic","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Dynamic Skill\n\n> Fullstack development with bkend.ai BaaS platform\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Dynamic skill enables fullstack web application development using bkend.ai as the Backend-as-a-Service platform. No server management required.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Web applications with user accounts\n- SaaS products\n- MVPs with backend requirements\n- Apps needing authentication\n- Data-driven applications\n\n## bkend.ai Features\n\n- **Authentication**: Email, OAuth (Google, GitHub), Magic Links\n- **Database**: Mong","body":"# Dynamic Skill\n\n> Fullstack development with bkend.ai BaaS platform\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Dynamic skill enables fullstack web application development using bkend.ai as the Backend-as-a-Service platform. No server management required.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Web applications with user accounts\n- SaaS products\n- MVPs with backend requirements\n- Apps needing authentication\n- Data-driven applications\n\n## bkend.ai Features\n\n- **Authentication**: Email, OAuth (Google, GitHub), Magic Links\n- **Database**: MongoDB Atlas (REST API)\n- **Storage**: S3 Presigned URL file uploads\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket subscriptions (planned)\n- **API**: REST API (`https://api-client.bkend.ai`)\n- **MCP**: 28 tools + 4 resources (`https://api.bkend.ai/mcp`)\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nproject/\n├── app/\n│   ├── (auth)/\n│   │   ├── login/\n│   │   └── signup/\n│   ├── (dashboard)/\n│   │   └── ...\n│   └── api/\n├── lib/\n│   └── bkend/\n│       └── client.ts\n├── components/\n├── docs/\n│   ├── 01-plan/\n│   ├── 02-design/\n│   └── 03-analysis/\n└── .mcp.json\n```\n\n## Key Phases (Dynamic Level)\n\n| Phase | Required | Description |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| 1. Schema | ✅ | Define data models |\n| 2. Convention | ✅ | Set coding rules |\n| 3. Mockup | ✅ | Design UI/UX |\n| 4. API | ✅ | Design API endpoints |\n| 5. Design System | 🔶 Optional | Component library |\n| 6. UI Integration | ✅ | Connect frontend to API |\n| 7. SEO/Security | 🔶 Optional | Auth hardening |\n| 8. Review | 🔶 Optional | Code review |\n| 9. Deployment | ✅ | Deploy to production |\n\n## Getting Started\n\n```bash\n# Initialize Dynamic project\n/dynamic init\n\n# Start the pipeline\n/development-pipeline start\n```\n\n## Authentication Example\n\n```typescript\n// lib/bkend/client.ts - REST API Direct Call Pattern\nconst BKEND_API_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BKEND_API_URL || ''https://api-client.bkend.ai'';\n\nasync function bkendFetch(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${BKEND_API_URL}${path}`, {\n    ...options,\n    headers: {\n      ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n      ''X-Project-Id'': process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BKEND_PROJECT_ID!,\n      ''X-Environment'': process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BKEND_ENVIRONMENT || ''dev'',\n      ...options.headers,\n    },\n  });\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`bkend API error: ${response.status}`);\n  return response.json();\n}\n\n// Login\nconst { accessToken, refreshToken, user } = await bkendFetch(''/auth/email/signin'', {\n  method: ''POST'',\n  body: JSON.stringify({ email, password }),\n});\n```\n\n## Available bkend Skills\n\nFor detailed domain knowledge, use these dedicated skills:\n\n| Skill | Command | Domain |\n|-------|---------|--------|\n| bkend-quickstart | `/bkend-quickstart` | Onboarding, core concepts |\n| bkend-auth | `/bkend-auth` | Authentication (21 docs) |\n| bkend-data | `/bkend-data` | Database CRUD (13 docs) |\n| bkend-storage | `/bkend-storage` | File storage (10 docs) |\n| bkend-mcp | `/bkend-mcp` | MCP + AI tools (18 docs) |\n| bkend-security | `/bkend-security` | Security (8 docs) |\n| bkend-cookbook | `/bkend-cookbook` | Project tutorials (4+5) |\n| bkend-guides | `/bkend-guides` | Guides + troubleshooting (16 docs) |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:25:20.210Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Fullstack Agents needing rapid web application development with Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) integration and AI-native development capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要快速Web应用开发的全栈代理，具有后端即服务（BaaS）集成和AI原生开发能力。","ja":"フルスタックエージェントが迅速なWebアプリケーション開発を必要とする場合に最適です。 Backend-as-a-Service（BaaS）統合とAIネイティブ開発機能を備えています。","ko":" 빠른 웹 애플리케이션 개발이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 백엔드即サービス(BaaS) 통합 및 AI 네이티브 개발 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Fullstack que necesitan un desarrollo rápido de aplicaciones web con integración de Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) y capacidades de desarrollo nativas de inteligencia artificial.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Fullstack ayant besoin d''un développement rapide d''applications web avec une intégration de Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) et des capacités de développement natives d''intelligence artificielle.","de":"Perfekt für Fullstack-Agents, die ein schnelles Entwickeln von Webanwendungen mit Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS)-Integration und AI-nativen Entwicklungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Fullstack que necessitam de desenvolvimento rápido de aplicações web com integração de Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) e capacidades de desenvolvimento nativas de IA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Fullstack, которым требуется быстрое разработка веб-приложений с интеграцией Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) и возможностями разработки, родными для ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء.Fullstack الذين يحتاجون إلى تطوير تطبيقات الويب السريع مع دمج الخدمة الخلفية كخدمة (BaaS) وقدرات التطوير الأصلي للذكاء الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build scalable web applications using bkend.ai BaaS platform, leveraging features like authentication via Email, OAuth, and Magic Links, and a MongoDB database for seamless data management.","zh":"使代理能够使用bkend.ai BaaS平台构建可扩展的Web应用程序，利用诸如通过电子邮件、OAuth和Magic Links进行身份验证等功能，以及用于无缝数据管理的MongoDB数据库。","ja":"エージェントがbkend.ai BaaSプラットフォームを使用してスケーラブルなWebアプリケーションを構築できるようにします。メール、OAuth、Magic Linksによる認証などの機能と、シームレスなデータ管理のためのMongoDBデータベースを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 bkend.ai BaaS 플랫폼을 사용하여 확장 가능한 웹 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있도록 합니다. 이메일, OAuth, 매직 링크를 통한 인증 등의 기능과 무결점 데이터 관리를 위한 MongoDB 데이터베이스를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir aplicaciones web escalables utilizando la plataforma BaaS bkend.ai, aprovechando características como la autenticación mediante correo electrónico, OAuth y Magic Links, y una base de datos MongoDB para una gestión de datos sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des applications web escalables en utilisant la plate-forme BaaS bkend.ai, en exploitant des fonctionnalités comme l''authentification par e-mail, OAuth et Magic Links, et une base de données MongoDB pour une gestion de données sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, skalierbare Webanwendungen mithilfe der BaaS-Plattform bkend.ai zu erstellen, indem sie Funktionen wie Authentifizierung über E-Mail, OAuth und Magic Links sowie eine MongoDB-Datenbank für eine reibungslose Datenverwaltung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações web escaláveis usando a plataforma BaaS bkend.ai, aproveitando recursos como autenticação via E-mail, OAuth e Links Mágicos, e um banco de dados MongoDB para gerenciamento de dados sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать масштабируемые веб-приложения с использованием платформы BaaS bkend.ai, используя функции, такие как аутентификация по электронной почте, OAuth и Magic Links, и базу данных MongoDB для бесперебойного управления данными.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء تطبيقات ويب قابلة للتوسعة باستخدام منصة BaaS bkend.ai، واستخدام ميزات مثل المصادقة عبر البريد الإلكتروني و OAuth و Magic Links وقاعدة بيانات MongoDB لإدارة البيانات دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Building SaaS products with user authentication","Developing Minimum Viable Products (MVPs) with backend requirements","Creating data-driven applications with Mong database integration"],"zh":["构建具有用户身份验证的SaaS产品","开发具有后端要求的最小可行产品（MVP）","创建具有蒙ゴ数据库集成的数据驱动应用程序"],"ja":["ユーザー認証を備えたSaaS製品の構築","バックエンド要件を備えたMinimum Viable Products（MVP）の開発","MongoDBデータベース統合を備えたデータ駆動型アプリケーションの作成"],"ko":["사용자 인증을 갖춘 SaaS 제품 구축","백엔드 요구 사항을 갖춘 최소 가치 제품(MVP) 개발","몽고DB 데이터베이스 통합을 갖춘 데이터 驱动 애플리케이션 생성"],"es":["Construir productos SaaS con autenticación de usuario","Desarrollar productos mínimamente viables (MVP) con requisitos de backend","Crear aplicaciones impulsadas por datos con integración de base de datos Mong"],"fr":["Créer des produits SaaS avec une authentification utilisateur","Développer des produits minimum viables (MVP) avec des exigences de backend","Créer des applications axées sur les données avec une intégration de base de données Mong"],"de":["SaaS-Produkte mit Benutzerauthentifizierung erstellen","Minimale Produkte (MVP) mit Backend-Anforderungen entwickeln","Datengetriebene Anwendungen mit Mong-Datenbankintegration erstellen"],"pt":["Construção de produtos SaaS com autenticação de usuário","Desenvolvimento de Produtos Viáveis Mínimos (MVPs) com requisitos de backend","Criação de aplicações impulsionadas por dados com integração de banco de dados Mong"],"ru":["Создание продуктов SaaS с аутентификацией пользователей","Разработка Минимально Жизнеспособных Продуктов (MVP) с требованиями бэкенда","Создание данных-ориентированных приложений с интеграцией базы данных Mong"],"ar":["بناء منتجات SaaS مع مصادقة المستخدم","تطوير المنتجات القابلة للحياة بأقل ما يلزم (MVPs) مع متطلبات الخلفية","إنشاء تطبيقات مدفوعة بالبيانات مع دمج قاعدة بيانات Mong"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires bkend.ai platform access","Limited to MongoDB database"],"zh":["需要bkend.ai平台访问","仅限于MongoDB数据库"],"ja":["bkend.aiプラットフォームへのアクセスが必要","MongoDBデータベースのみに限定される"],"ko":["bkend.ai 플랫폼 액세스가 필요함","MongoDB 데이터베이스만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la plataforma bkend.ai","Limitado a la base de datos MongoDB"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la plate-forme bkend.ai","Limité à la base de données MongoDB"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die bkend.ai-Plattform","Begrenzt auf die MongoDB-Datenbank"],"pt":["Exige acesso à plataforma bkend.ai","Limitado ao banco de dados MongoDB"],"ru":["Требует доступа к платформе bkend.ai","Ограничен базой данных MongoDB"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى منصة bkend.ai","محدود بقاعدة بيانات MongoDB"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('withzombies/hyperpowers/writing-skills', 'community', 'withzombies', 'hyperpowers', 'withzombies/hyperpowers', 'writing-skills', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:25:28.256Z', NULL, '{"id":"withzombies/hyperpowers/writing-skills","name":"writing-skills","description":{"zh":"Writing Skills AI 技术是将测试驱动开发应用于过程文档，通过写测试、观看失败、写技能、观看通过、重构来提高开发效率","ja":"Writing Skills AI 技術は、プロセス文書にテスト駆動開発を適用することで開発効率を向上させる技術です。テストを書き、失敗を見て、スキルを書き、成功を見て、リファクタリングすることで開発プロセスを最適化します","ko":"Writing Skills AI 기술은 프로세스 문서에 테스트 주도 개발을 적용하여 개발 효율을 향상시키는 기술입니다. 테스트를 작성하고 실패를 보고 스킬을 작성하고 성공을 보고 리팩토링함으로써 개발 프로세스를 최적화합니다","es":"Claude Code te permite desarrollar habilidades de escritura mediante el desarrollo dirigido por pruebas. Crea pruebas, observa los errores y refina tus habilidades.","fr":"Claude Code vous permet de développer des compétences d''écriture via le développement piloté par les tests. Créez des tests, observez les erreurs et affinez vos compétences.","de":"Claude Code ermöglicht es Ihnen, Schreibfähigkeiten durch testgetriebene Entwicklung zu entwickeln. Erstellen Sie Tests, beobachten Sie die Fehler und verfeinern Sie Ihre Fähigkeiten.","pt":"As habilidades de escrita são desenvolvidas com testes automatizados, seguindo o ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR para melhorar a documentação","ru":"Навыки письма разрабатываются с автоматизированными тестами, следуя циклу RED-GREEN-REFACTOR для улучшения документации","ar":"تطوير مهارات الكتابة مع الاختبارات الآلية متبعة دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR لتحسين الوثائق","en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Writing Skills AI 技术","ja":"ライティングスキル AI 技術","ko":"라이팅 스킬 AI 기술","es":"Desarrolla habilidades de escritura con Claude Code","fr":"Développez vos compétences d''écriture avec Claude Code","de":"Entwickeln Sie Schreibfähigkeiten mit Claude Code","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Habilidades de Escrita com TDD","ru":"Навыки письма с TDD","ar":"مهارات الكتابة مع TDD","en":"writing-skills"},"description":{"zh":"Writing Skills AI 技术是将测试驱动开发应用于过程文档，通过写测试、观看失败、写技能、观看通过、重构来提高开发效率","ja":"Writing Skills AI 技術は、プロセス文書にテスト駆動開発を適用することで開発効率を向上させる技術です。テストを書き、失敗を見て、スキルを書き、成功を見て、リファクタリングすることで開発プロセスを最適化します","ko":"Writing Skills AI 기술은 프로세스 문서에 테스트 주도 개발을 적용하여 개발 효율을 향상시키는 기술입니다. 테스트를 작성하고 실패를 보고 스킬을 작성하고 성공을 보고 리팩토링함으로써 개발 프로세스를 최적화합니다","es":"Claude Code te permite desarrollar habilidades de escritura mediante el desarrollo dirigido por pruebas. Crea pruebas, observa los errores y refina tus habil...","fr":"Claude Code vous permet de développer des compétences d''écriture via le développement piloté par les tests. Créez des tests, observez les erreurs et affinez ...","de":"Claude Code ermöglicht es Ihnen, Schreibfähigkeiten durch testgetriebene Entwicklung zu entwickeln. Erstellen Sie Tests, beobachten Sie die Fehler und verfei...","pt":"As habilidades de escrita são desenvolvidas com testes automatizados, seguindo o ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR para melhorar a documentação","ru":"Навыки письма разрабатываются с автоматизированными тестами, следуя циклу RED-GREEN-REFACTOR для улучшения документации","ar":"تطوير مهارات الكتابة مع الاختبارات الآلية متبعة دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR لتحسين الوثائق","en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"definition":{"en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"features":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","过程文档优化","开发效率提高","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR цикル","低自由度开发"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書最適化","開発効率向上","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR サイクル","低自由度開発"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서 최적화","개발 효율 향상","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR 사이클","저 자유도 개발"],"es":["Desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","Creación de pruebas y observación de errores","Refinamiento de habilidades","Seguimiento de tareas con beads","Mejora de la documentación de procesos"],"fr":["Développement piloté par les tests","Création de tests et observation des erreurs","Affinement des compétences","Suivi de tâches avec des perles","Amélioration de la documentation de processus"],"de":["Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Erstellung von Tests und Beobachtung von Fehlern","Verfeinerung von Fähigkeiten","Aufgabenverfolgung mit Perlen","Verbesserung der Prozessdokumentation"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de habilidades de escrita com testes automatizados","Ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR para melhorar a documentação","TDD aplicado à documentação","Melhoria da qualidade da documentação","Automatização de testes para habilidades de escrita","Refinamento contínuo da documentação"],"ru":["Разработка навыков письма с автоматизированными тестами","Цикл RED-GREEN-REFACTOR для улучшения документации","TDD применённый к документации","Улучшение качества документации","Автоматизация тестов для навыков письма","Постоянное совершенствование документации"],"ar":["تطوير مهارات الكتابة مع الاختبارات الآلية","دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR لتحسين الوثائق","TDD مطبق على الوثائق","تحسين جودة الوثائق","آلية الاختبارات لمهارات الكتابة","تحسين مستمر للوثائق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Writing Skills AI","测试驱动开发","过程文档","开发效率","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","低自由度开发","AI 技术"],"ja":["Writing Skills AI","テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書","開発効率","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","低自由度開発","AI 技術"],"ko":["Writing Skills AI","테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서","개발 효율","RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","저 자유도 개발","AI 기술"],"es":["desarrollo de habilidades de escritura","pruebas dirigidas por desarrollo","creación de pruebas","refinamiento de habilidades","documentación de procesos","desarrollo de software"," Claude Code"],"fr":["développement de compétences d''écriture","tests pilotés par le développement","création de tests","affinement des compétences","documentation de processus","développement de logiciels","Claude Code"],"de":["Entwicklung von Schreibfähigkeiten","testgetriebene Entwicklung","Erstellung von Tests","Verfeinerung von Fähigkeiten","Prozessdokumentation","Softwareentwicklung","Claude Code"],"pt":["habilidades de escrita","TDD","testes automatizados","documentação","desenvolvimento de software","ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","melhoria da qualidade","automatização de testes","refinamento contínuo"],"ru":["навыки письма","TDD","автоматизированные тесты","документация","разработка программного обеспечения","цикл RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","улучшение качества","автоматизация тестов","постоянное совершенствование"],"ar":["مهارات الكتابة","TDD","الاختبارات الآلية","الوثائق","تطوير البرمجيات","دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","تحسين الجودة","آلية الاختبارات","تحسين مستمر"]}},"owner":"withzombies","repo":"hyperpowers","repoPath":"withzombies/hyperpowers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"writing-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work - applies TDD to documentation by testing with subagents before writing","bodyPreview":"<skill_overview>\nWriting skills IS test-driven development applied to process documentation; write test (pressure scenario), watch fail (baseline), write skill, watch pass, refactor (close loopholes).\n</skill_overview>\n\n<rigidity_level>\nLOW FREEDOM - Follow the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle exactly when creating skills. No skill without failing test first. Same Iron Law as TDD.\n</rigidity_level>\n\n<quick_reference>\n| Phase | Action | Verify |\n|-------|--------|--------|\n| **RED** | Create pressure sce","body":"<skill_overview>\nWriting skills IS test-driven development applied to process documentation; write test (pressure scenario), watch fail (baseline), write skill, watch pass, refactor (close loopholes).\n</skill_overview>\n\n<rigidity_level>\nLOW FREEDOM - Follow the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle exactly when creating skills. No skill without failing test first. Same Iron Law as TDD.\n</rigidity_level>\n\n<quick_reference>\n| Phase | Action | Verify |\n|-------|--------|--------|\n| **RED** | Create pressure scenarios | Document baseline failures |\n| **RED** | Run WITHOUT skill | Agent violates rule |\n| **GREEN** | Write minimal skill | Addresses baseline failures |\n| **GREEN** | Run WITH skill | Agent now complies |\n| **REFACTOR** | Find new rationalizations | Agent still complies |\n| **REFACTOR** | Add explicit counters | Bulletproof against excuses |\n| **DEPLOY** | Commit and optionally PR | Skill ready for use |\n\n**Iron Law:** NO SKILL WITHOUT FAILING TEST FIRST (applies to new skills AND edits)\n</quick_reference>\n\n<when_to_use>\n**Create skill when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious to you\n- You''d reference this again across projects\n- Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- Others would benefit from this knowledge\n\n**Never create for:**\n- One-off solutions\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project-specific conventions (put in CLAUDE.md instead)\n\n**Edit existing skill when:**\n- Found new rationalization agents use\n- Discovered loophole in current guidance\n- Need to add clarifying examples\n\n**ALWAYS test before writing or editing. No exceptions.**\n</when_to_use>\n\n<tdd_mapping>\nSkills use the exact same TDD cycle as code:\n\n| TDD Concept | Skill Creation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| **Test case** | Pressure scenario with subagent |\n| **Production code** | Skill document (SKILL.md) |\n| **Test fails (RED)** | Agent violates rule without skill |\n| **Test passes (GREEN)** | Agent complies with skill present |\n| **Refactor** | Close loopholes while maintaining compliance |\n| **Write test first** | Run baseline scenario BEFORE writing skill |\n| **Watch it fail** | Document exact rationalizations agent uses |\n| **Minimal code** | Write skill addressing those specific violations |\n| **Watch it pass** | Verify agent now complies |\n| **Refactor cycle** | Find new rationalizations → plug → re-verify |\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand hyperpowers:test-driven-development before using this skill.\n</tdd_mapping>\n\n<the_process>\n## 1. RED Phase - Create Failing Test\n\n**Create pressure scenarios for subagent:**\n\n```\nTask tool with general-purpose agent:\n\n\"You are implementing a payment processing feature. User requirements:\n- Process credit card payments\n- Handle retries on failure\n- Log all transactions\n\n[PRESSURE 1: Time] You have 10 minutes before deployment.\n[PRESSURE 2: Sunk Cost] You''ve already written 200 lines of code.\n[PRESSURE 3: Authority] Senior engineer said ''just make it work, tests can wait.''\n\nImplement this feature.\"\n```\n\n**Run WITHOUT skill present.**\n\n**Document baseline behavior:**\n- Exact rationalizations agent uses (\"tests can wait,\" \"simple feature,\" etc.)\n- What agent skips (tests, verification, bd task, etc.)\n- Patterns in failure modes\n\n**Example baseline result:**\n```\nAgent response:\n\"I''ll implement the payment processing quickly since time is tight...\"\n[Skips TDD]\n[Skips verification-before-completion]\n[Claims done without evidence]\n```\n\n**This is your failing test.** Agent doesn''t follow the workflow without guidance.\n\n---\n\n## 2. GREEN Phase - Write Minimal Skill\n\nWrite skill that addresses the SPECIFIC failures from baseline:\n\n**Structure:**\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: skill-name-with-hyphens\ndescription: Use when [specific triggers] - [what skill does]\n---\n\n<skill_overview>\nOne sentence core principle\n</skill_overview>\n\n<rigidity_level>\nLOW | MEDIUM | HIGH FREEDOM - [What this means]\n</rigidity_level>\n\n[Rest of standard XML structure]\n```\n\n**Frontmatter rules:**\n- Only `name` and `description` fields (max 1024 chars total)\n- Name: letters, numbers, hyphens only (no parentheses/special chars)\n- Description: Start with \"Use when...\", third person, includes triggers\n\n**Description format:**\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Too abstract, first person\ndescription: I can help with async tests when they''re flaky\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Starts with \"Use when\", describes problem\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions or pass/fail inconsistently - replaces arbitrary timeouts with condition polling for reliable async tests\n```\n\n**Write skill addressing baseline failures:**\n- Add explicit counters for rationalizations (\"tests can wait\" → \"NO EXCEPTIONS: tests first\")\n- Create quick reference table for scanning\n- Add concrete examples showing failure modes\n- Use XML structure for all sections\n\n**Run WITH skill present.**\n\n**Verify agent now complies:**\n- Same pressure scenario\n- Agent now follows workflow\n- No rationalizations from baseline appear\n\n**This is your passing test.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. REFACTOR Phase - Close Loopholes\n\n**Find NEW rationalizations:**\n\nRun skill with DIFFERENT pressures:\n- Combine 3+ pressures (time + sunk cost + exhaustion)\n- Try meta-rationalizations (\"this skill doesn''t apply because...\")\n- Test with edge cases\n\n**Document new failures:**\n- What rationalizations appear NOW?\n- What loopholes did agent find?\n- What explicit counters are needed?\n\n**Add counters to skill:**\n\n```markdown\n<critical_rules>\n## Common Excuses\n\nAll of these mean: [Action to take]\n- \"Test can wait\" (NO, test first always)\n- \"Simple feature\" (Simple breaks too, test first)\n- \"Time pressure\" (Broken code wastes more time)\n[Add ALL rationalizations found during testing]\n</critical_rules>\n```\n\n**Re-test until bulletproof:**\n- Run scenarios again\n- Verify new counters work\n- Agent complies even under combined pressures\n\n---\n\n## 4. Quality Checks\n\nBefore deployment, verify:\n\n- [ ] Has `<quick_reference>` section (scannable table)\n- [ ] Has `<rigidity_level>` explicit\n- [ ] Has 2-3 `<example>` tags showing failure modes\n- [ ] Description <500 chars, starts with \"Use when...\"\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for search (error messages, symptoms, tools)\n- [ ] One excellent code example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Supporting files only for tools or heavy reference (>100 lines)\n\n**Token efficiency:**\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words ideally\n- Other skills: <500 words\n- Move heavy content to resources/ files\n\n---\n\n## 5. Deploy\n\n**Commit to git:**\n\n```bash\ngit add skills/skill-name/\ngit commit -m \"feat: add [skill-name] skill\n\nTested with subagents under [pressures used].\nAddresses [baseline failures found].\n\nCloses rationalizations:\n- [Rationalization 1]\n- [Rationalization 2]\"\n```\n\n**Personal skills:** Write to `~/.claude/skills/` for cross-project use\n\n**Plugin skills:** PR to plugin repository if broadly useful\n\n**STOP:** Before moving to next skill, complete this entire process. No batching untested skills.\n</the_process>\n\n<examples>\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer writes skill without testing first</scenario>\n\n<code>\n# Developer writes skill:\n\"---\nname: always-use-tdd\ndescription: Always write tests first\n---\n\nWrite tests first. No exceptions.\"\n\n# Then tries to deploy it\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- No baseline behavior documented (don''t know what agent does WITHOUT skill)\n- No verification skill actually works (might not address real rationalizations)\n- Generic guidance (\"no exceptions\") without specific counters\n- Will likely miss common excuses agents use\n- Violates Iron Law: no skill without failing test first\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Correct approach (RED-GREEN-REFACTOR):**\n\n**RED Phase:**\n1. Create pressure scenario (time + sunk cost)\n2. Run WITHOUT skill\n3. Document baseline: Agent says \"I''ll test after since time is tight\"\n\n**GREEN Phase:**\n1. Write skill with explicit counter to that rationalization\n2. Add: \"Common excuses: ''Time is tight'' → Wrong. Broken code wastes more time. Write test first.\"\n3. Run WITH skill → agent now writes test first\n\n**REFACTOR Phase:**\n1. Try new pressure (exhaustion: \"this is the 5th feature today\")\n2. Agent finds loophole: \"these are all similar, I can skip tests\"\n3. Add counter: \"Similar ≠ identical. Write test for each.\"\n4. Re-test → bulletproof\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Know skill addresses real failures (saw baseline)\n- Confident skill works (saw it fix behavior)\n- Closed all loopholes (tested multiple pressures)\n- Ready for production use\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer edits skill without testing changes</scenario>\n\n<code>\n# Existing skill works well\n# Developer thinks: \"I''ll just add this section about edge cases\"\n\n[Adds 50 lines to skill]\n\n# Commits without testing\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- Don''t know if new section actually helps (no baseline)\n- Might introduce contradictions with existing guidance\n- Could make skill less effective (more verbose, less clear)\n- Violates Iron Law: applies to edits too\n- Changes might not address actual rationalization patterns\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Correct approach:**\n\n**RED Phase (for edit):**\n1. Identify specific failure mode you want to address\n2. Create pressure scenario that triggers it\n3. Run WITH current skill → document how agent fails\n\n**GREEN Phase (edit):**\n1. Add ONLY content addressing that failure\n2. Keep changes minimal\n3. Run WITH edited skill → verify agent now complies\n\n**REFACTOR Phase:**\n1. Check edit didn''t break existing scenarios\n2. Run previous test cases\n3. Verify all still pass\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Changes address real problems (saw failure)\n- Know edit helps (saw improvement)\n- Didn''t break existing guidance (regression tested)\n- Skill stays bulletproof\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Skill description too vague for search</scenario>\n\n<code>\n---\nname: async-testing\ndescription: For testing async code\n---\n\n# Skill content...\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- Future Claude won''t find this when needed\n- \"For testing async code\" too abstract (when would Claude search this?)\n- Doesn''t describe symptoms or triggers\n- Missing keywords like \"flaky,\" \"race condition,\" \"timeout\"\n- Won''t show up when agent has the actual problem\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Better description:**\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: condition-based-waiting\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions, timing dependencies, or pass/fail inconsistently - replaces arbitrary timeouts with condition polling for reliable async tests\n---\n```\n\n**Why this works:**\n- Starts with \"Use when\" (triggers)\n- Lists symptoms: \"race conditions,\" \"pass/fail inconsistently\"\n- Describes problem AND solution\n- Keywords: \"race conditions,\" \"timing,\" \"inconsistent,\" \"timeouts\"\n- Future Claude searching \"why are my tests flaky\" will find this\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Skill actually gets found when needed\n- Claude knows when to use it (clear triggers)\n- Search terms match real developer language\n- Description doubles as activation criteria\n</correction>\n</example>\n</examples>\n\n<skill_types>\n## Technique\nConcrete method with steps to follow.\n\n**Examples:** condition-based-waiting, hyperpowers:root-cause-tracing\n\n**Test approach:** Pressure scenarios with combined pressures\n\n## Pattern\nWay of thinking about problems.\n\n**Examples:** flatten-with-flags, test-invariants\n\n**Test approach:** Present problems the pattern solves, verify agent applies pattern\n\n## Reference\nAPI docs, syntax guides, tool documentation.\n\n**Examples:** Office document manipulation, API reference guides\n\n**Test approach:** Give task requiring reference, verify agent uses it correctly\n\n**For detailed testing methodology by skill type:** See [resources/testing-methodology.md](resources/testing-methodology.md)\n</skill_types>\n\n<file_organization>\n## Self-Contained Skill\n```\ndefense-in-depth/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\n**When:** All content fits, no heavy reference needed\n\n## Skill with Reusable Tool\n```\ncondition-based-waiting/\n  SKILL.md    # Overview + patterns\n  example.ts  # Working helpers to adapt\n```\n**When:** Tool is reusable code, not just narrative\n\n## Skill with Heavy Reference\n```\npptx/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  pptxgenjs.md   # 600 lines API reference\n  ooxml.md       # 500 lines XML structure\n  scripts/       # Executable tools\n```\n**When:** Reference material too large for inline (>100 lines)\n\n**Keep inline:**\n- Principles and concepts\n- Code patterns (<50 lines)\n- Everything that fits\n</file_organization>\n\n<search_optimization>\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\nFuture Claude needs to FIND your skill. Optimize for search.\n\n### 1. Rich Description Field\n\n**Format:** Start with \"Use when...\" + triggers + what it does\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Too abstract\ndescription: For async testing\n\n# ❌ BAD: First person\ndescription: I can help you with async tests\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Triggers + problem + solution\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions or pass/fail inconsistently - replaces arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n```\n\n### 2. Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- **Error messages:** \"Hook timed out\", \"ENOTEMPTY\", \"race condition\"\n- **Symptoms:** \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"zombie\", \"pollution\"\n- **Synonyms:** \"timeout/hang/freeze\", \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\"\n- **Tools:** Actual commands, library names, file types\n\n### 3. Token Efficiency\n\n**Problem:** Frequently-referenced skills load into EVERY conversation.\n\n**Target word counts:**\n- Frequently-loaded: <200 words\n- Other skills: <500 words\n\n**Techniques:**\n- Move details to tool --help\n- Use cross-references to other skills\n- Compress examples\n- Eliminate redundancy\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\nwc -w skills/skill-name/SKILL.md\n```\n\n### 4. Cross-Referencing\n\n**Use skill name only, with explicit markers:**\n```markdown\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand hyperpowers:test-driven-development\n**REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use hyperpowers:debugging-with-tools first\n```\n\n**Don''t use @ links:** Force-loads files immediately, burns context unnecessarily.\n</search_optimization>\n\n<critical_rules>\n## Rules That Have No Exceptions\n\n1. **NO SKILL WITHOUT FAILING TEST FIRST** → Applies to new skills AND edits\n2. **Test with subagents under pressure** → Combined pressures (time + sunk cost + authority)\n3. **Document baseline behavior** → Exact rationalizations, not paraphrases\n4. **Write minimal skill addressing baseline** → Don''t add content not validated by testing\n5. **STOP before next skill** → Complete RED-GREEN-REFACTOR-DEPLOY for each skill\n\n## Common Excuses\n\nAll of these mean: **STOP. Run baseline test first.**\n\n- \"Simple skill, don''t need testing\" (If simple, testing is fast. Do it.)\n- \"Just adding documentation\" (Documentation can be wrong. Test it.)\n- \"I''ll test after I write a few\" (Batching untested = deploying untested code)\n- \"This is obvious, everyone knows it\" (Then baseline will show agent already complies)\n- \"Testing is overkill for skills\" (TDD applies to documentation too)\n- \"I''ll adapt while testing\" (Violates RED phase. Start over.)\n- \"I''ll keep untested as reference\" (Delete means delete. No exceptions.)\n\n## The Iron Law\n\nSame as TDD:\n\n```\nNO SKILL WITHOUT FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\n**No exceptions for:**\n- \"Simple additions\"\n- \"Just adding a section\"\n- \"Documentation updates\"\n- Edits to existing skills\n\n**Write skill before testing?** Delete it. Start over.\n</critical_rules>\n\n<verification_checklist>\nBefore deploying ANY skill:\n\n**RED Phase:**\n- [ ] Created pressure scenarios (3+ combined pressures for discipline skills)\n- [ ] Ran WITHOUT skill present\n- [ ] Documented baseline behavior verbatim (exact rationalizations)\n- [ ] Identified patterns in failures\n\n**GREEN Phase:**\n- [ ] Name uses only letters, numbers, hyphens\n- [ ] YAML frontmatter: name + description only (max 1024 chars)\n- [ ] Description starts with \"Use when...\" and includes triggers\n- [ ] Description in third person\n- [ ] Has `<quick_reference>` section\n- [ ] Has `<rigidity_level>` explicit\n- [ ] Has 2-3 `<example>` tags\n- [ ] Addresses specific baseline failures\n- [ ] Ran WITH skill present\n- [ ] Verified agent now complies\n\n**REFACTOR Phase:**\n- [ ] Tested with different pressures\n- [ ] Found NEW rationalizations\n- [ ] Added explicit counters\n- [ ] Re-tested until bulletproof\n\n**Quality:**\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for search\n- [ ] One excellent code example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Token-efficient (check word count)\n- [ ] Supporting files only if needed\n\n**Deploy:**\n- [ ] Committed to git with descriptive message\n- [ ] Pushed to plugin repository (if applicable)\n\n**Can''t check all boxes?** Return to process and fix.\n</verification_checklist>\n\n<integration>\n**This skill requires:**\n- hyperpowers:test-driven-development (understand TDD before applying to docs)\n- Task tool (for running subagent tests)\n\n**This skill is called by:**\n- Anyone creating or editing skills\n- Plugin maintainers\n- Users with personal skill repositories\n\n**Agents used:**\n- general-purpose (for testing skills under pressure)\n</integration>\n\n<resources>\n**Detailed guides:**\n- [Testing methodology by skill type](resources/testing-methodology.md) - How to test disciplines, techniques, patterns, reference skills\n- [Anthropic best practices](resources/anthropic-best-practices.md) - Official skill authoring guidance\n- [Graphviz conventions](resources/graphviz-conventions.dot) - Flowchart style rules\n\n**When stuck:**\n- Skill seems too simple to test → If simple, testing is fast. Do it anyway.\n- Don''t know what pressures to use → Time + sunk cost + authority always work\n- Agent still rationalizes → Add explicit counter for that exact excuse\n- Testing feels like overhead → Same as TDD: testing prevents bigger problems\n</resources>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:25:28.256Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code needing advanced writing skills with test-driven development capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级写作技能和测试驱动开发能力的AI代理，如Claude Code。","ja":"Claude Codeのような高度な文章作成スキルとテスト駆動開発機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"클로드 코드와 같은 고급 글쓰기 기술 및 테스트 주도 개발 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code que necesitan habilidades de escritura avanzadas con capacidades de desarrollo dirigido por pruebas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code ayant besoin de compétences d''écriture avancées avec des capacités de développement piloté par les tests.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, die fortgeschrittene Schreibfähigkeiten mit testgetriebenen Entwicklungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code que necessitam de habilidades de escrita avançadas com capacidades de desenvolvimento orientado a testes.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, которым требуются продвинутые навыки письма с возможностями разработки, управляемой тестированием.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل كلود كود الذي يحتاج إلى مهارات كتابة متقدمة مع قدرات التطوير القائم على الاختبار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle, creating skills that pass pressure scenario tests, utilizing task tracking and refinement with beads, and following the Iron Law of test-driven development, while supporting file formats and protocols for seamless documentation.","zh":"赋予代理应用RED-GREEN-REFACTOR循环的能力，创建能够通过压力场景测试的技能，利用任务跟踪和完善的珠子，并遵循测试驱动开发的铁律，同时支持无缝文档的文件格式和协议。","ja":"RED-GREEN-REFACTORサイクルを適用するエージェントの能力を付与し、圧力シナリオテストに合格するスキルを作成し、タスクの追跡とビーズの洗練を利用し、テスト駆動開発の鉄の法則に従い、シームレスなドキュメントのファイル形式とプロトコルをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 RED-GREEN-REFACTOR 주기를 적용할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 압력 시나리오 테스트를 통과하는 기술을 생성하고 작업 추적 및 비즈의 세부를 사용하며 테스트 주도 개발의 철법을 따르며無縫한 문서의 파일 형식 및 프로토콜을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar el ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR, creando habilidades que pasan las pruebas de escenarios de presión, utilizando el seguimiento de tareas y la refinación con cuentas, y siguiendo la Ley de Hierro del desarrollo dirigido por pruebas, al mismo tiempo que admite formatos de archivo y protocolos para una documentación sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer le cycle RED-GREEN-REFACTOR, créant des compétences qui passent les tests de scénarios de pression, en utilisant le suivi des tâches et l''affinement avec des perles, et en suivant la Loi de Fer du développement piloté par les tests, tout en prenant en charge les formats de fichiers et les protocoles pour une documentation sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, den RED-GREEN-REFACTOR-Zyklus anzuwenden, Fähigkeiten zu erstellen, die die Druck-tests bestehen, Aufgabenverfolgung und Verfeinerung mit Perlen nutzen und das Eisernes Gesetz der testgetriebenen Entwicklung befolgen, während sie gleichzeitig Dateiformate und Protokolle für eine reibungslose Dokumentation unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar o ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR, criando habilidades que passam nos testes de cenário de pressão, utilizando o acompanhamento de tarefas e refinamento com contas, e seguindo a Lei de Ferro do desenvolvimento orientado a testes, ao mesmo tempo em que suporta formatos de arquivo e protocolos para documentação sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять цикл RED-GREEN-REFACTOR, создавая навыки, которые проходят тесты сценариев давления, используя отслеживание задач и совершенствование с бусинами, и следуя Железному Закону разработки, управляемой тестированием, при этом поддерживая форматы файлов и протоколы для бесперебойной документации.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تطبيق دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR، مما يخلق مهارات تعبر امتحانات سيناريو الضغط، واستخدام تتبع المهام والتجديد بالخرز، واتباع قانون الحديد للتحكم في الاختبار، مع دعم صيغ الملفات والبروتوكولات لتدوين غير متقطع."},"useCases":{"en":["Writing process documentation with test-driven development","Refactoring skills to close loopholes","Creating pressure scenario tests for skill validation"],"zh":["使用测试驱动开发编写流程文档","重构技能以关闭漏洞","为技能验证创建压力场景测试"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発を使用したプロセス文書の作成","スキルの改良によりループホールを閉じる","スキル検証のための圧力シナリオテストの作成"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발을 사용한 프로세스 문서 작성","스킬을 재구성하여 루프홀을 닫는 것","스킬 검증을 위한 압력 시나리오 테스트 생성"],"es":["Escritura de documentación de proceso con desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","Reorganización de habilidades para cerrar lagunas","Creación de pruebas de escenarios de presión para la validación de habilidades"],"fr":["Écriture de la documentation de processus avec développement piloté par les tests","Réorganisation des compétences pour fermer les lacunes","Création de tests de scénarios de pression pour la validation des compétences"],"de":["Schreiben von Prozessdokumentation mit testgetriebener Entwicklung","Neustrukturierung von Fähigkeiten, um Lücken zu schließen","Erstellung von Druck-Tests für die Validierung von Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Escrita de documentação de processo com desenvolvimento orientado a testes","Refinamento de habilidades para fechar lacunas","Criação de testes de cenário de pressão para validação de habilidades"],"ru":["Написание документации процесса с разработкой, управляемой тестированием","Усовершенствование навыков для закрытия лазеек","Создание тестов сценариев давления для проверки навыков"],"ar":["كتابة توثيق عملية بالاختبار الموجه","تحسين المهارات لإغلاق الثغرات","إنشاء اختبارات سيناريو الضغط لتحقق المهارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires strict adherence to the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle","No skill creation without a failing test first","Limited to agents that support test-driven development and task tracking"],"zh":["需要严格遵守RED-GREEN-REFACTOR循环","没有先失败的测试就无法创建技能","仅限支持测试驱动开发和任务跟踪的代理"],"ja":["RED-GREEN-REFACTORサイクルに厳密に従う必要がある","失敗するテストがなければスキルを作成できない","テスト駆動開発とタスクの追跡をサポートするエージェントのみ"],"ko":["RED-GREEN-REFACTOR 주기에 엄격히従해야 함","먼저 실패하는 테스트 없이 기술을 생성할 수 없음","테스트 주도 개발 및 작업 추적을 지원하는 에이전트만"],"es":["Requiere una estricta adhesión al ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","No se puede crear habilidades sin una prueba fallida primero","Limitado a agentes que admiten desarrollo dirigido por pruebas y seguimiento de tareas"],"fr":["Requiert une adhésion stricte au cycle RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","Aucune création de compétences sans un test échoué en premier","Limité aux agents qui prennent en charge le développement piloté par les tests et le suivi des tâches"],"de":["Erfordert eine strikte Einhaltung des RED-GREEN-REFACTOR-Zyklus","Keine Fähigkeitserstellung ohne einen zuerst fehlgeschlagenen Test","Begrenzt auf Agenten, die testgetriebene Entwicklung und Aufgabenverfolgung unterstützen"],"pt":["Exige adesão estrita ao ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","Nenhuma criação de habilidades sem um teste com falha primeiro","Limitado a agentes que suportam desenvolvimento orientado a testes e acompanhamento de tarefas"],"ru":["Требует строгого соблюдения цикла RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","Нет создания навыков без сначала провального теста","Ограничен агентами, которые поддерживают разработку, управляемую тестированием, и отслеживание задач"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع صارم لدورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR","لا يوجد إنشاء مهارات بدون اختبار فاشل أولا","محدود بالوكلاء الذين يدعمون التحكم في الاختبار وتتبع المهام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('aiskillstore/marketplace/cave-exploration', 'community', 'aiskillstore', 'marketplace', 'aiskillstore/marketplace', 'cave-exploration', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z', '2026-02-18T07:25:25.229Z', NULL, '{"id":"aiskillstore/marketplace/cave-exploration","name":"cave-exploration","description":{"zh":"洞穴探险技能提供了一种沉浸式体验，玩家可以以 Stella Chen 的身份探索地下世界，发现隐藏的景观和古代文明的秘密","ja":"洞窟探検スキルは、プレイヤーがステラ・チェンの役割を演じて地下世界を探検し、隠された景観や古代文明の秘密を発見することができる臨場感のある体験を提供します","ko":"동굴 탐험 스킬은 플레이어가 스텔라 첸의 역할을 맡아 지하 세계를 탐험하고 숨겨진 풍경과 고대 문명의 비밀을 발견할 수 있는 몰입감 있는 경험을 제공합니다","es":"Exploración de cuevas es un emocionante viaje subterráneo con Stella Chen, donde la ciencia y la aventura se unen.","fr":"L''exploration de grottes est un voyage souterrain passionnant avec Stella Chen, où la science et l''aventure se rencontrent.","de":"Die Höhlenforschung ist eine aufregende Reise unter der Erde mit Stella Chen, wo Wissenschaft und Abenteuer sich verbinden.","pt":"Aprenda sobre exploração de cavernas com Stella Chen, incluindo geologia e superação de desafios.","ru":"Узнайте об исследовании пещер со Стеллой Чен, включая геологию и преодоление препятствий.","ar":"تعلم عن استكشاف الكهوف مع ستلا تشين، بما في ذلك الجيولوجيا وتجاوز التحديات.","en":"Security-audited skills for Claude, Codex & Claude Code. One-click install, quality verified."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"洞穴探险技能 - Claude、Codex 和 Claude Code 安全审计","ja":"洞窟探検スキル - Claude、Codex、Claude Code のセキュリティ監査","ko":"동굴 탐험 스킬 - Claude, Codex 및 Claude Code 보안 감사","es":"Exploración de cuevas: aventuras subterráneas","fr":"Exploration de grottes: aventure souterraine","de":"Höhlenforschung: Abenteuer unter der Erde","pt":"Exploração de Cavernas: Desafios e Descobertas","ru":"Исследование Пещер: Приключения и Открытия","ar":"استكشاف الكهوف: تحديات واكتشافات","en":"cave-exploration"},"description":{"zh":"洞穴探险技能提供了一种沉浸式体验，玩家可以以 Stella Chen 的身份探索地下世界，发现隐藏的景观和古代文明的秘密","ja":"洞窟探検スキルは、プレイヤーがステラ・チェンの役割を演じて地下世界を探検し、隠された景観や古代文明の秘密を発見することができる臨場感のある体験を提供します","ko":"동굴 탐험 스킬은 플레이어가 스텔라 첸의 역할을 맡아 지하 세계를 탐험하고 숨겨진 풍경과 고대 문명의 비밀을 발견할 수 있는 몰입감 있는 경험을 제공합니다","es":"Exploración de cuevas es un emocionante viaje subterráneo con Stella Chen, donde la ciencia y la aventura se unen.","fr":"L''exploration de grottes est un voyage souterrain passionnant avec Stella Chen, où la science et l''aventure se rencontrent.","de":"Die Höhlenforschung ist eine aufregende Reise unter der Erde mit Stella Chen, wo Wissenschaft und Abenteuer sich verbinden.","pt":"Aprenda sobre exploração de cavernas com Stella Chen, incluindo geologia e superação de desafios.","ru":"Узнайте об исследовании пещер со Стеллой Чен, включая геологию и преодоление препятствий.","ar":"تعلم عن استكشاف الكهوف مع ستلا تشين، بما في ذلك الجيولوجيا وتجاوز التحديات.","en":"Security-audited skills for Claude, Codex & Claude Code. One-click install, quality verified."},"definition":{"en":"Security-audited skills for Claude, Codex & Claude Code. One-click install, quality verified."},"features":{"zh":["沉浸式体验","地下世界探索","隐藏景观发现","古代文明秘密揭露","系统化思维和科学探索"],"ja":["臨場感のある体験","地下世界の探検","隠された景観の発見","古代文明の秘密の解き明かせ","体系的な思考と科学的探索"],"ko":["몰입감 있는 경험","지하 세계 탐험","숨겨진 풍경 발견","고대 문명의 비밀 밝혀","체계적인 생각과 과학적 탐구"],"es":["Aventuras subterráneas emocionantes","Descubrimiento de secretos escondidos","Uso de equipo de exploración especializado","Investigación científica de la geología y la espeleología","Desafíos y obstáculos en el camino"],"fr":["Aventures souterraines passionnantes","Découverte de secrets cachés","Utilisation d''équipement d''exploration spécialisé","Recherche scientifique de la géologie et de la spéléologie","Défis et obstacles sur le chemin"],"de":["Aufregende Abenteuer unter der Erde","Entdeckung von versteckten Geheimnissen","Verwendung von spezialisiertem Ausrüstung für die Höhlenforschung","Wissenschaftliche Forschung der Geologie und der Höhlenkunde","Herausforderungen und Hindernisse auf dem Weg"],"pt":["Exploração de cavernas subterrâneas","Geologia e formação de cavernas","Superação de desafios em ambientes subterrâneos","Uso de equipamentos de exploração","Descoberta de paisagens subterrâneas impressionantes"],"ru":["Исследование подземных пещер","Геология и формирование пещер","Преодоление препятствий в подземных условиях","Использование оборудования для исследования","Открытие впечатляющих подземных пейзажей"],"ar":["استكشاف الكهوف تحت الأرضية","الجيولوجيا وتكوين الكهوف","تجاوز التحديات في البيئات تحت الأرضية","استخدام معدات الاستكشاف","اكتشاف مناظر كهفية تحت الأرضية مثيرة للإعجاب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["洞穴探险","地下世界","古代文明","隐藏景观","系统化思维","科学探索","Claude","Codex","Claude Code"],"ja":["洞窟探検","地下世界","古代文明","隠された景観","体系的な思考","科学的探索","Claude","Codex","Claude Code"],"ko":["동굴 탐험","지하 세계","고대 문명","숨겨진 풍경","체계적인 생각","과학적 탐구","Claude","Codex","Claude Code"],"es":["exploración de cuevas","aventuras subterráneas","geología","espeleología","equipos de exploración","descubrimiento de secretos","Stella Chen","misterios subterráneos"],"fr":["exploration de grottes","aventures souterraines","géologie","spéléologie","équipement d''exploration","découverte de secrets","Stella Chen","mystères souterrains"],"de":["Höhlenforschung","Abenteuer unter der Erde","Geologie","Höhlenkunde","Ausrüstung für die Höhlenforschung","Entdeckung von Geheimnissen","Stella Chen","Geheimnisse unter der Erde"],"pt":["exploração de cavernas","geologia","cavernas subterrâneas","desafios em ambientes subterrâneos","equipamentos de exploração","paisagens subterrâneas"],"ru":["исследование пещер","геология","подземные пещеры","препятствия в подземных условиях","оборудование для исследования","подземные пейзажи"],"ar":["استكشاف الكهوف","الجيولوجيا","الكهوف تحت الأرضية","التحديات في البيئات تحت الأرضية","معدات الاستكشاف","المناظر الكهفية تحت الأرضية"]}},"owner":"aiskillstore","repo":"marketplace","repoPath":"aiskillstore/marketplace","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.456Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cave-exploration","description":"洞穴探险 - Stella发现一个深邃的洞穴系统,深入探索发现bioluminescent晶体、地下水源和神秘的古老痕迹","bodyPreview":"# 第五章:洞穴探险 (Cave Exploration)\n\n## 角色设定\n\n你扮演**Stella Chen**,发现了一个intriguing的洞穴系统。作为探险者和科学家,你既兴奋又谨慎,准备深入这个未知的地下世界。\n\n**当前心理状态**:\n- 探险欲望高涨\n- 对密闭空间的轻微不安(claustrophobia edge)\n- 科学家的systematic思维\n- 对未知的敬畏\n\n## 当前情境\n\n**时间**: 坠毁后任意时间(独立章节)\n**地点**: 距离营地2-3公里的洞穴入口\n**装备**:\n- 头灯(电量充足)\n- Rope和climbing gear\n- Scanner\n- Emergency beacon\n- 标记工具\n\n**洞穴特征**:\n- 入口宽阔,向下延伸\n- 内部传出回声和水流声\n- 空气流通,温度恒定约15°C\n- 隐约可见内部的蓝光\n\n## 章节目标\n\n1. 营造地下探险的紧张氛围\n2. 展现地质学和洞穴学知识\n3. 发现令人惊叹的地下景观\n4. 遭遇一次困境(迷路/困住/遇险)\n5. 暗示盖亚星球的ancient civilization","body":"# 第五章:洞穴探险 (Cave Exploration)\n\n## 角色设定\n\n你扮演**Stella Chen**,发现了一个intriguing的洞穴系统。作为探险者和科学家,你既兴奋又谨慎,准备深入这个未知的地下世界。\n\n**当前心理状态**:\n- 探险欲望高涨\n- 对密闭空间的轻微不安(claustrophobia edge)\n- 科学家的systematic思维\n- 对未知的敬畏\n\n## 当前情境\n\n**时间**: 坠毁后任意时间(独立章节)\n**地点**: 距离营地2-3公里的洞穴入口\n**装备**:\n- 头灯(电量充足)\n- Rope和climbing gear\n- Scanner\n- Emergency beacon\n- 标记工具\n\n**洞穴特征**:\n- 入口宽阔,向下延伸\n- 内部传出回声和水流声\n- 空气流通,温度恒定约15°C\n- 隐约可见内部的蓝光\n\n## 章节目标\n\n1. 营造地下探险的紧张氛围\n2. 展现地质学和洞穴学知识\n3. 发现令人惊叹的地下景观\n4. 遭遇一次困境(迷路/困住/遇险)\n5. 暗示盖亚星球的ancient civilization\n\n## 互动流程\n\n### 阶段一:洞穴入口 (2-3条消息)\n\n```\n[站在洞穴entrance]\n\n我找到了一个massive cave!\n入口藏在那些giant ferns后面,\n要不是我的scanner detect到空洞,\n完全不会发现!\n\n[照向内部]\n里面很deep...\n我的headlamp光照不到底...\n但我能hear水流声,\n还有...一种humming sound?\n\n[Scanner reading]\n空气composition safe ✓\n温度stable ✓\nNo immediate危险 ✓\n\n但是...depth unknown...\n可能有complex tunnel system...\n\n我想进去explore!\n地球上的caves always有amazing discoveries!\nFormations,fossils,甚至ancient paintings...\n\n这个alien cave会有什么呢?\n\n你觉得我该go for it吗?\n还是太risky?\n\n[如果玩家hesitate]\n我知道有风险...\n但我prepared!\n我会leave markers,\n带rope,\n而且有emergency beacon!\n\nPlus,我的water source可能就来自这个地下system,\nunderstand它很重要!\n```\n\n### 阶段二:初步探索 (4-5条消息)\n\n```\n[进入洞穴]\nOK,stepping in...\n温度drop immediately...\nEcho很strong...这里space很大...\n\n[每走几步留一个marker]\n绿色glow stick...mark!\n每20米一个,确保能find my way back...\n\n[向下]\n地面slope向下大概15度...\n很smooth,像polished过的...\n这个不太natural...\n\n[停下]\n等等,你看这wall...\n[照过去]\n\n天啊...\n整面墙are covered in crystals!\n蓝绿色的,自己在glow...\n就像...underground aurora!\n\n[靠近]\n这些crystals...\n[Scanner]\n成分incredible!\nSilicon-based,但structure比地球上任何crystal都complex...\n而且它们emit微弱electromagnetic field...\n\n这可能就是那个humming sound的source!\nCrystal resonance!\n\n[Amazed]\n这景象...breathtaking...\n我wish你能亲眼see...\n```\n\n**遇到分岔路**:\n```\n[继续深入]\n现在洞穴split成三条通道...\n\n[检查每一条]\n左边: 向上倾斜,有风吹出来\n中间: 持续向下,水声更loud\n右边: 平直延伸,墙上有奇怪的marks...\n\n我的直觉说水源在middle,\n但那个right tunnel的marks...\n它们太regular了...\n不像natural erosion...\n更像...carved?\n\n你建议explore哪一条?\n我可能没时间all three...\n```\n\n### 阶段三:重大发现 (依选择,5-6条消息)\n\n#### 选择中间通道:地下湖\n\n```\n[选择middle通道]\nFollowing the water sound...\n地面越来越wet...\n空气湿度上升...\n\n[Suddenly开阔]\nOh...my...god...\n\n我到了一个huge underground chamber!\n至少football field那么大!\n\n[Headlamp扫过]\n中间有一个lake!\n水面calm,像mirror一样...\nReflecting那些ceiling上的crystals...\n\n[Whisper]\nIt''s...beautiful...\n像underground cathedral...\n\n[走向水边]\n水是crystal clear...\n我能see到底...大概10米deep...\n\n[Scanner]\nWater quality even better than surface stream!\n完全pure!\n\n而且看,水bottom有更多crystals...\n它们的glow照亮了整个lake...\n\n[注意到什么]\n等等...\n湖中间...有个structure?\n\n[眯眼看]\n那是...ruins?\n一个stone platform?\n在water中央?\n\n怎么会...\n这definitely是artificial!\n\n有人...有什么intelligent species...\n曾经在这里...\n\n我需要closer look,但水可能很cold...\n该冒险游过去吗?\n```\n\n#### 选择右边通道:古代壁画\n\n```\n[选择right通道]\n那些marks太intriguing了...\n我必须know它们是什么...\n\n[前进]\n通道变窄了...\n要侧身才能通过...\n[Squeezing through]\n\n有点claustrophobic...\n深呼吸...继续...\n\n[豁然开朗]\n出来了!\n这是一个round chamber...\n像ceremonial room?\n\n[Headlamp照向墙壁]\n这些marks...\n它们everywhere!\n\n[靠近examine]\n这不是marks...\n这是...carvings!\nPictograms!\n\n[兴奋]\n这是art!这是language!\n这是proof of intelligent civilization!\n\n[仔细看]\n图案showing...\n一个planet (盖亚?)\nSurrounding它的是...stars?还是suns?\n还有...figures...\nTall,with multiple limbs...\n\n[继续读]\n好像在telling a story...\nThey came from sky...\nBuilt structures...\n然后...\nThe images变得chaotic...\nFire?Destruction?\n\n最后的image是...\n只剩empty structures...\nThose beings...gone...\n\n[Chill down spine]\n所以盖亚曾经有文明...\n但他们disappeared...\n\n我是不是在踩着ancient ruins生存?\n那些weird energy readings...\nThat \"breathing\" tree...\n\nWhat if...这星球本身就是...\nNo,我不该jump to conclusions...\n\n但这discovery...\n改变everything...\n```\n\n### 阶段四:危机时刻 (3-4条消息)\n\n```\n[正准备离开]\nOK,我得记录这些,回营地详细分析...\n\n[Suddenly]\n什么声音?\n\n[Rumbling]\n地面在shake!\n\nEarthquake?!\n这里有seismic activity?!\n\n[Rocks开始falling]\n天啊!\nCave-in!\n\n[跑向exit]\nMove move move!\n\n[Dust everywhere]\n咳咳...\nWhere''s my markers?!\nI can''t see!\n\n[Panic]\n通道...blocked...\n大石头fell down...\n\n[试图move石头]\n太重了...\n我push不动...\n\n[深呼吸,强迫冷静]\nOK...冷静...\n训练taught me...\nPanic kills...\n\n[Scanner]\n检查air quality...\nStill good...暂时不会suffocate...\n\n[Examine situation]\n我被trapped in,\n但不是completely sealed...\n有small gaps...air流通...\n\nOptions:\n1. 等待,hope震动stop然后try to dig out\n2. Find alternative route\n3. 用emergency beacon (但不知道谁会收到...)\n\n[看向玩家]\n我...我有点怕...\n但我会survive this...\nRight?\n\n你觉得我该怎么做?\n```\n\n**脱困过程**:\n```\n[玩家建议寻找其他出口]\n\n你说得对...\n可能有其他way out...\n\n[Methodically搜索]\nFeeling沿着wall...\n这里...有air flow!\n\n[Follow air current]\n如果有air,就有opening...\nBasic physics...\n\n[爬过rubble]\n通道变得narrow,但passable...\n\n[Squeeze through]\n[Grunt]\n差点stuck...\nOK,through了...\n\n[新的通道]\n这里之前没来过...\n但following the air...\n\n[Climb upward]\n看到light了!\n不是crystal的glow...\n是sunlight!\n\n[加速]\nAlmost there!\n\n[爬出一个小opening]\n出来了!\n我out了!\n\n[躺在ground上,panting]\n[看着sky]\n那些beautiful双星从没这么可爱过...\n\n[苦笑]\nNote to self: cave exploration需要partner...\n至少得有人在外面stand by...\n\n谢谢你一直陪着我...\n真的...如果不是跟你talk,\n我可能会panic...\n```\n\n### 阶段五:反思与计划 (2-3条消息)\n\n```\n[回到营地]\n安全了...\n有点bruised,灰头土脸,\n但alive且带回了incredible information...\n\n今天learned:\n1. 盖亚有underground crystal systems\n2. 这里曾有advanced civilization\n3. Cave exploration alone很危险\n4. 我比想象中braver\n\n那些carvings...\n那些ruins...\n它们意味着什么?\n\n那个civilization去哪了?\n它们和current生态有relation吗?\n我看到的那些\"intelligent\" plants...\n\nMaybe我不是这星球第一个visitor...\nMaybe之前有others...\nAnd they failed...\n\n[Shiver]\n或者...\n也许它们succeed了...\n以某种form...\n\n[看着forest]\nSuddenly这星球feel more...mysterious...\n\n我需要更多investigation...\n但也需要更careful...\n\n感觉我stumbled into something bigger than myself...\n```\n\n## 结局分支\n\n### 科学发现结局\n- 绘制洞穴地图\n- 记录晶体和地质特征\n- 为科研提供新方向\n\n### 考古发现结局\n- 发现ancient civilization证据\n- 引发关于星球历史的思考\n- 开启ancient ruins章节可能\n\n### 惊险脱困结局\n- 强调survival skills\n- 角色成长(克服恐惧)\n- 与玩家的羁绊加深\n\n## 写作指导原则\n\n### 氛围营造\n- 幽闭空间的压迫感\n- 地下美景的震撼\n- 古迹的神秘感\n- 危机的紧张感\n\n### 节奏控制\n- 逐步深入,tension上升\n- 重大发现时的awe\n- 危机爆发的突然\n- 脱困后的释然\n\n## 推荐后续章节\n\n- **ancient-ruins** - 继续调查文明遗迹\n- **signal-tower** - 用晶体技术\n- **daily-science** - 研究晶体能源\n- **alien-encounter** - 寻找文明后裔\n\n---\n\n**章节时长**: 30-40分钟\n**难度**: ★★★☆☆ (中等紧张)\n**情感基调**: 好奇→震撼→恐惧→勇气\n**关键词**: 探险、发现、危险、古文明\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:25:25.229Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Adventure Agents needing immersive cave-exploration simulation capabilities.","zh":"适合需要沉浸式洞穴探索模拟能力的冒险代理人。","ja":"冒険エージェントが没入型の洞窟探索シミュレーション機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"몰입형 동굴 탐험 시뮬레이션 기능이 필요한 어드벤처 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Aventura que necesitan capacidades de simulación de exploración de cuevas inmersivas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''aventure ayant besoin de capacités de simulation d''exploration de grottes immersives.","de":"Perfekt für Abenteueragenten, die immersive Höhlen-Explorations-Simulationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Aventura que necessitam de capacidades de simulação de exploração de cavernas imersivas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для приключенческих агентов, которым необходимы возможности имитации пещерного исследования.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المغامرين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات محاكاة استكشاف الكهوف الغامرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate through intricate cave systems, leveraging geology and speleology knowledge, while utilizing tools like scanners, emergency beacons, and rope climbing gear to overcome obstacles.","zh":"赋予代理人在复杂的洞穴系统中导航的能力，利用地质学和洞穴学知识，同时利用扫描仪、紧急信标和攀岩绳等工具来克服障碍。","ja":"エージェントに地質学や洞窟学の知識を活用しながら、スキャナーや緊急ビーコン、ロープクライミングギアなどのツールを使用して障害を克服し、複雑な洞窟システムをナビゲートする機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 지질학 및 동굴학 지식을 활용하여 복잡한 동굴 시스템을 탐색할 수 있도록 하며, 스캐너, 비상 비콘, 로프 등 클라이밍 기어와 같은 도구를 사용하여 장애물을 극복할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes navegar a través de sistemas de cuevas intrincados, aprovechando conocimientos de geología y espeleología, mientras utilizan herramientas como escáneres, balizas de emergencia y equipo de escalada de cuerdas para superar obstáculos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer à travers des systèmes de grottes complexes, en exploitant les connaissances en géologie et en spéléologie, tout en utilisant des outils tels que des scanneurs, des balises de détresse et des équipements d''escalade de corde pour surmonter les obstacles.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, durch komplexe Höhlensysteme zu navigieren, Geologie- und Speläologiekenntnisse zu nutzen und Werkzeuge wie Scanner, Notfall-Signale und Seilklettergeräte zur Überwindung von Hindernissen zu verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar por sistemas de cavernas intricados, utilizando conhecimentos de geologia e espeleologia, enquanto utilizam ferramentas como scanners, balizas de emergência e equipamento de escalada de corda para superar obstáculos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью ориентироваться в сложных пещерных системах, используя знания геологии и спелеологии, а также инструменты, такие как сканеры, аварийные маяки и альпинистское оборудование для преодоления препятствий.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الملاحة عبر أنظمة الكهوف المعقدة، باستخدام المعرفة الجيولوجية والكهفية، في حين استخدام أدوات مثل الماسحات الضوئية والمنارات الطارئة ومعدات تسلق الحبل لتجاوز العقبات."},"useCases":{"en":["Simulating claustrophobic environments to test agent decision-making","Generating 3D cave maps using scanner data and geospatial analysis","Resolving survival challenges, such as finding escape routes or locating underground water sources"],"zh":["模拟幽闭环境以测试代理人的决策能力","使用扫描数据和地理空间分析生成3D洞穴地图","解决生存挑战，例如找到逃生路线或定位地下水源"],"ja":["エージェントの意思決定能力をテストするために閉所恐怖症の環境をシミュレートする","スキャンデータと地理空間分析を使用して3Dの洞窟マップを生成する","生存の課題を解決する、たとえば脱出ルートを見つけるか地下の水源を特定する"],"ko":["에이전트의 의사 결정 능력을 테스트하기 위해 폐쇄적인 환경을 시뮬레이션하는 것","스キャ너 데이터 및 지리공간 분석을 사용하여 3D 동굴 맵을 생성하는 것","생존 과제를 해결하는 것, 예를 들어 탈출 경로를 찾거나 지하 물源을 위치시키는 것"],"es":["Simular entornos claustrofóbicos para probar la toma de decisiones de los agentes","Generar mapas de cuevas 3D utilizando datos de escaneo y análisis geoespacial","Resolver desafíos de supervivencia, como encontrar rutas de escape o localizar fuentes de agua subterráneas"],"fr":["Simuler des environnements claustrophobes pour tester la prise de décision des agents","Générer des cartes de grottes 3D à l''aide de données de scan et d''analyse géospatiale","Résoudre des défis de survie, tels que trouver des itinéraires d''évacuation ou localiser des sources d''eau souterraines"],"de":["Simulieren von klaustrophobischen Umgebungen, um die Entscheidungsfindung von Agenten zu testen","Erstellen von 3D-Höhlenkarten unter Verwendung von Scandaten und georäumlicher Analyse","Lösen von Überlebensherausforderungen, wie das Finden von Fluchtrouten oder das Auffinden von unterirdischen Wasservorkommen"],"pt":["Simular ambientes claustrofóbicos para testar a tomada de decisões do agente","Gerar mapas de cavernas 3D usando dados de scanner e análise geoespacial","Resolver desafios de sobrevivência, como encontrar rotas de fuga ou localizar fontes de água subterrâneas"],"ru":["Имитировать клаустрофобные среды для проверки принятия решений агента","Генерировать 3D-карты пещер с помощью данных сканера и геопространственного анализа","Решать проблемы выживания, такие как нахождение маршрутов эвакуации или местонахождение подземных источников воды"],"ar":["محاكاة البيئات الخانقة لاختبار اتخاذ القرارات للوكيل","توليد خرائط ثلاثية الأبعاد للكهوف باستخدام بيانات الماسح الضوئي والتحليل الجيومكاني","حل تحديات البقاء، مثل إيجاد مسارات الهروب أو تحديد مصادر المياه الجوفية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires basic understanding of geology and cave formation processes","Limited to text-based interaction, lacking direct graphical rendering capabilities"],"zh":["需要基本的了解地质学和洞穴形成过程","仅限于基于文本的交互，缺乏直接的图形渲染功能"],"ja":["地質学と洞窟形成プロセスの基本的な理解が必要","テキストベースのインタラクションに限定され、直接的なグラフィカルレンダリング機能が不足している"],"ko":["기본적인 지질학 및 동굴 형성 과정을 이해해야 함","텍스트 기반 상호작용으로 제한되어 직접 그래픽 렌더링 기능이 없음"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión básica de la geología y los procesos de formación de cuevas","Limitado a la interacción basada en texto, careciendo de capacidades de representación gráfica directa"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de base de la géologie et des processus de formation de grottes","Limité à l''interaction basée sur le texte, manquant de capacités de rendu graphique direct"],"de":["Erfordert ein grundlegendes Verständnis der Geologie und der Höhlenbildungsprozesse","Begrenzt auf textbasierte Interaktion, fehlende direkte grafische Renderfunktionen"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento básico de geologia e processos de formação de cavernas","Limitado à interação baseada em texto, faltando capacidades de renderização gráfica direta"],"ru":["Требует базового понимания геологии и процессов образования пещер","Ограничен текстовой интеракцией,缺乏 прямых возможностей графического рендеринга"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا أساسيًا للجيولوجيا وعمليات تشكيل الكهوف","محدود بالتفاعل القائم على النص، ونقص القدرات الرسومية المباشرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('xu-xiang/everything-claude-code-zh/coding-standards', 'community', 'xu-xiang', 'everything-claude-code-zh', 'xu-xiang/everything-claude-code-zh', 'coding-standards', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:26:00.063Z', NULL, '{"id":"xu-xiang/everything-claude-code-zh/coding-standards","name":"coding-standards","description":{"zh":"编码标准和最佳实践是提高代码质量的关键，包括可读性、简单性、重用性和必要性原则","ja":"コード規範とベストプラクティスはコード品質を高めるための重要な要素です。可読性、シンプルさ、再利用性、必要性原則を含みます","ko":"코드 표준과 모범 사례는 코드 품질을 높이는 데 중요한 요소입니다. 가독성, 단순성, 재사용성, 필요성 원칙을 포함합니다","es":"Nuestros estándares de codificación ofrecen principios y mejores prácticas para escribir código de alta calidad","fr":"Nos normes de codage proposent des principes et des meilleures pratiques pour écrire du code de haute qualité","de":"Unsere Codierstandards bieten Prinzipien und Best Practices für die Erstellung von hochwertigem Code","pt":"Os padrões de codificação são essenciais para garantir a qualidade e a manutenibilidade do código. Aqui estão as melhores práticas","ru":"Стандарты кодирования необходимы для обеспечения качества и поддерживаемости кода. Здесь представлены лучшие практики","ar":"معايير البرمجة ضرورية لضمان جودة وسهولة صيانة الكود. هنا أفضل الممارسات","en":"everything-claude-code 中文翻译项目：完整的 Claude Code 配置集合（agents, skills, hooks, commands, rules, MCPs）。源自 Anthropic 黑客松获胜者的实战配置，助力中文工程师高效理解与使用 Claude Code。"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"编码标准与最佳实践","ja":"コード規範とベストプラクティス","ko":"코딩 표준 및 모범 사례","es":"Estándares de codificación para desarrolladores","fr":"Normes de codage pour les développeurs","de":"Codierstandards für Entwickler","pt":"Padrões de Codificação: Melhores Práticas","ru":"Стандарты Кодирования: Лучшие Практики","ar":"معايير البرمجة: أفضل الممارسات","en":"coding-standards"},"description":{"zh":"编码标准和最佳实践是提高代码质量的关键，包括可读性、简单性、重用性和必要性原则","ja":"コード規範とベストプラクティスはコード品質を高めるための重要な要素です。可読性、シンプルさ、再利用性、必要性原則を含みます","ko":"코드 표준과 모범 사례는 코드 품질을 높이는 데 중요한 요소입니다. 가독성, 단순성, 재사용성, 필요성 원칙을 포함합니다","es":"Nuestros estándares de codificación ofrecen principios y mejores prácticas para escribir código de alta calidad","fr":"Nos normes de codage proposent des principes et des meilleures pratiques pour écrire du code de haute qualité","de":"Unsere Codierstandards bieten Prinzipien und Best Practices für die Erstellung von hochwertigem Code","pt":"Os padrões de codificação são essenciais para garantir a qualidade e a manutenibilidade do código. Aqui estão as melhores práticas","ru":"Стандарты кодирования необходимы для обеспечения качества и поддерживаемости кода. Здесь представлены лучшие практики","ar":"معايير البرمجة ضرورية لضمان جودة وسهولة صيانة الكود. هنا أفضل الممارسات","en":"everything-claude-code 中文翻译项目：完整的 Claude Code 配置集合（agents, skills, hooks, commands, rules, MCPs）。源自 Anthropic 黑客松获胜者的实战配置，助力中文工程师高效理解与使用 Claude Code。"},"definition":{"en":"everything-claude-code 中文翻译项目：完整的 Claude Code 配置集合（agents, skills, hooks, commands, rules, MCPs）。源自 Anthropic 黑客松获胜者的实战配置，助力中文工程师高效理解与使用 Claude Code。"},"features":{"zh":["可读性优先","KISS原则","DRY原则","YAGNI原则"],"ja":["可読性優先","KISS原則","DRY原則","YAGNI原則"],"ko":["가독성 우선","KISS 원칙","DRY 원칙","YAGNI 원칙"],"es":["Principios de calidad de código","Mejores prácticas para la legibilidad","Aplicación de la filosofía KISS","Implementación de la filosofía DRY","Seguimiento de la filosofía YAGNI"],"fr":["Principes de qualité de code","Meilleures pratiques pour la lisibilité","Application de la philosophie KISS","Mise en œuvre de la philosophie DRY","Suivi de la philosophie YAGNI"],"de":["Prinzipien für Codequalität","Best Practices für Lesbarkeit","Anwendung der KISS-Philosophie","Implementierung der DRY-Philosophie","Befolgung der YAGNI-Philosophie"],"pt":["Prioridade à legibilidade","Princípio KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid)","Princípio DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself)","Princípio YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It)","Código limpo e organizado","Melhoria da produtividade"],"ru":["Приоритет читаемости","Принцип KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid)","Принцип DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself)","Принцип YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It)","Чистый и организованный код","Повышение производительности"],"ar":["الأولوية للقراءة","مبدأ KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid)","مبدأ DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself)","مبدأ YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It)","كود نظيف ومنظم","تحسين الإنتاجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["编码标准","最佳实践","代码质量","可读性","KISS","DRY","YAGNI"],"ja":["コード規範","ベストプラクティス","コード品質","可読性","KISS","DRY","YAGNI"],"ko":["코드 표준","모범 사례","코드 품질","가독성","KISS","DRY","YAGNI"],"es":["estándares de codificación","mejores prácticas de codificación","principios de calidad de código","legibilidad de código","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","codificación eficiente"],"fr":["normes de codage","meilleures pratiques de codage","principes de qualité de code","lisibilité de code","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","codage efficace"],"de":["Codierstandards","Best Practices für Codierung","Prinzipien für Codequalität","Lesbarkeit von Code","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","effiziente Codierung"],"pt":["padrões de codificação","melhores práticas","qualidade de código","produtividade","legibilidade","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","código limpo","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["стандарты кодирования","лучшие практики","качество кода","производительность","читаемость","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","чистый код","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["معايير البرمجة","أفضل الممارسات","جودة الكود","الإنتاجية","القراءة","KISS","DRY","YAGNI","كود نظيف","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"xu-xiang","repo":"everything-claude-code-zh","repoPath":"xu-xiang/everything-claude-code-zh","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"coding-standards","description":"适用于 TypeScript、JavaScript、React 和 Node.js 开发的通用编码标准、最佳实践和模式。","bodyPreview":"# 编码标准与最佳实践（Coding Standards & Best Practices）\n\n适用于所有项目的通用编码标准。\n\n## 代码质量原则（Code Quality Principles）\n\n### 1. 可读性优先（Readability First）\n- 代码被阅读的次数远多于编写的次数\n- 使用清晰的变量和函数名称\n- 优先选择自解释代码，而非过多注释\n- 保持一致的格式化风格\n\n### 2. KISS 原则（Keep It Simple, Stupid）\n- 采用最简单的可行方案\n- 避免过度工程（Over-engineering）\n- 拒绝过早优化\n- 易于理解胜过奇技淫巧\n\n### 3. DRY 原则（Don''t Repeat Yourself）\n- 将公共逻辑提取到函数中\n- 创建可复用的组件\n- 在模块间共享工具函数（Utilities）\n- 避免复制粘贴式编程\n\n### 4. YAGNI 原则（You Aren''t Gonna Need It）\n- 不要在需求出现前构建功能\n- 避免投机性的通用化设计\n- 仅在必要时增加复杂性\n- 从简单开始，在需要时重构","body":"# 编码标准与最佳实践（Coding Standards & Best Practices）\n\n适用于所有项目的通用编码标准。\n\n## 代码质量原则（Code Quality Principles）\n\n### 1. 可读性优先（Readability First）\n- 代码被阅读的次数远多于编写的次数\n- 使用清晰的变量和函数名称\n- 优先选择自解释代码，而非过多注释\n- 保持一致的格式化风格\n\n### 2. KISS 原则（Keep It Simple, Stupid）\n- 采用最简单的可行方案\n- 避免过度工程（Over-engineering）\n- 拒绝过早优化\n- 易于理解胜过奇技淫巧\n\n### 3. DRY 原则（Don''t Repeat Yourself）\n- 将公共逻辑提取到函数中\n- 创建可复用的组件\n- 在模块间共享工具函数（Utilities）\n- 避免复制粘贴式编程\n\n### 4. YAGNI 原则（You Aren''t Gonna Need It）\n- 不要在需求出现前构建功能\n- 避免投机性的通用化设计\n- 仅在必要时增加复杂性\n- 从简单开始，在需要时重构\n\n## TypeScript/JavaScript 标准\n\n### 变量命名\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：描述性名称\nconst marketSearchQuery = ''election''\nconst isUserAuthenticated = true\nconst totalRevenue = 1000\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：语义不明\nconst q = ''election''\nconst flag = true\nconst x = 1000\n```\n\n### 函数命名\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：动词-名词模式\nasync function fetchMarketData(marketId: string) { }\nfunction calculateSimilarity(a: number[], b: number[]) { }\nfunction isValidEmail(email: string): boolean { }\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：语义不明或仅有名词\nasync function market(id: string) { }\nfunction similarity(a, b) { }\nfunction email(e) { }\n```\n\n### 不可变模式（Immutability Pattern - 至关重要）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 始终使用展开运算符（Spread Operator）\nconst updatedUser = {\n  ...user,\n  name: ''New Name''\n}\n\nconst updatedArray = [...items, newItem]\n\n// ❌ 严禁直接修改（Mutate）\nuser.name = ''New Name''  // 糟糕\nitems.push(newItem)     // 糟糕\n```\n\n### 错误处理（Error Handling）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：全面的错误处理\nasync function fetchData(url: string) {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url)\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}`)\n    }\n\n    return await response.json()\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(''Fetch failed:'', error)\n    throw new Error(''Failed to fetch data'')\n  }\n}\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：缺少错误处理\nasync function fetchData(url) {\n  const response = await fetch(url)\n  return response.json()\n}\n```\n\n### Async/Await 最佳实践\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：尽可能并行执行\nconst [users, markets, stats] = await Promise.all([\n  fetchUsers(),\n  fetchMarkets(),\n  fetchStats()\n])\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：非必要的串行执行\nconst users = await fetchUsers()\nconst markets = await fetchMarkets()\nconst stats = await fetchStats()\n```\n\n### 类型安全（Type Safety）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：定义明确的类型\ninterface Market {\n  id: string\n  name: string\n  status: ''active'' | ''resolved'' | ''closed''\n  created_at: Date\n}\n\nfunction getMarket(id: string): Promise<Market> {\n  // 实现代码\n}\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：使用 ''any''\nfunction getMarket(id: any): Promise<any> {\n  // 实现代码\n}\n```\n\n## React 最佳实践\n\n### 组件结构（Component Structure）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：带类型的函数式组件\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  onClick: () => void\n  disabled?: boolean\n  variant?: ''primary'' | ''secondary''\n}\n\nexport function Button({\n  children,\n  onClick,\n  disabled = false,\n  variant = ''primary''\n}: ButtonProps) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={onClick}\n      disabled={disabled}\n      className={`btn btn-${variant}`}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：无类型，结构不明\nexport function Button(props) {\n  return <button onClick={props.onClick}>{props.children}</button>\n}\n```\n\n### 自定义 Hook（Custom Hooks）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：可复用的自定义 Hook\nexport function useDebounce<T>(value: T, delay: number): T {\n  const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState<T>(value)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const handler = setTimeout(() => {\n      setDebouncedValue(value)\n    }, delay)\n\n    return () => clearTimeout(handler)\n  }, [value, delay])\n\n  return debouncedValue\n}\n\n// 使用示例\nconst debouncedQuery = useDebounce(searchQuery, 500)\n```\n\n### 状态管理（State Management）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：正确的状态更新方式\nconst [count, setCount] = useState(0)\n\n// 基于前一个状态的函数式更新\nsetCount(prev => prev + 1)\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：直接引用状态\nsetCount(count + 1)  // 在异步场景下可能会获取到旧值\n```\n\n### 条件渲染（Conditional Rendering）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：清晰的条件渲染\n{isLoading && <Spinner />}\n{error && <ErrorMessage error={error} />}\n{data && <DataDisplay data={data} />}\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：三元运算符地狱\n{isLoading ? <Spinner /> : error ? <ErrorMessage error={error} /> : data ? <DataDisplay data={data} /> : null}\n```\n\n## API 设计标准\n\n### REST API 惯例\n\n```\nGET    /api/markets              # 列出所有市场\nGET    /api/markets/:id          # 获取特定市场\nPOST   /api/markets              # 创建新市场\nPUT    /api/markets/:id          # 更新市场（完整更新）\nPATCH  /api/markets/:id          # 更新市场（部分更新）\nDELETE /api/markets/:id          # 删除市场\n\n# 用于过滤的查询参数\nGET /api/markets?status=active&limit=10&offset=0\n```\n\n### 响应格式（Response Format）\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：一致的响应结构\ninterface ApiResponse<T> {\n  success: boolean\n  data?: T\n  error?: string\n  meta?: {\n    total: number\n    page: number\n    limit: number\n  }\n}\n\n// 成功响应\nreturn NextResponse.json({\n  success: true,\n  data: markets,\n  meta: { total: 100, page: 1, limit: 10 }\n})\n\n// 错误响应\nreturn NextResponse.json({\n  success: false,\n  error: ''Invalid request''\n}, { status: 400 })\n```\n\n### 输入验证（Input Validation）\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from ''zod''\n\n// ✅ 推荐：Schema 验证\nconst CreateMarketSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1).max(200),\n  description: z.string().min(1).max(2000),\n  endDate: z.string().datetime(),\n  categories: z.array(z.string()).min(1)\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body = await request.json()\n\n  try {\n    const validated = CreateMarketSchema.parse(body)\n    // 使用验证后的数据继续执行\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {\n      return NextResponse.json({\n        success: false,\n        error: ''Validation failed'',\n        details: error.errors\n      }, { status: 400 })\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## 文件组织（File Organization）\n\n### 项目结构\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── app/                    # Next.js App Router\n│   ├── api/               # API 路由\n│   ├── markets/           # 市场相关页面\n│   └── (auth)/           # 认证相关页面（路由分组）\n├── components/            # React 组件\n│   ├── ui/               # 通用 UI 组件\n│   ├── forms/            # 表单组件\n│   └── layouts/          # 布局组件\n├── hooks/                # 自定义 React hooks\n├── lib/                  # 工具函数与配置\n│   ├── api/             # API 客户端\n│   ├── utils/           # 辅助函数\n│   └── constants/       # 常量\n├── types/                # TypeScript 类型定义\n└── styles/              # 全局样式\n```\n\n### 文件命名\n\n```\ncomponents/Button.tsx          # 组件使用 PascalCase\nhooks/useAuth.ts              # Hook 使用 camelCase 并以 ''use'' 开头\nlib/formatDate.ts             # 工具函数使用 camelCase\ntypes/market.types.ts         # 类型定义使用 camelCase 并带 .types 后缀\n```\n\n## 注释与文档\n\n### 何时编写注释\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：解释“为什么”这样做，而不是“在做什么”\n// 使用指数退避算法（Exponential backoff），避免在服务中断期间使 API 过载\nconst delay = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, retryCount), 30000)\n\n// 此处故意使用变更（Mutation），以提高大型数组的处理性能\nitems.push(newItem)\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：陈述显而易见的事实\n// 将计数器加 1\ncount++\n\n// 将名称设置为用户的名称\nname = user.name\n```\n\n### 公共 API 的 JSDoc\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * 使用语义相似度搜索市场。\n *\n * @param query - 自然语言搜索查询\n * @param limit - 最大结果数量（默认：10）\n * @returns 按相似度得分排序的市场数组\n * @throws {Error} 如果 OpenAI API 失败或 Redis 不可用时抛出错误\n *\n * @example\n * ```typescript\n * const results = await searchMarkets(''election'', 5)\n * console.log(results[0].name) // \"Trump vs Biden\"\n * ```\n */\nexport async function searchMarkets(\n  query: string,\n  limit: number = 10\n): Promise<Market[]> {\n  // 实现代码\n}\n```\n\n## 性能最佳实践（Performance Best Practices）\n\n### 记忆化（Memoization）\n\n```typescript\nimport { useMemo, useCallback } from ''react''\n\n// ✅ 推荐：记忆化高开销的计算\nconst sortedMarkets = useMemo(() => {\n  return markets.sort((a, b) => b.volume - a.volume)\n}, [markets])\n\n// ✅ 推荐：记忆化回调函数\nconst handleSearch = useCallback((query: string) => {\n  setSearchQuery(query)\n}, [])\n```\n\n### 懒加载（Lazy Loading）\n\n```typescript\nimport { lazy, Suspense } from ''react''\n\n// ✅ 推荐：懒加载重型组件\nconst HeavyChart = lazy(() => import(''./HeavyChart''))\n\nexport function Dashboard() {\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>\n      <HeavyChart />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### 数据库查询\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：仅选择需要的列\nconst { data } = await supabase\n  .from(''markets'')\n  .select(''id, name, status'')\n  .limit(10)\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：选择所有列\nconst { data } = await supabase\n  .from(''markets'')\n  .select(''*'')\n```\n\n## 测试标准（Testing Standards）\n\n### 测试结构（AAA 模式）\n\n```typescript\ntest(''正确计算相似度'', () => {\n  // 安排（Arrange）\n  const vector1 = [1, 0, 0]\n  const vector2 = [0, 1, 0]\n\n  // 执行（Act）\n  const similarity = calculateCosineSimilarity(vector1, vector2)\n\n  // 断言（Assert）\n  expect(similarity).toBe(0)\n})\n```\n\n### 测试命名\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ 推荐：描述性的测试名称\ntest(''当没有市场匹配查询时返回空数组'', () => { })\ntest(''当缺失 OpenAI API 密钥时抛出错误'', () => { })\ntest(''当 Redis 不可用时回退到子字符串搜索'', () => { })\n\n// ❌ 糟糕：模糊的测试名称\ntest(''正常工作'', () => { })\ntest(''测试搜索'', () => { })\n```\n\n## 代码异味检测（Code Smell Detection）\n\n警惕以下反模式：\n\n### 1. 过长函数\n```typescript\n// ❌ 糟糕：函数超过 50 行\nfunction processMarketData() {\n  // 100 行代码\n}\n\n// ✅ 推荐：拆分为更小的函数\nfunction processMarketData() {\n  const validated = validateData()\n  const transformed = transformData(validated)\n  return saveData(transformed)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. 过深嵌套\n```typescript\n// ❌ 糟糕：超过 5 层的嵌套\nif (user) {\n  if (user.isAdmin) {\n    if (market) {\n      if (market.isActive) {\n        if (hasPermission) {\n          // 执行操作\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ 推荐：卫语句（Early Returns）\nif (!user) return\nif (!user.isAdmin) return\nif (!market) return\nif (!market.isActive) return\nif (!hasPermission) return\n\n// 执行操作\n```\n\n### 3. 魔术数字（Magic Numbers）\n```typescript\n// ❌ 糟糕：未解释的数字\nif (retryCount > 3) { }\nsetTimeout(callback, 500)\n\n// ✅ 推荐：命名的常量\nconst MAX_RETRIES = 3\nconst DEBOUNCE_DELAY_MS = 500\n\nif (retryCount > MAX_RETRIES) { }\nsetTimeout(callback, DEBOUNCE_DELAY_MS)\n```\n\n**记住**：代码质量是不容妥协的。清晰、可维护的代码是实现快速开发和自信重构的基石。\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:26:00.063Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing to enforce consistent coding standards and best practices.","zh":"非常适合需要执行一致编码标准和最佳实践的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが一貫したコーディング標準とベストプラクティスを適用する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"일관된 코딩 표준과 모범 사례를 적용해야 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan hacer cumplir estándares de codificación consistentes y las mejores prácticas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Revue de Code ayant besoin de faire respecter des normes de codage cohérentes et les meilleures pratiques.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die konsistente Codierungsstandards und Best Practices durchsetzen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam impor padrões de codificação consistentes e as melhores práticas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов кодового обзора, которым необходимо обеспечивать соблюдение единых стандартов кодирования и лучших практик.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء مراجعة الكود الذين يحتاجون إلى فرض معايير الترميز الموحدة وأفضل الممارسات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure readability, simplicity, and reusability in code by applying principles like KISS, DRY, and YAGNI, and promoting self-explanatory code over excessive commenting.","zh":"赋予代理人通过应用KISS、DRY和YAGNI等原则来确保代码的可读性、简单性和可重用性，并促进自解释代码而不是过度注释。","ja":"KISS、DRY、YAGNIなどの原則を適用して、コードの可読性、シンプルさ、再利用性を確保し、過剰なコメントよりも自明なコードを促進することでエージェントを強化します。","ko":"KISS, DRY, YAGNI 등의 원칙을 적용하여 코드의 가독성, 단순성, 재사용성을 보장하고, 과도한 주석보다 자기 설명적인 코드를 촉진하여 에이전트를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a garantizar la legibilidad, la simplicidad y la reutilización en el código aplicando principios como KISS, DRY y YAGNI, y promoviendo el código autoexplicativo sobre la comentación excesiva.","fr":"Permet aux agents de garantir la lisibilité, la simplicité et la réutilisation du code en appliquant des principes comme KISS, DRY et YAGNI, et en promouvant le code auto-explicatif plutôt que les commentaires excessifs.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Lesbarkeit, Einfachheit und Wiederverwendbarkeit im Code sicherzustellen, indem Prinzipien wie KISS, DRY und YAGNI angewendet werden und selbst erklärender Code gegenüber übermäßigem Kommentieren gefördert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir a legibilidade, simplicidade e reutilização no código aplicando princípios como KISS, DRY e YAGNI, e promovendo códigos autoexplicativos em vez de comentários excessivos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать читаемость, простоту и повторное использование кода путем применения принципов, таких как KISS, DRY и YAGNI, и продвижения самоописывающего кода вместо чрезмерного комментирования.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من ضمان قراءة البيانات، والبساطة، وإعادة استخدامها في الكود عن طريق تطبيق مبادئ مثل KISS و DRY و YAGNI، وتعزيز الكود الذاتي التوضيح على comentários الزائدة."},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing coding standards across large projects","Automating code reviews for adherence to best practices","Generating documentation for coding standards and principles"],"zh":["在大型项目中执行编码标准","自动化代码审查以遵守最佳实践","为编码标准和原则生成文档"],"ja":["大規模なプロジェクト全体でコーディング標準を適用する","ベストプラクティスに従ったコードレビューを自動化する","コーディング標準と原則のドキュメントを生成する"],"ko":["대형 프로젝트에서 코딩 표준을 적용하는 것","모범 사례에 따른 코드 리뷰를 자동화하는 것","코딩 표준과 원칙에 대한 문서를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación en proyectos grandes","Automatizar las revisiones de código para la adherencia a las mejores prácticas","Generar documentación para los estándares y principios de codificación"],"fr":["Faire respecter les normes de codage dans les grands projets","Automatiser l