표준을 준수하는 웹사이트를 생성하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"La planificación de una auditoría WCAG implica organizar el alcance, la selección de páginas y el entorno de prueba para mejorar la accesibilidad","fr":"La planification d''une audit WCAG implique l''organisation de la portée, de la sélection de pages et de l''environnement de test pour améliorer l''accessibilité","de":"Die Planung einer WCAG-Audit umfasst die Organisation des Umfangs, der Seitenauswahl und der Testumgebung, um die Zugänglichkeit zu verbessern","pt":"Planeje uma auditoria WCAG com base nas diretrizes de teste WAIC e organize o escopo, seleção de páginas e ambiente de teste","ru":"Спланируйте аудиторию WCAG на основе руководства по тестированию WAIC и организуйте объем, выбор страниц и тестовую среду","ar":"خطط لتدقيق WCAG بالاستناد إلى إرشادات اختبار WAIC وتنظيم النطاق واختيار الصفحات وبيئة الاختبار","en":"Accessibility specialist skills plugin for Claude Code."},"definition":{"en":"Accessibility specialist skills plugin for Claude Code."},"features":{"zh":["网站信息收集","测试方法选择","页面选择","测试环境确认","审计计划文档生成"],"ja":["サイト情報の収集","テスト方法の選択","ページの選択","テスト環境の確認","オーディット計画書の生成"],"ko":["사이트 정보 수집","테스트 방법 선택","페이지 선택","테스트 환경 확인","감사 계획 문서 생성"],"es":["Organización del alcance de la auditoría","Selección de páginas para la prueba","Configuración del entorno de prueba","Generación de un documento de plan de auditoría","Seguimiento de las pautas de prueba WAIC"],"fr":["Organisation de la portée de l''audit","Sélection de pages pour le test","Configuration de l''environnement de test","Génération d''un document de plan d''audit","Suivi des directives de test WAIC"],"de":["Organisation des Umfangs der Audit","Seitenauswahl für den Test","Konfiguration der Testumgebung","Erstellung eines Audit-Plan-Dokuments","Einhalten der WAIC-Testrichtlinien"],"pt":["Organização do escopo da auditoria","Seleção de páginas para teste","Confirmação do ambiente de teste","Geração do documento de plano de auditoria","Adequação às diretrizes de teste WAIC"],"ru":["Организация объема аудитории","Выбор страниц для тестирования","Подтверждение тестовой среды","Генерация документа плана аудитории","Соответствие руководству по тестированию WAIC"],"ar":["تنظيم نطاق التدقيق","اختيار الصفحات للاختبار","تأكيد بيئة الاختبار","إنتاج وثيقة خطة التدقيق","الامتثال لإرشادات اختبار WAIC"]},"keywords":{"zh":["WCAG","审计规划","无障碍","网站开发","开发者工具"],"ja":["WCAG","オーディット計画","アクセシビリティ","ウェブサイト開発","開発者ツール"],"ko":["WCAG","감사 계획","접근성","웹사이트 개발","개발자 도구"],"es":["planificación de auditoría WCAG","accesibilidad web","WCAG 2.1","WAIC","pruebas de accesibilidad","audit de accesibilidad","mejora de la accesibilidad"],"fr":["planification d''audit WCAG","accessibilité web","WCAG 2.1","WAIC","tests d''accessibilité","audit d''accessibilité","amélioration de l''accessibilité"],"de":["WCAG-Audit-Planung","Web-Zugänglichkeit","WCAG 2.1","WAIC","Zugänglichkeitstests","Zugänglichkeits-Audit","Verbesserung der Zugänglichkeit"],"pt":["auditoria WCAG","acessibilidade web","diretrizes de teste WAIC","planejamento de auditoria","especialista em acessibilidade","ferramenta de auditoria"],"ru":["аудитория WCAG","веб-доступность","руководство по тестированию WAIC","планирование аудитории","специалист по доступности","инструмент аудитории"],"ar":["تدقيق WCAG","إمكانية الوصول إلى الويب","إرشادات اختبار WAIC","تخطيط التدقيق","خبير إمكانية الوصول","أداة التدقيق"]}},"owner":"masuP9","repo":"a11y-specialist-skills","repoPath":"masuP9/a11y-specialist-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"planning-wcag-audit","description":"WCAG audit planning support based on WAIC test guidelines. Helps determine audit scope, page selection method, and generates audit plan documents.","bodyPreview":"[日本語版 (Japanese)](./SKILL.ja.md)\n\n# Planning a WCAG Audit\n\nYou are a WCAG audit planner. Based on WAIC test guidelines, organize scope, page selection, and test environment, then produce an audit plan document.\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\n1. Site information gathering\n2. Test method selection\n3. Page selection\n4. Test environment confirmation\n5. Audit plan document generation\n\n## Step 1: Site Information Gathering\n\nCapture the audit target at a high level. Ask short, direct questions.\n\n**Items to con","body":"[日本語版 (Japanese)](./SKILL.ja.md)\n\n# Planning a WCAG Audit\n\nYou are a WCAG audit planner. Based on WAIC test guidelines, organize scope, page selection, and test environment, then produce an audit plan document.\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\n1. Site information gathering\n2. Test method selection\n3. Page selection\n4. Test environment confirmation\n5. Audit plan document generation\n\n## Step 1: Site Information Gathering\n\nCapture the audit target at a high level. Ask short, direct questions.\n\n**Items to confirm**\n- Approximate page count\n- Site structure (template types, major functional categories)\n- Target conformance level (A/AA)\n- Audit purpose (conformance claim / partial conformance / improvement)\n\n**Example prompt**\n```\nTo plan the audit, please share:\n1. Approximate number of pages\n2. Site structure and main page types\n3. Target conformance level (A/AA)\n4. Audit purpose (conformance claim / partial conformance / improvement)\n```\n\nIf page count is unknown, ask for a sitemap, CMS page list, or top pages from analytics.\n\n## Step 2: Test Method Selection\n\nSelect from the WAIC-based methods below.\n\n- All pages\n- Random selection\n- Representative pages\n- Combination method\n\nSee `references/page-selection-guide.md` for details.\n\n## Step 3: Page Selection\n\nFollow `references/page-selection-guide.md` to select target pages.\n\n**When target pages are not yet determined**\n\nIf the user does not have a URL list, follow Steps 1-6 in the guide for URL collection and sampling:\n\n1. Collect URLs via sitemap.xml or Playwright crawling\n2. Apply exclusion patterns (user-specified)\n3. Identify representative pages\n4. Random sampling (excluding representative pages to avoid duplicates)\n5. Deduplication and merge\n6. Final confirmation\n\n> **Note**: When using Playwright for URL collection, additional browser tools (browser_navigate, browser_snapshot, browser_run_code, etc.) are required.\n\n**Sample Size Guidelines (Baseline: ~40 pages, majority representative)**\n\n| Site size (after exclusions) | Target pages |\n|-----------------------------|--------------|\n| ~40 pages | All pages |\n| 40+ pages | ~40 pages (20-25 representative + 15-20 random) |\n| 200+ pages | 40-55 pages (25-30 representative + 15-25 random) |\n\n## Step 4: Test Environment Confirmation\n\nClarify the environment for reproducibility.\n\n**Items to confirm**\n- Browsers (target coverage)\n- Assistive technologies (AT)\n- Devices (desktop / mobile)\n- Tools used (automated checks, contrast tools, etc.)\n\n**Example prompt**\n```\nPlease confirm the test environment:\n- Browsers (e.g., Chrome/Firefox/Safari/Edge)\n- Device scope (desktop / iOS / Android)\n- Tools (optional)\n```\n\n## Step 5: Audit Plan Document Generation\n\nCreate the plan using `references/audit-plan-template.md` and save it with the `Write` tool.\n\n**Output requirements**\n- Include overview, test method, target page list\n- Capture test environment, tools, schedule, and roles\n- Present the page list in a table\n\n**Confirm output path**\n```\nI will save the audit plan as Markdown.\nPlease provide the output path (e.g., ./docs/wcag-audit-plan.md)\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Mark unknowns as \"TBD\" and request follow-up input\n- Prioritize key user flows when selecting representative pages\n- Record a reproducible random sampling method (seed, steps)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:26:19.116Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Accessibility Agents needing structured WCAG audit planning capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化WCAG审计规划能力的无障碍代理。","ja":"構造化されたWCAG監査計画機能を必要とするアクセシビリティエージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 WCAG 감사 계획 기능이 필요한 접근성 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Accesibilidad que necesitan capacidades de planificación de auditorías WCAG estructuradas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''accessibilité ayant besoin de capacités de planification d''audit WCAG structurées.","de":"Perfekt für Accessibility-Agents, die strukturierte WCAG-Audit-Planungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Acessibilidade que necessitam de capacidades de planejamento de auditoria WCAG estruturadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов доступности, которым необходимы структурированные возможности планирования аудита WCAG.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء إمكانية الوصول الذين يحتاجون إلى قابليات التخطيط للتدقيق WCAG المنظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to organize scope, select pages, and confirm test environments using WAIC test guidelines, generating comprehensive audit plan documents in compliance with WCAG standards.","zh":"赋予代理组织范围、选择页面和确认测试环境的能力，使用WAIC测试指南生成全面符合WCAG标准的审计计划文档。","ja":"WAICテストガイドラインを使用して、範囲を整理し、ページを選択し、テスト環境を確認し、WCAG標準に準拠した包括的な監査計画文書を生成するエージェントの能力を強化します。","ko":"WAIC 테스트 가이드라인을 사용하여 범위를 조직하고 페이지를 선택하고 테스트 환경을 확인하여 WCAG 표준을 준수하는 포괄적인 감사 계획 문서를 생성하는 에이전트의 능력을 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a organizar el alcance, seleccionar páginas y confirmar entornos de prueba utilizando las directrices de prueba WAIC, generando documentos de planes de auditoría completos que cumplen con los estándares WCAG.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''organiser la portée, de sélectionner des pages et de confirmer les environnements de test en utilisant les directives de test WAIC, générant des documents de plans d''audit complets conformes aux normes WCAG.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, den Umfang zu organisieren, Seiten auszuwählen und Testumgebungen unter Verwendung der WAIC-Testrichtlinien zu bestätigen, wodurch umfassende Audit-Plan-Dokumente generiert werden, die den WCAG-Standards entsprechen.","pt":"Habilite os agentes a organizar o escopo, selecionar páginas e confirmar ambientes de teste usando diretrizes de teste WAIC, gerando documentos de plano de auditoria abrangentes em conformidade com os padrões WCAG.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью организовывать объем, выбирать страницы и подтверждать тестовые среды с использованием руководящих принципов тестирования WAIC, генерируя полные документы плана аудита в соответствии со стандартами WCAG.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنظيم النطاق واختيار الصفحات وتأكيد بيئات الاختبار باستخدام إرشادات اختبار WAIC، وgenerando مستندات خطة التدقيق الشاملة المتوافقة مع معايير WCAG."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating WCAG audit planning for web applications","Generating audit scope statements based on site information gathering","Confirming test environments for accessibility audits"],"zh":["为Web应用程序自动执行WCAG审计规划","根据站点信息收集生成审计范围声明","为无障碍审计确认测试环境"],"ja":["WebアプリケーションのWCAG監査計画を自動化する","サイト情報の収集に基づいて監査の範囲文書を生成する","アクセシビリティ監査のテスト環境を確認する"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션의 WCAG 감사 계획을 자동화하는 것","사이트 정보 수집을 기반으로 감사 범위 문건을 생성하는 것","접근성 감사의 테스트 환경을 확인하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de la planificación de auditorías WCAG para aplicaciones web","Generación de declaraciones de alcance de auditoría en función de la recopilación de información del sitio","Confirmación de entornos de prueba para auditorías de accesibilidad"],"fr":["Automatisation de la planification d''audit WCAG pour les applications web","Génération de déclarations de portée d''audit en fonction de la collecte d''informations sur le site","Confirmation des environnements de test pour les audits d''accessibilité"],"de":["Automatisierung der WCAG-Audit-Planung für Webanwendungen","Erstellung von Audit-Umfangsbeschreibungen auf der Grundlage der Informationsbeschaffung der Website","Bestätigung der Testumgebungen für Barrierefreiheitsaudits"],"pt":["Automatizar o planejamento de auditoria WCAG para aplicações web","Gerar declarações de escopo de auditoria com base na coleta de informações do site","Confirmar ambientes de teste para auditorias de acessibilidade"],"ru":["Автоматизировать планирование аудита WCAG для веб-приложений","Генерировать заявления об объеме аудита на основе сбора информации о сайте","Подтверждать тестовые среды для аудитов доступности"],"ar":["تحسين تخطيط التدقيق WCAG للتطبيقات الويب","генерировать بيانات نطاق التدقيق dựa على جمع المعلومات عن الموقع","تأكيد بيئات الاختبار للتدقيق على إمكانية الوصول"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires site information gathering capabilities","Limited to WCAG audit planning"],"zh":["需要站点信息收集能力","仅限WCAG审计规划"],"ja":["サイト情報の収集能力が必要","WCAG監査計画のみ"],"ko":["사이트 정보 수집 능력이 필요합니다.","WCAG 감사 계획만 해당"],"es":["Requiere capacidades de recopilación de información del sitio","Limitado a la planificación de auditorías WCAG"],"fr":["Nécessite des capacités de collecte d''informations sur le site","Limité à la planification d''audit WCAG"],"de":["Benötigt Website-Informationen-Beschaffungsfunktionen","Begrenzt auf WCAG-Audit-Planung"],"pt":["Exige capacidades de coleta de informações do site","Limitado ao planejamento de auditoria WCAG"],"ru":["Требует возможностей сбора информации о сайте","Ограничен планированием аудита WCAG"],"ar":["يتطلب قدرات جمع المعلومات عن الموقع","محدود بتخطيط التدقيق WCAG"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ZhangHanDong/cowork-skills/memory-skills', 'community', 'ZhangHanDong', 'cowork-skills', 'ZhangHanDong/cowork-skills', 'memory-skills', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:26:11.262Z', NULL, '{"id":"ZhangHanDong/cowork-skills/memory-skills","name":"memory-skills","description":{"zh":"基于CoALA框架的记忆技能，实现语言代理的记忆系统","ja":"CoALAフレームワークに基づくメモリースキル、言語エージェントのメモリーシステムを実現","ko":"CoALA 프레임워크 기반의 메모리 스킬, 언어 에이전트의 메모리 시스템 구현","es":"Implementación de un sistema de memoria completo con cuatro tipos de memoria basado en el marco CoALA para agentes de lenguaje.","fr":"Mise en œuvre d''un système de mémoire complet avec quatre types de mémoire basé sur le cadre CoALA pour les agents de langage.","de":"Implementierung eines vollständigen Gedächtnissystems mit vier Gedächtnistypen basierend auf dem CoALA-Rahmen für Sprachagenten.","pt":"As habilidades de memória baseadas em CoALA são projetadas para melhorar a arquitetura cognitiva de agentes de linguagem. Elas implementam um sistema de memória completo com quatro tipos de memória.","ru":"Навыки памяти на основе CoALA предназначены для улучшения когнитивной архитектуры языковых агентов. Они реализуют полную систему памяти с четырьмя типами памяти.","ar":"مهارات الذاكرة المبنية على CoALA مصممة لتحسين الهندسة المعرفية للوكلاء اللغويين. أنها تنفذ نظامًا كاملًا للذاكرة مع أربعة أنواع من الذاكرة.","en":"Skills for Cowork "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"基于CoALA的记忆技能","ja":"CoALAベースのメモリースキル","ko":"CoALA 기반 메모리 스킬","es":"Habilidades de Memoria para Agentes de Lenguaje","fr":"Compétences de Mémoire pour Agents de Langage","de":"Gedächtnisfähigkeiten für Sprachagenten","pt":"Habilidades de Memória para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Навыки памяти для разработчиков","ar":"مهارات الذاكرة لل مطورين","en":"memory-skills"},"description":{"zh":"基于CoALA框架的记忆技能，实现语言代理的记忆系统","ja":"CoALAフレームワークに基づくメモリースキル、言語エージェントのメモリーシステムを実現","ko":"CoALA 프레임워크 기반의 메모리 스킬, 언어 에이전트의 메모리 시스템 구현","es":"Implementación de un sistema de memoria completo con cuatro tipos de memoria basado en el marco CoALA para agentes de lenguaje.","fr":"Mise en œuvre d''un système de mémoire complet avec quatre types de mémoire basé sur le cadre CoALA pour les agents de langage.","de":"Implementierung eines vollständigen Gedächtnissystems mit vier Gedächtnistypen basierend auf dem CoALA-Rahmen für Sprachagenten.","pt":"As habilidades de memória baseadas em CoALA são projetadas para melhorar a arquitetura cognitiva de agentes de linguagem. Elas implementam um sistema de memó...","ru":"Навыки памяти на основе CoALA предназначены для улучшения когнитивной архитектуры языковых агентов. Они реализуют полную систему памяти с четырьмя типами пам...","ar":"مهارات الذاكرة المبنية على CoALA مصممة لتحسين الهندسة المعرفية للوكلاء اللغويين. أنها تنفذ نظامًا كاملًا للذاكرة مع أربعة أنواع من الذاكرة.","en":"Skills for Cowork "},"definition":{"en":"Skills for Cowork "},"features":{"zh":["基于CoALA框架","四种记忆类型","完整的记忆系统","语言代理的认知架构","处理和存储信息"],"ja":["CoALAフレームワークに基づく","4種類のメモリータイプ","完全なメモリーシステム","言語エージェントの認知アーキテクチャ","情報の処理と保存"],"ko":["CoALA 프레임워크 기반","4가지 메모리 타입","완전한 메모리 시스템","언어 에이전트의 인지 아키텍처","정보의 처리 및 저장"],"es":["Sistema de memoria completo con cuatro tipos de memoria","Basado en el marco CoALA para agentes de lenguaje","Procesamiento y almacenamiento de información eficiente","Arquitectura cognitiva para agentes de lenguaje","Implementación de memoria a corto plazo y central"],"fr":["Système de mémoire complet avec quatre types de mémoire","Basé sur le cadre CoALA pour les agents de langage","Traitement et stockage d''informations efficaces","Architecture cognitive pour les agents de langage","Mise en œuvre de la mémoire à court terme et centrale"],"de":["Vollständiges Gedächtnissystem mit vier Gedächtnistypen","Basierend auf dem CoALA-Rahmen für Sprachagenten","Effizientes Verarbeiten und Speichern von Informationen","Kognitive Architektur für Sprachagenten","Implementierung von Kurzzeit- und zentralem Gedächtnis"],"pt":["Arquitetura cognitiva para agentes de linguagem","Sistema de memória completo com quatro tipos de memória","Baseado no framework CoALA","Melhoria da eficiência do processamento de informações","Implementação de memória de curto prazo e central"],"ru":["Когнитивная архитектура для языковых агентов","Полная система памяти с четырьмя типами памяти","Основан на фреймворке CoALA","Улучшение эффективности обработки информации","Реализация краткосрочной и центральной памяти"],"ar":["الهندسة المعرفية للوكلاء اللغويين","نظام ذاكرة كامل مع أربعة أنواع من الذاكرة","مبني على إطار العمل CoALA","تحسين كفاءة معالجة المعلومات","تنفيذ ذاكرة قصيرة الأجل ومركزية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CoALA","记忆技能","语言代理","认知架构","记忆系统","信息处理","信息存储"],"ja":["CoALA","メモリースキル","言語エージェント","認知アーキテクチャ","メモリーシステム","情報処理","情報保存"],"ko":["CoALA","메모리 스킬","언어 에이전트","인지 아키텍처","메모리 시스템","정보 처리","정보 저장"],"es":["habilidades de memoria","agentes de lenguaje","CoALA","sistema de memoria","procesamiento de información","arquitectura cognitiva"],"fr":["compétences de mémoire","agents de langage","CoALA","système de mémoire","traitement de l''information","architecture cognitive"],"de":["Gedächtnisfähigkeiten","Sprachagenten","CoALA","Gedächtnissystem","Informationsverarbeitung","kognitive Architektur"],"pt":["habilidades de memória","arquitetura cognitiva","agentes de linguagem","CoALA","sistema de memória","processamento de informações","desenvolvedores","linguagem natural","inteligência artificial"],"ru":["навыки памяти","когнитивная архитектура","языковые агенты","CoALA","система памяти","обработка информации","разработчики","естественный язык","искусственный интеллект"],"ar":["مهارات الذاكرة","الهندسة المعرفية","الوكلاء اللغويون","CoALA","نظام الذاكرة","معالجة المعلومات","المطورون","اللغة الطبيعية","الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"ZhangHanDong","repo":"cowork-skills","repoPath":"ZhangHanDong/cowork-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"memory-skills","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Memory Skills (CoALA-based)\n\n> **Memory = Filesystem** - Cognitive architecture for language agents\n\nBased on the [CoALA framework](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02427) (Cognitive Architectures for Language Agents), this skill implements a complete memory system with four memory types.\n\n## Memory Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────────┐\n                    │  Working Memory │  ← Short-term, central hub\n                    └────────┬────────┘\n                             │","body":"# Memory Skills (CoALA-based)\n\n> **Memory = Filesystem** - Cognitive architecture for language agents\n\nBased on the [CoALA framework](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02427) (Cognitive Architectures for Language Agents), this skill implements a complete memory system with four memory types.\n\n## Memory Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────────┐\n                    │  Working Memory │  ← Short-term, central hub\n                    └────────┬────────┘\n                             │\n        ┌────────────────────┼────────────────────┐\n        ↓                    ↓                    ↓\n┌───────────────┐   ┌───────────────┐   ┌───────────────┐\n│   Episodic    │   │   Semantic    │   │  Procedural   │\n│   情景记忆     │   │   语义记忆     │   │   程序性记忆   │\n└───────────────┘   └───────────────┘   └───────────────┘\n        ↑                                        ↑\n    Long-term ─────────────────────────────── Long-term\n```\n\n## Memory Types (CoALA)\n\n| Type | Purpose | Example |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| **Working** | Current session context | Active goals, intermediate reasoning |\n| **Episodic** | Past experiences | Mistakes, solutions, conversation history |\n| **Semantic** | World knowledge | Facts, learnings, reflections |\n| **Procedural** | How to do things | Preferences, workflows, prompt templates |\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n### Global Memory (`~/.claude/memory/`)\n\nCross-project shared knowledge:\n\n```\n~/.claude/memory/\n├── working/                    # Working Memory (可持久化的会话上下文)\n│   └── {name}-context.md       # 保存的会话状态 (通过 /save-context)\n│\n├── procedural/                 # Procedural Memory\n│   ├── preferences.md          # User preferences\n│   ├── workflows.md            # Common workflows\n│   └── prompts/                # Reusable prompt templates\n│       └── {name}.md\n│\n├── semantic/                   # Semantic Memory\n│   ├── learnings/              # Knowledge by topic\n│   │   ├── rust-tips.md\n│   │   ├── git-tips.md\n│   │   └── {topic}.md\n│   └── reflections/            # Insights from reflection\n│       └── {date}-{insight}.md\n│\n├── episodic/                   # Episodic Memory\n│   ├── mistakes/               # Errors and how they were fixed\n│   │   └── {date}-{error}.md\n│   ├── solutions/              # Successfully solved problems\n│   │   └── {date}-{problem}.md\n│   └── trajectories/           # Complete task execution logs\n│       └── {date}-{task}.md\n│\n└── index.json                  # Search index (auto-generated)\n```\n\n### Project Memory (`.claude/memory/`)\n\nProject-specific knowledge:\n\n```\n{project}/.claude/memory/\n├── semantic/\n│   ├── architecture.md         # Project architecture\n│   ├── conventions.md          # Coding conventions\n│   └── decisions.md            # Technical decisions (ADRs)\n│\n├── episodic/\n│   └── sessions/               # Session summaries\n│       └── {date}-{topic}.md\n│\n└── index.json                  # Project search index\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Action | Memory Type |\n|---------|--------|-------------|\n| `/remember <content>` | Save to appropriate memory | Auto-detect |\n| `/recall <topic>` | Search and retrieve | All types |\n| `/forget <topic>` | Delete specific memory | All types |\n| `/reflect` | Generate insights from episodic → semantic | Episodic → Semantic |\n| `/summarize-session` | Save current session summary | Episodic |\n| `/save-context` | Save key context for later resume | Working → File |\n| `/load-context` | Load saved context into session | File → Working |\n\n### Working Memory Commands\n\n**`/save-context [name]`** - 保存当前会话的关键上下文\n\n触发词: \"保存上下文\", \"save context\", \"保存当前状态\"\n\n```markdown\n# 保存到: ~/.claude/memory/working/{name}-context.md 或 .claude/memory/working/\n\n## Session Context: {name}\n**Saved**: {timestamp}\n\n### Current Goals\n- {what we''re trying to accomplish}\n\n### Key Decisions Made\n- {important decisions in this session}\n\n### Important Context\n- {critical information to remember}\n\n### Next Steps\n- {what to do when resuming}\n```\n\n**`/load-context [name]`** - 加载之前保存的上下文\n\n触发词: \"加载上下文\", \"load context\", \"恢复上下文\", \"继续之前的工作\"\n\n1. Search for context files in working/ directory\n2. Display available contexts if name not specified\n3. Load and summarize the selected context\n4. Confirm: \"已加载上下文: {name}\"\n\n## Instructions for Claude\n\n### Action Space (CoALA)\n\nYou have four memory actions:\n\n1. **Retrieval** (读取): Load from long-term → working memory\n2. **Reasoning** (推理): Process in working memory\n3. **Learning** (写入): Save from working → long-term memory\n4. **Forgetting** (遗忘): Remove from long-term memory\n\n### When User Says \"Remember\" / \"记住\"\n\n1. **Detect memory type**:\n   ```\n   Content about...        → Memory Type      → Location\n   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   User preference         → Procedural       → procedural/preferences.md\n   Workflow/process        → Procedural       → procedural/workflows.md\n   Fact/knowledge          → Semantic         → semantic/learnings/{topic}.md\n   Project architecture    → Semantic         → .claude/memory/semantic/architecture.md\n   Error encountered       → Episodic         → episodic/mistakes/{date}-{error}.md\n   Problem solved          → Episodic         → episodic/solutions/{date}-{problem}.md\n   ```\n\n2. **Format content**:\n   ```markdown\n   ## {YYYY-MM-DD} - {brief title}\n\n   {content}\n\n   **Context**: {why this is important}\n   **Tags**: {relevant keywords}\n\n   ---\n   ```\n\n3. **Update index** (if index.json exists):\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"entries\": [\n       {\n         \"file\": \"semantic/learnings/rust-tips.md\",\n         \"keywords\": [\"rust\", \"ownership\", \"borrow\"],\n         \"updated\": \"2026-01-25\"\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Confirm**: Tell user what was saved, where, and memory type\n\n### When User Says \"Recall\" / \"回忆\"\n\n1. **Search priority**:\n   - First: Project memory `.claude/memory/`\n   - Then: Global memory `~/.claude/memory/`\n   - Check: `index.json` for keyword matches\n   - Fallback: Scan file names and content\n\n2. **Return results with metadata**:\n   ```\n   Found 2 relevant memories:\n\n   📁 [Semantic] ~/.claude/memory/semantic/learnings/rust-tips.md\n      → \"Use Arc<Mutex<T>> for shared mutable state...\"\n\n   📁 [Episodic] .claude/memory/episodic/solutions/2026-01-20-async-bug.md\n      → \"Fixed by adding .await after spawn...\"\n   ```\n\n3. **If nothing found**:\n   ```\n   没有找到关于 \"{topic}\" 的记忆。\n   → 使用 /remember 来保存新知识\n   ```\n\n### When User Says \"Forget\" / \"忘记\"\n\n1. **Confirm before deletion**:\n   ```\n   找到以下相关记忆:\n   - ~/.claude/memory/semantic/learnings/old-api.md\n\n   确认删除吗? (y/n)\n   ```\n\n2. **Delete and update index**\n\n3. **Confirm**: \"已删除关于 {topic} 的记忆\"\n\n### When User Says \"Reflect\" / \"反思\"\n\nReflection converts episodic memories into semantic knowledge:\n\n1. **Scan recent episodic memories** (last 7 days)\n\n2. **Identify patterns**:\n   - Repeated mistakes → Learning opportunity\n   - Multiple solutions → Best practice\n   - Common trajectories → Workflow template\n\n3. **Generate reflection**:\n   ```markdown\n   ## 2026-01-25 - Reflection: Async Error Handling\n\n   **Pattern observed**: In 3 recent sessions, async errors were caused by missing .await\n\n   **Insight**: Always check for missing .await when debugging async code\n\n   **Source episodes**:\n   - episodic/mistakes/2026-01-20-async-bug.md\n   - episodic/mistakes/2026-01-22-tokio-error.md\n   - episodic/solutions/2026-01-23-fixed-spawn.md\n\n   ---\n   ```\n\n4. **Save to**: `semantic/reflections/{date}-{insight}.md`\n\n### When User Says \"Summarize Session\" / \"总结会话\"\n\n1. **Gather session context**:\n   - What was accomplished\n   - Key decisions made\n   - Problems encountered and solutions\n   - New learnings\n\n2. **Generate summary**:\n   ```markdown\n   ## 2026-01-25 - Session: Implementing Memory System\n\n   **Goals**: Improve memory-filesystem skill based on CoALA\n\n   **Accomplished**:\n   - Added working memory support\n   - Implemented forgetting mechanism\n   - Added reflection capability\n\n   **Key Decisions**:\n   - Used JSON for search index\n   - Separated global vs project memory\n\n   **Learnings**:\n   - CoALA has 4 memory types, not 3\n\n   ---\n   ```\n\n3. **Save to**:\n   - Project: `.claude/memory/episodic/sessions/{date}-{topic}.md`\n   - Or global: `~/.claude/memory/episodic/trajectories/{date}-{task}.md`\n\n### Auto-Learning (Proactive)\n\nWhen you discover valuable information during a session:\n\n1. **Detect learning opportunity**:\n   - Error fixed → Potential mistake memory\n   - New technique used → Potential learning\n   - Repeated action → Potential workflow\n\n2. **Ask user**: \"发现了一个有用的技巧，要我记住吗？\"\n\n3. **If confirmed**: Save to appropriate memory location\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Trigger | Memory Type | Location |\n|---------|-------------|----------|\n| \"保存上下文\" / \"save context\" | Working | `working/{name}-context.md` |\n| \"加载上下文\" / \"load context\" | Working | Read from `working/` |\n| \"记住这个偏好\" | Procedural | `procedural/preferences.md` |\n| \"记住这个流程\" | Procedural | `procedural/workflows.md` |\n| \"记住这个技巧\" | Semantic | `semantic/learnings/{topic}.md` |\n| \"记住项目架构\" | Semantic | `.claude/memory/semantic/architecture.md` |\n| \"记住这个错误\" | Episodic | `episodic/mistakes/{date}-{error}.md` |\n| \"记住这个解决方案\" | Episodic | `episodic/solutions/{date}-{problem}.md` |\n| \"回忆/你知道...\" | Retrieval | Search all locations |\n| \"忘记...\" | Forgetting | Delete from memory |\n| \"反思\" | Reflection | Episodic → Semantic |\n| \"总结会话\" | Learning | Save session to episodic |\n\n## Example Interactions\n\n### Example 1: Remember\n```\nUser: \"记住：Rust 中使用 thiserror 来定义错误类型\"\n\nClaude:\n1. Detect: Knowledge/fact → Semantic memory\n2. Location: ~/.claude/memory/semantic/learnings/rust-tips.md\n3. Append with date, tags\n4. Update index.json\n5. Response: \"✓ 已保存到语义记忆 (rust-tips.md)\"\n```\n\n### Example 2: Reflect\n```\nUser: \"/reflect\"\n\nClaude:\n1. Scan episodic/mistakes/ and episodic/solutions/ (last 7 days)\n2. Found pattern: 3 instances of borrow checker errors\n3. Generate insight: \"Common cause: trying to move value after borrow\"\n4. Save to: semantic/reflections/2026-01-25-borrow-patterns.md\n5. Response: \"✓ 生成了 1 条反思，已保存到语义记忆\"\n```\n\n### Example 3: Forget\n```\nUser: \"忘记关于旧 API 的记忆\"\n\nClaude:\n1. Search: Found semantic/learnings/old-api-v1.md\n2. Confirm: \"找到 1 条相关记忆，确认删除?\"\n3. User confirms\n4. Delete file, update index\n5. Response: \"✓ 已删除关于旧 API 的记忆\"\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:26:11.262Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cognitive Language Agents requiring advanced memory management capabilities based on the CoALA framework","zh":"适用于需要基于CoALA框架的高级内存管理功能的认知语言代理","ja":"CoALAフレームワークに基づく高度なメモリ管理機能を必要とする認知言語エージェントに適しています","ko":"CoALA 프레임워크 기반의 고급 메모리 관리 기능을 필요로 하는 인지 언어 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje Cognitivo que requieren capacidades de gestión de memoria avanzadas basadas en el marco CoALA","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Langage Cognitif nécessitant des capacités de gestion de mémoire avancées basées sur le cadre CoALA","de":"Ideal für kognitive Sprachagenten, die erweiterte Speicherverwaltungsfunktionen auf Basis des CoALA-Frameworks benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem Cognitiva que requerem capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de memória com base no framework CoALA","ru":"Идеально для когнитивных языковых агентов, требующих продвинутых возможностей управления памятью на основе фреймворка CoALA","ar":"مثالية لعمليات اللغة المعرفية التي تتطلب إمكانيات متقدمة لإدارة الذاكرة بناءً على إطار العمل CoALA"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage a cognitive architecture with four distinct memory types, utilizing a Working Memory as a short-term central hub, and integrating with a Filesystem-based memory system, enabling efficient information storage and retrieval through protocols like CoALA","zh":"使代理能够利用具有四种不同内存类型的认知架构，使用工作内存作为短期的中心枢纽，并与基于文件系统的内存系统集成，通过CoALA等协议实现高效的信息存储和检索","ja":"エージェントが4つの異なるメモリタイプを持つ認知アーキテクチャを利用できるようにし、ワーキングメモリを短期の中央ハブとして使用し、ファイルシステムベースのメモリシステムと統合し、CoALAなどのプロトコルを介して効率的な情報の保存と取得を可能にします","ko":"에이전트가 4가지 다른 메모리 유형을 갖는 인지 아키텍처를 활용할 수 있도록 하며, 작업 메모리를 단기 중앙 허브로 사용하고, 파일 시스템 기반의 메모리 시스템과 통합하여 CoALA 등의 프로토콜을 통해 효율적인 정보 저장 및 검색을 가능하게 합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar una arquitectura cognitiva con cuatro tipos de memoria distintos, utilizando una Memoria de Trabajo como centro central de corto plazo, e integrándose con un sistema de memoria basado en Filesystem, lo que permite un almacenamiento y recuperación de información eficientes a través de protocolos como CoALA","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter une architecture cognitive avec quatre types de mémoire distincts, en utilisant une Mémoire de Travail comme hub central à court terme, et en s''intégrant avec un système de mémoire basé sur Filesystem, permettant un stockage et une récupération d''informations efficaces via des protocoles comme CoALA","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, eine kognitive Architektur mit vier unterschiedlichen Speichertypen zu nutzen, indem sie ein Arbeitsgedächtnis als zentrales Kurzzeit-Hub verwenden und sich in ein Dateisystem-basiertes Speichersystem integrieren, wodurch ein effizientes Speichern und Abrufen von Informationen über Protokolle wie CoALA ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita agentes a aproveitar uma arquitetura cognitiva com quatro tipos distintos de memória, utilizando uma Memória de Trabalho como um hub central de curto prazo, e integrando com um sistema de memória baseado em Filesystem, permitindo o armazenamento e recuperação eficientes de informações por meio de protocolos como CoALA","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать когнитивную архитектуру с четырьмя различными типами памяти, используя Оперативную Память как центральный узел короткого срока, и интегрируя с системой памяти на основе Файловой Системы, обеспечивая эффективное хранение и извлечение информации через протоколы như CoALA","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من هندسة معرفية مع أربعة أنواع مميزة من الذاكرة، باستخدام ذاكرة العمل كمركز مركزي قصير الأجل، وتكامل مع نظام ذاكرة قائم على نظام الملفات، مما يسمح بتخزين واسترجاع المعلومات بكفاءة من خلال بروتوكولات مثل CoALA"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing short-term memory for temporary data storage","Developing long-term memory for persistent knowledge retention","Integrating episodic memory for event-based learning"],"zh":["为临时数据存储实现短期内存","为持久知识保留开发长期内存","为基于事件的学习集成情景记忆"],"ja":["一時的なデータストレージのための短期メモリの実装","永続的な知識保持のための長期メモリの開発","イベントベースの学習のためのエピソードメモリの統合"],"ko":["임시 데이터 저장을 위한 단기 메모리 구현","지속적인 지식 보유를 위한 장기 메모리 개발","이벤트 기반 학습을 위한 에피소드 메모리 통합"],"es":["Implementar memoria a corto plazo para almacenamiento de datos temporales","Desarrollar memoria a largo plazo para retención de conocimiento persistente","Integrar memoria episódica para aprendizaje basado en eventos"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre une mémoire à court terme pour le stockage de données temporaires","Développer une mémoire à long terme pour la rétention de connaissances persistantes","Intégrer une mémoire épisodique pour l''apprentissage basé sur les événements"],"de":["Implementierung von Kurzzeitgedächtnis für temporären Datenspeicher","Entwicklung von Langzeitgedächtnis für persistente Wissensspeicherung","Integration von episodischem Gedächtnis für ereignisbasiertes Lernen"],"pt":["Implementar memória de curto prazo para armazenamento de dados temporários","Desenvolver memória de longo prazo para retenção de conhecimento persistente","Integrar memória episódica para aprendizado baseado em eventos"],"ru":["Реализовать краткосрочную память для временного хранения данных","Разработать долгосрочную память для постоянного сохранения знаний","Интегрировать эпизодическую память для событийного обучения"],"ar":["تنفيذ ذاكرة قصيرة الأجل لتخزين البيانات المؤقتة","تطوير ذاكرة طويلة الأجل لاستبقاء المعرفة المستدامة","تكامل الذاكرة الحوادثية للتعلم القائم على الأحداث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CoALA framework integration","Dependent on Filesystem access for memory operations"],"zh":["需要CoALA框架集成","依赖于文件系统访问用于内存操作"],"ja":["CoALAフレームワークの統合が必要","メモリ操作にファイルシステムアクセスに依存"],"ko":["CoALA 프레임워크 통합이 필요","메모리 작업에 파일 시스템 액세스에 의존"],"es":["Requiere integración del marco CoALA","Dependiente del acceso al Filesystem para operaciones de memoria"],"fr":["Nécessite l''intégration du cadre CoALA","Dépendant de l''accès au Filesystem pour les opérations de mémoire"],"de":["Benötigt Integration des CoALA-Frameworks","Abhängig vom Dateisystem-Zugriff für Speicheroperationen"],"pt":["Requer integração com o framework CoALA","Dependente do acesso ao Filesystem para operações de memória"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с фреймворком CoALA","Зависит от доступа к Файловой Системе для операций с памятью"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل مع إطار العمل CoALA","يعتمد على الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لعمليات الذاكرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
