 빠르게 이해하고 사용할 수 있도록 한다","es":"La habilidad Kata Help muestra la referencia completa de habilidades con información de versión. Se utiliza para obtener la versión instalada y mostrar la re...","fr":"La compétence Kata Help affiche la référence complète des compétences avec des informations de version. Elle est utilisée pour obtenir la version installée e...","de":"Die Fähigkeit Kata Help zeigt die vollständige Referenz der Fähigkeiten mit Versionsinformationen an. Sie wird verwendet, um die installierte Version zu erha...","pt":"A habilidade Kata Help fornece uma referência técnica completa para desenvolvedores","ru":"Навык Kata Help предоставляет полную техническую справку для разработчиков","ar":"تمكن مهارة كاتا هيلب المطورين من الحصول على مرجع تقني كامل","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["版本信息","功能参考","快速查阅","开发者工具","技术支持"],"ja":["バージョン情報","機能リファレンス","迅速な参照","開発者ツール","技術サポート"],"ko":["버전 정보","기능 참조","快速 참조","개발자 도구","기술 지원"],"es":["Muestra la versión instalada de la habilidad","Proporciona la referencia completa de habilidades","No incluye análisis de proyectos específicos","No incluye estado de Git o contexto de archivo","No incluye sugerencias de siguientes pasos"],"fr":["Affiche la version installée de la compétence","Fournit la référence complète des compétences","N''inclut pas d''analyse de projets spécifiques","N''inclut pas d''état de Git ou de contexte de fichier","N''inclut pas de suggestions de prochaines étapes"],"de":["Zeigt die installierte Version der Fähigkeit an","Bietet die vollständige Referenz der Fähigkeiten","Enthält keine Analyse von Projekten","Enthält keinen Git-Status oder Dateikontext","Enthält keine Vorschläge für nächste Schritte"],"pt":["Fornece referência técnica completa","Inclui informações de versão","Não inclui análise de projeto específico","Não inclui status do Git ou contexto de arquivos","Não inclui sugestões de próximas etapas"],"ru":["Предоставляет полную техническую справку","Включает информацию о версии","Не включает анализ конкретного проекта","Не включает статус Git или контекст файлов","Не включает предложения следующих шагов"],"ar":["تقدم مرجع تقني كامل","يتضمن معلومات عن الإصدار","لا يتضمن تحليل مشروع محدد","لا يتضمن حالة Git أو سياق الملفات","لا يتضمن اقتراحات الخطوات التالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kata 技能","版本信息","功能参考","开发者工具","技术支持","快速查阅"],"ja":["Kata スキル","バージョン情報","機能リファレンス","開発者ツール","技術サポート","迅速な参照"],"ko":["Kata 기술","버전 정보","기능 참조","개발자 도구","기술 지원","快速 참조"],"es":["Kata Help","referencia de habilidad","información de versión","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","competencias técnicas"],"fr":["Kata Help","référence de compétence","informations de version","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","compétences techniques"],"de":["Kata Help","Fähigkeitsreferenz","Versionsinformationen","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","technische Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Kata Help","Referência Técnica","Desenvolvimento de Soluções","Habilidades Técnicas","Versão de Software","Desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Kata Help","Техническая Справка","Разработка Решений","Технические Навыки","Версия Программного Обеспечения","Разработчики"],"ar":["كата هيلب","مرجع تقني","تطوير حلول","مهارات تقنية","إصدار البرمجيات","مطورون"]}},"owner":"gannonh","repo":"kata-skills","repoPath":"gannonh/kata-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kata-help","description":"Show available Kata skills, displaying the usage guide, explaining skill reference, or when the user asks for help with Kata. Triggers include help, show skills, list skills, what skills, kata skills, and usage guide.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nDisplay the complete Kata skill reference with version info.\n\nFirst, read the installed version:\n\n```bash\nif [ -n \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\" ]; then\n  cat \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null\nelse\n  echo \"unknown\"\nfi\n```\n\nThen output the reference content below, inserting the version at the top. Do NOT add:\n\n- Project-specific analysis\n- Git status or file context\n- Next-step suggestions\n- Any commentary beyond the reference\n  </objective>\n\n<reference>\n# Kata Skill Reference\n\n**Versi","body":"<objective>\nDisplay the complete Kata skill reference with version info.\n\nFirst, read the installed version:\n\n```bash\nif [ -n \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\" ]; then\n  cat \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null\nelse\n  echo \"unknown\"\nfi\n```\n\nThen output the reference content below, inserting the version at the top. Do NOT add:\n\n- Project-specific analysis\n- Git status or file context\n- Next-step suggestions\n- Any commentary beyond the reference\n  </objective>\n\n<reference>\n# Kata Skill Reference\n\n**Version:** {version from bash above}\n\n**Kata** is a spec-driven development framework for Claude Code. It creates hierarchical project plans optimized for agentic development.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n1. `/kata-new-project` - Initialize project (includes research, requirements, roadmap)\n2. `/kata-plan-phase 1` - Create detailed plan for first phase\n3. `/kata-execute-phase 1` - Execute the phase\n\n## Staying Updated\n\nKata evolves fast. Check for updates periodically:\n\n```\n/kata-whats-new\n```\n\nShows what changed since your installed version and how to update.\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n```\n/kata-new-project → /kata-plan-phase → /kata-execute-phase → repeat\n```\n\n### Project Initialization\n\n**`/kata-new-project`**\nInitialize new project through unified flow.\n\nOne skill takes you from idea to ready-for-planning:\n\n- Deep questioning to understand what you''re building\n- Optional domain research (spawns 4 parallel researcher agents)\n- Requirements definition with v1/v2/out-of-scope scoping\n- Roadmap creation with phase breakdown and success criteria\n\nCreates all `.planning/` artifacts:\n\n- `PROJECT.md` — vision and requirements\n- `config.json` — workflow mode (interactive/yolo)\n- `research/` — domain research (if selected)\n- `REQUIREMENTS.md` — scoped requirements with REQ-IDs\n- `ROADMAP.md` — phases mapped to requirements\n- `STATE.md` — project memory\n\nUsage: `/kata-new-project`\n\n**`/kata-map-codebase`**\nMap an existing codebase for brownfield projects.\n\n- Analyzes codebase with parallel Explore agents\n- Creates `.planning/codebase/` with 7 focused documents\n- Covers stack, architecture, structure, conventions, testing, integrations, concerns\n- Use before `/kata-new-project` on existing codebases\n\nUsage: `/kata-map-codebase`\n\n### Phase Planning\n\n**`/kata-discuss-phase <number>`**\nHelp articulate your vision for a phase before planning.\n\n- Captures how you imagine this phase working\n- Creates CONTEXT.md with your vision, essentials, and boundaries\n- Use when you have ideas about how something should look/feel\n\nUsage: `/kata-discuss-phase 2`\n\n**`/kata-research-phase <number>`**\nComprehensive ecosystem research for niche/complex domains.\n\n- Discovers standard stack, architecture patterns, pitfalls\n- Creates RESEARCH.md with \"how experts build this\" knowledge\n- Use for 3D, games, audio, shaders, ML, and other specialized domains\n- Goes beyond \"which library\" to ecosystem knowledge\n\nUsage: `/kata-research-phase 3`\n\n**`/kata-listing-phase-assumptions <number>`**\nSee what Claude is planning to do before it starts.\n\n- Shows Claude''s intended approach for a phase\n- Lets you course-correct if Claude misunderstood your vision\n- No files created - conversational output only\n\nUsage: `/kata-listing-phase-assumptions 3`\n\n**`/kata-plan-phase <number>`**\nCreate detailed execution plan for a specific phase.\n\n- Generates `.planning/phases/pending/XX-phase-name/XX-YY-PLAN.md`\n- Breaks phase into concrete, actionable tasks\n- Includes verification criteria and success measures\n- Multiple plans per phase supported (XX-01, XX-02, etc.)\n\nUsage: `/kata-plan-phase 1`\nResult: Creates `.planning/phases/pending/01-foundation/01-01-PLAN.md`\n\n### Execution\n\n**`/kata-execute-phase <phase-number>`**\nExecute all plans in a phase.\n\n- Moves phase from `pending/` → `active/` → `completed/`\n- Groups plans by wave (from frontmatter), executes waves sequentially\n- Plans within each wave run in parallel via Task tool\n- Verifies phase goal after all plans complete\n- Updates REQUIREMENTS.md, ROADMAP.md, STATE.md\n\nUsage: `/kata-execute-phase 5`\n\n### Quick Mode\n\n**`/kata-execute-quick-task`**\nExecute small, ad-hoc tasks with Kata guarantees but skip optional agents.\n\nQuick mode uses the same system with a shorter path:\n\n- Spawns planner + executor (skips researcher, checker, verifier)\n- Quick tasks live in `.planning/quick/` separate from planned phases\n- Updates STATE.md tracking (not ROADMAP.md)\n\nUse when you know exactly what to do and the task is small enough to not need research or verification.\n\nUsage: `/kata-execute-quick-task`\nResult: Creates `.planning/quick/NNN-slug/PLAN.md`, `.planning/quick/NNN-slug/SUMMARY.md`\n\n### Roadmap Management\n\n**`/kata-add-phase <description>`**\nAdd new phase to end of current milestone.\n\n- Appends to ROADMAP.md\n- Uses next sequential number\n- Creates phase directory in `pending/`\n\nUsage: `/kata-add-phase \"Add admin dashboard\"`\n\n**`/kata-insert-phase <after> <description>`**\nInsert urgent work as decimal phase between existing phases.\n\n- Creates intermediate phase (e.g., 7.1 between 7 and 8)\n- Useful for discovered work that must happen mid-milestone\n- Maintains phase ordering\n\nUsage: `/kata-insert-phase 7 \"Fix critical auth bug\"`\nResult: Creates Phase 7.1\n\n**`/kata-remove-phase <number>`**\nRemove a future phase and renumber subsequent phases.\n\n- Deletes phase directory and all references\n- Renumbers all subsequent phases to close the gap\n- Only works on future (unstarted) phases\n- Git commit preserves historical record\n\nUsage: `/kata-remove-phase 17`\nResult: Phase 17 deleted, phases 18-20 become 17-19\n\n**`/kata-move-phase <phase> <operation>`**\nMove a phase between milestones or reorder within a milestone.\n\n- Cross-milestone: moves phase to target milestone, renumbers both\n- Reorder: changes phase position within milestone, renumbers all\n- Only pending phases can be moved\n\nUsage: `/kata-move-phase 3 to v1.6.0` (cross-milestone)\nUsage: `/kata-move-phase 3 before 1` (reorder within milestone)\n\n### Milestone Management\n\n**`/kata-add-milestone <name>`**\nStart a new milestone through unified flow.\n\n- Deep questioning to understand what you''re building next\n- Optional domain research (spawns 4 parallel researcher agents)\n- Requirements definition with scoping\n- Roadmap creation with phase breakdown\n\nMirrors `/kata-new-project` flow for brownfield projects (existing PROJECT.md).\n\nUsage: `/kata-add-milestone \"v2.0 Features\"`\n\n**`/kata-complete-milestone <version>`**\nArchive completed milestone and prepare for next version.\n\n- Creates MILESTONES.md entry with stats\n- Archives full details to milestones/ directory\n- Creates git tag for the release\n- Prepares workspace for next version\n\nUsage: `/kata-complete-milestone 1.0.0`\n\n### Progress Tracking\n\n**`/kata-track-progress`**\nCheck project status and intelligently route to next action.\n\n- Shows visual progress bar and completion percentage\n- Summarizes recent work from SUMMARY files\n- Displays current position and what''s next\n- Lists key decisions and open issues\n- Offers to execute next plan or create it if missing\n- Detects 100% milestone completion\n\nUsage: `/kata-track-progress`\n\n### Session Management\n\n**`/kata-resume-work`**\nResume work from previous session with full context restoration.\n\n- Reads STATE.md for project context\n- Shows current position and recent progress\n- Offers next actions based on project state\n\nUsage: `/kata-resume-work`\n\n**`/kata-pause-work`**\nCreate context handoff when pausing work mid-phase.\n\n- Creates .continue-here file with current state\n- Updates STATE.md session continuity section\n- Captures in-progress work context\n\nUsage: `/kata-pause-work`\n\n### Debugging\n\n**`/kata-debug [issue description]`**\nSystematic debugging with persistent state across context resets.\n\n- Gathers symptoms through adaptive questioning\n- Creates `.planning/debug/[slug].md` to track investigation\n- Investigates using scientific method (evidence → hypothesis → test)\n- Survives `/clear` — run `/kata-debug` with no args to resume\n- Archives resolved issues to `.planning/debug/resolved/`\n\nUsage: `/kata-debug \"login button doesn''t work\"`\nUsage: `/kata-debug` (resume active session)\n\n### Issue Management\n\n**`/kata-add-issue [description]`**\nCapture idea or task as issue from current conversation.\n\n- Extracts context from conversation (or uses provided description)\n- Creates structured issue file in `.planning/issues/open/`\n- Infers area from file paths for grouping\n- Checks for duplicates before creating\n- Updates STATE.md issue count\n\nUsage: `/kata-add-issue` (infers from conversation)\nUsage: `/kata-add-issue Add auth token refresh`\n\n**`/kata-check-issues [area]`**\nList pending issues and select one to work on.\n\n- Lists all pending issues with title, area, age\n- Optional area filter (e.g., `/kata-check-issues api`)\n- Loads full context for selected issue\n- Routes to appropriate action (work now, add to phase, brainstorm)\n- Moves issue to done/ when work begins\n\nUsage: `/kata-check-issues`\nUsage: `/kata-check-issues api`\n\n### User Acceptance Testing\n\n**`/kata-verify-work [phase]`**\nValidate built features through conversational UAT.\n\n- Extracts testable deliverables from SUMMARY.md files\n- Presents tests one at a time (yes/no responses)\n- Automatically diagnoses failures and creates fix plans\n- Ready for re-execution if issues found\n\nUsage: `/kata-verify-work 3`\n\n### Milestone Auditing\n\n**`/kata-audit-milestone [version]`**\nAudit milestone completion against original intent.\n\n- Reads all phase VERIFICATION.md files\n- Checks requirements coverage\n- Spawns integration checker for cross-phase wiring\n- Creates MILESTONE-AUDIT.md with gaps and tech debt\n\nUsage: `/kata-audit-milestone`\n\n**`/kata-plan-milestone-gaps`**\nCreate phases to close gaps identified by audit.\n\n- Reads MILESTONE-AUDIT.md and groups gaps into phases\n- Prioritizes by requirement priority (must/should/nice)\n- Adds gap closure phases to ROADMAP.md\n- Ready for `/kata-plan-phase` on new phases\n\nUsage: `/kata-plan-milestone-gaps`\n\n### Configuration\n\n**`/kata-customize`**\nManage template overrides for customizing Kata output formats.\n\n- List all customizable templates with override status\n- Copy a default template for local editing\n- Edit an override with conversational changes\n- Validate overrides against required schemas\n\nUsage: `/kata-customize`\nUsage: `/kata-customize list`\nUsage: `/kata-customize copy summary-template.md`\nUsage: `/kata-customize validate`\n\n**`/kata-configure-settings`**\nConfigure workflow toggles and model profile interactively.\n\n- Toggle researcher, plan checker, verifier agents\n- Select model profile (quality/balanced/budget)\n- Updates `.planning/config.json`\n\nUsage: `/kata-configure-settings`\n\n**`/kata-set-profile <profile>`**\nQuick switch model profile for Kata agents.\n\n- `quality` — Opus everywhere except verification\n- `balanced` — Opus for planning, Sonnet for execution (default)\n- `budget` — Sonnet for writing, Haiku for research/verification\n\nUsage: `/kata-set-profile budget`\n\n### Utility Skills\n\n**`/kata-help`**\nShow this skill reference.\n\n**`/kata-whats-new`**\nSee what''s changed since your installed version.\n\n- Shows installed vs latest version comparison\n- Displays changelog entries for versions you''ve missed\n- Highlights breaking changes\n- Provides update instructions when behind\n\nUsage: `/kata-whats-new`\n\n## Files & Structure\n\n```\n.planning/\n├── PROJECT.md            # Project vision\n├── REQUIREMENTS.md       # Scoped requirements with REQ-IDs\n├── ROADMAP.md            # Current phase breakdown\n├── STATE.md              # Project memory & context\n├── MILESTONES.md         # Completed milestone history\n├── config.json           # Workflow mode & gates\n├── templates/            # Template overrides (customized output formats)\n├── research/             # Domain research (from project init)\n├── issues/               # Captured ideas and tasks\n│   ├── open/             # Issues waiting to be worked on\n│   └── done/             # Completed issues\n├── debug/                # Active debug sessions\n│   └── resolved/         # Archived resolved issues\n├── codebase/             # Codebase map (brownfield projects)\n│   ├── STACK.md          # Languages, frameworks, dependencies\n│   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md   # Patterns, layers, data flow\n│   ├── STRUCTURE.md      # Directory layout, key files\n│   ├── CONVENTIONS.md    # Coding standards, naming\n│   ├── TESTING.md        # Test setup, patterns\n│   ├── INTEGRATIONS.md   # External services, APIs\n│   └── CONCERNS.md       # Tech debt, known issues\n├── milestones/           # Archived milestone details\n├── quick/                # Quick task plans and summaries\n│   └── NNN-slug/\n│       ├── PLAN.md\n│       └── SUMMARY.md\n└── phases/\n    ├── pending/          # Phases not yet started\n    │   └── 03-next-phase/\n    │       └── 03-01-PLAN.md\n    ├── active/           # Phase currently being executed\n    │   └── 02-in-progress/\n    │       ├── 02-01-PLAN.md\n    │       └── 02-01-SUMMARY.md\n    └── completed/        # Finished phases\n        └── 01-foundation/\n            ├── 01-01-PLAN.md\n            └── 01-01-SUMMARY.md\n```\n\n## Workflow Modes\n\nSet during `/kata-new-project`:\n\n**Interactive Mode**\n\n- Confirms each major decision\n- Pauses at checkpoints for approval\n- More guidance throughout\n\n**YOLO Mode**\n\n- Auto-approves most decisions\n- Executes plans without confirmation\n- Only stops for critical checkpoints\n\nChange anytime by editing `.planning/config.json`\n\n## Planning Configuration\n\nConfigure how planning artifacts are managed in `.planning/config.json`:\n\n**`planning.commit_docs`** (default: `true`)\n\n- `true`: Planning artifacts committed to git (standard workflow)\n- `false`: Planning artifacts kept local-only, not committed\n\nWhen `commit_docs: false`:\n\n- Add `.planning/` to your `.gitignore`\n- Useful for OSS contributions, client projects, or keeping planning private\n- All planning files still work normally, just not tracked in git\n\n**`planning.search_gitignored`** (default: `false`)\n\n- `true`: Add `--no-ignore` to broad ripgrep searches\n- Only needed when `.planning/` is gitignored and you want project-wide searches to include it\n\nExample config:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"planning\": {\n    \"commit_docs\": false,\n    \"search_gitignored\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n**Starting a new project:**\n\n```\n/kata-new-project        # Unified flow: questioning → research → requirements → roadmap\n/clear\n/kata-plan-phase 1       # Create plans for first phase\n/clear\n/kata-execute-phase 1    # Execute all plans in phase\n```\n\n**Resuming work after a break:**\n\n```\n/kata-track-progress  # See where you left off and continue\n```\n\n**Adding urgent mid-milestone work:**\n\n```\n/kata-insert-phase 5 \"Critical security fix\"\n/kata-plan-phase 5.1\n/kata-execute-phase 5.1\n```\n\n**Completing a milestone:**\n\n```\n/kata-complete-milestone 1.0.0\n/clear\n/kata-add-milestone  # Start next milestone (questioning → research → requirements → roadmap)\n```\n\n**Capturing ideas during work:**\n\n```\n/kata-add-issue                    # Capture from conversation context\n/kata-add-issue Fix modal z-index  # Capture with explicit description\n/kata-check-issues                 # Review and work on issues\n/kata-check-issues api             # Filter by area\n```\n\n**Debugging an issue:**\n\n```\n/kata-debug \"form submission fails silently\"  # Start debug session\n# ... investigation happens, context fills up ...\n/clear\n/kata-debug                                    # Resume from where you left off\n```\n\n## Getting Help\n\n- Read `.planning/PROJECT.md` for project vision\n- Read `.planning/STATE.md` for current context\n- Check `.planning/ROADMAP.md` for phase status\n- Run `/kata-track-progress` to check where you''re up to\n  </reference>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:29:30.158Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing detailed skill reference documentation.","zh":"非常适合需要详细技能参考文档的开发者代理。","ja":"詳細なスキル参照ドキュメントが必要な開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"상세한 스킬 참조 문서가 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan documentación de referencia de habilidades detallada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une documentation de référence de compétences détaillée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwickler-Agenten, die eine detaillierte Fertigkeitsreferenzdokumentation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que necessitam de documentação de referência de habilidades detalhada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-разработчиков, которым необходима подробная документация по навыкам.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى توثيق مرجعي مفصل للمهارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to display complete Kata skill references with version information, utilizing bash commands for version retrieval and plain text output for reference content, including objectives and references.","zh":"赋予代理显示完整的Kata技能参考，包括版本信息，利用bash命令进行版本检索和纯文本输出参考内容，包括目标和参考。","ja":"エージェントがKataスキル参照を完全に表示できるようにし、バージョン情報を含め、bashコマンドを使用してバージョン情報を取得し、プレーンテキスト出力で参照内容、目標、および参照を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Kata 스킬 참조를 완전히 표시할 수 있도록 하며, 버전 정보를 포함하여 bash 명령을 사용하여 버전 정보를 검색하고 평문 출력으로 참조 내용, 목표 및 참조를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mostrar referencias de habilidades Kata completas con información de versión, utilizando comandos bash para la recuperación de versiones y salida de texto plano para el contenido de referencia, incluyendo objetivos y referencias.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''afficher des références de compétences Kata complètes avec des informations de version, en utilisant des commandes bash pour la récupération de versions et une sortie de texte brut pour le contenu de référence, y compris les objectifs et les références.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, vollständige Kata-Fertigkeitsreferenzen mit Versionsinformationen anzuzeigen, indem Bash-Befehle für die Versionsabruf und einfacher Textausgabe für den Referenzinhalt verwendet werden, einschließlich Ziele und Referenzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a exibir referências de habilidades Kata completas com informações de versão, utilizando comandos bash para recuperação de versão e saída de texto simples para conteúdo de referência, incluindo objetivos e referências.","ru":"Позволяет агентам отображать полные справочные материалы по навыкам Kata с информацией о версии, используя команды bash для получения версии и вывода простого текста для справочного контента, включая цели и ссылки.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من عرض مرجعيات كاملة لمهارات كاتا مع معلومات إصدار، باستخدام أوامر باش لاسترجاع الإصدار وخرج نص عادي لمحتوى المرجع، بما في ذلك الأهداف والمراجع."},"useCases":{"en":["Displaying skill version information","Generating reference documentation","Providing objective-based content previews"],"zh":["显示技能版本信息","生成参考文档","提供基于目标的内容预览"],"ja":["スキルバージョン情報の表示","参照ドキュメントの生成","目標ベースのコンテンツプレビューの提供"],"ko":["스킬 버전 정보 표시","참조 문서 생성","목표 기반 콘텐츠 미리 보기 제공"],"es":["Mostrar información de versión de habilidad","Generar documentación de referencia","Proporcionar vistas previas de contenido basadas en objetivos"],"fr":["Afficher les informations de version de compétence","Générer une documentation de référence","Fournir des aperçus de contenu basés sur des objectifs"],"de":["Anzeigen von Fertigkeitsversionsinformationen","Erzeugen von Referenzdokumentation","Bereitstellen von inhaltsbasierten Vorschauen"],"pt":["Exibir informações de versão de habilidade","Gerar documentação de referência","Fornecer visualizações de conteúdo baseadas em objetivos"],"ru":["Отображение информации о версии навыка","Генерация справочной документации","Предоставление предварительных просмотров контента на основе целей"],"ar":["عرض معلومات إصدار المهارة","генерация توثيق مرجعي","توفير معاينة المحتوى المعتمد على الأهداف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT environment variable","Limited to Kata skill reference documentation"],"zh":["需要访问CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT环境变量","仅限Kata技能参考文档"],"ja":["CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT環境変数へのアクセスが必要","Kataスキル参照ドキュメントのみ"],"ko":["CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT 환경 변수에 접근해야 함","Kata 스킬 참조 문서만"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la variable de entorno CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","Limitado a la documentación de referencia de habilidades Kata"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la variable d''environnement CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","Limité à la documentation de référence de compétences Kata"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Umgebungsvariable CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","Begrenzt auf die Referenzdokumentation von Kata-Fertigkeiten"],"pt":["Requer acesso à variável de ambiente CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","Limitado à documentação de referência de habilidades Kata"],"ru":["Требует доступа к переменной среды CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","Ограничен справочной документацией по навыкам Kata"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى متغير البيئة CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT","محدود بالتوثيق المرجعي لمهارات كاتا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/vibe-coding', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'vibe-coding', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:29:38.111Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/vibe-coding","name":"vibe-coding","description":{"zh":"Vibe Coding - AI","ja":"Vibe Coding - AI","ko":"Vibe Coding - AI","es":"Vibe Coding es una habilidad que ayuda a los desarrolladores a crear software utilizando herramientas de IA y lenguaje natural","fr":"Vibe Coding est une compétence qui aide les développeurs à créer des logiciels en utilisant des outils d''IA et du langage naturel","de":"Vibe Coding ist eine Fähigkeit, die Entwicklern hilft, Software mit KI-Tools und natürlicher Sprache zu erstellen","pt":"O Vibe Coding é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que utiliza ferramentas de IA e linguagem natural para criar soluções personalizadas","ru":"Vibe Coding - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который использует инструменты ИИ и естественный язык для создания индивидуальных решений","ar":"كود النبض هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يستخدم أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي واللغة الطبيعية لإنشاء حلول مخصصة","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Vibe Coding - AI","ja":"Vibe Coding - AI","ko":"Vibe Coding - AI","es":"Vibe Coding: Desarrollo de Software con IA","fr":"Vibe Coding: Développement de Logiciels avec l''IA","de":"Vibe Coding: Softwareentwicklung mit KI","pt":"Vibe Coding: Desenvolvimento de Software com IA","ru":"Vibe Coding: Создание Программного Обеспечения с ИИ","ar":"كود النبض: تطوير البرمجيات باستخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"vibe-coding"},"description":{"zh":"Vibe Coding - AI","ja":"Vibe Coding - AI","ko":"Vibe Coding - AI","es":"Vibe Coding es una habilidad que ayuda a los desarrolladores a crear software utilizando herramientas de IA y lenguaje natural","fr":"Vibe Coding est une compétence qui aide les développeurs à créer des logiciels en utilisant des outils d''IA et du langage naturel","de":"Vibe Coding ist eine Fähigkeit, die Entwicklern hilft, Software mit KI-Tools und natürlicher Sprache zu erstellen","pt":"O Vibe Coding é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que utiliza ferramentas de IA e linguagem natural para criar soluções personalizadas","ru":"Vibe Coding - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который использует инструменты ИИ и естественный язык для создания индивидуальных решений","ar":"كود النبض هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يستخدم أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي واللغة الطبيعية لإنشاء حلول مخصصة","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["AI","Vibe Coding"," "," "," "],"ja":["AI","Vibe Coding"," "," "," "],"ko":["AI","Vibe Coding"," "," "," "],"es":["Desarrollo de software con herramientas de IA","Uso de lenguaje natural para crear código","Guía para la creación de prototipos y aplicaciones de producción","Iteración y refinamiento del código con prompts de IA","Colaboración con líderes de productos para obtener insights y conocimientos"],"fr":["Développement de logiciels avec des outils d''IA","Utilisation du langage naturel pour créer du code","Guide pour la création de prototypes et d''applications de production","Itération et raffinement du code avec des prompts d''IA","Collaboration avec des leaders de produits pour obtenir des insights et des connaissances"],"de":["Softwareentwicklung mit KI-Tools","Verwendung von natürlicher Sprache zur Code-Erstellung","Leitfaden für die Erstellung von Prototypen und Produktionsanwendungen","Iteration und Verfeinerung des Codes mit KI-Prompts","Zusammenarbeit mit Produktleitern für Erkenntnisse und Wissen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de software personalizado","Utilização de ferramentas de IA","Linguagem natural para criação de soluções","Abordagem iterativa para resolução de problemas","Otimização de processos de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Индивидуальное разработка программного обеспечения","Использование инструментов ИИ","Естественный язык для создания решений","Итеративный подход к решению проблем","Оптимизация процессов разработки"],"ar":["تطوير برمجيات مخصص","استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","اللغة الطبيعية لإنشاء حلول","نهج تكراري لحل المشكلات","تحسين عمليات التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Vibe Coding","AI"," "," "," "," "],"ja":["Vibe Coding","AI"," "," "," "," "],"ko":["Vibe Coding","AI"," "," "," "," "],"es":["vibe coding","desarrollo de software","herramientas de IA","lenguaje natural","prototipos","aplicaciones de producción","code iteration","refinamiento de código"],"fr":["vibe coding","développement de logiciels","outils d''IA","langage naturel","prototypes","applications de production","itération de code","raffinement de code"],"de":["vibe coding","softwareentwicklung","KI-Tools","natürliche Sprache","Prototypen","Produktionsanwendungen","Code-Iteration","Code-Verfeinerung"],"pt":["vibe coding","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de ia","linguagem natural","soluções personalizadas","tecnologia de ia","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","programação de software"],"ru":["vibe coding","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты ии","естественный язык","индивидуальные решения","технология ии","разработка приложений","программирование программного обеспечения"],"ar":["كود النبض","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","اللغة الطبيعية","حلول مخصصة","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير التطبيقات","برمجة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vibe-coding","description":"Help users build software using AI coding tools. Use when someone is using AI to generate code, building prototypes without deep technical skills, or exploring how non-engineers can create functional software through natural language.","bodyPreview":"# Vibe Coding\n\nHelp the user build software using AI tools and natural language, using frameworks and insights from 3 product leaders.\n\n## How to Help\n\nWhen the user asks for help with vibe coding:\n\n1. **Understand the goal** - Ask what they''re trying to build and who it''s for (prototype, internal tool, production app)\n2. **Guide the approach** - Help them break down the problem into smaller pieces for iterative AI prompts\n3. **Set expectations** - Discuss what vibe coding is good for (prototype","body":"# Vibe Coding\n\nHelp the user build software using AI tools and natural language, using frameworks and insights from 3 product leaders.\n\n## How to Help\n\nWhen the user asks for help with vibe coding:\n\n1. **Understand the goal** - Ask what they''re trying to build and who it''s for (prototype, internal tool, production app)\n2. **Guide the approach** - Help them break down the problem into smaller pieces for iterative AI prompts\n3. **Set expectations** - Discuss what vibe coding is good for (prototypes, MVPs) versus when professional engineering is needed\n4. **Coach on iteration** - Help them understand how to refine output through follow-up prompts\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Vibe coding is a new skill\nElena Verna: \"I vibe code myself so I would put that as even as a skill on my resume now.\" This is a distinct, transformative skill for non-technical roles - PMs, marketers, designers - to build functional software using natural language.\n\n### Replace Figma with prototypes\nKevin Weil: \"Instead of showing stuff in Figma, we should be showing prototypes that people are vibe coding over the course of 30 minutes to illustrate proofs of concept.\" Functional code prototypes can be built in the time it takes to create static mockups.\n\n### Build tools to build tools\nAlexander Embiricos: \"They''ll vibe code an animation editor and then they use the animation editor to build the animation.\" Non-engineers can now build functional software and custom tools without deep technical mastery.\n\n### Go beyond prompt engineering\nVibe coding is not just writing prompts - it''s iteratively building functional software through conversation with AI. It requires understanding how to break problems down, test outputs, and refine through follow-up.\n\n### Know the limits\nVibe-coded software is great for prototypes, internal tools, and MVPs. Production-grade systems with complex requirements still need professional engineering review.\n\n## Questions to Help Users\n\n- \"What are you trying to build, and who will use it?\"\n- \"Is this a throwaway prototype or something that needs to scale?\"\n- \"Can you break this down into smaller pieces to build incrementally?\"\n- \"What''s the simplest version that would let you test your hypothesis?\"\n- \"Have you tried describing what''s not working and asking the AI to fix it?\"\n- \"Do you need this to be production-grade, or is it okay if it''s rough?\"\n\n## Common Mistakes to Flag\n\n- **Trying to build everything at once** - Break complex projects into smaller, iterative builds\n- **Not testing the output** - Always run and test what the AI generates; don''t assume it works\n- **Expecting production quality** - Vibe-coded apps are great for validation but may need engineering for production\n- **Unclear specifications** - The clearer your description of what you want, the better the output\n- **Giving up after one try** - Vibe coding is iterative; refine through follow-up prompts\n\n## Deep Dive\n\nFor all 3 insights from 3 guests, see `references/guest-insights.md`\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- Writing PRDs\n- Usability Testing\n- Building with LLMs\n- Shipping Products\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:29:38.111Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Coding Assistants like Claude Code that help developers build software through natural language and iterative prompting.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude Code 这样的 AI 编码助手，它帮助开发人员通过自然语言和迭代提示构建软件。","ja":"Claude Code のような AI コーディング アシスタントに最適で、開発者が自然言語と反復的なプロンプトを使用してソフトウェアを構築するのに役立ちます。","ko":"Claude Code와 같은 AI 코딩 어시스턴트에 적합하며 개발자가 자연어와 반복적인 프롬프트를 통해 소프트웨어를 구축하는 데 도움이 됩니다.","es":"Perfecto para asistentes de codificación de IA como Claude Code que ayudan a los desarrolladores a crear software a través del lenguaje natural y la llamada iterativa.","fr":"Parfait pour les assistants de codage de l''IA comme Claude Code qui aident les développeurs à créer des logiciels par le biais du langage naturel et de la sollicitation itérative.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Coding-Assistenten wie Claude Code, die Entwicklern helfen, Software durch natürliche Sprache und iterative Aufforderung zu erstellen.","pt":"Perfeito para Assistente de Codificação de IA, como Claude Code, que ajudam os desenvolvedores a construir software por meio de linguagem natural e promptings iterativos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для помощников кодирования ИИ, таких как Claude Code, которые помогают разработчикам создавать программное обеспечение через естественный язык и итеративные подсказки.","ar":"เหมาะ لمرافقة kod الإيادي الحاسوبية مثل كلود كود التي تساعد المطورين على بناء البرمجيات من خلال اللغة الطبيعية والتحفيزات المتكررة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to guide users through AI-powered software development by breaking down complex problems into iterative prompt sequences. Leverages frameworks from product leaders to help users build prototypes, internal tools, and production applications using natural language specifications.","zh":"使代理能够通过将复杂问题分解为迭代提示序列来指导用户完成 AI 驱动的软件开发。利用产品领导者的框架帮助用户使用自然语言规范构建原型、内部工具和生产应用。","ja":"エージェントが複雑な問題を反復的なプロンプト シーケンスに分解して、AI ドリブンのソフトウェア開発をユーザーに導くことを可能にします。プロトタイプ、内部ツール、生産アプリケーションを自然言語の仕様で構築するために、製品リーダーのフレームワークを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 문제를 반복적인 프롬프트 시퀀스로 분해하여 AI 주도 소프트웨어 개발을 사용자에게 안내할 수 있도록 합니다. 프로토タイプ, 내부 도구 및 프로덕션 애플리케이션을 자연어 사양으로 구축하는 데 제품 리더의 프레임워크를 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes guiar a los usuarios a través del desarrollo de software impulsado por IA al descomponer problemas complejos en secuencias de solicitudes iterativas. Utiliza marcos de líderes de productos para ayudar a los usuarios a crear prototipos, herramientas internas y aplicaciones de producción utilizando especificaciones de lenguaje natural.","fr":"Permet aux agents de guider les utilisateurs à travers le développement de logiciels alimentés par l''IA en décomposant des problèmes complexes en séquences de sollicitations itératives. Utilise des cadres de leaders de produits pour aider les utilisateurs à créer des prototypes, des outils internes et des applications de production en utilisant des spécifications de langage naturel.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Benutzer durch die KI-gestützte Softwareentwicklung zu führen, indem komplexe Probleme in iterative Prompt-Sequenzen aufgeteilt werden. Nutzt Frameworks von Produktführern, um Benutzern zu helfen, Prototypen, interne Tools und Produktionsanwendungen mithilfe von natürlichen Sprachspezifikationen zu erstellen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes guiem os usuários pelo desenvolvimento de software impulsionado por IA, dividindo problemas complexos em sequências de prompts iterativos. Utiliza estruturas de líderes de produto para ajudar os usuários a criar protótipos, ferramentas internas e aplicações de produção usando especificações de linguagem natural.","ru":"Позволяет агентам направлять пользователей через разработку программного обеспечения на основе ИИ, разбивая сложные проблемы на итеративные последовательности подсказок. Использует框架 от лидеров продукта, чтобы помочь пользователям создавать прототипы, внутренние инструменты и приложения для производства с использованием спецификаций естественного языка.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بإرشاد المستخدمين من خلال تطوير البرامج المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي من خلال تقسيم المشكلات المعقدة إلى تسلسلات تحفيزية متكررة. يستخدم إطارات من قادة المنتجات لمساعدة المستخدمين على بناء نماذج أولية وأدوات داخلية وتطبيقات الإنتاج باستخدام مواصفات اللغة الطبيعية."},"useCases":{"en":["Breaking down software requirements into iterative AI prompts","Guiding developers through prototype creation workflows","Setting expectations for AI-assisted development outcomes","Facilitating natural language to code translation"],"zh":["将软件需求分解为迭代的 AI 提示","指导开发人员完成原型创建工作流","为 AI輔助开发结果设定预期","促进自然语言到代码的翻译"],"ja":["ソフトウェア要件を反復的な AI プロンプトに分解する","開発者がプロトタイプの作成ワークフローを通じてユーザーを導く","AI アシスト開発の結果についての期待を設定する","自然言語からコードへの翻訳を促進する"],"ko":["소프트웨어 요구 사항을 반복적인 AI 프롬프트로 분해하는 것","개발자가 프로토タイプ 생성 워크플로를 통해 사용자를 안내하는 것","AI 보조 개발 결과에 대한 기대를 설정하는 것","자연어에서 코드로의 번역을 촉진하는 것"],"es":["Descomponer los requisitos de software en solicitudes de IA iterativas","Guiar a los desarrolladores a través de flujos de trabajo de creación de prototipos","Establecer expectativas para los resultados del desarrollo asistido por IA","Facilitar la traducción del lenguaje natural al código"],"fr":["Décomposer les exigences logicielles en sollicitations itératives de l''IA","Guider les développeurs à travers les flux de travail de création de prototypes","Établir des attentes pour les résultats du développement assisté par l''IA","Faciliter la traduction du langage naturel en code"],"de":["Software-Anforderungen in iterative KI-Prompts aufteilen","Entwickler durch Prototyp-Erstellungs-Workflows führen","Erwartungen an die Ergebnisse der KI-gestützten Entwicklung festlegen","Die Übersetzung von natürlicher Sprache in Code erleichtern"],"pt":["Dividir os requisitos de software em prompts de IA iterativos","Orientar os desenvolvedores pela criação de fluxos de trabalho de protótipos","Definir expectativas para os resultados do desenvolvimento assistido por IA","Facilitar a tradução de linguagem natural para código"],"ru":["Разбить требования программного обеспечения на итеративные подсказки ИИ","Направлять разработчиков через создание прототипов рабочих процессов","Установить ожидания для результатов разработки с помощью ИИ","Облегчить перевод естественного языка в код"],"ar":["تقسيم متطلبات البرامج إلى تحفيزات متكررة للمعالجة الفكرية","توجيه المطورين من خلال إنشاء سلاسل عمل لإنشاء النماذج الأولية","تحديد التوقعات للنتائج التي تم تطويرها بمساعدة الذكاء الاصطناعي","تسهيل ترجمة اللغة الطبيعية إلى كود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Primarily focused on prototyping and iterative development phases","Requires clear user input about target audience and application type","Optimized for natural language interaction rather than direct code execution"],"zh":["主要针对原型设计和迭代开发阶段","需要用户关于目标受众和应用程序类型的明确输入","针对自然语言交互进行优化，而不是直接代码执行"],"ja":["主にプロトタイピングと反復開発フェーズに焦点を当てている","ターゲット オーディエンスとアプリケーションの種類についての明確なユーザー入力を必要とする","直接のコード実行ではなく自然言語の対話に最適化されている"],"ko":["주로 프로토 타이핑 및 반복 개발 단계에 중점을 둠","대상 사용자 및 애플리케이션 유형에 대한 명확한 사용자 입력이 필요함","직접 코드 실행보다는 자연어 상호 작용을 최적화함"],"es":["Enfocado principalmente en las fases de prototipado y desarrollo iterativo","Requiere una entrada de usuario clara sobre el público objetivo y el tipo de aplicación","Optimizado para la interacción de lenguaje natural en lugar de la ejecución de código directa"],"fr":["Principalement axé sur les phases de prototypage et de développement itératif","Nécessite une entrée utilisateur claire sur le public cible et le type d''application","Optimisé pour l''interaction de langage naturel plutôt que pour l''exécution de code directe"],"de":["Hauptsächlich auf Prototyping- und iterative Entwicklungsphasen fokussiert","Benötigt eine klare Benutzereingabe über die Zielgruppe und die Anwendungstyp","Optimiert für natürliche Sprachinteraktion anstelle von direkter Codeausführung"],"pt":["Focado principalmente nas fases de prototipagem e desenvolvimento iterativo","Exige entrada clara do usuário sobre o público-alvo e o tipo de aplicação","Otimizado para interação de linguagem natural em vez de execução direta de código"],"ru":["В основном ориентирован на фазы прототипирования и итеративной разработки","Требует четкого ввода пользователя о целевой аудитории и типе приложения","Оптимизирован для взаимодействия естественного языка, а не прямой выполнения кода"],"ar":["يركز بشكل رئيسي على مراحل إنشاء النماذج الأولية والتنمية المتكررة","يتطلب إدخال واضح للمستخدم حول الجمهور المستهدف ونوع التطبيق","مُحسَّن لتفاعل اللغة الطبيعية بدلاً من تنفيذ الكود المباشر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/swift-best-practices', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'swift-best-practices', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:29:01.807Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/swift-best-practices","name":"swift-best-practices","description":{"zh":"本技能涵盖Swift 6+的现代开发最佳实践，包括并发安全、API设计和代码质量指南","ja":"このスキルでは、Swift 6+のモダンな開発ベストプラクティスを紹介します。並行性の安全性、API設計、コード品質ガイドなど","ko":"본 실천은 스위프트 6+의 최신 개발 최적화 실천을 다룹니다. 동시성 안전, API 설계, 코드 품질 가이드 등","es":"Aplica las mejores prácticas de desarrollo Swift para crear aplicaciones iOS y macOS seguras y eficientes","fr":"Appliquez les bonnes pratiques de développement Swift pour créer des applications iOS et macOS sécurisées et efficaces","de":"Wenden Sie die besten Praktiken für die Swift-Entwicklung an, um sichere und effiziente iOS- und macOS-Anwendungen zu erstellen","pt":"Melhores práticas de desenvolvimento Swift para projetos iOS e macOS, com foco em recursos de Swift 6+ e concorrência segura","ru":"Лучшие практики разработки на Swift для проектов iOS и macOS, с фокусом на функциях Swift 6+ и безопасной конкурентности","ar":"أفضل الممارسات لتطوير سويفت لمشاريع iOS و macOS، مع التركيز على ميزات سويفت 6+ وسلامة التنافس","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Swift最佳实践","ja":"Swiftベストプラクティス","ko":"스위프트 최적화 실천","es":"Mejores prácticas Swift para desarrollo iOS y macOS","fr":"Bonnes pratiques Swift pour le développement iOS et macOS","de":"Best Practices für Swift-Entwicklung für iOS und macOS","pt":"Melhores Práticas Swift para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Лучшие практики Swift для разработчиков","ar":"أفضل الممارسات سويفت للمطورين","en":"swift-best-practices"},"description":{"zh":"本技能涵盖Swift 6+的现代开发最佳实践，包括并发安全、API设计和代码质量指南","ja":"このスキルでは、Swift 6+のモダンな開発ベストプラクティスを紹介します。並行性の安全性、API設計、コード品質ガイドなど","ko":"본 실천은 스위프트 6+의 최신 개발 최적화 실천을 다룹니다. 동시성 안전, API 설계, 코드 품질 가이드 등","es":"Aplica las mejores prácticas de desarrollo Swift para crear aplicaciones iOS y macOS seguras y eficientes","fr":"Appliquez les bonnes pratiques de développement Swift pour créer des applications iOS et macOS sécurisées et efficaces","de":"Wenden Sie die besten Praktiken für die Swift-Entwicklung an, um sichere und effiziente iOS- und macOS-Anwendungen zu erstellen","pt":"Melhores práticas de desenvolvimento Swift para projetos iOS e macOS, com foco em recursos de Swift 6+ e concorrência segura","ru":"Лучшие практики разработки на Swift для проектов iOS и macOS, с фокусом на функциях Swift 6+ и безопасной конкурентности","ar":"أفضل الممارسات لتطوير سويفت لمشاريع iOS و macOS، مع التركيز على ميزات سويفت 6+ وسلامة التنافس","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["Swift 6+特性","并发安全","API设计原则","代码质量指南","iOS和macOS项目支持"],"ja":["Swift 6+の機能","並行性の安全性","API設計原則","コード品質ガイドライン","iOSとmacOSプロジェクトのサポート"],"ko":["스위프트 6+ 기능","동시성 안전","API 설계 원칙","코드 품질 가이드라인","iOS와 macOS 프로젝트 지원"],"es":["Desarrollo de aplicaciones iOS y macOS con Swift 6+","Concurrencia segura con async/await y actores","Diseño de API con principios de diseño de API","Directrices de calidad de código para proyectos de macOS 15.7+"],"fr":["Développement d''applications iOS et macOS avec Swift 6+","Concurrence sûre avec async/await et acteurs","Conception d''API avec des principes de conception d''API","Lignes directrices de qualité de code pour les projets macOS 15.7+"],"de":["Entwicklung von iOS- und macOS-Anwendungen mit Swift 6+","Sichere Konkurrenz mit async/await und Akteuren","API-Design mit API-Design-Prinzipien","Richtlinien für die Codequalität für macOS 15.7+-Projekte"],"pt":["Recursos de Swift 6+","Concorrência segura","Design de API","Diretrizes de qualidade de código","Suporte a macOS 15.7+"],"ru":["Функции Swift 6+","Безопасная конкурентность","Проектирование API","Руководящие принципы качества кода","Поддержка macOS 15.7+"],"ar":["ميزات سويفت 6+","سلامة التنافس","تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","إرشادات جودة الرمز","دعم macOS 15.7+"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Swift开发","Swift最佳实践","并发安全","API设计","代码质量","iOS开发","macOS开发"],"ja":["Swift開発","Swiftベストプラクティス","並行性の安全性","API設計","コード品質","iOS開発","macOS開発"],"ko":["스위프트 개발","스위프트 최적화 실천","동시성 안전","API 설계","코드 품질","iOS 개발","macOS 개발"],"es":["desarrollo Swift","mejores prácticas Swift","iOS","macOS","concurrency","diseño de API","calidad de código"],"fr":["développement Swift","bonnes pratiques Swift","iOS","macOS","concurrence","conception d''API","qualité de code"],"de":["Swift-Entwicklung","beste Praktiken für Swift","iOS","macOS","Konkurrenz","API-Design","Codequalität"],"pt":["desenvolvimento Swift","melhores práticas Swift","concorrência segura","design de API","qualidade de código","iOS","macOS","Swift 6+"],"ru":["разработка на Swift","лучшие практики Swift","безопасная конкурентность","проектирование API","качество кода","iOS","macOS","Swift 6+"],"ar":["تطوير سويفت","أفضل الممارسات سويفت","سلامة التنافس","تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","جودة الرمز","iOS","macOS","سويفت 6+"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"swift-best-practices","description":"This skill should be used when writing or reviewing Swift code for iOS or macOS projects. Apply modern Swift 6+ best practices, concurrency patterns, API design guidelines, and migration strategies. Covers async/await, actors, MainActor, Sendable, typed throws, and Swift 6 breaking changes.","bodyPreview":"# Swift Best Practices Skill\n\n## Overview\n\nApply modern Swift development best practices focusing on Swift 6+ features, concurrency safety, API design principles, and code quality guidelines for iOS and macOS projects targeting macOS 15.7+.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Writing new Swift code for iOS or macOS applications\n- Reviewing Swift code for correctness, safety, and style\n- Implementing Swift concurrency features (async/await, actors, MainActor)\n- Designing Swift APIs","body":"# Swift Best Practices Skill\n\n## Overview\n\nApply modern Swift development best practices focusing on Swift 6+ features, concurrency safety, API design principles, and code quality guidelines for iOS and macOS projects targeting macOS 15.7+.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Writing new Swift code for iOS or macOS applications\n- Reviewing Swift code for correctness, safety, and style\n- Implementing Swift concurrency features (async/await, actors, MainActor)\n- Designing Swift APIs and public interfaces\n- Migrating code from Swift 5 to Swift 6\n- Addressing concurrency warnings, data race issues, or compiler errors related to Sendable/isolation\n- Working with modern Swift language features introduced in Swift 6 and 6.2\n\n## Core Guidelines\n\n### Fundamental Principles\n\n1. **Clarity at point of use** is paramount - evaluate designs by examining use cases, not just declarations\n2. **Clarity over brevity** - compact code comes from the type system, not minimal characters\n3. **Write documentation for every public declaration** - if you can''t describe functionality simply, the API may be poorly designed\n4. **Name by role, not type** - `var greeting = \"Hello\"` not `var string = \"Hello\"`\n5. **Favour elegance through simplicity** - avoid over-engineering unless complexity genuinely warrants it\n\n### Swift 6 Concurrency Model\n\nSwift 6 enables complete concurrency checking by default with region-based isolation (SE-0414). The compiler now proves code safety, eliminating many false positives whilst catching real concurrency issues at compile time.\n\n**Critical understanding:**\n- **Async ≠ background** - async functions can suspend but don''t automatically run on background threads\n- Actors protect mutable shared state through automatic synchronisation\n- `@MainActor` ensures UI-related code executes on the main thread\n- Global actor-isolated types are automatically `Sendable`\n\n### Essential Patterns\n\n#### Async/Await\n```swift\n// Parallel execution with async let\nfunc fetchData() async -> (String, Int) {\n    async let stringData = fetchString()\n    async let intData = fetchInt()\n    return await (stringData, intData)\n}\n\n// Always check cancellation in long-running operations\nfunc process(_ items: [Item]) async throws -> [Result] {\n    var results: [Result] = []\n    for item in items {\n        try Task.checkCancellation()\n        results.append(await process(item))\n    }\n    return results\n}\n```\n\n#### MainActor for UI Code\n```swift\n// Apply at type level for consistent isolation\n@MainActor\nclass ContentViewModel: ObservableObject {\n    @Published var images: [UIImage] = []\n\n    func fetchData() async throws {\n        self.images = try await fetchImages()\n    }\n}\n\n// Avoid MainActor.run when direct await works\nawait doMainActorStuff()  // Good\nawait MainActor.run { doMainActorStuff() }  // Unnecessary\n```\n\n#### Actor Isolation\n```swift\nactor DataCache {\n    private var cache: [String: Data] = [:]\n\n    func store(_ data: Data, forKey key: String) {\n        cache[key] = data  // No await needed inside actor\n    }\n\n    nonisolated func cacheType() -> String {\n        return \"DataCache\"  // No await needed - doesn''t access isolated state\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n1. **Don''t mark functions as `async` unnecessarily** - async calling convention has overhead\n2. **Never use `DispatchSemaphore` with async/await** - risk of deadlock\n3. **Don''t create stateless actors** - use non-isolated async functions instead\n4. **Avoid split isolation** - don''t mix isolation domains within one type\n5. **Check task cancellation** - long operations must check `Task.checkCancellation()`\n6. **Don''t assume async means background** - explicitly move work to background if needed\n7. **Avoid excessive context switching** - group operations within same isolation domain\n\n### API Design Quick Reference\n\n#### Naming Conventions\n- Types/protocols: `UpperCamelCase`\n- Everything else: `lowerCamelCase`\n- Protocols describing capabilities: `-able`, `-ible`, `-ing` suffixes (`Equatable`, `ProgressReporting`)\n- Factory methods: Begin with `make` (`x.makeIterator()`)\n- Mutating pairs: imperative vs past participle (`x.sort()` / `x.sorted()`)\n\n#### Method Naming by Side Effects\n- No side effects: Noun phrases (`x.distance(to: y)`)\n- With side effects: Imperative verbs (`x.append(y)`, `x.sort()`)\n\n#### Argument Labels\n- Omit when arguments can''t be distinguished: `min(number1, number2)`\n- Value-preserving conversions omit first label: `Int64(someUInt32)`\n- Prepositional phrases label at preposition: `x.removeBoxes(havingLength: 12)`\n- Label all other arguments\n\n### Swift 6 Breaking Changes\n\n#### Must Explicitly Mark Types with @MainActor (SE-0401)\nProperty wrappers no longer infer actor isolation automatically.\n\n```swift\n@MainActor\nstruct LogInView: View {\n    @StateObject private var model = ViewModel()\n}\n```\n\n#### Global Variables Must Be Concurrency-Safe (SE-0412)\n```swift\nstatic let config = Config()  // Constant - OK\n@MainActor static var state = State()  // Actor-isolated - OK\nnonisolated(unsafe) var cache = [String: Data]()  // Unsafe - use with caution\n```\n\n#### Other Changes\n- `@UIApplicationMain`/`@NSApplicationMain` deprecated (use `@main`)\n- `any` required for existential types\n- Import visibility requires explicit access control\n\n### API Availability Patterns\n\n```swift\n// Basic availability\n@available(macOS 15, iOS 18, *)\nfunc modernAPI() { }\n\n// Deprecation with message\n@available(*, deprecated, message: \"Use newMethod() instead\")\nfunc oldMethod() { }\n\n// Renaming with auto-fix\n@available(*, unavailable, renamed: \"newMethod\")\nfunc oldMethod() { }\n\n// Runtime checking\nif #available(iOS 18, *) {\n    // iOS 18+ code\n}\n\n// Inverted checking (Swift 5.6+)\nif #unavailable(iOS 18, *) {\n    // iOS 17 and lower\n}\n```\n\n**Key differences:**\n- `deprecated` - Warning, allows usage\n- `obsoleted` - Error from specific version\n- `unavailable` - Error, completely prevents usage\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\n### When Writing Code\n\n1. Apply naming conventions following role-based, clarity-first principles\n2. Use appropriate isolation (`@MainActor` for UI, actors for mutable state)\n3. Implement async/await patterns correctly with proper cancellation handling\n4. Follow Swift 6 concurrency model - trust compiler''s flow analysis\n5. Document public APIs with clear, concise summaries\n\n### When Reviewing Code\n\n1. Check for concurrency safety violations\n2. Verify proper actor isolation and Sendable conformance\n3. Ensure async functions handle cancellation appropriately\n4. Validate API naming follows Swift guidelines\n5. Confirm availability annotations are correct for target platforms\n\n### Code Quality Standards\n\n- Minimise comments - code should be self-documenting where possible\n- Avoid over-engineering and unnecessary abstractions\n- Use meaningful variable names based on role, not type\n- Follow established project architecture and patterns\n- Prefer `count(where:)` over `filter().count`\n- Use `InlineArray` for fixed-size, performance-critical data\n- Trust compiler''s concurrency flow analysis - avoid unnecessary `Sendable` conformances\n\n## Resources\n\n### references/\n\nDetailed reference material to load when in-depth information is needed:\n\n- **api-design.md** - Complete API design conventions, documentation standards, parameter guidelines, and naming patterns\n- **concurrency.md** - Detailed async/await patterns, actor best practices, common pitfalls, performance considerations, and thread safety patterns\n- **swift6-features.md** - New language features in Swift 6/6.2, breaking changes, migration strategies, and modern patterns\n- **availability-patterns.md** - Comprehensive `@available` attribute usage, deprecation strategies, and platform version management\n\nLoad these references when detailed information is needed beyond the core guidelines provided above.\n\n## Platform Requirements\n\n- Swift 6.0+ compiler for Swift 6 features\n- Swift 6.2+ for InlineArray and enhanced concurrency features\n- macOS 15.7+ with appropriate SDK\n- iOS 18+ for latest platform features\n- Use `#available` for runtime platform detection\n- Use `@available` for API availability marking\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:29:01.807Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for iOS and macOS Development Agents seeking to implement modern Swift development best practices with a focus on concurrency safety and API design principles.","zh":"适用于寻求实施现代Swift开发最佳实践、注重并发安全和API设计原则的iOS和macOS开发代理。","ja":"iOSおよびmacOS開発エージェントがモダンなSwift開発のベストプラクティスを実装し、並行性の安全性とAPI設計原則に焦点を当てるのに最適です。","ko":"최신 Swift 개발 모범 사례를 구현하고 병렬성 안전성 및 API 설계 원칙에 중점을 둔 iOS 및 macOS 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo de iOS y macOS que buscan implementar las mejores prácticas de desarrollo de Swift modernas con un enfoque en la seguridad de concurrencia y los principios de diseño de API.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement d''iOS et de macOS souhaitant mettre en œuvre les meilleures pratiques de développement Swift modernes en mettant l''accent sur la sécurité de la concurrence et les principes de conception d''API.","de":"Ideal für iOS- und macOS-Entwicklungsagenten, die moderne Swift-Entwicklungsbestpraktiken mit Fokus auf Konkurrenzsicherheit und API-Designprinzipien umsetzen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento do iOS e macOS que buscam implementar as melhores práticas de desenvolvimento Swift moderno com foco em segurança de concorrência e princípios de design de API.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки iOS и macOS, стремящихся реализовать современные лучшие практики разработки Swift с фокусом на безопасности согласованности и принципах дизайна API.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير iOS و macOS الذين يแสعون لتنفيذ أفضل الممارسات لتطوير Swift الحديثة مع التركيز على سلامة التزامن ومبادئ تصميم واجهة البرنامج."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write high-quality Swift code leveraging Swift 6+ features, async/await, actors, and MainActor for enhanced concurrency safety, while adhering to strict code quality guidelines and API design principles for seamless integration with macOS 15.7+ projects.","zh":"赋予代理编写高质量的Swift代码的能力，利用Swift 6+功能、异步/等待、actors和MainActor增强并发安全性，同时遵守严格的代码质量指南和API设计原则，以实现与macOS 15.7+项目的无缝集成。","ja":"Swift 6+の機能、async/await、actors、MainActorを利用して、高品質のSwiftコードを書き、並行性の安全性を高め、厳格なコード品質ガイドラインとAPI設計原則に従い、macOS 15.7+プロジェクトとのシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 Swift 6+ 기능, 비동기/대기, 액터 및 MainActor를 사용하여 높은 품질의 Swift 코드를 작성하여 병렬성 안전성을 향상시키고, 엄격한 코드 품질 지침 및 API 설계 원칙을 준수하여 macOS 15.7+ 프로젝트와의 무縫한 통합을 달성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes escribir código Swift de alta calidad aprovechando las características de Swift 6+, async/await, actores y MainActor para una mayor seguridad de concurrencia, al tiempo que se adhieren a estrictas pautas de calidad de código y principios de diseño de API para una integración perfecta con proyectos de macOS 15.7+.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire du code Swift de haute qualité en exploitant les fonctionnalités de Swift 6+, async/await, les acteurs et MainActor pour une sécurité de concurrence améliorée, tout en respectant des directives de qualité de code strictes et des principes de conception d''API pour une intégration transparente avec les projets macOS 15.7+.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, hochwertigen Swift-Code zu schreiben, der Swift 6+-Funktionen, async/await, Akteure und MainActor für eine verbesserte Konkurrenzsicherheit nutzt, während sie sich an strenge Codequalitätsrichtlinien und API-Designprinzipien halten, um eine nahtlose Integration mit macOS 15.7+-Projekten zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever código Swift de alta qualidade, aproveitando recursos do Swift 6+, async/await, atores e MainActor para uma segurança de concorrência aprimorada, ao mesmo tempo em que adere a diretrizes rigorosas de qualidade de código e princípios de design de API para integração sem problemas com projetos macOS 15.7+.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать высококачественный код Swift, используя функции Swift 6+, async/await, актеры и MainActor для улучшения безопасности согласованности, а также придерживаясь строгих руководств по качеству кода и принципам дизайна API для бесшовной интеграции с проектами macOS 15.7+.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من كتابة كود Swift عالي الجودة باستخدام ميزات Swift 6+، و async/await، و الممثلين و MainActor من أجل تعزيز سلامة التزامن، مع اتباع إرشادات صارمة لجودة الكود ومبادئ تصميم واجهة البرنامج من أجل التكامل السلس مع مشاريع macOS 15.7+."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing Swift concurrency features for safer asynchronous programming","Designing and reviewing Swift APIs for optimal performance and security","Optimizing Swift code for correctness, style, and adherence to modern development best practices"],"zh":["为更安全的异步编程实现Swift并发功能","为最佳性能和安全性设计和审查Swift API","优化Swift代码以实现正确性、样式和现代开发最佳实践的遵守"],"ja":["より安全な非同期プログラミングのためにSwiftの並行性機能を実装する","最適なパフォーマンスとセキュリティのためにSwift APIを設計し、レビューする","Swiftコードを正しさ、スタイル、モダンな開発のベストプラクティスに従って最適化する"],"ko":["보다 안전한 비동기 프로그래밍을 위해 Swift 병렬성 기능을 구현하는 것","최상의 성능 및 보안을 위해 Swift API를 설계하고 검토하는 것","Swift 코드를 올바름, 스타일 및 최신 개발 모범 사례를 따르는 방식으로 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Implementar características de concurrencia de Swift para una programación asíncrona más segura","Diseñar y revisar API de Swift para un rendimiento y seguridad óptimos","Optimizar el código Swift para la corrección, el estilo y el cumplimiento de las mejores prácticas de desarrollo modernas"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre les fonctionnalités de concurrence de Swift pour une programmation asynchrone plus sûre","Concevoir et examiner les API Swift pour des performances et une sécurité optimales","Optimiser le code Swift pour la correction, le style et le respect des meilleures pratiques de développement modernes"],"de":["Implementierung von Swift-Konkurrenzfunktionen für eine sicherere asynchrone Programmierung","Entwerfen und Überprüfen von Swift-APIs für optimale Leistung und Sicherheit","Optimieren des Swift-Codes für Korrektheit, Stil und Einhaltung moderner Entwicklungsbestpraktiken"],"pt":["Implementação de recursos de concorrência Swift para programação assíncrona mais segura","Projeto e revisão de APIs Swift para desempenho e segurança ótimos","Otimização de código Swift para correção, estilo e aderência às melhores práticas de desenvolvimento moderno"],"ru":["Реализация функций согласованности Swift для более безопасного асинхронного программирования","Проектирование и проверка API Swift для оптимальной производительности и безопасности","Оптимизация кода Swift для правильности, стиля и соблюдения современных лучших практик разработки"],"ar":["تنفيذ ميزات التزامن Swift لتطوير برمجي غير متزامن أكثر أمانًا","تصميم ومراجعة واجهات برمجة تطبيقات Swift للاداء والأمان الأمثل","تحسين كود Swift من أجل الصحة والأسلوب والامتثال لأفضل الممارسات الحديثة لتطوير البرمجيات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Swift 6+ compatibility","Targeted for iOS and macOS projects only","Optimized for macOS 15.7+"],"zh":["需要Swift 6+兼容性","仅针对iOS和macOS项目","针对macOS 15.7+优化"],"ja":["Swift 6+の互換性が必要","iOSおよびmacOSプロジェクトのみを対象としています","macOS 15.7+に最適化"],"ko":["Swift 6+ 호환성 필요","iOS 및 macOS 프로젝트만 대상으로 함","macOS 15.7+ 최적화"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Swift 6+","Dirigido a proyectos de iOS y macOS exclusivamente","Optimizado para macOS 15.7+"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec Swift 6+","Ciblé pour les projets iOS et macOS uniquement","Optimisé pour macOS 15.7+"],"de":["Erfordert Swift 6+-Kompatibilität","Gerichtet auf iOS- und macOS-Projekte ausschließlich","Optimiert für macOS 15.7+"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com Swift 6+","Destinado apenas a projetos iOS e macOS","Otimizado para macOS 15.7+"],"ru":["Требует совместимости со Swift 6+","Предназначен только для проектов iOS и macOS","Оптимизирован для macOS 15.7+"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع Swift 6+","يستهدف مشاريع iOS و macOS فقط","مُحسّن لمنصة macOS 15.7+"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/commit', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'commit', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:29:32.384Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/commit","name":"commit","description":{"zh":"Commit 消息规范是一套用于编写清晰、有意义的提交消息的规则，提高代码可读性和可维护性。","ja":"コミット メッセージの規約は、明確で意味のあるコミット メッセージを書くためのルールです。コードの可読性と保守性を向上させます。","ko":"커밋 메시지 규칙은 明確하고 의미 있는 커밋 메시지를 작성하기 위한 규칙입니다. 코드의 가독성과 유지 보수를 향상시킵니다.","es":"Las convenciones de commit para Sentry definen un formato estándar para los mensajes de commit","fr":"Les conventions de commit pour Sentry définissent un format standard pour les messages de commit","de":"Die Commit-Konventionen für Sentry definieren ein Standardformat für Commit-Mitteilungen","pt":"As convenções de commit são essenciais para manter um histórico de versão limpo e organizado. Aprenda as melhores práticas para criar mensagens de commit eficazes.","ru":"Условия коммита необходимы для поддержания чистой и организованной истории версий. Узнайте о лучших практиках для создания эффективных сообщений коммита.","ar":"اتفاقيات Commit ضرورية للاحتفاظ بسجل إصدار نظيف ومنظم. تعلم أفضل الممارسات لإنشاء رسائل Commit فعالة.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Commit 消息规范","ja":"コミット メッセージの規約","ko":"커밋 메시지 규칙","es":"Convenciones de commit para Sentry","fr":"Conventions de commit pour Sentry","de":"Commit-Konventionen für Sentry","pt":"Convenções de Commit: Melhores Práticas para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Коммит сообщения: лучшие практики для разработчиков","ar":"اتفاقيات Commit: أفضل الممارسات للمطورين","en":"commit"},"description":{"zh":"Commit 消息规范是一套用于编写清晰、有意义的提交消息的规则，提高代码可读性和可维护性。","ja":"コミット メッセージの規約は、明確で意味のあるコミット メッセージを書くためのルールです。コードの可読性と保守性を向上させます。","ko":"커밋 메시지 규칙은 明確하고 의미 있는 커밋 메시지를 작성하기 위한 규칙입니다. 코드의 가독성과 유지 보수를 향상시킵니다.","es":"Las convenciones de commit para Sentry definen un formato estándar para los mensajes de commit","fr":"Les conventions de commit pour Sentry définissent un format standard pour les messages de commit","de":"Die Commit-Konventionen für Sentry definieren ein Standardformat für Commit-Mitteilungen","pt":"As convenções de commit são essenciais para manter um histórico de versão limpo e organizado. Aprenda as melhores práticas para criar mensagens de commit efi...","ru":"Условия коммита необходимы для поддержания чистой и организованной истории версий. Узнайте о лучших практиках для создания эффективных сообщений коммита.","ar":"اتفاقيات Commit ضرورية للاحتفاظ بسجل إصدار نظيف ومنظم. تعلم أفضل الممارسات لإنشاء رسائل Commit فعالة.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["Commit 消息格式","提交类型","作用域和主题","正文和脚注","代码可读性提高"],"ja":["コミット メッセージのフォーマット","コミットの種類","スコープとサブジェクト","ボディとフッター","コードの可読性の向上"],"ko":["커밋 메시지 형식","커밋 유형","범위 및 주제","본문 및 바닥글","코드 가독성 향상"],"es":["Formato de commit estándar","Tipos de commit definidos","Cuerpo y pie de página opcionales","Límites de longitud de línea","Convenciones de redacción"],"fr":["Format de commit standard","Types de commit définis","Corps et pied de page optionnels","Limites de longueur de ligne","Conventions d''écriture"],"de":["Standard-Commit-Format","Definierte Commit-Typen","Optional: Body und Footer","Zeichenbegrenzung pro Zeile","Schreibkonventionen"],"pt":["Formato de commit padrão","Tipos de commit (feat, fix, ref, perf, docs, test)","Convenções de escrita de mensagens de commit","Importância da clareza e consistência","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Organização do histórico de versão"],"ru":["Стандартный формат коммита","Типы коммита (feat, fix, ref, perf, docs, test)","Условия написания сообщений коммита","Важность ясности и последовательности","Улучшение качества кода","Организация истории версий"],"ar":["تنسيق Commit القياسي","أنواع Commit (feat, fix, ref, perf, docs, test)","اتفاقيات كتابة رسائل Commit","أهمية الوضوح والاستمرارية","تحسين جودة الكود","تنظيم سجل الإصدار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Commit 消息规范","代码质量","可维护性","提交消息","代码可读性"],"ja":["コミット メッセージの規約","コードの品質","保守性","コミット メッセージ","コードの可読性"],"ko":["커밋 메시지 규칙","코드 품질","유지 보수","커밋 메시지","코드 가독성"],"es":["convenciones de commit","commit para Sentry","formato de commit","tipos de commit","desarrollo de software","gestión de código"],"fr":["conventions de commit","commit pour Sentry","format de commit","types de commit","développement de logiciels","gestion de code"],"de":["Commit-Konventionen","Commit für Sentry","Commit-Format","Commit-Typen","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Verwaltung"],"pt":["convenções de commit","melhores práticas de commit","commit padrão","tipos de commit","mensagens de commit","qualidade do código","histórico de versão","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["условия коммита","лучшие практики коммита","стандартный коммит","типы коммита","сообщения коммита","качество кода","история версий","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["اتفاقيات Commit","أفضل الممارسات ل Commit","Commit القياسي","أنواع Commit","رسائل Commit","جودة الكود","سجل الإصدار","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"Create commit messages following Sentry conventions. Use when committing code changes, writing commit messages, or formatting git history. Follows conventional commits with Sentry-specific issue references.","bodyPreview":"# Sentry Commit Messages\n\nFollow these conventions when creating commits for Sentry projects.\n\n## Format\n\n```\n<type>(<scope>): <subject>\n\n<body>\n\n<footer>\n```\n\nThe header is required. Scope is optional. All lines must stay under 100 characters.\n\n## Commit Types\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature |\n| `fix` | Bug fix |\n| `ref` | Refactoring (no behavior change) |\n| `perf` | Performance improvement |\n| `docs` | Documentation only |\n| `test` | Test additions or corrections","body":"# Sentry Commit Messages\n\nFollow these conventions when creating commits for Sentry projects.\n\n## Format\n\n```\n<type>(<scope>): <subject>\n\n<body>\n\n<footer>\n```\n\nThe header is required. Scope is optional. All lines must stay under 100 characters.\n\n## Commit Types\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature |\n| `fix` | Bug fix |\n| `ref` | Refactoring (no behavior change) |\n| `perf` | Performance improvement |\n| `docs` | Documentation only |\n| `test` | Test additions or corrections |\n| `build` | Build system or dependencies |\n| `ci` | CI configuration |\n| `chore` | Maintenance tasks |\n| `style` | Code formatting (no logic change) |\n| `meta` | Repository metadata |\n| `license` | License changes |\n\n## Subject Line Rules\n\n- Use imperative, present tense: \"Add feature\" not \"Added feature\"\n- Capitalize the first letter\n- No period at the end\n- Maximum 70 characters\n\n## Body Guidelines\n\n- Explain **what** and **why**, not how\n- Use imperative mood and present tense\n- Include motivation for the change\n- Contrast with previous behavior when relevant\n\n## Footer: Issue References\n\nReference issues in the footer using these patterns:\n\n```\nFixes GH-1234\nFixes #1234\nFixes SENTRY-1234\nRefs LINEAR-ABC-123\n```\n\n- `Fixes` closes the issue when merged\n- `Refs` links without closing\n\n## Examples\n\n### Simple fix\n\n```\nfix(api): Handle null response in user endpoint\n\nThe user API could return null for deleted accounts, causing a crash\nin the dashboard. Add null check before accessing user properties.\n\nFixes SENTRY-5678\n```\n\n### Feature with scope\n\n```\nfeat(alerts): Add Slack thread replies for alert updates\n\nWhen an alert is updated or resolved, post a reply to the original\nSlack thread instead of creating a new message. This keeps related\nnotifications grouped together.\n\nRefs GH-1234\n```\n\n### Refactor\n\n```\nref: Extract common validation logic to shared module\n\nMove duplicate validation code from three endpoints into a shared\nvalidator class. No behavior change.\n```\n\n### Breaking change\n\n```\nfeat(api)!: Remove deprecated v1 endpoints\n\nRemove all v1 API endpoints that were deprecated in version 23.1.\nClients should migrate to v2 endpoints.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: v1 endpoints no longer available\nFixes SENTRY-9999\n```\n\n## Revert Format\n\n```\nrevert: feat(api): Add new endpoint\n\nThis reverts commit abc123def456.\n\nReason: Caused performance regression in production.\n```\n\n## Principles\n\n- Each commit should be a single, stable change\n- Commits should be independently reviewable\n- The repository should be in a working state after each commit\n\n## References\n\n- [Sentry Commit Messages](https://develop.sentry.dev/engineering-practices/commit-messages/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:29:32.384Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Management Agents needing standardized commit message formatting.","zh":"适合需要标准化提交消息格式的代码管理代理。","ja":"コード管理エージェントが標準化されたコミットメッセージ形式を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"표준화된 커밋 메시지 형식을 필요로 하는 코드 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de código que necesitan un formato de mensaje de confirmación estandarizado.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion de code ayant besoin d''un format de message de validation standardisé.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Management-Agents, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Nachrichten-Format benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Código que necessitam de formatação de mensagens de commit padronizadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления кодом, требующих стандартизированного форматирования сообщений о коммитах.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة الشفرة التي تحتاج إلى تنسيق رسائل الالتزام الموحدة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate conventional commit messages using specific types like ''feat'' for new features, ''fix'' for bug fixes, and ''docs'' for documentation updates, all while adhering to a strict format and character limit.","zh":"赋予代理生成使用特定类型（如新功能的''feat''、错误修复的''fix''、文档更新的''docs''）的传统提交消息的能力，同时遵守严格的格式和字符限制。","ja":"エージェントが新機能の''feat''、バグ修正の''fix''、ドキュメントの更新の''docs''などの特定のタイプを使用して従来のコミットメッセージを生成する能力を提供し、厳格な形式と文字制限に従う。","ko":"에이전트가 새로운 기능의 ''feat'', 버그 수정의 ''fix'', 문서 업데이트 의 ''docs'' 등의 특정 유형을 사용하여 전통적인 커밋 메시지를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 엄格한 형식과 문자 제한을 준수합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar mensajes de confirmación convencionales utilizando tipos específicos como ''feat'' para nuevas características, ''fix'' para correcciones de errores y ''docs'' para actualizaciones de documentación, todo mientras se adhiere a un formato estricto y un límite de caracteres.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des messages de validation conventionnels en utilisant des types spécifiques tels que ''feat'' pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités, ''fix'' pour les corrections de bogues et ''docs'' pour les mises à jour de documentation, tout en respectant un format strict et une limite de caractères.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, konventionelle Commit-Nachrichten zu generieren, die spezifische Typen wie ''feat'' für neue Funktionen, ''fix'' für Fehlerkorrekturen und ''docs'' für Dokumentationsaktualisierungen verwenden, und dabei ein strenges Format und eine Zeichenbegrenzung einhalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar mensagens de commit convencionais usando tipos específicos como ''feat'' para novos recursos, ''fix'' para correções de bugs e ''docs'' para atualizações de documentação, tudo isso seguindo um formato estrito e limite de caracteres.","ru":"Позволяет агентам генерировать стандартные сообщения о коммитах, используя определенные типы, такие как ''feat'' для новых функций, ''fix'' для исправления ошибок и ''docs'' для обновления документации, все при этом соблюдая строгий формат и ограничение на количество символов.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من生成 رسائل التزام تقليدية باستخدام أنواع محددة مثل ''feat'' لميزات جديدة و ''fix'' لتصحيح الأخطاء و ''docs'' لتحديثات الوثائق ، مع اتباع تنسيق صارم وحد أقصى للcharacters."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing commit messages for Sentry projects","Automating commit type classification","Generating commit messages with scopes and subjects under 100 characters"],"zh":["为Sentry项目标准化提交消息","自动提交类型分类","生成带有范围和主题的提交消息，且字符数少于100个"],"ja":["Sentryプロジェクトのコミットメッセージを標準化する","コミットタイプの自動分類","スコープとサブジェクトを含むコミットメッセージを生成する、文字数は100文字未満"],"ko":["Sentry 프로젝트를 위한 커밋 메시지 표준화","커밋 유형 자동 분류","범위와 제목을 포함한 커밋 메시지 생성, 문자수 100자 미만"],"es":["Estandarizar mensajes de confirmación para proyectos de Sentry","Automatizar la clasificación de tipo de confirmación","Generar mensajes de confirmación con ámbitos y asuntos con menos de 100 caracteres"],"fr":["Standardiser les messages de validation pour les projets Sentry","Automatiser la classification du type de validation","Générer des messages de validation avec des portées et des sujets en moins de 100 caractères"],"de":["Standardisieren von Commit-Nachrichten für Sentry-Projekte","Automatisieren der Commit-Typ-Klassifizierung","Generieren von Commit-Nachrichten mit Bereichen und Betreffzeilen unter 100 Zeichen"],"pt":["Padronizar mensagens de commit para projetos Sentry","Automatizar classificação de tipo de commit","Gerar mensagens de commit com escopos e assuntos com menos de 100 caracteres"],"ru":["Стандартизация сообщений о коммитах для проектов Sentry","Автоматизация классификации типов коммитов","Генерация сообщений о коммитах со сферами и темами менее 100 символов"],"ar":["توحيد رسائل الالتزام لمشاريع Sentry","تأتمتة تصنيف نوع الالتزام","генерация رسائل الالتزام مع نطاقات ومواضيع أقل من 100 حرف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to specific commit message format","Limited to six predefined commit types","All lines must be under 100 characters"],"zh":["需要遵守特定的提交消息格式","仅限六种预定义的提交类型","所有行必须少于100个字符"],"ja":["特定のコミットメッセージ形式に従わなければならない","六種類の事前定義されたコミットタイプのみ","すべての行は100文字以下でなければならない"],"ko":["특정 커밋 메시지 형식을 준수해야 함","6개의 사전 정의된 커밋 유형만 해당","모든 줄은 100자 미만이어야 함"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a un formato de mensaje de confirmación específico","Limitado a seis tipos de confirmación predefinidos","Todas las líneas deben tener menos de 100 caracteres"],"fr":["Nécessite de se conformer à un format de message de validation spécifique","Limité à six types de validation prédéfinis","Toutes les lignes doivent avoir moins de 100 caractères"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung eines bestimmten Commit-Nachrichten-Formats","Begrenzt auf sechs vordefinierte Commit-Typen","Alle Zeilen müssen unter 100 Zeichen haben"],"pt":["Exige aderência a um formato de mensagem de commit específico","Limitado a seis tipos de commit predefinidos","Todas as linhas devem ter menos de 100 caracteres"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения определенного формата сообщения о коммитах","Ограничен шестью предопределенными типами коммитов","Все строки должны быть менее 100 символов"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع تنسيق رسالة التزام معين","محدود بستة أنواع من الالتزام محددة مسبقا","جميع السطور يجب أن تكون أقل من 100 حرف"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
