aude Code pour automatiser les flux de travail et documenter les processus complexes","de":"Erstellen von Fähigkeiten in Claude Code, um Arbeitsabläufe zu automatisieren und komplexe Prozesse zu dokumentieren","pt":"Criar habilidades para automatizar fluxos de trabalho e melhorar a produtividade da equipe","ru":"Создание навыков для автоматизации рабочих процессов и повышения производительности команды","ar":"إنشاء مهارات لتحسين إنتاجية الفريق وتحسين سير العمل","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["标准化工作流程","减少错误","提高开发效率","支持多步骤过程","支持自动化脚本"],"ja":["ワークフローの標準化","エラーの減少","開発効率の向上","複数ステップのプロセスのサポート","自動化スクリプトのサポート"],"ko":["작업 흐름 표준화","오류 감소","개발 효율성 향상","다단계 프로세스 지원","자동화 스크립트 지원"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo","Documentación de procesos complejos","Estructura de directorio personalizable","Soporte para scripts de automatización","Compatibilidad con múltiples sesiones","Estándarización de tareas para equipos"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail","Documentation de processus complexes","Structure de répertoire personnalisable","Prise en charge des scripts d''automatisation","Compatibilité avec plusieurs sessions","Standardisation des tâches pour les équipes"],"de":["Automatisierung von Arbeitsabläufen","Dokumentation komplexer Prozesse","Anpassbare Verzeichnisstruktur","Unterstützung für Automatisierungsskripte","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Sitzungen","Standardisierung von Aufgaben für Teams"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho","Documentar processos complexos","Padronizar abordagens de tarefas","Prevenir erros com procedimentos documentados","Estrutura de diretório personalizável"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие процессы","Документировать сложные процессы","Стандартизировать подходы к задачам","Предотвратить ошибки с помощью документированных процедур","Настраиваемая структура директории"],"ar":["تحسين سير العمل","توثيق العمليات المعقدة","تقديم نهج موحد للمهام","منع الأخطاء بإجراءات موثقة","هيكل دليل قابل للتخصيص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["创建技能","开发效率","标准化工作流程","减少错误","自动化脚本","开发工具"],"ja":["スキルの作成","開発効率","ワークフローの標準化","エラーの減少","自動化スクリプト","開発ツール"],"ko":["스킬 생성","개발 효율성","작업 흐름 표준화","오류 감소","자동화 스크립트","개발 도구"],"es":["crear habilidades","automatización de flujos de trabajo","documentación de procesos","Claude Code","desarrollo de habilidades","automatización de tareas","gestión de procesos","optimización de flujos de trabajo","tecnologías de automatización"],"fr":["créer des compétences","automatisation des flux de travail","documentation de processus","Claude Code","développement de compétences","automatisation de tâches","gestion de processus","optimisation des flux de travail","technologies d''automatisation"],"de":["Fähigkeiten erstellen","Automatisierung von Arbeitsabläufen","Dokumentation von Prozessen","Claude Code","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Prozessmanagement","Optimierung von Arbeitsabläufen","Automatisierungstechnologien"],"pt":["criar habilidades","automatizar fluxos de trabalho","documentar processos","padronizar tarefas","prevenir erros","desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["создание навыков","автоматизировать рабочие процессы","документировать процессы","стандартизировать задачи","предотвратить ошибки","разработка навыков"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات","تحسين سير العمل","توثيق العمليات","تقديم نهج موحد","منع الأخطاء","تطوير المهارات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"creating-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, documenting workflows, or standardizing processes into reusable skill definitions.","bodyPreview":"# Creating Skills\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\nCreate a skill when:\n- A workflow is repeated across multiple sessions\n- Complex multi-step processes need documentation\n- Team needs standardized approach to a task\n- Errors occur that a documented procedure would prevent\n\n## Skill Directory Structure\n\n```\n.claude/skills/{skill-name}/\n├── SKILL.md          # Required: Main skill document\n├── reference/        # Optional: Supporting documents\n└── scripts/          # Optional: Automation scripts\n```","body":"# Creating Skills\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\nCreate a skill when:\n- A workflow is repeated across multiple sessions\n- Complex multi-step processes need documentation\n- Team needs standardized approach to a task\n- Errors occur that a documented procedure would prevent\n\n## Skill Directory Structure\n\n```\n.claude/skills/{skill-name}/\n├── SKILL.md          # Required: Main skill document\n├── reference/        # Optional: Supporting documents\n└── scripts/          # Optional: Automation scripts\n```\n\n## SKILL.md Template\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: skill-name\ndescription: Third-person description of what the skill does. Under 1024 chars.\n---\n\n# Skill Title\n\n## When to Use\n\nDescribe trigger conditions.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. First step\n2. Second step\n3. Third step\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\ncommand1\ncommand2\n```\n\n## Examples\n\nShow usage examples.\n```\n\n## Frontmatter Rules\n\n**Required fields (only these two allowed):**\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|-------|\n| `name` | Lowercase, hyphenated, gerund form (e.g., `creating-skills`) |\n| `description` | Under 1024 chars, 3rd-person voice, no \"you\" |\n\n**Not allowed:** Any other fields (version, author, tags, etc.)\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n| Rule | Good | Bad |\n|------|------|-----|\n| Lowercase | `reviewing-code` | `Reviewing-Code` |\n| Hyphens, not underscores | `creating-skills` | `creating_skills` |\n| Gerund form (-ing) | `implementing-with-tdd` | `implement-tdd` |\n| Match directory name | `name: foo` in `foo/` | `name: bar` in `foo/` |\n\n### Gerund Suggestions\n\n| Instead of | Use |\n|------------|-----|\n| `code-review` | `reviewing-code` |\n| `plan` | `planning` |\n| `implement` | `implementing` |\n| `design` | `designing` |\n| `finish` | `finishing` |\n\n## Description Guidelines\n\n**Good (3rd person):**\n> Manages task lifecycle transitions and coordinates Trello sync.\n\n**Bad (2nd person):**\n> Use when you need to manage task lifecycle.\n\n## File Size Limits\n\n- SKILL.md: **Under 500 lines**\n- Description: **Under 1024 characters**\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing a skill:\n\n- [ ] Frontmatter has only `name` and `description`\n- [ ] Name is lowercase-hyphenated gerund\n- [ ] Name matches directory name\n- [ ] Description under 1024 characters\n- [ ] Description uses 3rd-person voice\n- [ ] SKILL.md under 500 lines\n- [ ] No \"Claude already knows this\" content\n- [ ] Includes actionable steps or commands\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n```bash\n# List all skills\nbpsai-pair skill list\n\n# Validate all skills\nbpsai-pair skill validate\n\n# Validate specific skill\nbpsai-pair skill validate creating-skills\n\n# Auto-fix simple issues\nbpsai-pair skill validate --fix\n```\n\n## Common Validation Errors\n\n| Error | Fix |\n|-------|-----|\n| Extra frontmatter fields | Remove all fields except name/description |\n| Name mismatch | Make frontmatter name match directory name |\n| Description too long | Shorten to under 1024 characters |\n| File too long | Split into SKILL.md + reference docs |\n\n## Creating a New Skill\n\n1. **Create directory**: `mkdir -p .claude/skills/{skill-name}`\n2. **Create SKILL.md** with template above\n3. **Add content**: Steps, commands, examples\n4. **Validate**: `bpsai-pair skill validate {skill-name}`\n5. **Fix issues**: Address any errors or warnings\n6. **Test**: Verify skill works in practice\n\n## Anti-patterns to Avoid\n\n- **Generic knowledge**: Don''t document things Claude already knows\n- **Excessive length**: Keep focused, link to reference docs\n- **2nd person voice**: Use \"Performs X\" not \"Use when you need X\"\n- **Extra metadata**: No version, author, tags in frontmatter\n- **Underscores**: Use hyphens for multi-word names\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:29:54.451Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing structured skill development and documentation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化技能开发和文档记录能力的AI代理，如Claude Code、AutoGPT和LangChain。","ja":"構造化されたスキル開発とドキュメント作成機能が必要なAIエージェント seperti Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain に適しています。","ko":"구조화된 스킬 개발과 문서화 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트인 Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan un desarrollo de habilidades estructurado y capacidades de documentación.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant un développement de compétences structuré et des capacités de documentation.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die ein strukturiertes Skill-Entwicklung und Dokumentationsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de desenvolvimento de habilidades estruturado e capacidades de documentação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которым необходимы структурированное развитие навыков и возможности документации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل ذكاء اصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى تنمية مهارات منظمة وقدرات توثيقية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create standardized, repeatable, and documented workflows using Markdown for SKILL.md files, organize reference materials, and leverage automation scripts, streamlining complex multi-step processes and reducing errors through a standardized skill directory structure.","zh":"赋予代理创建标准化、可重复和文档化的工作流程的能力，使用Markdown创建SKILL.md文件，组织参考材料，并利用自动化脚本，简化复杂的多步骤流程，通过标准化的技能目录结构减少错误。","ja":"エージェントが標準化された、繰り返し可能な、ドキュメント化されたワークフローを作成する能力を付与し、Markdownを使用してSKILL.mdファイルを作成し、参考資料を整理し、自動化スクリプトを利用して、複雑なマルチステップのプロセスを合理化し、標準化されたスキルディレクトリ構造を通じてエラーを減らす。","ko":"에이전트가 표준화된 반복 가능하고 문서화된 워크플ローを作成할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, Markdown를 사용하여 SKILL.md 파일을 만들고, 참조 자료를 구성하고, 자동화 스크립트를 활용하여 복잡한 멀티스텝 프로세스를 간소화하고, 표준화된 스킬 디렉토리 구조를 통해 오류를 줄입니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear flujos de trabajo estandarizados, repetibles y documentados utilizando Markdown para archivos SKILL.md, organizar materiales de referencia y aprovechar scripts de automatización, simplificando procesos complejos de varios pasos y reduciendo errores a través de una estructura de directorio de habilidades estandarizada.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des flux de travail standardisés, reproductibles et documentés en utilisant Markdown pour les fichiers SKILL.md, organiser les documents de référence et exploiter les scripts d''automatisation, simplifiant les processus complexes à plusieurs étapes et réduisant les erreurs grâce à une structure de répertoire de compétences standardisée.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, standardisierte, wiederholbare und dokumentierte Workflows mit Markdown für SKILL.md-Dateien zu erstellen, Referenzmaterialien zu organisieren und Automatisierungsskripte zu nutzen, um komplexe Mehrschrittprozesse zu vereinfachen und Fehler durch eine standardisierte Skill-Verzeichnisstruktur zu reduzieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem fluxos de trabalho padronizados, repetíveis e documentados usando Markdown para arquivos SKILL.md, organizar materiais de referência e aproveitar scripts de automação, simplificando processos complexos de várias etapas e reduzindo erros por meio de uma estrutura de diretório de habilidades padronizada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать стандартизированные, повторяемые и документированные рабочие процессы с использованием Markdown для файлов SKILL.md, организовывать справочные материалы и использовать автоматизированные сценарии, упрощая сложные многоступенчатые процессы и снижая количество ошибок за счет стандартизированной структуры каталога навыков.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على إنشاء سير عمل موحدة ومتكررة ومدونة باستخدام Markdown لملفات SKILL.md، وتنظيم المواد المرجعية وتحقيق سكريبتات أوتوماتيكية، مما يبسط العمليات المعقدة المتعددة الخطوات ويقلل من الأخطاء من خلال هيكل دليل مهارات موحد."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing team approaches to tasks","Documenting complex workflows","Automating repeated processes across sessions"],"zh":["标准化团队对任务的方法","记录复杂的工作流程","跨会话自动化重复的过程"],"ja":["チームのタスクに対するアプローチを標準化する","複雑なワークフローをドキュメント化する","セッション間で繰り返しのプロセスを自動化する"],"ko":["팀의 작업에 대한 접근 방식을 표준화하는 것","복잡한 워크플로우를 문서화하는 것","세션 간에 반복되는 프로세스를 자동화하는 것"],"es":["Estandarizar los enfoques del equipo para las tareas","Documentar flujos de trabajo complejos","Automatizar procesos repetidos en sesiones"],"fr":["Standardiser les approches de l''équipe pour les tâches","Documenter les flux de travail complexes","Automatiser les processus répétitifs lors des sessions"],"de":["Standardisieren des Teamansatzes für Aufgaben","Dokumentieren komplexer Workflows","Automatisieren wiederholter Prozesse über Sitzungen"],"pt":["Padronizando as abordagens da equipe para tarefas","Documentando fluxos de trabalho complexos","Automatizando processos repetidos em várias sessões"],"ru":["Стандартизация подходов команды к задачам","Документирование сложных рабочих процессов","Автоматизация повторяющихся процессов в нескольких сессиях"],"ar":["مواءمة نهج الفريق للواجبات","توثيق سير العمل المعقدة","أتمتة العمليات المتكررة عبر عدة جلسات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires SKILL.md file for each skill","Directory structure adherence necessary","Optional but beneficial: familiarity with Markdown and scripting for automation"],"zh":["需要为每个技能创建SKILL.md文件","目录结构的遵守是必要的","可选但有益的：Markdown和脚本自动化的熟悉度"],"ja":["各スキルにSKILL.mdファイルを作成する必要がある","ディレクトリ構造の遵守が必要","オプションだが有益：Markdownとスクリプト自動化の熟練度"],"ko":["각각의 스킬에 대해 SKILL.md 파일을 생성해야 함","디렉토리 구조의 준수는 필수적임","선택 사항이지만 유용한 것: Markdown 및 스크립트 자동화에 대한 熟練度"],"es":["Requiere un archivo SKILL.md para cada habilidad","Es necesaria la adhesión a la estructura del directorio","Opcional pero beneficioso: familiaridad con Markdown y scripting para la automatización"],"fr":["Nécessite un fichier SKILL.md pour chaque compétence","L''adhésion à la structure du répertoire est nécessaire","Optionnel mais bénéfique : familiarité avec Markdown et la programmation pour l''automatisation"],"de":["Benötigt eine SKILL.md-Datei für jede Fähigkeit","Einhaltung der Verzeichnisstruktur ist erforderlich","Optional, aber vorteilhaft: Vertrautheit mit Markdown und Skripten für die Automatisierung"],"pt":["Requer arquivo SKILL.md para cada habilidade","Adesão à estrutura de diretório necessária","Opcional, mas benéfico: familiaridade com Markdown e programação para automação"],"ru":["Требуется файл SKILL.md для каждого навыка","Необходимо соблюдение структуры каталога","Необязательно, но полезно: знакомство с Markdown и скриптингом для автоматизации"],"ar":["يتطلب ملف SKILL.md لكل مهارة","الامتثال لهيكل الدليل ضروري","إختياري ولكن مفيد: إلمام بذاكرة التخزين المؤقت وبرمجة الأتمتة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('sundial-org/awesome-openclaw-skills/copywriting', 'community', 'sundial-org', 'awesome-openclaw-skills', 'sundial-org/awesome-openclaw-skills', 'copywriting', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:30:35.468Z', NULL, '{"id":"sundial-org/awesome-openclaw-skills/copywriting","name":"copywriting","description":{"zh":"copywriting","ja":"copywriting","ko":"copywriting","es":"Copywriting es la técnica de escribir contenido de marketing claro y atractivo. Aprende a aplicarla para impulsar acciones.","fr":"Le copywriting est la technique d''écriture de contenu marketing clair et attrayant. Apprenez à l''appliquer pour stimuler les actions.","de":"Copywriting ist die Technik, klar und ansprechendes Marketing-Inhalt zu schreiben. Lernen Sie, es anzuwenden, um Aktionen zu fördern.","pt":"O copywriting é uma técnica de redação que visa aumentar as conversões e melhorar a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Копирайтинг - это техника написания текстов, направленная на увеличение конверсий и улучшение пользовательского опыта.","ar":"كتابة المحتوى هي تقنية للكتابة تهدف إلى زيادة التحويلات وتحسين تجربة المستخدم.","en":"Top OpenClaw skills, regularly updated with the most popular and useful ones."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"copywriting","ja":"copywriting","ko":"copywriting","es":"Escribe como un experto con Copywriting","fr":"Rédige comme un expert avec Copywriting","de":"Schreiben wie ein Experte mit Copywriting","pt":"Copywriting: Técnicas de Redação para Conversão","ru":"Копирайтинг: Техники для Конверсии","ar":"كتابة المحتوى: تقنيات للتحويل","en":"copywriting"},"description":{"zh":"copywriting","ja":"copywriting","ko":"copywriting","es":"Copywriting es la técnica de escribir contenido de marketing claro y atractivo. Aprende a aplicarla para impulsar acciones.","fr":"Le copywriting est la technique d''écriture de contenu marketing clair et attrayant. Apprenez à l''appliquer pour stimuler les actions.","de":"Copywriting ist die Technik, klar und ansprechendes Marketing-Inhalt zu schreiben. Lernen Sie, es anzuwenden, um Aktionen zu fördern.","pt":"O copywriting é uma técnica de redação que visa aumentar as conversões e melhorar a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Копирайтинг - это техника написания текстов, направленная на увеличение конверсий и улучшение пользовательского опыта.","ar":"كتابة المحتوى هي تقنية للكتابة تهدف إلى زيادة التحويلات وتحسين تجربة المستخدم.","en":"Top OpenClaw skills, regularly updated with the most popular and useful ones."},"definition":{"en":"Top OpenClaw skills, regularly updated with the most popular and useful ones."},"features":{"zh":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"ja":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"ko":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"es":["Escribe contenido claro y atractivo","Impulsa acciones con palabras clave efectivas","Aprende a aplicar técnicas de copywriting","Mejora tus habilidades de escritura","Crea contenido de marketing personalizado","Aumenta la conversión con copywriting efectivo"],"fr":["Écrivez du contenu clair et attrayant","Stimulez les actions avec des mots-clés efficaces","Apprenez à appliquer des techniques de copywriting","Améliorez vos compétences en écriture","Créez du contenu marketing personnalisé","Augmentez la conversion avec un copywriting efficace"],"de":["Schreiben Sie klar und ansprechendes Inhalt","Fördern Sie Aktionen mit effektiven Schlüsselwörtern","Lernen Sie, Copywriting-Techniken anzuwenden","Verbessern Sie Ihre Schreibfähigkeiten","Erstellen Sie personalisierten Marketing-Inhalt","Erhöhen Sie die Konvertierung mit effektivem Copywriting"],"pt":["Técnicas de redação para conversão","Análise de público-alvo","Definição de objetivos claros","Criação de textos atraentes","Otimização para experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Техники написания текстов для конверсии","Анализ целевой аудитории","Определение четких целей","Создание привлекательных текстов","Оптимизация для пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["تقنيات الكتابة للتحويل","تحليل الجمهور المستهدف","تحديد أهداف واضحة","إنشاء نصوص جذابة","تحسين تجربة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"ja":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"ko":["copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting","copywriting"],"es":["copywriting","contenido de marketing","redacción publicitaria","palabras clave","impulsar acciones","marketing digital","publicidad en línea","redacción efectiva","contenido atractivo"],"fr":["copywriting","contenu marketing","rédaction publicitaire","mots-clés","stimuler les actions","marketing digital","publicité en ligne","rédaction efficace","contenu attrayant"],"de":["copywriting","marketing-inhalt","werbetext","schlüsselwörter","aktionen fördern","digitales marketing","online-werbung","effektive schreibung","ansprechender inhalt"],"pt":["copywriting","redação para conversão","otimização para usuário","análise de público-alvo","criação de textos atraentes","técnicas de copywriting"],"ru":["копирайтинг","написание текстов для конверсии","оптимизация для пользователя","анализ целевой аудитории","создание привлекательных текстов","техники копирайтинга"],"ar":["كتابة المحتوى","كتابة للتحويل","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","تحليل الجمهور المستهدف","إنشاء نصوص جذابة","تقنيات كتابة المحتوى"]}},"owner":"sundial-org","repo":"awesome-openclaw-skills","repoPath":"sundial-org/awesome-openclaw-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"copywriting","description":"When the user wants to write, rewrite, or improve marketing copy for any page — including homepage, landing pages, pricing pages, feature pages, about pages, or product pages. Also use when the user says write copy for, improve this copy, rewrite this page, marketing copy, headline help, or CTA copy. For email copy, see email-sequence. For popup copy, see popup-cro.","bodyPreview":"# Copywriting\n\nYou are an expert conversion copywriter. Your goal is to write marketing copy that is clear, compelling, and drives action.\n\n## Before Writing\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Page Purpose\n- What type of page is this? (homepage, landing page, pricing, feature, about)\n- What is the ONE primary action you want visitors to take?\n- What''s the secondary action (if any)?\n\n### 2. Audience\n- Who is the ideal customer for this page?\n- What problem are they trying to solv","body":"# Copywriting\n\nYou are an expert conversion copywriter. Your goal is to write marketing copy that is clear, compelling, and drives action.\n\n## Before Writing\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Page Purpose\n- What type of page is this? (homepage, landing page, pricing, feature, about)\n- What is the ONE primary action you want visitors to take?\n- What''s the secondary action (if any)?\n\n### 2. Audience\n- Who is the ideal customer for this page?\n- What problem are they trying to solve?\n- What have they already tried?\n- What objections or hesitations do they have?\n- What language do they use to describe their problem?\n\n### 3. Product/Offer\n- What are you selling or offering?\n- What makes it different from alternatives?\n- What''s the key transformation or outcome?\n- Any proof points (numbers, testimonials, case studies)?\n\n### 4. Context\n- Where is traffic coming from? (ads, organic, email)\n- What do visitors already know before arriving?\n- What messaging are they seeing before this page?\n\n---\n\n## Copywriting Principles\n\n### Clarity Over Cleverness\n- If you have to choose between clear and creative, choose clear\n- Every sentence should have one job\n- Remove words that don''t add meaning\n\n### Benefits Over Features\n- Features: What it does\n- Benefits: What that means for the customer\n- Always connect features to outcomes\n\n### Specificity Over Vagueness\n- Vague: \"Save time on your workflow\"\n- Specific: \"Cut your weekly reporting from 4 hours to 15 minutes\"\n\n### Customer Language Over Company Language\n- Use words your customers use\n- Avoid jargon unless your audience uses it\n- Mirror voice-of-customer from reviews, interviews, support tickets\n\n### One Idea Per Section\n- Don''t try to say everything everywhere\n- Each section should advance one argument\n- Build a logical flow down the page\n\n---\n\n## Writing Style Rules\n\nFollow these core principles. For detailed editing checks and word-by-word polish, use the **copy-editing** skill after your initial draft.\n\n### Core Style Principles\n\n1. **Simple over complex** — Use everyday words. \"Use\" instead of \"utilize,\" \"help\" instead of \"facilitate.\"\n\n2. **Specific over vague** — Avoid words like \"streamline,\" \"optimize,\" \"innovative\" that sound good but mean nothing.\n\n3. **Active over passive** — \"We generate reports\" not \"Reports are generated.\"\n\n4. **Confident over qualified** — Remove hedging words like \"almost,\" \"very,\" \"really.\"\n\n5. **Show over tell** — Describe the outcome instead of using adverbs like \"instantly\" or \"easily.\"\n\n6. **Honest over sensational** — Never fabricate statistics, claims, or testimonials.\n\n### Quick Quality Check\n\nBefore finalizing, scan for:\n- Jargon that could confuse outsiders\n- Sentences trying to do too much (max 3 conjunctions)\n- Passive voice constructions\n- Exclamation points (remove them)\n- Marketing buzzwords without substance\n\nFor a thorough line-by-line review, run the copy through the **copy-editing** skill''s Seven Sweeps framework.\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Be Direct\nGet to the point. Don''t bury the value in qualifications.\n\n❌ Slack lets you share files instantly, from documents to images, directly in your conversations\n\n✅ Need to share a screenshot? Send as many documents, images, and audio files as your heart desires.\n\n### Use Rhetorical Questions\nQuestions engage readers and make them think about their own situation.\n\n✅ Hate returning stuff to Amazon?\n\n✅ Need to share a screenshot?\n\n✅ Tired of chasing approvals?\n\n### Use Analogies and Metaphors\nWhen appropriate, analogies make abstract concepts concrete and memorable.\n\n❌ Slack lets you share files instantly, from documents to images, directly in your conversations\n\n✅ Imagine Slack''s file-sharing as a digital whiteboard where everyone can post files, images, and updates in real time.\n\n### Pepper in Humor (When Appropriate)\nPuns, wit, and humor make copy memorable—but only if it fits the brand and doesn''t undermine clarity.\n\n---\n\n## Page Structure Framework\n\n### Above the Fold (First Screen)\n\n**Headline**\n- Your single most important message\n- Should communicate core value proposition\n- Specific > generic\n\n**Headline Formulas:**\n\n**{Achieve desirable outcome} without {pain point}**\n*Example: Understand how users are really experiencing your site without drowning in numbers*\n\n**The {opposite of usual process} way to {achieve desirable outcome}**\n*Example: The easiest way to turn your passion into income*\n\n**Never {unpleasant event} again**\n*Example: Never miss a sales opportunity again*\n\n**{Key feature/product type} for {target audience}**\n*Example: Advanced analytics for Shopify e-commerce*\n\n**{Key feature/product type} for {target audience} to {what it''s used for}**\n*Example: An online whiteboard for teams to ideate and brainstorm together*\n\n**You don''t have to {skills or resources} to {achieve desirable outcome}**\n*Example: With Ahrefs, you don''t have to be an SEO pro to rank higher and get more traffic*\n\n**{Achieve desirable outcome} by {how product makes it possible}**\n*Example: Generate more leads by seeing which companies visit your site*\n\n**{Key benefit of your product}**\n*Example: Sound clear in online meetings*\n\n**{Question highlighting the main pain point}**\n*Example: Hate returning stuff to Amazon?*\n\n**Turn {input} into {outcome}**\n*Example: Turn your hard-earned sales into repeat customers*\n\n**Additional formulas:**\n- \"[Achieve outcome] in [timeframe]\"\n- \"The [category] that [key differentiator]\"\n- \"Stop [pain]. Start [pleasure].\"\n- \"[Number] [people] use [product] to [outcome]\"\n\n**Subheadline**\n- Expands on the headline\n- Adds specificity or addresses secondary concern\n- 1-2 sentences max\n\n**Primary CTA**\n- Action-oriented button text\n- Communicate what they get, not what they do\n- \"Start Free Trial\" > \"Sign Up\"\n- \"Get Your Report\" > \"Submit\"\n\n**Supporting Visual**\n- Product screenshot, demo, or hero image\n- Should reinforce the message, not distract\n\n### Social Proof Section\n\nOptions (use 1-2):\n- Customer logos (recognizable > many)\n- Key metric (\"10,000+ teams\")\n- Short testimonial with attribution\n- Star rating with review count\n\n### Problem/Pain Section\n\n- Articulate the problem better than they can\n- Show you understand their situation\n- Create recognition (\"that''s exactly my problem\")\n\nStructure:\n- \"You know the feeling...\" or \"If you''re like most [role]...\"\n- Describe the specific frustrations\n- Hint at the cost of not solving it\n\n### Solution/Benefits Section\n\n- Bridge from problem to your solution\n- Focus on 3-5 key benefits (not 10)\n- Each benefit: headline + short explanation + proof point if available\n\nFormat options:\n- Benefit blocks with icons\n- Before/after comparison\n- Feature → Benefit → Proof structure\n\n### How It Works Section\n\n- Reduce perceived complexity\n- 3-4 step process\n- Each step: simple action + outcome\n\nExample:\n1. \"Connect your tools (2 minutes)\"\n2. \"Set your preferences\"\n3. \"Get automated reports every Monday\"\n\n### Social Proof (Detailed)\n\n- Full testimonials with:\n  - Specific results\n  - Customer name, role, company\n  - Photo if possible\n- Case study snippets\n- Logos section (if not above)\n\n### Objection Handling\n\nCommon objections to address:\n- \"Is this right for my situation?\"\n- \"What if it doesn''t work?\"\n- \"Is it hard to set up?\"\n- \"How is this different from X?\"\n\nFormats:\n- FAQ section\n- Comparison table\n- Guarantee/promise section\n- \"Built for [specific audience]\" section\n\n### Final CTA Section\n\n- Recap the value proposition\n- Repeat the primary CTA\n- Add urgency if genuine (deadline, limited availability)\n- Risk reversal (guarantee, free trial, no credit card)\n\n---\n\n## Landing Page Section Variety\n\nA great landing page isn''t just a list of features. Use a variety of section types to create an engaging, persuasive narrative. Mix and match from these:\n\n### Section Types to Include\n\n**How It Works (Numbered Steps)**\nWalk users through the process in 3-4 clear steps. Reduces perceived complexity and shows the path to value.\n\n**Alternative/Competitor Comparison**\nShow how you stack up against the status quo or competitors. Tables, side-by-side comparisons, or \"Unlike X, we...\" sections.\n\n**Founder Manifesto / Our Story**\nShare why you built this and what you believe. Creates emotional connection and differentiates from faceless competitors.\n\n**Testimonials**\nCustomer quotes with names, photos, and specific results. Multiple formats: quote cards, video testimonials, tweet embeds.\n\n**Case Studies**\nDeeper stories of customer success. Problem → Solution → Results format with specific metrics.\n\n**Use Cases**\nShow different ways the product is used. Helps visitors self-identify: \"This is for people like me.\"\n\n**Personas / \"Built For\" Sections**\nExplicitly call out who the product is for: \"Perfect for marketers,\" \"Built for agencies,\" etc.\n\n**Stats and Social Proof**\nKey metrics that build credibility: \"10,000+ customers,\" \"4.9/5 rating,\" \"$2M saved for customers.\"\n\n**Demo / Product Tour**\nInteractive demos, video walkthroughs, or GIF previews showing the product in action.\n\n**FAQ Section**\nAddress common objections and questions. Good for SEO and reducing support burden.\n\n**Integrations / Partners**\nShow what tools you connect with. Logos build credibility and answer \"Will this work with my stack?\"\n\n**Pricing Preview**\nEven on non-pricing pages, a pricing teaser can move decision-makers forward.\n\n**Guarantee / Risk Reversal**\nMoney-back guarantee, free trial terms, or \"cancel anytime\" messaging reduces friction.\n\n### Recommended Section Mix\n\nFor a landing page, aim for variety. Don''t just stack features:\n\n**Typical Feature-Heavy Page (Weak):**\n1. Hero\n2. Feature 1\n3. Feature 2\n4. Feature 3\n5. Feature 4\n6. CTA\n\n**Varied, Engaging Page (Strong):**\n1. Hero with clear value prop\n2. Social proof bar (logos or stats)\n3. Problem/pain section\n4. How it works (3 steps)\n5. Key benefits (2-3, not 10)\n6. Testimonial\n7. Use cases or personas\n8. Comparison to alternatives\n9. Case study snippet\n10. FAQ\n11. Final CTA with guarantee\n\n---\n\n## CTA Copy Guidelines\n\n**Weak CTAs (avoid):**\n- Submit\n- Sign Up\n- Learn More\n- Click Here\n- Get Started\n\n**Strong CTAs (use):**\n- Start Free Trial\n- Get [Specific Thing]\n- See [Product] in Action\n- Create Your First [Thing]\n- Book My Demo\n- Download the Guide\n- Try It Free\n\n**CTA formula:**\n[Action Verb] + [What They Get] + [Qualifier if needed]\n\nExamples:\n- \"Start My Free Trial\"\n- \"Get the Complete Checklist\"\n- \"See Pricing for My Team\"\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\nWhen writing copy, provide:\n\n### Page Copy\nOrganized by section with clear labels:\n- Headline\n- Subheadline\n- CTA\n- Section headers\n- Body copy\n- Secondary CTAs\n\n### Annotations\nFor key elements, explain:\n- Why you made this choice\n- What principle it applies\n- Alternatives considered\n\n### Alternatives\nFor headlines and CTAs, provide 2-3 options:\n- Option A: [copy] — [rationale]\n- Option B: [copy] — [rationale]\n- Option C: [copy] — [rationale]\n\n### Meta Content (if relevant)\n- Page title (for SEO)\n- Meta description\n\n---\n\n## Page-Specific Guidance\n\n### Homepage Copy\n- Serve multiple audiences without being generic\n- Lead with broadest value proposition\n- Provide clear paths for different visitor intents\n- Balance \"ready to buy\" and \"still researching\"\n\n### Landing Page Copy\n- Single message, single CTA\n- Match headline to ad/traffic source\n- Complete argument on one page\n- Remove distractions (often no nav)\n\n### Pricing Page Copy\n- Help visitors choose the right plan\n- Clarify what''s included at each level\n- Address \"which is right for me?\" anxiety\n- Make recommended plan obvious\n\n### Feature Page Copy\n- Connect feature to benefit to outcome\n- Show use cases and examples\n- Differentiate from competitors'' versions\n- Clear path to try or buy\n\n### About Page Copy\n- Tell the story of why you exist\n- Connect company mission to customer benefit\n- Build trust through transparency\n- Still include a CTA (it''s still a marketing page)\n\n---\n\n## Voice and Tone Considerations\n\nBefore writing, establish:\n\n**Formality level:**\n- Casual/conversational\n- Professional but friendly\n- Formal/enterprise\n\n**Brand personality:**\n- Playful or serious?\n- Bold or understated?\n- Technical or accessible?\n\nMaintain consistency throughout, but adjust intensity:\n- Headlines can be bolder\n- Body copy should be clearer\n- CTAs should be action-oriented\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **copy-editing**: For polishing and improving existing copy (use after writing your first draft)\n- **page-cro**: If the page structure/strategy needs work, not just copy\n- **email-sequence**: For email copywriting\n- **popup-cro**: For popup and modal copy\n- **ab-test-setup**: To test copy variations properly\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:30:35.468Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Marketing Agents needing compelling conversion copywriting capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要撰写令人信服的转换复制内容的营销代理。","ja":"マーケティングエージェントが説得力のあるコンベージョンコピーを書く必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"説得력을 갖춘 전환 복제 기능이 필요한 마케팅 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing que necesitan capacidades de redacción de copias de conversión convincentes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing ayant besoin de capacités de rédaction de copies de conversion convaincantes.","de":"Perfekt für Marketing-Agenten, die überzeugende Konversions-Kopie-Schreibaufgaben benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing que precisam de capacidades de redação de cópia de conversão convincente.","ru":"Идеально для маркетинговых агентов, которым требуются возможности убедительной копирайтинга для конверсии.","ar":"مثالي لعمال التسويق الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات كتابة نسخ متقنّة لتحويل المبيعات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft clear, compelling marketing copy that drives action, utilizing context such as page purpose and audience insights to inform their writing, and leveraging techniques like gathering audience context and understanding page goals to optimize conversion rates.","zh":"使代理能够利用上下文（如页面目的和受众见解）来撰写清晰、令人信服的营销文案，并利用技术（如收集受众上下文和了解页面目标）来优化转换率。","ja":"エージェントがページの目的やオーディエンスの洞察などのコンテキストを利用して、明確で説得力のあるマーケティングコピーを作成できるようにし、オーディエンスのコンテキストを収集したりページの目標を理解したりするなどのテクニックを利用してコンバージョン率を最適化します。","ko":"에이전트가 페이지 목적 및 대상자 인사이트와 같은 컨텍스트를 사용하여 명확하고 설득力的 인 마케팅 복사본을 작성할 수 있도록 하며, 대상자 컨텍스트 수집 및 페이지 목표 이해와 같은 기술을 사용하여 전환률을 최적화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear copias de marketing claras y convincentes que impulsan la acción, utilizando contextos como el propósito de la página y las perspectivas de la audiencia para informar su escritura, y aprovechando técnicas como la recopilación de contextos de audiencia y la comprensión de los objetivos de la página para optimizar las tasas de conversión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des copies de marketing claires et convaincantes qui poussent à l''action, en utilisant des contextes tels que le but de la page et les insights du public pour éclairer leur écriture, et en exploitant des techniques comme la collecte de contextes d''audience et la compréhension des objectifs de page pour optimiser les taux de conversion.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, klare und überzeugende Marketing-Kopien zu erstellen, die Aktionen auslösen, unter Nutzung von Kontexten wie der Seitenzweck und die Einblicke der Zielgruppe, um ihre Schreibweise zu informieren, und unter Nutzung von Techniken wie der Sammlung von Zielgruppenkontexten und dem Verständnis der Seitenziele, um die Konversionsraten zu optimieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar cópias de marketing claras e convincentes que impulsionam ações, utilizando contextos como o propósito da página e insights do público para informar sua escrita, e utilizando técnicas como coletar contexto do público e entender os objetivos da página para otimizar as taxas de conversão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать ясные и убедительные маркетинговые копии, которые стимулируют действие, используя контекст, такой как цель страницы и информация о аудитории, для информирования их письма, и используя техники, такие как сбор контекста аудитории и понимание целей страницы для оптимизации коэффициентов конверсии.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من صياغة نسخ تسويقية واضحة ومقنعة تدفع إلى العمل، مستخدمين سياقات مثل غرض الصفحة واطّلاعات الجمهور لإبلاغ كتابتهم، واستخدام تقنيات مثل جمع سياق الجمهور وفهم أهداف الصفحة لتحسين معدلات التحويل."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating landing page copy","Crafting homepage headlines","Writing persuasive feature descriptions"],"zh":["生成着陆页复制内容","撰写首页标题","编写令人信服的功能描述"],"ja":["ランディングページのコピー生成","ホームページのヘッドライン作成","説得力のある機能説明の作成"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지 복사본 생성","홈페이지 헤드라인 작성","설득력 있는 기능 설명 작성"],"es":["Generación de copias de página de destino","Creación de titulares de página de inicio","Escritura de descripciones de características persuasivas"],"fr":["Génération de copies de page de destination","Création de titres de page d''accueil","Rédaction de descriptions de fonctionnalités persuasives"],"de":["Generierung von Landingpage-Kopien","Erstellung von Homepage-Überschriften","Schreiben von überzeugenden Funktionsbeschreibungen"],"pt":["Geração de cópia de página de destino","Criação de títulos de página inicial","Escrita de descrições de recursos persuasivas"],"ru":["Генерация копии целевой страницы","Создание заголовков домашней страницы","Написание убедительных описаний функций"],"ar":["توليد نسخ صفحة الوجهة","صياغة عناوين الصفحة الرئيسية","كتابة描述ات ممتعة للمميزات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of target audience and page purpose","Limited to text-based copywriting"],"zh":["需要了解目标受众和页面目的","仅限文本基于复制内容"],"ja":["ターゲットオーディエンスとページの目的を理解する必要がある","テキストベースのコピー作成のみ"],"ko":["대상자 및 페이지 목적을 이해해야 함","텍스트 기반 복사본 작성만 가능"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la audiencia objetivo y el propósito de la página","Limitado a la creación de copias de texto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du public cible et du but de la page","Limité à la création de copies de texte"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Zielgruppe und des Seitenzwecks","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von Textkopien"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do público-alvo e propósito da página","Limitado à criação de cópia baseada em texto"],"ru":["Требует понимания целевой аудитории и цели страницы","Ограничен созданием текстовой копии"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم الجمهور المستهدف وغرض الصفحة","محدود بكتابة النسخ القائمة على النص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('9tykeshav/mern-ninja-cc/code-reviewer', 'community', '9tykeshav', 'mern-ninja-cc', '9tykeshav/mern-ninja-cc', 'code-reviewer', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z', '2026-02-18T07:30:30.535Z', NULL, '{"id":"9tykeshav/mern-ninja-cc/code-reviewer","name":"code-reviewer","description":{"zh":"MERN ","ja":"MERN ","ko":"MERN ","es":"Herramientas de revisión de código MERN para mejorar la salud de tus proyectos. Analiza el estado de compilación y documentos.","fr":"Outils de révision de code MERN pour améliorer la santé de vos projets. Analysez l''état de compilation et les documents.","de":"MERN-Code-Review-Tools für die Verbesserung der Gesundheit Ihrer Projekte. Analysieren Sie den Kompilierungsstatus und Dokumente.","pt":"O Code Reviewer é uma ferramenta de revisão de código MERN que ajuda a garantir a saúde do projeto antes de revisar o código.","ru":"Code Reviewer — это инструмент для проверки кода MERN, который помогает обеспечить здоровье проекта перед проверкой кода.","ar":"مُراجع الشفرة هو أداة مراجعة شفرة MERN تساعد على ضمان صحة المشروع قبل مراجعة الشفرة.","en":" MERN stack mastery tools for Claude Code – code reviewer and test generator for MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js projects"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"MERN ","ja":"MERN","ko":"MERN ","es":"Revisión de código MERN - Herramientas de maestría","fr":"Réviseur de code MERN - Outils de maîtrise","de":"MERN-Code-Reviewer - Meisterwerkzeuge","pt":"Code Reviewer: Ferramentas de revisão de código MERN","ru":"Code Reviewer: Инструменты для проверки кода MERN","ar":"مُراجع الشفرة: أدوات مراجعة الشفرة MERN","en":"code-reviewer"},"description":{"zh":"MERN ","ja":"MERN ","ko":"MERN ","es":"Herramientas de revisión de código MERN para mejorar la salud de tus proyectos. Analiza el estado de compilación y documentos.","fr":"Outils de révision de code MERN pour améliorer la santé de vos projets. Analysez l''état de compilation et les documents.","de":"MERN-Code-Review-Tools für die Verbesserung der Gesundheit Ihrer Projekte. Analysieren Sie den Kompilierungsstatus und Dokumente.","pt":"O Code Reviewer é uma ferramenta de revisão de código MERN que ajuda a garantir a saúde do projeto antes de revisar o código.","ru":"Code Reviewer — это инструмент для проверки кода MERN, который помогает обеспечить здоровье проекта перед проверкой кода.","ar":"مُراجع الشفرة هو أداة مراجعة شفرة MERN تساعد على ضمان صحة المشروع قبل مراجعة الشفرة.","en":" MERN stack mastery tools for Claude Code – code reviewer and test generator for MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js projects"},"definition":{"en":" MERN stack mastery tools for Claude Code – code reviewer and test generator for MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js projects"},"features":{"zh":["MERN "," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README"],"ja":["MERN "," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README"],"ko":["MERN "," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README"],"es":["Análisis de estado de compilación","Revisión de documentos de proyecto","Generación de pruebas para MongoDB, Express, React y Node.js","Mejora de la salud del proyecto","Soporte para proyectos MERN","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Analyse de l''état de compilation","Révision des documents de projet","Génération de tests pour MongoDB, Express, React et Node.js","Amélioration de la santé du projet","Support pour les projets MERN","Intégration avec les outils de développement"],"de":["Analyse des Kompilierungsstatus","Überprüfung von Projektdokumenten","Generierung von Tests für MongoDB, Express, React und Node.js","Verbesserung der Gesundheit des Projekts","Unterstützung für MERN-Projekte","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Verificação do status de compilação","Leitura de documentação do projeto","Análise de saúde do projeto","Suporte a MERN","Geração de testes","Revisão de código personalizada"],"ru":["Проверка статуса сборки","Чтение документации проекта","Анализ здоровья проекта","Поддержка MERN","Генерация тестов","Пользовательская проверка кода"],"ar":["فحص حالة الترجمة","قراءة وثائق المشروع","تحليل صحة المشروع","دعم MERN","توليد الاختبارات","مراجعة الشفرة المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["MERN"," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"ja":["MERN"," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"ko":["MERN"," "," ","tsc --noEmit","README","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"es":["revisor de código MERN","herramientas de revisión de código","análisis de proyecto","mejora de la salud del proyecto","desarrollo de software","MERN","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"fr":["réviseur de code MERN","outils de révision de code","analyse de projet","amélioration de la santé du projet","développement de logiciels","MERN","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"de":["MERN-Code-Reviewer","Code-Review-Tools","Projektanalyse","Verbesserung der Gesundheit des Projekts","Software-Entwicklung","MERN","MongoDB","Express","React","Node.js"],"pt":["revisão de código MERN","ferramentas de revisão de código","saúde do projeto","compilação","documentação","MERN","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["проверка кода MERN","инструменты для проверки кода","здоровье проекта","сборка","документация","MERN","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مراجعة الشفرة MERN","أدوات مراجعة الشفرة","صحة المشروع","الترجمة","وثائق","MERN","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"9tykeshav","repo":"mern-ninja-cc","repoPath":"9tykeshav/mern-ninja-cc","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.457Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-reviewer","description":"Use when asked to review MERN stack code - comprehensive code reviewer that checks project health, security, maintainability, performance, testing, and architecture. Combines general code quality analysis with MERN-specific expertise.","bodyPreview":"# Code Reviewer\n\n## Overview\n\nComprehensive code review: General intelligence + MERN specialization.\n\n**Philosophy:** Check project health FIRST, then dive into code. A 6,000-line file is a problem regardless of what''s in it.\n\n## Review Workflow\n\n### Phase 0: Project Health (Do This First)\n\nBefore reading any code, assess project health:\n\n1. **Build status:** Run `tsc --noEmit` or check for compilation errors\n2. **Project docs:** Read README, any STATUS/BUGS/TODO files - look for deployment bloc","body":"# Code Reviewer\n\n## Overview\n\nComprehensive code review: General intelligence + MERN specialization.\n\n**Philosophy:** Check project health FIRST, then dive into code. A 6,000-line file is a problem regardless of what''s in it.\n\n## Review Workflow\n\n### Phase 0: Project Health (Do This First)\n\nBefore reading any code, assess project health:\n\n1. **Build status:** Run `tsc --noEmit` or check for compilation errors\n2. **Project docs:** Read README, any STATUS/BUGS/TODO files - look for deployment blockers\n3. **Test health:** Do tests exist? Check `package.json` scripts, look for test directories\n4. **File sizes:** `find src -name \"*.ts\" -o -name \"*.tsx\" | xargs wc -l | sort -n | tail -20`\n5. **Dependencies:** Check for `npm audit` issues, unusual deps (Angular in React?)\n\n**Stop here if:** Build is broken, docs say \"DO NOT DEPLOY\", or critical blockers found. Report immediately.\n\n### Phase 1: Scope Detection\n\n1. Identify scope from context:\n   - Full repo → Broad review, sample key files\n   - Feature/PR → All changed files\n   - Single file → Deep dive\n2. Detect layers: React? Express? MongoDB? Node.js?\n3. If ambiguous → ask user\n\n### Phase 2: Review by Priority\n\n| Priority | Focus | Severity |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| 0. Blockers | Build failures, \"DO NOT DEPLOY\", broken deploys | STOP |\n| 1. Security | Injection, auth, secrets, XSS | Critical |\n| 2. Maintainability | God files, complexity, duplication | Critical/Important |\n| 3. Performance | N+1, missing indexes, re-renders | Important |\n| 4. Testing | No tests, low coverage, flaky tests | Important |\n| 5. Best Practices | Error handling, async patterns | Suggestion |\n| 6. Architecture | API design, state management | Suggestion |\n\nLoad reference files ON-DEMAND when you hit MERN-specific edge cases.\n\n### Phase 3: Report\n\nUse the output format below. Offer to fix starting with Critical.\n\n## Output Format\n\n```markdown\n# MERN Code Review\n\n## Project Health\n- Build: [Compiles / X errors / Not checked]\n- Tests: [X passing / X failing / None found]\n- Blockers: [Any deployment blockers from docs]\n- Large files: [Files >500 lines]\n\n## Scope\n[What was reviewed]\n\n## Summary\n- Files reviewed: X\n- Issues: X Critical, X Important, X Suggestions\n\n## Critical (Must Fix)\n### [C1] Category: Title\n**File:** `path:line`\n**Why:** [1-2 sentences]\n**Fix:** [Code or instruction]\n\n## Important (Should Fix)\n### [I1] Category: Title\n...\n\n## Suggestions\n- `file:line` - Note\n\n## What''s Good\n- [Positive observations]\n\n## Verdict\n[Ready to deploy / Blocked / Needs fixes] - [1 sentence reason]\n\n---\n**Ready to fix these?** Starting with Critical issues.\n```\n\n## Checklists\n\n**Minimum required checks.** Report other issues you find during review.\n\n### Blockers (Check First)\n- [ ] Project compiles without errors\n- [ ] No \"DO NOT DEPLOY\" or similar warnings in docs\n- [ ] No critical security advisories in `npm audit`\n\n### Security\n- [ ] No `$where`, `$ne`, `$regex` with user input (NoSQL injection/ReDoS)\n- [ ] No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without DOMPurify\n- [ ] JWT in httpOnly cookies, not localStorage\n- [ ] Secrets in env vars, not hardcoded (check config files too, not just code)\n- [ ] Helmet middleware configured\n- [ ] CORS properly restricted\n- [ ] Rate limiting on auth endpoints\n- [ ] Input validation on all endpoints\n- [ ] No `eval()` or `new Function()` with user input\n\n### Maintainability\n- [ ] No file >500 lines (god files)\n- [ ] No function >50 lines\n- [ ] No class/component with >20 methods\n- [ ] No deep nesting (>4 levels)\n- [ ] No copy-paste blocks >10 lines (DRY)\n- [ ] Clear naming (no cryptic abbreviations)\n- [ ] Consistent code style\n\n### Performance\n- [ ] No N+1 queries (use populate/$lookup)\n- [ ] Indexes on frequently queried fields\n- [ ] `.lean()` for read-only Mongoose queries\n- [ ] No `fs.readFileSync` in request handlers\n- [ ] React.memo on expensive components\n- [ ] useCallback/useMemo where beneficial\n- [ ] Pagination on list endpoints\n\n### Testing\n- [ ] Tests exist for critical paths (auth, payments, core flows)\n- [ ] Test coverage reasonable (>50% for services)\n- [ ] No skipped/commented-out tests\n- [ ] Tests actually assert behavior (not just \"doesn''t crash\")\n- [ ] Mocks don''t hide real integration issues\n\n### Best Practices\n- [ ] Async errors handled (try/catch or error middleware)\n- [ ] useEffect cleanup functions present\n- [ ] No floating promises (unhandled async)\n- [ ] Middleware order correct (body-parser before routes, error handler last)\n- [ ] Environment variables validated at startup\n- [ ] Graceful shutdown handlers\n\n### Architecture\n- [ ] Consistent API response format\n- [ ] Service layer between controllers and DB\n- [ ] Types aligned frontend/backend\n- [ ] No circular dependencies\n- [ ] Clear module boundaries\n- [ ] No god components (React >300 lines)\n- [ ] State management appropriate for complexity\n\n## Red Flags (Immediate Critical)\n\nThese are automatic Critical issues:\n\n- `eval()`, `new Function()` with user input\n- Hardcoded secrets/credentials in code\n- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization\n- JWT/auth tokens in localStorage\n- Missing auth middleware on protected routes\n- `$where` clause with user input\n- File >1000 lines\n- \"DO NOT DEPLOY\" in project docs\n- `npm audit` critical vulnerabilities\n\n## Scope Calibration\n\n| Scope | Phase 0 | Code Depth | Focus |\n|-------|---------|------------|-------|\n| Single file | Skip | Deep | All checklists on that file |\n| Last commit | Quick | Medium | Changed lines + immediate context |\n| Feature/PR | Quick | Medium | All changed files |\n| Full repo | Full | Broad | Sample key files, architecture |\n\n## Reference Files\n\nLoad ONLY when you encounter MERN-specific patterns you need to verify:\n\n| When to Load | Reference |\n|--------------|-----------|\n| NoSQL query security question | [security.md](reference/security.md) |\n| React hooks/re-render issue | [react.md](reference/react.md) |\n| Express middleware question | [express.md](reference/express.md) |\n| MongoDB schema/index question | [mongodb.md](reference/mongodb.md) |\n| Node.js async/memory issue | [nodejs.md](reference/nodejs.md) |\n| API design/auth flow question | [fullstack.md](reference/fullstack.md) |\n\n**Do NOT load all references upfront.** They''re for edge cases, not general review.\n\n## Don''t\n\n- Don''t claim \"no issues found\" without actually searching for them\n- Don''t report on code you haven''t read\n- Don''t classify style issues as Critical\n\n## Examples\n\n### God File Detection\n```\nFound: EventService.ts - 6,165 lines\n→ Critical [C1] Maintainability: God file\n→ Recommend split into: EventQueryService, EventBookingService,\n   EventGuestService, EventInviteService (~500 lines each)\n```\n\n### Missing Health Check\n```\nFound: CURRENT_STATUS_AND_BUGS.md contains \"DO NOT DEPLOY\"\n→ Critical [C1] Blocker: Deployment blocked by known issues\n→ Fix TypeScript errors in EditEventModal.tsx before proceeding\n```\n\n### Security + Specific Fix\n```\nFound: No Helmet middleware in index.ts\n→ Critical [C2] Security: Missing security headers\n→ Fix: npm install helmet && app.use(helmet())\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:30:30.535Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing comprehensive MERN stack code review and testing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要全面 MERN 技术栈代码审查和测试功能的全栈智能体。","ja":"包括的な MERN スタックのコードレビューとテスト機能を必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"포괄적인 MERN 스택 코드 검토 및 테스트 기능이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full Stack que necesitan una revisión y prueba de código de pila MERN completa.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack qui ont besoin d''une révision et de tests de code de pile MERN complet.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine umfassende Code-Überprüfung und Testfunktionen für den MERN-Stack benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de uma revisão e teste de código abrangentes da pilha MERN.","ru":"Идеально подходит для полнофункциональных агентов, которым необходим комплексный обзор и тестирование кода стека MERN.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الويب الكامل الذين يحتاجون إلى مراجعة شاملة وقدرات اختبار للكود المكون من المجموعة MERN."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to assess project health, check build status with `tsc --noEmit`, and review code quality for MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js projects, ensuring adherence to best practices and philosophies like checking project health first.","zh":"赋能智能体评估项目健康状况，使用 `tsc --noEmit` 检查构建状态，并为 MongoDB、Express、React 和 Node.js 项目审查代码质量，确保遵循最佳实践和理念（如优先检查项目健康状况）。","ja":"エージェントがプロジェクトの健全性を評価し、`tsc --noEmit` でビルドステータスをチェックし、MongoDB、Express、React、Node.js プロジェクトのコード品質をレビューする能力を付与し、プロジェクトの健全性を最初に確認するなどのベストプラクティスと理念への準拠を保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 프로젝트 상태를 평가하고, `tsc --noEmit`으로 빌드 상태를 확인하며, MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js 프로젝트의 코드 품질을 검토하여 프로젝트 상태를 우선 확인하는 것과 같은 모범 사례 및 철학을 준수하도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a evaluar la salud del proyecto, verificar el estado de compilación con `tsc --noEmit` y revisar la calidad del código para proyectos de MongoDB, Express, React y Node.js, garantizando el cumplimiento de las mejores prácticas y filosofías como la comprobación de la salud del proyecto primero.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer la santé du projet, de vérifier le statut de build avec `tsc --noEmit` et d''examiner la qualité du code pour les projets MongoDB, Express, React et Node.js, en garantissant le respect des meilleures pratiques et philosophies comme la vérification de la santé du projet en premier.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Projektgesundheit zu bewerten, den Build-Status mit `tsc --noEmit` zu überprüfen und die Codequalität für MongoDB-, Express-, React- und Node.js-Projekte zu überprüfen, wodurch die Einhaltung der besten Praktiken und Philosophien wie die Überprüfung der Projektgesundheit als Erstes sichergestellt wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes avaliem a saúde do projeto, verifiquem o status da compilação com `tsc --noEmit` e revisem a qualidade do código para projetos MongoDB, Express, React e Node.js, garantindo a adesão às melhores práticas e filosofias, como verificar a saúde do projeto primeiro.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оценить здоровье проекта, проверить статус сборки с помощью `tsc --noEmit` и просмотреть качество кода для проектов MongoDB, Express, React и Node.js, обеспечивая соблюдение лучших практик и философий, таких как проверка здоровья проекта в первую очередь.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تقييم صحة المشروع، ومراجعة حالة البناء باستخدام `tsc --noEmit` ومراجعة جودة الكود لمشاريع MongoDB و Express و React و Node.js، وضمان الالتزام بأفضل الممارسات والمفاهيم مثل التحقق من صحة المشروع أولاً."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for MERN stack projects","Generating tests for Node.js applications","Debugging compilation errors with `tsc --noEmit`"],"zh":["自动化 MERN 技术栈项目的代码审查","为 Node.js 应用程序生成测试","使用 `tsc --noEmit` 调试编译错误"],"ja":["MERN スタックプロジェクトのコードレビューの自動化","Node.js アプリケーションのテスト生成","`tsc --noEmit` を使用したコンパイルエラーのデバッグ"],"ko":["MERN 스택 프로젝트의 코드 검토 자동화","Node.js 애플리케이션용 테스트 생성","`tsc --noEmit`으로 컴파일 오류 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para proyectos de pila MERN","Generación de pruebas para aplicaciones Node.js","Depuración de errores de compilación con `tsc --noEmit`"],"fr":["Automatisation des revues de code pour les projets de pile MERN","Génération de tests pour les applications Node.js","Débogage des erreurs de compilation avec `tsc --noEmit`"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für MERN-Stack-Projekte","Generierung von Tests für Node.js-Anwendungen","Fehlerbehebung bei Kompilierungsfehlern mit `tsc --noEmit`"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para projetos da pilha MERN","Gerar testes para aplicações Node.js","Depurar erros de compilação com `tsc --noEmit`"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обзор кода для проектов стека MERN","Генерировать тесты для приложений Node.js","Отлаживать ошибки компиляции с помощью `tsc --noEmit`"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي لمراجعة الكود لمشاريع المجموعة MERN","توليد الاختبارات للتطبيقات Node.js","تصحيح الأخطاء عند الترجمة باستخدام `tsc --noEmit`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires MERN stack project setup","Limited to MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js technologies"],"zh":["需要 MERN 技术栈项目设置","仅限于 MongoDB、Express、React 和 Node.js 技术"],"ja":["MERN スタックプロジェクトのセットアップが必要","MongoDB、Express、React、Node.js 技術に限定される"],"ko":["MERN 스택 프로젝트 설정 필요","MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js 기술로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración de proyecto de pila MERN","Limitado a tecnologías de MongoDB, Express, React y Node.js"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de projet de pile MERN","Limité aux technologies MongoDB, Express, React et Node.js"],"de":["Benötigt eine MERN-Stack-Projekt-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf MongoDB-, Express-, React- und Node.js-Technologien"],"pt":["Requer configuração do projeto da pilha MERN","Limitado às tecnologias MongoDB, Express, React e Node.js"],"ru":["Требует настройки проекта стека MERN","Ограничен технологиями MongoDB, Express, React и Node.js"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مشروع المجموعة MERN","محدود بتكنولوجيا MongoDB و Express و React و Node.js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
