 et de l''authentification","Configuration des variables d''environnement","Prise en charge des scénarios hors ligne"],"de":["Implementierung von API-Anfragen","Konfiguration von Cachestrategien","Fehlersuche bei Netzwerkfehlern","Verwaltung von Token und Authentifizierung","Konfiguration von Umgebungsvariablen","Unterstützung für Offline-Szenarien"],"pt":["Requisições de API seguras","Fetch de dados com React Query e SWR","Depuração de falhas de rede","Estratégias de caching","Gestão de autenticação e tokens","Configuração de URLs de API e variáveis de ambiente"],"ru":["Безопасные запросы API","Загрузка данных с React Query и SWR","Отладка сетевых сбоев","Стратегии кэширования","Управление аутентификацией и токенами","Настройка URL-адресов API и переменных среды"],"ar":["طلبات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الآمنة","استرجاع البيانات مع React Query و SWR","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","إدارة مصادقة وتوكن","تكوين عناوين URL ل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات ومتغيرات البيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["原生数据获取","API请求","数据获取","缓存","网络调试","安全保障","链上安全","Agent安全"],"ja":["ネイティブデータ取得","APIリクエスト","データ取得","キャッシュ","ネットワークデバッグ","安全性","チェーン上の安全","エージェントの安全"],"ko":["네이티브 데이터 가져오기","API 요청","데이터 가져오기","캐싱","네트워크 디버깅","안전 보장","체인 상의 안전","에이전트의 안전"],"es":["recopilación de datos nativa","solicitudes de API","depuración de errores","estrategias de caché","gestión de tokens","autenticación","variables de entorno","desarrollo de agentes"],"fr":["récupération de données native","requêtes API","débogage","stratégies de cache","gestion des tokens","authentification","variables d''environnement","développement d''agents"],"de":["native Datenabfrage","API-Anfragen","Fehlersuche","Cachestrategien","Tokenverwaltung","Authentifizierung","Umgebungsvariablen","Agentenentwicklung"],"pt":["native-data-fetching","segurança em cadeia","requisições de API","fetch de dados","caching","depuração de rede","autenticação","tokens"],"ru":["нативная загрузка данных","безопасность цепочки","запросы API","загрузка данных","кэширование","отладка сетевых сбоев","аутентификация","токены"],"ar":["استرجاع البيانات الأصلي","حاجز أمان للشبكة","طلبات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","استرجاع البيانات","التخزين المؤقت","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","مصادقة","توكن"]}},"owner":"keep-starknet-strange","repo":"starkclaw","repoPath":"keep-starknet-strange/starkclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.458Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"native-data-fetching","description":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strategies, offline support.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues &","body":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues & Solutions\n\n### 1. Basic Fetch Usage\n\n**Simple GET request**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchUser = async (userId: string) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${userId}`);\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**POST request with body**:\n\n```tsx\nconst createUser = async (userData: UserData) => {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify(userData),\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const error = await response.json();\n    throw new Error(error.message);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Query (TanStack Query)\n\n**Setup**:\n\n```tsx\n// app/_layout.tsx\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 5, // 5 minutes\n      retry: 2,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nexport default function RootLayout() {\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <Stack />\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Fetching data**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data, isLoading, error, refetch } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"user\", userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchUser(userId),\n  });\n\n  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;\n  if (error) return <Error message={error.message} />;\n\n  return <Profile user={data} />;\n}\n```\n\n**Mutations**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMutation, useQueryClient } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction CreateUserForm() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n\n  const mutation = useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createUser,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      // Invalidate and refetch\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"users\"] });\n    },\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (data: UserData) => {\n    mutation.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  return <Form onSubmit={handleSubmit} isLoading={mutation.isPending} />;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Error Handling\n\n**Comprehensive error handling**:\n\n```tsx\nclass ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(message: string, public status: number, public code?: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n  }\n}\n\nconst fetchWithErrorHandling = async (url: string, options?: RequestInit) => {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, options);\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      const error = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n      throw new ApiError(\n        error.message || \"Request failed\",\n        response.status,\n        error.code\n      );\n    }\n\n    return response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n      throw error;\n    }\n    // Network error (no internet, timeout, etc.)\n    throw new ApiError(\"Network error\", 0, \"NETWORK_ERROR\");\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Retry logic**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchWithRetry = async (\n  url: string,\n  options?: RequestInit,\n  retries = 3\n) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fetchWithErrorHandling(url, options);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;\n      // Exponential backoff\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 1000));\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authentication\n\n**Token management**:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as SecureStore from \"expo-secure-store\";\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"auth_token\";\n\nexport const auth = {\n  getToken: () => SecureStore.getItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n  setToken: (token: string) => SecureStore.setItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY, token),\n  removeToken: () => SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n};\n\n// Authenticated fetch wrapper\nconst authFetch = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}) => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  return fetch(url, {\n    ...options,\n    headers: {\n      ...options.headers,\n      Authorization: token ? `Bearer ${token}` : \"\",\n    },\n  });\n};\n```\n\n**Token refresh**:\n\n```tsx\nlet isRefreshing = false;\nlet refreshPromise: Promise<string> | null = null;\n\nconst getValidToken = async (): Promise<string> => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  if (!token || isTokenExpired(token)) {\n    if (!isRefreshing) {\n      isRefreshing = true;\n      refreshPromise = refreshToken().finally(() => {\n        isRefreshing = false;\n        refreshPromise = null;\n      });\n    }\n    return refreshPromise!;\n  }\n\n  return token;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Offline Support\n\n**Check network status**:\n\n```tsx\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Hook for network status\nfunction useNetworkStatus() {\n  const [isOnline, setIsOnline] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n      setIsOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  return isOnline;\n}\n```\n\n**Offline-first with React Query**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { onlineManager } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Sync React Query with network status\nonlineManager.setEventListener((setOnline) => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n  });\n});\n\n// Queries will pause when offline and resume when online\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Using environment variables for API configuration**:\n\nExpo supports environment variables with the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix. These are inlined at build time and available in your JavaScript code.\n\n```tsx\n// .env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION=v1\n\n// Usage in code\nconst API_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nconst fetchUsers = async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_URL}/users`);\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**Environment-specific configuration**:\n\n```tsx\n// .env.development\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000\n\n// .env.production\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.production.com\n```\n\n**Creating an API client with environment config**:\n\n```tsx\n// api/client.ts\nconst BASE_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nif (!BASE_URL) {\n  throw new Error(\"EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is not defined\");\n}\n\nexport const apiClient = {\n  get: async <T,>(path: string): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`);\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n\n  post: async <T,>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Important notes**:\n\n- Only variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the client bundle\n- Never put secrets (API keys with write access, database passwords) in `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables—they''re visible in the built app\n- Environment variables are inlined at **build time**, not runtime\n- Restart the dev server after changing `.env` files\n- For server-side secrets in API routes, use variables without the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix\n\n**TypeScript support**:\n\n```tsx\n// types/env.d.ts\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL: string;\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION?: string;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Request Cancellation\n\n**Cancel on unmount**:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n\n  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })\n    .then((response) => response.json())\n    .then(setData)\n    .catch((error) => {\n      if (error.name !== \"AbortError\") {\n        setError(error);\n      }\n    });\n\n  return () => controller.abort();\n}, [url]);\n```\n\n**With React Query** (automatic):\n\n```tsx\n// React Query automatically cancels requests when queries are invalidated\n// or components unmount\n```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```\nUser asks about networking\n  |-- Basic fetch?\n  |   \\-- Use fetch API with error handling\n  |\n  |-- Need caching/state management?\n  |   |-- Complex app -> React Query (TanStack Query)\n  |   \\-- Simpler needs -> SWR or custom hooks\n  |\n  |-- Authentication?\n  |   |-- Token storage -> expo-secure-store\n  |   \\-- Token refresh -> Implement refresh flow\n  |\n  |-- Error handling?\n  |   |-- Network errors -> Check connectivity first\n  |   |-- HTTP errors -> Parse response, throw typed errors\n  |   \\-- Retries -> Exponential backoff\n  |\n  |-- Offline support?\n  |   |-- Check status -> NetInfo\n  |   \\-- Queue requests -> React Query persistence\n  |\n  |-- Environment/API config?\n  |   |-- Client-side URLs -> EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix in .env\n  |   |-- Server secrets -> Non-prefixed env vars (API routes only)\n  |   \\-- Multiple environments -> .env.development, .env.production\n  |\n  \\-- Performance?\n      |-- Caching -> React Query with staleTime\n      |-- Deduplication -> React Query handles this\n      \\-- Cancellation -> AbortController or React Query\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Wrong: No error handling**\n\n```tsx\nconst data = await fetch(url).then((r) => r.json());\n```\n\n**Right: Check response status**\n\n```tsx\nconst response = await fetch(url);\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n```\n\n**Wrong: Storing tokens in AsyncStorage**\n\n```tsx\nawait AsyncStorage.setItem(\"token\", token); // Not secure!\n```\n\n**Right: Use SecureStore for sensitive data**\n\n```tsx\nawait SecureStore.setItemAsync(\"token\", token);\n```\n\n## Example Invocations\n\nUser: \"How do I make API calls in React Native?\"\n-> Use fetch, wrap with error handling\n\nUser: \"Should I use React Query or SWR?\"\n-> React Query for complex apps, SWR for simpler needs\n\nUser: \"My app needs to work offline\"\n-> Use NetInfo for status, React Query persistence for caching\n\nUser: \"How do I handle authentication tokens?\"\n-> Store in expo-secure-store, implement refresh flow\n\nUser: \"API calls are slow\"\n-> Check caching strategy, use React Query staleTime\n\nUser: \"How do I configure different API URLs for dev and prod?\"\n-> Use EXPO*PUBLIC* env vars with .env.development and .env.production files\n\nUser: \"Where should I put my API key?\"\n-> Client-safe keys: EXPO*PUBLIC* in .env. Secret keys: non-prefixed env vars in API routes only\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:35:22.035Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor and AutoGPT that require secure and reliable data fetching for their operations.","zh":"适合像Cursor和AutoGPT这样的AI代理，它们需要安全可靠的数据获取以进行操作。","ja":"CursorやAutoGPTのような、操作のために安全で信頼できるデータ取得を必要とするAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"Cursor와 AutoGPT 같은 에이전트가 작동을 위해 안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 데이터를 가져와야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor y AutoGPT que requieren una obtención de datos segura y confiable para sus operaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor et AutoGPT qui nécessitent une récupération de données sécurisée et fiable pour leurs opérations.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor und AutoGPT, die eine sichere und zuverlässige Datenabfrage für ihre Operationen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor e AutoGPT que exigem busca de dados segura e confiável para suas operações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor и AutoGPT, которые требуют безопасного и надежного получения данных для своих операций.","ar":"مثالية لعمليات الوكلاء الذكية مثل Cursor و AutoGPT التي تتطلب استرجاع بيانات آمن وموثوق لعملياتها."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle API requests, data caching, and network debugging using Expo''s fetch API, providing a robust on-chain safety rail for their networking tasks, including React Query and SWR integration, offline scenario handling, and authentication management.","zh":"赋予代理处理API请求、数据缓存和网络调试的能力，使用Expo的fetch API提供强大的链上安全功能，包括React Query和SWR集成、离线场景处理和身份验证管理。","ja":"Expoのfetch APIを使用して、APIリクエスト、データキャッシュ、ネットワークデバッグを扱う能力をエージェントに与え、React QueryおよびSWRの統合、オフラインシナリオの処理、認証管理を含むネットワークタスクのための堅牢なチェーン上の安全レールを提供する。","ko":"Expo의 fetch API를 사용하여 API 요청, 데이터 캐싱 및 네트워크 디버깅을 처리할 수 있는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여하여 React Query 및 SWR 통합, 오프라인 시나리오 처리 및 인증 관리를 포함한 네트워크 작업을 위한 강력한 체인 상 안전 레일을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes manejar solicitudes de API, caché de datos y depuración de red utilizando la API de fetch de Expo, proporcionando un sólido sistema de seguridad en cadena para sus tareas de red, incluyendo integración con React Query y SWR, manejo de escenarios sin conexión y administración de autenticación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les requêtes API, le cache de données et le débogage du réseau en utilisant l''API de fetch d''Expo, fournissant un solide système de sécurité en chaîne pour leurs tâches de réseau, y compris l''intégration avec React Query et SWR, la gestion des scénarios hors ligne et la gestion de l''authentification.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, API-Anfragen, Daten-Caching und Netzwerk-Debugging mithilfe von Expo''s fetch-API zu handhaben, wodurch ein robustes Sicherheitssystem für ihre Netzwerkaufgaben bereitgestellt wird, einschließlich Integration mit React Query und SWR, Offline-Szenario-Handhabung und Authentifizierungsmanagement.","pt":"Habilita agentes a lidar com solicitações de API, cache de dados e depuração de rede usando a API de fetch do Expo, fornecendo uma proteção de segurança robusta em cadeia para suas tarefas de rede, incluindo integração com React Query e SWR, tratamento de cenários offline e gerenciamento de autenticação.","ru":"Позволяет агентам обрабатывать запросы API, кэширование данных и сетевую отладку, используя API fetch от Expo, обеспечивая надежную защиту на цепочке для сетевых задач, включая интеграцию с React Query и SWR, обработку автономных сценариев и управление аутентификацией.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التعامل مع طلبات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات، وذاكرة التخزين المؤقت للبيانات، وتصحيح الأخطاء الشبكية باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لاسترجاع Expo، وتوفير حماية أمان قوية على السلسلة لمهام الشبكة، بما في ذلك التكامل مع React Query و SWR، ومعالجة السيناريوهات دون اتصال وإدارة المصادقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing secure API requests with Expo/fetch","Debugging network failures and optimizing data fetching strategies","Handling offline scenarios and implementing caching strategies with React Query or SWR"],"zh":["使用Expo/fetch实现安全的API请求","调试网络故障并优化数据获取策略","使用React Query或SWR处理离线场景并实现缓存策略"],"ja":["Expo/fetchを使用してセキュアなAPIリクエストを実装する","ネットワーク障害のデバッグとデータ取得戦略の最適化","React QueryまたはSWRを使用してオフラインシナリオを処理し、キャッシュ戦略を実装する"],"ko":["Expo/fetch를 사용하여 보안 API 요청을 구현하는 것","네트워크 오류를 디버깅하고 데이터 가져오기 전략을 최적화하는 것","React Query 또는 SWR를 사용하여 오프라인 시나리오를 처리하고 캐싱 전략을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Implementar solicitudes de API seguras con Expo/fetch","Depurar fallos de red y optimizar estrategias de obtención de datos","Manejar escenarios sin conexión e implementar estrategias de caché con React Query o SWR"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des requêtes API sécurisées avec Expo/fetch","Déboguer les défaillances du réseau et optimiser les stratégies de récupération de données","Gérer les scénarios hors ligne et mettre en œuvre des stratégies de cache avec React Query ou SWR"],"de":["Implementieren von sicheren API-Anfragen mit Expo/fetch","Debuggen von Netzwerkfehlern und Optimieren von Datenabfragestrategien","Handhaben von Offline-Szenarien und Implementieren von Caching-Strategien mit React Query oder SWR"],"pt":["Implementação de solicitações de API seguras com Expo/fetch","Depuração de falhas de rede e otimização de estratégias de busca de dados","Tratamento de cenários offline e implementação de estratégias de cache com React Query ou SWR"],"ru":["Реализация безопасных запросов API с помощью Expo/fetch","Отладка сетевых сбоев и оптимизация стратегий получения данных","Обработка автономных сценариев и реализация стратегий кэширования с помощью React Query или SWR"],"ar":["تنفيذ طلبات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الآمنة مع Expo/ استرجاع","تصحيح الأخطاء الشبكية وتحسين استراتيجيات استرجاع البيانات","معالجة السيناريوهات دون اتصال وتنفيذ استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت مع استفسار React أو SWR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo environment","Prefer Expo/fetch over axios for API requests"],"zh":["需要Expo环境","更推荐使用Expo/fetch而不是axios进行API请求"],"ja":["Expo環境が必要","APIリクエストにはaxiosよりもExpo/fetchを優先する"],"ko":["Expo 환경이 필요함","API 요청에는 axios보다 Expo/fetch를 선호함"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Expo","Preferir Expo/fetch sobre axios para solicitudes de API"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Expo","Préférer Expo/fetch à axios pour les requêtes API"],"de":["Benötigt Expo-Umgebung","Expo/fetch bevorzugen gegenüber axios für API-Anfragen"],"pt":["Exige ambiente Expo","Prefira Expo/fetch em vez de axios para solicitações de API"],"ru":["Требует среды Expo","Предпочитайте Expo/fetch вместо axios для запросов API"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Expo","افضل Expo/استرجاع بدلاً من axios لطلبات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('GrupoUS/gpus/mobile-design', 'community', 'GrupoUS', 'gpus', 'GrupoUS/gpus', 'mobile-design', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.458Z', '2026-02-18T07:35:19.019Z', NULL, '{"id":"GrupoUS/gpus/mobile-design","name":"mobile-design","description":{"zh":"移动设计系统遵循Touch-first、Battery-conscious、Platform-respectful和Offline-capable的设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、タッチファースト、バッテリー意識、プラットフォーム尊重、オフライン対応の設計哲学に基づいています","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 터치 우선, 배터리 의식, 플랫폼尊重, 오프라인対応의 설계 철학을 따릅니다","es":"El diseño móvil se centra en crear experiencias únicas para dispositivos móviles, considerando restricciones y plataformas.","fr":"La conception mobile se concentre sur la création d''expériences uniques pour les appareils mobiles, en tenant compte des contraintes et des plateformes.","de":"Das Mobile Design konzentriert sich auf die Erstellung einzigartiger Erfahrungen für mobile Geräte, unter Berücksichtigung von Einschränkungen und Plattformen.","pt":"O sistema de design móvel é baseado em uma filosofia de toque, economia de bateria e respeito à plataforma. Ele ajuda a criar experiências móveis eficazes.","ru":"Мобильная система дизайна основана на философии осязания, экономии батареи и уважении к платформе. Она помогает создать эффективные мобильные trải nghiệm.","ar":"نظام تصميم الجوال يقوم على فلسفة اللمس وتوفير البطارية والاحترام للمنصة. يساعد على إنشاء تجارب جوال فعالة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"移动设计系统 -Touch-first 设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステム - タッチファースト設計哲学","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템 - 터치 우선 설계 철학","es":"Diseño Móvil: Crea Experiencias Únicas","fr":"Conception Mobile: Créez des Expériences Uniques","de":"Mobile Design: Erstellen Sie Einzigartige Erfahrungen","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Design Móvel","ru":"Мобильный дизайн","ar":"تصميم الجوال","en":"mobile-design"},"description":{"zh":"移动设计系统遵循Touch-first、Battery-conscious、Platform-respectful和Offline-capable的设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、タッチファースト、バッテリー意識、プラットフォーム尊重、オフライン対応の設計哲学に基づいています","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 터치 우선, 배터리 의식, 플랫폼尊重, 오프라인対応의 설계 철학을 따릅니다","es":"El diseño móvil se centra en crear experiencias únicas para dispositivos móviles, considerando restricciones y plataformas.","fr":"La conception mobile se concentre sur la création d''expériences uniques pour les appareils mobiles, en tenant compte des contraintes et des plateformes.","de":"Das Mobile Design konzentriert sich auf die Erstellung einzigartiger Erfahrungen für mobile Geräte, unter Berücksichtigung von Einschränkungen und Plattformen.","pt":"O sistema de design móvel é baseado em uma filosofia de toque, economia de bateria e respeito à plataforma. Ele ajuda a criar experiências móveis eficazes.","ru":"Мобильная система дизайна основана на философии осязания, экономии батареи и уважении к платформе. Она помогает создать эффективные мобильные trải nghiệm.","ar":"نظام تصميم الجوال يقوم على فلسفة اللمس وتوفير البطارية والاحترام للمنصة. يساعد على إنشاء تجارب جوال فعالة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Touch-first 设计哲学","Battery-conscious 设计原则","Platform-respectful 设计方法","Offline-capable 设计支持","移动UX和Touch审计脚本"],"ja":["タッチファースト設計哲学","バッテリー意識設計原則","プラットフォーム尊重設計方法","オフライン対応設計サポート","モバイルUXとタッチ審計スクリプト"],"ko":["터치 우선 설계 철학","배터리 의식 설계 원칙","플랫폼尊重 설계 방법","오프라인対応 설계 지원","모바일 UX와 터치審計 스크립트"],"es":["Enfoque touch-first","Conciencia de la batería","Respeto a la plataforma","Capacidad sin conexión","Validación con scripts de ejecución"],"fr":["Approche touch-first","Conscience de la batterie","Respect de la plateforme","Capacité hors ligne","Validation avec des scripts d''exécution"],"de":["Touch-first-Ansatz","Batteriebewusstsein","Plattformrespekt","Offline-Fähigkeit","Validierung mit Laufzeitskripten"],"pt":["Filosofia de toque","Economia de bateria","Respeito à plataforma","Capacidade offline","Otimização para dispositivos móveis"],"ru":["Философия осязания","Экономия батареи","Уважение к платформе","Возможность офлайн","Оптимизация для мобильных устройств"],"ar":["فلسفة اللمس","توفير البطارية","الاحترام للمنصة","القدرة على العمل دون اتصال","تحسين الأداء للجهاز الجوال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["移动设计系统","Touch-first 设计","Battery-conscious 设计","Platform-respectful 设计","Offline-capable 设计","移动UX","Touch审计"],"ja":["モバイルデザインシステム","タッチファースト設計","バッテリー意識設計","プラットフォーム尊重設計","オフライン対応設計","モバイルUX","タッチ審計"],"ko":["모바일 디자인 시스템","터치 우선 설계","배터리 의식 설계","플랫폼尊重 설계","오프라인対応 설계","모바일 UX","터치審計"],"es":["diseño móvil","experiencia del usuario","aplicaciones móviles","desarrollo móvil","optimización de aplicaciones","mejora de la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["conception mobile","expérience utilisateur","applications mobiles","développement mobile","optimisation des applications","amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Mobile Design","Benutzererfahrung","Mobile Anwendungen","Mobile Entwicklung","Optimierung von Anwendungen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["design móvel","experiência de usuário","dispositivos móveis","otimização para móveis","ux móvel","ui móvel","desenvolvimento móvel"],"ru":["мобильный дизайн","пользовательский trải nghiệm","мобильные устройства","оптимизация для мобильных","мобильная ux","мобильная ui","мобильное разработка"],"ar":["تصميم الجوال","تجربة المستخدم","أجهزة الجوال","تحسين الأداء للجوال","واجهة المستخدم الجوال","تطوير الجوال","تجربة المستخدم الجوال"]}},"owner":"GrupoUS","repo":"gpus","repoPath":"GrupoUS/gpus","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.458Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mobile-design","description":"Mobile-first design thinking and decision-making for iOS and Android apps. Touch interaction, performance patterns, platform conventions. Teaches principles, not fixed values. Use when building React Native, Flutter, or native mobile apps.","bodyPreview":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference","body":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference Files Before Working!\n\n**⛔ DO NOT start development until you read the relevant files:**\n\n### Universal (Always Read)\n\n| File | Content | Status |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| **[mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md)** | **⚠️ ANTI-MEMORIZATION: Forces thinking, prevents AI defaults** | **⬜ CRITICAL FIRST** |\n| **[touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)** | **Fitts'' Law, gestures, haptics, thumb zone** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)** | **RN/Flutter performance, 60fps, memory** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-backend.md](mobile-backend.md)** | **Push notifications, offline sync, mobile API** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-testing.md](mobile-testing.md)** | **Testing pyramid, E2E, platform-specific** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-debugging.md](mobile-debugging.md)** | **Native vs JS debugging, Flipper, Logcat** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Tab/Stack/Drawer, deep linking | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | System fonts, Dynamic Type, a11y | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED, dark mode, battery-aware | ⬜ Read |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework/state/storage selection | ⬜ Read |\n\n> 🧠 **mobile-design-thinking.md is PRIORITY!** This file ensures AI thinks instead of using memorized patterns.\n\n### Platform-Specific (Read Based on Target)\n\n| Platform | File | Content | When to Read |\n|----------|------|---------|--------------|\n| **iOS** | [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | Human Interface Guidelines, SF Pro, SwiftUI patterns | Building for iPhone/iPad |\n| **Android** | [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Material Design 3, Roboto, Compose patterns | Building for Android |\n| **Cross-Platform** | Both above | Platform divergence points | React Native / Flutter |\n\n> 🔴 **If building for iOS → Read platform-ios.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If building for Android → Read platform-android.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If cross-platform → Read BOTH and apply conditional platform logic!**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### You MUST Ask If Not Specified:\n\n| Aspect | Ask | Why |\n|--------|-----|-----|\n| **Platform** | \"iOS, Android, or both?\" | Affects EVERY design decision |\n| **Framework** | \"React Native, Flutter, or native?\" | Determines patterns and tools |\n| **Navigation** | \"Tab bar, drawer, or stack-based?\" | Core UX decision |\n| **State** | \"What state management? (Zustand/Redux/Riverpod/BLoC?)\" | Architecture foundation |\n| **Offline** | \"Does this need to work offline?\" | Affects data strategy |\n| **Target devices** | \"Phone only, or tablet support?\" | Layout complexity |\n\n### ⛔ AI MOBILE ANTI-PATTERNS (YASAK LİSTESİ)\n\n> 🚫 **These are AI default tendencies that MUST be avoided!**\n\n#### Performance Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **ScrollView for long lists** | Renders ALL items, memory explodes | Use `FlatList` / `FlashList` / `ListView.builder` |\n| **Inline renderItem function** | New function every render, all items re-render | `useCallback` + `React.memo` |\n| **Missing keyExtractor** | Index-based keys cause bugs on reorder | Unique, stable ID from data |\n| **Skip getItemLayout** | Async layout = janky scroll | Provide when items have fixed height |\n| **setState() everywhere** | Unnecessary widget rebuilds | Targeted state, `const` constructors |\n| **Native driver: false** | Animations blocked by JS thread | `useNativeDriver: true` always |\n| **console.log in production** | Blocks JS thread severely | Remove before release build |\n| **Skip React.memo/const** | Every item re-renders on any change | Memoize list items ALWAYS |\n\n#### Touch/UX Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Touch target < 44px** | Impossible to tap accurately, frustrating | Minimum 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) |\n| **Spacing < 8px between targets** | Accidental taps on neighbors | Minimum 8-12px gap |\n| **Gesture-only interactions** | Motor impaired users excluded | Always provide button alternative |\n| **No loading state** | User thinks app crashed | ALWAYS show loading feedback |\n| **No error state** | User stuck, no recovery path | Show error with retry option |\n| **No offline handling** | Crash/block when network lost | Graceful degradation, cached data |\n| **Ignore platform conventions** | Users confused, muscle memory broken | iOS feels iOS, Android feels Android |\n\n#### Security Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Token in AsyncStorage** | Easily accessible, stolen on rooted device | `SecureStore` / `Keychain` / `EncryptedSharedPreferences` |\n| **Hardcode API keys** | Reverse engineered from APK/IPA | Environment variables, secure storage |\n| **Skip SSL pinning** | MITM attacks possible | Pin certificates in production |\n| **Log sensitive data** | Logs can be extracted | Never log tokens, passwords, PII |\n\n#### Architecture Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Business logic in UI** | Untestable, unmaintainable | Service layer separation |\n| **Global state for everything** | Unnecessary re-renders, complexity | Local state default, lift when needed |\n| **Deep linking as afterthought** | Notifications, shares broken | Plan deep links from day one |\n| **Skip dispose/cleanup** | Memory leaks, zombie listeners | Clean up subscriptions, timers |\n\n---\n\n## 📱 Platform Decision Matrix\n\n### When to Unify vs Diverge\n\n```\n                    UNIFY (same on both)          DIVERGE (platform-specific)\n                    ───────────────────           ──────────────────────────\nBusiness Logic      ✅ Always                     -\nData Layer          ✅ Always                     -\nCore Features       ✅ Always                     -\n                    \nNavigation          -                             ✅ iOS: edge swipe, Android: back button\nGestures            -                             ✅ Platform-native feel\nIcons               -                             ✅ SF Symbols vs Material Icons\nDate Pickers        -                             ✅ Native pickers feel right\nModals/Sheets       -                             ✅ iOS: bottom sheet vs Android: dialog\nTypography          -                             ✅ SF Pro vs Roboto (or custom)\nError Dialogs       -                             ✅ Platform conventions for alerts\n```\n\n### Quick Reference: Platform Defaults\n\n| Element | iOS | Android |\n|---------|-----|---------|\n| **Primary Font** | SF Pro / SF Compact | Roboto |\n| **Min Touch Target** | 44pt × 44pt | 48dp × 48dp |\n| **Back Navigation** | Edge swipe left | System back button/gesture |\n| **Bottom Tab Icons** | SF Symbols | Material Symbols |\n| **Action Sheet** | UIActionSheet from bottom | Bottom Sheet / Dialog |\n| **Progress** | Spinner | Linear progress (Material) |\n| **Pull to Refresh** | Native UIRefreshControl | SwipeRefreshLayout |\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Mobile UX Psychology (Quick Reference)\n\n### Fitts'' Law for Touch\n\n```\nDesktop: Cursor is precise (1px)\nMobile:  Finger is imprecise (~7mm contact area)\n\n→ Touch targets MUST be 44-48px minimum\n→ Important actions in THUMB ZONE (bottom of screen)\n→ Destructive actions AWAY from easy reach\n```\n\n### Thumb Zone (One-Handed Usage)\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────┐\n│      HARD TO REACH          │ ← Navigation, menu, back\n│        (stretch)            │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      OK TO REACH            │ ← Secondary actions\n│       (natural)             │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      EASY TO REACH          │ ← PRIMARY CTAs, tab bar\n│    (thumb''s natural arc)    │ ← Main content interaction\n└─────────────────────────────┘\n        [  HOME  ]\n```\n\n### Mobile-Specific Cognitive Load\n\n| Desktop | Mobile Difference |\n|---------|-------------------|\n| Multiple windows | ONE task at a time |\n| Keyboard shortcuts | Touch gestures |\n| Hover states | NO hover (tap or nothing) |\n| Large viewport | Limited space, scroll vertical |\n| Stable attention | Interrupted constantly |\n\nFor deep dive: [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Performance Principles (Quick Reference)\n\n### React Native Critical Rules\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT: Memoized renderItem + React.memo wrapper\nconst ListItem = React.memo(({ item }: { item: Item }) => (\n  <View style={styles.item}>\n    <Text>{item.title}</Text>\n  </View>\n));\n\nconst renderItem = useCallback(\n  ({ item }: { item: Item }) => <ListItem item={item} />,\n  []\n);\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: FlatList with all optimizations\n<FlatList\n  data={items}\n  renderItem={renderItem}\n  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}  // Stable ID, NOT index\n  getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({\n    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,\n    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,\n    index,\n  })}\n  removeClippedSubviews={true}\n  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}\n  windowSize={5}\n/>\n```\n\n### Flutter Critical Rules\n\n```dart\n// ✅ CORRECT: const constructors prevent rebuilds\nclass MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  const MyWidget({super.key}); // CONST!\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return const Column( // CONST!\n      children: [\n        Text(''Static content''),\n        MyConstantWidget(),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: Targeted state with ValueListenableBuilder\nValueListenableBuilder<int>(\n  valueListenable: counter,\n  builder: (context, value, child) => Text(''$value''),\n  child: const ExpensiveWidget(), // Won''t rebuild!\n)\n```\n\n### Animation Performance\n\n```\nGPU-accelerated (FAST):     CPU-bound (SLOW):\n├── transform               ├── width, height\n├── opacity                 ├── top, left, right, bottom\n└── (use these ONLY)        ├── margin, padding\n                            └── (AVOID animating these)\n```\n\nFor complete guide: [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📝 CHECKPOINT (MANDATORY Before Any Mobile Work)\n\n> **Before writing ANY mobile code, you MUST complete this checkpoint:**\n\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   [ iOS / Android / Both ]\nFramework:  [ React Native / Flutter / SwiftUI / Kotlin ]\nFiles Read: [ List the skill files you''ve read ]\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n3. _______________\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   iOS + Android (Cross-platform)\nFramework:  React Native + Expo\nFiles Read: touch-psychology.md, mobile-performance.md, platform-ios.md, platform-android.md\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. FlatList with React.memo + useCallback for all lists\n2. 48px touch targets, thumb zone for primary CTAs\n3. Platform-specific navigation (edge swipe iOS, back button Android)\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. ScrollView for lists → FlatList\n2. Inline renderItem → Memoized\n3. AsyncStorage for tokens → SecureStore\n```\n\n> 🔴 **Can''t fill the checkpoint? → GO BACK AND READ THE SKILL FILES.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Framework Decision Tree\n\n```\nWHAT ARE YOU BUILDING?\n        │\n        ├── Need OTA updates + rapid iteration + web team\n        │   └── ✅ React Native + Expo\n        │\n        ├── Need pixel-perfect custom UI + performance critical\n        │   └── ✅ Flutter\n        │\n        ├── Deep native features + single platform focus\n        │   ├── iOS only → SwiftUI\n        │   └── Android only → Kotlin + Jetpack Compose\n        │\n        ├── Existing RN codebase + new features\n        │   └── ✅ React Native (bare workflow)\n        │\n        └── Enterprise + existing Flutter codebase\n            └── ✅ Flutter\n```\n\nFor complete decision trees: [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Development Checklist\n\n### Before Starting ANY Mobile Project\n\n- [ ] **Platform confirmed?** (iOS / Android / Both)\n- [ ] **Framework chosen?** (RN / Flutter / Native)\n- [ ] **Navigation pattern decided?** (Tabs / Stack / Drawer)\n- [ ] **State management selected?** (Zustand / Redux / Riverpod / BLoC)\n- [ ] **Offline requirements known?**\n- [ ] **Deep linking planned from day one?**\n- [ ] **Target devices defined?** (Phone / Tablet / Both)\n\n### Before Every Screen\n\n- [ ] **Touch targets ≥ 44-48px?**\n- [ ] **Primary CTA in thumb zone?**\n- [ ] **Loading state exists?**\n- [ ] **Error state with retry exists?**\n- [ ] **Offline handling considered?**\n- [ ] **Platform conventions followed?**\n\n### Before Release\n\n- [ ] **console.log removed?**\n- [ ] **SecureStore for sensitive data?**\n- [ ] **SSL pinning enabled?**\n- [ ] **Lists optimized (memo, keyExtractor)?**\n- [ ] **Memory cleanup on unmount?**\n- [ ] **Tested on low-end devices?**\n- [ ] **Accessibility labels on all interactive elements?**\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n| File | When to Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| [mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md) | **FIRST! Anti-memorization, forces context-based thinking** |\n| [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md) | Understanding touch interaction, Fitts'' Law, gesture design |\n| [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md) | Optimizing RN/Flutter, 60fps, memory/battery |\n| [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | iOS-specific design, HIG compliance |\n| [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Android-specific design, Material Design 3 |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Navigation patterns, deep linking |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | Type scale, system fonts, accessibility |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED optimization, dark mode, battery |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework, state, storage decisions |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Mobile users are impatient, interrupted, and using imprecise fingers on small screens. Design for the WORST conditions: bad network, one hand, bright sun, low battery. If it works there, it works everywhere.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:35:19.019Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for UI/UX Agents focused on touch-first, battery-conscious, and platform-respectful design principles.","zh":"适用于专注于触摸优先、电池节能和平台尊重设计原则的UI/UX代理。","ja":"タッチファースト、バッテリー意識、プラットフォーム尊重設計原則に焦点を当てたUI/UXエージェントに最適です。","ko":"터치 우선, 배터리 효율, 플랫폼 존중 설계 원칙에 중점을 둔 UI/UX 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de UI/UX centrados en principios de diseño de primera interacción táctil, conciencia de la batería y respeto a la plataforma.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents UI/UX axés sur les principes de conception tactiles en premier, consommateurs de batterie et respectueux de la plate-forme.","de":"Ideal für UI/UX-Agenten, die auf touch-first-, batteriebewusste und plattformrespektierende Designprinzipien ausgerichtet sind.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de UI/UX focados em princípios de design touch-first, conscientes da bateria e respeitosos com a plataforma.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов UI/UX, ориентированных на проектирование с учетом сенсорных интерфейсов, экономии батареи и уважения к платформе.","ar":"مثالية لعميل واجهة المستخدم / الخبرة العميل مع التركيز على تصميم اللمس أولا ، ووعي البطارية ، والاحترام للمنصة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create mobile designs that respect platform choice and mobile constraints, utilizing runtime scripts like mobile_audit.py for validation and adhering to a touch-first philosophy, ensuring offline capability and battery efficiency.","zh":"赋予代理创建移动设计的能力，这些设计尊重平台选择和移动约束，利用运行时脚本（如mobile_audit.py）进行验证，并遵循触摸优先的理念，确保离线能力和电池效率。","ja":"エージェントが、プラットフォームの選択とモバイルの制約を尊重したモバイル設計を作成できるようにし、mobile_audit.pyなどのランタイムスクリプトを使用して検証を行い、タッチファーストの哲学に従ってオフライン機能とバッテリー効率を確保する。","ko":"에이전트가 플랫폼 선택과 모바일 제약을尊重하는 모바일 디자인을 생성할 수 있도록 하며, mobile_audit.py와 같은 런타임 스크립트를 사용하여 검증을 수행하고, 터치 우선 철학을 따르며, 오프라인 기능과 배터리 효율을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear diseños móviles que respeten la elección de plataforma y las limitaciones móviles, utilizando scripts de tiempo de ejecución como mobile_audit.py para la validación y siguiendo una filosofía de primera interacción táctil, garantizando la capacidad fuera de línea y la eficiencia de la batería.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des conceptions mobiles qui respectent le choix de plate-forme et les contraintes mobiles, en utilisant des scripts d''exécution tels que mobile_audit.py pour la validation et en suivant une philosophie tactile en premier, garantissant la capacité hors ligne et l''efficacité de la batterie.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, mobile Designs zu erstellen, die die Plattformwahl und mobile Einschränkungen respektieren, indem Runtime-Skripte wie mobile_audit.py für die Validierung verwendet und einer touch-first-Philosophie gefolgt wird, um die Offline-Fähigkeit und die Batterieeffizienz zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem designs móveis que respeitem a escolha da plataforma e as restrições móveis, utilizando scripts de tempo de execução como mobile_audit.py para validação e aderindo a uma filosofia touch-first, garantindo capacidade offline e eficiência de bateria.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать мобильные дизайны, уважающие выбор платформы и мобильные ограничения, используя скрипты runtime, такие как mobile_audit.py, для проверки и соблюдения философии сенсорного интерфейса, обеспечивая возможность работы offline и экономию батареи.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من إنشاء تصاميم موبايل تحترم اختيار المنصة والقيود الموبايل ، باستخدام سكريبتات زمن التشغيل مثل mobile_audit.py للتحقق والامتثال لفلسفة اللمس أولا ، مما يضمن القدرة على العمل بدون اتصال والكفاءة في البطارية."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing mobile UX and touch interactions with scripts like mobile_audit.py","Designing platform-respectful interfaces that adapt to mobile constraints","Validating mobile design systems for offline capability and battery consciousness"],"zh":["使用脚本（如mobile_audit.py）审计移动UX和触摸交互","设计适应移动约束的平台尊重界面","验证移动设计系统的离线能力和电池意识"],"ja":["mobile_audit.pyなどのスクリプトを使用してモバイルUXとタッチのやり取りを監査する","モバイルの制約に適応するプラットフォーム尊重インターフェイスを設計する","モバイル設計システムのオフライン機能とバッテリー意識を検証する"],"ko":["mobile_audit.py와 같은 스크립트를 사용하여 모바일 UX와 터치 상호 작용을 감사합니다.","모바일 제약에 적응하는 플랫폼 존중 인터페이스를 설계합니다.","모바일 디자인 시스템의 오프라인 기능과 배터리 효율을 검증합니다."],"es":["Auditoría de la experiencia del usuario móvil y las interacciones táctiles con scripts como mobile_audit.py","Diseño de interfaces respetuosas con la plataforma que se adapten a las limitaciones móviles","Validación de sistemas de diseño móviles para capacidad fuera de línea y conciencia de la batería"],"fr":["Audit de l''expérience utilisateur mobile et des interactions tactiles avec des scripts tels que mobile_audit.py","Conception d''interfaces respectueuses de la plate-forme qui s''adaptent aux contraintes mobiles","Validation des systèmes de conception mobile pour la capacité hors ligne et la conscience de la batterie"],"de":["Prüfung der mobilen Benutzeroberfläche und der Touch-Interaktionen mit Skripten wie mobile_audit.py","Entwurf plattformrespektierender Schnittstellen, die sich an mobile Einschränkungen anpassen","Validierung mobiler Designsysteme für Offline-Fähigkeit und Batteriebewusstsein"],"pt":["Auditoria de UX móvel e interações de toque com scripts como mobile_audit.py","Projeto de interfaces respeitosas com a plataforma que se adaptam às restrições móveis","Validação de sistemas de design móvel para capacidade offline e consciência de bateria"],"ru":["Аудит мобильного UX и сенсорных взаимодействий со сценариями, такими как mobile_audit.py","Проектирование интерфейсов, уважающих платформу, которые адаптируются к мобильным ограничениям","Проверка систем мобильного дизайна для работы offline и экономии батареи"],"ar":["تدقيق تجربة المستخدم الموبايل و تفاعلات اللمس مع سكريبتات مثل mobile_audit.py","تصميم واجهات تحترم المنصة والمتكيفة مع القيود الموبايل","التحقق من أنظمة التصميم الموبايل للعمل بدون اتصال ووعي البطارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment for script execution","Focused on mobile design principles, not desktop or web design"],"zh":["需要Python环境来执行脚本","专注于移动设计原则，而不是桌面或网络设计"],"ja":["スクリプトの実行にはPython環境が必要","モバイル設計原則に焦点を当てており、デスクトップまたはウェブ設計ではありません"],"ko":["스크립트 실행을 위해 파이썬 환경이 필요합니다.","모바일 디자인 원칙에 중점을 둔 데스크톱 또는 웹 디자인은 아닙니다."],"es":["Requiere un entorno de Python para la ejecución de scripts","Centrado en principios de diseño móvil, no en diseño de escritorio o web"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python pour l''exécution de scripts","Axé sur les principes de conception mobile, et non sur la conception de bureau ou web"],"de":["Benötigt eine Python-Umgebung für die Skriptausführung","Konzentriert sich auf mobile Designprinzipien, nicht auf Desktop- oder Webdesign"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python para execução de scripts","Focado em princípios de design móvel, não em design de desktop ou web"],"ru":["Требует среды Python для выполнения скриптов","Ориентирован на принципы мобильного дизайна, а не на дизайн настольных или веб-приложений"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون لتشغيل السكريبتات","موجه نحو مبادئ تصميم الموبايل ، وليس تصميم سطح المكتب أو الويب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
