zh":"该技能系统地修复代码审计中识别出的坏习惯，提高代码质量和可靠性。它遵循快速失败原则，确保代码错误及时可见","ja":"このスキルは、コード監査で特定された悪い習慣をシステム的に修正し、コードの品質と信頼性を向上させる。迅速に失敗する原則に従って、コードのエラーをすぐに可視化する","ko":"이 스킬은 코드 감사에서 식별된 나쁨 관행을 시스템적으로 수정하여 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 높인다. 빠른 실패 원칙을 따르며 코드 오류를 즉시 표시","es":"Nuestra habilidad de corrección de malas prácticas de codificación identifica y soluciona problemas de calidad de código de manera sistemática","fr":"Notre compétence de correction des mauvaises pratiques de codage identifie et résout les problèmes de qualité de code de manière systématique","de":"Unsere Fähigkeit, schlechte Codierungspraktiken zu beheben, identifiziert und löst Code-Qualitätsprobleme systematisch","pt":"A habilidade de correção de práticas ruins de codificação identifica e corrige problemas de codificação de acordo com os princípios de fail-fast.","ru":"Навык исправления плохих практик кодирования выявляет и исправляет проблемы кодирования в соответствии с принципами fail-fast.","ar":"مهارة إصلاح الممارسات السيئة للتعليمات البرمجية تعرف وتصلح مشاكل التعليمات البرمجية وفقًا لمبادئ Fail-Fast.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["系统地修复代码审计中识别出的坏习惯","提高代码质量和可靠性","遵循快速失败原则","确保代码错误及时可见","支持代码重构和优化","提高开发效率和代码可维护性"],"ja":["コード監査で特定された悪い習慣をシステム的に修正","コードの品質と信頼性を向上させる","迅速に失敗する原則に従う","コードのエラーをすぐに可視化する","コードのリファクタリングと最適化をサポート","開発効率とコードのメンテナンス性を向上させる"],"ko":["코드 감사에서 식별된 나쁨 관행을 시스템적으로 수정","코드 품질과 신뢰성을 높인다","빠른 실패 원칙을 따름","코드 오류를 즉시 표시","코드 리팩토링과 최적화를 지원","개발 효율과 코드 유지 보수성을 높임"],"es":["Identifica problemas de calidad de código","Soluciona malas prácticas de codificación de manera sistemática","Sigue los principios de fail-fast","Se puede utilizar de forma autónoma en flujos de trabajo de calidad","Mejora la visibilidad de los errores","Proporciona soluciones específicas para patrones de codificación problemáticos"],"fr":["Identifie les problèmes de qualité de code","Résout les mauvaises pratiques de codage de manière systématique","Suit les principes de fail-fast","Peut être utilisé de manière autonome dans les flux de travail de qualité","Améliore la visibilité des erreurs","Fournit des solutions spécifiques pour les modèles de codage problématiques"],"de":["Identifiziert Code-Qualitätsprobleme","Behebt schlechte Codierungspraktiken systematisch","Folgt den Prinzipien von fail-fast","Kann autonom in Qualitätsworkflows verwendet werden","Verbessert die Sichtbarkeit von Fehlern","Bietet spezifische Lösungen für problematische Codemuster"],"pt":["Correção sistemática de práticas ruins de codificação","Seguimento dos princípios de fail-fast","Identificação de problemas de codificação por auditoria","Correção de padrões ruins específicos","Refatoração para melhorar a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Систематическое исправление плохих практик кодирования","Следование принципам fail-fast","Выявление проблем кодирования с помощью аудита","Исправление конкретных плохих шаблонов","Рефакторинг для улучшения качества кода"],"ar":["إصلاح 系ماتي للممارسات السيئة للتعليمات البرمجية","اتباع مبادئ Fail-Fast","تحديد مشاكل التعليمات البرمجية بواسطة التدقيق","إصلاح أنماط سيئة محددة","إعادة هيكلة لتحسين جودة التعليمات البرمجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码优化","代码审计","坏习惯修复","快速失败原则","代码质量","代码可靠性","代码重构","代码优化技术"],"ja":["コード最適化","コード監査","悪い習慣の修正","迅速に失敗する原則","コードの品質","コードの信頼性","コードのリファクタリング","コード最適化技術"],"ko":["코드 최적화","코드 감사","나쁨 관행 수정","빠른 실패 원칙","코드 품질","코드 신뢰성","코드 리팩토링","코드 최적화 기술"],"es":["corrección de malas prácticas de codificación","mejora de la calidad de código","principios de fail-fast","codificación segura","desarrollo de software","calidad de código","análisis de código","refactorización de código"],"fr":["correction des mauvaises pratiques de codage","amélioration de la qualité de code","principes de fail-fast","codage sécurisé","développement de logiciels","qualité de code","analyse de code","refactorisation de code"],"de":["Behebung schlechter Codierungspraktiken","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität","Prinzipien von fail-fast","sichere Codierung","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Qualität","Code-Analyse","Code-Refactorierung"],"pt":["correção de práticas ruins de codificação","fail-fast","auditoria de código","refatoração de código","qualidade de código","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["исправление плохих практик кодирования","fail-fast","аудит кода","рефакторинг кода","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["إصلاح الممارسات السيئة للتعليمات البرمجية","Fail-Fast","تدقيق التعليمات البرمجية","إعادة هيكلة التعليمات البرمجية","جودة التعليمات البرمجية","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"benzwick","repo":"SlicerMouseMaster","repoPath":"benzwick/SlicerMouseMaster","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.458Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix-bad-practices","description":"Fix bad coding practices identified by audit, following fail-fast principles","bodyPreview":"# Fix Bad Practices Skill\n\nSystematically fix bad coding practices identified by audit, following fail-fast principles.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill:\n- After running `/audit-code-quality`\n- When fixing specific bad patterns\n- During refactoring for code quality\n- Autonomously as part of quality workflow\n\n## Philosophy: Fail Fast Fixes\n\nWhen fixing bad practices:\n\n1. **Make errors visible** - Replace silent failures with loud ones\n2. **Be specific** - Catch only exceptions you can handle\n3. **","body":"# Fix Bad Practices Skill\n\nSystematically fix bad coding practices identified by audit, following fail-fast principles.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill:\n- After running `/audit-code-quality`\n- When fixing specific bad patterns\n- During refactoring for code quality\n- Autonomously as part of quality workflow\n\n## Philosophy: Fail Fast Fixes\n\nWhen fixing bad practices:\n\n1. **Make errors visible** - Replace silent failures with loud ones\n2. **Be specific** - Catch only exceptions you can handle\n3. **Always log** - Enable debugging by humans and LLMs\n4. **Preserve stack traces** - Use `raise from` or `raise`\n5. **Test after fixing** - Ensure fixes don''t break functionality\n\n---\n\n## Fix Patterns\n\n### Fix 1: Bare `except: pass` → Specific Exception + Logging\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\ntry:\n    do_something()\nexcept:\n    pass\n```\n\n**After (GOOD)**:\n```python\ntry:\n    do_something()\nexcept SpecificError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"Failed to do_something: %s\", e)\n    raise\n```\n\n**Or if recovery is possible**:\n```python\ntry:\n    result = do_something()\nexcept SpecificError as e:\n    logger.warning(\"do_something failed, using fallback: %s\", e)\n    result = fallback_value  # Only if fallback is valid!\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 2: `except Exception` → Specific Exceptions\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\ntry:\n    data = parse_json(text)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    logger.error(e)\n    return None\n```\n\n**After (GOOD)**:\n```python\ntry:\n    data = parse_json(text)\nexcept json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"Invalid JSON: %s\", e)\n    raise ValueError(f\"Cannot parse JSON: {e}\") from e\nexcept FileNotFoundError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"File not found: %s\", e)\n    raise\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 3: Silent `continue` → Explicit Error Handling\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\nfor item in items:\n    if not item.is_valid():\n        continue\n    process(item)\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - Option A: Fail on first error**:\n```python\nfor item in items:\n    if not item.is_valid():\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid item: {item}\")\n    process(item)\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - Option B: Collect errors, report at end**:\n```python\nerrors = []\nfor item in items:\n    if not item.is_valid():\n        errors.append(f\"Invalid item: {item}\")\n        continue\n    process(item)\n\nif errors:\n    raise ValueError(f\"Processing failed with {len(errors)} invalid items:\\n\" +\n                     \"\\n\".join(errors))\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - Option C: Log warning if skip is intentional**:\n```python\nfor item in items:\n    if not item.is_valid():\n        logger.warning(\"Skipping invalid item: %s (reason: %s)\", item, item.validation_error)\n        continue\n    process(item)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 4: `return None` on Error → Raise Exception\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\ndef load_config(path):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return None\n    with open(path) as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n```\n\n**After (GOOD)**:\n```python\ndef load_config(path: Path) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Load configuration from path.\n\n    Raises:\n        FileNotFoundError: If config file doesn''t exist\n        json.JSONDecodeError: If config is not valid JSON\n    \"\"\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Config file not found: {path}\")\n\n    with open(path) as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 5: Error Return Codes → Exceptions\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\ndef process_data(data):\n    if not data:\n        return -1, \"No data provided\"\n    if not validate(data):\n        return -2, \"Invalid data\"\n    result = transform(data)\n    return 0, result\n```\n\n**After (GOOD)**:\n```python\ndef process_data(data):\n    \"\"\"Process the data.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If data is empty or invalid\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"No data provided\")\n    if not validate(data):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid data: {get_validation_errors(data)}\")\n    return transform(data)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 6: Defensive None Checks → Fail Fast\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\ndef process(data):\n    if data is None:\n        return\n    # ... rest of processing\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - If None is never valid**:\n```python\ndef process(data):\n    if data is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"data cannot be None\")\n    # ... rest of processing\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - If function should handle None gracefully**:\n```python\ndef process(data: Optional[Data]) -> Optional[Result]:\n    \"\"\"Process data if provided.\n\n    Args:\n        data: Data to process, or None to skip processing\n\n    Returns:\n        Result if data was processed, None if data was None\n    \"\"\"\n    if data is None:\n        logger.debug(\"process() called with None, returning None\")\n        return None\n    # ... rest of processing\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 7: subprocess Without Error Checking → check=True\n\n**Before (BAD)**:\n```python\nsubprocess.run([\"git\", \"commit\", \"-m\", \"message\"])\n```\n\n**After (GOOD)**:\n```python\ntry:\n    subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"commit\", \"-m\", \"message\"],\n        check=True,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True\n    )\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"Git commit failed: %s\\nstderr: %s\", e, e.stderr)\n    raise\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fix 8: Catch-Log-Reraise → Add Context or Remove\n\n**Before (BAD) - Adds noise**:\n```python\ntry:\n    do_something()\nexcept SomeError as e:\n    logger.error(f\"Error: {e}\")\n    raise\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - Option A: Add context**:\n```python\ntry:\n    do_something()\nexcept SomeError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"Failed during do_something in context X\")\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Operation failed in context X\") from e\n```\n\n**After (GOOD) - Option B: Just let it propagate**:\n```python\ndo_something()  # Let caller handle the exception\n```\n\n---\n\n## Adding Proper Logging\n\n### Logger Setup\n\nEnsure each module has a logger:\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n```\n\n### Logging Levels Guide\n\n| Level | Use For |\n|-------|---------|\n| `logger.debug()` | Detailed diagnostic info |\n| `logger.info()` | Normal operation milestones |\n| `logger.warning()` | Recoverable issues, degraded operation |\n| `logger.error()` | Errors that don''t stop execution |\n| `logger.exception()` | Errors with stack trace (use in except blocks) |\n| `logger.critical()` | Fatal errors, application cannot continue |\n\n### Logging Best Practices\n\n```python\n# GOOD - Use exception() in except blocks (includes stack trace)\nexcept SomeError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"Operation failed: %s\", e)\n\n# GOOD - Use lazy formatting\nlogger.debug(\"Processing item %s of %s\", i, total)\n\n# BAD - Eager string formatting\nlogger.debug(f\"Processing item {i} of {total}\")  # Formats even if debug disabled\n\n# GOOD - Include relevant context\nlogger.error(\"Failed to load preset ''%s'' from %s: %s\", preset_id, path, e)\n\n# BAD - Vague messages\nlogger.error(\"Error occurred\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Fix Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Run Audit\n\n```bash\n# Run audit first\n/audit-code-quality\n\n# Or run grep patterns directly\ngrep -rn \"except.*:$\" --include=\"*.py\" -A1 | grep -B1 \"pass$\"\n```\n\n### Step 2: Categorize Issues\n\nPriority order:\n1. `except: pass` or `except Exception: pass` (CRITICAL)\n2. Overly broad `except Exception` (HIGH)\n3. Silent continuation patterns (MEDIUM)\n4. Missing logging (MEDIUM)\n5. Return None on error (LOW)\n\n### Step 3: Fix Each Issue\n\nFor each issue:\n\n1. **Understand the intent** - Why was error suppressed?\n2. **Determine correct handling**:\n   - Should it fail fast? → Raise exception\n   - Is recovery possible? → Handle specifically with logging\n   - Is it truly optional? → Document and log at DEBUG level\n3. **Apply fix pattern** from above\n4. **Add/update tests** for error conditions\n5. **Run tests** to verify fix\n\n### Step 4: Verify Fixes\n\n```bash\n# Run tests\nuv run pytest MouseMaster/Testing/Python/ -v\n\n# Run linting\nuv run ruff check .\n\n# Re-run audit to confirm\n/audit-code-quality\n```\n\n---\n\n## Automated Fix Script\n\nFor simple patterns, use sed (review changes before committing!):\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# CAUTION: Review all changes manually!\n\n# Find files with except:pass (for manual review)\necho \"Files needing manual review:\"\ngrep -rl \"except.*:\" --include=\"*.py\" | while read f; do\n    if grep -q \"pass$\" \"$f\"; then\n        echo \"  $f\"\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\n**Note**: Automated fixes are risky. Always review manually and run tests.\n\n---\n\n## Exception Handling Decision Tree\n\n```\nIs this a programming error (bug)?\n├─ Yes → Let it crash (don''t catch)\n└─ No → Can user/system recover?\n         ├─ Yes → Catch, log, handle gracefully\n         └─ No → Catch, log with context, re-raise or wrap\n\nWhen catching:\n├─ Can you name the specific exception?\n│   ├─ Yes → Catch that specific type\n│   └─ No → Research what exceptions can occur\n└─ Is logging added?\n    ├─ Yes → Good\n    └─ No → Add logger.exception() call\n```\n\n---\n\n## Valid Exception Handling Cases\n\nNot all exception handling is bad. Valid cases include:\n\n### 1. User Input Validation\n```python\ntry:\n    value = int(user_input)\nexcept ValueError:\n    logger.warning(\"Invalid input ''%s'', prompting user\", user_input)\n    show_error_to_user(\"Please enter a valid number\")\n```\n\n### 2. Optional Feature Degradation\n```python\ntry:\n    import optional_dependency\n    FEATURE_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    logger.info(\"Optional feature unavailable: optional_dependency not installed\")\n    FEATURE_AVAILABLE = False\n```\n\n### 3. Resource Cleanup\n```python\ntry:\n    resource = acquire_resource()\n    use_resource(resource)\nfinally:\n    resource.cleanup()  # Always runs\n```\n\n### 4. Retry Logic\n```python\nfor attempt in range(max_retries):\n    try:\n        return do_operation()\n    except TransientError as e:\n        logger.warning(\"Attempt %d failed: %s\", attempt + 1, e)\n        if attempt == max_retries - 1:\n            raise\n        time.sleep(backoff)\n```\n\n### 5. Boundary/API Error Translation\n```python\ntry:\n    result = external_api.call()\nexcept ExternalAPIError as e:\n    logger.exception(\"External API failed\")\n    raise OurDomainError(f\"Service unavailable: {e}\") from e\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Error Paths\n\nAfter fixing, add tests for error conditions:\n\n```python\ndef test_load_config_missing_file():\n    \"\"\"Test that missing config raises FileNotFoundError.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(FileNotFoundError, match=\"Config file not found\"):\n        load_config(Path(\"/nonexistent/path\"))\n\ndef test_process_invalid_data():\n    \"\"\"Test that invalid data raises ValueError with details.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Invalid data\"):\n        process_data({\"bad\": \"data\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commit Message Template\n\nAfter fixes:\n\n```\nfix: replace exception swallowing with proper error handling\n\n- Remove except:pass in module_name.py\n- Add specific exception types with logging\n- Add error path tests\n\nFollows fail-fast principle: errors now surface immediately\nwith full context for debugging.\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:37:02.609Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents aiming to systematically fix bad coding practices following fail-fast principles.","zh":"适用于代码审查代理，旨在系统地修复不良编码实践，遵循快速失败原则。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントがバッドプラクティスを体系的に修正し、失敗すべきはすぐに失敗するという原則に従うために最適です。","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 나쁜 코딩 관행을 체계적으로 수정하고 실패 nhanh은 실패 원칙을 따르는 데 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código que buscan corregir sistemáticamente malas prácticas de codificación siguiendo principios de fail-fast.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code visant à corriger systématiquement de mauvaises pratiques de codage suivant les principes de fail-fast.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die darauf abzielen, schlechte Programmierpraktiken systematisch zu beheben, indem sie fail-fast-Prinzipien befolgen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que visam consertar sistematicamente más práticas de codificação seguindo princípios fail-fast.","ru":"Идеально для агентов проверки кода, nhằm систематически исправлять плохие практики программирования, следуя принципам fail-fast.","ar":"مثالي لعميل استعراض الشفرة الذي يهدف إلى إصلاح الممارسات البرمجية السيئة بشكل منهجي متبوعًا بمبادئ الفشل السريع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to replace silent failures with loud ones, catch specific exceptions, and refactor code for quality, all while adhering to fail-fast fixes and audit code quality standards like those from `/audit-code-quality`.","zh":"赋予代理人用响亮的失败取代静默的失败，捕捉特定的异常，并为了质量重构代码，同时遵守快速失败的修复和审计代码质量标准，如 `/audit-code-quality` 中的标准。","ja":"エージェントが静的な失敗を大きな失敗に置き換え、特定の例外を捕捉し、品質のためにコードをリファクタリングすることを可能にし、同時に失敗すべきはすぐに失敗するという修復と `/audit-code-quality` のようなコード品質基準の監査に従う。","ko":"에이전트가 무시된 실패를 큰 실패로 대체하고 특정 예외를 잡고 품질을 위해 코드를 개선하며 동시에 빠른 실패 수정과 `/audit-code-quality`와 같은 코드 품질 기준의 감사에 준수하도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes reemplazar fallos silenciosos con fallos audibles, capturar excepciones específicas y refactorizar el código para mejorar su calidad, todo mientras se adhieren a soluciones de fail-fast y estándares de auditoría de calidad de código como los de `/audit-code-quality`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de remplacer les défaillances silencieuses par des défaillances bruyantes, de capturer des exceptions spécifiques et de refactoriser le code pour améliorer sa qualité, tout en respectant les solutions de fail-fast et les normes d''audit de qualité de code comme celles de `/audit-code-quality`.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, stille Ausfälle durch laute Ausfälle zu ersetzen, spezifische Ausnahmen abzufangen und den Code zu refaktorisieren, um dessen Qualität zu verbessern, und dabei fail-fast-Lösungen und Code-Qualitätsaudit-Standards wie die von `/audit-code-quality` einzuhalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a substituir falhas silenciosas por falhas altas, capturar exceções específicas e refatorar o código para a qualidade, tudo isso seguindo os consertos fail-fast e os padrões de auditoria de qualidade de código como os da `/audit-code-quality`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью заменить молчаливые сбои громкими, поймать конкретные исключения и рефакторить код для качества, все это придерживаясь принципов fail-fast и стандартов аудита качества кода, таких как `/audit-code-quality`.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من استبدال الفشل الصامت بالفشل الصاخب وامتصاص الاستثناءات المحددة وإعادة هيكلة الشفرة من أجل الجودة، وكل ذلك مع اتباع إصلاحات الفشل السريع ومعايير تدقيق جودة الشفرة مثل تلك الموجودة في `/audit-code-quality`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code quality audits","Refactoring codebases for improved maintainability","Debugging silent failures in legacy code"],"zh":["自动化代码质量审计","重构代码库以提高可维护性","调试遗留代码中的静默失败"],"ja":["コード品質監査の自動化","メンテナンス性の向上のためにコードベースをリファクタリングする","レガシーコードの静的な失敗をデバッグする"],"ko":["코드 품질 감사의 자동화","유지 보수성을 개선하기 위해 코드베이스를 개선하는 것","레거시 코드의 무시된 실패를 디버깅하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de auditorías de calidad de código","Refactorización de bases de código para mejorar su mantenibilidad","Depuración de fallos silenciosos en código heredado"],"fr":["Automatisation des audits de qualité de code","Refactorisation de bases de code pour améliorer leur maintenabilité","Débogage des défaillances silencieuses dans le code hérité"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Qualitätsaudits","Refaktorisierung von Codebasen zur Verbesserung ihrer Wartbarkeit","Fehlerbehebung stiller Ausfälle in Legacy-Code"],"pt":["Automatizar auditorias de qualidade de código","Refatorar bases de código para melhorar a manutenção","Depurar falhas silenciosas em código legado"],"ru":["Автоматизировать аудит качества кода","Рефакторить кодовые базы для улучшения поддержки","Отладить молчаливые сбои в устаревшем коде"],"ar":["تحسين عمليات تدقيق جودة الشفرة تلقائيًا","إعادة هيكلة قواعد الشفرة لتحسين الصيانة","تصحيح الفشل الصامت في الشفرة القديمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires prior code quality audit data","Adherence to fail-fast principles"],"zh":["需要之前的代码质量审计数据","遵循快速失败原则"],"ja":["以前のコード品質監査データが必要","失敗すべきはすぐに失敗するという原則に従う"],"ko":["이전에 코드 품질 감사 데이터가 필요함","빠른 실패 원칙을 따름"],"es":["Requiere datos de auditoría de calidad de código previos","Adhesión a principios de fail-fast"],"fr":["Nécessite des données d''audit de qualité de code préalables","Respect des principes de fail-fast"],"de":["Benötigt vorherige Code-Qualitätsaudit-Daten","Einhaltung von fail-fast-Prinzipien"],"pt":["Requer dados de auditoria de qualidade de código anteriores","Adesão aos princípios fail-fast"],"ru":["Требует предварительных данных аудита качества кода","Соблюдение принципов fail-fast"],"ar":["يتطلب بيانات التدقيق السابقة لجودة الشفرة","الامتثال لمبادئ الفشل السريع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
