Tailwind CSS","es":"Guía experta para crear componentes UI accesibles y personalizables con shadcn-ui, Radix UI y Tailwind CSS. Aprende a configurar y utilizar estos frameworks ...","fr":"Guide expert pour créer des composants UI accessibles et personnalisables avec shadcn-ui, Radix UI et Tailwind CSS. Apprenez à configurer et utiliser ces fra...","de":"Leitfaden für die Erstellung von zugänglichen und anpassbaren UI-Komponenten mit shadcn-ui, Radix UI und Tailwind CSS. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Frameworks...","pt":"Guia de componentes UI shadcn-ui para desenvolvedores, com foco em acessibilidade e personalização","ru":"Руководство по компонентам shadcn-ui для разработчиков, с фокусом на доступности и настройке","ar":"دليل مكونات شادسن-يو آي للمطورين، مع التركيز على سهولة الوصول والتخصيص","en":"My personal environment settings"},"definition":{"en":"My personal environment settings"},"features":{"zh":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields"],"ja":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields"],"ko":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields"],"es":["Componentes UI personalizables","Accesibilidad y compatibilidad","Integración con Radix UI y Tailwind CSS","Guía de configuración y uso","Ejemplos de componentes UI predefinidos","Validación de formularios"],"fr":["Composants UI personnalisables","Accessibilité et compatibilité","Intégration avec Radix UI et Tailwind CSS","Guide de configuration et d''utilisation","Exemples de composants UI prédéfinis","Validation de formulaires"],"de":["Anpassbare UI-Komponenten","Zugänglichkeit und Kompatibilität","Integration mit Radix UI und Tailwind CSS","Konfigurations- und Benutzerhandbuch","Beispiele für vorkonfigurierte UI-Komponenten","Formularvalidierung"],"pt":["Componentes UI acessíveis","Personalização com Tailwind CSS","Integração com Radix UI","Guia de instalação e configuração","Exemplos de componentes UI"],"ru":["Доступные компоненты UI","Настройка с помощью Tailwind CSS","Интеграция с Radix UI","Руководство по установке и настройке","Примеры компонентов UI"],"ar":["مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للوصول","التخصيص باستخدام تايلويند سي إس إس","التكامل مع راديكس يو آي","دليل التثبيت والتهيئة","أمثلة على مكونات واجهة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields","UI","shadcn-ui"],"ja":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields","UI","shadcn-ui"],"ko":["shadcn-ui","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","UI","Button","Input & Form Fields","UI","shadcn-ui"],"es":["shadcn-ui","componentes UI","accesibilidad web","personalización de interfaces","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","desarrollo web","frameworks de UI","validación de formularios"],"fr":["shadcn-ui","composants UI","accessibilité web","personnalisation d''interfaces","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","développement web","frameworks de UI","validation de formulaires"],"de":["shadcn-ui","UI-Komponenten","Web-Zugänglichkeit","Benutzeroberflächen-Anpassung","Radix UI","Tailwind CSS","Webentwicklung","UI-Frameworks","Formularvalidierung"],"pt":["shadcn-ui","componentes UI","acessibilidade","personalização","Tailwind CSS","Radix UI","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["shadcn-ui","компоненты UI","доступность","настройка","Tailwind CSS","Radix UI","веб-разработка"],"ar":["شادسن-يو آي","مكونات واجهة المستخدم","سهولة الوصول","التخصيص","تايلويند سي إس إس","راديكس يو آي","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"dandedotdev","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"dandedotdev/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"shadcn-ui","description":"Complete shadcn/ui component library guide including installation, configuration, and implementation of accessible React components. Use when setting up shadcn/ui, installing components, building forms with React Hook Form and Zod, customizing themes with Tailwind CSS, or implementing UI patterns like buttons, dialogs, dropdowns, tables, and complex form layouts.","bodyPreview":"# shadcn/ui Component Patterns\n\nExpert guide for building accessible, customizable UI components with shadcn/ui, Radix UI, and Tailwind CSS.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [When to Use](#when-to-use)\n- [Quick Start](#quick-start)\n- [Installation & Setup](#installation--setup)\n- [Project Configuration](#project-configuration)\n- [Core Components](#core-components)\n  - [Button](#button-component)\n  - [Input & Form Fields](#input--form-fields)\n  - [Forms with Validation](#forms-with-validation)\n  - [Card]","body":"# shadcn/ui Component Patterns\n\nExpert guide for building accessible, customizable UI components with shadcn/ui, Radix UI, and Tailwind CSS.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [When to Use](#when-to-use)\n- [Quick Start](#quick-start)\n- [Installation & Setup](#installation--setup)\n- [Project Configuration](#project-configuration)\n- [Core Components](#core-components)\n  - [Button](#button-component)\n  - [Input & Form Fields](#input--form-fields)\n  - [Forms with Validation](#forms-with-validation)\n  - [Card](#card-component)\n  - [Dialog (Modal)](#dialog-modal-component)\n  - [Select (Dropdown)](#select-dropdown-component)\n  - [Sheet (Slide-over)](#sheet-slide-over-component)\n  - [Menubar & Navigation](#menubar--navigation)\n  - [Table](#table-component)\n  - [Toast Notifications](#toast-notifications)\n- [Advanced Patterns](#advanced-patterns)\n- [Customization](#customization)\n- [Next.js Integration](#nextjs-integration)\n- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n- [Common Component Combinations](#common-component-combinations)\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Setting up a new project with shadcn/ui\n- Installing or configuring individual components\n- Building forms with React Hook Form and Zod validation\n- Creating accessible UI components (buttons, dialogs, dropdowns, sheets)\n- Customizing component styling with Tailwind CSS\n- Implementing design systems with shadcn/ui\n- Building Next.js applications with TypeScript\n- Creating complex layouts and data displays\n\n## Quick Start\n\nFor new projects, use the automated setup:\n\n```bash\n# Create Next.js project with shadcn/ui\nnpx create-next-app@latest my-app --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app\ncd my-app\nnpx shadcn@latest init\n\n# Install essential components\nnpx shadcn@latest add button input form card dialog select\n```\n\nFor existing projects:\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install tailwindcss-animate class-variance-authority clsx tailwind-merge lucide-react\n\n# Initialize shadcn/ui\nnpx shadcn@latest init\n```\n\n## What is shadcn/ui?\n\nshadcn/ui is **not** a traditional component library or npm package. Instead:\n\n- It''s a **collection of reusable components** that you can copy into your project\n- Components are **yours to customize** - you own the code\n- Built with **Radix UI** primitives for accessibility\n- Styled with **Tailwind CSS** utilities\n- Includes CLI tool for easy component installation\n\n## Installation & Setup\n\n### Initial Setup\n\n```bash\n# Initialize shadcn/ui in your project\nnpx shadcn@latest init\n```\n\nDuring setup, you''ll configure:\n- TypeScript or JavaScript\n- Style (Default, New York, etc.)\n- Base color theme\n- CSS variables or Tailwind CSS classes\n- Component installation path\n\n### Installing Individual Components\n\n```bash\n# Install a single component\nnpx shadcn@latest add button\n\n# Install multiple components\nnpx shadcn@latest add button input form\n\n# Install all components\nnpx shadcn@latest add --all\n```\n\n### Manual Installation\n\nIf you prefer manual setup:\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies for a specific component\nnpm install @radix-ui/react-slot\n\n# Copy component code from ui.shadcn.com\n# Place in src/components/ui/\n```\n\n## Project Configuration\n\n### Required Dependencies\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@radix-ui/react-accordion\": \"^1.1.2\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-alert-dialog\": \"^1.0.5\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-dialog\": \"^1.0.5\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu\": \"^2.0.6\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-label\": \"^2.0.2\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-select\": \"^2.0.0\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-separator\": \"^1.0.3\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-slot\": \"^1.0.2\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-toast\": \"^1.1.5\",\n    \"class-variance-authority\": \"^0.7.0\",\n    \"clsx\": \"^2.0.0\",\n    \"lucide-react\": \"^0.294.0\",\n    \"tailwind-merge\": \"^2.0.0\",\n    \"tailwindcss-animate\": \"^1.0.7\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### TSConfig Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"es5\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"es6\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"node\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"next\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"baseUrl\": \".\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/components/*\": [\"./src/components/*\"],\n      \"@/lib/*\": [\"./src/lib/*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Tailwind Configuration\n\n```js\n// tailwind.config.js\n/** @type {import(''tailwindcss'').Config} */\nmodule.exports = {\n  darkMode: [\"class\"],\n  content: [\n    ''./pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}'',\n    ''./components/**/*.{ts,tsx}'',\n    ''./app/**/*.{ts,tsx}'',\n    ''./src/**/*.{ts,tsx}'',\n  ],\n  prefix: \"\",\n  theme: {\n    container: {\n      center: true,\n      padding: \"2rem\",\n      screens: {\n        \"2xl\": \"1400px\",\n      },\n    },\n    extend: {\n      colors: {\n        border: \"hsl(var(--border))\",\n        input: \"hsl(var(--input))\",\n        ring: \"hsl(var(--ring))\",\n        background: \"hsl(var(--background))\",\n        foreground: \"hsl(var(--foreground))\",\n        primary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--primary))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--primary-foreground))\",\n        },\n        secondary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--secondary))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--secondary-foreground))\",\n        },\n        destructive: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--destructive))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--destructive-foreground))\",\n        },\n        muted: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--muted))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--muted-foreground))\",\n        },\n        accent: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--accent))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--accent-foreground))\",\n        },\n        popover: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--popover))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--popover-foreground))\",\n        },\n        card: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--card))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--card-foreground))\",\n        },\n      },\n      borderRadius: {\n        lg: \"var(--radius)\",\n        md: \"calc(var(--radius) - 2px)\",\n        sm: \"calc(var(--radius) - 4px)\",\n      },\n      keyframes: {\n        \"accordion-down\": {\n          from: { height: \"0\" },\n          to: { height: \"var(--radix-accordion-content-height)\" },\n        },\n        \"accordion-up\": {\n          from: { height: \"var(--radix-accordion-content-height)\" },\n          to: { height: \"0\" },\n        },\n      },\n      animation: {\n        \"accordion-down\": \"accordion-down 0.2s ease-out\",\n        \"accordion-up\": \"accordion-up 0.2s ease-out\",\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  plugins: [require(\"tailwindcss-animate\")],\n}\n```\n\n### CSS Variables (globals.css)\n\n```css\n@tailwind base;\n@tailwind components;\n@tailwind utilities;\n\n@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --background: 0 0% 100%;\n    --foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --card: 0 0% 100%;\n    --card-foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --popover: 0 0% 100%;\n    --popover-foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --primary: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --primary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --secondary: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --secondary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --muted: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --muted-foreground: 215.4 16.3% 46.9%;\n    --accent: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --accent-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --destructive: 0 84.2% 60.2%;\n    --destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --border: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;\n    --input: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;\n    --ring: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --radius: 0.5rem;\n  }\n\n  .dark {\n    --background: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --card: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --card-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --popover: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --popover-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --secondary: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --secondary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --muted: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --muted-foreground: 215 20.2% 65.1%;\n    --accent: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --accent-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --destructive: 0 62.8% 30.6%;\n    --destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --border: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --input: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --ring: 212.7 26.8% 83.9%;\n  }\n}\n\n@layer base {\n  * {\n    @apply border-border;\n  }\n  body {\n    @apply bg-background text-foreground;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Core Components\n\n### Button Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add button\n```\n\nBasic usage:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n\nexport function ButtonDemo() {\n  return <Button>Click me</Button>;\n}\n```\n\nButton variants:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n\nexport function ButtonVariants() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex gap-4\">\n      <Button variant=\"default\">Default</Button>\n      <Button variant=\"destructive\">Destructive</Button>\n      <Button variant=\"outline\">Outline</Button>\n      <Button variant=\"secondary\">Secondary</Button>\n      <Button variant=\"ghost\">Ghost</Button>\n      <Button variant=\"link\">Link</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nButton sizes:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"flex gap-4 items-center\">\n  <Button size=\"default\">Default</Button>\n  <Button size=\"sm\">Small</Button>\n  <Button size=\"lg\">Large</Button>\n  <Button size=\"icon\">\n    <Icon className=\"h-4 w-4\" />\n  </Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nWith loading state:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\nimport { Loader2 } from \"lucide-react\";\n\nexport function ButtonLoading() {\n  return (\n    <Button disabled>\n      <Loader2 className=\"mr-2 h-4 w-4 animate-spin\" />\n      Please wait\n    </Button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Input & Form Fields\n\n#### Input Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add input\n```\n\nBasic input:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\";\n\nexport function InputDemo() {\n  return <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" />;\n}\n```\n\nInput with label:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\";\nimport { Label } from \"@/components/ui/label\";\n\nexport function InputWithLabel() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"grid w-full max-w-sm items-center gap-1.5\">\n      <Label htmlFor=\"email\">Email</Label>\n      <Input type=\"email\" id=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nInput with button:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\";\n\nexport function InputWithButton() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex w-full max-w-sm items-center gap-2\">\n      <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" />\n      <Button type=\"submit\" variant=\"outline\">Subscribe</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Forms with Validation\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add form\n```\n\nThis installs React Hook Form, Zod, and form components.\n\nComplete form example:\n\n```tsx\n\"use client\"\n\nimport { zodResolver } from \"@hookform/resolvers/zod\"\nimport { useForm } from \"react-hook-form\"\nimport * as z from \"zod\"\n\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Form,\n  FormControl,\n  FormDescription,\n  FormField,\n  FormItem,\n  FormLabel,\n  FormMessage,\n} from \"@/components/ui/form\"\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"\nimport { toast } from \"@/components/ui/use-toast\"\n\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  username: z.string().min(2, {\n    message: \"Username must be at least 2 characters.\",\n  }),\n  email: z.string().email({\n    message: \"Please enter a valid email address.\",\n  }),\n})\n\nexport function ProfileForm() {\n  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof formSchema>>({\n    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),\n    defaultValues: {\n      username: \"\",\n      email: \"\",\n    },\n  })\n\n  function onSubmit(values: z.infer<typeof formSchema>) {\n    toast({\n      title: \"You submitted the following values:\",\n      description: (\n        <pre className=\"mt-2 w-[340px] rounded-md bg-slate-950 p-4\">\n          <code className=\"text-white\">{JSON.stringify(values, null, 2)}</code>\n        </pre>\n      ),\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <Form {...form}>\n      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-8\">\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"username\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Username</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input placeholder=\"shadcn\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormDescription>\n                This is your public display name.\n              </FormDescription>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n        \n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"email\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Email</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"you@example.com\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n        \n        <Button type=\"submit\">Submit</Button>\n      </form>\n    </Form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Card Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add card\n```\n\nBasic card:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Card,\n  CardContent,\n  CardDescription,\n  CardFooter,\n  CardHeader,\n  CardTitle,\n} from \"@/components/ui/card\"\n\nexport function CardDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Card>\n      <CardHeader>\n        <CardTitle>Card Title</CardTitle>\n        <CardDescription>Card Description</CardDescription>\n      </CardHeader>\n      <CardContent>\n        <p>Card Content</p>\n      </CardContent>\n      <CardFooter>\n        <p>Card Footer</p>\n      </CardFooter>\n    </Card>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nCard with form:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Card,\n  CardContent,\n  CardDescription,\n  CardFooter,\n  CardHeader,\n  CardTitle,\n} from \"@/components/ui/card\"\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"\nimport { Label } from \"@/components/ui/label\"\n\nexport function CardWithForm() {\n  return (\n    <Card className=\"w-[350px]\">\n      <CardHeader>\n        <CardTitle>Create project</CardTitle>\n        <CardDescription>Deploy your new project in one-click.</CardDescription>\n      </CardHeader>\n      <CardContent>\n        <form>\n          <div className=\"grid w-full items-center gap-4\">\n            <div className=\"flex flex-col space-y-1.5\">\n              <Label htmlFor=\"name\">Name</Label>\n              <Input id=\"name\" placeholder=\"Name of your project\" />\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </form>\n      </CardContent>\n      <CardFooter className=\"flex justify-between\">\n        <Button variant=\"outline\">Cancel</Button>\n        <Button>Deploy</Button>\n      </CardFooter>\n    </Card>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Dialog (Modal) Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add dialog\n```\n\nBasic dialog:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Dialog,\n  DialogContent,\n  DialogDescription,\n  DialogFooter,\n  DialogHeader,\n  DialogTitle,\n  DialogTrigger,\n} from \"@/components/ui/dialog\"\n\nexport function DialogDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Dialog>\n      <DialogTrigger asChild>\n        <Button variant=\"outline\">Open Dialog</Button>\n      </DialogTrigger>\n      <DialogContent className=\"sm:max-w-[425px]\">\n        <DialogHeader>\n          <DialogTitle>Edit profile</DialogTitle>\n          <DialogDescription>\n            Make changes to your profile here. Click save when you''re done.\n          </DialogDescription>\n        </DialogHeader>\n        <div className=\"grid gap-4 py-4\">\n          <div className=\"grid grid-cols-4 items-center gap-4\">\n            <Label htmlFor=\"name\" className=\"text-right\">\n              Name\n            </Label>\n            <Input id=\"name\" value=\"Pedro Duarte\" className=\"col-span-3\" />\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <DialogFooter>\n          <Button type=\"submit\">Save changes</Button>\n        </DialogFooter>\n      </DialogContent>\n    </Dialog>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Sheet (Slide-over) Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add sheet\n```\n\nBasic sheet:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Sheet,\n  SheetContent,\n  SheetDescription,\n  SheetHeader,\n  SheetTitle,\n  SheetTrigger,\n} from \"@/components/ui/sheet\"\n\nexport function SheetDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Sheet>\n      <SheetTrigger asChild>\n        <Button variant=\"outline\">Open Sheet</Button>\n      </SheetTrigger>\n      <SheetContent>\n        <SheetHeader>\n          <SheetTitle>Edit profile</SheetTitle>\n          <SheetDescription>\n            Make changes to your profile here. Click save when you''re done.\n          </SheetDescription>\n        </SheetHeader>\n        <div className=\"grid gap-4 py-4\">\n          <div className=\"grid grid-cols-4 items-center gap-4\">\n            <Label htmlFor=\"name\" className=\"text-right\">\n              Name\n            </Label>\n            <Input id=\"name\" value=\"Pedro Duarte\" className=\"col-span-3\" />\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"grid grid-cols-4 items-center gap-4\">\n            <Label htmlFor=\"username\" className=\"text-right\">\n              Username\n            </Label>\n            <Input id=\"username\" value=\"@peduarte\" className=\"col-span-3\" />\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </SheetContent>\n    </Sheet>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSheet with side placement:\n\n```tsx\n<Sheet>\n  <SheetTrigger asChild>\n    <Button variant=\"outline\">Open Right Sheet</Button>\n  </SheetTrigger>\n  <SheetContent side=\"right\">\n    <SheetHeader>\n      <SheetTitle>Settings</SheetTitle>\n      <SheetDescription>\n        Configure your application settings here.\n      </SheetDescription>\n    </SheetHeader>\n    {/* Settings content */}\n  </SheetContent>\n</Sheet>\n```\n\n### Menubar & Navigation\n\n#### Menubar Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add menubar\n```\n\nBasic menubar:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Menubar,\n  MenubarContent,\n  MenubarItem,\n  MenubarMenu,\n  MenubarSeparator,\n  MenubarShortcut,\n  MenubarSub,\n  MenubarSubContent,\n  MenubarSubTrigger,\n  MenubarTrigger,\n} from \"@/components/ui/menubar\"\n\nexport function MenubarDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Menubar>\n      <MenubarMenu>\n        <MenubarTrigger>File</MenubarTrigger>\n        <MenubarContent>\n          <MenubarItem>\n            New Tab <MenubarShortcut>⌘T</MenubarShortcut>\n          </MenubarItem>\n          <MenubarItem>\n            New Window <MenubarShortcut>⌘N</MenubarShortcut>\n          </MenubarItem>\n          <MenubarSeparator />\n          <MenubarItem>Share</MenubarItem>\n          <MenubarSeparator />\n          <MenubarItem>Print</MenubarItem>\n        </MenubarContent>\n      </MenubarMenu>\n      <MenubarMenu>\n        <MenubarTrigger>Edit</MenubarTrigger>\n        <MenubarContent>\n          <MenubarItem>\n            Undo <MenubarShortcut>⌘Z</MenubarShortcut>\n          </MenubarItem>\n          <MenubarItem>\n            Redo <MenubarShortcut>⌘Y</MenubarShortcut>\n          </MenubarItem>\n          <MenubarSeparator />\n          <MenubarSub>\n            <MenubarSubTrigger>Find</MenubarSubTrigger>\n            <MenubarSubContent>\n              <MenubarItem>Search the web</MenubarItem>\n              <MenubarItem>Find...</MenubarItem>\n              <MenubarItem>Find Next</MenubarItem>\n              <MenubarItem>Find Previous</MenubarItem>\n            </MenubarSubContent>\n          </MenubarSub>\n        </MenubarContent>\n      </MenubarMenu>\n    </Menubar>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Select (Dropdown) Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add select\n```\n\nBasic select:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Select,\n  SelectContent,\n  SelectItem,\n  SelectTrigger,\n  SelectValue,\n} from \"@/components/ui/select\"\n\nexport function SelectDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Select>\n      <SelectTrigger className=\"w-[180px]\">\n        <SelectValue placeholder=\"Select a fruit\" />\n      </SelectTrigger>\n      <SelectContent>\n        <SelectItem value=\"apple\">Apple</SelectItem>\n        <SelectItem value=\"banana\">Banana</SelectItem>\n        <SelectItem value=\"orange\">Orange</SelectItem>\n      </SelectContent>\n    </Select>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSelect in form:\n\n```tsx\n<FormField\n  control={form.control}\n  name=\"role\"\n  render={({ field }) => (\n    <FormItem>\n      <FormLabel>Role</FormLabel>\n      <Select onValueChange={field.onChange} defaultValue={field.value}>\n        <FormControl>\n          <SelectTrigger>\n            <SelectValue placeholder=\"Select a role\" />\n          </SelectTrigger>\n        </FormControl>\n        <SelectContent>\n          <SelectItem value=\"admin\">Admin</SelectItem>\n          <SelectItem value=\"user\">User</SelectItem>\n          <SelectItem value=\"guest\">Guest</SelectItem>\n        </SelectContent>\n      </Select>\n      <FormMessage />\n    </FormItem>\n  )}\n/>\n```\n\n### Toast Notifications\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add toast\n```\n\nSetup toast provider in root layout:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Toaster } from \"@/components/ui/toaster\"\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Toaster />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nUsing toast:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useToast } from \"@/components/ui/use-toast\"\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\n\nexport function ToastDemo() {\n  const { toast } = useToast()\n\n  return (\n    <Button\n      onClick={() => {\n        toast({\n          title: \"Scheduled: Catch up\",\n          description: \"Friday, February 10, 2023 at 5:57 PM\",\n        })\n      }}\n    >\n      Show Toast\n    </Button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nToast variants:\n\n```tsx\n// Success\ntoast({\n  title: \"Success\",\n  description: \"Your changes have been saved.\",\n})\n\n// Error\ntoast({\n  variant: \"destructive\",\n  title: \"Error\",\n  description: \"Something went wrong.\",\n})\n\n// With action\ntoast({\n  title: \"Uh oh! Something went wrong.\",\n  description: \"There was a problem with your request.\",\n  action: <ToastAction altText=\"Try again\">Try again</ToastAction>,\n})\n```\n\n### Table Component\n\nInstallation:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add table\n```\n\nBasic table:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Table,\n  TableBody,\n  TableCaption,\n  TableCell,\n  TableHead,\n  TableHeader,\n  TableRow,\n} from \"@/components/ui/table\"\n\nconst invoices = [\n  { invoice: \"INV001\", status: \"Paid\", method: \"Credit Card\", amount: \"$250.00\" },\n  { invoice: \"INV002\", status: \"Pending\", method: \"PayPal\", amount: \"$150.00\" },\n]\n\nexport function TableDemo() {\n  return (\n    <Table>\n      <TableCaption>A list of your recent invoices.</TableCaption>\n      <TableHeader>\n        <TableRow>\n          <TableHead>Invoice</TableHead>\n          <TableHead>Status</TableHead>\n          <TableHead>Method</TableHead>\n          <TableHead className=\"text-right\">Amount</TableHead>\n        </TableRow>\n      </TableHeader>\n      <TableBody>\n        {invoices.map((invoice) => (\n          <TableRow key={invoice.invoice}>\n            <TableCell className=\"font-medium\">{invoice.invoice}</TableCell>\n            <TableCell>{invoice.status}</TableCell>\n            <TableCell>{invoice.method}</TableCell>\n            <TableCell className=\"text-right\">{invoice.amount}</TableCell>\n          </TableRow>\n        ))}\n      </TableBody>\n    </Table>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Customization\n\n### Theming with CSS Variables\n\nshadcn/ui uses CSS variables for theming. Configure in `globals.css`:\n\n```css\n@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --background: 0 0% 100%;\n    --foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --primary: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --primary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --secondary: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --secondary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --muted: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --muted-foreground: 215.4 16.3% 46.9%;\n    --accent: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --accent-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --destructive: 0 84.2% 60.2%;\n    --destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --border: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;\n    --input: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;\n    --ring: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --radius: 0.5rem;\n  }\n\n  .dark {\n    --background: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    /* ... other dark mode variables */\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Customizing Components\n\nSince you own the code, customize directly:\n\n```tsx\n// components/ui/button.tsx\nimport * as React from \"react\"\nimport { Slot } from \"@radix-ui/react-slot\"\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from \"class-variance-authority\"\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/utils\"\n\nconst buttonVariants = cva(\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-colors\",\n  {\n    variants: {\n      variant: {\n        default: \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90\",\n        destructive: \"bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90\",\n        outline: \"border border-input bg-background hover:bg-accent\",\n        // Add custom variant\n        custom: \"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-500 to-pink-500 text-white\",\n      },\n      size: {\n        default: \"h-10 px-4 py-2\",\n        sm: \"h-9 rounded-md px-3\",\n        lg: \"h-11 rounded-md px-8\",\n        // Add custom size\n        xl: \"h-14 rounded-md px-10 text-lg\",\n      },\n    },\n    defaultVariants: {\n      variant: \"default\",\n      size: \"default\",\n    },\n  }\n)\n\nexport interface ButtonProps\n  extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>,\n    VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {\n  asChild?: boolean\n}\n\nconst Button = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(\n  ({ className, variant, size, asChild = false, ...props }, ref) => {\n    const Comp = asChild ? Slot : \"button\"\n    return (\n      <Comp\n        className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}\n        ref={ref}\n        {...props}\n      />\n    )\n  }\n)\nButton.displayName = \"Button\"\n\nexport { Button, buttonVariants }\n```\n\n## Next.js Integration\n\n### App Router Setup\n\nFor Next.js 13+ with App Router, ensure components use `\"use client\"` directive:\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/ui/button.tsx\n\"use client\"\n\nimport * as React from \"react\"\nimport { Slot } from \"@radix-ui/react-slot\"\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from \"class-variance-authority\"\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/utils\"\n\n// ... rest of component\n```\n\n### Layout Integration\n\nAdd the Toaster to your root layout:\n\n```tsx\n// app/layout.tsx\nimport { Toaster } from \"@/components/ui/toaster\"\nimport \"./globals.css\"\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\" suppressHydrationWarning>\n      <body className=\"min-h-screen bg-background font-sans antialiased\">\n        {children}\n        <Toaster />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Server Components\n\nWhen using shadcn/ui components in Server Components, wrap them in a Client Component:\n\n```tsx\n// app/dashboard/page.tsx\nimport { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from \"@/components/ui/card\"\nimport { ButtonClient } from \"@/components/ui/button-client\"\n\nexport default function DashboardPage() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"container mx-auto p-6\">\n      <Card>\n        <CardHeader>\n          <CardTitle>Dashboard</CardTitle>\n        </CardHeader>\n        <CardContent>\n          <ButtonClient>Interactive Button</ButtonClient>\n        </CardContent>\n      </Card>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/ui/button-client.tsx\n\"use client\"\n\nimport { Button } from \"./button\"\n\nexport function ButtonClient(props: React.ComponentProps<typeof Button>) {\n  return <Button {...props} />\n}\n```\n\n### Route Handlers with Forms\n\nCreate API routes for form submissions:\n\n```tsx\n// app/api/contact/route.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst contactSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(2),\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  message: z.string().min(10),\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  try {\n    const body = await request.json()\n    const validated = contactSchema.parse(body)\n\n    // Process form data\n    console.log(\"Form submission:\", validated)\n\n    return NextResponse.json({ success: true })\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { errors: error.errors },\n        { status: 400 }\n      )\n    }\n\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"Internal server error\" },\n      { status: 500 }\n    )\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Form with Server Action\n\nUsing Next.js 14+ Server Actions:\n\n```tsx\n// app/contact/page.tsx\n\"use client\"\n\nimport { zodResolver } from \"@hookform/resolvers/zod\"\nimport { useForm } from \"react-hook-form\"\nimport * as z from \"zod\"\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport {\n  Form,\n  FormControl,\n  FormField,\n  FormItem,\n  FormLabel,\n  FormMessage,\n} from \"@/components/ui/form\"\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"\nimport { Textarea } from \"@/components/ui/textarea\"\nimport { toast } from \"@/components/ui/use-toast\"\n\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(2),\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  message: z.string().min(10),\n})\n\nasync function onSubmit(values: z.infer<typeof formSchema>) {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(\"/api/contact\", {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(values),\n    })\n\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(\"Failed to submit\")\n\n    toast({\n      title: \"Success!\",\n      description: \"Your message has been sent.\",\n    })\n  } catch (error) {\n    toast({\n      variant: \"destructive\",\n      title: \"Error\",\n      description: \"Failed to send message. Please try again.\",\n    })\n  }\n}\n\nexport default function ContactPage() {\n  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof formSchema>>({\n    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"container mx-auto max-w-2xl py-8\">\n      <Form {...form}>\n        <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-6\">\n          <FormField\n            control={form.control}\n            name=\"name\"\n            render={({ field }) => (\n              <FormItem>\n                <FormLabel>Name</FormLabel>\n                <FormControl>\n                  <Input placeholder=\"Your name\" {...field} />\n                </FormControl>\n                <FormMessage />\n              </FormItem>\n            )}\n          />\n\n          <FormField\n            control={form.control}\n            name=\"email\"\n            render={({ field }) => (\n              <FormItem>\n                <FormLabel>Email</FormLabel>\n                <FormControl>\n                  <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"your@email.com\" {...field} />\n                </FormControl>\n                <FormMessage />\n              </FormItem>\n            )}\n          />\n\n          <FormField\n            control={form.control}\n            name=\"message\"\n            render={({ field }) => (\n              <FormItem>\n                <FormLabel>Message</FormLabel>\n                <FormControl>\n                  <Textarea\n                    placeholder=\"Your message...\"\n                    className=\"resize-none\"\n                    {...field}\n                  />\n                </FormControl>\n                <FormMessage />\n              </FormItem>\n            )}\n          />\n\n          <Button type=\"submit\" className=\"w-full\">\n            Send Message\n          </Button>\n        </form>\n      </Form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Metadata with shadcn/ui\n\nUsing shadcn/ui components in metadata:\n\n```tsx\n// app/layout.tsx\nimport { Metadata } from \"next\"\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: {\n    default: \"My App\",\n    template: \"%s | My App\",\n  },\n  description: \"Built with shadcn/ui and Next.js\",\n}\n\n// app/about/page.tsx\nimport { Metadata } from \"next\"\nimport { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from \"@/components/ui/card\"\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: \"About Us\",\n  description: \"Learn more about our company\",\n}\n\nexport default function AboutPage() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"container mx-auto py-8\">\n      <Card>\n        <CardHeader>\n          <CardTitle>About Our Company</CardTitle>\n        </CardHeader>\n        <CardContent>\n          <p>We build amazing products with modern web technologies.</p>\n        </CardContent>\n      </Card>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Font Optimization\n\nOptimize fonts with next/font:\n\n```tsx\n// app/layout.tsx\nimport { Inter } from \"next/font/google\"\nimport { Toaster } from \"@/components/ui/toaster\"\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/utils\"\nimport \"./globals.css\"\n\nconst inter = Inter({ subsets: [\"latin\"] })\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\" suppressHydrationWarning>\n      <body className={cn(\"min-h-screen bg-background font-sans antialiased\", inter.className)}>\n        {children}\n        <Toaster />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Form with Multiple Fields\n\n```tsx\nconst formSchema = z.object({\n  username: z.string().min(2).max(50),\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  bio: z.string().max(160).min(4),\n  role: z.enum([\"admin\", \"user\", \"guest\"]),\n  notifications: z.boolean().default(false),\n})\n\nexport function AdvancedForm() {\n  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof formSchema>>({\n    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),\n    defaultValues: {\n      username: \"\",\n      email: \"\",\n      bio: \"\",\n      role: \"user\",\n      notifications: false,\n    },\n  })\n\n  function onSubmit(values: z.infer<typeof formSchema>) {\n    console.log(values)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <Form {...form}>\n      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-8\">\n        {/* Username field */}\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"username\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Username</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input placeholder=\"johndoe\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n\n        {/* Email field */}\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"email\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Email</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"john@example.com\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n\n        {/* Textarea field */}\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"bio\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Bio</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Textarea\n                  placeholder=\"Tell us about yourself\"\n                  className=\"resize-none\"\n                  {...field}\n                />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n\n        {/* Select field */}\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"role\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Role</FormLabel>\n              <Select onValueChange={field.onChange} defaultValue={field.value}>\n                <FormControl>\n                  <SelectTrigger>\n                    <SelectValue placeholder=\"Select a role\" />\n                  </SelectTrigger>\n                </FormControl>\n                <SelectContent>\n                  <SelectItem value=\"admin\">Admin</SelectItem>\n                  <SelectItem value=\"user\">User</SelectItem>\n                  <SelectItem value=\"guest\">Guest</SelectItem>\n                </SelectContent>\n              </Select>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n\n        {/* Checkbox field */}\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"notifications\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem className=\"flex flex-row items-start space-x-3 space-y-0\">\n              <FormControl>\n                <Checkbox\n                  checked={field.value}\n                  onCheckedChange={field.onChange}\n                />\n              </FormControl>\n              <div className=\"space-y-1 leading-none\">\n                <FormLabel>Email notifications</FormLabel>\n                <FormDescription>\n                  Receive emails about your account activity.\n                </FormDescription>\n              </div>\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n\n        <Button type=\"submit\">Submit</Button>\n      </form>\n    </Form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Accessibility**: Components use Radix UI primitives for ARIA compliance\n2. **Customization**: Modify components directly in your codebase\n3. **Type Safety**: Use TypeScript for type-safe props and state\n4. **Validation**: Use Zod schemas for form validation\n5. **Styling**: Leverage Tailwind utilities and CSS variables\n6. **Consistency**: Use the same component patterns across your app\n7. **Testing**: Components are testable with React Testing Library\n8. **Performance**: Components are optimized and tree-shakeable\n\n## Common Component Combinations\n\n### Login Form\n\n```tsx\n<Card className=\"w-[350px]\">\n  <CardHeader>\n    <CardTitle>Login</CardTitle>\n    <CardDescription>Enter your credentials to continue</CardDescription>\n  </CardHeader>\n  <CardContent>\n    <Form {...form}>\n      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-4\">\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"email\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Email</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"you@example.com\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n        <FormField\n          control={form.control}\n          name=\"password\"\n          render={({ field }) => (\n            <FormItem>\n              <FormLabel>Password</FormLabel>\n              <FormControl>\n                <Input type=\"password\" {...field} />\n              </FormControl>\n              <FormMessage />\n            </FormItem>\n          )}\n        />\n        <Button type=\"submit\" className=\"w-full\">Login</Button>\n      </form>\n    </Form>\n  </CardContent>\n</Card>\n```\n\n## References\n\n- Official Docs: https://ui.shadcn.com\n- Radix UI: https://www.radix-ui.com\n- React Hook Form: https://react-hook-form.com\n- Zod: https://zod.dev\n- Tailwind CSS: https://tailwindcss.com\n- Examples: https://ui.shadcn.com/examples\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:39:33.794Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing customizable and accessible UI components with shadcn/ui, Radix UI, and Tailwind CSS.","zh":"非常适合需要可定制和可访问的UI组件的前端代理，支持shadcn/ui、Radix UI和Tailwind CSS。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントに最適で、カスタマイズ可能でアクセス可能なUIコンポーネントが必要です。shadcn/ui、Radix UI、Tailwind CSSをサポートしています。","ko":"사용자 지정 가능한 UI 구성 요소와 접근 가능한 사용자 인터페이스 구성 요소가 필요한 프런트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다. shadcn/ui, Radix UI 및 Tailwind CSS를 지원합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizables y accesibles con shadcn/ui, Radix UI y Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin de composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisables et accessibles avec shadcn/ui, Radix UI et Tailwind CSS.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die anpassbare und zugängliche Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit shadcn/ui, Radix UI und Tailwind CSS benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de componentes de UI personalizáveis e acessíveis com shadcn/ui, Radix UI e Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым необходимы настраиваемые и доступные компоненты пользовательского интерфейса с shadcn/ui, Radix UI и Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتعديل والقابلة للوصول مع shadcn/ui و Radix UI و Tailwind CSS."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build responsive and validated forms using shadcn/ui''s Core Components, such as Button, Input & Form Fields, and Forms with Validation, all while leveraging the styling capabilities of Tailwind CSS.","zh":"赋予代理构建响应式和验证表单的能力，使用shadcn/ui的核心组件，如按钮、输入和表单字段，以及带有验证的表单，同时利用Tailwind CSS的样式能力。","ja":"shadcn/uiのコアコンポーネント（例：ボタン、入力およびフォームフィールド、バリデーション付きフォーム）を使用して、エージェントがレスポンシブで検証されたフォームを構築できるようにし、Tailwind CSSのスタイリング機能を活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 반응형 및 유효성 검사된 양식을 생성할 수 있도록 하며, shadcn/ui의 핵심 구성 요소(예: 버튼, 입력 및 양식 필드, 유효성 검사 양식)를 사용하여 Tailwind CSS의 스타일링 기능을 활용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear formularios responsivos y validados utilizando los Componentes principales de shadcn/ui, como Botón, Entrada y Campos de formulario, y Formularios con validación, aprovechando al mismo tiempo las capacidades de estilo de Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des formulaires responsifs et validés en utilisant les Composants principaux de shadcn/ui, tels que Bouton, Entrée et Champs de formulaire, et Formulaires avec validation, tout en exploitant les capacités de style de Tailwind CSS.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, responsive und valide Formulare zu erstellen, indem sie die Kernkomponenten von shadcn/ui, wie Schaltfläche, Eingabe und Formularfelder sowie Formulare mit Validierung, verwenden und gleichzeitig die Styling-Fähigkeiten von Tailwind CSS nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir formulários responsivos e validados usando os Componentes Principais do shadcn/ui, como Botão, Entrada e Campos de Formulário e Formulários com Validação, aproveitando ao mesmo tempo as capacidades de estilização do Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать адаптивные и проверенные формы с помощью основных компонентов shadcn/ui, таких как Кнопка, Ввод и поля формы и формы с проверкой, одновременно используя возможности стилизации Tailwind CSS.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من إنشاء استمارات مستجيبة ومدققة باستخدام المكونات الأساسية ل shadcn/ui، مثل الزر وادخال وحقول الاستمارة والاستمارات مع التحقق، مع الاستفادة من قدرات التنسيق في Tailwind CSS في نفس الوقت."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating customizable UI components with shadcn/ui","Creating accessible forms with validation using Radix UI and Tailwind CSS","Building responsive card layouts with shadcn/ui''s Core Components"],"zh":["使用shadcn/ui生成可定制的UI组件","使用Radix UI和Tailwind CSS创建带有验证的可访问表单","使用shadcn/ui的核心组件构建响应式卡片布局"],"ja":["shadcn/uiを使用してカスタマイズ可能なUIコンポーネントを生成する","Radix UIとTailwind CSSを使用して検証付きのアクセス可能なフォームを作成する","shadcn/uiのコアコンポーネントを使用してレスポンシブなカードレイアウトを構築する"],"ko":["shadcn/ui를 사용하여 사용자 지정 가능한 UI 구성 요소를 생성하는 것","Radix UI 및 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 유효성 검사된 접근 가능한 양식을 생성하는 것","shadcn/ui의 핵심 구성 요소를 사용하여 반응형 카드 레이아웃을 구축하는 것"],"es":["Generar componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizables con shadcn/ui","Crear formularios accesibles con validación usando Radix UI y Tailwind CSS","Crear diseños de tarjetas responsivos con los Componentes principales de shadcn/ui"],"fr":["Générer des composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisables avec shadcn/ui","Créer des formulaires accessibles avec validation en utilisant Radix UI et Tailwind CSS","Créer des dispositions de cartes responsives avec les Composants principaux de shadcn/ui"],"de":["Erstellen von anpassbaren Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit shadcn/ui","Erstellen von zugänglichen Formularen mit Validierung unter Verwendung von Radix UI und Tailwind CSS","Erstellen von responsiven Kartenlayouts mit den Kernkomponenten von shadcn/ui"],"pt":["Geração de componentes de UI personalizáveis com shadcn/ui","Criação de formulários acessíveis com validação usando Radix UI e Tailwind CSS","Construção de layouts de cartões responsivos com os Componentes Principais do shadcn/ui"],"ru":["Генерация настраиваемых компонентов пользовательского интерфейса с shadcn/ui","Создание доступных форм с проверкой с помощью Radix UI и Tailwind CSS","Построение адаптивных макетов карточек с помощью основных компонентов shadcn/ui"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتعديل مع shadcn/ui","إنشاء استمارات قابلة للوصول مع التحقق باستخدام Radix UI و Tailwind CSS","بناء تخطيطات بطاقات مستجيبة باستخدام المكونات الأساسية ل shadcn/ui"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires setup and configuration of shadcn/ui, Radix UI, and Tailwind CSS","Limited to building UI components with the specified libraries"],"zh":["需要设置和配置shadcn/ui、Radix UI和Tailwind CSS","仅限于使用指定的库构建UI组件"],"ja":["shadcn/ui、Radix UI、Tailwind CSSの設定と構成が必要","指定されたライブラリを使用してUIコンポーネントを構築することのみ"],"ko":["shadcn/ui, Radix UI 및 Tailwind CSS의 설정 및 구성이 필요","지정된 라이브러리를 사용하여 UI 구성 요소를 빌드하는 것만"],"es":["Requiere la configuración y el ajuste de shadcn/ui, Radix UI y Tailwind CSS","Limitado a la creación de componentes de interfaz de usuario con las bibliotecas especificadas"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration et la mise en place de shadcn/ui, Radix UI et Tailwind CSS","Limité à la création de composants d''interface utilisateur avec les bibliothèques spécifiées"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung und Konfiguration von shadcn/ui, Radix UI und Tailwind CSS","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit den angegebenen Bibliotheken"],"pt":["Requer configuração e instalação do shadcn/ui, Radix UI e Tailwind CSS","Limitado à construção de componentes de UI com as bibliotecas especificadas"],"ru":["Требует настройки и конфигурации shadcn/ui, Radix UI и Tailwind CSS","Ограничен построением компонентов пользовательского интерфейса только с помощью указанных библиотек"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد وتثبيت shadcn/ui و Radix UI و Tailwind CSS","محدود ببناء مكونات واجهة المستخدم مع المكتبات المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Khaledaun/Yalla-london/nextjs-best-practices', 'community', 'Khaledaun', 'Yalla-london', 'Khaledaun/Yalla-london', 'nextjs-best-practices', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z', '2026-02-18T07:40:24.505Z', NULL, '{"id":"Khaledaun/Yalla-london/nextjs-best-practices","name":"nextjs-best-practices","description":{"es":"Desarrolla aplicaciones de Next.js de manera efectiva con nuestros principios de diseño de App Router","fr":"Développez des applications Next.js de manière efficace avec nos principes de conception de App Router","de":"Entwickeln Sie Next.js-Anwendungen effektiv mit unseren Prinzipien für die App-Router-Entwicklung","pt":"As melhores práticas para desenvolver aplicações Next.js com o App Router. Aprenda sobre componentes de servidor e cliente.","ru":"Лучшие практики для разработки приложений Next.js с помощью App Router. Узнайте о компонентах сервера и клиента.","ar":"أفضل الممارسات لتطوير تطبيقات Next.js مع App Router. تعلم عن مكونات الخادم والعميل.","en":"yalla london website system"},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Prácticas recomendadas de Next.js","fr":"Meilleures pratiques Next.js","de":"Next.js-Best-Practices","pt":"Melhores Práticas Next.js","ru":"Лучшие практики Next.js","ar":"أفضل الممارسات ل Next.js","en":"nextjs-best-practices"},"description":{"es":"Desarrolla aplicaciones de Next.js de manera efectiva con nuestros principios de diseño de App Router","fr":"Développez des applications Next.js de manière efficace avec nos principes de conception de App Router","de":"Entwickeln Sie Next.js-Anwendungen effektiv mit unseren Prinzipien für die App-Router-Entwicklung","pt":"As melhores práticas para desenvolver aplicações Next.js com o App Router. Aprenda sobre componentes de servidor e cliente.","ru":"Лучшие практики для разработки приложений Next.js с помощью App Router. Узнайте о компонентах сервера и клиента.","ar":"أفضل الممارسات لتطوير تطبيقات Next.js مع App Router. تعلم عن مكونات الخادم والعميل.","en":"yalla london website system"},"definition":{"en":"yalla london website system"},"features":{"es":["Diseño de App Router","Componentes del servidor y del cliente","Uso de useState y useEffect","Manejo de eventos","Fecthing de datos directos"],"fr":["Conception de App Router","Composants serveur et client","Utilisation de useState et useEffect","Gestion d''événements","Fecthing de données directes"],"de":["App-Router-Entwicklung","Server- und Client-Komponenten","Verwendung von useState und useEffect","Ereignisbehandlung","Direktes Datenfetching"],"pt":["Componentes de servidor e cliente","Decisão de uso de componentes","Uso de useState e useEffect","Uso de event handlers","Fetch de dados direto","Layout e conteúdo estático"],"ru":["Компоненты сервера и клиента","Принятие решения об использовании компонентов","Использование useState и useEffect","Использование обработчиков событий","Прямая загрузка данных","Макет и статический контент"],"ar":["مكونات الخادم والعميل","قرار استخدام المكونات","استخدام useState و useEffect","استخدام معالجات الأحداث","استرجاع البيانات المباشر","التخطيط والمحتوى الثابت"]},"keywords":{"es":["Next.js","prácticas recomendadas","desarrollo de aplicaciones","App Router","componentes del servidor","componentes del cliente"],"fr":["Next.js","meilleures pratiques","développement d''applications","App Router","composants serveur","composants client"],"de":["Next.js","Best-Practices","Anwendungsentwicklung","App-Router","Server-Komponenten","Client-Komponenten"],"pt":["nextjs","melhores práticas","app router","componentes de servidor","componentes de cliente","desenvolvimento de aplicações","escalabilidade","eficiência","useState","useEffect"],"ru":["nextjs","лучшие практики","app router","компоненты сервера","компоненты клиента","разработка приложений","масштабируемость","эффективность","useState","useEffect"],"ar":["nextjs","أفضل الممارسات","app router","مكونات الخادم","مكونات العميل","تطوير التطبيقات","القابلية للتوسعة","الكفاءة","useState","useEffect"]}},"owner":"Khaledaun","repo":"Yalla-london","repoPath":"Khaledaun/Yalla-london","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nextjs-best-practices","description":"Next.js App Router principles. Server Components, data fetching, routing patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles for Next.js App Router development.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Server vs Client Components\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nDoes it need...?\n│\n├── useState, useEffect, event handlers\n│   └── Client Component (''use client'')\n│\n├── Direct data fetching, no interactivity\n│   └── Server Component (default)\n│\n└── Both? \n    └── Split: Server parent + Client child\n```\n\n### By Default\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| **Server** | Data fetching, layout, static content |\n| **Client** | Form","body":"# Next.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles for Next.js App Router development.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Server vs Client Components\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nDoes it need...?\n│\n├── useState, useEffect, event handlers\n│   └── Client Component (''use client'')\n│\n├── Direct data fetching, no interactivity\n│   └── Server Component (default)\n│\n└── Both? \n    └── Split: Server parent + Client child\n```\n\n### By Default\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| **Server** | Data fetching, layout, static content |\n| **Client** | Forms, buttons, interactive UI |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Fetching Patterns\n\n### Fetch Strategy\n\n| Pattern | Use |\n|---------|-----|\n| **Default** | Static (cached at build) |\n| **Revalidate** | ISR (time-based refresh) |\n| **No-store** | Dynamic (every request) |\n\n### Data Flow\n\n| Source | Pattern |\n|--------|---------|\n| Database | Server Component fetch |\n| API | fetch with caching |\n| User input | Client state + server action |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Routing Principles\n\n### File Conventions\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `page.tsx` | Route UI |\n| `layout.tsx` | Shared layout |\n| `loading.tsx` | Loading state |\n| `error.tsx` | Error boundary |\n| `not-found.tsx` | 404 page |\n\n### Route Organization\n\n| Pattern | Use |\n|---------|-----|\n| Route groups `(name)` | Organize without URL |\n| Parallel routes `@slot` | Multiple same-level pages |\n| Intercepting `(.)` | Modal overlays |\n\n---\n\n## 4. API Routes\n\n### Route Handlers\n\n| Method | Use |\n|--------|-----|\n| GET | Read data |\n| POST | Create data |\n| PUT/PATCH | Update data |\n| DELETE | Remove data |\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Validate input with Zod\n- Return proper status codes\n- Handle errors gracefully\n- Use Edge runtime when possible\n\n---\n\n## 5. Performance Principles\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n- Use next/image component\n- Set priority for above-fold\n- Provide blur placeholder\n- Use responsive sizes\n\n### Bundle Optimization\n\n- Dynamic imports for heavy components\n- Route-based code splitting (automatic)\n- Analyze with bundle analyzer\n\n---\n\n## 6. Metadata\n\n### Static vs Dynamic\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| Static export | Fixed metadata |\n| generateMetadata | Dynamic per-route |\n\n### Essential Tags\n\n- title (50-60 chars)\n- description (150-160 chars)\n- Open Graph images\n- Canonical URL\n\n---\n\n## 7. Caching Strategy\n\n### Cache Layers\n\n| Layer | Control |\n|-------|---------|\n| Request | fetch options |\n| Data | revalidate/tags |\n| Full route | route config |\n\n### Revalidation\n\n| Method | Use |\n|--------|-----|\n| Time-based | `revalidate: 60` |\n| On-demand | `revalidatePath/Tag` |\n| No cache | `no-store` |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Server Actions\n\n### Use Cases\n\n- Form submissions\n- Data mutations\n- Revalidation triggers\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Mark with ''use server''\n- Validate all inputs\n- Return typed responses\n- Handle errors\n\n---\n\n## 9. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| ''use client'' everywhere | Server by default |\n| Fetch in client components | Fetch in server |\n| Skip loading states | Use loading.tsx |\n| Ignore error boundaries | Use error.tsx |\n| Large client bundles | Dynamic imports |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Project Structure\n\n```\napp/\n├── (marketing)/     # Route group\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── (dashboard)/\n│   ├── layout.tsx   # Dashboard layout\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── api/\n│   └── [resource]/\n│       └── route.ts\n└── components/\n    └── ui/\n```\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Server Components are the default for a reason. Start there, add client only when needed.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:40:24.505Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing advanced Next.js app development with optimized App Router configuration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Next.js 应用开发和优化的 App Router 配置的全栈代理。","ja":"Next.js アプリの開発と最適化された App Router 構成が必要なフルスタック エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Next.js 애플리케이션 개발 및 최적화된 앱 라우터 구성이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full Stack que necesitan desarrollo de aplicaciones avanzadas de Next.js con configuración de App Router optimizada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack qui ont besoin d''un développement d''applications Next.js avancé avec une configuration de App Router optimisée.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine fortschrittliche Next.js-App-Entwicklung mit optimierter App-Router-Konfiguration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de desenvolvimento de aplicativos avançados Next.js com configuração de App Router otimizada.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Full Stack, которым необходимы продвинутые разработки приложений Next.js с оптимизированной конфигурацией App Router.","ar":"مثالي لعميل برامج完整 النطاق الذي يحتاج إلى تطوير تطبيقات متقدمة Next.js مع تكوين App Router محسّن."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop scalable Next.js applications by leveraging Server and Client Components, enabling efficient data fetching and interactivity using useState, useEffect, and event handlers, while optimizing for direct data fetching and layout rendering.","zh":"通过利用服务端和客户端组件，实现高效的数据获取和交互，使用 useState、useEffect 和事件处理程序，同时优化直接数据获取和布局渲染，从而使代理能够开发可扩展的 Next.js 应用程序。","ja":"Server Components と Client Components を活用して、useState、useEffect、イベントハンドラーを使用した効率的なデータ取得とインタラクティブ性を実現し、直接のデータ取得とレイアウトレンダリングを最適化することで、エージェントがスケーラブルな Next.js アプリケーションを開発できるようにします。","ko":"서버 컴포넌트와 클라이언트 컴포넌트를 활용하여 useState, useEffect 및 이벤트 핸들러를 사용한 효율적인 데이터 가져오기 및 상호 작용을 구현하고 직접 데이터 가져오기 및 레이아웃 렌더링을 최적화하여 에이전트가 확장 가능한 Next.js 애플리케이션을 개발할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar aplicaciones escalables de Next.js aprovechando los componentes del servidor y del cliente, lo que permite una recolección de datos eficiente y una interactividad mediante useState, useEffect y controladores de eventos, al tiempo que se optimiza para la recolección directa de datos y la representación de diseños.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des applications Next.js évolutives en exploitant les composants serveur et client, ce qui permet une récupération de données efficace et une interactivité à l''aide de useState, useEffect et des gestionnaires d''événements, tout en optimisant la récupération directe de données et le rendu de mise en page.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, skalierbare Next.js-Anwendungen zu entwickeln, indem Server- und Client-Komponenten genutzt werden, was eine effiziente Datenerfassung und Interaktivität mithilfe von useState, useEffect und Ereignishandlern ermöglicht, während gleichzeitig die direkte Datenerfassung und die Layoutrendition optimiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver aplicações escaláveis Next.js aproveitando os Componentes do Servidor e do Cliente, permitindo a obtenção eficiente de dados e interatividade usando useState, useEffect e manipuladores de eventos, ao mesmo tempo em que otimiza a obtenção direta de dados e renderização de layout.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разрабатывать масштабируемые приложения Next.js, используя Компоненты Сервера и Клиента, обеспечивая эффективную выборку данных и интерактивность с помощью useState, useEffect и обработчиков событий, а также оптимизируя прямую выборку данных и рендеринг макета.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من تطوير تطبيقات Next.js القابلة للتوسيع من خلال استخدام مكونات الخادم والعميل، وتمكين الحصول على البيانات بكفاءة والتفاعل باستخدام useState و useEffect ومعالجات الأحداث، مع تحسين الحصول المباشر على البيانات وتصيير التصميم في نفس الوقت."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing decision trees for Server vs Client Components","Optimizing data fetching for Next.js App Router","Splitting components for hybrid Server-Client functionality"],"zh":["为服务器组件和客户端组件实现决策树","优化 Next.js 应用路由器的数据获取","拆分组件以实现混合服务器-客户端功能"],"ja":["Server Components と Client Components のための決定木の実装","Next.js アプリケーション ルーターのデータ取得の最適化","ハイブリッド サーバー クライアント機能の実現のためのコンポーネントの分割"],"ko":["서버 컴포넌트와 클라이언트 컴포넌트를 위한 의사 결정 트리의 구현","Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터의 데이터 가져오기 최적화","하이브리드 서버-클라이언트 기능을 위한 컴포넌트 분할"],"es":["Implementar árboles de decisión para componentes del servidor frente a componentes del cliente","Optimizar la recolección de datos para el enrutador de aplicaciones de Next.js","Dividir componentes para funcionalidad híbrida del servidor y del cliente"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des arbres de décision pour les composants serveur par rapport aux composants client","Optimiser la récupération de données pour le routeur d''applications Next.js","Diviser les composants pour une fonctionnalité hybride serveur-client"],"de":["Implementierung von Entscheidungsbäumen für Server-Komponenten im Vergleich zu Client-Komponenten","Optimierung der Datenerfassung für den Next.js-App-Router","Aufteilung von Komponenten für hybride Server-Client-Funktionalität"],"pt":["Implementação de árvores de decisão para Componentes do Servidor vs Cliente","Otimização da obtenção de dados para Next.js App Router","Divisão de componentes para funcionalidade híbrida Servidor-Cliente"],"ru":["Реализация деревьев решений для Компонентов Сервера и Клиента","Оптимизация выборки данных для Next.js App Router","Разделение компонентов для гибридной функциональности Сервер-Клиент"],"ar":["تنفيذ أشجار القرار لمكونات الخادم مقابل العميل","تحسين الحصول على البيانات لتوجيه التطبيق Next.js","تقسيم المكونات لوظيفة هجينة للخادم والعميل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Next.js App Router principles","Limited to Next.js framework"],"zh":["需要了解 Next.js 应用路由器的原理","仅限 Next.js 框架"],"ja":["Next.js アプリケーション ルーターの原理の理解が必要","Next.js フレームワークのみに限定される"],"ko":["Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터의 원리를 이해해야 함","Next.js 프레임워크만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios del enrutador de aplicaciones de Next.js","Limitado al marco de Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes du routeur d''applications Next.js","Limité au cadre Next.js"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der Grundlagen des Next.js-App-Routers","Begrenzt auf das Next.js-Framework"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios do Next.js App Router","Limitado ao framework Next.js"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов Next.js App Router","Ограничен фреймворком Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ توجيه التطبيق Next.js","محدود بإطار العمل Next.js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('GrupoUS/gpus/nextjs-best-practices', 'community', 'GrupoUS', 'gpus', 'GrupoUS/gpus', 'nextjs-best-practices', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z', '2026-02-18T07:40:04.200Z', NULL, '{"id":"GrupoUS/gpus/nextjs-best-practices","name":"nextjs-best-practices","description":{"zh":"Next.js最佳实践指南，帮助开发者优化应用路由器开发","ja":"Next.jsのベストプラクティスを紹介します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션을 최적화하는 방법을 소개합니다","es":"Conoce las mejores prácticas para desarrollar aplicaciones Next.js con principios para el desarrollo de la App Router","fr":"Découvrez les meilleures pratiques pour développer des applications Next.js avec des principes pour le développement de l''App Router","de":"Erfahren Sie die besten Praktiken für die Entwicklung von Next.js-Anwendungen mit Grundsätzen für die Entwicklung der App Router","pt":"Princípios para desenvolvimento de roteadores de aplicações Next.js.","ru":"Принципы разработки маршрутизаторов приложений Next.js.","ar":"مبادئ لتطوير موجهات تطبيقات Next.js.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Next.js最佳实践指南","ja":"Next.jsベストプラクティス","ko":"Next.js 최적화 가이드","es":"Mejores prácticas para Next.js","fr":"Meilleures pratiques pour Next.js","de":"Best Practices für Next.js","pt":"Melhores Práticas Next.js","ru":"Лучшие практики Next.js","ar":"أفضل ممارسات Next.js","en":"nextjs-best-practices"},"description":{"zh":"Next.js最佳实践指南，帮助开发者优化应用路由器开发","ja":"Next.jsのベストプラクティスを紹介します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션을 최적화하는 방법을 소개합니다","es":"Conoce las mejores prácticas para desarrollar aplicaciones Next.js con principios para el desarrollo de la App Router","fr":"Découvrez les meilleures pratiques pour développer des applications Next.js avec des principes pour le développement de l''App Router","de":"Erfahren Sie die besten Praktiken für die Entwicklung von Next.js-Anwendungen mit Grundsätzen für die Entwicklung der App Router","pt":"Princípios para desenvolvimento de roteadores de aplicações Next.js.","ru":"Принципы разработки маршрутизаторов приложений Next.js.","ar":"مبادئ لتطوير موجهات تطبيقات Next.js.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["服务器组件与客户端组件的选择","数据获取和交互的优化","路由器开发的最佳实践","性能优化技巧"],"ja":["サーバーコンポーネントとクライアントコンポーネントの選択","データ取得とインタラクティブな最適化","ルーターの開発のベストプラクティス","パフォーマンス最適化テクニック"],"ko":["서버 컴포넌트와 클라이언트 컴포넌트 선택","데이터 가져오기 및 상호 작용 최적화","라우터 개발 최적화","성능 최적화 기술"],"es":["Diferenciación entre componentes del servidor y del cliente","Uso de useState, useEffect y controladores de eventos","Optimización del rendimiento con la App Router","Desarrollo de aplicaciones escalables y seguras","Uso de componentes de servidor para la fetching de datos","Uso de componentes de cliente para la interactividad"],"fr":["Différenciation entre les composants serveur et client","Utilisation de useState, useEffect et gestionnaires d''événements","Optimisation des performances avec l''App Router","Développement d''applications évolutives et sécurisées","Utilisation de composants serveur pour la récupération de données","Utilisation de composants client pour l''interactivité"],"de":["Unterscheidung zwischen Server- und Client-Komponenten","Verwendung von useState, useEffect und Ereignishandlern","Leistungsoptimierung mit der App Router","Entwicklung von skalierbaren und sicheren Anwendungen","Verwendung von Server-Komponenten für die Datenabfrage","Verwendung von Client-Komponenten für die Interaktivität"],"pt":["Separação de componentes servidor e cliente","Uso de useState e useEffect","Manipulação de eventos","Otimização de desempenho","Desenvolvimento de layouts estáticos"],"ru":["Разделение серверных и клиентских компонентов","Использование useState и useEffect","Обработка событий","Оптимизация производительности","Разработка статических макетов"],"ar":["فصل المكونات الخادم والعميل","استخدام useState و useEffect","تعامل الأحداث","تحسين الأداء","إنشاء تخطيطات ثابتة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js","最佳实践","应用路由器","服务器组件","客户端组件","性能优化"],"ja":["Next.js","ベストプラクティス","アプリケーションルーター","サーバーコンポーネント","クライアントコンポーネント","パフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["Next.js","최적화 가이드","애플리케이션 라우터","서버 컴포넌트","클라이언트 컴포넌트","성능 최적화"],"es":["Next.js","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de aplicaciones","App Router","componentes del servidor","componentes del cliente","rendimiento óptimo","escalabilidad","seguridad"],"fr":["Next.js","meilleures pratiques","développement d''applications","App Router","composants serveur","composants client","rendement optimal","évolution","sécurité"],"de":["Next.js","beste Praktiken","Anwendungsentwicklung","App Router","Server-Komponenten","Client-Komponenten","optimale Leistung","Skalierbarkeit","Sicherheit"],"pt":["Next.js","desenvolvimento web","roteadores de aplicações","componentes servidor","componentes cliente","otimização de desempenho","melhores práticas"],"ru":["Next.js","веб-разработка","маршрутизаторы приложений","серверные компоненты","клиентские компоненты","оптимизация производительности","лучшие практики"],"ar":["Next.js","تطوير الويب","موجهات التطبيقات","مكونات الخادم","مكونات العميل","تحسين الأداء","أفضل الممارسات"]}},"owner":"GrupoUS","repo":"gpus","repoPath":"GrupoUS/gpus","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nextjs-best-practices","description":"Next.js App Router principles. Server Components, data fetching, routing patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles for Next.js App Router development.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Server vs Client Components\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nDoes it need...?\n│\n├── useState, useEffect, event handlers\n│   └── Client Component (''use client'')\n│\n├── Direct data fetching, no interactivity\n│   └── Server Component (default)\n│\n└── Both? \n    └── Split: Server parent + Client child\n```\n\n### By Default\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| **Server** | Data fetching, layout, static content |\n| **Client** | Form","body":"# Next.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles for Next.js App Router development.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Server vs Client Components\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nDoes it need...?\n│\n├── useState, useEffect, event handlers\n│   └── Client Component (''use client'')\n│\n├── Direct data fetching, no interactivity\n│   └── Server Component (default)\n│\n└── Both? \n    └── Split: Server parent + Client child\n```\n\n### By Default\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| **Server** | Data fetching, layout, static content |\n| **Client** | Forms, buttons, interactive UI |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Fetching Patterns\n\n### Fetch Strategy\n\n| Pattern | Use |\n|---------|-----|\n| **Default** | Static (cached at build) |\n| **Revalidate** | ISR (time-based refresh) |\n| **No-store** | Dynamic (every request) |\n\n### Data Flow\n\n| Source | Pattern |\n|--------|---------|\n| Database | Server Component fetch |\n| API | fetch with caching |\n| User input | Client state + server action |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Routing Principles\n\n### File Conventions\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `page.tsx` | Route UI |\n| `layout.tsx` | Shared layout |\n| `loading.tsx` | Loading state |\n| `error.tsx` | Error boundary |\n| `not-found.tsx` | 404 page |\n\n### Route Organization\n\n| Pattern | Use |\n|---------|-----|\n| Route groups `(name)` | Organize without URL |\n| Parallel routes `@slot` | Multiple same-level pages |\n| Intercepting `(.)` | Modal overlays |\n\n---\n\n## 4. API Routes\n\n### Route Handlers\n\n| Method | Use |\n|--------|-----|\n| GET | Read data |\n| POST | Create data |\n| PUT/PATCH | Update data |\n| DELETE | Remove data |\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Validate input with Zod\n- Return proper status codes\n- Handle errors gracefully\n- Use Edge runtime when possible\n\n---\n\n## 5. Performance Principles\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n- Use next/image component\n- Set priority for above-fold\n- Provide blur placeholder\n- Use responsive sizes\n\n### Bundle Optimization\n\n- Dynamic imports for heavy components\n- Route-based code splitting (automatic)\n- Analyze with bundle analyzer\n\n---\n\n## 6. Metadata\n\n### Static vs Dynamic\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| Static export | Fixed metadata |\n| generateMetadata | Dynamic per-route |\n\n### Essential Tags\n\n- title (50-60 chars)\n- description (150-160 chars)\n- Open Graph images\n- Canonical URL\n\n---\n\n## 7. Caching Strategy\n\n### Cache Layers\n\n| Layer | Control |\n|-------|---------|\n| Request | fetch options |\n| Data | revalidate/tags |\n| Full route | route config |\n\n### Revalidation\n\n| Method | Use |\n|--------|-----|\n| Time-based | `revalidate: 60` |\n| On-demand | `revalidatePath/Tag` |\n| No cache | `no-store` |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Server Actions\n\n### Use Cases\n\n- Form submissions\n- Data mutations\n- Revalidation triggers\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Mark with ''use server''\n- Validate all inputs\n- Return typed responses\n- Handle errors\n\n---\n\n## 9. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| ''use client'' everywhere | Server by default |\n| Fetch in client components | Fetch in server |\n| Skip loading states | Use loading.tsx |\n| Ignore error boundaries | Use error.tsx |\n| Large client bundles | Dynamic imports |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Project Structure\n\n```\napp/\n├── (marketing)/     # Route group\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── (dashboard)/\n│   ├── layout.tsx   # Dashboard layout\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── api/\n│   └── [resource]/\n│       └── route.ts\n└── components/\n    └── ui/\n```\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Server Components are the default for a reason. Start there, add client only when needed.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:40:04.200Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing optimized Next.js application development with Server and Client Components.","zh":"非常适合需要优化 Next.js 应用程序开发的全栈代理，包括服务器和客户端组件。","ja":"Next.js アプリケーション開発を最適化する必要があるフルスタック エージェントに最適です。サーバーとクライアントのコンポーネントが含まれます。","ko":"서버 및 클라이언트 컴포넌트를 사용하는 Next.js 애플리케이션 개발을 최적화해야 하는 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full Stack que necesitan un desarrollo de aplicaciones optimizadas de Next.js con componentes de servidor y cliente.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin d''un développement d''applications Next.js optimisé avec des composants serveur et client.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die optimierte Next.js-Anwendungsentwicklung mit Server- und Client-Komponenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de desenvolvimento de aplicativos Next.js otimizados com Componentes de Servidor e Cliente.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Full Stack, которым необходим оптимизированный разработка приложений Next.js с компонентами сервера и клиента.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الخدمة الكاملة الذين يحتاجون إلى تطبيق تطبيقات Next.js المُختبر مع مكونات الخادم والعميل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop scalable Next.js applications using App Router, with best practices for Server vs Client Components, direct data fetching, and interactivity using useState, useEffect, and event handlers.","zh":"赋予代理开发人员使用 App Router 创建可扩展的 Next.js 应用程序的能力，包括有关服务器与客户端组件、直接数据获取、使用 useState、useEffect 和事件处理程序的交互性的最佳实践。","ja":"App Router を使用して拡張可能な Next.js アプリケーションを作成するエージェントをEmpowerします。サーバーコンポーネントとクライアントコンポーネント、直接データ取得、および useState、useEffect、およびイベントハンドラーを使用したインタラクティブ性のベストプラクティスが含まれます。","ko":"에이전트가 App Router를 사용하여 확장 가능한 Next.js 애플리케이션을 개발할 수 있도록 합니다. 서버 컴포넌트와 클라이언트 컴포넌트, 직접 데이터 가져오기, useState, useEffect, 이벤트 핸들러를 사용한 상호 작용에 대한 모범 사례가 포함됩니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar aplicaciones escalables de Next.js utilizando App Router, con las mejores prácticas para componentes de servidor frente a componentes de cliente, obtención directa de datos y interactividad utilizando useState, useEffect y controladores de eventos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des applications Next.js évolutives en utilisant App Router, avec les meilleures pratiques pour les composants serveur par rapport aux composants client, la récupération directe de données et l''interactivité en utilisant useState, useEffect et gestionnaires d''événements.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare Next.js-Anwendungen mit App Router zu entwickeln, mit Best Practices für Server-Komponenten im Vergleich zu Client-Komponenten, direktes Datenabrufen und Interaktivität unter Verwendung von useState, useEffect und Ereignishandlern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver aplicações Next.js escaláveis usando App Router, com as melhores práticas para Componentes de Servidor vs Componentes de Cliente, busca de dados direta e interatividade usando useState, useEffect e manipuladores de eventos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разрабатывать масштабируемые приложения Next.js с использованием App Router, с лучшими практиками для компонентов сервера и клиента, прямой выборки данных и интерактивности с использованием useState, useEffect и обработчиков событий.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تطوير تطبيقات Next.js القابلة للتوسيع باستخدام App Router، مع أفضل الممارسات لمكونات الخادم مقابل مكونات العميل، واسترجاع البيانات المباشر والتفاعل باستخدام useState و useEffect ومعالجات الأحداث."},"useCases":{"en":["Splitting components into Server parents and Client children for optimal performance","Determining component type using decision trees for useState, useEffect, and event handlers","Implementing data fetching and layout with Server Components and forms with Client Components"],"zh":["将组件分为服务器父组件和客户端子组件以实现最佳性能","使用决策树确定组件类型，使用 useState、useEffect 和事件处理程序","使用服务器组件实现数据获取和布局，使用客户端组件实现表单"],"ja":["サーバー親コンポーネントとクライアントの子コンポーネントにコンポーネントを分割して最適なパフォーマンスを実現する","useState、useEffect、イベントハンドラーを使用するためのコンポーネントの種類を決定ツリーを使用して決定する","サーバーコンポーネントを使用してデータ取得とレイアウトを実装し、クライアントコンポーネントを使用してフォームを実装する"],"ko":["최적의 성능을 위해 컴포넌트를 서버 부모 컴포넌트와 클라이언트 자식 컴포넌트로 분할","useState, useEffect, 이벤트 핸들러를 사용하여 컴포넌트 유형을 결정 트리를 사용하여 결정","서버 컴포넌트를 사용하여 데이터 가져오기와 레이아웃을 구현하고 클라이언트 컴포넌트를 사용하여 폼을 구현"],"es":["Dividir componentes en padres de servidor y niños de cliente para un rendimiento óptimo","Determinar el tipo de componente utilizando árboles de decisión para useState, useEffect y controladores de eventos","Implementar la obtención de datos y el diseño con componentes de servidor y formularios con componentes de cliente"],"fr":["Diviser les composants en parents serveur et enfants client pour une performance optimale","Déterminer le type de composant en utilisant des arbres de décision pour useState, useEffect et gestionnaires d''événements","Mettre en œuvre la récupération de données et la disposition avec des composants serveur et des formulaires avec des composants client"],"de":["Komponenten in Server-Eltern und Client-Kinder aufteilen, um optimale Leistung zu erzielen","Den Komponententyp mithilfe von Entscheidungsbäumen für useState, useEffect und Ereignishandler bestimmen","Datenabruf und Layout mit Server-Komponenten und Formularen mit Client-Komponenten implementieren"],"pt":["Dividir componentes em pais Servidor e filhos Cliente para desempenho ótimo","Determinar tipo de componente usando árvores de decisão para useState, useEffect e manipuladores de eventos","Implementar busca de dados e layout com Componentes de Servidor e formulários com Componentes de Cliente"],"ru":["Разделить компоненты на родительские компоненты сервера и дочерние компоненты клиента для оптимальной производительности","Определить тип компонента с использованием деревьев решений для useState, useEffect и обработчиков событий","Реализовать выборку данных и макет с помощью компонентов сервера и форм с помощью компонентов клиента"],"ar":["تقسيم المكونات إلى آباء الخادم وأبناء العميل لتحقيق الأداء الأمثل","تحديد نوع المكون باستخدام أشجار القرار ل useState و useEffect ومعالجات الأحداث","تنفيذ استرجاع البيانات وتخطيط مع مكونات الخادم والاستمارات مع مكونات العميل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Next.js framework knowledge","Limited to Next.js App Router development"],"zh":["需要 Next.js 框架知识","仅限 Next.js App Router 开发"],"ja":["Next.js フレームワークの知識が必要","Next.js App Router の開発に限定される"],"ko":["Next.js 프레임워크 지식이 필요","Next.js App Router 개발에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del marco de trabajo Next.js","Limitado al desarrollo de App Router de Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances sur le framework Next.js","Limité au développement d''App Router de Next.js"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse des Next.js-Frameworks","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Next.js App Router"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento do framework Next.js","Limitado ao desenvolvimento do App Router Next.js"],"ru":["Требует знания фреймворка Next.js","Ограничен разработкой App Router Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة إطار العمل Next.js","محدود بتطوير App Router Next.js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('markus41/Demo-0.2/harness-ci', 'community', 'markus41', 'Demo-0.2', 'markus41/Demo-0.2', 'harness-ci', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z', '2026-02-18T07:40:13.948Z', NULL, '{"id":"markus41/Demo-0.2/harness-ci","name":"harness-ci","description":{"zh":"Harness CI技能提供了容器原生构建、测试智能、缓存和构建基础设施管理功能","ja":"Harness CIスキルは、コンテナネイティブビルド、テストインテリジェンス、キャッシング、ビルドインフラストラクチャ管理機能を提供します","ko":"Harness CI 스킬은 컨테이너 네이티브 빌드, 테스트 인텔리전스, 캐싱 및 빌드 인프라스트럭처 관리 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Harness CI es una solución de integración continua para builds nativos de contenedores con inteligencia de pruebas, caching y gestión de infraestructura de compilación","fr":"Harness CI est une solution d''intégration continue pour les builds natifs de conteneurs avec intelligence de test, caching et gestion d''infrastructure de build","de":"Harness CI ist eine Lösung für kontinuierliche Integration für container-native Builds mit Testintelligenz, Caching und Build-Infrastruktur-Management","pt":"O Harness CI é uma ferramenta de integração contínua para builds nativa de contêiner, oferecendo inteligência de teste, caching e gerenciamento de infraestrutura de build. Ele ajuda a melhorar a eficiência das pipelines de desenvolvimento.","ru":"Harness CI — это инструмент непрерывной интеграции для контейнерных сборок, предлагающий тестовую интеллект, кэширование и управление инфраструктурой сборки. Он помогает повысить эффективность конвейеров разработки.","ar":"Harness CI هو أداة دمج مستمر لبيئات حاويات الأعمال، تقدم ذكاء الاختبار والتفريغ وإدارة بنية تحتية البناء. يساعد على تحسين كفاءة خطوط أنابيب التطوير.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Harness CI技能：持续集成和测试智能","ja":"Harness CIスキル：コンテナネイティブビルドとテストインテリジェンス","ko":"Harness CI 스킬: 컨테이너 네이티브 빌드와 테스트 인텔리전스","es":"Harness CI: Integración Continua para Desarrolladores","fr":"Harness CI : Intégration Continue pour les Développeurs","de":"Harness CI: Kontinuierliche Integration für Entwickler","pt":"Harness CI: Integração Contínua para Builds Nativa de Con...","ru":"Harness CI: непрерывная интеграция для контейнерных сборок","ar":"Harness CI: دمج مستمر لبيئات حاويات الأعمال","en":"harness-ci"},"description":{"zh":"Harness CI技能提供了容器原生构建、测试智能、缓存和构建基础设施管理功能","ja":"Harness CIスキルは、コンテナネイティブビルド、テストインテリジェンス、キャッシング、ビルドインフラストラクチャ管理機能を提供します","ko":"Harness CI 스킬은 컨테이너 네이티브 빌드, 테스트 인텔리전스, 캐싱 및 빌드 인프라스트럭처 관리 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Harness CI es una solución de integración continua para builds nativos de contenedores con inteligencia de pruebas, caching y gestión de infraestructura de c...","fr":"Harness CI est une solution d''intégration continue pour les builds natifs de conteneurs avec intelligence de test, caching et gestion d''infrastructure de build","de":"Harness CI ist eine Lösung für kontinuierliche Integration für container-native Builds mit Testintelligenz, Caching und Build-Infrastruktur-Management","pt":"O Harness CI é uma ferramenta de integração contínua para builds nativa de contêiner, oferecendo inteligência de teste, caching e gerenciamento de infraestru...","ru":"Harness CI — это инструмент непрерывной интеграции для контейнерных сборок, предлагающий тестовую интеллект, кэширование и управление инфраструктурой сборки....","ar":"Harness CI هو أداة دمج مستمر لبيئات حاويات الأعمال، تقدم ذكاء الاختبار والتفريغ وإدارة بنية تحتية البناء. يساعد على تحسين كفاءة خطوط أنابيب التطوير.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["容器原生构建","测试智能","缓存策略","构建基础设施管理","并行执行","Kubernetes和Harness Cloud集成"],"ja":["コンテナネイティブビルド","テストインテリジェンス","キャッシング戦略","ビルドインフラストラクチャ管理","並列実行","KubernetesとHarness Cloudの統合"],"ko":["컨테이너 네이티브 빌드","테스트 인텔리전스","캐싱 전략","빌드 인프라스트럭처 관리","병렬 실행","Kubernetes와 Harness Cloud 통합"],"es":["Integración continua para builds de contenedores","Inteligencia de pruebas para una ejecución de pruebas más rápida","Caching y gestión de infraestructura de compilación","Compatibilidad con Kubernetes, Harness Cloud y VMs","Ejecución paralela de pasos de compilación"],"fr":["Intégration continue pour les builds de conteneurs","Intelligence de test pour une exécution de test plus rapide","Caching et gestion d''infrastructure de build","Compatibilité avec Kubernetes, Harness Cloud et VMs","Exécution parallèle des étapes de build"],"de":["Kontinuierliche Integration für container-native Builds","Testintelligenz für eine schnellere Testausführung","Caching und Build-Infrastruktur-Management","Kompatibilität mit Kubernetes, Harness Cloud und VMs","Parallele Ausführung von Build-Schritten"],"pt":["Integração contínua para builds nativa de contêiner","Inteligência de teste para execução de testes mais rápidos","Caching para reduzir o tempo de build","Gerenciamento de infraestrutura de build","Suporte a Kubernetes, Harness Cloud e VMs"],"ru":["Непрерывная интеграция для контейнерных сборок","Тестовая интеллект для более быстрой выполнения тестов","Кэширование для уменьшения времени сборки","Управление инфраструктурой сборки","Поддержка Kubernetes, Harness Cloud и VMs"],"ar":["دمج مستمر لبيئات حاويات الأعمال","ذكاء الاختبار لتنفيذ الاختبارات بشكل أسرع","التفريغ لتحسين وقت البناء","إدارة بنية تحتية البناء","دعم Kubernetes و Harness Cloud و VMs"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Harness CI","持续集成","测试智能","容器原生构建","缓存策略","构建基础设施管理","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","DevOps"],"ja":["Harness CI","継続的インテグレーション","テストインテリジェンス","コンテナネイティブビルド","キャッシング戦略","ビルドインフラストラクチャ管理","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","DevOps"],"ko":["Harness CI","지속적 통합","테스트 인텔리전스","컨테이너 네이티브 빌드","캐싱 전략","빌드 인프라스트럭처 관리","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","DevOps"],"es":["integración continua","builds de contenedores","inteligencia de pruebas","caching","gestión de infraestructura de compilación","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["intégration continue","builds de conteneurs","intelligence de test","caching","gestion d''infrastructure de build","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs","développement de logiciels"],"de":["kontinuierliche Integration","container-native Builds","Testintelligenz","Caching","Build-Infrastruktur-Management","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Harness CI","integração contínua","builds nativa de contêiner","inteligência de teste","caching","gerenciamento de infraestrutura de build","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs"],"ru":["Harness CI","непрерывная интеграция","контейнерные сборки","тестовая интеллект","кэширование","управление инфраструктурой сборки","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs"],"ar":["Harness CI","دمج مستمر","بيئات حاويات الأعمال","ذكاء الاختبار","التفريغ","إدارة بنية تحتية البناء","Kubernetes","Harness Cloud","VMs"]}},"owner":"markus41","repo":"Demo-0.2","repoPath":"markus41/Demo-0.2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"harness-ci","description":"Harness CI (Continuous Integration) for container-native builds, test intelligence, caching, parallelization, and build infrastructure management. Activate for build pipelines, CI steps, test automation, artifact publishing, and build optimization.","bodyPreview":"# Harness CI Skill\n\nComprehensive Harness CI (Continuous Integration) for container-native builds with test intelligence, caching, and build infrastructure management.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Creating or managing Harness CI pipelines\n- Configuring build steps (Run, RunTests, BuildAndPush)\n- Setting up test intelligence for faster test execution\n- Configuring caching strategies (S3, GCS)\n- Managing build infrastructure (Kubernetes, Harness Cloud, VMs)\n- Parallelizi","body":"# Harness CI Skill\n\nComprehensive Harness CI (Continuous Integration) for container-native builds with test intelligence, caching, and build infrastructure management.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Creating or managing Harness CI pipelines\n- Configuring build steps (Run, RunTests, BuildAndPush)\n- Setting up test intelligence for faster test execution\n- Configuring caching strategies (S3, GCS)\n- Managing build infrastructure (Kubernetes, Harness Cloud, VMs)\n- Parallelizing builds with matrix strategies\n- Publishing artifacts and container images\n- Integrating with code repositories\n- Troubleshooting build failures\n\n## Build Infrastructure Types\n\n### Harness Cloud (Recommended)\n\nZero-configuration hosted build infrastructure:\n\n```yaml\ninfrastructure:\n  type: Cloud\n  spec:\n    os: Linux  # Linux, MacOS, or Windows\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- No setup required\n- Auto-scaling\n- Pre-installed tools\n- Managed updates\n\n### Kubernetes Infrastructure\n\nSelf-hosted on your K8s cluster:\n\n```yaml\ninfrastructure:\n  type: KubernetesDirect\n  spec:\n    connectorRef: k8s_connector\n    namespace: harness-builds\n    automountServiceAccountToken: true\n    nodeSelector:\n      kubernetes.io/os: linux\n    tolerations:\n      - key: \"dedicated\"\n        operator: \"Equal\"\n        value: \"ci\"\n        effect: \"NoSchedule\"\n    harnessImageConnectorRef: docker_connector\n    os: Linux\n```\n\n### VM Infrastructure\n\nAWS, Azure, or GCP VMs:\n\n```yaml\ninfrastructure:\n  type: VM\n  spec:\n    type: Pool\n    spec:\n      poolName: linux-pool\n      os: Linux\n```\n\n## CI Pipeline Structure\n\n### Basic Pipeline\n\n```yaml\npipeline:\n  name: Build Pipeline\n  identifier: build_pipeline\n  projectIdentifier: my_project\n  orgIdentifier: default\n  properties:\n    ci:\n      codebase:\n        connectorRef: harness_code\n        repoName: my-service\n        build: <+input>\n  stages:\n    - stage:\n        name: Build and Test\n        identifier: build_test\n        type: CI\n        spec:\n          cloneCodebase: true\n          infrastructure:\n            type: Cloud\n            spec:\n              os: Linux\n          execution:\n            steps:\n              - step:\n                  name: Install Dependencies\n                  identifier: install\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm ci\n              - step:\n                  name: Run Tests\n                  identifier: test\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm test -- --coverage\n                    reports:\n                      type: JUnit\n                      spec:\n                        paths:\n                          - \"junit.xml\"\n              - step:\n                  name: Build\n                  identifier: build\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm run build\n```\n\n## Step Types\n\n### Run Step\n\nExecute shell commands:\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Run Script\n    identifier: run_script\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector  # Optional for Harness Cloud\n      image: node:18-alpine           # Optional for Harness Cloud\n      shell: Sh  # Sh, Bash, Powershell, Pwsh, Python\n      command: |\n        echo \"Building application\"\n        npm ci\n        npm run build\n      envVariables:\n        NODE_ENV: production\n        API_URL: https://api.company.com\n      outputVariables:\n        - name: BUILD_VERSION\n      reports:\n        type: JUnit\n        spec:\n          paths:\n            - \"**/test-results/*.xml\"\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 2Gi\n          cpu: \"1\"\n```\n\n### Run Tests Step (Test Intelligence)\n\nRun tests with intelligent test selection:\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Run Tests with TI\n    identifier: run_tests_ti\n    type: RunTests\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      image: maven:3.8-openjdk-17\n      language: Java  # Java, Kotlin, Scala, CSharp, Python, Ruby\n      buildTool: Maven  # Maven, Gradle, Bazel, SBT, Nunit, Pytest, Unittest, Rspec\n      args: test\n      packages: com.myapp\n      runOnlySelectedTests: true  # Enable Test Intelligence\n      testAnnotations: org.junit.Test\n      preCommand: |\n        echo \"Setting up test environment\"\n      postCommand: |\n        echo \"Test cleanup\"\n      reports:\n        type: JUnit\n        spec:\n          paths:\n            - \"**/surefire-reports/*.xml\"\n      enableTestSplitting: true  # For parallel execution\n```\n\n### Build and Push Docker\n\nBuild and push container images:\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Build and Push\n    identifier: build_push\n    type: BuildAndPushDockerRegistry\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      repo: myorg/myapp\n      tags:\n        - <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n        - <+codebase.shortCommitSha>\n        - latest\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile\n      context: .\n      optimize: true  # Harness build optimization\n      caching: true   # Layer caching\n      buildArgs:\n        VERSION: <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n        BUILD_DATE: <+pipeline.startTs>\n      labels:\n        maintainer: team@company.com\n        commit: <+codebase.commitSha>\n      target: production  # Multi-stage target\n      remoteCacheRepo: myorg/myapp-cache  # Remote cache\n```\n\n### Build and Push to ECR\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Build and Push ECR\n    identifier: build_push_ecr\n    type: BuildAndPushECR\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: aws_connector\n      region: us-east-1\n      account: \"123456789012\"\n      imageName: myapp\n      tags:\n        - <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile\n      caching: true\n```\n\n### Build and Push to GCR\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Build and Push GCR\n    identifier: build_push_gcr\n    type: BuildAndPushGCR\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: gcp_connector\n      host: gcr.io\n      projectID: my-gcp-project\n      imageName: myapp\n      tags:\n        - <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile\n      caching: true\n```\n\n### Build and Push to ACR\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Build and Push ACR\n    identifier: build_push_acr\n    type: BuildAndPushACR\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: azure_connector\n      repository: myacr.azurecr.io/myapp\n      tags:\n        - <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile\n      caching: true\n```\n\n## Caching Strategies\n\n### S3 Cache\n\n```yaml\n# Save cache\n- step:\n    name: Save Cache\n    identifier: save_cache\n    type: SaveCacheS3\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: aws_connector\n      region: us-east-1\n      bucket: harness-cache\n      key: node-modules-{{ checksum \"package-lock.json\" }}\n      sourcePaths:\n        - node_modules\n      archiveFormat: Tar\n\n# Restore cache\n- step:\n    name: Restore Cache\n    identifier: restore_cache\n    type: RestoreCacheS3\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: aws_connector\n      region: us-east-1\n      bucket: harness-cache\n      key: node-modules-{{ checksum \"package-lock.json\" }}\n      archiveFormat: Tar\n      failIfKeyNotFound: false\n```\n\n### GCS Cache\n\n```yaml\n# Save cache\n- step:\n    name: Save Cache\n    identifier: save_cache\n    type: SaveCacheGCS\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: gcp_connector\n      bucket: harness-cache\n      key: maven-{{ checksum \"pom.xml\" }}\n      sourcePaths:\n        - ~/.m2/repository\n      archiveFormat: Tar\n\n# Restore cache\n- step:\n    name: Restore Cache\n    identifier: restore_cache\n    type: RestoreCacheGCS\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: gcp_connector\n      bucket: harness-cache\n      key: maven-{{ checksum \"pom.xml\" }}\n      archiveFormat: Tar\n      failIfKeyNotFound: false\n```\n\n### Harness Cache Intelligence\n\n```yaml\n# Automatic caching based on build tool detection\n- step:\n    name: Build with Cache\n    identifier: build\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        npm ci\n        npm run build\n      caching:\n        enabled: true\n        key: npm-<+codebase.branch>\n        paths:\n          - node_modules\n```\n\n## Parallelism and Matrix\n\n### Matrix Strategy\n\nRun steps with multiple configurations:\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Test Matrix\n    identifier: test_matrix\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        echo \"Testing on Node $NODE_VERSION with $DB_TYPE\"\n        npm test\n      envVariables:\n        NODE_VERSION: <+matrix.nodeVersion>\n        DB_TYPE: <+matrix.database>\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        nodeVersion:\n          - \"16\"\n          - \"18\"\n          - \"20\"\n        database:\n          - postgres\n          - mysql\n        exclude:\n          - nodeVersion: \"16\"\n            database: mysql\n      maxConcurrency: 4\n```\n\n### Parallelism\n\nRun same step multiple times in parallel:\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Parallel Tests\n    identifier: parallel_tests\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        npm test -- --shard=$HARNESS_STAGE_INDEX/$HARNESS_STAGE_TOTAL\n    strategy:\n      parallelism: 4\n```\n\n### Step Groups for Parallelism\n\n```yaml\n- stepGroup:\n    name: Parallel Build\n    identifier: parallel_build\n    steps:\n      - parallel:\n          - step:\n              name: Build Frontend\n              identifier: build_frontend\n              type: Run\n              spec:\n                command: npm run build:frontend\n          - step:\n              name: Build Backend\n              identifier: build_backend\n              type: Run\n              spec:\n                command: npm run build:backend\n          - step:\n              name: Build Docs\n              identifier: build_docs\n              type: Run\n              spec:\n                command: npm run build:docs\n```\n\n## Background Services\n\nStart services for integration tests:\n\n```yaml\n# Database service\n- step:\n    name: Start PostgreSQL\n    identifier: postgres\n    type: Background\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      image: postgres:14\n      shell: Sh\n      envVariables:\n        POSTGRES_USER: test\n        POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test\n        POSTGRES_DB: testdb\n      portBindings:\n        \"5432\": \"5432\"\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 1Gi\n\n# Redis service\n- step:\n    name: Start Redis\n    identifier: redis\n    type: Background\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      image: redis:7-alpine\n      portBindings:\n        \"6379\": \"6379\"\n\n# Wait for services\n- step:\n    name: Wait for Services\n    identifier: wait\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        # Wait for PostgreSQL\n        until pg_isready -h localhost -p 5432; do\n          sleep 1\n        done\n\n        # Wait for Redis\n        until redis-cli -h localhost ping; do\n          sleep 1\n        done\n```\n\n## Test Intelligence\n\n### Configuration\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Run Tests with TI\n    identifier: test_ti\n    type: RunTests\n    spec:\n      language: Java\n      buildTool: Maven\n      runOnlySelectedTests: true  # Enable TI\n      testGlobs: \"**/test/**/*.java\"\n      testAnnotations: org.junit.Test, org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\n      packages: com.mycompany\n      args: test -Dmaven.test.failure.ignore=true\n      reports:\n        type: JUnit\n        spec:\n          paths:\n            - \"**/surefire-reports/*.xml\"\n```\n\n### Supported Languages\n\n| Language | Build Tools |\n|----------|-------------|\n| **Java** | Maven, Gradle, Bazel |\n| **Kotlin** | Maven, Gradle, Bazel |\n| **Scala** | Maven, Gradle, Bazel, SBT |\n| **C#** | NUnit, dotnet |\n| **Python** | Pytest, Unittest |\n| **Ruby** | RSpec |\n\n### Test Splitting\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Parallel Tests\n    identifier: parallel_tests\n    type: RunTests\n    spec:\n      language: Python\n      buildTool: Pytest\n      runOnlySelectedTests: true\n      enableTestSplitting: true  # Split across parallel instances\n      testSplitStrategy: ClassTiming  # or TestCount\n      args: --junitxml=report.xml\n    strategy:\n      parallelism: 4  # Run 4 parallel test containers\n```\n\n## Plugins\n\n### Harness Plugins\n\n```yaml\n# Slack notification\n- step:\n    name: Notify Slack\n    identifier: slack\n    type: Plugin\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      image: plugins/slack\n      settings:\n        webhook: <+secrets.getValue(\"slack_webhook\")>\n        channel: builds\n        template: |\n          Build {{#success build.status}}succeeded{{else}}failed{{/success}}\n          Repository: {{repo.name}}\n          Branch: {{build.branch}}\n          Commit: {{build.commit}}\n\n# Upload to S3\n- step:\n    name: Upload Artifacts\n    identifier: upload_s3\n    type: Plugin\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: docker_connector\n      image: plugins/s3\n      settings:\n        bucket: build-artifacts\n        region: us-east-1\n        access_key: <+secrets.getValue(\"aws_access_key\")>\n        secret_key: <+secrets.getValue(\"aws_secret_key\")>\n        source: dist/**/*\n        target: builds/<+pipeline.sequenceId>\n```\n\n### GitHub Actions\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: GitHub Action\n    identifier: github_action\n    type: Action\n    spec:\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n      with:\n        node-version: \"18\"\n        cache: npm\n```\n\n### Bitrise Steps\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Bitrise Step\n    identifier: bitrise\n    type: Bitrise\n    spec:\n      uses: script@1\n      with:\n        content: |\n          echo \"Running Bitrise step\"\n```\n\n## Artifact Management\n\n### Upload Artifacts\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Upload Artifact\n    identifier: upload_artifact\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        tar -czf dist.tar.gz dist/\n      outputVariables:\n        - name: ARTIFACT_PATH\n          type: String\n          value: dist.tar.gz\n```\n\n### GCS Artifacts\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Upload to GCS\n    identifier: upload_gcs\n    type: GCSUpload\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: gcp_connector\n      bucket: build-artifacts\n      sourcePath: dist/\n      target: builds/<+pipeline.sequenceId>/\n```\n\n### S3 Artifacts\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Upload to S3\n    identifier: upload_s3\n    type: S3Upload\n    spec:\n      connectorRef: aws_connector\n      region: us-east-1\n      bucket: build-artifacts\n      sourcePath: dist/\n      target: builds/<+pipeline.sequenceId>/\n```\n\n## CI Expressions\n\n| Expression | Description |\n|------------|-------------|\n| `<+codebase.branch>` | Git branch name |\n| `<+codebase.tag>` | Git tag (if tagged) |\n| `<+codebase.commitSha>` | Full commit SHA |\n| `<+codebase.shortCommitSha>` | Short commit SHA (7 chars) |\n| `<+codebase.commitMessage>` | Commit message |\n| `<+codebase.commitRef>` | Commit reference |\n| `<+codebase.repoUrl>` | Repository URL |\n| `<+codebase.gitUserId>` | Git user ID |\n| `<+codebase.gitUserEmail>` | Git user email |\n| `<+codebase.sourceBranch>` | PR source branch |\n| `<+codebase.targetBranch>` | PR target branch |\n| `<+codebase.prNumber>` | Pull request number |\n| `<+codebase.prTitle>` | Pull request title |\n| `<+codebase.prBody>` | Pull request body |\n| `<+pipeline.sequenceId>` | Build number |\n| `<+pipeline.executionId>` | Execution UUID |\n| `<+pipeline.startTs>` | Start timestamp |\n\n## Triggers\n\n### Push Trigger\n\n```yaml\ntrigger:\n  name: Build on Push\n  identifier: build_on_push\n  enabled: true\n  pipelineIdentifier: build_pipeline\n  source:\n    type: Webhook\n    spec:\n      type: Harness\n      spec:\n        type: Push\n        spec:\n          connectorRef: harness_code\n          repoName: my-service\n          autoAbortPreviousExecutions: true\n          payloadConditions:\n            - key: targetBranch\n              operator: In\n              value:\n                - main\n                - develop\n```\n\n### Pull Request Trigger\n\n```yaml\ntrigger:\n  name: Build on PR\n  identifier: build_on_pr\n  enabled: true\n  pipelineIdentifier: build_pipeline\n  source:\n    type: Webhook\n    spec:\n      type: Harness\n      spec:\n        type: PullRequest\n        spec:\n          connectorRef: harness_code\n          repoName: my-service\n          autoAbortPreviousExecutions: true\n          actions:\n            - Open\n            - Reopen\n            - Synchronize\n          payloadConditions:\n            - key: targetBranch\n              operator: Equals\n              value: main\n```\n\n### Tag Trigger\n\n```yaml\ntrigger:\n  name: Build on Tag\n  identifier: build_on_tag\n  enabled: true\n  pipelineIdentifier: release_pipeline\n  source:\n    type: Webhook\n    spec:\n      type: Harness\n      spec:\n        type: Tag\n        spec:\n          connectorRef: harness_code\n          repoName: my-service\n          tagCondition:\n            operator: Regex\n            value: \"^v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+$\"\n```\n\n## Complete CI/CD Pipeline Example\n\n```yaml\npipeline:\n  name: Full CI/CD Pipeline\n  identifier: full_cicd\n  projectIdentifier: my_project\n  orgIdentifier: default\n  properties:\n    ci:\n      codebase:\n        connectorRef: harness_code\n        repoName: my-service\n        build: <+input>\n  stages:\n    # CI Stage\n    - stage:\n        name: Build and Test\n        identifier: build_test\n        type: CI\n        spec:\n          cloneCodebase: true\n          infrastructure:\n            type: Cloud\n            spec:\n              os: Linux\n          caching:\n            enabled: true\n            key: npm-<+codebase.branch>\n            paths:\n              - node_modules\n          execution:\n            steps:\n              - step:\n                  name: Install\n                  identifier: install\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm ci\n              - parallel:\n                  - step:\n                      name: Lint\n                      identifier: lint\n                      type: Run\n                      spec:\n                        shell: Sh\n                        command: npm run lint\n                  - step:\n                      name: Type Check\n                      identifier: typecheck\n                      type: Run\n                      spec:\n                        shell: Sh\n                        command: npm run typecheck\n              - step:\n                  name: Test\n                  identifier: test\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm test -- --coverage\n                    reports:\n                      type: JUnit\n                      spec:\n                        paths:\n                          - junit.xml\n              - step:\n                  name: Build\n                  identifier: build\n                  type: Run\n                  spec:\n                    shell: Sh\n                    command: npm run build\n              - step:\n                  name: Build and Push\n                  identifier: build_push\n                  type: BuildAndPushDockerRegistry\n                  spec:\n                    connectorRef: docker_connector\n                    repo: myorg/myapp\n                    tags:\n                      - <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n                      - <+codebase.shortCommitSha>\n                    caching: true\n                    optimize: true\n\n    # CD Stage\n    - stage:\n        name: Deploy to Dev\n        identifier: deploy_dev\n        type: Deployment\n        spec:\n          deploymentType: Kubernetes\n          service:\n            serviceRef: my_service\n            serviceInputs:\n              serviceDefinition:\n                type: Kubernetes\n                spec:\n                  artifacts:\n                    primary:\n                      primaryArtifactRef: docker_image\n                      sources:\n                        - identifier: docker_image\n                          type: DockerRegistry\n                          spec:\n                            tag: <+pipeline.sequenceId>\n          environment:\n            environmentRef: development\n            infrastructureDefinitions:\n              - identifier: dev_k8s\n          execution:\n            steps:\n              - step:\n                  name: Rolling Deployment\n                  identifier: rollingDeployment\n                  type: K8sRollingDeploy\n                  timeout: 10m\n                  spec:\n                    skipDryRun: false\n            rollbackSteps:\n              - step:\n                  name: Rollback\n                  identifier: rollback\n                  type: K8sRollingRollback\n                  timeout: 10m\n                  spec: {}\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n| Issue | Cause | Solution |\n|-------|-------|----------|\n| Build timeout | Long-running step | Increase timeout, optimize build |\n| Cache miss | Key mismatch | Check checksum file path |\n| Image pull failed | Auth issue | Verify connector credentials |\n| Test Intelligence not working | Missing config | Check language/buildTool settings |\n| Out of memory | Resource limits | Increase memory in step spec |\n\n### Debug Logging\n\n```yaml\n- step:\n    name: Debug Info\n    identifier: debug\n    type: Run\n    spec:\n      shell: Sh\n      command: |\n        echo \"=== Build Debug Info ===\"\n        echo \"Branch: <+codebase.branch>\"\n        echo \"Commit: <+codebase.commitSha>\"\n        echo \"PR: <+codebase.prNumber>\"\n        echo \"Build: <+pipeline.sequenceId>\"\n        echo \"=== Environment ===\"\n        env | sort\n        echo \"=== Disk Usage ===\"\n        df -h\n        echo \"=== Memory ===\"\n        free -m\n```\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [Harness CI Docs](https://developer.harness.io/docs/continuous-integration)\n- [Test Intelligence](https://developer.harness.io/docs/continuous-integration/use-ci/run-tests/ti-overview)\n- [Caching](https://developer.harness.io/docs/continuous-integration/use-ci/caching-ci-data/caching-overview)\n- [Build Infrastructure](https://developer.harness.io/docs/continuous-integration/use-ci/set-up-build-infrastructure)\n- [Harness Knowledge Base](../docs/HARNESS-KNOWLEDGE-BASE.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:40:13.948Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring advanced container-native build automation with test intelligence and caching strategies.","zh":"适用于需要高级容器原生构建自动化、测试智能和缓存策略的 DevOps Agent。","ja":"DevOps エージェントが高度なコンテナネイティブビルド自動化、テストインテリジェンス、およびキャッシング戦略を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 컨테이너 네이티브 빌드 자동화, 테스트 인텔리전스 및 캐싱 전략이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren una automatización de compilación avanzada nativa de contenedores con inteligencia de prueba y estrategias de caché.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant une automatisation de construction avancée native de conteneurs avec une intelligence de test et des stratégies de mise en cache.","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die eine erweiterte container-native Build-Automatisierung mit Testintelligenz und Cachestrategien erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem automação de compilação avançada nativa de contêiner com inteligência de teste e estratégias de cache.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, требующих продвинутой контейнерно-ориентированной автоматизации сборки с интеллектом тестирования и стратегиями кэширования.","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذين يطلبون أتمتة بناء متقدمة أصلية للحاويات مع ذكاء الاختبار واستراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage Harness CI pipelines with features like build infrastructure management on Kubernetes, Harness Cloud, or VMs, and leverages caching strategies using S3 or GCS for efficient container-native builds and test execution.","zh":"赋予代理管理 Harness CI 流水线的能力，具有在 Kubernetes、Harness Cloud 或 VM 上管理构建基础设施的功能，并利用 S3 或 GCS 的缓存策略实现高效的容器原生构建和测试执行。","ja":"エージェントが Kubernetes、Harness Cloud、または VM 上のビルドインフラストラクチャ管理などの機能を使用して Harness CI パイプラインを管理できるようにし、S3 または GCS のキャッシング戦略を使用して効率的なコンテナネイティブビルドとテスト実行を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 Kubernets, Harness Cloud 또는 VM에서 빌드 인프라 관리와 같은 기능을 사용하여 Harness CI 파이프라인을 관리할 수 있도록 하며, S3 또는 GCS의 캐싱 전략을 사용하여 효율적인 컨테이너 네이티브 빌드 및 테스트 실행을 실현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a administrar tuberías de Harness CI con características como la administración de infraestructura de compilación en Kubernetes, Harness Cloud o máquinas virtuales, y aprovecha las estrategias de caché usando S3 o GCS para compilaciones y ejecuciones de pruebas nativas de contenedores eficientes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les pipelines Harness CI avec des fonctionnalités telles que la gestion de l''infrastructure de construction sur Kubernetes, Harness Cloud ou des machines virtuelles, et exploite les stratégies de mise en cache à l''aide de S3 ou GCS pour des constructions et exécutions de tests de conteneurs natifs efficaces.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Harness-CI-Pipelines mit Funktionen wie der Verwaltung von Build-Infrastrukturen auf Kubernetes, Harness Cloud oder VMs zu verwalten und nutzt Cachestrategien mit S3 oder GCS für effiziente container-native Builds und Testausführungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar pipelines Harness CI com recursos como gerenciamento de infraestrutura de compilação no Kubernetes, Harness Cloud ou VMs, e aproveita estratégias de cache usando S3 ou GCS para compilações e execuções de teste eficientes e nativas de contêiner.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять конвейерами Harness CI с функциями, такими как управление инфраструктурой сборки в Kubernetes, Harness Cloud или ВМ, и использует стратегии кэширования с помощью S3 или GCS для эффективных контейнерно-ориентированных сборок и выполнения тестов.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إدارة أنابيب Harness CI مع ميزات مثل إدارة بنية تحتية البناء في Kubernetes و Harness Cloud أو VMs ، وت tận dụng استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت باستخدام S3 أو GCS للحصول على بناء حاويات أصلي وكفء وتشغيل الاختبار."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring build steps for Run, RunTests, and BuildAndPush operations","Implementing test intelligence for faster and more efficient test execution","Managing build infrastructure across various environments such as Kubernetes and Harness Cloud"],"zh":["为 Run、RunTests 和 BuildAndPush 操作配置构建步骤","实现测试智能以实现更快、更高效的测试执行","在 Kubernetes 和 Harness Cloud 等各种环境中管理构建基础设施"],"ja":["Run、RunTests、BuildAndPush 操作のビルドステップを構成する","テストインテリジェンスを実装してテスト実行をより迅速かつ効率的にする","Kubernetes や Harness Cloud などのさまざまな環境でビルドインフラストラクチャを管理する"],"ko":["Run, RunTests 및 BuildAndPush 작업을 위한 빌드 단계 구성","테스트 인텔리전스를 구현하여 더 빠르고 효율적인 테스트 실행을 thực現","Kubernets 및 Harness Cloud와 같은 다양한 환경에서 빌드 인프라를 관리"],"es":["Configuración de los pasos de compilación para operaciones de Ejecutar, EjecutarPruebas y CompilarYPush","Implementación de la inteligencia de prueba para una ejecución de pruebas más rápida y eficiente","Administración de la infraestructura de compilación en varios entornos, como Kubernetes y Harness Cloud"],"fr":["Configuration des étapes de construction pour les opérations Exécuter, ExécuterDesTests et ConstruireEtPush","Mise en œuvre de l''intelligence de test pour une exécution de test plus rapide et plus efficace","Gestion de l''infrastructure de construction dans différents environnements tels que Kubernetes et Harness Cloud"],"de":["Konfiguration von Build-Schritten für Run-, RunTests- und BuildAndPush-Operationen","Implementierung von Testintelligenz für eine schnellere und effizientere Testausführung","Verwaltung von Build-Infrastrukturen in verschiedenen Umgebungen wie Kubernetes und Harness Cloud"],"pt":["Configurando etapas de compilação para operações Run, RunTests e BuildAndPush","Implementando inteligência de teste para execução de teste mais rápida e eficiente","Gerenciando infraestrutura de compilação em vários ambientes, como Kubernetes e Harness Cloud"],"ru":["Настройка шагов сборки для операций Run, RunTests и BuildAndPush","Реализация интеллекта тестирования для более быстрого и эффективного выполнения тестов","Управление инфраструктурой сборки в различных средах, таких как Kubernetes и Harness Cloud"],"ar":["تكوين خطوات البناء لعمليات التشغيل والاختبارات والبناء والدفع","تنفيذ ذكاء الاختبار من أجل تشغيل اختبار أسرع وأكثر كفاءة","إدارة بنية تحتية البناء في بيئات مختلفة مثل Kubernetes و Harness Cloud"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Harness CI setup and configuration","Dependent on specific build infrastructure such as Kubernetes, Harness Cloud, or VMs","Limited to container-native builds and may require additional setup for non-containerized environments"],"zh":["需要 Harness CI 设置和配置","依赖于特定的构建基础设施，例如 Kubernetes、Harness Cloud 或 VM","仅限容器原生构建，非容器化环境可能需要额外设置"],"ja":["Harness CI の設定と構成が必要","Kubernetes、Harness Cloud、または VM などの特定のビルドインフラストラクチャに依存する","コンテナネイティブビルドのみに限定され、非コンテナ化環境では追加の設定が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["Harness CI 설정 및 구성이 필요","Kubernets, Harness Cloud 또는 VM과 같은 특정 빌드 인프라에 의존","컨테이너 네이티브 빌드만 해당되며, 비컨테이너화 환경에서는 추가 설정이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere configuración y ajuste de Harness CI","Dependiente de infraestructura de compilación específica como Kubernetes, Harness Cloud o máquinas virtuales","Limitado a compilaciones nativas de contenedores y puede requerir una configuración adicional para entornos no contenerizados"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration et une mise en place de Harness CI","Dépendante d''une infrastructure de construction spécifique telle que Kubernetes, Harness Cloud ou des machines virtuelles","Limité aux constructions de conteneurs natifs et peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour des environnements non conteneurisés"],"de":["Benötigt Harness-CI-Setup und -Konfiguration","Abhängig von spezifischer Build-Infrastruktur wie Kubernetes, Harness Cloud oder VMs","Begrenzt auf container-native Builds und kann eine zusätzliche Einrichtung für nicht-containerte Umgebungen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige configuração e instalação do Harness CI","Depende de infraestrutura de compilação específica, como Kubernetes, Harness Cloud ou VMs","Limitado a compilações nativas de contêiner e pode exigir configuração adicional para ambientes não contêinerizados"],"ru":["Требует настройки и конфигурации Harness CI","Зависит от конкретной инфраструктуры сборки, такой как Kubernetes, Harness Cloud или ВМ","Ограничен контейнерно-ориентированными сборками и может требовать дополнительной настройки для неконтейнерных сред"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد وتكوين Harness CI","يعتمد على بنية تحتية لبناء محددة مثل Kubernetes و Harness Cloud أو VMs","مقيد ببناء الحاويات الأصلية وقد يتطلب إعدادًا إضافيًا لبيئات غير حاوية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ryu-qqq/AuthHub/legacy-controller', 'community', 'ryu-qqq', 'AuthHub', 'ryu-qqq/AuthHub', 'legacy-controller', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z', '2026-02-18T07:40:28.669Z', NULL, '{"id":"ryu-qqq/AuthHub/legacy-controller","name":"legacy-controller","description":{"zh":"Legacy 控制器是 API 开发的最后一步，自动创建 Controller 和 ApiMapper。使用此功能可以简化 API 开发流程","ja":"レガシーコントローラーは API 開発の最後のステップであり、コントローラーと ApiMapper を自動生成します。この機能を使用すると、API 開発プロセスを簡素化できます","ko":"레거시 컨트롤러는 API 개발의 마지막 단계로 Controller 및 ApiMapper를 자동 생성하여 API 개발 프로세스를 단순화합니다","es":"El legacy-controller es la última etapa de la migración, crea Controller y ApiMapper. Requiere la finalización de las etapas anteriores.","fr":"Le contrôleur legacy est la dernière étape de la migration, il crée des contrôleurs et des ApiMapper. Il nécessite la completion des étapes précédentes.","de":"Der Legacy-Controller ist der letzte Schritt der Migration, er erstellt Controller und ApiMapper. Er erfordert die Fertigstellung der vorherigen Schritte.","pt":"O Legacy Controller é uma ferramenta para migrar APIs legadas para um novo sistema, criando controladores e mapeadores de API.","ru":"Legacy Controller - это инструмент для миграции устаревших API в новую систему, создающий контроллеры и мапперы API.","ar":"_legacy-controller هو أداة للهجرة إلى نظام جديد، حيث يُنشئ متحكمات وخرائط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Legacy 控制器：简化 API 开发","ja":"レガシーコントローラー：API 開発の簡素化","ko":"레거시 컨트롤러: API 개발 단순화","es":"Legacy Controller: Último Paso de la Migración","fr":"Contrôleur Legacy : Dernière Étape de la Migration","de":"Legacy-Controller: Letzter Schritt der Migration","pt":"Legacy Controller: Migração de API","ru":"Legacy Controller: Миграция API","ar":"_legacy-controller: هجرة واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","en":"legacy-controller"},"description":{"zh":"Legacy 控制器是 API 开发的最后一步，自动创建 Controller 和 ApiMapper。使用此功能可以简化 API 开发流程","ja":"レガシーコントローラーは API 開発の最後のステップであり、コントローラーと ApiMapper を自動生成します。この機能を使用すると、API 開発プロセスを簡素化できます","ko":"레거시 컨트롤러는 API 개발의 마지막 단계로 Controller 및 ApiMapper를 자동 생성하여 API 개발 프로세스를 단순화합니다","es":"El legacy-controller es la última etapa de la migración, crea Controller y ApiMapper. Requiere la finalización de las etapas anteriores.","fr":"Le contrôleur legacy est la dernière étape de la migration, il crée des contrôleurs et des ApiMapper. Il nécessite la completion des étapes précédentes.","de":"Der Legacy-Controller ist der letzte Schritt der Migration, er erstellt Controller und ApiMapper. Er erfordert die Fertigstellung der vorherigen Schritte.","pt":"O Legacy Controller é uma ferramenta para migrar APIs legadas para um novo sistema, criando controladores e mapeadores de API.","ru":"Legacy Controller - это инструмент для миграции устаревших API в новую систему, создающий контроллеры и мапперы API.","ar":"_legacy-controller هو أداة للهجرة إلى نظام جديد، حيث يُنشئ متحكمات وخرائط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动创建 Controller","自动创建 ApiMapper","简化 API 开发流程","支持多种开发语言"],"ja":["コントローラーの自動生成","ApiMapper の自動生成","API 開発プロセスの簡素化","複数の開発言語をサポート"],"ko":["Controller 자동 생성","ApiMapper 자동 생성","API 개발 프로세스 단순화","다중 개발 언어 지원"],"es":["Crea Controller y ApiMapper","Último paso de la migración","Requiere la finalización de las etapas anteriores","Genera código para la capa de aplicación","Soporta la creación de API de administración"],"fr":["Crée des contrôleurs et des ApiMapper","Dernière étape de la migration","Nécessite la completion des étapes précédentes","Génère du code pour la couche d''application","Prend en charge la création d''API d''administration"],"de":["Erstellt Controller und ApiMapper","Letzter Schritt der Migration","Erfordert die Fertigstellung der vorherigen Schritte","Generiert Code für die Anwendungsebene","Unterstützt die Erstellung von Admin-APIs"],"pt":["Criação de controladores e mapeadores de API","Migração de APIs legadas para um novo sistema","Integração com o Persistence Layer","Integração com o Application Layer","Suporte a múltiplos domínios","Código de exemplo para facilitar a implementação"],"ru":["Создание контроллеров и мапперов API","Миграция устаревших API в новую систему","Интеграция с Persistence Layer","Интеграция с Application Layer","Поддержка множества доменов","Пример кода для облегчения реализации"],"ar":["إنشاء متحكمات وخرائط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","هجرة واجهات برمجة التطبيقات القديمة إلى نظام جديد","التكامل مع طبقة الاستمرار","التكامل مع طبقة التطبيق","دعم النطاقات المتعددة","كود مثال لتسهيل التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Legacy 控制器","API 开发","自动创建 Controller","自动创建 ApiMapper","简化开发流程","开发工具"],"ja":["レガシーコントローラー","API 開発","コントローラーの自動生成","ApiMapper の自動生成","開発プロセスの簡素化","開発ツール"],"ko":["레거시 컨트롤러","API 개발","Controller 자동 생성","ApiMapper 자동 생성","개발 프로세스 단순화","개발 도구"],"es":["legacy-controller","migración de software","desarrollo de aplicaciones","controladores y ApiMapper","capa de aplicación","API de administración"],"fr":["contrôleur legacy","migration de logiciel","développement d''applications","contrôleurs et ApiMapper","couche d''application","API d''administration"],"de":["Legacy-Controller","Software-Migration","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Controller und ApiMapper","Anwendungsebene","Admin-API"],"pt":["Legacy Controller","Migração de API","Controladores de API","Mapeadores de API","Persistence Layer","Application Layer","Desenvolvimento de software","Arquitetura de software","Integração de sistemas"],"ru":["Legacy Controller","Миграция API","Контроллеры API","Мапперы API","Persistence Layer","Application Layer","Разработка программного обеспечения","Архитектура программного обеспечения","Интеграция систем"],"ar":["_legacy-controller","هجرة واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","متحكمات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","خرائط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","طبقة الاستمرار","طبقة التطبيق","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","تكامل الأنظمة"]}},"owner":"ryu-qqq","repo":"AuthHub","repoPath":"ryu-qqq/AuthHub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"legacy-controller","description":"마이그레이션 사이클의 마지막 단계. Controller + ApiMapper 생성하여 전체 흐름 완성.","bodyPreview":"# /legacy-controller\n\n마이그레이션 사이클의 **마지막 단계**. Controller + ApiMapper를 생성합니다.\n\n## 사용법\n\n```bash\n/legacy-controller admin:BrandController.fetchBrands\n/legacy-controller web:ProductController.fetchProductGroups\n```\n\n## 전제조건\n\n이전 단계들이 완료되어 있어야 함:\n1. `/legacy-convert` - Request/Response DTO\n2. `/legacy-query` - Persistence Layer\n3. `/legacy-service` - Application Layer\n\n## 출력\n\n**Admin API:**\n```\nadapter-in/rest-api-admin/.../admin/v1/{domain}/\n├── controller/Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java\n└── map","body":"# /legacy-controller\n\n마이그레이션 사이클의 **마지막 단계**. Controller + ApiMapper를 생성합니다.\n\n## 사용법\n\n```bash\n/legacy-controller admin:BrandController.fetchBrands\n/legacy-controller web:ProductController.fetchProductGroups\n```\n\n## 전제조건\n\n이전 단계들이 완료되어 있어야 함:\n1. `/legacy-convert` - Request/Response DTO\n2. `/legacy-query` - Persistence Layer\n3. `/legacy-service` - Application Layer\n\n## 출력\n\n**Admin API:**\n```\nadapter-in/rest-api-admin/.../admin/v1/{domain}/\n├── controller/Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java\n└── mapper/Legacy{Domain}V1ApiMapper.java\n```\n\n**Web API:**\n```\nadapter-in/rest-api/.../v1/{domain}/\n├── controller/Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java\n└── mapper/Legacy{Domain}V1ApiMapper.java\n```\n\n## 생성 컴포넌트\n\n| 컴포넌트 | 역할 |\n|---------|------|\n| **Controller** | REST 엔드포인트, UseCase 호출 |\n| **ApiMapper** | Request→Command, Result→Response 변환 |\n\n## 마이그레이션 완료\n\n이 단계 완료 시 하나의 엔드포인트에 대한 전체 마이그레이션이 완료됩니다.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:40:28.669Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for API-focused Agents requiring automated Controller and ApiMapper generation for migration cycles.","zh":"适用于需要自动化控制器和ApiMapper生成的API聚焦代理的迁移周期的理想选择。","ja":"APIに焦点を当てたエージェントが移行サイクルで自動化されたコントローラーとApiMapperの生成を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"API에 중점을 둔 에이전트가 마이그레이션 주기에서 자동화된 컨트롤러 및 ApiMapper 생성을 필요로 하는 경우에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes enfocados en API que requieren generación automática de Controlador y ApiMapper para ciclos de migración.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents axés sur l''API nécessitant une génération automatisée de contrôleur et d''ApiMapper pour les cycles de migration.","de":"Ideal für API-fokussierte Agenten, die eine automatisierte Controller- und ApiMapper-Generierung für Migrationszyklen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes focados em API que exigem geração automática de Controlador e ApiMapper para ciclos de migração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на API, требующих автоматического создания контроллера и ApiMapper для циклов миграции.","ar":"مثالي لعميل برمجي يركز على واجهة برمجة التطبيقات والذي يتطلب توليد آلي لمتحكم و ApiMapper من أجل دورات الهجرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create Admin API controllers and mappings using LegacyController, streamlining the migration process with REST API support and Java-based implementations like Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java.","zh":"赋予代理创建使用LegacyController的Admin API控制器和映射，并通过REST API支持和基于Java的实现（如Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java）简化迁移过程。","ja":"LegacyControllerを使用したAdmin APIコントローラーとマッピングの作成をエージェントに可能にし、REST APIサポートとJavaベースの実装（例：Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java）で移行プロセスを簡素化します。","ko":"레거시 컨트롤러를 사용하여 Admin API 컨트롤러 및 매핑을 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하고 REST API 지원 및 Java 기반 구현(예: Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java)으로 마이그레이션 프로세스를 간소화합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear controladores de API de administración y asignaciones utilizando LegacyController, simplificando el proceso de migración con soporte de REST API y implementaciones basadas en Java como Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des contrôleurs d''API d''administration et des mappages à l''aide de LegacyController, en simplifiant le processus de migration avec un support REST API et des implementations basées sur Java comme Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Admin-API-Controller und Mappings mit LegacyController zu erstellen, wodurch der Migrationsprozess mit REST-API-Unterstützung und Java-basierten Implementierungen wie Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java vereinfacht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar controladores de API de administração e mapeamentos usando LegacyController, simplificando o processo de migração com suporte a API REST e implementações baseadas em Java, como Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать контроллеры административного API и сопоставления с помощью LegacyController, упрощая процесс миграции с поддержкой REST API и реализациями на основе Java, такими как Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java.","ar":"يسمح للعميل البرمجي بإنشاء متحكمات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الإدارية والتعيينات باستخدام LegacyController، وبذلك يبسط عملية الهجرة مع دعم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST والتنفيذات المعتمدة على لغة جافا، مثل Legacy{Domain}QueryV1Controller.java."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Controller generation for admin APIs","Creating ApiMapper configurations for product and brand data","Simplifying migration cycles with pre-built LegacyController templates"],"zh":["自动化管理API的控制器生成","为产品和品牌数据创建ApiMapper配置","使用预建的LegacyController模板简化迁移周期"],"ja":["管理APIのコントローラー生成の自動化","製品およびブランドデータのApiMapper構成の作成","事前に構築されたLegacyControllerテンプレートを使用した移行サイクルの簡素化"],"ko":["관리 API의 컨트롤러 생성 자동화","제품 및 브랜드 데이터를 위한 ApiMapper 구성 생성","사전 구축된 LegacyController 템플릿을 사용하여 마이그레이션 주기 간소화"],"es":["Automatizar la generación de controladores para API de administración","Crear configuraciones de ApiMapper para datos de producto y marca","Simplificar los ciclos de migración con plantillas de LegacyController preconstruidas"],"fr":["Automatiser la génération de contrôleurs pour les API d''administration","Créer des configurations de mappage d''API pour les données de produit et de marque","Simplifier les cycles de migration avec des modèles de LegacyController préconstruits"],"de":["Automatisieren der Controller-Generierung für Admin-APIs","Erstellen von ApiMapper-Konfigurationen für Produkt- und Markendaten","Vereinfachen der Migrationszyklen mit vorab erstellten LegacyController-Vorlagen"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de controladores para APIs de administração","Criar configurações de ApiMapper para dados de produtos e marcas","Simplificar ciclos de migração com modelos de LegacyController pré-construídos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание контроллеров для административных API","Создавать конфигурации ApiMapper для данных о продуктах и брендах","Упрощать циклы миграции с помощью предварительно созданных шаблонов LegacyController"],"ar":["توليد آلي لمتحكمات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الإدارية","إنشاء تعيينات ApiMapper لبيانات المنتجات والعلامات التجارية","تبسيط دورات الهجرة باستخدام قوالب LegacyController مسبقاً"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires completion of preceding migration steps (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Java-based implementation only","Specific to REST API admin interfaces"],"zh":["需要完成先前的迁移步骤(/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","仅限基于Java的实现","特定于REST API管理接口"],"ja":["先行する移行手順の完了が必要(/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Javaベースの実装のみ","REST API管理インターフェイスに特有"],"ko":["이전의 마이그레이션 단계 완료가 필요(/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Java 기반 구현만","REST API 관리 인터페이스에 특정"],"es":["Requiere la finalización de los pasos de migración anteriores (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Implementación basada en Java solo","Específico para interfaces de administración de API de REST"],"fr":["Nécessite la finalisation des étapes de migration précédentes (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Implémentation basée sur Java uniquement","Spécifique aux interfaces d''administration d''API REST"],"de":["Erfordert den Abschluss der vorherigen Migrationschritte (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Nur Java-basierte Implementierung","Spezifisch für REST-API-Admin-Oberflächen"],"pt":["Exige a conclusão dos passos de migração anteriores (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Implementação baseada em Java apenas","Específico para interfaces de administração de API REST"],"ru":["Требует завершения предыдущих шагов миграции (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","Только реализация на основе Java","Конкретно для административных интерфейсов API REST"],"ar":["يتطلب إكمال الخطوات السابقة للهجرة (/legacy-convert, /legacy-query, /legacy-service)","تنفيذ معتمد على لغة جافا فقط","محدد لواجهات برمجة التطبيقات الإدارية ل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/deploy-frappe', 'community', 'Bebang-Enterprise-Inc', 'hrms', 'Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms', 'deploy-frappe', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z', '2026-02-18T07:40:24.346Z', NULL, '{"id":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/deploy-frappe","name":"deploy-frappe","description":{"zh":"部署Frappe HRMS代码到AWS EC2，支持Docker和本地测试","ja":"Frappe HRMSのコードをAWS EC2にデプロイ、Dockerとローカルテストをサポート","ko":"Frappe HRMS 코드를 AWS EC2에 배포, Docker와 로컬 테스트 지원","es":"El comando deploy-frappe despliega cambios de código en la rama de producción a AWS EC2 con Frappe Docker","fr":"La commande deploy-frappe déploie les modifications de code dans la branche de production sur AWS EC2 avec Frappe Docker","de":"Der Befehl deploy-frappe stellt Änderungen im Produktionszweig auf AWS EC2 mit Frappe Docker bereit","pt":"O comando deploy-frappe implanta alterações de código do branch de produção para o AWS EC2 executando Frappe Docker","ru":"Команда deploy-frappe развертывает изменения кода из ветки производственной сборки на AWS EC2 с Frappe Docker","ar":"الأمر deploy-frappe يعمل على تثبيت التعديلات على الكود من الفرع الإنتاجي إلى AWS EC2 الذي يعمل بنظام Frappe Docker","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"部署Frappe HRMS","ja":"Frappe HRMSのデプロイ","ko":"Frappe HRMS 배포","es":"Despliegue de Frappe HRMS en AWS EC2","fr":"Déploiement de Frappe HRMS sur AWS EC2","de":"Bereitstellung von Frappe HRMS auf AWS EC2","pt":"Implantação de Frappe HRMS","ru":"Развертывание Frappe HRMS","ar":"تثبيت Frappe HRMS","en":"deploy-frappe"},"description":{"zh":"部署Frappe HRMS代码到AWS EC2，支持Docker和本地测试","ja":"Frappe HRMSのコードをAWS EC2にデプロイ、Dockerとローカルテストをサポート","ko":"Frappe HRMS 코드를 AWS EC2에 배포, Docker와 로컬 테스트 지원","es":"El comando deploy-frappe despliega cambios de código en la rama de producción a AWS EC2 con Frappe Docker","fr":"La commande deploy-frappe déploie les modifications de code dans la branche de production sur AWS EC2 avec Frappe Docker","de":"Der Befehl deploy-frappe stellt Änderungen im Produktionszweig auf AWS EC2 mit Frappe Docker bereit","pt":"O comando deploy-frappe implanta alterações de código do branch de produção para o AWS EC2 executando Frappe Docker","ru":"Команда deploy-frappe развертывает изменения кода из ветки производственной сборки на AWS EC2 с Frappe Docker","ar":"الأمر deploy-frappe يعمل على تثبيت التعديلات على الكود من الفرع الإنتاجي إلى AWS EC2 الذي يعمل بنظام Frappe Docker","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动部署代码到AWS EC2","支持Frappe Docker","支持本地测试","自动重建Docker镜像","支持生产环境部署"],"ja":["コードをAWS EC2に自動デプロイ","Frappe Dockerをサポート","ローカルテストをサポート","Dockerイメージを自動的に再構築","生産環境へのデプロイをサポート"],"ko":["코드를 AWS EC2에 자동 배포","Frappe Docker 지원","로컬 테스트 지원","Docker 이미지 자동 재구성","생산 환경 배포 지원"],"es":["Despliegue automático de cambios de código","Compatibilidad con Frappe Docker","Reconstrucción automática de la imagen de Docker","Soporte para pruebas locales","Implementación en AWS EC2"],"fr":["Déploiement automatique des modifications de code","Compatibilité avec Frappe Docker","Reconstruction automatique de l''image Docker","Prise en charge des tests locaux","Déploiement sur AWS EC2"],"de":["Automatische Bereitstellung von Codeänderungen","Kompatibilität mit Frappe Docker","Automatische Neuerstellung des Docker-Images","Unterstützung für lokale Tests","Bereitstellung auf AWS EC2"],"pt":["Implantação automática de alterações de código","Suporte ao AWS EC2","Integração com Frappe Docker","Reconstrução automática da imagem do Docker","Teste local antes da implantação em produção"],"ru":["Автоматическое развертывание изменений кода","Поддержка AWS EC2","Интеграция с Frappe Docker","Автоматическое перестроение образа Docker","Местное тестирование перед развертыванием в производственной среде"],"ar":["تثبيت تلقائي للتعديلات على الكود","دعم AWS EC2","تكامل مع Frappe Docker","إعادة بناء تلقائية لصورة Docker","اختبار محلي قبل التثبيت في بيئة الإنتاج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Frappe HRMS","AWS EC2","Docker","自动部署","本地测试","生产环境"],"ja":["Frappe HRMS","AWS EC2","Docker","自動デプロイ","ローカルテスト","生産環境"],"ko":["Frappe HRMS","AWS EC2","Docker","자동 배포","로컬 테스트","생산 환경"],"es":["despliegue de Frappe HRMS","Frappe Docker","AWS EC2","desarrollo de software","automatización de despliegue","pruebas locales"],"fr":["déploiement de Frappe HRMS","Frappe Docker","AWS EC2","développement de logiciels","automatisation du déploiement","tests locaux"],"de":["Bereitstellung von Frappe HRMS","Frappe Docker","AWS EC2","Softwareentwicklung","Automatisierung der Bereitstellung","Lokale Tests"],"pt":["Frappe HRMS","implantação de código","AWS EC2","Frappe Docker","desenvolvimento de software","deploy-frappe","gerenciamento de código"],"ru":["Frappe HRMS","развертывание кода","AWS EC2","Frappe Docker","разработка программного обеспечения","deploy-frappe","управление кодом"],"ar":["Frappe HRMS","تثبيت الكود","AWS EC2","Frappe Docker","تطوير البرمجيات","deploy-frappe","إدارة الكود"]}},"owner":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc","repo":"hrms","repoPath":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.459Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"deploy-frappe","description":"Deploy Frappe HRMS code changes to AWS production. Use when you need to deploy Python/API changes to the Frappe Docker container.","bodyPreview":"# /deploy-frappe - Frappe HRMS Deployment\n\n## What This Command Does\n\nDeploys code changes from the `production` branch to AWS EC2 running Frappe Docker.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Frappe Docker uses `--preload`, so Python code changes require rebuilding the Docker image. This command handles that automatically.\n\n**TEST LOCALLY FIRST:** Always test your changes in the local development environment before deploying to production. Use `/local-frappe` to set up and manage local development.\n\n## Quick Referenc","body":"# /deploy-frappe - Frappe HRMS Deployment\n\n## What This Command Does\n\nDeploys code changes from the `production` branch to AWS EC2 running Frappe Docker.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Frappe Docker uses `--preload`, so Python code changes require rebuilding the Docker image. This command handles that automatically.\n\n**TEST LOCALLY FIRST:** Always test your changes in the local development environment before deploying to production. Use `/local-frappe` to set up and manage local development.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Deployment Type | Method | Time |\n|-----------------|--------|------|\n| Python/API changes | Full rebuild via GitHub Actions | 5-10 min |\n| Python/API changes (no cache) | Full rebuild with `no_cache=true` | 8-12 min |\n| DocType schema changes | Rebuild + `bench migrate` | 8-12 min |\n| Config/data only | SSM command (no rebuild) | 2-3 min |\n| Emergency rollback | SSM with previous tag | 2-3 min |\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Docker Build Caching Issue\n\n**Problem discovered 2026-01-29:** When pushing Python/API code changes, the build may use cached Docker layers and **NOT include your new code**.\n\n### When to Use `no_cache=true`\n\n| Scenario | Use `no_cache=true`? |\n|----------|---------------------|\n| Python code changes (`.py` files) | **YES** - Always |\n| DocType JSON changes | **YES** - Always |\n| Workflow config changes | No - Cache is fine |\n| Dependencies changes (`apps.json`) | **YES** - Always |\n\n### How to Deploy with No Cache\n\n**Option 1: Manual Workflow Dispatch (Recommended)**\n```bash\ngh workflow run build-and-deploy.yml --repo Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms -f no_cache=true\n```\n\n**Option 2: Via GitHub UI**\n1. Go to https://github.com/Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/actions\n2. Select \"Build and Deploy Frappe HRMS\"\n3. Click \"Run workflow\"\n4. **Check `no_cache` checkbox** ← IMPORTANT\n5. Click \"Run workflow\"\n\n### Why This Happens\n\nThe Docker build uses layer caching. The HRMS app is cloned during build via `apps.json`. If the git clone step is cached, your new commits won''t be included even though they''re in the repo.\n\n**Build time comparison:**\n- With cache: ~30 seconds (may miss code changes)\n- Without cache: ~5 minutes (guaranteed fresh code)\n\n## Infrastructure (UPDATED 2026-01-29 - DOCKER SWARM)\n\n| Component | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| EC2 Instance | `i-026b7477d27bd46d6` |\n| Docker Image | `samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15` |\n| Site | `hq.bebang.ph` |\n| Region | `ap-southeast-1` |\n| Server Path | `/home/ubuntu/frappe_docker` |\n| **Orchestration** | **Docker Swarm** (migrated 2026-01-29) |\n| Stack Name | `frappe` |\n| Stack File | `stack.yml` |\n| Frontend Port | 80 (ADMS receiver uses 8080) |\n\n### Swarm Services (9 total)\n\n| Service | Replicas | Purpose |\n|---------|----------|---------|\n| `frappe_backend` | 1 | Gunicorn API server |\n| `frappe_frontend` | 1 | Nginx reverse proxy |\n| `frappe_websocket` | 1 | Socket.IO server |\n| `frappe_queue-short` | 1 | Short job queue worker |\n| `frappe_queue-long` | 1 | Long job queue worker |\n| `frappe_scheduler` | 1 | Background scheduler |\n| `frappe_db` | 1 | MariaDB database |\n| `frappe_redis-cache` | 1 | Redis cache |\n| `frappe_redis-queue` | 1 | Redis queue |\n\n### Volume Configuration\n\nThe site data is stored in external volumes:\n\n| Volume | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `bebang-hrms_sites` | Site data, configs |\n| `bebang-hrms_db-data` | MariaDB data |\n| `bebang-hrms_logs` | Application logs |\n| `bebang-hrms_redis-queue-data` | Redis queue data |\n\n**Backups:** `/home/ubuntu/backups/swarm-migration-20260129/` (pre-migration backup)\n\n## Deployment Methods\n\n### Method 1: PR Workflow (Recommended) - INCLUDES AUTO-CLEANUP\n\n**The `production` branch is protected.** Use the PR workflow.\n\n**Note:** The GitHub Actions workflow automatically cleans up old images after each successful deployment, keeping the 4 most recent versions. No manual cleanup needed when using this method.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create feature branch (if not already on one)\n/feature-branch my-api-change\n\n# 2. Commit your changes\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: Add employee_clearance API\"\n\n# 3. Deploy via PR (auto-merges when CI passes)\n/pr-deploy --auto-merge\n```\n\nThis creates a PR, enables auto-merge, and GitHub Actions builds and deploys when the PR merges.\n\nSee `/workflow` for the full deployment workflow.\n\n### Method 1b: Manual Workflow Dispatch\n\nFor triggering a rebuild without merging (e.g., to force `no_cache`):\n\n1. Go to https://github.com/Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/actions\n2. Select \"Build and Deploy Frappe HRMS\"\n3. Click \"Run workflow\"\n4. Options:\n   - **`no_cache`**: Build without Docker cache (**USE THIS FOR CODE CHANGES**)\n   - `skip_build`: Skip image rebuild (deploy existing)\n   - `run_migrate`: Run `bench migrate` after deploy\n\n### Method 2: AWS SSM Direct (Quick Deploy via Swarm Rolling Update)\n\nUse when image is already built and you need to update services with zero downtime:\n\n```bash\n# Get AWS credentials\nexport AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=$(doppler secrets get AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=$(doppler secrets get AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-1\n\n# Rolling update all services (ZERO DOWNTIME) + CLEANUP OLD IMAGES\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"echo === Updating services ===\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_backend\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_frontend\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_websocket\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_queue-short\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_queue-long\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15 frappe_scheduler\",\n    \"docker service ls\",\n    \"echo === Cleaning up old images (keeping 4 newest) ===\",\n    \"docker container prune -f\",\n    \"IMAGES=$(docker images samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms --format \\\"{{.ID}}\\\" | tail -n +5)\",\n    \"if [ -n \\\"$IMAGES\\\" ]; then docker rmi $IMAGES 2>/dev/null || true; fi\",\n    \"docker image prune -f\",\n    \"df -h / | tail -1\"\n  ]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n**Benefits of Swarm (migrated 2026-01-29):**\n- Zero-downtime rolling updates\n- Automatic rollback on failure (`docker service rollback <service>`)\n- No CSS 404 issues (containers fully recreated)\n\n**Check service status:**\n```bash\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker service ls\"]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Method 3: Manual Image Build (Recovery/Debug)\n\nUse when GitHub Actions fails or you need custom build:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Clone frappe_docker\ngit clone https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker.git\ncd frappe_docker\n\n# 2. Copy apps.json from BEI-ERP repo\ncat > apps.json << ''EOF''\n[\n    {\"url\": \"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext\", \"branch\": \"version-15\"},\n    {\"url\": \"https://github.com/frappe/payments\", \"branch\": \"version-15\"},\n    {\"url\": \"https://github.com/Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms\", \"branch\": \"production\"}\n]\nEOF\n# Note: Repo is public, so no authentication needed for cloning\n\n# 3. Build image\nexport APPS_JSON_BASE64=$(base64 -w 0 apps.json)\ndocker build \\\n  --no-cache \\\n  --build-arg FRAPPE_BRANCH=version-15 \\\n  --build-arg PYTHON_VERSION=3.11.6 \\\n  --build-arg NODE_VERSION=20.19.2 \\\n  --build-arg APPS_JSON_BASE64=$APPS_JSON_BASE64 \\\n  --file images/custom/Containerfile \\\n  --tag bebang/erpnext-hrms:v15-$(date +%Y%m%d) \\\n  --tag bebang/erpnext-hrms:v15 \\\n  .\n\n# 4. Push to Docker Hub\ndocker login\ndocker push bebang/erpnext-hrms:v15-$(date +%Y%m%d)\ndocker push bebang/erpnext-hrms:v15\n\n# 5. Deploy to server (via SSM - see Method 2)\n```\n\n## Post-Deployment Steps\n\n### Automatic Image Cleanup (ALWAYS RUN)\n\n**After every deployment, clean up old images to prevent disk space issues.**\n\nThe server has limited storage (50 GB). Each deployment creates a new ~2.5 GB image. Without cleanup, the disk fills up within days.\n\n**Policy:** Keep the 4 most recent images, remove all older ones.\n\n```bash\n# Run this after every successful deployment\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"echo \\\"=== Cleaning up old Docker images (keeping 4 newest) ===\\\"\",\n    \"docker container prune -f\",\n    \"IMAGES=$(docker images samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms --format \\\"{{.ID}}\\\" | tail -n +5)\",\n    \"if [ -n \\\"$IMAGES\\\" ]; then docker rmi $IMAGES 2>/dev/null || true; fi\",\n    \"docker image prune -f\",\n    \"echo \\\"=== Disk usage after cleanup ===\\\"\",\n    \"df -h / | tail -1\"\n  ]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n**What this does:**\n1. Removes exited containers (from previous deployments)\n2. Lists all bebang-erpnext-hrms images, skips the 4 newest, removes the rest\n3. Removes any remaining dangling images\n4. Reports disk usage\n\n**Expected savings:** ~2.5 GB per old image removed.\n\n### Run Migrations (if schema changed)\n\n```bash\n# Get the backend container ID\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend) bench --site hq.bebang.ph migrate\"]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Clear Cache\n\n```bash\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend) bench --site hq.bebang.ph clear-cache\"]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Verify API\n\n```bash\n# Use frappe.ping (doesn''t require auth)\ncurl https://hq.bebang.ph/api/method/frappe.ping\n# Expected: {\"message\":\"pong\"}\n\n# Or check login page\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://hq.bebang.ph/login\n# Expected: 200\n```\n\n## Emergency Rollback\n\n### Option A: Swarm Service Rollback (Fastest)\n\nDocker Swarm keeps previous service state for instant rollback:\n\n```bash\n# Rollback individual services\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_backend\",\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_frontend\",\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_websocket\",\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_queue-short\",\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_queue-long\",\n    \"docker service rollback frappe_scheduler\",\n    \"docker service ls\"\n  ]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Option B: Deploy Previous Image Tag\n\n```bash\n# Find previous tag from Docker Hub or deployment logs\n# Tags are formatted: v15-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS or v15-<short-sha>\n\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_backend\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_frontend\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_websocket\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_queue-short\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_queue-long\",\n    \"docker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-PREVIOUS_TAG frappe_scheduler\"\n  ]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Option C: Return to Docker Compose (Last Resort)\n\nIf Swarm has issues, revert to Docker Compose:\n\n```bash\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker stack rm frappe\",\n    \"sleep 30\",\n    \"cd /home/ubuntu/frappe_docker\",\n    \"docker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml up -d\"\n  ]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n## GitHub Secrets Required\n\nThese must be set in GitHub repo settings:\n\n| Secret | Description | Where to get |\n|--------|-------------|--------------|\n| `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` | Docker Hub username | Docker Hub account |\n| `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` | Docker Hub access token | Docker Hub > Account Settings > Security |\n| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | AWS IAM access key | `doppler secrets get AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID --project bei-erp --config dev --plain` |\n| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | AWS IAM secret key | `doppler secrets get AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY --project bei-erp --config dev --plain` |\n\n## Common Issues\n\n### Docker Cache Not Picking Up Code Changes (CRITICAL!)\n\n**Symptom:** Build completes quickly (~2 minutes instead of ~10-15), but new APIs/pages return \"module has no attribute\" or 404 errors.\n\n**Cause:** Docker''s build cache doesn''t detect when git repo contents change during `bench get-app`. Even though you pushed code, the build serves cached layers from previous builds.\n\n**Build Time Indicator:**\n| Build Time | What It Means | Action Required |\n|------------|---------------|-----------------|\n| ~2 min | CACHED - Old code deployed | Rebuild with `no_cache=true` |\n| ~5-10 min | FRESH - New code deployed | None - working correctly |\n\n**Fix:** ALWAYS use `no_cache=true` for code changes:\n```bash\ngh workflow run \"Build and Deploy Frappe HRMS\" --repo Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms -f no_cache=true -f run_migrate=true\n```\n\n**This is NORMAL Docker behavior**, not corruption. The `apps.json` file didn''t change, so Docker cached the layer where apps are cloned.\n\n**Prevention:** Use `no_cache=true` whenever deploying:\n- New API files\n- Modified API files\n- New www pages (like custom login)\n- DocType changes\n- Any Python code changes\n\n**When `no_cache` is NOT needed:**\n- Config-only changes (site_config.json)\n- Data imports via SQL\n- Clear cache operations\n\n### Custom Login Page Not Serving (404)\n\n**Symptom:** Created `hrms/www/login.html` but `/login` still shows Frappe''s default login.\n\n**Cause:** Frappe''s `/login` route is handled specially and bypasses `page_renderer` hook.\n\n**Fix:** Use `website_redirects` hook to redirect to a different route:\n\n```python\n# hrms/hooks.py\nwebsite_redirects = [\n    {\"source\": \"/login\", \"target\": \"/bei-login\", \"redirect_http_status\": 302},\n]\n```\n\nThen create `hrms/www/bei-login.html` and `hrms/www/bei-login.py`.\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\ncurl -sI https://hq.bebang.ph/login | grep -i location\n# Should show: Location: /bei-login\n```\n\n---\n\n### \"not whitelisted\" Error\n\n**Cause:** Function not in `@frappe.whitelist()` or `__init__.py` not updated\n\n**Fix:**\n1. Add `@frappe.whitelist()` decorator to function\n2. Add import to `hrms/api/__init__.py`\n3. Rebuild and deploy\n\n### Container starts but API fails\n\n**Check:**\n```bash\n# View logs\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"cd /home/ubuntu/frappe_docker && docker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml logs --tail=100 backend\"]'' \\\n  --output json\n```\n\n### Build fails: \"Could not find branch\"\n\n**Cause:** Branch name in apps.json doesn''t exist\n\n**Fix:** Verify branch exists: `git ls-remote https://github.com/Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms production`\n\n### Port 8080 already in use\n\n**Cause:** ADMS receiver nginx container uses port 8080\n\n**Fix:** Use port 80 for Frappe frontend instead:\n```bash\n# In pwd.yml, change frontend ports from 8080:8080 to 80:8080\nsed -i \"s/8080:8080/80:8080/g\" pwd.yml\n```\n\n### Frontend container won''t start\n\n**Cause:** Old containers from previous stacks still running\n\n**Check:**\n```bash\ndocker ps -a | grep -E \"bebang|frappe\"\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n```bash\n# Stop old stack containers\ndocker stop bebang-hrms-frontend-1 bebang-hrms-backend-1 ...\ndocker rm bebang-hrms-frontend-1 bebang-hrms-backend-1 ...\n```\n\n### New Domain Returns 404 (Site Not Found)\n\n**Symptom:** Added new domain (e.g., hq.bebang.ph) but all pages return 404 or \"Site not found\".\n\n**Cause 1:** Missing site symlink in `/home/frappe/frappe-bench/sites/`\n\n**Fix:**\n```bash\n# Create symlink for new domain pointing to actual site\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker exec frappe_docker-backend-1 bash -c \\\"cd /home/frappe/frappe-bench/sites && ln -sf hrms.bebang.ph hq.bebang.ph\\\"\"]''\n```\n\n**Cause 2:** Wrong `FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER` in pwd.yml\n\n| Setting | Effect |\n|---------|--------|\n| `FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER: frontend` | ❌ BROKEN - All requests routed to non-existent \"frontend\" site |\n| `FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER: $host` | ✅ CORRECT - Uses actual hostname for routing |\n\n**Fix:**\n```bash\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"cd /home/ubuntu/frappe_docker && sed -i \\\"s/FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER: frontend/FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER: \\\\$host/g\\\" pwd.yml && docker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml restart frontend\"]''\n```\n\n**Verify site routing:**\n```bash\ncurl -sI https://hq.bebang.ph/api/method/frappe.ping | grep -i x-frappe-site-name\n# Should show: X-Frappe-Site-Name: hrms.bebang.ph\n```\n\n## DO NOT DO\n\n1. **NEVER use `docker commit`** - Corrupts the Python environment (learned 2026-01-22)\n2. **NEVER edit files directly in container** - Changes lost on restart (--preload)\n3. **NEVER use `-v` flag with `docker compose down`** - Deletes all data volumes\n4. **NEVER skip `bench migrate`** after DocType changes\n5. **NEVER assume server paths** - Always verify with `ls` first\n6. **NEVER modify pwd.yml directly without restoring from git first** - sed errors accumulate\n7. **NEVER set `FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER: frontend`** - Breaks multi-site routing (learned 2026-01-28)\n8. **NEVER forget site symlinks for new domains** - Each domain needs symlink in sites/ directory (learned 2026-01-28)\n9. **NEVER run `bench build` in production containers** - Causes CSS 404 errors (learned 2026-01-28)\n10. **NEVER run `bench get-app` in production containers** - Official Frappe Docker policy\n11. **NEVER use `docker compose up --no-deps`** - Doesn''t refresh assets, causes CSS 404 (learned 2026-01-29)\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Setup Wizard Redirect Loop Issue (2026-01-29) ✅\n\n### Status: FIXED (Database Value Changed)\n\nIf `/app` causes infinite redirect loop after Google OAuth login with `setup_wizard.load_languages` being called repeatedly:\n\n**Root Cause:** `tabDefaultValue` table has:\n```sql\ndefkey=''desktop:home_page'' defvalue=''setup-wizard''\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n```sql\n-- Run via bench console or direct MariaDB\nUPDATE tabDefaultValue SET defvalue=''Workspaces''\nWHERE defkey=''desktop:home_page'' AND parent=''__default'';\n```\n\n**Also ensure these are set:**\n```sql\n-- Mark setup as complete\nUPDATE tabDefaultValue SET defvalue=''1''\nWHERE defkey=''setup_complete'' AND parent=''__default'';\n\n-- Mark HRMS app as setup complete\nUPDATE `tabInstalled Application` SET is_setup_complete=1\nWHERE app_name=''hrms'';\n```\n\n**Clear cache after:**\n```bash\ndocker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml exec -T backend bench --site hrms.bebang.ph clear-cache\n```\n\n**Reference:** `docs/plans/FRAPPE_DEPLOYMENT_FIX_PLAN_2026-01-29.md`\n\n---\n\n## CSS 404 Asset Desync Issue - RESOLVED (2026-01-29, Updated 2026-01-29) ✅\n\n### Status: PERMANENTLY FIXED\n\nThe GitHub Actions workflow has been updated to prevent CSS 404 errors. Every deployment now:\n1. Runs Swarm rolling updates (recreates containers with fresh assets)\n2. **Flushes Redis cache** (prevents stale HTML serving old asset hashes)\n3. Verifies CSS/JS assets load correctly after deploy (fails workflow on 404)\n\n**Commits:**\n- `48f1c2f9b` - fix: Add asset volume reset and CSS health check to deployment\n- `TBD` - fix: Add Redis flush step to prevent stale HTML caching\n\n### The Original Problem\n\nRunning `bench build` or `bench migrate` in production containers caused CSS/JS 404 errors:\n- Browser requests `desk.bundle.ABC123.css`\n- Server only has `desk.bundle.XYZ789.css`\n- Result: Entire application breaks (no styling)\n\n**This caused 4 production outages, now prevented by workflow fix.**\n\n### Root Cause\n\nFrom [GitHub Issue #790](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker/issues/790):\n> \"Any new nginx images which have new assets at `/usr/share/nginx/html`, will not propagate these changes if the volume already exists.\"\n\n**Architecture flaw:**\n1. Assets are baked into Docker image at build time\n2. Assets volume (`bebang-hrms_sites`) persists between deployments\n3. `bench migrate` regenerates assets in backend container\n4. Frontend container still has OLD assets from image/volume\n5. `assets.json` points to NEW hashes, CSS files have OLD hashes\n\n### Official Frappe Policy\n\nFrom [Frappe Docker FAQ](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker/wiki/Frequently-Asked-Questions):\n> \"You cannot build assets using `bench build` in running production containers. It will mess up the attached assets volume.\"\n\n### The Fix: Delete Assets Before Deploy\n\n**ALWAYS delete the assets volume before deployment:**\n\n```bash\n# Add to GitHub Actions BEFORE docker compose up\ndocker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml down\ndocker volume rm bebang-hrms_assets 2>/dev/null || true\ndocker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml up -d\n```\n\n**Or via SSM:**\n```bash\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"cd /home/ubuntu/frappe_docker && docker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml down && docker volume rm bebang-hrms_assets 2>/dev/null || true && docker compose -f pwd.yml -f volumes-override.yml up -d\"]''\n```\n\n### Permanent Fix: Docker Swarm - NOW ACTIVE ✅\n\nDocker Swarm was deployed on 2026-01-29. It automatically recreates containers on deployment:\n\n```bash\n# Swarm is already initialized and running\ndocker service ls  # View all 9 services\n\n# Deploy updates via rolling updates (zero downtime)\ndocker service update --image samkarazi/bebang-erpnext-hrms:v15-newtag frappe_backend\n```\n\n**Why Swarm works:** Rolling updates recreate containers with fresh assets, eliminating stale CSS/JS issues.\n\n### Volume Safety Reference\n\n| Volume | Contains | Safe to Delete? |\n|--------|----------|-----------------|\n| `bebang-hrms_sites` | Site configs, uploads | **NO** - Data loss |\n| `bebang-hrms_db-data` | MariaDB database | **NO** - Data loss |\n| `bebang-hrms_logs` | Log files | **YES** - Just logs |\n| `bebang-hrms_assets` | Compiled CSS/JS | **YES** - Regenerated from image |\n\n**Your DocTypes, employees, APIs - all safe.** Only compiled CSS/JS is deleted and recreated.\n\n### EMERGENCY FIX: CSS 404 (If It Happens Again)\n\n**Fastest fix (30 seconds):**\n```bash\nexport AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=$(doppler secrets get AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=$(doppler secrets get AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-1\n\n# 1. Force redeploy all services (recreates containers with fresh assets)\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker service update --force frappe_backend\",\n    \"docker service update --force frappe_frontend\"\n  ]''\n\n# 2. Wait 60 seconds for services to converge\n\n# 3. Flush Redis (CRITICAL - clears cached HTML with old hashes)\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_redis-cache) redis-cli FLUSHALL\",\n    \"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_redis-queue) redis-cli FLUSHALL\"\n  ]''\n```\n\n**Why this works:** The CSS 404 happens when:\n1. `assets.json` has hash A (from cache/migrate)\n2. Actual CSS files have hash B (from Docker image)\n3. Redis caches HTML referencing hash A\n4. Force redeploy syncs assets.json to hash B\n5. Redis flush clears cached HTML, forcing fresh generation with hash B\n\n### How to Diagnose CSS 404\n\n```bash\n# 1. Check what HTML is requesting\ncurl -s https://hq.bebang.ph/ | grep -oP \"website\\.bundle\\.[A-Z0-9]+\\.css\"\n\n# 2. Check what CSS files actually exist (Swarm)\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_frontend) ls /home/frappe/frappe-bench/sites/assets/frappe/dist/css/ | grep website\"]''\n\n# 3. Check what assets.json says\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend) cat /home/frappe/frappe-bench/sites/assets/assets.json | grep website.bundle.css\"]''\n\n# 4. If hashes don''t match → Force redeploy + Redis flush (see above)\n```\n\n### Research Reference\n\nFull research report: `docs/reports/FRAPPE_DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT_RESEARCH_2026-01-28.md`\n\nSources:\n- [GitHub Issue #790](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker/issues/790)\n- [Frappe Docker FAQ](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker/wiki/Frequently-Asked-Questions)\n- [Community Discussion](https://discuss.frappe.io/t/best-way-to-deploy-new-versions-of-custom-app-in-self-hosted-docker-setup/96317)\n\n## Server Discovery Commands\n\nIf you''re unsure about server configuration, run these:\n\n```bash\n# List home directory to find frappe location\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"ls -la /home/ubuntu/\"]'' --output text --query ''Command.CommandId''\n\n# List docker volumes\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker volume ls | grep -E bebang|frappe|sites\"]'' --output text --query ''Command.CommandId''\n\n# List running containers\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"docker ps --format \\\"{{.Names}} {{.Image}}\\\"\"]'' --output text --query ''Command.CommandId''\n\n# Check what''s using a port\naws ssm send-command --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\"lsof -i :8080 || ss -tlnp | grep 8080\"]'' --output text --query ''Command.CommandId''\n\n# Get command output\naws ssm get-command-invocation --command-id \"<COMMAND_ID>\" --instance-id \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --query ''[Status, StandardOutputContent]'' --output text\n```\n\n## Files Reference\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `.github/helper/apps.json` | Apps included in Docker image |\n| `.github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yml` | CI/CD workflow |\n| `hrms/api/__init__.py` | API function exports |\n| `hrms/api/*.py` | API endpoint files |\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `/local-frappe` - **Test locally first** before production deployment\n- `/frappe-sql-bulk` - For data imports (no rebuild needed)\n- `/frappe-external-app` - For React apps via API\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:40:24.346Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing automated Frappe HRMS deployment capabilities on AWS EC2","zh":"适合需要在AWS EC2上自动化部署Frappe HRMS的DevOps代理","ja":"AWS EC2上でFrappe HRMSを自動デプロイする必要があるDevOpsエージェントに最適","ko":"AWS EC2에서 Frappe HRMS를 자동으로 배포해야 하는 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan capacidades de implementación automatizada de Frappe HRMS en AWS EC2","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin de capacités de déploiement automatisé de Frappe HRMS sur AWS EC2","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die automatisierte Bereitstellungs-Funktionen für Frappe HRMS auf AWS EC2 benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes DevOps que necessitam de capacidades de implantação automatizada do Frappe HRMS no AWS EC2","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым необходимы автоматические возможности развертывания Frappe HRMS на AWS EC2","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تثبيت Frappe HRMS أوتوماتيكية على AWS EC2"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deploy code changes from the production branch to AWS EC2 running Frappe Docker, handling Python code changes by automatically rebuilding the Docker image using --preload","zh":"赋予代理从生产分支部署代码更改到在AWS EC2上运行的Frappe Docker，使用--preload自动重新构建Docker镜像以处理Python代码更改","ja":"エージェントに、プロダクションブランチからのコード変更をAWS EC2で実行しているFrappe Dockerにデプロイする機能を提供し、--preloadを使用してPythonコード変更を自動的にDockerイメージを再構築する","ko":"에이전트가 프로덕션 브랜치에서 코드 변경 사항을 AWS EC2에서 실행 중인 Frappe Docker에 배포할 수 있도록 하며, --preload를 사용하여 Python 코드 변경 사항을 자동으로 Docker 이미지를 다시 빌드","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar cambios de código desde la rama de producción en AWS EC2 con Frappe Docker, manejando cambios de código Python mediante la reconstrucción automática de la imagen de Docker utilizando --preload","fr":"Permet aux agents de déployer des modifications de code à partir de la branche de production sur AWS EC2 exécutant Frappe Docker, en gérant les modifications de code Python en reconstruisant automatiquement l''image Docker à l''aide de --preload","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Code-Änderungen aus dem Produktionszweig in AWS EC2 mit Frappe Docker bereitzustellen, indem Python-Code-Änderungen durch automatisches Neuverwenden des Docker-Images unter Verwendung von --preload gehandhabt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implantar alterações de código da branch de produção para o AWS EC2 que executa o Frappe Docker, lidando com alterações de código Python reconstruindo automaticamente a imagem do Docker usando --preload","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью развертывать изменения кода из производственной ветки в AWS EC2, запускающий Frappe Docker, обрабатывая изменения кода Python, автоматически перестраивая образ Docker с помощью --preload","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على نشر تغييرات الشفرة من فرع الإنتاج إلى AWS EC2 الذي يعمل بنظام Frappe Docker، ويتعامل مع تغييرات شفرة Python من خلال إعادة بناء صورة Docker تلقائيًا باستخدام --preload"},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying Frappe HRMS updates to production environments","Automating Docker image rebuilds for Python code changes","Streamlining AWS EC2 deployments for Frappe applications"],"zh":["将Frappe HRMS更新部署到生产环境","自动重新构建Docker镜像以处理Python代码更改","简化Frappe应用程序的AWS EC2部署"],"ja":["Frappe HRMSの更新をプロダクション環境にデプロイする","Pythonコード変更に自動的にDockerイメージを再構築する","FrappeアプリケーションのAWS EC2デプロイを簡素化する"],"ko":["Frappe HRMS 업데이트를 프로덕션 환경에 배포","Python 코드 변경 사항에 대해 Docker 이미지를 자동으로 다시 빌드","Frappe 애플리케이션의 AWS EC2 배포를 간소화"],"es":["Implementar actualizaciones de Frappe HRMS en entornos de producción","Automatizar la reconstrucción de imágenes de Docker para cambios de código Python","Optimizar las implementaciones de AWS EC2 para aplicaciones Frappe"],"fr":["Déployer des mises à jour de Frappe HRMS dans des environnements de production","Automatiser la reconstruction d''images Docker pour les modifications de code Python","Optimiser les déploiements AWS EC2 pour les applications Frappe"],"de":["Frappe-HRMS-Updates in Produktionsumgebungen bereitzustellen","Automatisieren des Docker-Image-Neuverwendens für Python-Code-Änderungen","Optimieren der AWS-EC2-Bereitstellungen für Frappe-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Implantação de atualizações do Frappe HRMS para ambientes de produção","Automatização da reconstrução de imagens do Docker para alterações de código Python","Otimização de implantações do AWS EC2 para aplicações Frappe"],"ru":["Развертывание обновлений Frappe HRMS в производственной среде","Автоматизация перестройки образов Docker для изменений кода Python","Оптимизация развертывания AWS EC2 для приложений Frappe"],"ar":["نشر تحديثات Frappe HRMS إلى بيئات الإنتاج","أتمتة إعادة بناء صور Docker لتغييرات شفرة Python","تحسين عمليات نشر AWS EC2 لتطبيقات Frappe"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires AWS EC2 setup","Frappe Docker must be configured with --preload","Python code changes require rebuilding the Docker image"],"zh":["需要AWS EC2设置","Frappe Docker必须配置--preload","Python代码更改需要重新构建Docker镜像"],"ja":["AWS EC2の設定が必要","Frappe Dockerは--preloadで構成する必要がある","Pythonコード変更にはDockerイメージの再構築が必要"],"ko":["AWS EC2 설정이 필요","Frappe Docker는 --preload로 구성되어야 함","Python 코드 변경 사항에는 Docker 이미지를 다시 빌드해야 함"],"es":["Requiere configuración de AWS EC2","Frappe Docker debe estar configurado con --preload","Los cambios de código Python requieren la reconstrucción de la imagen de Docker"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration AWS EC2","Frappe Docker doit être configuré avec --preload","Les modifications de code Python nécessitent la reconstruction de l''image Docker"],"de":["Benötigt AWS-EC2-Konfiguration","Frappe-Docker muss mit --preload konfiguriert werden","Python-Code-Änderungen erfordern das Neuverwenden des Docker-Images"],"pt":["Requer configuração do AWS EC2","O Frappe Docker deve ser configurado com --preload","Alterações de código Python requerem reconstrução da imagem do Docker"],"ru":["Требуется настройка AWS EC2","Frappe Docker должен быть настроен с --preload","Изменения кода Python требуют перестройки образа Docker"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد AWS EC2","