e et gratuite"],"de":["220.945 Metabolit-Einträge","Detaillierte Informationen über kleine Metabolite","Wichtiges Tool für die metabolomische Forschung","Version 5.0 verfügbar","Umfassende und kostenlose Datenbank"],"pt":["220.945 entradas de metabólitos","Informações detalhadas sobre metabólitos","Recursos para pesquisa de metabolômica","Identificação de metabólitos","Biomarcadores de descoberta"],"ru":["220.945 записей метаболитов","Подробная информация о метаболитах","Ресурсы для исследований метаболомики","Идентификация метаболитов","Обнаружение биомаркеров"],"ar":["220.945 مدخل من المركبات الأيضية","معلومات مفصلة عن المركبات الأيضية","مورد للبحث في الأيض","التعرف على المركبات الأيضية","اكتشاف العلامات الحيوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["HMDB","人类代谢物","代谢组学","临床化学","生物标志物","代谢物识别","代谢物数据库"],"ja":["HMDB","人間の代謝物","代謝組学","臨床化学","生物標識","代謝物の識別","代謝物データベース"],"ko":["HMDB","인간 대사체","대사체학","임상 화학","생물 표지자","대사체의 식별","대사체 데이터베이스"],"es":["HMDB","base de datos metabolómica","investigación metabolómica","identificación de metabolitos","metabolitos pequeños","biomarcadores"],"fr":["HMDB","base de données métabolomique","recherche métabolomique","identification des métabolites","métabolites petits","biomarqueurs"],"de":["HMDB","metabolomische Datenbank","metabolomische Forschung","Identifizierung von Metaboliten","kleine Metabolite","Biomarker"],"pt":["Base de Dados HMDB","pesquisa de metabolômica","identificação de metabólitos","biomarcadores de descoberta","metabolômica","metabólitos","recursos para pesquisa científica"],"ru":["База данных HMDB","исследования метаболомики","идентификация метаболитов","обнаружение биомаркеров","метаболомика","метаболиты","ресурсы для научных исследований"],"ar":["قاعدة بيانات HMDB","البحث في الأيض","التعرف على المركبات الأيضية","اكتشاف العلامات الحيوية","الأيض","المركبات الأيضية","مورد للبحث العلمي"]}},"owner":"sanand0","repo":"scientific-research","repoPath":"sanand0/scientific-research","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.460Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hmdb-database","description":"Access Human Metabolome Database (220K+ metabolites). Search by name/ID/structure, retrieve chemical properties, biomarker data, NMR/MS spectra, pathways, for metabolomics and identification.","bodyPreview":"# HMDB Database\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Human Metabolome Database (HMDB) is a comprehensive, freely available resource containing detailed information about small molecule metabolites found in the human body.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill should be used when performing metabolomics research, clinical chemistry, biomarker discovery, or metabolite identification tasks.\n\n## Database Contents\n\nHMDB version 5.0 (current as of 2025) contains:\n\n- **220,945 metabolite entries** covering both water-so","body":"# HMDB Database\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Human Metabolome Database (HMDB) is a comprehensive, freely available resource containing detailed information about small molecule metabolites found in the human body.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill should be used when performing metabolomics research, clinical chemistry, biomarker discovery, or metabolite identification tasks.\n\n## Database Contents\n\nHMDB version 5.0 (current as of 2025) contains:\n\n- **220,945 metabolite entries** covering both water-soluble and lipid-soluble compounds\n- **8,610 protein sequences** for enzymes and transporters involved in metabolism\n- **130+ data fields per metabolite** including:\n  - Chemical properties (structure, formula, molecular weight, InChI, SMILES)\n  - Clinical data (biomarker associations, diseases, normal/abnormal concentrations)\n  - Biological information (pathways, reactions, locations)\n  - Spectroscopic data (NMR, MS, MS-MS spectra)\n  - External database links (KEGG, PubChem, MetaCyc, ChEBI, PDB, UniProt, GenBank)\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Web-Based Metabolite Searches\n\nAccess HMDB through the web interface at https://www.hmdb.ca/ for:\n\n**Text Searches:**\n- Search by metabolite name, synonym, or identifier (HMDB ID)\n- Example HMDB IDs: HMDB0000001, HMDB0001234\n- Search by disease associations or pathway involvement\n- Query by biological specimen type (urine, serum, CSF, saliva, feces, sweat)\n\n**Structure-Based Searches:**\n- Use ChemQuery for structure and substructure searches\n- Search by molecular weight or molecular weight range\n- Use SMILES or InChI strings to find compounds\n\n**Spectral Searches:**\n- LC-MS spectral matching\n- GC-MS spectral matching\n- NMR spectral searches for metabolite identification\n\n**Advanced Searches:**\n- Combine multiple criteria (name, properties, concentration ranges)\n- Filter by biological locations or specimen types\n- Search by protein/enzyme associations\n\n### 2. Accessing Metabolite Information\n\nWhen retrieving metabolite data, HMDB provides:\n\n**Chemical Information:**\n- Systematic name, traditional names, and synonyms\n- Chemical formula and molecular weight\n- Structure representations (2D/3D, SMILES, InChI, MOL file)\n- Chemical taxonomy and classification\n\n**Biological Context:**\n- Metabolic pathways and reactions\n- Associated enzymes and transporters\n- Subcellular locations\n- Biological roles and functions\n\n**Clinical Relevance:**\n- Normal concentration ranges in biological fluids\n- Biomarker associations with diseases\n- Clinical significance\n- Toxicity information when applicable\n\n**Analytical Data:**\n- Experimental and predicted NMR spectra\n- MS and MS-MS spectra\n- Retention times and chromatographic data\n- Reference peaks for identification\n\n### 3. Downloadable Datasets\n\nHMDB offers bulk data downloads at https://www.hmdb.ca/downloads in multiple formats:\n\n**Available Formats:**\n- **XML**: Complete metabolite, protein, and spectra data\n- **SDF**: Metabolite structure files for cheminformatics\n- **FASTA**: Protein and gene sequences\n- **TXT**: Raw spectra peak lists\n- **CSV/TSV**: Tabular data exports\n\n**Dataset Categories:**\n- All metabolites or filtered by specimen type\n- Protein/enzyme sequences\n- Experimental and predicted spectra (NMR, GC-MS, MS-MS)\n- Pathway information\n\n**Best Practices:**\n- Download XML format for comprehensive data including all fields\n- Use SDF format for structure-based analysis and cheminformatics workflows\n- Parse CSV/TSV formats for integration with data analysis pipelines\n- Check version dates to ensure up-to-date data (current: v5.0, 2023-07-01)\n\n**Usage Requirements:**\n- Free for academic and non-commercial research\n- Commercial use requires explicit permission (contact samackay@ualberta.ca)\n- Cite HMDB publication when using data\n\n### 4. Programmatic API Access\n\n**API Availability:**\nHMDB does not provide a public REST API. Programmatic access requires contacting the development team:\n\n- **Academic/Research groups:** Contact eponine@ualberta.ca (Eponine) or samackay@ualberta.ca (Scott)\n- **Commercial organizations:** Contact samackay@ualberta.ca (Scott) for customized API access\n\n**Alternative Programmatic Access:**\n- **R/Bioconductor**: Use the `hmdbQuery` package for R-based queries\n  - Install: `BiocManager::install(\"hmdbQuery\")`\n  - Provides HTTP-based querying functions\n- **Downloaded datasets**: Parse XML or CSV files locally for programmatic analysis\n- **Web scraping**: Not recommended; contact team for proper API access instead\n\n### 5. Common Research Workflows\n\n**Metabolite Identification in Untargeted Metabolomics:**\n1. Obtain experimental MS or NMR spectra from samples\n2. Use HMDB spectral search tools to match against reference spectra\n3. Verify candidates by checking molecular weight, retention time, and MS-MS fragmentation\n4. Review biological plausibility (expected in specimen type, known pathways)\n\n**Biomarker Discovery:**\n1. Search HMDB for metabolites associated with disease of interest\n2. Review concentration ranges in normal vs. disease states\n3. Identify metabolites with strong differential abundance\n4. Examine pathway context and biological mechanisms\n5. Cross-reference with literature via PubMed links\n\n**Pathway Analysis:**\n1. Identify metabolites of interest from experimental data\n2. Look up HMDB entries for each metabolite\n3. Extract pathway associations and enzymatic reactions\n4. Use linked SMPDB (Small Molecule Pathway Database) for pathway diagrams\n5. Identify pathway enrichment for biological interpretation\n\n**Database Integration:**\n1. Download HMDB data in XML or CSV format\n2. Parse and extract relevant fields for local database\n3. Link with external IDs (KEGG, PubChem, ChEBI) for cross-database queries\n4. Build local tools or pipelines incorporating HMDB reference data\n\n## Related HMDB Resources\n\nThe HMDB ecosystem includes related databases:\n\n- **DrugBank**: ~2,832 drug compounds with pharmaceutical information\n- **T3DB (Toxin and Toxin Target Database)**: ~3,670 toxic compounds\n- **SMPDB (Small Molecule Pathway Database)**: Pathway diagrams and maps\n- **FooDB**: ~70,000 food component compounds\n\nThese databases share similar structure and identifiers, enabling integrated queries across human metabolome, drug, toxin, and food databases.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n**Data Quality:**\n- Verify metabolite identifications with multiple evidence types (spectra, structure, properties)\n- Check experimental vs. predicted data quality indicators\n- Review citations and evidence for biomarker associations\n\n**Version Tracking:**\n- Note HMDB version used in research (current: v5.0)\n- Databases are updated periodically with new entries and corrections\n- Re-query for updates when publishing to ensure current information\n\n**Citation:**\n- Always cite HMDB in publications using the database\n- Reference specific HMDB IDs when discussing metabolites\n- Acknowledge data sources for downloaded datasets\n\n**Performance:**\n- For large-scale analysis, download complete datasets rather than repeated web queries\n- Use appropriate file formats (XML for comprehensive data, CSV for tabular analysis)\n- Consider local caching of frequently accessed metabolite information\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\nSee `references/hmdb_data_fields.md` for detailed information about available data fields and their meanings.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:42:49.476Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Scientific Research Agents needing access to comprehensive metabolite databases like HMDB","zh":"非常适合需要访问全面代谢物数据库（如HMDB）的科学研究代理","ja":"科学研究エージェントが包括的な代謝物データベース such as HMDB にアクセスする必要がある場合に最適","ko":"과학 연구 에이전트가 포괄적인 대사물 데이터베이스(HMDB 등)에 접근해야 하는 경우 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de investigación científica que necesitan acceso a bases de datos de metabolitos completas como HMDB","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de recherche scientifique ayant besoin d''accéder à des bases de données de métabolites complètes comme HMDB","de":"Perfekt für wissenschaftliche Forschungsagenten, die Zugang zu umfassenden Metabolit-Datenbanken wie HMDB benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Pesquisa Científica que necessitam de acesso a bases de dados de metabolitos abrangentes como o HMDB","ru":"Идеально подходит для научных исследовательских агентов, которым требуется доступ к всесторонним базам данных метаболитов, таким как HMDB","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البحثيين العلميين الذين يحتاجون إلى الوصول إلى قواعد بيانات شاملة عن المستقلبات مثل قاعدة بيانات HMDB"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform advanced metabolomics research, clinical chemistry, and biomarker discovery tasks by leveraging the vast repository of 220,945 metabolite entries in HMDB version 5.0, utilizing detailed information about small molecule metabolites found in the human body","zh":"通过利用HMDB 5.0版本中的220,945个代谢物条目，赋予代理执行高级代谢组学研究、临床化学和生物标志物发现任务的能力，利用有关人体中小分子代谢物的详细信息","ja":"HMDBバージョン5.0の220,945の代謝物エントリを利用して、代理が高級な代謝組学研究、臨床化学、バイオマーカー発見タスクを実行できるようにし、人体内での小分子代謝物に関する詳細な情報を利用する","ko":"HMDB 버전 5.0의 220,945개 대사물 항목을 활용하여 에이전트가 고급 대사체학 연구, 임상 화학 및 바이오 마커 발견 작업을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 인체 내的小 분자 대사물에 대한 자세한 정보를 활용함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar tareas de investigación de metabolómica avanzada, química clínica y descubrimiento de biomarcadores mediante la explotación del vasto repositorio de 220,945 entradas de metabolitos en la versión 5.0 de HMDB, utilizando información detallada sobre metabolitos de moléculas pequeñas encontrados en el cuerpo humano","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des tâches de recherche de métabolomique avancée, de chimie clinique et de découverte de biomarqueurs en exploitant le vaste répertoire de 220,945 entrées de métabolites dans la version 5.0 de HMDB, en utilisant des informations détaillées sur les petit molécules métabolites trouvés dans le corps humain","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, fortgeschrittene Metabolomik-Forschung, klinische Chemie und Biomarker-Entdeckungsaufgaben durchzuführen, indem sie das umfangreiche Repository von 220,945 Metabolit-Einträgen in der Version 5.0 von HMDB nutzen und detaillierte Informationen über kleine Molekül-Metabolite im menschlichen Körper verwenden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizarem pesquisas avançadas de metabolômica, química clínica e descoberta de biomarcadores, aproveitando o vasto repositório de 220.945 entradas de metabolitos na versão 5.0 do HMDB, utilizando informações detalhadas sobre metabolitos de moléculas pequenas encontradas no corpo humano","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить передовые исследования метаболомики, клинической химии и открытия биомаркеров, используя обширный репозиторий 220 945 записей метаболитов в версии 5.0 HMDB, используя подробную информацию о малых молекулах метаболитов, найденных в человеческом теле","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إجراء بحوث متقدمة في مجال الأيضوميات والكيمياء السريرية واكتشاف العلامات الحيوية من خلال الاستفادة من المستودع الضخم الذي يحتوي على 220,945 مدخلاً لمستقلبات في الإصدار 5.0 من قاعدة بيانات HMDB، مع استخدام المعلومات المفصلة حول المستقلبات الصغيرة الجزيئية الموجودة في الجسم البشري"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating metabolite identification","Generating biomarker discovery workflows","Analyzing clinical chemistry data with HMDB integration"],"zh":["自动化代谢物识别","生成生物标志物发现工作流","分析具有HMDB集成的临床化学数据"],"ja":["代謝物識別の自動化","バイオマーカー発見ワークフローの生成","HMDB統合を使用した臨床化学データの分析"],"ko":["대사물 식별 자동화","바이오 마커 발견 워크플로 생성","HMDB 통합을 사용한 임상 화학 데이터 분석"],"es":["Automatizar la identificación de metabolitos","Generar flujos de trabajo de descubrimiento de biomarcadores","Analizar datos de química clínica con integración de HMDB"],"fr":["Automatiser l''identification des métabolites","Générer des flux de travail de découverte de biomarqueurs","Analyser des données de chimie clinique avec intégration de HMDB"],"de":["Automatisierung der Identifizierung von Metaboliten","Erzeugen von Biomarker-Entdeckungs-Workflows","Analyse von klinischen Chemie-Daten mit HMDB-Integration"],"pt":["Automatizar a identificação de metabolitos","Gerar fluxos de trabalho para a descoberta de biomarcadores","Analisar dados de química clínica com integração do HMDB"],"ru":["Автоматизировать идентификацию метаболитов","Генерировать рабочие процессы для открытия биомаркеров","Анализировать данные клинической химии с интеграцией HMDB"],"ar":["أتمتة تحديد المستقلبات","إنشاء تدفقات عمل لاكتشاف العلامات الحيوية","تحليل بيانات الكيمياء السريرية مع دمج قاعدة بيانات HMDB"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires HMDB version 5.0 or later for optimal results","Limited to human metabolome data"],"zh":["需要HMDB 5.0或更高版本才能获得最佳结果","仅限于人类代谢组数据"],"ja":["最適な結果を得るにはHMDB 5.0以降が必要","ヒトの代謝組データに限定される"],"ko":["최적의 결과를 얻으려면 HMDB 5.0 이상이 필요함","인간 대사체 데이터에만 한정됨"],"es":["Requiere la versión 5.0 de HMDB o posterior para resultados óptimos","Limitado a datos del metaboloma humano"],"fr":["Nécessite la version 5.0 de HMDB ou ultérieure pour des résultats optimaux","Limité aux données du métabolome humain"],"de":["Benötigt HMDB-Version 5.0 oder höher für optimale Ergebnisse","Begrenzt auf Daten des menschlichen Metaboloms"],"pt":["Requer a versão 5.0 ou posterior do HMDB para resultados ótimos","Limitado a dados do metaboloma humano"],"ru":["Требуется версия 5.0 или более поздняя версия HMDB для оптимальных результатов","Ограничен данными человеческого метаболома"],"ar":["يتطلب الإصدار 5.0 أو الإصدارات الأحدث من قاعدة بيانات HMDB للحصول على نتائج مثالية","محدود ببيانات الميتابولوم البشري"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
