Práticas","ru":"Создайте PR для вашей ветки с лучшими практиками","ar":"إنشاء طلب سحب لفرعك مع أفضل الممارسات","en":"pr"},"description":{"zh":"PR技能用于自动创建和更新Pull Request，确保代码变更清晰可审查。","ja":"PRスキルは自動的にプルリクエストを作成および更新して、コードの変更を明確にレビューできるようにします。","ko":"PR 스킬은 자동으로 풀 리퀘스트를 생성 및 업데이트하여 코드 변경 사항을 명확하게 검토할 수 있습니다.","es":"El protocolo de servidor de colaboración de datos narrativos para PR permite crear y actualizar solicitudes de extracción de forma eficiente","fr":"Le protocole de serveur de collaboration de données narratives pour PR permet de créer et de mettre à jour des demandes d''extraction de manière efficace","de":"Das Modell-Kontext-Protokoll für die Narrative Data Collaboration Platform ermöglicht das effiziente Erstellen und Aktualisieren von Pull-Requests","pt":"O skill ''pr'' cria um PR para o branch atual, se não existir, ou atualiza se já existir, seguindo as melhores práticas para títulos e descrições de PR","ru":"Навык ''pr'' создает PR для текущей ветки, если она не существует, или обновляет ее, если она уже существует, следуя лучшим практикам для названий и описаний PR","ar":"مهارة ''pr'' tạo طلب سحب لفرعك الحالي، إذا لم يكن موجودًا، أو تحديثه إذا كان موجودًا، متبعة أفضل الممارسات لأسماء ووصف طلبات السحب","en":"Model Context Protocol server for the Narrative Data Collaboration Platform. "},"definition":{"en":"Model Context Protocol server for the Narrative Data Collaboration Platform. "},"features":{"zh":["自动创建Pull Request","更新现有的Pull Request","清晰的代码变更描述","一致的Pull Request标题格式","最佳实践指南"],"ja":["プルリクエストの自動作成","既存のプルリクエストの更新","コードの変更の明確な説明","一貫したプルリクエストタイトルの形式","ベストプラクティスガイド"],"ko":["풀 리퀘스트 자동 생성","既存의 풀 리퀘스트 업데이트","코드 변경 사항의 명확한 설명","일貫된 풀 리퀘스트 제목 형식","베스트 프랙티스 가이드"],"es":["Creación y actualización de solicitudes de extracción","Mejores prácticas para títulos y descripciones de PR","Consistencia en el código","Colaboración de datos narrativos","Protocolo de servidor de colaboración"],"fr":["Création et mise à jour de demandes d''extraction","Meilleures pratiques pour les titres et les descriptions de PR","Consistance dans le code","Collaboration de données narratives","Protocole de serveur de collaboration"],"de":["Erstellen und Aktualisieren von Pull-Requests","Best Practices für PR-Titel und -Beschreibungen","Konsistenz im Code","Narrative Data Collaboration","Modell-Kontext-Protokoll-Server"],"pt":["Criação de PR para branch atual","Atualização de PR existente","Melhores práticas para títulos de PR","Melhores práticas para descrições de PR","Integração com Narrative Data Collaboration Platform"],"ru":["Создание PR для текущей ветки","Обновление существующего PR","Лучшие практики для названий PR","Лучшие практики для описаний PR","Интеграция с платформой Narrative Data Collaboration"],"ar":["إنشاء طلب سحب لفرعك الحالي","تحديث طلب سحب موجود","أفضل الممارسات لأسماء طلبات السحب","أفضل الممارسات لوصف طلبات السحب","التكامل مع منصة Narrative Data Collaboration"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PR技能","Pull Request","代码审查","自动化","Model Context Protocol","Narrative Data Collaboration Platform"],"ja":["PRスキル","プルリクエスト","コードレビュー","自動化","Model Context Protocol","Narrative Data Collaboration Platform"],"ko":["PR 스킬","풀 리퀘스트","코드 리뷰","자동화","Model Context Protocol","Narrative Data Collaboration Platform"],"es":["protocolo de servidor de colaboración","colaboración de datos narrativos","solicitudes de extracción","PR","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de software","colaboración de código"],"fr":["protocole de serveur de collaboration","collaboration de données narratives","demandes d''extraction","PR","meilleures pratiques","développement de logiciels","collaboration de code"],"de":["Modell-Kontext-Protokoll-Server","Narrative Data Collaboration","Pull-Requests","PR","Best Practices","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Collaboration"],"pt":["PR","Pull Request","Melhores Práticas","Narrative Data Collaboration Platform","Desenvolvimento de Software","Colaboração de Código","Revisão de Código"],"ru":["PR","Запрос на вытягивание","Лучшие практики","Платформа Narrative Data Collaboration","Разработка программного обеспечения","Сотрудничество по коду","Обзор кода"],"ar":["طلب السحب","طلب السحب Pull Request","أفضل الممارسات","منصة Narrative Data Collaboration","تطوير البرمجيات","التعاون في الكود","مراجعة الكود"]}},"owner":"narrative-io","repo":"data-collaboration-mcp","repoPath":"narrative-io/data-collaboration-mcp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.460Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pr","description":"Create a new PR for the current branch or update an existing one. Follows team PR best practices for titles, descriptions, and checklists.","bodyPreview":"Create a PR for the current branch if one doesn''t exist.  If one does exist, update it.  Use the guide below for best practices.\n\n# Pull Request Best Practices Guide\n\n## Overview\nThis guide outlines best practices for writing pull request (PR) titles and descriptions. Following these guidelines ensures your PRs are clear, reviewable, and maintain a consistent standard across our codebase.\n\n## PR Title Guidelines\n\n### Format\nUse a consistent format that clearly communicates the change type and sc","body":"Create a PR for the current branch if one doesn''t exist.  If one does exist, update it.  Use the guide below for best practices.\n\n# Pull Request Best Practices Guide\n\n## Overview\nThis guide outlines best practices for writing pull request (PR) titles and descriptions. Following these guidelines ensures your PRs are clear, reviewable, and maintain a consistent standard across our codebase.\n\n## PR Title Guidelines\n\n### Format\nUse a consistent format that clearly communicates the change type and scope:\n\n```\n[Type] Brief description of change\n```\n\n### Types\n- `[Feature]` - New functionality or capability\n- `[Fix]` - Bug fixes or corrections\n- `[Refactor]` - Code restructuring without changing functionality\n- `[Perf]` - Performance improvements\n- `[Docs]` - Documentation updates\n- `[Test]` - Test additions or modifications\n- `[Chore]` - Maintenance tasks, dependency updates\n- `[Style]` - Code formatting, naming conventions\n\n### Title Best Practices\n1. **Be concise but descriptive** (50-72 characters ideal)\n   - ✅ `[Feature] Add user authentication via OAuth2`\n   - ❌ `[Feature] Added auth`\n\n2. **Use imperative mood** (as if giving a command)\n   - ✅ `[Fix] Resolve memory leak in data processor`\n   - ❌ `[Fix] Fixed memory leak in data processor`\n\n3. **Include ticket/issue reference when applicable**\n   - ✅ `[Feature] Add payment gateway integration (PROJ-1234)`\n   - ✅ `[Fix] Prevent duplicate submissions in checkout flow #5678`\n\n4. **Be specific about what changed**\n   - ✅ `[Refactor] Extract validation logic into separate service`\n   - ❌ `[Refactor] Code cleanup`\n\n## PR Description Template\n\nUse this template for all PRs:\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\nBrief overview of what this PR accomplishes and why it''s needed.\n\n## Changes Made\n- Bullet point list of specific changes\n- Group related changes together\n- Be specific about what was modified\n\n## Type of Change\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change fixing an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change adding functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature causing existing functionality to change)\n- [ ] Refactoring (no functional changes)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Performance improvement\n\n## Testing\nDescribe the testing performed:\n- Unit tests added/modified\n- Integration tests\n- Manual testing steps\n- Test coverage impact\n\n## Screenshots/Recordings (if applicable)\nInclude visual evidence for UI changes\n\n## Related Issues\nCloses #(issue number)\nRelated to #(issue number)\n\n## Deployment Notes\nAny special deployment considerations, migrations, or configuration changes\n\n## Checklist\n- [ ] Code follows team style guidelines\n- [ ] Self-review completed\n- [ ] Comments added for complex logic\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n- [ ] Tests added/updated\n- [ ] All tests passing\n- [ ] No console.log or debug code left\n- [ ] Breaking changes documented\n- [ ] If this PR completes a Shortcut Ticket, move the Ticket into Review (in Workflow: Default)\n```\n\n## Writing Effective Descriptions\n\n### Summary Section\nThe summary should answer three questions:\n1. **What** does this PR do?\n2. **Why** is this change necessary?\n3. **How** does it solve the problem?\n\nExample:\n```markdown\n## Summary\nThis PR implements rate limiting for our public API endpoints to prevent abuse and ensure service stability. Previously, there were no limits on API calls, which led to service degradation during high-traffic periods. This solution uses Redis to track and limit requests per IP address to 100 requests per minute.\n```\n\n### Changes Made Section\nBe specific and organize changes logically:\n\n```markdown\n## Changes Made\nAuthentication Changes:\n- Added JWT token validation middleware\n- Implemented refresh token rotation\n- Added token expiration handling\n\nDatabase Changes:\n- Created user_sessions table\n- Added indexes for performance optimization\n- Updated user table with last_login timestamp\n\nAPI Changes:\n- New endpoint: POST /api/auth/refresh\n- Modified: GET /api/user/profile (now requires authentication)\n- Deprecated: GET /api/user/public-profile\n```\n\n### Testing Section\nProvide enough detail for reviewers to verify your testing:\n\n```markdown\n## Testing\nUnit Tests:\n- Added 15 new tests for AuthService\n- Modified existing UserController tests for new auth flow\n- Test coverage increased from 78% to 85%\n\nManual Testing:\n1. Login with valid credentials - Success\n2. Login with invalid credentials - Returns 401\n3. Access protected endpoint with valid token - Success\n4. Access protected endpoint with expired token - Returns 401, prompts refresh\n5. Refresh token flow - Successfully generates new token pair\n\nLoad Testing:\n- Tested with 1000 concurrent users\n- Average response time: 45ms\n- No memory leaks detected\n```\n\n## Best Practices by PR Type\n\n### Feature PRs\n- Clearly explain the business value\n- Include user-facing changes\n- Document any new APIs or interfaces\n- Provide usage examples if applicable\n\n### Bug Fix PRs\n- Describe the bug and its impact\n- Explain root cause if known\n- Include steps to reproduce\n- Verify fix doesn''t introduce regressions\n\n### Refactoring PRs\n- Justify why refactoring is needed\n- Confirm no functional changes\n- Highlight performance improvements if any\n- Include before/after metrics when relevant\n\n### Performance PRs\n- Include benchmark results\n- Show before/after comparisons\n- Explain optimization techniques used\n- Document any trade-offs\n\n## Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n1. **Vague descriptions**\n   - ❌ \"Fixed stuff\"\n   - ✅ \"Fixed null pointer exception in user profile loader when email is missing\"\n\n2. **Missing context**\n   - ❌ \"Updated API\"\n   - ✅ \"Updated API to support pagination for large result sets (>1000 items)\"\n\n3. **Combining unrelated changes**\n   - Keep PRs focused on a single concern\n   - Create separate PRs for unrelated fixes\n\n4. **Insufficient testing information**\n   - Always describe how changes were tested\n   - Include edge cases considered\n\n5. **Forgetting deployment considerations**\n   - Note any database migrations\n   - Mention configuration changes\n   - Flag breaking changes prominently\n\n## Review-Friendly Practices\n\n1. **Keep PRs small and focused**\n   - Aim for <400 lines of changes\n   - Split large features into smaller PRs\n\n2. **Provide context for reviewers**\n   - Link to design docs or discussions\n   - Explain complex algorithms or business logic\n\n3. **Use draft PRs for work in progress**\n   - Mark PR as draft if not ready for review\n   - Update description when ready\n\n4. **Respond to feedback constructively**\n   - Address all comments before requesting re-review\n   - Explain if you disagree with suggestions\n\n## Examples of Excellent PR Descriptions\n\n### Feature Example\n```markdown\n## Summary\nImplements real-time notifications for order status updates. Customers previously had to refresh the page to see order updates, leading to poor user experience and increased server load. This PR adds WebSocket support to push updates instantly when order status changes.\n\n## Changes Made\nBackend:\n- Added WebSocket server using Socket.io\n- Created NotificationService for managing connections\n- Integrated with existing OrderService for status updates\n\nFrontend:\n- Added WebSocket client connection handling\n- Created notification toast component\n- Updated order tracking page with real-time updates\n\nInfrastructure:\n- Added Redis for managing WebSocket sessions across servers\n- Updated nginx configuration for WebSocket support\n\n[... continues with full template ...]\n```\n\n### Bug Fix Example\n```markdown\n## Summary\nFixes critical bug where users could place duplicate orders by rapidly clicking the submit button. This resulted in multiple charges and inventory discrepancies. The fix implements request debouncing and adds server-side duplicate detection.\n\n## Changes Made\n- Added 2-second debounce to order submit button\n- Implemented idempotency key for order creation endpoint\n- Added database constraint to prevent duplicate orders within 5-minute window\n- Updated error handling to show user-friendly messages\n\n[... continues with full template ...]\n```\n\nRemember: A well-written PR description saves review time, prevents misunderstandings, and serves as valuable documentation for future reference. Take the time to write clear, comprehensive PR descriptions—your teammates and future self will thank you!\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:44:26.676Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing standardized pull request management and Narrative Data Collaboration Platform integration.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化拉取请求管理和Narrative Data Collaboration Platform集成的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが標準化されたプルリクエスト管理とナラティブデータコラボレーションプラットフォームの統合を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"표준화된 풀 리퀘스트 관리 및 내러티브 데이터 협업 플랫폼 통합이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan una gestión de solicitudes de extracción estandarizada y una integración con la Plataforma de Colaboración de Datos Narrativos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Revue de Code nécessitant une gestion standardisée des demandes d''extraction et une intégration à la Plateforme de Collaboration de Données Narratives.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die eine standardisierte Pull-Request-Verwaltung und eine Integration in die Narrative Data Collaboration Platform benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de gerenciamento de solicitações de pull padronizado e integração com a Plataforma de Colaboração de Dados Narrativos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, требующих стандартизированного управления запросами на включение и интеграции с Платформой сотрудничества в области повествовательных данных.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة طلبات السحب المعيارية وتكامل منصة تعاون بيانات السرد."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and update pull requests following best practices, utilizing consistent formats for PR titles and descriptions, and maintaining a reviewable standard across the codebase using the Model Context Protocol server.","zh":"赋予代理创建和更新拉取请求的能力，遵循最佳实践，使用一致的格式为PR标题和描述，并在代码库中使用模型上下文协议服务器维护可审查的标准。","ja":"エージェントがプルリクエストを作成および更新する能力を付与し、ベストプラクティスに従い、PRタイトルと説明のための一貫した形式を使用し、コードベース全体でレビュー可能な標準をモデルコンテキストプロトコルサーバーを使用して維持します。","ko":"에이전트가 풀 리퀘스트를 생성 및 업데이트할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 최선의 실践을 따르며, PR 제목 및 설명을 위한 일관된 형식을 사용하며, 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜 서버를 사용하여 코드베이스 전반에 걸쳐 검토 가능한 표준을 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y actualizar solicitudes de extracción siguiendo las mejores prácticas, utilizando formatos consistentes para títulos y descripciones de PR, y manteniendo un estándar revisable en todo el código utilizando el servidor del Protocolo de Contexto del Modelo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de mettre à jour des demandes d''extraction en suivant les meilleures pratiques, en utilisant des formats cohérents pour les titres et les descriptions des PR, et en maintenant un standard révisable dans tout le codebase en utilisant le serveur du Protocole de Contexte de Modèle.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Pull-Requests zu erstellen und zu aktualisieren, indem sie Best Practices befolgen, konsistente Formate für PR-Titel und -Beschreibungen verwenden und einen überprüfbaren Standard im gesamten Codebase mithilfe des Model Context Protocol-Servers beibehalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e atualizar solicitações de pull seguindo as melhores práticas, utilizando formatos consistentes para títulos e descrições de PR e mantendo um padrão revisável em todo o código-fonte usando o servidor do Protocolo de Contexto do Modelo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и обновлять запросы на включение, следуя лучшим практикам, используя последовательные форматы для названий и описаний PR, и поддерживая проверяемый стандарт на всём кодовом базисе с помощью сервера Протокола контекста модели.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء وتحديث طلبات السحب اتباعًا لأفضل الممارسات، واستخدام تنسيقات متسقة لأسماء ووصفات PR، والاحتفاظ بمعيار قابل للاستعراض في جميع أنحاء قاعدة الشفرة باستخدام خادم بروتوكول سياق النموذج."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pull request creation for new branches","Updating existing pull requests with standardized descriptions","Ensuring consistent pull request formatting across the codebase"],"zh":["自动为新分支创建拉取请求","使用标准化描述更新现有拉取请求","确保代码库中拉取请求的一致性格式"],"ja":["新しいブランチのプルリクエストの自動作成","標準化された説明を使用して既存のプルリクエストを更新する","コードベース全体でプルリクエストのフォーマットの一貫性を確保する"],"ko":["새로운 브랜치에 대한 풀 리퀘스트 자동 생성","표준화된 설명을 사용하여 기존 풀 리퀘스트를 업데이트하는 것","코드베이스 전반에 걸쳐 풀 리퀘스트 형식의 일관성을 보장하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de solicitudes de extracción para nuevas ramas","Actualización de solicitudes de extracción existentes con descripciones estandarizadas","Garantía de un formato de solicitud de extracción coherente en todo el código"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de demandes d''extraction pour les nouvelles branches","Mise à jour des demandes d''extraction existantes avec des descriptions standardisées","Assurance d''un format de demande d''extraction cohérent dans tout le codebase"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Pull-Requests für neue Branches","Aktualisierung bestehender Pull-Requests mit standardisierten Beschreibungen","Gewährleistung eines konsistenten Pull-Request-Formats im gesamten Codebase"],"pt":["Automação da criação de solicitações de pull para novos ramos","Atualização de solicitações de pull existentes com descrições padronizadas","Garantia de formatação consistente de solicitações de pull em todo o código-fonte"],"ru":["Автоматизация создания запросов на включение для новых веток","Обновление существующих запросов на включение с стандартизированными описаниями","Обеспечение последовательного форматирования запросов на включение на всём кодовом базисе"],"ar":["أتمتة إنشاء طلبات السحب للفروع الجديدة","تحديث طلبات السحب الحالية bằngوصفات معيارية","ضمان تنسيق متسق لطلبات السحب في جميع أنحاء قاعدة الشفرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the Narrative Data Collaboration Platform","Must follow the Pull Request Best Practices Guide"],"zh":["需要访问Narrative Data Collaboration Platform","必须遵循Pull Request Best Practices Guide"],"ja":["ナラティブデータコラボレーションプラットフォームへのアクセスが必要","プルリクエストベストプラクティスガイドに従う必要がある"],"ko":["내러티브 데이터 협업 플랫폼에 대한 액세스가 필요함","풀 리퀘스트 최고의 실践 가이드를 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la Plataforma de Colaboración de Datos Narrativos","Debe seguir la Guía de Mejores Prácticas para Solicitudes de Extracción"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la Plateforme de Collaboration de Données Narratives","Doit suivre le Guide des Meilleures Pratiques pour les Demandes d''Extraction"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Narrative Data Collaboration Platform","Muss dem Leitfaden für Best Practices für Pull-Requests folgen"],"pt":["Requer acesso à Plataforma de Colaboração de Dados Narrativos","Deve seguir o Guia de Melhores Práticas para Solicitações de Pull"],"ru":["Требует доступа к Платформе сотрудничества в области повествовательных данных","Должно следовать Руководству по лучшим практикам для запросов на включение"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى منصة تعاون بيانات السرد","يجب اتباع دليل أفضل الممارسات لطلبات السحب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
