 issues in the Freshbooks website"},"features":{"zh":["使用context7 MCP优化Ember.js应用","提高Freshbooks网站速度","遵循Ember Octane约定","支持当前最佳实践","提供项目特定约定和架构模式","确保编码标准和技术决策"],"ja":["context7 MCPを使用してEmber.jsアプリを最適化する","Freshbooksウェブサイトの速度を向上させる","Ember Octane約定に従う","現在のベストプラクティスをサポートする","プロジェクト特有の約定とアーキテクチャパターンを提供する","コーディング規範と技術的決定を確保する"],"ko":["context7 MCP를 사용하여 Ember.js 애플리케이션을 최적화합니다","Freshbooks 웹사이트의 속도를 개선합니다","Ember Octane 규칙을 따릅니다","현재의 베스트 프랙티스를 지원합니다","프로젝트 특정 규약과 아키텍처 패턴을 제공합니다","코딩 표준과 기술적 결정을 보장합니다"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de aplicações Ember.js performáticas","Uso de convenções Ember Octane","Seguimento das melhores práticas atuais","Uso do context7 MCP para verificar documentação","Criação de aplicações web modernas","Melhoria da velocidade e do desempenho"],"ru":["Создание производительных приложений Ember.js","Использование конвенций Ember Octane","Следование текущим лучшим практикам","Использование context7 MCP для проверки документации","Создание современных веб-приложений","Улучшение скорости и производительности"],"ar":["إنشاء تطبيقات إمبير جيه إس قادرة على التنفيذ","استخدام اتفاقيات إمبير أوكتان","اتباع أفضل الممارسات الحالية","استخدام سياق 7 إم سي بي لتحقق الوثائق","إنشاء تطبيقات ويب حديثة","تحسين السرعة والأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Ember.js性能优化","Freshbooks网站速度优化","context7 MCP","Ember Octane","最佳实践","项目特定约定","架构模式","编码标准","技术决策"],"ja":["Ember.jsパフォーマンス最適化","Freshbooksウェブサイトの速度最適化","context7 MCP","Ember Octane","ベストプラクティス","プロジェクト特有の約定","アーキテクチャパターン","コーディング規範","技術的決定"],"ko":["Ember.js 성능 최적화","Freshbooks 웹사이트 속도 최적화","context7 MCP","Ember Octane","베스트 프랙티스","프로젝트 특정 규약","아키텍처 패턴","코딩 표준","기술적 결정을"],"pt":["Ember.js","Desenvolvimento web","Aplicações performáticas","Convenções Ember Octane","Melhores práticas","Context7 MCP","JavaScript","Framework","Desenvolvimento de aplicações"],"ru":["Ember.js","Веб-разработка","Производительные приложения","Конвенции Ember Octane","Лучшие практики","Context7 MCP","JavaScript","Фреймворк","Создание приложений"],"ar":["إمبير جيه إس","تطوير الويب","تطبيقات قادرة على التنفيذ","اتفاقيات إمبير أوكتان","أفضل الممارسات","سياق 7 إم سي بي","جافاسكريبت","إطار العمل","إنشاء التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"jaredlander","repo":"freshbooks-speed","repoPath":"jaredlander/freshbooks-speed","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.460Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"javascript-ember","description":"Expert-level Ember.js development. Use when asked to (1) write Ember.js applications with components, services, routes, or controllers, (2) implement Ember Data models and adapters, (3) work with Ember Octane patterns (Glimmer components, tracked properties, modifiers), (4) optimize Ember application performance, (5) write Ember tests with QUnit or testing-library, or when phrases like Ember component, Ember route, Glimmer, tracked property, Ember addon appear.","bodyPreview":"# Expert Ember.js Development\n\nWrite modern, performant Ember.js applications following Ember Octane conventions and current best practices.\n\n## Critical First Step: Use context7 MCP\n\n**ALWAYS use context7 MCP before writing or editing ANY Ember code** - Before generating, modifying, or reviewing any Ember code, you MUST use the context7 MCP to check for relevant documentation. Context7 provides project-specific conventions, architectural patterns, coding standards, and technical decisions that","body":"# Expert Ember.js Development\n\nWrite modern, performant Ember.js applications following Ember Octane conventions and current best practices.\n\n## Critical First Step: Use context7 MCP\n\n**ALWAYS use context7 MCP before writing or editing ANY Ember code** - Before generating, modifying, or reviewing any Ember code, you MUST use the context7 MCP to check for relevant documentation. Context7 provides project-specific conventions, architectural patterns, coding standards, and technical decisions that override these general guidelines.\n\n### When to Use context7\n\nUse context7 MCP in these situations:\n- Before writing any new Ember component, route, service, or model\n- Before modifying existing Ember code\n- When implementing features that might have project-specific patterns\n- When unsure about architectural decisions\n- Before suggesting refactors or improvements\n\n### How to Use context7\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Check for Ember component patterns before creating a component\n// Use the context7 MCP to search for relevant documentation\n// Query examples:\n// - \"ember component patterns\"\n// - \"ember routing conventions\" \n// - \"ember data models\"\n// - \"ember testing standards\"\n// - \"glimmer component lifecycle\"\n\n// Apply the documentation from context7 to your implementation\n```\n\n**If context7 returns relevant documentation, follow it EXACTLY even if it conflicts with this skill''s general guidance.** Project-specific conventions always take precedence.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Embrace Ember Octane** - Use Glimmer components, tracked properties, and native classes\n2. **Convention over configuration** - Follow Ember''s resolver patterns and file structure\n3. **Use the platform** - Prefer native JavaScript features over framework-specific abstractions when possible\n4. **Composition through services and modifiers** - Extract reusable logic into services and UI behavior into modifiers\n5. **Data down, actions up (DDAU)** - Maintain clear data flow patterns\n\n## Context7 MCP Workflow\n\nBefore implementing any Ember code, follow this workflow:\n\n1. **Query context7** - Search for relevant documentation using specific terms:\n   - Component type (e.g., \"ember glimmer component\")\n   - Feature area (e.g., \"ember routing\", \"ember data\")\n   - Specific pattern (e.g., \"form validation\", \"authentication\")\n\n2. **Review results** - Read any returned documentation carefully\n   - Note project-specific naming conventions\n   - Identify required patterns or abstractions\n   - Check for mandatory testing requirements\n   - Look for deprecated approaches to avoid\n\n3. **Apply documentation** - Implement code following context7 guidance\n   - Use project-specific utilities and helpers\n   - Follow established architectural patterns\n   - Match existing code style and structure\n   - Include required metadata or annotations\n\n4. **Fall back to general patterns** - If context7 has no relevant docs, use this skill''s patterns\n   - Apply standard Ember Octane conventions\n   - Follow community best practices\n   - Use examples from this skill as templates\n\n**Remember: context7 documentation always overrides this skill''s general guidance.**\n\n### Context7 Query Examples\n\nWhen implementing different types of Ember code, use these query patterns:\n\n**For Components:**\n```\n- \"ember component patterns\"\n- \"ember component architecture\"\n- \"glimmer component conventions\"\n- \"[specific component type]\" (e.g., \"button component\", \"form component\")\n- \"component props\" or \"component arguments\"\n- \"component lifecycle\"\n- \"component testing\"\n```\n\n**For Routes:**\n```\n- \"ember routing patterns\"\n- \"ember route conventions\"\n- \"route data loading\"\n- \"route guards\" or \"route authentication\"\n- \"nested routes\"\n- \"query parameters\"\n```\n\n**For Ember Data:**\n```\n- \"ember data models\"\n- \"ember data adapters\"\n- \"ember data serializers\"\n- \"api integration\"\n- \"data relationships\"\n- \"data layer patterns\"\n```\n\n**For Services:**\n```\n- \"ember services\"\n- \"service patterns\"\n- \"shared state management\"\n- \"[specific service]\" (e.g., \"authentication service\", \"api service\")\n```\n\n**For Testing:**\n```\n- \"ember testing\"\n- \"component testing\"\n- \"integration tests\"\n- \"acceptance tests\"\n- \"test patterns\"\n- \"test data\" or \"fixtures\"\n```\n\n**For Styling:**\n```\n- \"ember styling\"\n- \"css conventions\"\n- \"component styles\"\n- \"tailwind\" or \"[css framework]\"\n```\n\n**When Editing Existing Code:**\n```\n- Search for the specific feature: \"user profile\", \"login form\", etc.\n- Search for the pattern you''re implementing: \"form validation\", \"dropdown menu\"\n- Search for utilities you might need: \"validation utilities\", \"date helpers\"\n```\n\n## Modern Ember Patterns (Octane+)\n\n### Glimmer Components\n\n```javascript\n// app/components/user-profile.js\nimport Component from ''@glimmer/component'';\nimport { tracked } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\nimport { action } from ''@ember/object'';\nimport { inject as service } from ''@ember/service'';\n\nexport default class UserProfileComponent extends Component {\n  @service currentUser;\n  @service router;\n  \n  @tracked isEditing = false;\n  @tracked formData = null;\n\n  constructor(owner, args) {\n    super(owner, args);\n    // Use constructor for one-time setup\n    this.formData = { ...this.args.user };\n  }\n\n  @action\n  toggleEdit() {\n    this.isEditing = !this.isEditing;\n    if (this.isEditing) {\n      this.formData = { ...this.args.user };\n    }\n  }\n\n  @action\n  async saveUser(event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    \n    try {\n      await this.args.onSave(this.formData);\n      this.isEditing = false;\n    } catch (error) {\n      // Handle error\n      console.error(''Save failed:'', error);\n    }\n  }\n\n  @action\n  updateField(field, event) {\n    this.formData = {\n      ...this.formData,\n      [field]: event.target.value\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```handlebars\n{{! app/components/user-profile.hbs }}\n<div class=\"user-profile\">\n  {{#if this.isEditing}}\n    <form {{on \"submit\" this.saveUser}}>\n      <label>\n        Name:\n        <input \n          type=\"text\" \n          value={{this.formData.name}}\n          {{on \"input\" (fn this.updateField \"name\")}}\n        />\n      </label>\n      \n      <label>\n        Email:\n        <input \n          type=\"email\" \n          value={{this.formData.email}}\n          {{on \"input\" (fn this.updateField \"email\")}}\n        />\n      </label>\n      \n      <button type=\"submit\">Save</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" {{on \"click\" this.toggleEdit}}>Cancel</button>\n    </form>\n  {{else}}\n    <div class=\"profile-display\">\n      <h2>{{@user.name}}</h2>\n      <p>{{@user.email}}</p>\n      \n      {{#if this.currentUser.canEdit}}\n        <button {{on \"click\" this.toggleEdit}}>Edit Profile</button>\n      {{/if}}\n    </div>\n  {{/if}}\n</div>\n```\n\n### Tracked Properties and Getters\n\n```javascript\nimport Component from ''@glimmer/component'';\nimport { tracked } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\nimport { cached } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\n\nexport default class DataGridComponent extends Component {\n  @tracked sortColumn = ''name'';\n  @tracked sortDirection = ''asc'';\n  @tracked filterText = '''';\n\n  // Use @cached for expensive computations that depend on tracked properties\n  @cached\n  get filteredData() {\n    const { filterText } = this;\n    if (!filterText) return this.args.data;\n    \n    const lower = filterText.toLowerCase();\n    return this.args.data.filter(item => \n      item.name.toLowerCase().includes(lower) ||\n      item.email.toLowerCase().includes(lower)\n    );\n  }\n\n  @cached\n  get sortedData() {\n    const data = [...this.filteredData];\n    const { sortColumn, sortDirection } = this;\n    \n    return data.sort((a, b) => {\n      const aVal = a[sortColumn];\n      const bVal = b[sortColumn];\n      const result = aVal < bVal ? -1 : aVal > bVal ? 1 : 0;\n      return sortDirection === ''asc'' ? result : -result;\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Services\n\n```javascript\n// app/services/notification.js\nimport Service from ''@ember/service'';\nimport { tracked } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\nimport { action } from ''@ember/object'';\n\nexport default class NotificationService extends Service {\n  @tracked notifications = [];\n  \n  @action\n  add(message, type = ''info'', duration = 5000) {\n    const id = Date.now() + Math.random();\n    const notification = { id, message, type };\n    \n    this.notifications = [...this.notifications, notification];\n    \n    if (duration > 0) {\n      setTimeout(() => this.remove(id), duration);\n    }\n    \n    return id;\n  }\n  \n  @action\n  remove(id) {\n    this.notifications = this.notifications.filter(n => n.id !== id);\n  }\n  \n  @action\n  success(message, duration) {\n    return this.add(message, ''success'', duration);\n  }\n  \n  @action\n  error(message, duration = 10000) {\n    return this.add(message, ''error'', duration);\n  }\n  \n  @action\n  clear() {\n    this.notifications = [];\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Modifiers\n\n```javascript\n// app/modifiers/click-outside.js\nimport { modifier } from ''ember-modifier'';\n\nexport default modifier((element, [callback]) => {\n  function handleClick(event) {\n    if (!element.contains(event.target)) {\n      callback(event);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  document.addEventListener(''click'', handleClick, true);\n  \n  return () => {\n    document.removeEventListener(''click'', handleClick, true);\n  };\n});\n```\n\n```handlebars\n{{! Usage }}\n<div {{click-outside this.closeDropdown}} class=\"dropdown\">\n  {{! dropdown content }}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Routing\n\n### Route Definitions\n\n```javascript\n// app/router.js\nimport EmberRouter from ''@ember/routing/router'';\nimport config from ''my-app/config/environment'';\n\nexport default class Router extends EmberRouter {\n  location = config.locationType;\n  rootURL = config.rootURL;\n}\n\nRouter.map(function () {\n  this.route(''dashboard'', { path: ''/'' });\n  \n  this.route(''users'', function () {\n    this.route(''index'', { path: ''/'' });\n    this.route(''new'');\n    this.route(''user'', { path: ''/:user_id'' }, function () {\n      this.route(''edit'');\n      this.route(''settings'');\n    });\n  });\n  \n  this.route(''not-found'', { path: ''/*path'' });\n});\n```\n\n### Route Class\n\n```javascript\n// app/routes/users/user.js\nimport Route from ''@ember/routing/route'';\nimport { inject as service } from ''@ember/service'';\n\nexport default class UsersUserRoute extends Route {\n  @service store;\n  @service router;\n\n  async model(params) {\n    try {\n      return await this.store.findRecord(''user'', params.user_id, {\n        include: ''profile,settings''\n      });\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error.errors?.[0]?.status === ''404'') {\n        this.router.transitionTo(''not-found'');\n      }\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Redirect if user doesn''t have permission\n  afterModel(model) {\n    if (!this.currentUser.canViewUser(model)) {\n      this.router.transitionTo(''dashboard'');\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Reset controller state on exit\n  resetController(controller, isExiting) {\n    if (isExiting) {\n      controller.setProperties({\n        queryParams: {},\n        isEditing: false\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Loading and Error States\n\n```javascript\n// app/routes/users/user/loading.js\nimport Route from ''@ember/routing/route'';\n\nexport default class UsersUserLoadingRoute extends Route {}\n```\n\n```handlebars\n{{! app/templates/users/user/loading.hbs }}\n<div class=\"loading-spinner\">\n  <p>Loading user...</p>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Ember Data\n\n### Models\n\n```javascript\n// app/models/user.js\nimport Model, { attr, hasMany, belongsTo } from ''@ember-data/model'';\n\nexport default class UserModel extends Model {\n  @attr(''string'') name;\n  @attr(''string'') email;\n  @attr(''date'') createdAt;\n  @attr(''boolean'', { defaultValue: true }) isActive;\n  @attr(''number'') loginCount;\n  \n  @belongsTo(''profile'', { async: true, inverse: ''user'' }) profile;\n  @hasMany(''post'', { async: true, inverse: ''author'' }) posts;\n  \n  // Computed properties still work but use native getters\n  get displayName() {\n    return this.name || this.email?.split(''@'')[0] || ''Anonymous'';\n  }\n  \n  get isNewUser() {\n    const daysSinceCreation = (Date.now() - this.createdAt) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24);\n    return daysSinceCreation < 7;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Adapters\n\n```javascript\n// app/adapters/application.js\nimport JSONAPIAdapter from ''@ember-data/adapter/json-api'';\nimport { inject as service } from ''@ember/service'';\n\nexport default class ApplicationAdapter extends JSONAPIAdapter {\n  @service session;\n  \n  host = ''https://api.example.com'';\n  namespace = ''v1'';\n\n  get headers() {\n    const headers = {};\n    \n    if (this.session.isAuthenticated) {\n      headers[''Authorization''] = `Bearer ${this.session.data.authenticated.token}`;\n    }\n    \n    return headers;\n  }\n\n  handleResponse(status, headers, payload, requestData) {\n    if (status === 401) {\n      this.session.invalidate();\n    }\n    \n    return super.handleResponse(status, headers, payload, requestData);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Serializers\n\n```javascript\n// app/serializers/application.js\nimport JSONAPISerializer from ''@ember-data/serializer/json-api'';\n\nexport default class ApplicationSerializer extends JSONAPISerializer {\n  // Normalize date strings to Date objects\n  normalizeDateFields(hash) {\n    const dateFields = [''createdAt'', ''updatedAt'', ''publishedAt''];\n    \n    dateFields.forEach(field => {\n      if (hash[field]) {\n        hash[field] = new Date(hash[field]);\n      }\n    });\n    \n    return hash;\n  }\n\n  normalize(modelClass, resourceHash) {\n    this.normalizeDateFields(resourceHash.attributes || {});\n    return super.normalize(modelClass, resourceHash);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n### Component Integration Tests\n\n```javascript\n// tests/integration/components/user-profile-test.js\nimport { module, test } from ''qunit'';\nimport { setupRenderingTest } from ''ember-qunit'';\nimport { render, click, fillIn } from ''@ember/test-helpers'';\nimport { hbs } from ''ember-cli-htmlbars'';\n\nmodule(''Integration | Component | user-profile'', function (hooks) {\n  setupRenderingTest(hooks);\n\n  test(''it displays user information'', async function (assert) {\n    this.set(''user'', {\n      name: ''Jane Doe'',\n      email: ''jane@example.com''\n    });\n\n    await render(hbs`<UserProfile @user={{this.user}} />`);\n\n    assert.dom(''h2'').hasText(''Jane Doe'');\n    assert.dom(''p'').hasText(''jane@example.com'');\n  });\n\n  test(''it allows editing when canEdit is true'', async function (assert) {\n    this.owner.lookup(''service:current-user'').canEdit = true;\n    this.set(''user'', {\n      name: ''Jane Doe'',\n      email: ''jane@example.com''\n    });\n    this.set(''onSave'', () => {});\n\n    await render(hbs`\n      <UserProfile @user={{this.user}} @onSave={{this.onSave}} />\n    `);\n\n    await click(''button:contains(\"Edit Profile\")'');\n    \n    assert.dom(''form'').exists();\n    assert.dom(''input[type=\"text\"]'').hasValue(''Jane Doe'');\n    \n    await fillIn(''input[type=\"text\"]'', ''Jane Smith'');\n    await click(''button[type=\"submit\"]'');\n    \n    assert.dom(''form'').doesNotExist();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Route/Acceptance Tests\n\n```javascript\n// tests/acceptance/user-flow-test.js\nimport { module, test } from ''qunit'';\nimport { visit, currentURL, click, fillIn } from ''@ember/test-helpers'';\nimport { setupApplicationTest } from ''ember-qunit'';\nimport { setupMirage } from ''ember-cli-mirage/test-support'';\n\nmodule(''Acceptance | user flow'', function (hooks) {\n  setupApplicationTest(hooks);\n  setupMirage(hooks);\n\n  test(''visiting /users and creating a new user'', async function (assert) {\n    await visit(''/users'');\n    \n    assert.strictEqual(currentURL(), ''/users'');\n    assert.dom(''h1'').hasText(''Users'');\n    \n    await click(''a:contains(\"New User\")'');\n    assert.strictEqual(currentURL(), ''/users/new'');\n    \n    await fillIn(''[data-test-name-input]'', ''John Doe'');\n    await fillIn(''[data-test-email-input]'', ''john@example.com'');\n    await click(''[data-test-submit]'');\n    \n    assert.strictEqual(currentURL(), ''/users/1'');\n    assert.dom(''[data-test-user-name]'').hasText(''John Doe'');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\nSee [references/performance.md](references/performance.md) for comprehensive optimization strategies.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Unnecessary component re-renders | Use `@cached` for expensive getters |\n| Large lists | Use `ember-collection` or virtual scrolling |\n| Slow Ember Data queries | Optimize includes, use custom serializers |\n| Bundle size | Use route-based code splitting, lazy engines |\n| Memory leaks | Properly clean up in willDestroy, cancel timers |\n\n### Critical Anti-patterns\n\n```javascript\n// ❌ Mutating tracked properties directly\nthis.items.push(newItem); // Won''t trigger reactivity\n\n// ✅ Replace the entire array\nthis.items = [...this.items, newItem];\n\n// ❌ Creating new functions in templates\n{{on \"click\" (fn this.handleClick item)}}\n\n// ✅ Use actions or stable references\n@action handleItemClick(item) { /* ... */ }\n{{on \"click\" (fn this.handleItemClick item)}}\n\n// ❌ Not using @cached for expensive computations\nget expensiveComputation() {\n  return this.data.filter(/* complex logic */);\n}\n\n// ✅ Use @cached\n@cached\nget expensiveComputation() {\n  return this.data.filter(/* complex logic */);\n}\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\napp/\n├── components/           # Glimmer components\n│   └── user-profile/\n│       ├── component.js\n│       ├── index.hbs\n│       └── styles.css\n├── controllers/          # Controllers (use sparingly in Octane)\n├── helpers/             # Template helpers\n├── modifiers/           # Custom modifiers\n├── models/              # Ember Data models\n├── routes/              # Route classes\n├── services/            # Services\n├── templates/           # Route templates\n├── adapters/            # Ember Data adapters\n├── serializers/         # Ember Data serializers\n├── styles/              # Global styles\n└── app.js\n\ntests/\n├── integration/         # Component tests\n├── unit/               # Unit tests (models, services, etc.)\n└── acceptance/         # Full application tests\n```\n\n## Tooling Recommendations\n\n| Category | Tool | Notes |\n|----------|------|-------|\n| CLI | ember-cli | Official tooling |\n| Testing | QUnit + ember-qunit | Built-in, well integrated |\n| Linting | ESLint + ember-template-lint | Catch template issues |\n| Formatting | Prettier | Use with ember-template-lint |\n| Mocking | ember-cli-mirage | API mocking for tests |\n| State management | Services + tracked | Built-in, no extra deps |\n| HTTP | fetch or ember-fetch | Native or polyfilled |\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Form Handling with Validation\n\n```javascript\n// app/components/registration-form.js\nimport Component from ''@glimmer/component'';\nimport { tracked } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\nimport { action } from ''@ember/object'';\nimport { inject as service } from ''@ember/service'';\n\nexport default class RegistrationFormComponent extends Component {\n  @service notification;\n  \n  @tracked email = '''';\n  @tracked password = '''';\n  @tracked confirmPassword = '''';\n  @tracked errors = {};\n  @tracked isSubmitting = false;\n\n  get isValid() {\n    return (\n      this.email &&\n      this.password.length >= 8 &&\n      this.password === this.confirmPassword &&\n      Object.keys(this.errors).length === 0\n    );\n  }\n\n  @action\n  updateEmail(event) {\n    this.email = event.target.value;\n    this.validateEmail();\n  }\n\n  @action\n  updatePassword(event) {\n    this.password = event.target.value;\n    this.validatePassword();\n  }\n\n  @action\n  updateConfirmPassword(event) {\n    this.confirmPassword = event.target.value;\n    this.validateConfirmPassword();\n  }\n\n  validateEmail() {\n    const emailRegex = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\n    \n    if (!this.email) {\n      this.errors = { ...this.errors, email: ''Email is required'' };\n    } else if (!emailRegex.test(this.email)) {\n      this.errors = { ...this.errors, email: ''Invalid email format'' };\n    } else {\n      const { email, ...rest } = this.errors;\n      this.errors = rest;\n    }\n  }\n\n  validatePassword() {\n    if (this.password.length < 8) {\n      this.errors = { ...this.errors, password: ''Password must be at least 8 characters'' };\n    } else {\n      const { password, ...rest } = this.errors;\n      this.errors = rest;\n    }\n    \n    // Re-validate confirm password if it''s filled\n    if (this.confirmPassword) {\n      this.validateConfirmPassword();\n    }\n  }\n\n  validateConfirmPassword() {\n    if (this.password !== this.confirmPassword) {\n      this.errors = { ...this.errors, confirmPassword: ''Passwords do not match'' };\n    } else {\n      const { confirmPassword, ...rest } = this.errors;\n      this.errors = rest;\n    }\n  }\n\n  @action\n  async submit(event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    \n    if (!this.isValid) return;\n    \n    this.isSubmitting = true;\n    \n    try {\n      await this.args.onSubmit({\n        email: this.email,\n        password: this.password\n      });\n      \n      this.notification.success(''Registration successful!'');\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.notification.error(error.message || ''Registration failed'');\n    } finally {\n      this.isSubmitting = false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Infinite Scroll with Modifier\n\n```javascript\n// app/modifiers/infinite-scroll.js\nimport { modifier } from ''ember-modifier'';\n\nexport default modifier((element, [callback], { threshold = 200 }) => {\n  let isLoading = false;\n  \n  function handleScroll() {\n    if (isLoading) return;\n    \n    const { scrollTop, scrollHeight, clientHeight } = element;\n    const distanceFromBottom = scrollHeight - (scrollTop + clientHeight);\n    \n    if (distanceFromBottom < threshold) {\n      isLoading = true;\n      callback().finally(() => {\n        isLoading = false;\n      });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  element.addEventListener(''scroll'', handleScroll, { passive: true });\n  \n  return () => {\n    element.removeEventListener(''scroll'', handleScroll);\n  };\n});\n```\n\n## TypeScript Support\n\nEmber has strong TypeScript support. Enable it with:\n\n```bash\nember install ember-cli-typescript\n```\n\n```typescript\n// app/components/user-profile.ts\nimport Component from ''@glimmer/component'';\nimport { tracked } from ''@glimmer/tracking'';\nimport { action } from ''@ember/object'';\nimport type { TOC } from ''@ember/component/template-only'';\n\ninterface UserProfileArgs {\n  user: {\n    name: string;\n    email: string;\n    avatarUrl?: string;\n  };\n  onSave: (data: UserData) => Promise<void>;\n  canEdit?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface UserData {\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n}\n\nexport default class UserProfileComponent extends Component<UserProfileArgs> {\n  @tracked isEditing = false;\n  @tracked formData: UserData | null = null;\n\n  @action\n  async saveUser(event: SubmitEvent): Promise<void> {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    \n    if (!this.formData) return;\n    \n    await this.args.onSave(this.formData);\n    this.isEditing = false;\n  }\n}\n\n// Template-only component signature\nexport interface GreetingSignature {\n  Element: HTMLDivElement;\n  Args: {\n    name: string;\n  };\n}\n\nconst Greeting: TOC<GreetingSignature> = <template>\n  <div ...attributes>Hello {{@name}}!</div>\n</template>;\n\nexport default Greeting;\n```\n\n## Remember: Always Use context7 MCP First!\n\nBefore implementing any Ember code, query the context7 MCP for relevant project documentation. Context7 provides project-specific guidelines that always supersede these general best practices.\n\n### Quick context7 Query Guide\n\n**Before writing components:**\n- Query: \"ember component patterns\", \"glimmer component\", \"component architecture\"\n\n**Before routing work:**\n- Query: \"ember routing\", \"route patterns\", \"navigation\"\n\n**Before Ember Data:**\n- Query: \"ember data models\", \"api integration\", \"data layer\"\n\n**Before tests:**\n- Query: \"ember testing\", \"test patterns\", \"test requirements\"\n\n**When editing existing code:**\n- Query the specific feature or pattern you''re working with\n\nThe context7 MCP is your source of truth for this project''s Ember conventions.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:46:08.466Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Ember.js Development Agents working on Freshbooks performance optimization.","zh":"对于使用Freshbooks性能优化的Ember.js开发代理来说是必不可少的。","ja":"Freshbooksのパフォーマンス最適化でEmber.jsを使用する開発エージェントにとって不可欠です。","ko":"프레쉬북スの 성능 최적화를 위해 엠버.js를 사용하는 개발 에이전트에게 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para Agentes de Desarrollo Ember.js que trabajan en la optimización del rendimiento de Freshbooks.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de développement Ember.js travaillant sur l''optimisation des performances de Freshbooks.","de":"Wichtig für Ember.js-Entwicklungsagenten, die an der Leistungsoptimierung von Freshbooks arbeiten.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Ember.js que trabalham na otimização de desempenho do Freshbooks.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов по разработке Ember.js, работающих над оптимизацией производительности Freshbooks.","ar":"ضروري لعميل تطوير Ember.js الذي يعمل على تحسين أداء Freshbooks."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables immediate identification and resolution of performance bottlenecks in Freshbooks'' Ember.js implementation through Chrome extension capabilities. Directly implements Ember Octane conventions and project-specific patterns verified via context7 MCP integration.","zh":"通过Chrome扩展功能，能够立即识别和解决Freshbooks的Ember.js实现中的性能瓶颈。直接实现Ember Octane惯例和项目特定模式，通过context7 MCP集成验证。","ja":"Chrome拡張機能を通じて、FreshbooksのEmber.js実装におけるパフォーマンスのボトルネックを即時的に特定して解決できる。Ember Octaneの規約やプロジェクト固有のパターンを直接実装し、context7 MCP統合を通じて検証する。","ko":"크롬 확장 기능을 통해 프레쉬북스의 엠버.js 구현에서 성능 병목 현상을 즉시 식별하고 해결할 수 있습니다. 엠버 옥테인 규약 및 프로젝트 특정 패턴을 직접 구현하고 컨텍스트7 MCP 통합을 통해 검증합니다.","es":"Permite la identificación y resolución inmediatas de cuellos de botella de rendimiento en la implementación de Ember.js de Freshbooks a través de las capacidades de la extensión de Chrome. Implementa directamente las convenciones de Ember Octane y patrones específicos del proyecto verificados a través de la integración de context7 MCP.","fr":"Permet l''identification et la résolution immédiate des goulots d''étranglement de performances dans la mise en œuvre d''Ember.js de Freshbooks via les capacités de l''extension Chrome. Met directement en œuvre les conventions Ember Octane et les modèles spécifiques au projet vérifiés via l''intégration de context7 MCP.","de":"Ermöglicht die sofortige Identifizierung und Behebung von Leistungsengpässen in der Ember.js-Implementierung von Freshbooks durch die Funktionen der Chrome-Erweiterung. Implementiert direkt die Ember-Octane-Konventionen und projektspezifische Muster, die über die context7-MCP-Integration verifiziert werden.","pt":"Permite a identificação e resolução imediata de gargalos de desempenho na implementação do Ember.js do Freshbooks por meio de capacidades de extensão do Chrome. Implementa diretamente convenções do Ember Octane e padrões específicos do projeto verificados por meio da integração do context7 MCP.","ru":"Позволяет сразу же выявлять и решать проблемы с производительностью в реализации Ember.js в Freshbooks с помощью возможностей расширения Chrome. Прямо реализует конвенции Ember Octane и проектно-специфические шаблоны, проверенные через интеграцию с context7 MCP.","ar":"يمكن التعرف الفوري وحل مشاكل أداءFreshbooks في تطبيق Ember.js من خلال إمكانات ملحقات Chrome. ينفذ بشكل مباشر اتفاقيات Ember Octane والأنماط المحددة للمشروع التي تم التحقق منها من خلال دمج context7 MCP."},"useCases":{"en":["Diagnosing Freshbooks-specific rendering performance issues","Implementing Ember Octane patterns for code modernization","Validating code against project-specific conventions via context7 MCP"],"zh":["诊断Freshbooks特定的渲染性能问题","实施Ember Octane模式以进行代码现代化","通过context7 MCP验证代码是否符合项目特定惯例"],"ja":["Freshbooks固有のレンダリングパフォーマンスの問題を診断する","コードの近代化のためにEmber Octaneパターンを実装する","context7 MCPを通じてコードがプロジェクト固有の規約に準拠していることを検証する"],"ko":["프레쉬북스 특정의 렌더링 성능 문제를 진단합니다.","코드 현대화를 위해 엠버 옥테인 패턴을 구현합니다.","컨텍스트7 MCP를 통해 코드가 프로젝트 특정 규약을 준수하는지 검증합니다."],"es":["Diagnóstico de problemas de rendimiento de renderizado específicos de Freshbooks","Implementación de patrones Ember Octane para la modernización del código","Validación del código contra convenciones específicas del proyecto a través de context7 MCP"],"fr":["Diagnostic des problèmes de performances de rendu spécifiques à Freshbooks","Mise en œuvre de modèles Ember Octane pour la modernisation du code","Validation du code contre les conventions spécifiques au projet via context7 MCP"],"de":["Diagnose von Freshbooks-spezifischen Renderleistungsproblemen","Implementierung von Ember-Octane-Mustern für die Code-Modernisierung","Validierung des Codes gegen projektspezifische Konventionen über context7 MCP"],"pt":["Diagnosticar problemas de renderização específicos do Freshbooks","Implementar padrões do Ember Octane para modernização de código","Validar código contra convenções específicas do projeto por meio do context7 MCP"],"ru":["Диагностика проблем с отрисовкой, специфичных для Freshbooks","Реализация шаблонов Ember Octane для модернизации кода","Проверка кода на соответствие проектно-специфическим конвенциям через context7 MCP"],"ar":["التشخيص لمشاكل عرض محددة لبرنامج Freshbooks","تنفيذ أنماط Ember Octane لتدوين الشفرة الحديثة","التحقق من الشفرة مقابل اتفاقيات مشروع محددة من خلال دمج context7 MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Chrome extension environment required","Dependent on context7 MCP for architectural context","Freshbooks website specific implementation"],"zh":["需要Chrome扩展环境","依赖context7 MCP获取架构背景","仅适用于Freshbooks网站的特定实现"],"ja":["Chrome拡張機能の環境が必要","アーキテクチャの背景を得るためにcontext7 MCPに依存する","Freshbooksウェブサイトの特定の実装にのみ適用可能"],"ko":["크롬 확장 환경이 필요합니다.","아키텍처 배경을 얻기 위해 컨텍스트7 MCP에 의존합니다.","프레쉬북스 웹 사이트의 특정 구현에만 적용 가능합니다."],"es":["Entorno de extensión de Chrome requerido","Dependiente de context7 MCP para el contexto arquitectónico","Implementación específica del sitio web de Freshbooks"],"fr":["Environnement d''extension Chrome requis","Dépendant de context7 MCP pour le contexte architectural","Mise en œuvre spécifique du site Web de Freshbooks"],"de":["Chrome-Erweiterungsumgebung erforderlich","Abhängig von context7 MCP für den architektonischen Kontext","Freshbooks-Websitespezifische Implementierung"],"pt":["Ambiente de extensão do Chrome necessário","Dependente do context7 MCP para contexto arquitetônico","Implementação específica do site do Freshbooks"],"ru":["Требуется среда расширения Chrome","Зависит от context7 MCP для архитектурного контекста","Реализация, специфичная для сайта Freshbooks"],"ar":["بيئة ملحقات Chrome مطلوبة","يعتمد على context7 MCP للسياق المعماري","تنفيذ محدد لموقع Freshbooks على الويب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('TheCactusBlue/nixfiles/review', 'community', 'TheCactusBlue', 'nixfiles', 'TheCactusBlue/nixfiles', 'review', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.460Z', '2026-02-18T07:46:10.892Z', NULL, '{"id":"TheCactusBlue/nixfiles/review","name":"review","description":{"zh":"NixOS setup代码审查工具，用于检测代码中的错误、安全问题和风格不一致，提高代码质量","ja":"NixOS セットアップ コードレビューツールは、コードのエラー、セキュリティ問題、スタイルの不一致を検出してコード品質を向上させる","ko":"NixOS 설정 코드 리뷰 도구는 코드의 오류, 보안 문제, 스타일 불일치를 감지하여 코드 품질을 향상","es":"La revisión de código es un proceso que analiza el conjunto de cambios para detectar errores, problemas de seguridad y inconsistencias de estilo antes de commit.","fr":"La révision de code est un processus qui analyse l''ensemble des modifications pour détecter les erreurs, les problèmes de sécurité et les incohérences de style avant de commit.","de":"Die Code-Review ist ein Prozess, der den Änderungssatz analysiert, um Fehler, Sicherheitsprobleme und Stilinkonsistenzen vor dem Commit zu erkennen.","pt":"A revisão de código NixOS é uma ferramenta que analisa as alterações no código antes de commitar, verificando bugs, problemas de segurança e inconsistências de estilo.","ru":"Проверка кода NixOS - это инструмент, который анализирует изменения в коде перед коммитом, проверяя ошибки, проблемы безопасности и несоответствия стиля.","ar":"مراجعة رمز NixOS هي أداة تحليل التغييرات في الرمز قبل الالتزام، وتتحقق من الأخطاء ومشاكل الأمان وعدم التطابق في الأسلوب.","en":"NixOS setup"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"NixOS setup 代码审查","ja":"NixOS セットアップ コードレビュー","ko":"NixOS 설정 코드 리뷰","es":"Revisión de código antes de commit en NixOS","fr":"Révision de code avant commit dans NixOS","de":"Code-Review vor Commit in NixOS","pt":"Revisão de Código NixOS - Ferramenta de Análise","ru":"Проверка кода NixOS - Инструмент анализ","ar":"مراجعة رمز NixOS - أداة تحليل","en":"review"},"description":{"zh":"NixOS setup代码审查工具，用于检测代码中的错误、安全问题和风格不一致，提高代码质量","ja":"NixOS セットアップ コードレビューツールは、コードのエラー、セキュリティ問題、スタイルの不一致を検出してコード品質を向上させる","ko":"NixOS 설정 코드 리뷰 도구는 코드의 오류, 보안 문제, 스타일 불일치를 감지하여 코드 품질을 향상","es":"La revisión de código es un proceso que analiza el conjunto de cambios para detectar errores, problemas de seguridad y inconsistencias de estilo antes de com...","fr":"La révision de code est un processus qui analyse l''ensemble des modifications pour détecter les erreurs, les problèmes de sécurité et les incohérences de sty...","de":"Die Code-Review ist ein Prozess, der den Änderungssatz analysiert, um Fehler, Sicherheitsprobleme und Stilinkonsistenzen vor dem Commit zu erkennen.","pt":"A revisão de código NixOS é uma ferramenta que analisa as alterações no código antes de commitar, verificando bugs, problemas de segurança e inconsistências ...","ru":"Проверка кода NixOS - это инструмент, который анализирует изменения в коде перед коммитом, проверяя ошибки, проблемы безопасности и несоответствия стиля.","ar":"مراجعة رمز NixOS هي أداة تحليل التغييرات في الرمز قبل الالتزام، وتتحقق من الأخطاء ومشاكل الأمان وعدم التطابق في الأسلوب.","en":"NixOS setup"},"definition":{"en":"NixOS setup"},"features":{"zh":["自动检测代码错误","安全问题检测","风格不一致检测","代码质量提高","支持NixOS setup"],"ja":["コードのエラーを自動的に検出","セキュリティ問題の検出","スタイルの不一致の検出","コード品質の向上","NixOS セットアップのサポート"],"ko":["코드 오류 자동 감지","보안 문제 감지","스타일 불일치 감지","코드 품질 향상","NixOS 설정 지원"],"es":["Análisis de diff para detectar errores y problemas de seguridad","Revisión de código para inconsistencias de estilo","Soporte para staged y unstaged changes","Informes de resultados para que el usuario decida","Integración con Git para un flujo de trabajo simplificado"],"fr":["Analyse de diff pour détecter les erreurs et les problèmes de sécurité","Révision de code pour les incohérences de style","Prise en charge des modifications staged et unstaged","Rapports de résultats pour que l''utilisateur décide","Intégration avec Git pour un flux de travail simplifié"],"de":["Diff-Analyse zur Erkennung von Fehlern und Sicherheitsproblemen","Code-Review für Stilinkonsistenzen","Unterstützung für staged und unstaged Änderungen","Berichte über die Ergebnisse, damit der Benutzer entscheiden kann","Integration mit Git für einen vereinfachten Workflow"],"pt":["Análise de diferenças no código","Detecção de bugs e problemas de segurança","Verificação de inconsistências de estilo","Suporte a Git para staged e unstaged changes","Informações detalhadas para tomada de decisões"],"ru":["Анализ различий в коде","Обнаружение ошибок и проблем безопасности","Проверка несоответствий стиля","Поддержка Git для staged и unstaged изменений","Дetailed информация для принятия решений"],"ar":["تحليل الاختلافات في الرمز","الكشف عن الأخطاء ومشاكل الأمان","التحقق من عدم التطابق في الأسلوب","دعم Git لالتزامات المسرح و غير المسرح","معلومات مفصلة لاتخاذ القرارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NixOS setup","代码审查","代码质量","自动检测","安全问题","风格不一致"],"ja":["NixOS セットアップ","コードレビュー","コード品質","自動検出","セキュリティ問題","スタイルの不一致"],"ko":["NixOS 설정","코드 리뷰","코드 품질","자동 감지","보안 문제","스타일 불일치"],"es":["revisión de código","NixOS","desarrollo de software","git","commit","seguridad","estilo de código","análisis de diff"],"fr":["révision de code","NixOS","développement de logiciels","git","commit","sécurité","style de code","analyse de diff"],"de":["Code-Review","NixOS","Software-Entwicklung","Git","Commit","Sicherheit","Code-Stil","Diff-Analyse"],"pt":["revisão de código NixOS","análise de código","detecção de bugs","problemas de segurança","inconsistências de estilo","Git","staged changes","unstaged changes","qualidade de código"],"ru":["проверка кода NixOS","анализ кода","обнаружение ошибок","проблемы безопасности","несоответствия стиля","Git","staged изменения","unstaged изменения","качество кода"],"ar":["مراجعة رمز NixOS","تحليل الرمز","الكشف عن الأخطاء","مشاكل الأمان","عدم التطابق في الأسلوب","Git","التزامات المسرح","التزامات غير المسرح","جودة الرمز"]}},"owner":"TheCactusBlue","repo":"nixfiles","repoPath":"TheCactusBlue/nixfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.460Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review","description":"Pre-commit self-review. Use this to catch bugs, security issues, debug artifacts, and style problems in your changes before committing.","bodyPreview":"# Pre-Commit Self-Review\n\n## Overview\n\nReview the current changeset for issues before committing. Analyzes the diff for bugs, security problems, leftover debug code, and style inconsistencies. Presents findings for the user to decide on — does not auto-fix.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Gather the changeset:**\n\n- Run `git diff --staged` to get staged changes\n- If nothing is staged, fall back to `git diff` for unstaged changes\n- If both are empty, inform the user there''s nothing to review\n\n**Check project c","body":"# Pre-Commit Self-Review\n\n## Overview\n\nReview the current changeset for issues before committing. Analyzes the diff for bugs, security problems, leftover debug code, and style inconsistencies. Presents findings for the user to decide on — does not auto-fix.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Gather the changeset:**\n\n- Run `git diff --staged` to get staged changes\n- If nothing is staged, fall back to `git diff` for unstaged changes\n- If both are empty, inform the user there''s nothing to review\n\n**Check project conventions:**\n\n- If `CLAUDE.md` exists at the project root, read it for project-specific rules\n- Note any conventions around naming, error handling, imports, or formatting\n- Use these as additional review criteria alongside the defaults\n\n**Analyze changes for issues:**\n\n- **Bugs and logic errors** - Off-by-one, null/undefined access, wrong comparisons, missing edge cases, race conditions\n- **Leftover debug code** - `console.log`, `debugger`, `print()` statements, `TODO`/`FIXME`/`HACK` comments added in this diff\n- **Security issues** - Hardcoded secrets, SQL injection, XSS, unsanitized input, overly permissive permissions\n- **Missing error handling** - Unhandled promise rejections, unchecked return values, bare `except`/`catch` blocks\n- **Style inconsistencies** - Naming convention mismatches, inconsistent patterns compared to surrounding code\n\n**Present findings:**\n\n- Group issues by severity:\n  - **Blocking** - Bugs, security issues, or errors that must be fixed before committing\n  - **Warning** - Likely problems worth addressing but not strictly required\n  - **Nitpick** - Style or preference issues, take-or-leave\n- For blocking issues, suggest a specific fix with code\n- For warnings and nitpicks, describe the issue and location\n- If the changeset is clean, confirm with a brief summary of what was reviewed\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **Diff-focused** - Only review what changed, not the entire file\n- **Advisory, not automatic** - Present findings for the user to act on\n- **Convention-aware** - Respect project-specific rules from `CLAUDE.md`\n- **Severity-driven** - Clearly separate must-fix from nice-to-have\n- **Concise** - Don''t repeat the code back; reference file and line, describe the issue, suggest the fix\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:46:10.892Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents needing advanced diff analysis and pre-commit validation capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级 diff 分析和 pre-commit 验证功能的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビュー代理が高度な diff 分析およびコミット前の検証機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 diff 분석 및 커밋 전 유효성 검사 기능이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan un análisis de diferencias avanzado y capacidades de validación previa a la confirmación.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code qui ont besoin d''une analyse de différences avancée et de capacités de validation préalable à la validation.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die eine erweiterte Differenzanalyse und Vor-Commit-Validierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise de diff avançada e capacidades de validação pré-commit.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов код-ревью, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа diff и валидации до фиксации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل متقدم ل diff وقدرات التحقق من الصحة قبل التعهد."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to analyze Git changesets for bugs, security problems, and style inconsistencies using `git diff` and staged changes, providing detailed findings for user decision-making.","zh":"使代理能够使用 `git diff` 和暂存更改来分析 Git 更改集中的 bug、安全问题和样式不一致性，为用户决策提供详细的发现。","ja":"エージェントが `git diff` とステージングされた変更を使用して Git の変更セット内のバグ、セキュリティの問題、スタイルの不一致を分析し、ユーザーの意思決定のために詳細な発見を提供する力を与えます。","ko":"에이전트가 `git diff`와 스테이징된 변경 사항을 사용하여 Git 변경 세트 내의 버그, 보안 문제 및 스타일 불일치를 분석하여 사용자의 의사 결정에 대한 자세한 발견을 제공할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar conjuntos de cambios de Git para errores, problemas de seguridad y inconsistencias de estilo utilizando `git diff` y cambios en espera, proporcionando resultados detallados para la toma de decisiones del usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser les jeux de modifications Git pour les bogues, les problèmes de sécurité et les incohérences de style en utilisant `git diff` et les modifications en attente, fournissant des résultats détaillés pour la prise de décision de l''utilisateur.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Git-Änderungssätze auf Fehler, Sicherheitsprobleme und Stilinkonsistenzen mithilfe von `git diff` und gestagten Änderungen zu analysieren und detaillierte Ergebnisse für die Entscheidungsfindung des Benutzers bereitzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar conjuntos de alterações do Git para bugs, problemas de segurança e inconsistências de estilo usando `git diff` e alterações em estágio, fornecendo descobertas detalhadas para tomada de decisão do usuário.","ru":"Позволяет агентам анализировать наборы изменений Git на наличие ошибок, проблем безопасности и несоответствий стиля с помощью `git diff` и запланированных изменений, предоставляя подробные результаты для принятия решений пользователем.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تحليل مجموعات التغييرات في جيت للبحث عن العلل ومشاكل الأمان وعدم انتظام الأسلوب باستخدام `git diff` والتغييرات في مرحلة الإعداد ، وتقديم نتائج مفصلة لاتخاذ قرارات المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing staged changes for pre-commit validation","Identifying leftover debug code in unstaged changes","Detecting style inconsistencies in Git changesets"],"zh":["分析预提交验证的暂存更改","在未暂存更改中识别剩余的调试代码","检测 Git 更改集中的样式不一致性"],"ja":["コミット前の検証のためにステージングされた変更を分析する","ステージングされていない変更で残されたデバッグコードを識別する","Git の変更セット内のスタイルの不一致を検出する"],"ko":["커밋 전 유효성 검사에 대한 스테이징된 변경 사항 분석","스테이징되지 않은 변경 사항에서 남은 디버깅 코드 식별","Git 변경 세트 내의 스타일 불일치検출"],"es":["Análisis de cambios en espera para la validación previa a la confirmación","Identificación de código de depuración sobrante en cambios no en espera","Detección de inconsistencias de estilo en conjuntos de cambios de Git"],"fr":["Analyse des modifications en attente pour la validation préalable à la validation","Identification du code de débogage restant dans les modifications non en attente","Détection des incohérences de style dans les jeux de modifications Git"],"de":["Analyse von gestagten Änderungen für die Vor-Commit-Validierung","Identifizierung von überbleibendem Debug-Code in nicht gestagten Änderungen","Erkennung von Stilinkonsistenzen in Git-Änderungssätzen"],"pt":["Analisar alterações em estágio para validação pré-commit","Identificar código de depuração residual em alterações não em estágio","Detectar inconsistências de estilo em conjuntos de alterações do Git"],"ru":["Анализ изменений в стадии для валидации до фиксации","Определение оставшегося отладочного кода в не запланированных изменениях","Обнаружение несоответствий стиля в наборах изменений Git"],"ar":["تحليل التغييرات في مرحلة الإعداد للتحقق من الصحة قبل التعهد","تحديد رمز تصحيح متبقي في التغييرات غير المخطط لها","اكتشاف عدم انتظام الأسلوب في مجموعات التغييرات في جيت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to analyzing changesets, does not auto-fix issues"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","仅限于分析更改集，不会自动修复问题"],"ja":["Git のインストールと設定が必要","変更セットの分析のみに限定され、問題は自動的に修正されない"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성이 필요함","변경 세트 분석のみ로 제한되며, 문제는 자동으로 수정되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado al análisis de conjuntos de cambios, no corrige automáticamente los problemas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité à l''analyse des jeux de modifications, ne corrige pas automatiquement les problèmes"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Analyse von Änderungssätzen, behebt Probleme nicht automatisch"],"pt":["Exige instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado à análise de conjuntos de alterações, não corrige problemas automaticamente"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки Git","Ограничен анализом наборов изменений, не исправляет проблемы автоматически"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت جيت وتفصيله","محدود بتحليل مجموعات التغييرات ، ولا يصلح المشاكل تلقائيًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
