s. Activates for debug, fix bug, not working, error, broken, issue, fails, crash, undefined, null problems.","bodyPreview":"# Debugging Protocol\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n- \"Debug this\", \"fix this bug\", \"not working\"\n- Error messages, stack traces\n- \"Undefined\", \"null\", \"crash\", \"fails\"\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance issues\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### Phase 1: Reproduce\nBefore fixing anything:\n```\n1. Can I reproduce the bug consistently?\n2. What are the exact steps to trigger it?\n3. What is the expected behavior?\n4. What is the actual behavior?\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Isolate\nNarrow down the problem:\n```","body":"# Debugging Protocol\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n- \"Debug this\", \"fix this bug\", \"not working\"\n- Error messages, stack traces\n- \"Undefined\", \"null\", \"crash\", \"fails\"\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance issues\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### Phase 1: Reproduce\nBefore fixing anything:\n```\n1. Can I reproduce the bug consistently?\n2. What are the exact steps to trigger it?\n3. What is the expected behavior?\n4. What is the actual behavior?\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Isolate\nNarrow down the problem:\n```\n1. When did it last work? (check git history)\n2. What changed recently?\n3. Is it specific to certain inputs?\n4. Does it happen in all environments?\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Investigate\n\n#### Read the Error Message Carefully\n```\nError: Cannot read property ''map'' of undefined\n       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n       This tells you: something is undefined that should be an array\n\nat UserList.render (UserList.tsx:15:23)\n   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n   Component name    File and line number\n```\n\n#### Key Investigation Commands\n```bash\n# Find where variable is defined\ngrep -r \"variableName\" --include=\"*.ts\" -n\n\n# Find where function is called\ngrep -r \"functionName(\" --include=\"*.ts\" -n\n\n# Check git history for recent changes\ngit log --oneline -20\ngit diff HEAD~5 -- path/to/file\n\n# Find related tests\nfind . -name \"*.test.ts\" | xargs grep \"FunctionName\"\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Hypothesize\nForm specific hypotheses:\n```\nNOT: \"Something is wrong with the data\"\nYES: \"The API returns null when user has no orders, but we expect an empty array\"\n```\n\n### Phase 5: Test Hypothesis\nAdd strategic logging:\n```typescript\n// Before the error\nconsole.log(''DEBUG: data before map:'', JSON.stringify(data, null, 2));\nconsole.log(''DEBUG: data type:'', typeof data, Array.isArray(data));\n\n// Or use conditional breakpoints in debugger\n```\n\n### Phase 6: Fix\nApply minimal fix:\n```typescript\n// BAD: Overly broad fix\nconst items = data?.items?.map?.(x => x) ?? [];\n\n// GOOD: Fix the actual problem\nif (!data.items) {\n  throw new Error(''Expected items array but got: '' + typeof data.items);\n}\n// Or handle the null case explicitly where data is fetched\n```\n\n## Common Bug Patterns\n\n### 1. Undefined/Null Access\n```typescript\n// BUG\nuser.profile.name  // crashes if profile is undefined\n\n// FIX\nuser?.profile?.name  // safe access\n// OR\nif (!user?.profile) throw new Error(''User profile required'');\n```\n\n### 2. Async/Await Issues\n```typescript\n// BUG: Missing await\nconst data = fetchData();  // Returns Promise, not data\nconsole.log(data.items);   // undefined\n\n// FIX\nconst data = await fetchData();\n```\n\n### 3. State Race Conditions\n```typescript\n// BUG: State not updated yet\nsetCount(count + 1);\nconsole.log(count);  // Still old value\n\n// FIX: Use callback form\nsetCount(prev => prev + 1);\n```\n\n### 4. Closure Stale Values\n```typescript\n// BUG: Stale closure\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const interval = setInterval(() => {\n    console.log(count);  // Always logs initial value\n  }, 1000);\n}, []);  // Missing dependency\n\n// FIX\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const interval = setInterval(() => {\n    console.log(count);\n  }, 1000);\n  return () => clearInterval(interval);\n}, [count]);  // Add dependency\n```\n\n### 5. Off-by-One Errors\n```typescript\n// BUG\nfor (let i = 0; i <= array.length; i++)  // Goes one too far\n\n// FIX\nfor (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++)\n```\n\n### 6. Type Coercion\n```typescript\n// BUG\nif (value == 0)   // \"\" == 0 is true!\nif (value == \"\")  // 0 == \"\" is true!\n\n// FIX\nif (value === 0)\nif (value === \"\")\n```\n\n## Debugging Tools\n\n### Console Methods\n```typescript\nconsole.log(variable);                    // Basic output\nconsole.table(arrayOfObjects);            // Formatted table\nconsole.trace();                          // Stack trace\nconsole.time(''label''); /* code */ console.timeEnd(''label'');  // Timing\nconsole.group(''Section''); /* logs */ console.groupEnd();     // Grouping\n```\n\n### Node.js Debugging\n```bash\n# Start with inspector\nnode --inspect dist/index.js\n\n# Break on first line\nnode --inspect-brk dist/index.js\n\n# Then open Chrome DevTools at chrome://inspect\n```\n\n### React DevTools\n- Components tab: Inspect props/state\n- Profiler tab: Find re-render issues\n\n## Performance Debugging\n\n### Identify Slow Code\n```typescript\nconsole.time(''operation'');\n// ... code to measure\nconsole.timeEnd(''operation'');\n```\n\n### Memory Leaks\n```typescript\n// Common causes:\n// 1. Uncleared intervals/timeouts\n// 2. Event listeners not removed\n// 3. Closures holding references\n// 4. Growing arrays/maps\n\n// Fix: Always cleanup\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const handler = () => {};\n  window.addEventListener(''resize'', handler);\n  return () => window.removeEventListener(''resize'', handler);  // Cleanup!\n}, []);\n```\n\n## Bug Report Format\nWhen documenting bugs:\n```markdown\n## Bug: [Short description]\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n1. [Step 1]\n2. [Step 2]\n3. [Step 3]\n\n### Expected Behavior\n[What should happen]\n\n### Actual Behavior\n[What actually happens]\n\n### Environment\n- OS: [macOS/Windows/Linux]\n- Node: [version]\n- Browser: [if applicable]\n\n### Error Message\n```\n[Full error message and stack trace]\n```\n\n### Root Cause\n[After investigation]\n\n### Fix\n[Solution applied]\n```\n\n## Key Principle\nDon''t guess. Gather evidence. Form hypotheses. Test them. The bug tells you what''s wrong if you listen.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:49:03.615Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain requiring systematic error resolution and performance optimization.","zh":"适用于像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要系统性的错误解决和性能优化。","ja":"AutoGPT や LangChain などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、体系的なエラ解決とパフォーマンスの最適化が必要です。","ko":"AutoGPT 및 LangChain과 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 체계적인 오류 해결 및 성능 최적화가 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren una resolución de errores sistemática y optimización del rendimiento.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une résolution d''erreurs systématique et une optimisation des performances.","de":"Ideal für erweiterte KI-Agents wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine systematische Fehlerbehebung und Leistungsoptimierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados, como AutoGPT e LangChain, que exigem resolução sistemática de erros e otimização de desempenho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих системного решения ошибок и оптимизации производительности.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمين مثل AutoGPT و LangChain التي تتطلب حلًا منهجيًا للأخطاء وتحسين الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically reproduce, isolate, and resolve issues using a phased debugging protocol, analyzing error messages, stack traces, and unexpected behavior to ensure reliable operation and optimal performance.","zh":"使代理能够系统地重现、隔离和解决问题，使用分阶段的调试协议，分析错误消息、堆栈跟踪和意外行为，以确保可靠的操作和最佳性能。","ja":"エージェントが段階的なデバッグ プロトコルを使用して、システム的に問題を再現、分離、解決できるようにし、エラーメッセージ、スタック トレース、予期しない動作を分析して、信頼性の高い動作と最適なパフォーマンスを確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 계층적 디버깅 프로토콜을 사용하여 시스템적으로 문제를 재현, 분리 및 해결할 수 있도록 하며, 에러 메시지, 스택 트레이스 및 예기치 않은 동작을 분석하여 안정적인 작동 및 최적의 성능을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes reproducir, aislar y resolver problemas de manera sistemática utilizando un protocolo de depuración por fases, analizando mensajes de error, trazas de pila y comportamiento inesperado para garantizar un funcionamiento confiable y un rendimiento óptimo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de reproduire, d''isoler et de résoudre les problèmes de manière systématique en utilisant un protocole de débogage par phases, en analysant les messages d''erreur, les traces de pile et le comportement inattendu pour assurer un fonctionnement fiable et des performances optimales.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Probleme systematisch zu reproduzieren, zu isolieren und zu lösen, indem sie ein phasenweises Debugging-Protokoll verwenden, Fehlermeldungen, Stack-Traces und unerwartetes Verhalten analysieren, um einen zuverlässigen Betrieb und optimale Leistung zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reproduzir, isolar e resolver problemas de forma sistemática, utilizando um protocolo de depuração por fases, analisando mensagens de erro, rastros de pilha e comportamento inesperado para garantir operação confiável e desempenho ótimo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически воспроизводить, изолировать и решать проблемы, используя фазовый протокол отладки, анализируя сообщения об ошибках, трассировки стека и неожиданное поведение для обеспечения надежной работы и оптимальной производительности.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إعادة إنتاج المشكلات و عزلها و حلها بشكل منهجي، باستخدام بروتوكول تصحيح الأخطاء المرحلي، وتحليل رسائل الأخطاء و مسارات المكدس و السلوك غير المتوقع لضمان تشغيل موثوق و أداء ممتاز."},"useCases":{"en":["Reproducing and isolating bugs in complex codebases","Analyzing error messages and stack traces for root cause identification","Optimizing performance issues in AI-driven applications"],"zh":["在复杂代码库中重现和隔离 bug","分析错误消息和堆栈跟踪以确定根本原因","优化 AI 驱动应用程序中的性能问题"],"ja":["複雑なコードベースでのバグの再現と分離","エラーメッセセージとスタックトレースの分析による根本原因の特定","AI駆動アプリケーションのパフォーマンス問題の最適化"],"ko":["복잡한 코드베이스에서 버그를 재현하고 분리하기","에러 메시지 및 스택 트레이스를 분석하여根本 원인을 식별하기","AI 구동 애플리케이션의 성능 문제 최적화"],"es":["Reproducir y aislar errores en bases de código complejas","Analizar mensajes de error y trazas de pila para la identificación de la causa raíz","Optimizar problemas de rendimiento en aplicaciones impulsadas por IA"],"fr":["Reproduire et isoler les bogues dans des bases de code complexes","Analyser les messages d''erreur et les traces de pile pour l''identification de la cause racine","Optimiser les problèmes de performances dans les applications pilotées par l''IA"],"de":["Reproduzieren und Isolieren von Fehlern in komplexen Codebasen","Analysieren von Fehlermeldungen und Stack-Traces zur Identifizierung der Wurzelursache","Optimieren von Leistungsproblemen in KI-getriebenen Anwendungen"],"pt":["Reproduzir e isolar bugs em bases de código complexas","Analizar mensagens de erro e rastros de pilha para identificação da causa raiz","Otimizar problemas de desempenho em aplicações impulsionadas por IA"],"ru":["Воспроизводить и изолировать ошибки в сложных базах кода","Анализировать сообщения об ошибках и трассировки стека для выявления коренной причины","Оптимизировать проблемы производительности в приложениях, управляемых ИИ"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج الأخطاء و عزلها في قواعد الشفرة المعقدة","تحليل رسائل الأخطاء و مسارات المكدس للتعرف على السبب الجذري","تحسين مشاكل الأداء في التطبيقات التي تعمل بالذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to error logs and system outputs","May not be effective for highly specialized or niche errors without additional context"],"zh":["需要访问错误日志和系统输出","可能无法有效地解决没有额外上下文的高级专业或细节错误"],"ja":["エラーログとシステム出力へのアクセスが必要","追加のコンテキストなしで高度に専門化されたエラーまたはニッチエラーには効果的ではない可能性があります"],"ko":["오류 로그 및 시스템 출력에 대한 액세스가 필요함","추가적인 컨텍스트가 없는 고도로 전문화된 오류 또는 니치 오류의 경우 효과적이지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a registros de errores y salidas del sistema","Puede no ser eficaz para errores altamente especializados o de nicho sin contexto adicional"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux journaux d''erreurs et aux sorties du système","Peut ne pas être efficace pour les erreurs hautement spécialisées ou de niche sans contexte supplémentaire"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Fehlerprotokolle und Systemausgaben","Kann für hochspezialisierte oder Nischenfehler ohne zusätzlichen Kontext nicht wirksam sein"],"pt":["Exige acesso a registros de erros e saídas do sistema","Pode não ser eficaz para erros altamente especializados ou de nicho sem contexto adicional"],"ru":["Требует доступа к журналам ошибок и выходным данным системы","Может быть неэффективным для высокоспециализированных или нишевых ошибок без дополнительного контекста"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى سجلات الأخطاء و مخرجات النظام","قد لا يكون فعالاً对于 الأخطاء المتخصصة للغاية أو الأخطاء النادرة دون سياق إضافي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
