para mejorar la eficiencia de tus UI en Compose, aplicando el estado de elevación y flujo de datos unidireccional","fr":"Compose State Hoisting est une technique pour améliorer l''efficacité de vos UI dans Compose, en appliquant l''état d''élévation et le flux de données unidirect...","de":"Compose State Hoisting ist eine Technik, um die Effizienz Ihrer UI in Compose zu verbessern, indem Sie den Zustand der Anhebung und den unidirektionalen Date...","pt":"Compose State Hoisting é uma técnica para aplicar state hoisting e fluxo de dados unidirecional em UIs Compose, melhorando a manutenção e escalabilidade.","ru":"Compose State Hoisting - это техника для применения state hoisting и унидирекционального потока данных в UI Compose, улучшающая поддержку и масштабируемость.","ar":"تجميع حالة الرفع هو تقنية لتطبيق رفع الحالة وتدفق البيانات الموحد في واجهات المستخدم Compose، مما يحسن الصيانة وال escalabilidade.","en":"Self-hosted service that helps me share to multiple social media platforms at the same time."},"definition":{"en":"Self-hosted service that helps me share to multiple social media platforms at the same time."},"features":{"es":["Aplicación del estado de elevación","Flujo de datos unidireccional","Mejora del rendimiento de la UI","Simplificación del código","Flexibilidad en la elección del propietario del estado","Integración con Android ViewModel"],"fr":["Application de l''état d''élévation","Flux de données unidirectionnel","Amélioration des performances de l''UI","Simplification du code","Flexibilité dans le choix du propriétaire de l''état","Intégration avec Android ViewModel"],"de":["Anwendung des Zustands der Anhebung","Unidirektionaler Datenfluss","Verbesserung der Leistung der UI","Vereinfachung des Codes","Flexibilität bei der Wahl des Zustandseigners","Integration mit Android ViewModel"],"pt":["Aplicação de state hoisting em UIs Compose","Fluxo de dados unidirecional","Escolha do proprietário de estado correto","Estratégias de salvamento de estado","Melhoria da manutenção e escalabilidade","Compatibilidade com Android ViewModel"],"ru":["Применение state hoisting в UI Compose","Унидирекциональный поток данных","Выбор правильного владельца состояния","Стратегии сохранения состояния","Улучшение поддержки и масштабируемости","Совместимость с Android ViewModel"],"ar":["تطبيق رفع الحالة في واجهات المستخدم Compose","تدفق البيانات الموحد","اختيار مالك الحالة الصحيح","استراتيجيات الحفظ الحالة","تحسين الصيانة وال escalabilidade","التوافق مع Android ViewModel"]},"keywords":{"es":["Compose State Hoisting","estado de elevación","flujo de datos unidireccional","UI de Compose","rendimiento de la UI","Android ViewModel","programación de Compose","optimización de la UI"],"fr":["Compose State Hoisting","état d''élévation","flux de données unidirectionnel","UI de Compose","performances de l''UI","Android ViewModel","programmation de Compose","optimisation de l''UI"],"de":["Compose State Hoisting","Zustand der Anhebung","unidirektionaler Datenfluss","UI von Compose","Leistung der UI","Android ViewModel","Programmierung von Compose","Optimierung der UI"],"pt":["Compose State Hoisting","state hoisting","fluxo de dados unidirecional","UI Compose","Android ViewModel","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","programação android","tecnologia de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Compose State Hoisting","state hoisting","унидирекциональный поток данных","UI Compose","Android ViewModel","разработка приложений","программирование для android","технология разработки"],"ar":["تجميع حالة الرفع","رفع الحالة","تدفق البيانات الموحد","واجهات المستخدم Compose","Android ViewModel","تطوير التطبيقات","برمجة أندرويد","تكنولوجيا التطوير"]}},"owner":"alexandru","repo":"social-publish","repoPath":"alexandru/social-publish","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.461Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"compose-state-hoisting","description":"Compose state management with a strong state-hoisting preference for Kotlin Compose (Android, Multiplatform, Compose for Web). Use for refactors or new UI that needs clear state ownership, unidirectional data flow, saved state decisions, or guidance on remember/retain/rememberSaveable/rememberSerializable, and for designing stateless composables with event callbacks.","bodyPreview":"# Compose State Hoisting\n\n## Overview\nApply state hoisting and unidirectional data flow to Compose UIs, choosing the right state owner, lifespan, and saving strategy.\n\nFor condensed reference and examples, see `references/compose-state-guidance.md`.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Identify the state and the logic that reads/writes it.\n2. Decide the state owner (lowest common ancestor; or a plain state holder class, or a screen-level state holder like Android ViewModel for complex UI/business logic).\n3. Choose t","body":"# Compose State Hoisting\n\n## Overview\nApply state hoisting and unidirectional data flow to Compose UIs, choosing the right state owner, lifespan, and saving strategy.\n\nFor condensed reference and examples, see `references/compose-state-guidance.md`.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Identify the state and the logic that reads/writes it.\n2. Decide the state owner (lowest common ancestor; or a plain state holder class, or a screen-level state holder like Android ViewModel for complex UI/business logic).\n3. Choose the lifespan API (remember/retain/rememberSaveable/rememberSerializable) based on how long it must survive.\n4. Make UI composables stateless: pass `value` and event callbacks; state goes down, events go up.\n5. Decide what must be saved and how (rememberSaveable, SavedStateHandle, or platform storage).\n6. Verify that state and callbacks are not duplicated or leaked.\n\n## Rules of thumb\n- Hoist state to the lowest common ancestor of all readers/writers.\n- Keep composables stateless: state down, events up.\n- Pick the lifespan API explicitly; default to `remember` only for ephemeral UI state.\n- Save minimal data and rehydrate anything larger or derived.\n\n## Decision hints\n- If multiple parts of the UI must read/write the same state, hoist it.\n- If state survives config changes or process death, choose `retain` or `rememberSaveable` and document why.\n- For business logic, use a screen-level state holder; do not pass it down the tree.\n\n## Common pitfalls\n- Duplicated state owners causing divergence.\n- Over-saving large objects in `rememberSaveable`/`SavedStateHandle`.\n- Mixing `remember` and `retain` for the same object.\n\n## State Hoisting Rules\n- Hoist state to the lowest common ancestor of all composables that read and write it; keep it as close to consumers as possible.\n- If multiple states change from the same events, hoist them together.\n- Over-hoisting (e.g., hoisting to screen level when a subtree would suffice) is acceptable and safer than under-hoisting; under-hoisting breaks unidirectional flow and creates duplicate sources of truth. Over-hoisting may trigger more recompositions or lose state on navigation.\n- Prefer exposing immutable state plus event callbacks from the state owner.\n\n## Stateless vs Stateful Composables\n- Provide a stateless API: `value: T` and `onValueChange: (T) -> Unit` (or more specific event lambdas).\n- Keep state internal only if no other composable needs to read or change it and the UI logic is simple.\n- Offer both stateful and stateless variants when useful; the stateless version is the reusable/testable one.\n\n## Decide Where to Hoist\n- **UI element state + simple UI logic**: keep internal or hoist within the UI subtree.\n- **Complex UI logic**: move state and UI logic into a plain state holder class scoped to the Composition.\n- **Business logic or screen UI state**: hoist to a screen-level state holder (Android: ViewModel; Multiplatform: platform-specific or library solutions like Circuit, Molecule). Do not pass screen-level state holders down the tree; inject at the screen level and pass state/events instead.\n- **Deep prop drilling**: for state needed by many distant descendants (theme, user session), consider `CompositionLocal` to avoid passing parameters through many layers. Use sparingly; prefer explicit parameter passing when practical.\n\n## Choose the Correct Lifespan\n- `remember`: survives recomposition only; same instance. Use for composition-scoped objects and small internal UI state. Do not use for user input that must be preserved.\n- `retain`: survives recomposition + window/configuration changes (Android: activity recreation), not process death. Use for non-serializable objects (players, caches, flows, lambdas). **Do not retain** platform-specific lifecycle objects (Android: Activity, View, Fragment, ViewModel, Context, Lifecycle). **Do not retain** objects that were already created with `remember` by the caller—`retain` and `remember` are mutually exclusive for the same object.\n- `rememberSaveable` / `rememberSerializable`: survives recomposition + configuration changes + process death (Android) by saving to the platform''s saved state mechanism (Android: Bundle; other platforms may vary). Use for user input or UI state that cannot be reloaded from another source. Restored objects are equal but not the same instance.\n\n**Remember Keys**: Control when state resets by passing keys to `remember(key1, key2) { }`. State recreates when any key changes. Omit keys only when state should survive all recompositions.\n\n## Saving UI State\n- Use `rememberSaveable` for UI state hoisted in composables or plain state holders; save only minimal, small data.\n- Saved state storage is limited (Android Bundle: ~1MB); do not store large objects or lists. Store IDs/keys and rehydrate from data/persistent storage.\n- Android: Use `SavedStateHandle` in a ViewModel for UI element state that must survive process death; keep it small and session-scoped (not persistent app data).\n- Do not save full screen UI state; rebuild it from the data layer on restoration.\n\n## Observable Types in Compose\n- Convert observable types to `State<T>` before reading in composables.\n- `Flow`: use `collectAsState` (platform-agnostic, always collects) or `collectAsStateWithLifecycle` (Android only, lifecycle-aware, pauses collection when UI is not visible).\n- `LiveData` (Android): use `observeAsState`.\n- For custom observables, create a `State<T>` via `produceState`.\n\n## State Callbacks (RememberObserver / RetainObserver)\n- Run initialization side-effects in `onRemembered` / `onRetained`, not in constructors or remember/retain lambdas.\n- Always cancel work in `onForgotten` / `onRetired`; handle `onAbandoned` for canceled compositions.\n- Keep implementations private; expose safe factory functions like `rememberX()` to avoid misuse.\n- Do not remember the same object twice; do not pass parameters that are already wrapped in `State<T>` to another `remember` call—this creates unnecessary nested observability.\n\n## Common Anti-Patterns\n- Storing mutable collections or mutable data classes directly as state; prefer immutable containers wrapped in `State` or use snapshot state collections (`mutableStateListOf`, `mutableStateMapOf`).\n- Duplicating state in multiple owners instead of hoisting to a single source of truth.\n- Mixing remember and retain for the same object; remembering/retaining objects with mismatched lifespans.\n- Saving large or complex objects in `rememberSaveable`/`SavedStateHandle` (Android); save IDs and rehydrate instead.\n- Computing derived values inside composables without `derivedStateOf`, causing unnecessary recompositions.\n\n## Output Expectations\n- Favor stateless composables with `value` + callbacks.\n- Prefer lowest common ancestor hoisting.\n- Choose lifecycle APIs intentionally; call out saving strategy explicitly.\n- Keep state minimal, immutable, and observable.\n\n## References\n- Load `references/compose-state-guidance.md` for decision trees, tables, and code examples.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:49:30.142Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Android Agents needing advanced UI state management capabilities with Compose UIs and unidirectional data flow.","zh":"适合需要使用Compose UI和单向数据流的高级UI状态管理功能的Android代理。","ja":"Compose UIと単方向のデータフローを使用した高度なUI状態管理機能を必要とするAndroidエージェントに適しています。","ko":"Compose UI와 단방향 데이터 흐름을 사용한 고급 UI 상태 관리 기능이 필요한 Android 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Android que necesitan capacidades de gestión de estado de UI avanzadas con Compose UI y flujo de datos unidireccional.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Android nécessitant des capacités de gestion d''état de l''UI avancées avec Compose UI et flux de données unidirectionnel.","de":"Perfekt für Android-Agents, die erweiterte UI-Zustandsverwaltungsfähigkeiten mit Compose-UI und unidirektionalem Datenfluss benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Android que precisam de capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de estado de UI com Compose UIs e fluxo de dados unidirecional.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Android, которым требуются продвинутые возможности управления состоянием UI с Compose UI и односторонним потоком данных.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء Android الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لإدارة حالة واجهة المستخدم مع Compose UIs وتدفق البيانات بالاتجاه الواحد."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply state hoisting and choose the right state owner, lifespan, and saving strategy, utilizing Android ViewModel for complex UI/business logic and ensuring efficient data flow with Compose UIs.","zh":"赋予代理应用状态提升和选择合适的状态所有者、生命周期和保存策略的能力，利用Android ViewModel处理复杂的UI/业务逻辑，并确保Compose UI的高效数据流。","ja":"エージェントに状態の引き上げと適切な状態の所有者、ライフサイクル、保存戦略の選択を適用する能力を与え、Android ViewModelを使用して複雑なUI/ビジネスロジックを処理し、Compose UIの効率的なデータフローを確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 상태 호이스팅을 적용하고 적절한 상태 소유자, 수명주기 및 저장 전략을 선택할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, Android ViewModel을 사용하여 복잡한 UI/비즈니스 논리를 처리하고 Compose UI의 효율적인 데이터 흐름을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar el elevamiento de estado y elegir el propietario de estado, la vida útil y la estrategia de guardado adecuados, utilizando Android ViewModel para lógica de UI/comercial compleja y asegurando un flujo de datos eficiente con Compose UI.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer le hoisting d''état et de choisir le propriétaire d''état, la durée de vie et la stratégie d''enregistrement appropriés, en utilisant Android ViewModel pour une logique d''UI/entreprise complexe et en assurant un flux de données efficace avec Compose UI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, den Zustand zu überlagern und den richtigen Zustandseigner, die Lebensdauer und die Speicherstrategie zu wählen, indem Android ViewModel für komplexe UI/Geschäftslogik verwendet wird und einen effizienten Datenfluss mit Compose-UI sichergestellt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar o carregamento de estado e escolher o proprietário de estado, vida útil e estratégia de salvamento certos, utilizando Android ViewModel para lógica de UI/negócios complexa e garantindo um fluxo de dados eficiente com Compose UIs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять подъем состояния и выбирать правильного владельца состояния, срок службы и стратегию сохранения, используя Android ViewModel для сложной логики UI/бизнес и обеспечивая эффективный поток данных с Compose UI.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تطبيق رفع الحالة واختيار مالك الحالة ومدة الحياة واستراتيجية الحفظ المناسبة، باستخدام Android ViewModel للlogic UI/الاعمال المعقدة وضمان تدفق بيانات فعال مع Compose UIs."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing UI state management for multiple social media platforms","Implementing unidirectional data flow in Compose UIs","Choosing the right state owner for complex UI/business logic"],"zh":["为多个社交媒体平台优化UI状态管理","在Compose UI中实现单向数据流","为复杂的UI/业务逻辑选择合适的状态所有者"],"ja":["複数のソーシャルメディアプラットフォームのUI状態管理を最適化する","Compose UI内で単方向のデータフローを実現する","複雑なUI/ビジネスロジックに適切な状態の所有者を選択する"],"ko":["여러 소셜 미디어 플랫폼에 대한 UI 상태 관리 최적화","Compose UI에서 단방향 데이터 흐름 구현","복잡한 UI/비즈니스 논리에 적합한 상태 소유자 선택"],"es":["Optimizar la gestión de estado de UI para múltiples plataformas de redes sociales","Implementar un flujo de datos unidireccional en Compose UI","Elegir el propietario de estado adecuado para lógica de UI/comercial compleja"],"fr":["Optimiser la gestion d''état de l''UI pour plusieurs plateformes de réseaux sociaux","Mettre en œuvre un flux de données unidirectionnel dans Compose UI","Choisir le propriétaire d''état approprié pour une logique d''UI/entreprise complexe"],"de":["Optimieren der UI-Zustandsverwaltung für mehrere soziale Medienplattformen","Implementieren eines unidirektionalen Datenflusses in Compose-UI","Wählen des richtigen Zustandseigners für komplexe UI/Geschäftslogik"],"pt":["Otimizar o gerenciamento de estado de UI para várias plataformas de mídia social","Implementar fluxo de dados unidirecional em Compose UIs","Escolher o proprietário de estado certo para lógica de UI/negócios complexa"],"ru":["Оптимизировать управление состоянием UI для нескольких социальных медиа-платформ","Реализовать односторонний поток данных в Compose UI","Выбрать правильного владельца состояния для сложной логики UI/бизнес"],"ar":["تحسين إدارة حالة واجهة المستخدم لمختلف منصات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية","تنفيذ تدفق بيانات بالاتجاه الواحد في Compose UIs","اختيار مالك الحالة المناسب للlogic UI/الأعمال المعقدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Compose UIs and Android ViewModel","Limited to Android-based applications"],"zh":["需要了解Compose UI和Android ViewModel","仅限于基于Android的应用程序"],"ja":["Compose UIとAndroid ViewModelの知識が必要","Androidベースのアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["Compose UI 및 Android ViewModel에 대한 지식이 필요","Android 기반 애플리케이션으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de Compose UI y Android ViewModel","Limitado a aplicaciones basadas en Android"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en Compose UI et Android ViewModel","Limité aux applications basées sur Android"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Compose-UI und Android ViewModel","Begrenzt auf Android-basierte Anwendungen"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de Compose UIs e Android ViewModel","Limitado a aplicações baseadas em Android"],"ru":["Требует знания Compose UI и Android ViewModel","Ограничен для приложений на основе Android"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة Compose UIs و Android ViewModel","محدود للتطبيقات المستندة إلى Android"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
