ыков для плагинов Claude Code, расширяя его возможности с помощью специализированных...","ar":"تطوير المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة لملحقات Claude Code، وتوسيع إمكانياتها باستخدام المعرفة المتخصصة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["模块化、自包含的包","提供专业知识和工具","扩展 Claude 的能力","支持特定领域或任务","易于集成和使用"],"ja":["モジュール化された、自包含的なパッケージ","専門知識とツールを提供","Claude の機能を拡張","特定のドメインまたはタスクをサポート","簡単に統合および使用"],"ko":["모듈화된, 자체 포함된 패키지","전문 지식과 도구를 제공","Claude의 기능을 확장","특정 도메인 또는 작업을 지원","쉽게 통합 및 사용"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades modulares","Extensão das capacidades de Claude","Conhecimento especializado para domínios específicos","Transformação de Claude em agente especializado","Fornecimento de ferramentas e workflows especializados"],"ru":["Создание модульных навыков","Расширение возможностей Claude","Специализированные знания для конкретных доменов","Преобразование Claude в специализированного агента","Предоставление специализированных инструментов и рабочих процессов"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات متكاملة","توسيع إمكانيات Claude","معرفة متخصصة لمناطق معينة","تحويل Claude إلى وكيل متخصص","توفير أدوات وعمليات عمل متخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Claude Code 插件","技能开发","模块化包","专业知识","工具","扩展功能","特定领域","任务"],"ja":["Claude Code プラグイン","スキル開発","モジュール化されたパッケージ","専門知識","ツール","機能拡張","特定のドメイン","タスク"],"ko":["Claude Code 플러그인","스킬 개발","모듈화된 패키지","전문 지식","도구","기능 확장","특정 도메인","작업"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades","Claude Code","plugins","conhecimento especializado","domínios específicos","agente especializado","ferramentas","workflows","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["разработка навыков","Claude Code","плагины","специализированные знания","конкретные домены","специализированный агент","инструменты","рабочие процессы","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تطوير المهارات","Claude Code","ملحقات","معرفة متخصصة","مناطق معينة","وكيل متخصص","أدوات","عمليات عمل","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"powerhouse-inc","repo":"service-offering","repoPath":"powerhouse-inc/service-offering","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.461Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Skill Development","description":"This skill should be used when the user wants to create a skill, add a skill to plugin, write a new skill, improve skill description, organize skill content, or needs guidance on skill structure, progressive disclosure, or skill development best practices for Claude Code plugins.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Skill Development for Claude Code Plugins\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills for Claude Code plugins.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### W","body":"# Skill Development for Claude Code Plugins\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills for Claude Code plugins.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\n**Metadata Quality:** The `name` and `description` in YAML frontmatter determine when Claude will use the skill. Be specific about what the skill does and when to use it. Use the third-person (e.g. \"This skill should be used when...\" instead of \"Use this skill when...\").\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited*)\n\n*Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nTo create a skill, follow the \"Skill Creation Process\" in order, skipping steps only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\n**For Claude Code plugins:** When building a hooks skill, the analysis shows:\n1. Developers repeatedly need to validate hooks.json and test hook scripts\n2. `scripts/validate-hook-schema.sh` and `scripts/test-hook.sh` utilities would be helpful\n3. `references/patterns.md` for detailed hook patterns to avoid bloating SKILL.md\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Create Skill Structure\n\nFor Claude Code plugins, create the skill directory structure:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p plugin-name/skills/skill-name/{references,examples,scripts}\ntouch plugin-name/skills/skill-name/SKILL.md\n```\n\n**Note:** Unlike the generic skill-creator which uses `init_skill.py`, plugin skills are created directly in the plugin''s `skills/` directory with a simpler manual structure.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-created or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Focus on including information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAlso, delete any example files and directories not needed for the skill. Create only the directories you actually need (references/, examples/, scripts/).\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Style:** Write the entire skill using **imperative/infinitive form** (verb-first instructions), not second person. Use objective, instructional language (e.g., \"To accomplish X, do Y\" rather than \"You should do X\" or \"If you need to do X\"). This maintains consistency and clarity for AI consumption.\n\n**Description (Frontmatter):** Use third-person format with specific trigger phrases:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: Skill Name\ndescription: This skill should be used when the user asks to \"specific phrase 1\", \"specific phrase 2\", \"specific phrase 3\". Include exact phrases users would say that should trigger this skill. Be concrete and specific.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n```\n\n**Good description examples:**\n```yaml\ndescription: This skill should be used when the user asks to \"create a hook\", \"add a PreToolUse hook\", \"validate tool use\", \"implement prompt-based hooks\", or mentions hook events (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, Stop).\n```\n\n**Bad description examples:**\n```yaml\ndescription: Use this skill when working with hooks.  # Wrong person, vague\ndescription: Load when user needs hook help.  # Not third person\ndescription: Provides hook guidance.  # No trigger phrases\n```\n\nTo complete SKILL.md body, answer the following questions:\n\n1. What is the purpose of the skill, in a few sentences?\n2. When should the skill be used? (Include this in frontmatter description with specific triggers)\n3. In practice, how should Claude use the skill? All reusable skill contents developed above should be referenced so that Claude knows how to use them.\n\n**Keep SKILL.md lean:** Target 1,500-2,000 words for the body. Move detailed content to references/:\n- Detailed patterns → `references/patterns.md`\n- Advanced techniques → `references/advanced.md`\n- Migration guides → `references/migration.md`\n- API references → `references/api-reference.md`\n\n**Reference resources in SKILL.md:**\n```markdown\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n\nFor detailed patterns and techniques, consult:\n- **`references/patterns.md`** - Common patterns\n- **`references/advanced.md`** - Advanced use cases\n\n### Example Files\n\nWorking examples in `examples/`:\n- **`example-script.sh`** - Working example\n```\n\n### Step 5: Validate and Test\n\n**For plugin skills, validation is different from generic skills:**\n\n1. **Check structure**: Skill directory in `plugin-name/skills/skill-name/`\n2. **Validate SKILL.md**: Has frontmatter with name and description\n3. **Check trigger phrases**: Description includes specific user queries\n4. **Verify writing style**: Body uses imperative/infinitive form, not second person\n5. **Test progressive disclosure**: SKILL.md is lean (~1,500-2,000 words), detailed content in references/\n6. **Check references**: All referenced files exist\n7. **Validate examples**: Examples are complete and correct\n8. **Test scripts**: Scripts are executable and work correctly\n\n**Use the skill-reviewer agent:**\n```\nAsk: \"Review my skill and check if it follows best practices\"\n```\n\nThe skill-reviewer agent will check description quality, content organization, and progressive disclosure.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n\n**Common improvements:**\n- Strengthen trigger phrases in description\n- Move long sections from SKILL.md to references/\n- Add missing examples or scripts\n- Clarify ambiguous instructions\n- Add edge case handling\n\n## Plugin-Specific Considerations\n\n### Skill Location in Plugins\n\nPlugin skills live in the plugin''s `skills/` directory:\n\n```\nmy-plugin/\n├── .claude-plugin/\n│   └── plugin.json\n├── commands/\n├── agents/\n└── skills/\n    └── my-skill/\n        ├── SKILL.md\n        ├── references/\n        ├── examples/\n        └── scripts/\n```\n\n### Auto-Discovery\n\nClaude Code automatically discovers skills:\n- Scans `skills/` directory\n- Finds subdirectories containing `SKILL.md`\n- Loads skill metadata (name + description) always\n- Loads SKILL.md body when skill triggers\n- Loads references/examples when needed\n\n### No Packaging Needed\n\nPlugin skills are distributed as part of the plugin, not as separate ZIP files. Users get skills when they install the plugin.\n\n### Testing in Plugins\n\nTest skills by installing plugin locally:\n\n```bash\n# Test with --plugin-dir\ncc --plugin-dir /path/to/plugin\n\n# Ask questions that should trigger the skill\n# Verify skill loads correctly\n```\n\n## Examples from Plugin-Dev\n\nStudy the skills in this plugin as examples of best practices:\n\n**hook-development skill:**\n- Excellent trigger phrases: \"create a hook\", \"add a PreToolUse hook\", etc.\n- Lean SKILL.md (1,651 words)\n- 3 references/ files for detailed content\n- 3 examples/ of working hooks\n- 3 scripts/ utilities\n\n**agent-development skill:**\n- Strong triggers: \"create an agent\", \"agent frontmatter\", etc.\n- Focused SKILL.md (1,438 words)\n- References include the AI generation prompt from Claude Code\n- Complete agent examples\n\n**plugin-settings skill:**\n- Specific triggers: \"plugin settings\", \".local.md files\", \"YAML frontmatter\"\n- References show real implementations (multi-agent-swarm, ralph-loop)\n- Working parsing scripts\n\nEach demonstrates progressive disclosure and strong triggering.\n\n## Progressive Disclosure in Practice\n\n### What Goes in SKILL.md\n\n**Include (always loaded when skill triggers):**\n- Core concepts and overview\n- Essential procedures and workflows\n- Quick reference tables\n- Pointers to references/examples/scripts\n- Most common use cases\n\n**Keep under 3,000 words, ideally 1,500-2,000 words**\n\n### What Goes in references/\n\n**Move to references/ (loaded as needed):**\n- Detailed patterns and advanced techniques\n- Comprehensive API documentation\n- Migration guides\n- Edge cases and troubleshooting\n- Extensive examples and walkthroughs\n\n**Each reference file can be large (2,000-5,000+ words)**\n\n### What Goes in examples/\n\n**Working code examples:**\n- Complete, runnable scripts\n- Configuration files\n- Template files\n- Real-world usage examples\n\n**Users can copy and adapt these directly**\n\n### What Goes in scripts/\n\n**Utility scripts:**\n- Validation tools\n- Testing helpers\n- Parsing utilities\n- Automation scripts\n\n**Should be executable and documented**\n\n## Writing Style Requirements\n\n### Imperative/Infinitive Form\n\nWrite using verb-first instructions, not second person:\n\n**Correct (imperative):**\n```\nTo create a hook, define the event type.\nConfigure the MCP server with authentication.\nValidate settings before use.\n```\n\n**Incorrect (second person):**\n```\nYou should create a hook by defining the event type.\nYou need to configure the MCP server.\nYou must validate settings before use.\n```\n\n### Third-Person in Description\n\nThe frontmatter description must use third person:\n\n**Correct:**\n```yaml\ndescription: This skill should be used when the user asks to \"create X\", \"configure Y\"...\n```\n\n**Incorrect:**\n```yaml\ndescription: Use this skill when you want to create X...\ndescription: Load this skill when user asks...\n```\n\n### Objective, Instructional Language\n\nFocus on what to do, not who should do it:\n\n**Correct:**\n```\nParse the frontmatter using sed.\nExtract fields with grep.\nValidate values before use.\n```\n\n**Incorrect:**\n```\nYou can parse the frontmatter...\nClaude should extract fields...\nThe user might validate values...\n```\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing a skill:\n\n**Structure:**\n- [ ] SKILL.md file exists with valid YAML frontmatter\n- [ ] Frontmatter has `name` and `description` fields\n- [ ] Markdown body is present and substantial\n- [ ] Referenced files actually exist\n\n**Description Quality:**\n- [ ] Uses third person (\"This skill should be used when...\")\n- [ ] Includes specific trigger phrases users would say\n- [ ] Lists concrete scenarios (\"create X\", \"configure Y\")\n- [ ] Not vague or generic\n\n**Content Quality:**\n- [ ] SKILL.md body uses imperative/infinitive form\n- [ ] Body is focused and lean (1,500-2,000 words ideal, <5k max)\n- [ ] Detailed content moved to references/\n- [ ] Examples are complete and working\n- [ ] Scripts are executable and documented\n\n**Progressive Disclosure:**\n- [ ] Core concepts in SKILL.md\n- [ ] Detailed docs in references/\n- [ ] Working code in examples/\n- [ ] Utilities in scripts/\n- [ ] SKILL.md references these resources\n\n**Testing:**\n- [ ] Skill triggers on expected user queries\n- [ ] Content is helpful for intended tasks\n- [ ] No duplicated information across files\n- [ ] References load when needed\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n### Mistake 1: Weak Trigger Description\n\n❌ **Bad:**\n```yaml\ndescription: Provides guidance for working with hooks.\n```\n\n**Why bad:** Vague, no specific trigger phrases, not third person\n\n✅ **Good:**\n```yaml\ndescription: This skill should be used when the user asks to \"create a hook\", \"add a PreToolUse hook\", \"validate tool use\", or mentions hook events. Provides comprehensive hooks API guidance.\n```\n\n**Why good:** Third person, specific phrases, concrete scenarios\n\n### Mistake 2: Too Much in SKILL.md\n\n❌ **Bad:**\n```\nskill-name/\n└── SKILL.md  (8,000 words - everything in one file)\n```\n\n**Why bad:** Bloats context when skill loads, detailed content always loaded\n\n✅ **Good:**\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md  (1,800 words - core essentials)\n└── references/\n    ├── patterns.md (2,500 words)\n    └── advanced.md (3,700 words)\n```\n\n**Why good:** Progressive disclosure, detailed content loaded only when needed\n\n### Mistake 3: Second Person Writing\n\n❌ **Bad:**\n```markdown\nYou should start by reading the configuration file.\nYou need to validate the input.\nYou can use the grep tool to search.\n```\n\n**Why bad:** Second person, not imperative form\n\n✅ **Good:**\n```markdown\nStart by reading the configuration file.\nValidate the input before processing.\nUse the grep tool to search for patterns.\n```\n\n**Why good:** Imperative form, direct instructions\n\n### Mistake 4: Missing Resource References\n\n❌ **Bad:**\n```markdown\n# SKILL.md\n\n[Core content]\n\n[No mention of references/ or examples/]\n```\n\n**Why bad:** Claude doesn''t know references exist\n\n✅ **Good:**\n```markdown\n# SKILL.md\n\n[Core content]\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n- **`references/patterns.md`** - Detailed patterns\n- **`references/advanced.md`** - Advanced techniques\n\n### Examples\n- **`examples/script.sh`** - Working example\n```\n\n**Why good:** Claude knows where to find additional information\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Minimal Skill\n\n```\nskill-name/\n└── SKILL.md\n```\n\nGood for: Simple knowledge, no complex resources needed\n\n### Standard Skill (Recommended)\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md\n├── references/\n│   └── detailed-guide.md\n└── examples/\n    └── working-example.sh\n```\n\nGood for: Most plugin skills with detailed documentation\n\n### Complete Skill\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md\n├── references/\n│   ├── patterns.md\n│   └── advanced.md\n├── examples/\n│   ├── example1.sh\n│   └── example2.json\n└── scripts/\n    └── validate.sh\n```\n\nGood for: Complex domains with validation utilities\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n✅ **DO:**\n- Use third-person in description (\"This skill should be used when...\")\n- Include specific trigger phrases (\"create X\", \"configure Y\")\n- Keep SKILL.md lean (1,500-2,000 words)\n- Use progressive disclosure (move details to references/)\n- Write in imperative/infinitive form\n- Reference supporting files clearly\n- Provide working examples\n- Create utility scripts for common operations\n- Study plugin-dev''s skills as templates\n\n❌ **DON''T:**\n- Use second person anywhere\n- Have vague trigger conditions\n- Put everything in SKILL.md (>3,000 words without references/)\n- Write in second person (\"You should...\")\n- Leave resources unreferenced\n- Include broken or incomplete examples\n- Skip validation\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Study These Skills\n\nPlugin-dev''s skills demonstrate best practices:\n- `../hook-development/` - Progressive disclosure, utilities\n- `../agent-development/` - AI-assisted creation, references\n- `../mcp-integration/` - Comprehensive references\n- `../plugin-settings/` - Real-world examples\n- `../command-development/` - Clear critical concepts\n- `../plugin-structure/` - Good organization\n\n### Reference Files\n\nFor complete skill-creator methodology:\n- **`references/skill-creator-original.md`** - Full original skill-creator content\n\n## Implementation Workflow\n\nTo create a skill for your plugin:\n\n1. **Understand use cases**: Identify concrete examples of skill usage\n2. **Plan resources**: Determine what scripts/references/examples needed\n3. **Create structure**: `mkdir -p skills/skill-name/{references,examples,scripts}`\n4. **Write SKILL.md**:\n   - Frontmatter with third-person description and trigger phrases\n   - Lean body (1,500-2,000 words) in imperative form\n   - Reference supporting files\n5. **Add resources**: Create references/, examples/, scripts/ as needed\n6. **Validate**: Check description, writing style, organization\n7. **Test**: Verify skill loads on expected triggers\n8. **Iterate**: Improve based on usage\n\nFocus on strong trigger descriptions, progressive disclosure, and imperative writing style for effective skills that load when needed and provide targeted guidance.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:52:46.816Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skill development","zh":"非常适合需要专门知识和工作流扩展的AI代理，如Claude Code，通过模块化技能开发","ja":"Claude Codeのような、専門知識とワークフローの拡張が必要なAIエージェントに最適なものです。モジュラーなスキル開発を通じて","ko":"클라우드 코드 같은 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 모듈화된 스킬 개발을 통해","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo a través del desarrollo modular de habilidades","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code ayant besoin de connaissances spécialisées et d''extensions de workflow grâce au développement modulaire de compétences","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen durch modulare Fähigkeitsentwicklung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code que precisam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho por meio do desenvolvimento de habilidades modulares","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса через модульное развитие навыков","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code الذي يحتاج إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيع سير العمل من خلال تطوير المهارات المودular"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular packages that extend capabilities, and providing onboarding guides for specific domains or tasks through Claude Code plugins, leveraging specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools","zh":"赋予代理转化为具有程序化知识的专门实体的能力，利用模块化包扩展能力，并通过Claude Code插件为特定领域或任务提供入门指南，利用专门知识、工作流和工具","ja":"エージェントが手順きょう知識を備えた専門エンティティに変化する力を与え、モジュラーなパッケージを使用して機能を拡張し、Claude Codeプラグインを通じて特定のドメインまたはタスクのためのオンボーディングガイドを提供し、専門知識、ワークフロー、およびツールを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 절차 지식으로 특별한 엔티티로 변신할 수 있는 힘을 부여하고, 모듈화된 패키지를 사용하여 기능을 확장하며, 클라우드 코드 플러그인을 통해 특정 도메인 또는 작업에 대한 온보딩 가이드를 제공하고, 전문 지식, 워크플로, 도구를 활용한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimientos procedimentales, utilizando paquetes modulares que amplían las capacidades y proporcionando guías de incorporación para dominios o tareas específicas a través de plugins de Claude Code, aprovechando conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, en utilisant des packages modulaires qui étendent les capacités et en fournissant des guides d''intégration pour des domaines ou des tâches spécifiques via les plugins de Claude Code, en exploitant des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Einheiten zu verwandeln, die mit prozeduralem Wissen ausgestattet sind, indem sie modulare Pakete verwenden, die die Fähigkeiten erweitern und Onboarding-Anleitungen für bestimmte Bereiche oder Aufgaben über Claude Code-Plugins bereitstellen, wobei spezialisiertes Wissen, Workflows und Tools genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, utilizando pacotes modulares que estendem as capacidades e fornecendo guias de integração para domínios ou tarefas específicas por meio de plugins do Claude Code, aproveitando conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, используя модульные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности, и предоставляя руководства по интеграции для конкретных областей или задач через плагины Claude Code, используя специализированные знания, рабочие процессы и инструменты","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تحويل نفسه إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بالمعرفة الإجرائية، باستخدام حزم موديولر تمدد القدرات وتوفر إرشادات للتسجيل في مجالات أو مهام محددة من خلال ملحقات كلود كود، مستفيداً من المعرفة المتخصصة والعمليات والادوات"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating customized plugins for domain-specific tasks","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Extending agent capabilities with modular skill packages"],"zh":["为特定领域任务创建自定义插件","为代理开发程序化知识","使用模块化技能包扩展代理功能"],"ja":["特定ドメインタスク用のカスタムプラグインを作成する","エージェントのための手順きょう知識を開発する","モジュラーなスキルパッケージを使用してエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["특정 도메인 작업을 위한 사용자 정의 플러그인을 생성한다","에이전트를 위한 절차 지식을 개발한다","모듈화된 스킬 패키지를 사용하여 에이전트의 기능을 확장한다"],"es":["Crear plugins personalizados para tareas específicas de dominio","Desarrollar conocimientos procedimentales para agentes","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con paquetes de habilidades modulares"],"fr":["Créer des plugins personnalisés pour des tâches spécifiques de domaine","Développer des connaissances procédurales pour les agents","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des packages de compétences modulaires"],"de":["Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Plugins für domänen-spezifische Aufgaben","Entwickeln von prozeduralem Wissen für Agenten","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten mit modularen Fähigkeitspaketen"],"pt":["Criar plug-ins personalizados para tarefas específicas de domínio","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para agentes","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com pacotes de habilidades modulares"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских плагинов для задач, специфичных для домена","Разработка процедурных знаний для агентов","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью модульных пакетов навыков"],"ar":["إنشاء ملحقات مخصصة لمهام محددة للمجال","تطوير معرفة إجرائية للوكيل","توسيع قدرات الوكيل باستخدام حزم مهارات موديولر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code plugin compatibility","Procedural knowledge limitations apply"],"zh":["需要Claude Code插件兼容性","程序化知识的限制适用"],"ja":["Claude Codeプラグインの互換性が必要","手順きょう知識の制限が適用される"],"ko":["클라우드 코드 플러그인 호환성이 필요하다","절차 지식 제한이 적용된다"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con plugins de Claude Code","Se aplican limitaciones de conocimiento procedimental"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité des plugins de Claude Code","Les limites des connaissances procédurales s''appliquent"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit Claude Code-Plugins","Prozedurales Wissen-Grenzen gelten"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade com plugin do Claude Code","Limitações do conhecimento procedural se aplicam"],"ru":["Требуется совместимость с плагином Claude Code","Применяются ограничения процедурных знаний"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقاً مع ملحقات كلود كود","تطبق قيود المعرفة الإجرائية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('juninmd/KamisamaLoader/Modding Core Logic', 'community', 'juninmd', 'KamisamaLoader', 'juninmd/KamisamaLoader', 'Modding Core Logic', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.461Z', '2026-02-18T07:52:19.111Z', NULL, '{"id":"juninmd/KamisamaLoader/Modding Core Logic","name":"Modding Core Logic","description":{"zh":"Modding Core Logic 是一个用于游戏模组开发的核心逻辑，包括依赖、实体和目录结构","ja":"Modding Core Logic はゲームモッド開発のためのコアロジックであり、依存関係、エンティティ、ディレクトリ構造を含む","ko":"Modding Core Logic 는 게임 모드 개발을 위한 핵심 로직으로, 종속성, 엔티티 및 디렉토리 구조를 포함","es":"El núcleo de modificación es un conjunto de herramientas para desarrolladores de juegos. Permite la creación y gestión de paquetes de modificación y perfiles de juego.","fr":"Le core de modding est un ensemble d''outils pour les développeurs de jeux. Il permet la création et la gestion de packages de mod et de profils de jeu.","de":"Der Modding-Core ist ein Satz von Tools für Spielentwickler. Er ermöglicht die Erstellung und Verwaltung von Mod-Paketen und Spielprofilen.","pt":"Modding Core Logic é uma habilidade que permite desenvolver mods personalizados. Ela inclui dependências como Zip Handling e Networking.","ru":"Основная логика моддинга - это навык, который позволяет разрабатывать кастомные моды. Она включает зависимости, такие как обработка zip и сетевое взаимодействие.","ar":"لوジك التعديل الأساسي هو مهارة تسمح بتطوير تعديلات مخصصة. تشمل اعتماديات مثل التعامل مع الملفات المضغوطة والشبكات.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Modding Core Logic 核心模组开发","ja":"Modding Core Logic モッディングコアロジック","ko":"Modding Core Logic 핵심 모딩 로직","es":"Núcleo de Modificación: Desarrollo de Lógica de Juegos","fr":"Modding Core Logic : Développement de Jeux","de":"Modding-Core-Logik: Spiel-Entwicklung","pt":"Modding Core Logic: Desenvolvimento de Mods","ru":"Основная логика моддинга: разработка модов","ar":"لوジك التعديل الأساسي: تطوير التعديلات","en":"Modding Core Logic"},"description":{"zh":"Modding Core Logic 是一个用于游戏模组开发的核心逻辑，包括依赖、实体和目录结构","ja":"Modding Core Logic はゲームモッド開発のためのコアロジックであり、依存関係、エンティティ、ディレクトリ構造を含む","ko":"Modding Core Logic 는 게임 모드 개발을 위한 핵심 로직으로, 종속성, 엔티티 및 디렉토리 구조를 포함","es":"El núcleo de modificación es un conjunto de herramientas para desarrolladores de juegos. Permite la creación y gestión de paquetes de modificación y perfiles...","fr":"Le core de modding est un ensemble d''outils pour les développeurs de jeux. Il permet la création et la gestion de packages de mod et de profils de jeu.","de":"Der Modding-Core ist ein Satz von Tools für Spielentwickler. Er ermöglicht die Erstellung und Verwaltung von Mod-Paketen und Spielprofilen.","pt":"Modding Core Logic é uma habilidade que permite desenvolver mods personalizados. Ela inclui dependências como Zip Handling e Networking.","ru":"Основная логика моддинга - это навык, который позволяет разрабатывать кастомные моды. Она включает зависимости, такие как обработка zip и сетевое взаимодейст...","ar":"لوジك التعديل الأساسي هو مهارة تسمح بتطوير تعديلات مخصصة. تشمل اعتماديات مثل التعامل مع الملفات المضغوطة والشبكات.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Zip 处理","网络请求","路径操作","模组管理","配置文件管理","GameBanana 集成"],"ja":["Zip 処理","ネットワークリクエスト","パス操作","モッド管理","設定ファイル管理","GameBanana 統合"],"ko":["Zip 처리","네트워크 요청","경로 조작","모드 관리","구성 파일 관리","GameBanana 통합"],"es":["Gestión de paquetes de modificación","Creación y edición de perfiles de juego","Integración con GameBanana","Soporte para Zip Handling y Networking","Uso de dependencias como adm-zip y fetch","Compatibilidad con Node.js"],"fr":["Gestion de packages de mod","Création et édition de profils de jeu","Intégration avec GameBanana","Prise en charge de Zip Handling et Networking","Utilisation de dépendances comme adm-zip et fetch","Compatibilité avec Node.js"],"de":["Verwaltung von Mod-Paketen","Erstellung und Bearbeitung von Spielprofilen","Integration mit GameBanana","Unterstützung für Zip-Handling und Networking","Verwendung von Abhängigkeiten wie adm-zip und fetch","Kompatibilität mit Node.js"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de mods personalizados","Manipulação de arquivos zip","Integração com redes","Criação de perfis de mods","Integração com GameBanana"],"ru":["Разработка кастомных модов","Обработка zip-файлов","Интеграция с сетями","Создание профилей модов","Интеграция с GameBanana"],"ar":["تطوير تعديلات مخصصة","التعامل مع الملفات المضغوطة","التكامل مع الشبكات","إنشاء ملفات تعريف التعديلات","التكامل مع GameBanana"]},"keywords":{"zh":["游戏模组开发","Modding Core Logic","模组管理","配置文件管理","GameBanana","Zip 处理","网络请求","路径操作"],"ja":["ゲームモッド開発","Modding Core Logic","モッド管理","設定ファイル管理","GameBanana","Zip 処理","ネットワークリクエスト","パス操作"],"ko":["게임 모드 개발","Modding Core Logic","모드 관리","구성 파일 관리","GameBanana","Zip 처리","네트워크 요청","경로 조작"],"es":["modificación de juegos","desarrollo de juegos","núcleo de modificación","paquetes de modificación","perfiles de juego","GameBanana","adm-zip","fetch","Node.js"],"fr":["modding de jeux","développement de jeux","core de modding","packages de mod","profils de jeu","GameBanana","adm-zip","fetch","Node.js"],"de":["Spielmodifizierung","Spielentwicklung","Modding-Core","Mod-Pakete","Spielprofile","GameBanana","adm-zip","fetch","Node.js"],"pt":["modding core logic","desenvolvimento de mods","manipulação de arquivos","integração com redes","criação de perfis de mods","gamebanana","mods de jogos"],"ru":["основная логика моддинга","разработка модов","обработка файлов","интеграция с сетями","создание профилей модов","gamebanana","моды игр"],"ar":["لوジك التعديل الأساسي","تطوير التعديلات","التعامل مع الملفات","التكامل مع الشبكات","إنشاء ملفات تعريف التعديلات","gamebanana","تعديلات الألعاب"]}},"owner":"juninmd","repo":"KamisamaLoader","repoPath":"juninmd/KamisamaLoader","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.461Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Modding Core Logic","description":"Domain logic for mod management, GameBanana integration, and file handling","bodyPreview":"# Modding Core Logic\n\n## Dependencies\n- **Zip Handling**: `adm-zip`\n- **Networking**: `fetch` (native) or `axios` (if added)\n- **Path Manipulation**: `path` (Node.js built-in)\n\n## Domain Entities\n- **Mod**: A modifiction package.\n- **Profile**: A collection of enabled mods.\n- **GameBanana**: The primary source for online mods.\n\n## Key Directories\n- **Game Directory**: Where the game is installed (e.g., `Steam/steamapps/common/...`).\n- **Mods Directory**: Where mods are stored (often a subfolder","body":"# Modding Core Logic\n\n## Dependencies\n- **Zip Handling**: `adm-zip`\n- **Networking**: `fetch` (native) or `axios` (if added)\n- **Path Manipulation**: `path` (Node.js built-in)\n\n## Domain Entities\n- **Mod**: A modifiction package.\n- **Profile**: A collection of enabled mods.\n- **GameBanana**: The primary source for online mods.\n\n## Key Directories\n- **Game Directory**: Where the game is installed (e.g., `Steam/steamapps/common/...`).\n- **Mods Directory**: Where mods are stored (often a subfolder of the game or a dedicated `mods` folder).\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Installing a Mod\n1. Extract the zip file using `adm-zip`.\n2. Validate the structure (check for specific mod files).\n3. Move files to the correct destination in the game directory.\n4. Record the installation in `installed-mods.json` (or database).\n\n### Uninstalling a Mod\n1. Look up files associated with the mod.\n2. Remove files safely.\n3. Update specific config files if necessary.\n4. Remove entry from `installed-mods.json`.\n\n### GameBanana Integration\n- Fetch mod info using GameBanana API endpoints.\n- Map API responses to the internal `OnlineMod` interface.\n- Handle rate limiting and errors gracefully.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:52:19.111Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Game Modding Agents needing to manage and integrate modification packages using adm-zip, fetch, and path manipulation.","zh":"非常适合需要管理和集成使用adm-zip、fetch和路径操作的修改包的游戏模组代理","ja":"adm-zip、fetch、パス操作を使用して修正パッケージを管理および統合する必要があるゲームモッディングエージェントに最適","ko":"adm-zip, fetch 및 경로 조작을 사용하여 수정 패키지를 관리 및 통합해야 하는 게임 모딩 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de modificación de juegos que necesitan administrar e integrar paquetes de modificación utilizando adm-zip, fetch y manipulación de rutas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de modification de jeux ayant besoin de gérer et d''intégrer des packages de modification en utilisant adm-zip, fetch et manipulation de chemins.","de":"Perfekt für Game-Modding-Agents, die Modifikationspakete mit adm-zip, fetch und Pfadmanipulation verwalten und integrieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Modificação de Jogos que precisam gerenciar e integrar pacotes de modificação usando adm-zip, fetch e manipulação de caminhos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов моддинга игр, которым необходимо управлять и интегрировать пакеты модификаций с помощью adm-zip, fetch и манипуляций с путями.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تعديل الألعاب الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة وتكامل حزم التعديل باستخدام adm-zip و fetch وMANIPULATION من المسارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle mod installations, updates, and removals by leveraging Zip Handling with adm-zip, networking capabilities via fetch or axios, and path manipulation using Node.js built-in path module, all while interacting with online mod sources like GameBanana.","zh":"通过利用adm-zip的Zip处理、fetch或axios的网络能力以及Node.js内置的路径模块的路径操作，赋予代理处理模组安装、更新和删除的能力，同时与GameBanana等在线模组源交互","ja":"adm-zipのZipハンドリング、fetchまたはaxiosのネットワーク機能、およびNode.jsのビルトインパスモジュールのパス操作を利用して、エージェントが修正のインストール、更新、削除を処理する能力を提供し、GameBananaなどのオンライン修正元とやり取り","ko":"adm-zip의 Zip 처리, fetch 또는 axios의 네트워크 기능 및 Node.js의 내장 경로 모듈의 경로 조작을 활용하여 에이전트가 모드 설치, 업데이트 및 제거를 처리할 수 있도록 하며 GameBananaなどの 온라인 모드 원과 상호 작용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar instalaciones, actualizaciones y eliminaciones de mods aprovechando el manejo de Zip con adm-zip, capacidades de networking a través de fetch o axios, y manipulación de rutas utilizando el módulo de ruta incorporado de Node.js, todo mientras interactúa con fuentes de mods en línea como GameBanana.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les installations, les mises à jour et les suppressions de mods en exploitant la gestion de Zip avec adm-zip, les capacités de réseau via fetch ou axios, et la manipulation de chemins en utilisant le module de chemin intégré de Node.js, le tout en interagissant avec des sources de mods en ligne comme GameBanana.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Mod-Installationen, -Updates und -Entfernungen zu handhaben, indem es die Verwendung von Zip-Handling mit adm-zip, Netzwerkfunktionen über fetch oder axios und Pfadmanipulation mit dem in Node.js integrierten Pfadmodul nutzt, während es mit Online-Mod-Quellen wie GameBanana interagiert.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidar com instalações de mods, atualizações e remoções, aproveitando o tratamento de Zip com adm-zip, capacidades de rede via fetch ou axios e manipulação de caminhos usando o módulo de caminho embutido do Node.js, tudo isso enquanto interage com fontes de mods online como GameBanana.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обрабатывать установки модов, обновления и удаления, используя обработку Zip с помощью adm-zip, сетевые возможности через fetch или axios и манипуляции с путями с помощью встроенного модуля пути Node.js, все это при взаимодействии с онлайн-источниками модов, такими как GameBanana.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية التعامل مع تثبيت التعديلات وتحديثها وإزالتها من خلال استخدام معالجة Zip مع adm-zip وامكانات الشبكة عبر fetch أو axios وMANIPULATION من المسارات باستخدام وحدة المسار المدمجة في Node.js، كل ذلك أثناء التفاعل مع مصادر التعديلات عبر الإنترنت مثل GameBanana."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating mod downloads from GameBanana","Managing mod profiles for different game configurations","Integrating mods into the game directory using path manipulation"],"zh":["从GameBanana自动下载模组","管理不同游戏配置的模组配置文件","使用路径操作将模组集成到游戏目录中"],"ja":["GameBananaから修正を自動ダウンロードする","異なるゲーム構成の修正プロファイルを管理する","パス操作を使用して修正をゲームディレクトリに統合する"],"ko":["GameBanana에서 모드를 자동으로 다운로드","다른 게임 구성의 모드 프로필 관리","경로 조작을 사용하여 모드를 게임 디렉토리에 통합"],"es":["Automatizar descargas de mods desde GameBanana","Administrar perfiles de mods para diferentes configuraciones de juegos","Integrar mods en el directorio del juego utilizando manipulación de rutas"],"fr":["Automatiser les téléchargements de mods à partir de GameBanana","Gérer les profils de mods pour différentes configurations de jeux","Intégrer des mods dans le répertoire du jeu en utilisant la manipulation de chemins"],"de":["Automatisieren von Mod-Downloads von GameBanana","Verwalten von Mod-Profilen für unterschiedliche Spielkonfigurationen","Integrieren von Mods in das Spielverzeichnis unter Verwendung von Pfadmanipulation"],"pt":["Automatizar downloads de mods do GameBanana","Gerenciar perfis de mods para diferentes configurações de jogo","Integrar mods no diretório do jogo usando manipulação de caminhos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать скачивание модов с GameBanana","Управлять профилями модов для разных конфигураций игры","Интегрировать моды в каталог игры с помощью манипуляций с путями"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في تحميل التعديلات من GameBanana","إدارة ملفات تعريف التعديلات لمختلف تكوينات الألعاب","دمج التعديلات في دليل اللعبة باستخدام MANIPULATION من المسارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Node.js environment for path manipulation","Dependent on adm-zip for Zip Handling","Limited to mods sourced from GameBanana or similar repositories"],"zh":["需要Node.js环境进行路径操作","依赖adm-zip进行Zip处理","仅限于GameBanana或类似仓库的模组"],"ja":["パス操作のためにNode.js環境が必要","Zipハンドリングのためにadm-zipに依存","GameBananaまたは同等のリポジトリからの修正に限定"],"ko":["경로 조작을 위해 Node.js 환경이 필요","Zip 처리를 위해 adm-zip에 의존","GameBanana 또는 유사한 리포지토리에서 제공하는 모드에만 한정"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Node.js para la manipulación de rutas","Dependiente de adm-zip para el manejo de Zip","Limitado a mods procedentes de GameBanana o repositorios similares"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Node.js pour la manipulation de chemins","Dépendant de adm-zip pour la gestion de Zip","Limité aux mods provenant de GameBanana ou de dépôts similaires"],"de":["Benötigt eine Node.js-Umgebung für die Pfadmanipulation","Abhängig von adm-zip für das Zip-Handling","Begrenzt auf Mods aus GameBanana oder ähnlichen Repositorien"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Node.js para manipulação de caminhos","Dependente de adm-zip para tratamento de Zip","Limitado a mods originados do GameBanana ou repositórios semelhantes"],"ru":["Требует среды Node.js для манипуляций с путями","Зависит от adm-zip для обработки Zip","Ограничен модами из GameBanana или подобных репозиториев"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Node.js لMANIPULATION من المسارات","يعتمد على adm-zip لمعالجة Zip","محدود بالتعديلات من GameBanana أو مستودعات مماثلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
