"fr":"L''évaluation des systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentsystemen erfordert unterschiedliche Ansätze als traditionelle Software","pt":"A avaliação de sistemas de agentes requer abordagens diferentes das tradicionais. Descubra como construir estruturas de avaliação eficazes","ru":"Оценка систем агентов требует нестандартных подходов. Узнайте, как создать эффективные оценочные рамки","ar":"تقييم أنظمة العوامل يتطلب نهجًا مختلفًا. تعلم كيفية بناء إطارات تقييم فعالة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["构建评估框架","评估代理系统的性能","支持动态决策","处理非确定性结果","适用于代理系统的评估方法"],"ja":["評価フレームワークを構築","エージェントシステムの性能を評価","動的意思決定をサポート","非決定性結果を処理","エージェントシステム用の評価方法"],"ko":["평가 프레임워크 구축","에이전트 시스템의 성능 평가","동적 의사결정 지원","비결정성 결과 처리","에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 방법"],"es":["Marco de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Métodos de evaluación para agentes","Decisiones dinámicas y no determinísticas","Falta de respuestas correctas únicas","Evaluación efectiva de sistemas de agentes"],"fr":["Cadre d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Méthodes d''évaluation pour les agents","Décisions dynamiques et non déterministes","Absence de réponses correctes uniques","Évaluation efficace des systèmes d''agents"],"de":["Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme","Bewertungsmethoden für Agenten","Dynamische und nicht-deterministische Entscheidungen","Fehlen eindeutiger korrekter Antworten","Effektive Bewertung von Agentsystemen"],"pt":["Construção de estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliação de decisões dinâmicas e não determinísticas","Abordagens personalizadas para avaliar sistemas de agentes","Integração com métodos de avaliação tradicionais","Suporte a múltiplos tipos de sistemas de agentes"],"ru":["Строительство оценочных рамок для систем агентов","Оценка динамических и неопределенных решений","Индивидуальные подходы к оценке систем агентов","Интеграция с традиционными методами оценки","Поддержка нескольких типов систем агентов"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة العوامل","تقييم القرارات الديناميكية وغير الحتمية","نهج شخصي لتقيم أنظمة العوامل","التكامل مع طرق التقييم التقليدية","دعم أنواع متعددة من أنظمة العوامل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Evaluation 技能","代理系统","评估框架","动态决策","非确定性结果","评估方法"],"ja":["エバリュエーションスキル","エージェントシステム","評価フレームワーク","動的意思決定","非決定性結果","評価方法"],"ko":["평가 스킬","에이전트 시스템","평가 프레임워크","동적 의사결정","비결정성 결과","평가 방법"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","marcos de evaluación","agentes","sistemas de agentes","evaluación de software","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["évaluation des systèmes d''agents","cadres d''évaluation","agents","systèmes d''agents","évaluation de logiciel","développement de logiciel"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","Bewertungsrahmen","Agenten","Agentsysteme","Software-Bewertung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","sistemas de agentes","decisões dinâmicas","não determinísticas","estruturas de avaliação","métodos de avaliação"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","системы агентов","динамические решения","неопределенные результаты","оценочные рамки","методы оценки"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة العوامل","أنظمة العوامل","قرارات ديناميكية","غير حتمية","إطارات تقييم","طرق تقييم"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"XXT-AGENT","repoPath":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:54:00.298Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等需要动态评估框架的 AI 代理","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの動的評価フレームワークを必要とする AI エージェントに適している","ko":"동적 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die dynamische Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem estruturas de avaliação dinâmica para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих динамических框架ов оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون إطارات تقييم ديناميكية لأنظمة الوكيل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and utilize evaluation frameworks that account for non-deterministic decisions and dynamic agent behaviors, incorporating approaches like probabilistic analysis and simulation-based evaluation methods","zh":"赋予代理构建和利用评估框架的能力，以考虑非确定性决策和动态代理行为，融合概率分析和基于模拟的评估方法","ja":"エージェントに、非決定性の決定と動的エージェントの動作を考慮した評価フレームワークを構築して利用する能力を付与し、確率分析やシミュレーションベースの評価方法などのアプローチを取り入れる","ko":"에이전트가 비결정적 결정과 동적 에이전트 동작을 고려한 평가 프레임워크를 구축하고 활용할 수 있도록 하며, 확률 분석 및 시뮬레이션 기반 평가 방법과 같은 접근 방식을 통합","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y utilizar marcos de evaluación que tengan en cuenta decisiones no deterministas y comportamientos dinámicos de los agentes, incorporando enfoques como el análisis probabilístico y los métodos de evaluación basados en simulación","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et d''utiliser des cadres d''évaluation qui tiennent compte de décisions non déterministes et de comportements dynamiques d''agents, en incorporant des approches telles que l''analyse probabiliste et les méthodes d''évaluation basées sur la simulation","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, Bewertungsframeworks zu erstellen und zu nutzen, die nicht-deterministische Entscheidungen und dynamische Agentenverhaltensweisen berücksichtigen, indem sie Ansätze wie probabilistische Analyse und simulationsbasierte Bewertungsmethoden einbeziehen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e utilizar estruturas de avaliação que consideram decisões não determinísticas e comportamentos de agentes dinâmicos, incorporando abordagens como análise probabilística e métodos de avaliação baseados em simulação","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и использовать框架ы оценки, которые учитывают неопределенные решения и динамическое поведение агентов, включая подходы, такие как вероятностный анализ и методы оценки на основе моделирования","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من بناء واستخدام إطارات تقييم تأخذ في الاعتبار القرارات غير المحددة وسلوكيات الوكيل الديناميكية، واستخدام نهج مثل التحليل الاحتمالي وأساليب التقييم القائمة على المحاكاة"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems with multiple correct answers","Assessing agent performance in dynamic environments with probabilistic outcomes","Developing simulation-based evaluation methods for non-deterministic agent behaviors"],"zh":["为具有多个正确答案的代理系统构建评估框架","评估动态环境中具有概率性结果的代理性能","为非确定性代理行为开发基于模拟的评估方法"],"ja":["複数の正解を持つエージェントシステムの評価フレームワークを構築する","確率的な結果を持つ動的環境におけるエージェントのパフォーマンスを評価する","非決定性的エージェントの動作に対するシミュレーションベースの評価方法を開発する"],"ko":["여러 개의 정답을 갖는 에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","시뮬레이션 기반 평가 방법을 통한 동적 환경에서 에이전트 성능 평가","비결정적 에이전트 동작을 위한 시뮬레이션 기반 평가 방법 개발"],"es":["Crear marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes con varias respuestas correctas","Evaluar el rendimiento de los agentes en entornos dinámicos con resultados probabilísticos","Desarrollar métodos de evaluación basados en simulación para comportamientos no deterministas de los agentes"],"fr":["Créer des cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents avec plusieurs réponses correctes","Évaluer les performances des agents dans des environnements dynamiques avec des résultats probabilistes","Développer des méthodes d''évaluation basées sur la simulation pour les comportements non déterministes des agents"],"de":["Erstellen von Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme mit mehreren richtigen Antworten","Bewerten der Leistung von Agents in dynamischen Umgebungen mit probabilistischen Ergebnissen","Entwickeln von simulationsbasierten Bewertungsmethoden für nicht-deterministische Agentenverhaltensweisen"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes com múltiplas respostas corretas","Avaliar o desempenho do agente em ambientes dinâmicos com resultados probabilísticos","Desenvolver métodos de avaliação baseados em simulação para comportamentos de agentes não determinísticos"],"ru":["Построение框架ов оценки для систем агентов с несколькими правильными ответами","Оценка производительности агента в динамических средах с вероятностными результатами","Разработка методов оценки на основе моделирования для неопределенного поведения агентов"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكيل مع إجابات صحيحة متعددة","تقييم أداء الوكيل في بيئات ديناميكية مع نتائج احتمالية","تطوير أساليب تقييم قائمة على المحاكاة لسلوكيات الوكيل غير المحددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent system characteristics like non-determinism and dynamic decision-making","May need additional computational resources for simulation-based evaluation methods"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统的特性，如非确定性和动态决策","可能需要额外的计算资源用于基于模拟的评估方法"],"ja":["非決定性や動的意思決定などのエージェントシステムの特性を理解する必要がある","シミュレーションベースの評価方法には追加の計算リソースが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["비결정성 및 동적 의사 결정을 포함한 에이전트 시스템의 특성을 이해해야 함","시뮬레이션 기반 평가 방법에는 추가적인 계산 리소스가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las características de los sistemas de agentes como la no determinismo y la toma de decisiones dinámica","Puede necesitar recursos computacionales adicionales para métodos de evaluación basados en simulación"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des caractéristiques des systèmes d''agents telles que la non-déterminisme et la prise de décision dynamique","Peut nécessiter des ressources computationnelles supplémentaires pour les méthodes d''évaluation basées sur la simulation"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Merkmale von Agentsystemen wie Nichtdeterminismus und dynamische Entscheidungsfindung","Kann zusätzliche Rechenressourcen für simulationsbasierte Bewertungsmethoden erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das características do sistema de agentes, como a não determinismo e a tomada de decisão dinâmica","Pode necessitar de recursos computacionais adicionais para métodos de avaliação baseados em simulação"],"ru":["Требует понимания характеристик системы агентов, таких как неопределенность и динамическое принятие решений","Может потребовать дополнительных вычислительных ресурсов для методов оценки на основе моделирования"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لخصائص نظام الوكيل، مثل عدم التحديد واتخاذ القرارات الديناميكية","قد يحتاج إلى موارد حاسوبية إضافية لأنواع التقييم القائمة على المحاكاة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
