von Änderungen in Echtzeit","Integration mit React","Verwendung von findAndObserve und query.observe()","Kompatibilität mit withObservables","Unterstützung für Bildschirme, die sich für Änderungen in der Datenbank anmelden"],"pt":["Modelos de dados reativos","Observação de mudanças nos dados","Atualização da interface do usuário em tempo real","Suporte a consultas reativas","Integração com React e outras bibliotecas"],"ru":["Модели реактивных данных","Наблюдение за изменениями в данных","Обновление пользовательского интерфейса в реальном времени","Поддержка реактивных запросов","Интеграция с React и другими библиотеками"],"ar":["نماذج البيانات التفاعلية","ملاحظة التغييرات في البيانات","تحديث واجهة المستخدم في الوقت الفعلي","دعم الاستعلامات التفاعلية","التكامل مع رياكت وبibliotecas الأخرى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["WatermelonDB","React","观察","Reactive查询","渲染优化","findAndObserve","query.observe()"],"ja":["WatermelonDB","React","観察","Reactiveクエリ","レンダリング最適化","findAndObserve","query.observe()"],"ko":["WatermelonDB","React","관찰","리액티브 쿼리","렌더링 최적화","findAndObserve","query.observe()"],"es":["WatermelonDB","modelos de datos","observación de cambios","React","findAndObserve","query.observe()","withObservables","bases de datos","desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["WatermelonDB","modèles de données","observation des changements","React","findAndObserve","query.observe()","withObservables","bases de données","développement d''applications"],"de":["WatermelonDB","Datenmodelle","Beobachtung von Änderungen","React","findAndObserve","query.observe()","withObservables","Datenbanken","Anwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["WatermelonDB","dados reativos","modelos de dados","observação de dados","React","gerenciamento de dados","bibliotecas de dados"],"ru":["WatermelonDB","реактивные данные","модели данных","наблюдение за данными","React","управление данными","библиотеки данных"],"ar":["واتر ميلون دي بي","بيانات تفاعلية","نماذج البيانات","ملاحظة البيانات","رياكت","إدارة البيانات","مكتبات البيانات"]}},"owner":"devAlgosAI","repo":"base-rn-app","repoPath":"devAlgosAI/base-rn-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"watermelondb","description":"WatermelonDB models, observation patterns, and React integration. Use when writing or debugging model code, observers (findAndObserve, query.observe), or screens that display live-updating DB data.","bodyPreview":"# WatermelonDB Model & Observation\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill covers WatermelonDB models (`database/models/`), observation\n(reactive queries), and **ensuring React re-renders when observed data\nchanges**. Use it when working with `findAndObserve`, `query.observe()`,\n`withObservables`, or any screen that subscribes to DB changes.\n\n---\n\n## Observation & React Re-rendering\n\n### `findAndObserve` and same-reference emission\n\n- **`findAndObserve(id)`** (on a collection): Fetches a record by ID, returns","body":"# WatermelonDB Model & Observation\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill covers WatermelonDB models (`database/models/`), observation\n(reactive queries), and **ensuring React re-renders when observed data\nchanges**. Use it when working with `findAndObserve`, `query.observe()`,\n`withObservables`, or any screen that subscribes to DB changes.\n\n---\n\n## Observation & React Re-rendering\n\n### `findAndObserve` and same-reference emission\n\n- **`findAndObserve(id)`** (on a collection): Fetches a record by ID, returns an\n  Observable that emits **immediately** on subscribe and **whenever the record\n  is updated or deleted**.\n- When a model is updated (e.g. via `model.update()` or `@writer` methods), the\n  observable **emits the same object reference** with updated properties — it\n  does **not** emit a new model instance.\n\n### React `useState` bailout\n\n- `useState` uses `Object.is` to decide whether to re-render. Passing the **same\n  reference** (e.g. `setPhrase(model)`) after an update means **no re-render**.\n- Result: DB updates (text, note, language, etc.) **don’t appear** until the\n  user navigates away and back, when a new subscription yields a fresh\n  reference.\n\n### Fix: store a wrapper so each emit is a new reference\n\nWhen subscribing to a **single model** (e.g. `findAndObserve`) and storing it in\nReact state, **don’t** store the raw model. Store a wrapper so every emission\nupdates state with a **new object**:\n\n```ts\nconst [phraseState, setPhraseState] = useState<\n  { phrase: Phrase; _key: number } | null\n>(null);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!id) return;\n  const sub = db.collections\n    .get<Phrase>(PHRASE_TABLE)\n    .findAndObserve(id)\n    .subscribe((result) => {\n      setPhraseState({ phrase: result, _key: result.updatedAt });\n    });\n  return () => sub.unsubscribe();\n}, [id, db]);\n\nconst phrase = phraseState?.phrase ?? null;\n```\n\n- Use `phrase` (derived) everywhere in the component. Updates persisted to the\n  DB will re-emit, update `phraseState` with a new wrapper, and trigger a\n  re-render.\n\n### Query `observe()` and arrays\n\n- **`query.observe()`** emits **arrays** of models. When the query result set\n  changes, WatermelonDB typically emits a **new array** reference, so\n  `setState(results)` usually triggers re-renders.\n- If you **build derived data** (e.g. `linked.filter(...)`, `assignments`) in\n  the subscribe callback and `setState` that, you’re already passing new\n  references — no extra wrapper needed.\n\n---\n\n## `withObservables` (HOC)\n\n- **`withObservables(triggerProps, getObservables)`** injects observable values\n  as props and **always** passes a **new state object** into `setState` (e.g.\n  `{ values, isFetching }`), so React re-renders on each emission even when\n  model references are unchanged.\n- Use it when you can **observe a model (or query) passed as a prop**: e.g.\n  `withObservables([''attempt''], ({ attempt }) => ({ attempt: attempt.observe(), ... }))`.\n  See `AttemptCard` in `features/lesson/components/AttemptCard.tsx`.\n- For **route params** (e.g. `id`) you typically **subscribe manually** in\n  `useEffect` (e.g. `findAndObserve(id)`). In that case, use the **wrapper\n  pattern** above instead of storing the raw model.\n\n---\n\n## Model patterns in this project\n\n- **Models**: `database/models/` (e.g. `Phrase`, `Lesson`, `Attempt`,\n  `Translation`, `Deck`). Use `@field`, `@writer`, and static helpers (e.g.\n  `Phrase.findOrCreatePhrase`, `Lesson.addLesson`).\n- **Observation**: `useDatabase()` from `@nozbe/watermelondb/react`; then\n  `collection.findAndObserve(id)` or `query.observe().subscribe(...)`.\n- **Schema/tables**: `database/schema.ts`; collection access via\n  `db.collections.get<Model>(TABLE)`.\n\n---\n\n## Quick reference\n\n| Scenario                                  | Pattern                                                                   | Re-render guarantee            |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Single model by `id` (e.g. detail screen) | `findAndObserve` + **wrapper state** `{ model, _key }`                    | Yes                            |\n| Query results (list)                      | `query.observe()` + `setState(results)` or derived structures             | Yes (new array/refs)           |\n| Model passed as prop                      | `withObservables([''model''], ({ model }) => ({ model: model.observe() }))` | Yes (HOC uses new state shape) |\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n\n- **DeepWiki**: [Nozbe/WatermelonDB](https://github.com/Nozbe/WatermelonDB) —\n  `findAndObserve`, `observe()`, `withObservables`, model updates.\n- **Project**: `PhraseDetailScreen`, `LessonDetailScreen`, `SetDetailScreen`\n  (findAndObserve + wrapper); `AttemptCard` (withObservables).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:55:12.697Z","qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('arsac/qb-sync/grpc-protobuf', 'community', 'arsac', 'qb-sync', 'arsac/qb-sync', 'grpc-protobuf', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z', '2026-02-18T07:55:14.865Z', NULL, '{"id":"arsac/qb-sync/grpc-protobuf","name":"grpc-protobuf","description":{"zh":"gRPC 和 Protocol Buffers 是一种高性能的 RPC 框架，用于构建可扩展的服务。proto 文件结构是其核心组成部分","ja":"gRPC と Protocol Buffers は、高性能の RPC フレームワークであり、拡張可能なサービスを構築するために使用されます。proto ファイル構造はその核心部分です","ko":"gRPC 및 프로토콜 버퍼는 확장 가능한 서비스를 구축하기 위한 고성능 RPC 프레임워크입니다. 프로토 파일 구조는 핵심 구성 요소입니다","es":"gRPC y Protocol Buffers son tecnologías clave para desarrollar servicios de alta disponibilidad. Aprende a estructurar tus archivos de proto y definir servicios.","fr":"gRPC et Protocol Buffers sont des technologies clés pour développer des services haute disponibilité. Apprenez à structurer vos fichiers de proto et à définir des services.","de":"gRPC und Protocol Buffers sind wichtige Technologien für die Entwicklung von Hochverfügbarkeitsdiensten. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Ihre Proto-Dateien strukturieren und Dienste definieren.","pt":"O gRPC é um framework de comunicação de alto desempenho e o Protocol Buffers é um mecanismo de serialização eficiente. Juntos, eles permitem a criação de serviços RPC escaláveis e eficientes.","ru":"gRPC - это фреймворк высокой производительности, а Protocol Buffers - это эффективный механизм сериализации. Вместе они позволяют создавать масштабируемые и эффективные сервисы RPC.","ar":"gRPC هو إطار اتصال ذو أداء عالي و بروتوكول بفرز هو آلية تسلسل فعالة. معا ، يسمحان بإنشاء خدمات RPC قابلة للتوسيع والفعالة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"gRPC 和 Protocol Buffers 模式","ja":"gRPC と Protocol Buffers パターン","ko":"gRPC 및 프로토콜 버퍼 패턴","es":"Patrones de gRPC y Protocol Buffers","fr":"Modèles gRPC et Protocol Buffers","de":"gRPC- und Protocol-Buffern-Muster","pt":"gRPC e Protocol Buffers: Pa