을 생성하고 권위를 구축하며 리드를 생성하는 콘텐츠를 계획하고 생성하는 것을 말합니다","es":"La estrategia de contenido es fundamental para atraer tráfico y generar leads. Aprende a planificar contenido efectivo","fr":"La stratégie de contenu est essentielle pour attirer du trafic et générer des leads. Apprenez à planifier du contenu efficace","de":"Die Content-Strategie ist entscheidend, um Verkehr anzuziehen und Leads zu generieren. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie effektive Inhalte planen","pt":"A estratégia de conteúdo é fundamental para aumentar o tráfego e gerar leads. Ela envolve planejar conteúdo de qualidade que seja searchable e shareable.","ru":"Стратегия контента является основой для увеличения трафика и генерации лидов. Она предполагает планирование качественного контента, который может быть найден...","ar":"استراتيجية المحتوى هي الأساس لزيادة حركة المرور وتوليد Leads. وهي تشمل تخطيط المحتوى الجيد الذي يمكن البحث عنه ومشاركته.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提高网站流量","建立品牌权威","生成高质量leads","提高搜索引擎排名","创建可共享的内容","提高用户参与度"],"ja":["Webサイトのトラフィックを増やす","ブランドの権威を築く","高品質のリードを生成する","検索エンジンのランキングを向上させる","共有可能なコンテンツを作成する","ユーザーの関与を高める"],"ko":["웹사이트 트래픽 증가","브랜드 권위 구축","고품질 리드 생성","검색 엔진 순위 향상","공유 가능한 콘텐츠 생성","사용자 참여도 향상"],"es":["Planificación de contenido personalizado","Análisis de keywords y tendencias","Creación de contenido searchable y shareable","Optimización para motores de búsqueda","Medición y análisis de resultados"],"fr":["Planification de contenu personnalisée","Analyse de mots-clés et de tendances","Création de contenu searchable et shareable","Optimisation pour les moteurs de recherche","Mesure et analyse des résultats"],"de":["Individualisierte Inhaltsplanung","Analyse von Keywords und Trends","Erstellung von searchable und shareable Inhalten","Optimierung für Suchmaschinen","Messung und Analyse der Ergebnisse"],"pt":["Planejamento de conteúdo personalizado","Otimização para motores de busca","Criação de conteúdo shareable","Análise de desempenho de conteúdo","Ajustes e melhorias contínuas"],"ru":["Планирование индивидуального контента","Оптимизация для поисковых систем","Создание контента для обмена","Анализ производительности контента","Постоянные корректировки и улучшения"],"ar":["تخطيط المحتوى المخصص","تحسين المحتوى لenginات البحث","إنشاء المحتوى القابل للمشاركة","تحليل أداء المحتوى","التعديلات والتحسينات المستمرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["内容策略","驱动流量","生成leads","搜索引擎优化","内容营销","数字营销","在线营销","网站优化"],"ja":["コンテンツ戦略","トラフィックを生み出す","リードを生成する","検索エンジン最適化","コンテンツマーケティング","デジタルマーケティング","オンラインマーケティング","Webサイト最適化"],"ko":["콘텐츠 전략","트래픽 생성","리드 생성","검색 엔진 최적화","콘텐츠 마케팅","디지털 마케팅","온라인 마케팅","웹사이트 최적화"],"es":["estrategia de contenido","planificación de contenido","contenido searchable","contenido shareable","optimización para motores de búsqueda","análisis de keywords","creación de contenido"],"fr":["stratégie de contenu","planification de contenu","contenu searchable","contenu shareable","optimisation pour les moteurs de recherche","analyse de mots-clés","création de contenu"],"de":["Content-Strategie","Inhaltsplanung","searchable Inhalte","shareable Inhalte","Optimierung für Suchmaschinen","Keyword-Analyse","Inhalterstellung"],"pt":["estratégia de conteúdo","desenvolvedores","conteúdo de qualidade","otimização para motores de busca","criação de conteúdo","análise de desempenho"],"ru":["стратегия контента","разработчики","качественный контент","оптимизация для поисковых систем","создание контента","анализ производительности"],"ar":["استراتيجية المحتوى","مطورون","محتوى جيد","تحسين المحتوى لenginات البحث","إنشاء المحتوى","تحليل الأداء"]}},"owner":"eurofit","repo":"store","repoPath":"eurofit/store","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"content-strategy","description":"When the user wants to plan a content strategy, decide what content to create, or figure out what topics to cover. Also use when the user mentions content strategy, what should I write about, content ideas, blog strategy, topic clusters, or content planning. For writing individual pieces, see copywriting. For SEO-specific audits, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Content Strategy\n\nYou are a content strategist. Your goal is to help plan content that drives traffic, builds authority, and generates leads by being either searchable, shareable, or both.\n\n## Before Planning\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Business Conte","body":"# Content Strategy\n\nYou are a content strategist. Your goal is to help plan content that drives traffic, builds authority, and generates leads by being either searchable, shareable, or both.\n\n## Before Planning\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Business Context\n\n- What does the company do?\n- Who is the ideal customer?\n- What''s the primary goal for content? (traffic, leads, brand awareness, thought leadership)\n- What problems does your product solve?\n\n### 2. Customer Research\n\n- What questions do customers ask before buying?\n- What objections come up in sales calls?\n- What topics appear repeatedly in support tickets?\n- What language do customers use to describe their problems?\n\n### 3. Current State\n\n- Do you have existing content? What''s working?\n- What resources do you have? (writers, budget, time)\n- What content formats can you produce? (written, video, audio)\n\n### 4. Competitive Landscape\n\n- Who are your main competitors?\n- What content gaps exist in your market?\n\n---\n\n## Searchable vs Shareable\n\nEvery piece of content must be searchable, shareable, or both. Prioritize in that order—search traffic is the foundation.\n\n**Searchable content** captures existing demand. Optimized for people actively looking for answers.\n\n**Shareable content** creates demand. Spreads ideas and gets people talking.\n\n### When Writing Searchable Content\n\n- Target a specific keyword or question\n- Match search intent exactly—answer what the searcher wants\n- Use clear titles that match search queries\n- Structure with headings that mirror search patterns\n- Place keywords in title, headings, first paragraph, URL\n- Provide comprehensive coverage (don''t leave questions unanswered)\n- Include data, examples, and links to authoritative sources\n- Optimize for AI/LLM discovery: clear positioning, structured content, brand consistency across the web\n\n### When Writing Shareable Content\n\n- Lead with a novel insight, original data, or counterintuitive take\n- Challenge conventional wisdom with well-reasoned arguments\n- Tell stories that make people feel something\n- Create content people want to share to look smart or help others\n- Connect to current trends or emerging problems\n- Share vulnerable, honest experiences others can learn from\n\n---\n\n## Content Types\n\n### Searchable Content Types\n\n**Use-Case Content**\nFormula: [persona] + [use-case]. Targets long-tail keywords.\n\n- \"Project management for designers\"\n- \"Task tracking for developers\"\n- \"Client collaboration for freelancers\"\n\n**Hub and Spoke**\nHub = comprehensive overview. Spokes = related subtopics.\n\n```\n/topic (hub)\n├── /topic/subtopic-1 (spoke)\n├── /topic/subtopic-2 (spoke)\n└── /topic/subtopic-3 (spoke)\n```\n\nCreate hub first, then build spokes. Interlink strategically.\n\n**Note:** Most content works fine under `/blog`. Only use dedicated hub/spoke URL structures for major topics with layered depth (e.g., Atlassian''s `/agile` guide). For typical blog posts, `/blog/post-title` is sufficient.\n\n**Template Libraries**\nHigh-intent keywords + product adoption.\n\n- Target searches like \"marketing plan template\"\n- Provide immediate standalone value\n- Show how product enhances the template\n\n### Shareable Content Types\n\n**Thought Leadership**\n\n- Articulate concepts everyone feels but hasn''t named\n- Challenge conventional wisdom with evidence\n- Share vulnerable, honest experiences\n\n**Data-Driven Content**\n\n- Product data analysis (anonymized insights)\n- Public data analysis (uncover patterns)\n- Original research (run experiments, share results)\n\n**Expert Roundups**\n15-30 experts answering one specific question. Built-in distribution.\n\n**Case Studies**\nStructure: Challenge → Solution → Results → Key learnings\n\n**Meta Content**\nBehind-the-scenes transparency. \"How We Got Our First $5k MRR,\" \"Why We Chose Debt Over VC.\"\n\nFor programmatic content at scale, see **programmatic-seo** skill.\n\n---\n\n## Content Pillars and Topic Clusters\n\nContent pillars are the 3-5 core topics your brand will own. Each pillar spawns a cluster of related content.\n\nMost of the time, all content can live under `/blog` with good internal linking between related posts. Dedicated pillar pages with custom URL structures (like `/guides/topic`) are only needed when you''re building comprehensive resources with multiple layers of depth.\n\n### How to Identify Pillars\n\n1. **Product-led**: What problems does your product solve?\n2. **Audience-led**: What does your ICP need to learn?\n3. **Search-led**: What topics have volume in your space?\n4. **Competitor-led**: What are competitors ranking for?\n\n### Pillar Structure\n\n```\nPillar Topic (Hub)\n├── Subtopic Cluster 1\n│   ├── Article A\n│   ├── Article B\n│   └── Article C\n├── Subtopic Cluster 2\n│   ├── Article D\n│   ├── Article E\n│   └── Article F\n└── Subtopic Cluster 3\n    ├── Article G\n    ├── Article H\n    └── Article I\n```\n\n### Pillar Criteria\n\nGood pillars should:\n\n- Align with your product/service\n- Match what your audience cares about\n- Have search volume and/or social interest\n- Be broad enough for many subtopics\n\n---\n\n## Keyword Research by Buyer Stage\n\nMap topics to the buyer''s journey using proven keyword modifiers:\n\n### Awareness Stage\n\nModifiers: \"what is,\" \"how to,\" \"guide to,\" \"introduction to\"\n\nExample: If customers ask about project management basics:\n\n- \"What is Agile Project Management\"\n- \"Guide to Sprint Planning\"\n- \"How to Run a Standup Meeting\"\n\n### Consideration Stage\n\nModifiers: \"best,\" \"top,\" \"vs,\" \"alternatives,\" \"comparison\"\n\nExample: If customers evaluate multiple tools:\n\n- \"Best Project Management Tools for Remote Teams\"\n- \"Asana vs Trello vs Monday\"\n- \"Basecamp Alternatives\"\n\n### Decision Stage\n\nModifiers: \"pricing,\" \"reviews,\" \"demo,\" \"trial,\" \"buy\"\n\nExample: If pricing comes up in sales calls:\n\n- \"Project Management Tool Pricing Comparison\"\n- \"How to Choose the Right Plan\"\n- \"[Product] Reviews\"\n\n### Implementation Stage\n\nModifiers: \"templates,\" \"examples,\" \"tutorial,\" \"how to use,\" \"setup\"\n\nExample: If support tickets show implementation struggles:\n\n- \"Project Template Library\"\n- \"Step-by-Step Setup Tutorial\"\n- \"How to Use [Feature]\"\n\n---\n\n## Content Ideation Sources\n\n### 1. Keyword Data\n\nIf user provides keyword exports (Ahrefs, SEMrush, GSC), analyze for:\n\n- Topic clusters (group related keywords)\n- Buyer stage (awareness/consideration/decision/implementation)\n- Search intent (informational, commercial, transactional)\n- Quick wins (low competition + decent volume + high relevance)\n- Content gaps (keywords competitors rank for that you don''t)\n\nOutput as prioritized table:\n| Keyword | Volume | Difficulty | Buyer Stage | Content Type | Priority |\n\n### 2. Call Transcripts\n\nIf user provides sales or customer call transcripts, extract:\n\n- Questions asked → FAQ content or blog posts\n- Pain points → problems in their own words\n- Objections → content to address proactively\n- Language patterns → exact phrases to use (voice of customer)\n- Competitor mentions → what they compared you to\n\nOutput content ideas with supporting quotes.\n\n### 3. Survey Responses\n\nIf user provides survey data, mine for:\n\n- Open-ended responses (topics and language)\n- Common themes (30%+ mention = high priority)\n- Resource requests (what they wish existed)\n- Content preferences (formats they want)\n\n### 4. Forum Research\n\nUse web search to find content ideas:\n\n**Reddit:** `site:reddit.com [topic]`\n\n- Top posts in relevant subreddits\n- Questions and frustrations in comments\n- Upvoted answers (validates what resonates)\n\n**Quora:** `site:quora.com [topic]`\n\n- Most-followed questions\n- Highly upvoted answers\n\n**Other:** Indie Hackers, Hacker News, Product Hunt, industry Slack/Discord\n\nExtract: FAQs, misconceptions, debates, problems being solved, terminology used.\n\n### 5. Competitor Analysis\n\nUse web search to analyze competitor content:\n\n**Find their content:** `site:competitor.com/blog`\n\n**Analyze:**\n\n- Top-performing posts (comments, shares)\n- Topics covered repeatedly\n- Gaps they haven''t covered\n- Case studies (customer problems, use cases, results)\n- Content structure (pillars, categories, formats)\n\n**Identify opportunities:**\n\n- Topics you can cover better\n- Angles they''re missing\n- Outdated content to improve on\n\n### 6. Sales and Support Input\n\nExtract from customer-facing teams:\n\n- Common objections\n- Repeated questions\n- Support ticket patterns\n- Success stories\n- Feature requests and underlying problems\n\n---\n\n## Prioritizing Content Ideas\n\nScore each idea on four factors:\n\n### 1. Customer Impact (40%)\n\n- How frequently did this topic come up in research?\n- What percentage of customers face this challenge?\n- How emotionally charged was this pain point?\n- What''s the potential LTV of customers with this need?\n\n### 2. Content-Market Fit (30%)\n\n- Does this align with problems your product solves?\n- Can you offer unique insights from customer research?\n- Do you have customer stories to support this?\n- Will this naturally lead to product interest?\n\n### 3. Search Potential (20%)\n\n- What''s the monthly search volume?\n- How competitive is this topic?\n- Are there related long-tail opportunities?\n- Is search interest growing or declining?\n\n### 4. Resource Requirements (10%)\n\n- Do you have expertise to create authoritative content?\n- What additional research is needed?\n- What assets (graphics, data, examples) will you need?\n\n### Scoring Template\n\n| Idea    | Customer Impact (40%) | Content-Market Fit (30%) | Search Potential (20%) | Resources (10%) | Total |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------- | --------------- | ----- |\n| Topic A | 8                     | 9                        | 7                      | 6               | 8.0   |\n| Topic B | 6                     | 7                        | 9                      | 8               | 7.1   |\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\nWhen creating a content strategy, provide:\n\n### 1. Content Pillars\n\n- 3-5 pillars with rationale\n- Subtopic clusters for each pillar\n- How pillars connect to product\n\n### 2. Priority Topics\n\nFor each recommended piece:\n\n- Topic/title\n- Searchable, shareable, or both\n- Content type (use-case, hub/spoke, thought leadership, etc.)\n- Target keyword and buyer stage\n- Why this topic (customer research backing)\n\n### 3. Topic Cluster Map\n\nVisual or structured representation of how content interconnects.\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What patterns emerge from your last 10 customer conversations?\n2. What questions keep coming up in sales calls?\n3. Where are competitors'' content efforts falling short?\n4. What unique insights from customer research aren''t being shared elsewhere?\n5. Which existing content drives the most conversions, and why?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **copywriting**: For writing individual content pieces\n- **seo-audit**: For technical SEO and on-page optimization\n- **programmatic-seo**: For scaled content generation\n- **email-sequence**: For email-based content\n- **social-content**: For social media content\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:56:26.093Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing advanced content planning and optimization capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级内容规划和优化能力的语言代理。","ja":"高度なコンテンツ計画と最適化機能が必要な言語エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 콘텐츠 계획 및 최적화 기능이 필요한 언어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de planificación y optimización de contenido.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langue ayant besoin de capacités avancées de planification et d''optimisation de contenu.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die erweiterte Inhaltsplanungs- und Optimierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de planejamento e otimização de conteúdo.","ru":"Идеально для языковых агентов, которым требуются продвинутые возможности планирования и оптимизации контента.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين الذين يحتاجون إلى قابليات متقدمة للتخطيط والتحسين للمحتوى."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to drive traffic, build authority, and generate leads by creating searchable and shareable content, leveraging product marketing context and utilizing markdown files like `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`.","zh":"赋予代理创建可搜索和可分享的内容的能力，驱动流量、建立权威和生成潜在客户，利用产品营销背景和markdown文件，如 `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`。","ja":"エージェントに検索可能で共有可能なコンテンツを作成する能力を与え、トラフィックを駆動し、権威を築き、リードを生成する。製品マーケティングのコンテキストとマークダウンファイル（`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`）を利用する。","ko":"에이전트가 검색 가능하고 공유 가능한 콘텐츠를 생성하여 트래픽을駆動하고 권위를 구축하며 리드를 생성하도록 합니다. 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트와 마크다운 파일(`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`)을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a impulsar tráfico, generar autoridad y producir leads creando contenido buscable y compartible, aprovechando el contexto de marketing de productos y utilizando archivos markdown como `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer du trafic, de créer une autorité et de produire des leads en créant un contenu recherchable et partageable, en exploitant le contexte de marketing de produits et en utilisant des fichiers markdown comme `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Verkehr zu erzeugen, Autorität aufzubauen und Leads zu generieren, indem sie durchsuchbaren und teilbaren Inhalt erstellen, den Produktmarketing-Kontext nutzen und Markdown-Dateien wie `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impulsionar o tráfego, construir autoridade e gerar leads criando conteúdo pesquisável e compartilhável, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos e utilizando arquivos markdown como `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью привлекать трафик, строить авторитет и генерировать лиды, создавая поисковый и деловой контент, используя контекст продуктивного маркетинга и файлы markdown, такие как `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من دفع Movement، بناء السلطة وتوليد Leads من خلال إنشاء محتوى يمكن البحث عنه ومشاركته، واستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج واستخدام ملفات markdown مثل `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`."},"useCases":{"en":["Planning SEO-optimized blog posts","Generating shareable social media content","Developing lead-generating email campaigns"],"zh":["规划SEO优化的博客文章","生成可分享的社交媒体内容","开发潜在客户生成的电子邮件活动"],"ja":["SEO最適化されたブログ投稿の計画","共有可能なソーシャルメディアコンテンツの生成","リード生成のためのメールキャンペーンの開発"],"ko":["SEO 최적화된 블로그 게시물 계획","공유 가능한 소셜 미디어 콘텐츠 생성","리드 생성을 위한 이메일 캠페인 개발"],"es":["Planificación de publicaciones de blog optimizadas para SEO","Generación de contenido de redes sociales compartible","Desarrollo de campañas de correo electrónico generadoras de leads"],"fr":["Planification de billets de blog optimisés pour le SEO","Génération de contenu de réseaux sociaux partageable","Développement de campagnes de courriel génératrices de leads"],"de":["Planung von SEO-optimierten Blog-Beiträgen","Generierung von teilbarem sozialem Medieninhalt","Entwicklung von leadgenerierenden E-Mail-Kampagnen"],"pt":["Planejamento de posts de blog otimizados para SEO","Geração de conteúdo compartilhável em mídias sociais","Desenvolvimento de campanhas de e-mail que geram leads"],"ru":["Планирование постов в блоге, оптимизированных для SEO","Генерация контента, который можно делиться в социальных сетях","Разработка электронных кампаний, генерирующих лиды"],"ar":["تخطيط منشورات مدونة محسّنة لتحسين محركات البحث","توليد محتوى يمكن مشاركته على وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية","تطوير حملات بريد إلكتروني توليد Leads"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires product marketing context file (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) for optimal performance","Limited to text-based content generation"],"zh":["需要产品营销背景文件（.cursor/product-marketing-context.md）以实现最佳性能","仅限于基于文本的内容生成"],"ja":["製品マーケティングのコンテキストファイル（`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`）が必要なため、最適なパフォーマンスを実現","テキストベースのコンテンツ生成のみ"],"ko":["제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 파일(`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`)이 필요하여 최적의 성능을 구현","텍스트 기반 콘텐츠 생성만"],"es":["Requiere un archivo de contexto de marketing de productos (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) para un rendimiento óptimo","Limitado a la generación de contenido basado en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite un fichier de contexte de marketing de produits (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) pour des performances optimales","Limité à la génération de contenu basé sur du texte"],"de":["Benötigt eine Produktmarketing-Kontext-Datei (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) für optimale Leistung","Begrenzt auf die Generierung von textbasiertem Inhalt"],"pt":["Requer arquivo de contexto de marketing de produtos (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) para desempenho ótimo","Limitado à geração de conteúdo baseado em texto"],"ru":["Требует файла контекста продуктивного маркетинга (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) для оптимальной производительности","Ограничен генерацией контента на основе текста"],"ar":["يتطلب ملف سياق تسويق المنتج (.cursor/product-marketing-context.md) لأداء مثالي","محدود بالمحتوى القائم على النص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fredeschmidt/tv2reg-designsystem/read-screenshot', 'community', 'fredeschmidt', 'tv2reg-designsystem', 'fredeschmidt/tv2reg-designsystem', 'read-screenshot', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z', '2026-02-18T07:56:27.373Z', NULL, '{"id":"fredeschmidt/tv2reg-designsystem/read-screenshot","name":"read-screenshot","description":{"es":"El skill read-screenshot permite reconstruir componentes con paridad visual estricta en móviles y escritorios a partir de capturas de pantalla","fr":"Le skill read-screenshot permet de reconstruire des composants avec une parité visuelle stricte sur mobile et bureau à partir de captures d''écran","de":"Der Skill read-screenshot ermöglicht die Rekonstruktion von Komponenten mit strenger visueller Parität auf Mobil- und Desktop-Geräten anhand von Screenshots","pt":"A habilidade de leitura de tela permite recriar componentes com paridade visual estrita em dispositivos móveis e de desktop.","ru":"Навык чтения скриншота позволяет восстановить компоненты с строгой визуальной паритетом на мобильных и настольных устройствах.","ar":"تسمح مهارة قراءة لقطة الشاشة بإعادة بناء المكونات مع تماثل بصري صارم على الأجهزة المحمولة وأجهزة سطح المكتب.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Lector de capturas de pantalla","fr":"Lecteur de captures d''écran","de":"Screenshot-Leser","pt":"Leitura de Tela: Recrie Componentes com Paridade Visual","ru":"Чтение Скриншота: Восстановите Компоненты с Визуальной Па...","ar":"قراءة لقطة الشاشة: أعد بناء المكونات مع التماثل البصري","en":"read-screenshot"},"description":{"es":"El skill read-screenshot permite reconstruir componentes con paridad visual estricta en móviles y escritorios a partir de capturas de pantalla","fr":"Le skill read-screenshot permet de reconstruire des composants avec une parité visuelle stricte sur mobile et bureau à partir de captures d''écran","de":"Der Skill read-screenshot ermöglicht die Rekonstruktion von Komponenten mit strenger visueller Parität auf Mobil- und Desktop-Geräten anhand von Screenshots","pt":"A habilidade de leitura de tela permite recriar componentes com paridade visual estrita em dispositivos móveis e de desktop.","ru":"Навык чтения скриншота позволяет восстановить компоненты с строгой визуальной паритетом на мобильных и настольных устройствах.","ar":"تسمح مهارة قراءة لقطة الشاشة بإعادة بناء المكونات مع تماثل بصري صارم على الأجهزة المحمولة وأجهزة سطح المكتب.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Reconstrucción de componentes con paridad visual estricta","Compatibilidad con móviles y escritorios","Uso de capturas de pantalla como fuente de diseño","Ejecución de pasos de flujo de trabajo en orden estricto","Capacidad para solicitar y esperar aclaraciones"],"fr":["Reconstruction de composants avec une parité visuelle stricte","Compatibilité avec les mobiles et les bureaux","Utilisation de captures d''écran comme source de conception","Exécution des étapes de flux de travail dans l''ordre strict","Capacité à demander et attendre des clarifications"],"de":["Rekonstruktion von Komponenten mit strenger visueller Parität","Kompatibilität mit Mobil- und Desktop-Geräten","Verwendung von Screenshots als Design-Quelle","Ausführung von Workflow-Schritten in strenger Reihenfolge","Fähigkeit, Anfragen zu stellen und auf Klärungen zu warten"],"pt":["Recriação de componentes com paridade visual estrita","Compatibilidade com dispositivos móveis e de desktop","Execução de fluxo de trabalho em ordem exata","Leitura de arquivos antes da execução"],"ru":["Восстановление компонентов с строгой визуальной паритетом","Совместимость с мобильными и настольными устройствами","Выполнение рабочего процесса в точном порядке","Чтение файлов перед выполнением"],"ar":["إعادة بناء المكونات مع تماثل بصري صارم","التأثير مع الأجهزة المحمولة وأجهزة سطح المكتب","تنفيذ سير العمل بالترتيب الصحيح","قراءة الملفات قبل التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"es":["reconstrucción de componentes","paridad visual","capturas de pantalla","diseño de interfaces","desarrollo de software","compatibilidad móvil y escritorio"],"fr":["reconstruction de composants","parité visuelle","captures d''écran","conception d''interfaces","développement de logiciels","compatibilité mobile et bureau"],"de":["Rekonstruktion von Komponenten","visuelle Parität","Screenshots","Benutzeroberflächendesign","Software-Entwicklung","Kompatibilität mit Mobil- und Desktop-Geräten"],"pt":["leitura de tela","recriação de componentes","paridade visual","dispositivos móveis","desktop","fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["чтение скриншота","восстановление компонентов","визуальная паритет","мобильные устройства","настольные устройства","рабочий процесс"],"ar":["قراءة لقطة الشاشة","إعادة بناء المكونات","تماثل بصري","أجهزة محمولة","أجهزة سطح المكتب","سير العمل"]}},"owner":"fredeschmidt","repo":"tv2reg-designsystem","repoPath":"fredeschmidt/tv2reg-designsystem","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"read-screenshot","description":"Extract complete visual details from screenshots and reconstruct the component with semantic HTML and scoped CSS.","bodyPreview":"# Read Screenshot\n\nUse this skill when screenshots are the design source of truth.\nGoal: reconstruct the component with strict mobile + desktop visual parity.\n\n## Mandatory Execution Rules\n\n- Read this file before acting.\n- Execute all workflow steps in exact order.\n- Execute all sub-bullets under each step.\n- Do not skip, combine, or reorder steps.\n- If blocked or input is missing, ask and wait.\n- When done, return to `build-component-screenshots`.\n\n## Trigger\n\nRun this skill when `build-compon","body":"# Read Screenshot\n\nUse this skill when screenshots are the design source of truth.\nGoal: reconstruct the component with strict mobile + desktop visual parity.\n\n## Mandatory Execution Rules\n\n- Read this file before acting.\n- Execute all workflow steps in exact order.\n- Execute all sub-bullets under each step.\n- Do not skip, combine, or reorder steps.\n- If blocked or input is missing, ask and wait.\n- When done, return to `build-component-screenshots`.\n\n## Trigger\n\nRun this skill when `build-component-screenshots` handles a screenshot-driven component request.\n\n## Required Inputs\n\nCollect before implementation:\n\n1. Two screenshots:\n   - one mobile,\n   - one desktop.\n2. Screenshot dimensions and viewport intent:\n   - provide intrinsic image size for each screenshot (`width x height` in px),\n   - provide viewport width used when the screenshot was captured when known.\n3. Placement target:\n   - `article.html` inside `<article>` wrapped in `<div class=\"article-component\">`, or\n   - `index.html` inside `<main>` wrapped in `<div class=\"frontpage-component\">`.\n4. Source theme (required):\n   - `tv2Oj`, `tv2Nord`, `tv2Syd`, `tv2Fyn`, `tv2East`, or `kosmopol`.\n5. Viewport assumptions (default, unless user says otherwise):\n   - first screenshot is mobile viewport at `390px` width,\n   - second screenshot is desktop viewport at `1728px` width.\n\nIf any required input is missing, ask before implementation.\n\n## Viewport Calibration Rules (Non-Negotiable)\n\n1. Assume screenshot order by default:\n   - screenshot 1 = mobile (`390px` wide),\n   - screenshot 2 = desktop (`1728px` wide).\n2. Start from intrinsic screenshot dimensions:\n   - read the real image width/height in pixels before deriving CSS values,\n   - never infer dimensions only by visual guess.\n3. Calibrate CSS sizing with screenshot-to-viewport ratio:\n   - map measured screenshot geometry to CSS pixels using the known or assumed viewport width,\n   - derive widths, spacing, and typography from this ratio for each breakpoint separately.\n4. Validate calibration across both screenshots before finalizing CSS values.\n5. Only deviate from these viewport defaults when the user explicitly provides different viewport sizes.\n\n## Extraction Rules (Non-Negotiable)\n\n1. Capture all visible details from both screenshots:\n   - layout, spacing, alignment, sizing, typography, colors, borders, radii, shadows, overlays, icons, and responsive behavior.\n2. Scan screenshots for visible text content before implementation:\n   - extract all readable copy (headlines, body, labels, quotes, captions, metadata, CTA text),\n   - preserve original wording and punctuation when legible,\n   - if text is partially unreadable, mark uncertain fragments explicitly as assumptions.\n3. Convert extracted text into semantic HTML based on editorial meaning:\n   - use tags that match intent (`h*`, `p`, `blockquote`, `figcaption`, `time`, `a`, `button`, etc.),\n   - avoid generic wrappers (`div`, `span`) when a semantic element fits,\n   - document ambiguous cases and why a semantic choice was made.\n4. No guesswork without disclosure:\n   - if a value is uncertain, state the assumption and mark as potential delta.\n5. Preserve semantic HTML.\n6. Keep CSS fully scoped to the component.\n7. Use existing tokens first.\n8. Token mapping is required for screenshot builds:\n   - colors: tokenized by default,\n   - typography: tokenized family, size, weight, line-height by default via `--base-type-*`, `--base-leading-*`, and `--base-weight-*`,\n   - apply typography/color tokens that match the chosen semantic role (for example quote text -> quote tokens, metadata -> meta tokens),\n   - typography must prefer semantic base token usage over legacy `--font-*`/`--md-*`/`--news-*` aliases in component CSS,\n   - when semantic base typography tokens are applied, do not override `font-size`, `font-weight`, or `line-height` unless absolutely required and documented as a delta,\n   - hardcoded fallback only when token coverage is missing, and document each exception.\n9. Text-size token matching is required:\n   - estimate visible text size from calibrated screenshot measurements (not by intuition),\n   - choose the nearest semantic typography token by size and role,\n   - keep token and measured size aligned within a small visual tolerance (target `<= 1px` delta at each breakpoint),\n   - if no token is a close match, use the closest semantic token and document the residual mismatch as a delta.\n\n## Workflow (Execute In Order)\n\n1. Inspect both screenshots and list observable primitives:\n   - frame/grid, blocks, spacing rhythm, type scale, color palette, effects, edge treatments.\n2. Run dimension calibration pass:\n   - record intrinsic dimensions for each screenshot,\n   - compute mobile and desktop scaling baselines from viewport assumptions or user-provided viewport widths.\n3. Run a text extraction pass:\n   - list all detected text strings by region/role,\n   - classify each string by semantic intent (headline, paragraph, quote, caption, metadata, control label, etc.).\n4. Derive DOM plan:\n   - map visible regions to semantic containers before CSS.\n5. Implement HTML first using the semantic mapping from step 3.\n6. Implement CSS in passes:\n   - Pass 1: layout + geometry,\n   - Pass 2: typography + spacing (semantic token-mapped first, size-calibrated per breakpoint),\n   - Pass 3: color + effects (token-mapped first),\n   - Pass 4: responsive adjustments.\n7. Run visual match pass:\n   - compare mobile and desktop against screenshots,\n   - iterate until mismatch is minimal.\n8. Run self-review pass again:\n   - re-check both screenshots after latest edits,\n   - if mismatch remains, loop back to HTML/CSS refinements.\n9. Report deltas:\n   - only remaining, non-removable deltas with exact reason.\n\n## 1:1 Acceptance Criteria\n\nAccepted only when all are true:\n\n1. Visual parity: geometry/layout match mobile and desktop.\n2. Typographic parity: family, size, weight, line-height, spacing match.\n   - text size must be calibrated from screenshot dimensions and mapped to nearest semantic token.\n3. Color/effect parity: backgrounds, text, borders, shadows, opacity/effects match.\n4. Token compliance: colors + typography tokenized by default; any hardcoded exceptions documented.\n5. Structural quality: semantic HTML + scoped CSS.\n6. Transparent assumptions: all uncertain values documented.\n\n## Output Requirements\n\nWhen reporting completion, include:\n\n1. What was recreated from screenshots.\n2. Files changed.\n3. Assumptions made.\n4. Remaining deltas and exact reason they cannot be removed.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:56:27.373Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Inspection Agents needing strict mobile and desktop visual parity in component reconstruction.","zh":"非常适合需要严格的移动和桌面视觉一致性组件重构的视觉检查代理。","ja":"厳密なモバイルとデスクトップの視覚的一貫性を必要とするビジュアルインスペクションエージェントに最適です。","ko":"엄격한 모바일 및 데스크톱 시각적 일관성을 필요로 하는 시각적 검사 에이전트에게 최적입니다.","es":"Perfect for Visual Inspection Agents needing strict mobile and desktop visual parity in component reconstruction.","fr":"Perfect for Visual Inspection Agents needing strict mobile and desktop visual parity in component reconstruction.","de":"Perfect for Visual Inspection Agents needing strict mobile and desktop visual parity in component reconstruction.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Inspeção Visual que precisam de estrita paridade móvel e de desktop na reconstrução de componentes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов визуального осмотра, требующих строгого соблюдения мобильной и настольной визуальной паритета при реконструкции компонентов.","ar":"เหมาะ للوكلاء التفتيش المرئي الذين يحتاجون إلى توافق مرئي صارم على الهاتف المحمول و سطح المكتب في إعادة بناء المكونات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reconstruct components from screenshots with precise visual parity, utilizing workflow execution rules and sub-bullets for accurate design source of truth, all while adhering to strict mobile and desktop compatibility protocols.","zh":"赋予代理从截图中重建组件的能力，利用工作流执行规则和子项目来实现准确的设计源真实性，同时遵守严格的移动和桌面兼容性协议。","ja":"スクリーンショットからコンポーネントを再構築するエージェントを可能にし、ワークフローの実行ルールとサブバレットを使用して設計ソースの真実性を保ち、厳格なモバイルとデスクトップの互換性プロトコルに従います。","ko":"스CREEN샷에서 구성 요소를 재구성 할 수있는 에이전트를 가능하게하며, 워크플로우 실행 규칙 및 서브 항목을 사용하여 설계 소스의 진실성을 제공하는 동시에 엄격한 모바일 및 데스크톱 호환성 규약을 준수합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to reconstruct components from screenshots with precise visual parity, utilizing workflow execution rules and sub-bullets for accurate design source of truth, all while adhering to strict mobile and desktop compatibility protocols.","fr":"Empowers agents to reconstruct components from screenshots with precise visual parity, utilizing workflow execution rules and sub-bullets for accurate design source of truth, all while adhering to strict mobile and desktop compatibility protocols.","de":"Empowers agents to reconstruct components from screenshots with precise visual parity, utilizing workflow execution rules and sub-bullets for accurate design source of truth, all while adhering to strict mobile and desktop compatibility protocols.","pt":"Permite que os agentes reconstruam componentes a partir de capturas de tela com paridade visual precisa, utilizando regras de execução de fluxo de trabalho e sub-pontos para fonte de design precisa, ao mesmo tempo em que adere a protocolos de compatibilidade móvel e de desktop estritos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реконструировать компоненты из скриншотов с точной визуальной паритетом, используя правила выполнения рабочего процесса и подпункты для точного источника дизайна, при этом соблюдая строгие протоколы совместимости для мобильных и настольных платформ.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء إمكانية إعادة بناء المكونات من لقطات الشاشة بدقة مرئية دقيقة، باستخدام قواعد تنفيذ سير العمل والنقاط الفرعية للحصول على مصدر تصميم دقيق، مع الالتزام ببروتوكولات التوافق المोबايل و سطح المكتب الصارمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Reconstructing UI components from design screenshots","Ensuring visual parity across mobile and desktop platforms","Validating design source of truth against actual component builds"],"zh":["从设计截图中重建UI组件","在移动和桌面平台上确保视觉一致性","验证设计源真实性与实际组件构建"],"ja":["設計スクリーンショットからUIコンポーネントを再構築する","モバイルとデスクトッププラットフォーム間で視覚的一貫性を確保する","設計ソースの真実性を実際のコンポーネントビルドと比較検証する"],"ko":["디자인 스크린샷에서 UI 구성 요소를 재구성하는 것","모바일 및 데스크톱 플랫폼 간에 시각적 일관성을 보장하는 것","디자인 소스의 진실성을 실제 구성 요소 빌드와 검증하는 것"],"es":["Reconstructing UI components from design screenshots","Ensuring visual parity across mobile and desktop platforms","Validating design source of truth against actual component builds"],"fr":["Reconstructing UI components from design screenshots","Ensuring visual parity across mobile and desktop platforms","Validating design source of truth against actual component builds"],"de":["Reconstructing UI components from design screenshots","Ensuring visual parity across mobile and desktop platforms","Validating design source of truth against actual component builds"],"pt":["Reconstruir componentes de interface do usuário a partir de capturas de tela de design","Garantir paridade visual em plataformas móveis e de desktop","Validar fonte de design contra construções reais de componentes"],"ru":["Реконструкция компонентов интерфейса пользователя из дизайн-скриншотов","Обеспечение визуальной паритета на мобильных и настольных платформах","Проверка источника дизайна против фактических построек компонентов"],"ar":["إعادة بناء مكونات واجهة المستخدم من لقطات الشاشة التصميمية","ضمان التوافق المرئي عبر منصات الموبايل و سطح المكتب","التحقق من مصدر التصميم مقابل بناء المكونات الفعلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact execution order of workflow steps","Mandatory reading of the file before acting","No skipping, combining, or reordering of steps allowed"],"zh":["需要工作流步骤的精确执行顺序","必须在执行前阅读文件","不允许跳过、合并或重新排序步骤"],"ja":["ワークフローの実行順序を正確に実行する必要がある","実行前にファイルを読む必要がある","ステップのスキップ、結合、または再配置は許可されない"],"ko":["워크플로우 단계의 정확한 실행 순서가 필요하다.","실행하기 전에 파일을 읽어야 한다.","단계를 건너뛰거나, 결합하거나, 재정렬하는 것은 허용되지 않는다."],"es":["Requires exact execution order of workflow steps","Mandatory reading of the file before acting","No skipping, combining, or reordering of steps allowed"],"fr":["Requires exact execution order of workflow steps","Mandatory reading of the file before acting","No skipping, combining, or reordering of steps allowed"],"de":["Requires exact execution order of workflow steps","Mandatory reading of the file before acting","No skipping, combining, or reordering of steps allowed"],"pt":["Exige ordem de execução exata das etapas do fluxo de trabalho","Leitura obrigatória do arquivo antes de agir","Não é permitido pular, combinar ou reordenar etapas"],"ru":["Требует точного порядка выполнения шагов рабочего процесса","Обязательное чтение файла перед действием","Не допускается пропуск, объединение или перестановка шагов"],"ar":["يتطلب ترتيب تنفيذ دقيق لخطوات سير العمل","يجب قراءة الملف قبل التصرف","لا يسمح بالتخطي أو الجمع أو إعادة ترتيب الخطوات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
