 de correo electrónico de SendGrid con Rube MCP, incluyendo campañas de marketing y gestión de contactos","fr":"Automatisez les flux d''e-mail de SendGrid avec Rube MCP, y compris les campagnes marketing et la gestion des contacts","de":"Automatisieren Sie die E-Mail-Workflows von SendGrid mit Rube MCP, einschließlich Marketingkampagnen und Kontaktverwaltung","pt":"O SendGrid Automation via Rube MCP permite automatizar fluxos de trabalho de entrega de e-mails, incluindo campanhas de marketing e gerenciamento de contatos","ru":"Автоматизация SendGrid через Rube MCP позволяет автоматизировать рабочие процессы доставки электронной почты, включая маркетинговые кампании и управление кон...","ar":"تتيح أتمتة SendGrid عبر Rube MCP أتمتة سير عمل تسليم البريد الإلكتروني، بما في ذلك حملات التسويق وإدارة الاتصالات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","Single Sends","Composio SendGrid","RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"ja":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","Single Sends","Composio SendGrid","RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"ko":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","Single Sends","Composio SendGrid","RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"es":["Automatización de campañas de marketing","Gestión de contactos y listas","Configuración de identidad de remitente","Análisis de correo electrónico"],"fr":["Automatisation des campagnes marketing","Gestion des contacts et des listes","Configuration de l''identité de l''expéditeur","Analyse d''e-mail"],"de":["Automatisierung von Marketingkampagnen","Kontakt- und Listenverwaltung","Einrichtung der Absenderidentität","E-Mail-Analyse"],"pt":["Automação de fluxos de trabalho de entrega de e-mails","Gerenciamento de contatos e listas","Configuração de identidade de remetente","Análise de e-mails"],"ru":["Автоматизация рабочих процессов доставки электронной почты","Управление контактами и списками","Настройка идентификатора отправителя","Анализ электронной почты"],"ar":["أتمتة سير عمل تسليم البريد الإلكتروني","إدارة الاتصالات والقوائم","إعداد هوية المرسل","تحليل البريد الإلكتروني"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","Composio SendGrid","SendGrid API","SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","SendGrid"],"ja":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","Composio SendGrid","SendGrid API","SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","SendGrid"],"ko":["SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","Composio SendGrid","SendGrid API","SendGrid","Rube MCP","SendGrid","SendGrid"],"es":["automatización de SendGrid","Rube MCP","correos electrónicos automatizados","campañas de marketing","gestión de contactos","análisis de correo electrónico"],"fr":["automatisation de SendGrid","Rube MCP","e-mails automatisés","campagnes marketing","gestion des contacts","analyse d''e-mail"],"de":["SendGrid-Automatisierung","Rube MCP","automatisierte E-Mails","Marketingkampagnen","Kontaktverwaltung","E-Mail-Analyse"],"pt":["SendGrid","Automação de e-mails","Rube MCP","Marketing de e-mails","Gerenciamento de contatos","Análise de e-mails"],"ru":["SendGrid","Автоматизация электронной почты","Rube MCP","Маркетинг электронной почты","Управление контактами","Анализ электронной почты"],"ar":["SendGrid","أتمتة البريد الإلكتروني","Rube MCP","تسويق البريد الإلكتروني","إدارة الاتصالات","تحليل البريد الإلكتروني"]}},"owner":"andre-sugai","repo":"cine-explorer-mvp-block","repoPath":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sendgrid-automation","description":"Automate SendGrid email operations including sending emails, managing contacts/lists, sender identities, templates, and analytics via Rube MCP (Composio). Always search tools first for current schemas.","bodyPreview":"# SendGrid Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate SendGrid email delivery workflows including marketing campaigns (Single Sends), contact and list management, sender identity setup, and email analytics through Composio''s SendGrid toolkit.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active SendGrid connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `sendgrid`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `htt","body":"# SendGrid Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate SendGrid email delivery workflows including marketing campaigns (Single Sends), contact and list management, sender identity setup, and email analytics through Composio''s SendGrid toolkit.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active SendGrid connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `sendgrid`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `https://rube.app/mcp` as an MCP server in your client configuration. No API keys needed — just add the endpoint and it works.\n\n\n1. Verify Rube MCP is available by confirming `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` responds\n2. Call `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `sendgrid`\n3. If connection is not ACTIVE, follow the returned auth link to complete SendGrid API key authentication\n4. Confirm connection status shows ACTIVE before running any workflows\n\n## Core Workflows\n\n### 1. Create and Send Marketing Campaigns (Single Sends)\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create and send a marketing email campaign to a contact list or segment.\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS` - List available marketing lists to target [Prerequisite]\n2. `SENDGRID_CREATE_A_LIST` - Create a new list if needed [Optional]\n3. `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT` - Add contacts to the list [Optional]\n4. `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_SENDER_IDENTITIES` - Get verified sender ID [Prerequisite]\n5. `SENDGRID_CREATE_SINGLE_SEND` - Create the campaign with content, sender, and recipients [Required]\n\n**Key parameters for SENDGRID_CREATE_SINGLE_SEND**:\n- `name`: Campaign name (required)\n- `email__config__subject`: Email subject line\n- `email__config__html__content`: HTML body content\n- `email__config__plain__content`: Plain text version\n- `email__config__sender__id`: Verified sender identity ID\n- `email__config__design__id`: Use instead of html_content for pre-built designs\n- `send__to__list__ids`: Array of list UUIDs to send to\n- `send__to__segment__ids`: Array of segment UUIDs\n- `send__to__all`: true to send to all contacts\n- `email__config__suppression__group__id` or `email__config__custom__unsubscribe__url`: One required for compliance\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Setting `send_at` on CREATE does NOT schedule the send; it only prepopulates the UI date; use the Schedule endpoint separately\n- `send_at: \"now\"` is only valid with the Schedule endpoint, not CREATE\n- Must provide either `suppression_group_id` or `custom_unsubscribe_url` for unsubscribe compliance\n- Sender must be verified before use; check with `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_SENDER_IDENTITIES`\n- Nested params use double-underscore notation (e.g., `email__config__subject`)\n\n### 2. Manage Contacts and Lists\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create contact lists, add/update contacts, search for contacts, or remove contacts from lists.\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS` - List all marketing lists [Required]\n2. `SENDGRID_CREATE_A_LIST` - Create a new contact list [Optional]\n3. `SENDGRID_GET_A_LIST_BY_ID` - Get list details and sample contacts [Optional]\n4. `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT` - Upsert contacts with list association [Required]\n5. `SENDGRID_GET_CONTACTS_BY_EMAILS` - Look up contacts by email [Optional]\n6. `SENDGRID_GET_CONTACTS_BY_IDENTIFIERS` - Look up contacts by email, phone, or external ID [Optional]\n7. `SENDGRID_GET_LIST_CONTACT_COUNT` - Verify contact count after operations [Optional]\n8. `SENDGRID_REMOVE_CONTACTS_FROM_A_LIST` - Remove contacts from a list without deleting [Optional]\n9. `SENDGRID_REMOVE_LIST_AND_OPTIONAL_CONTACTS` - Delete an entire list [Optional]\n10. `SENDGRID_IMPORT_CONTACTS` - Bulk import from CSV [Optional]\n\n**Key parameters for SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT**:\n- `contacts`: Array of contact objects (max 30,000 or 6MB), each with at least one identifier: `email`, `phone_number_id`, `external_id`, or `anonymous_id` (required)\n- `list_ids`: Array of list UUID strings to associate contacts with\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT` is asynchronous; returns 202 with `job_id`; contacts may take 10-30 seconds to appear\n- List IDs are UUIDs (e.g., \"ca7a3796-e8a8-4029-9ccb-df8937940562\"), not integers\n- List names must be unique; duplicate names cause 400 errors\n- `SENDGRID_ADD_A_SINGLE_RECIPIENT_TO_A_LIST` uses the legacy API; prefer `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT` with `list_ids`\n- `SENDGRID_REMOVE_LIST_AND_OPTIONAL_CONTACTS` is irreversible; require explicit user confirmation\n- Email addresses are automatically lowercased by SendGrid\n\n### 3. Manage Sender Identities\n\n**When to use**: User wants to set up or view sender identities (From addresses) for sending emails.\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_SENDER_IDENTITIES` - List all existing sender identities [Required]\n2. `SENDGRID_CREATE_A_SENDER_IDENTITY` - Create a new sender identity [Optional]\n3. `SENDGRID_VIEW_A_SENDER_IDENTITY` - View details for a specific sender [Optional]\n4. `SENDGRID_UPDATE_A_SENDER_IDENTITY` - Update sender details [Optional]\n5. `SENDGRID_CREATE_VERIFIED_SENDER_REQUEST` - Create and verify a new sender [Optional]\n6. `SENDGRID_AUTHENTICATE_A_DOMAIN` - Set up domain authentication for auto-verification [Optional]\n\n**Key parameters for SENDGRID_CREATE_A_SENDER_IDENTITY**:\n- `from__email`: From email address (required)\n- `from__name`: Display name (required)\n- `reply__to__email`: Reply-to address (required)\n- `nickname`: Internal identifier (required)\n- `address`, `city`, `country`: Physical address for CAN-SPAM compliance (required)\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- New senders must be verified before use; if domain is not authenticated, a verification email is sent\n- Up to 100 unique sender identities per account\n- Avoid using domains with strict DMARC policies (gmail.com, yahoo.com) as from addresses\n- `SENDGRID_CREATE_VERIFIED_SENDER_REQUEST` sends a verification email; sender is unusable until verified\n\n### 4. View Email Statistics and Activity\n\n**When to use**: User wants to review email delivery stats, bounce rates, open/click metrics, or message activity.\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_GLOBAL_EMAIL_STATISTICS` - Get account-wide delivery metrics [Required]\n2. `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_CATEGORIES` - Discover available categories for filtering [Optional]\n3. `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_EMAIL_STATISTICS_FOR_CATEGORIES` - Get stats broken down by category [Optional]\n4. `SENDGRID_FILTER_ALL_MESSAGES` - Search email activity feed by recipient, status, or date [Optional]\n5. `SENDGRID_FILTER_MESSAGES_BY_MESSAGE_ID` - Get detailed events for a specific message [Optional]\n6. `SENDGRID_REQUEST_CSV` - Export activity data as CSV for large datasets [Optional]\n7. `SENDGRID_DOWNLOAD_CSV` - Download the exported CSV file [Optional]\n\n**Key parameters for SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_GLOBAL_EMAIL_STATISTICS**:\n- `start_date`: Start date YYYY-MM-DD (required)\n- `end_date`: End date YYYY-MM-DD\n- `aggregated_by`: \"day\", \"week\", or \"month\"\n- `limit` / `offset`: Pagination (default 500)\n\n**Key parameters for SENDGRID_FILTER_ALL_MESSAGES**:\n- `query`: SQL-like query string, e.g., `status=\"delivered\"`, `to_email=\"user@example.com\"`, date ranges with `BETWEEN TIMESTAMP`\n- `limit`: 1-1000 (default 10)\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- `SENDGRID_FILTER_ALL_MESSAGES` requires the \"30 Days Additional Email Activity History\" paid add-on; returns 403 without it\n- Global statistics are nested under `details[].stats[0].metrics`, not a flat structure\n- Category statistics are only available for the previous 13 months\n- Maximum 10 categories per request in `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_EMAIL_STATISTICS_FOR_CATEGORIES`\n- CSV export is limited to one request per 12 hours; link expires after 3 days\n\n### 5. Manage Suppressions\n\n**When to use**: User wants to check or manage unsubscribe groups for email compliance.\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `SENDGRID_GET_SUPPRESSION_GROUPS` - List all suppression groups [Required]\n2. `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_SUPPRESSION_GROUPS_FOR_AN_EMAIL_ADDRESS` - Check suppression status for a specific email [Optional]\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Suppressed addresses remain undeliverable even if present on marketing lists\n- Campaign send counts may be lower than list counts due to suppressions\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### ID Resolution\nAlways resolve names to IDs before operations:\n- **List name -> list_id**: `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS` and match by name\n- **Sender name -> sender_id**: `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_SENDER_IDENTITIES` and match\n- **Contact email -> contact_id**: `SENDGRID_GET_CONTACTS_BY_EMAILS` with email array\n- **Template name -> template_id**: Use the SendGrid UI or template endpoints\n\n### Pagination\n- `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS`: Token-based with `page_token` and `page_size` (max 1000)\n- `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_GLOBAL_EMAIL_STATISTICS`: Offset-based with `limit` (max 500) and `offset`\n- Always paginate list retrieval to avoid missing existing lists\n\n### Async Operations\nContact operations (`ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT`, `IMPORT_CONTACTS`) are asynchronous:\n- Returns 202 with a `job_id`\n- Wait 10-30 seconds before verifying with `GET_CONTACTS_BY_EMAILS`\n- Use `GET_LIST_CONTACT_COUNT` to confirm list growth\n\n## Known Pitfalls\n\n### ID Formats\n- Marketing list IDs are UUIDs (e.g., \"ca7a3796-e8a8-4029-9ccb-df8937940562\")\n- Legacy list IDs are integers; do not mix with Marketing API endpoints\n- Sender identity IDs are integers\n- Template IDs: Dynamic templates start with \"d-\", legacy templates are UUIDs\n- Contact IDs are UUIDs\n\n### Rate Limits\n- SendGrid may return HTTP 429; respect `Retry-After` headers\n- CSV export limited to one request per 12 hours\n- Bulk contact upsert max: 30,000 contacts or 6MB per request\n\n### Parameter Quirks\n- Nested params use double-underscore: `email__config__subject`, `from__email`\n- `send_at` on CREATE_SINGLE_SEND only sets a UI default, does NOT schedule\n- `SENDGRID_ADD_A_SINGLE_RECIPIENT_TO_A_LIST` uses legacy API; `recipient_id` is Base64-encoded lowercase email\n- `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS` and `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_LISTS` both exist; prefer RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS for Marketing API\n- Contact adds are async (202); always verify after a delay\n\n### Legacy vs Marketing API\n- Some tools use the legacy Contact Database API (`/v3/contactdb/`) which may return 403 on newer accounts\n- Prefer Marketing API tools: `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT`, `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS`, `SENDGRID_CREATE_SINGLE_SEND`\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Tool Slug | Key Params |\n|------|-----------|------------|\n| List marketing lists | `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_ALL_LISTS` | `page_size`, `page_token` |\n| Create list | `SENDGRID_CREATE_A_LIST` | `name` |\n| Get list by ID | `SENDGRID_GET_A_LIST_BY_ID` | `id` |\n| Get list count | `SENDGRID_GET_LIST_CONTACT_COUNT` | `id` |\n| Add/update contacts | `SENDGRID_ADD_OR_UPDATE_A_CONTACT` | `contacts`, `list_ids` |\n| Search contacts by email | `SENDGRID_GET_CONTACTS_BY_EMAILS` | `emails` |\n| Search by identifiers | `SENDGRID_GET_CONTACTS_BY_IDENTIFIERS` | `identifier_type`, `identifiers` |\n| Remove from list | `SENDGRID_REMOVE_CONTACTS_FROM_A_LIST` | `id`, `contact_ids` |\n| Delete list | `SENDGRID_REMOVE_LIST_AND_OPTIONAL_CONTACTS` | `id`, `delete_contacts` |\n| Import contacts CSV | `SENDGRID_IMPORT_CONTACTS` | field mappings |\n| Create Single Send | `SENDGRID_CREATE_SINGLE_SEND` | `name`, `email__config__*`, `send__to__list__ids` |\n| List sender identities | `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_SENDER_IDENTITIES` | (none) |\n| Create sender | `SENDGRID_CREATE_A_SENDER_IDENTITY` | `from__email`, `from__name`, `address` |\n| Verify sender | `SENDGRID_CREATE_VERIFIED_SENDER_REQUEST` | `from_email`, `nickname`, `address` |\n| Authenticate domain | `SENDGRID_AUTHENTICATE_A_DOMAIN` | `domain` |\n| Global email stats | `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_GLOBAL_EMAIL_STATISTICS` | `start_date`, `aggregated_by` |\n| Category stats | `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_EMAIL_STATISTICS_FOR_CATEGORIES` | `start_date`, `categories` |\n| Filter email activity | `SENDGRID_FILTER_ALL_MESSAGES` | `query`, `limit` |\n| Message details | `SENDGRID_FILTER_MESSAGES_BY_MESSAGE_ID` | `msg_id` |\n| Export CSV | `SENDGRID_REQUEST_CSV` | `query` |\n| Download CSV | `SENDGRID_DOWNLOAD_CSV` | `download_uuid` |\n| List categories | `SENDGRID_GET_ALL_CATEGORIES` | (none) |\n| Suppression groups | `SENDGRID_GET_SUPPRESSION_GROUPS` | (none) |\n| Get template | `SENDGRID_RETRIEVE_A_SINGLE_TRANSACTIONAL_TEMPLATE` | `template_id` |\n| Duplicate template | `SENDGRID_DUPLICATE_A_TRANSACTIONAL_TEMPLATE` | `template_id`, `name` |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:58:09.106Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Email Automation Agents needing advanced SendGrid workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级SendGrid工作流集成的电子邮件自动化代理。","ja":"SendGridワークフローの高度な統合を必要とするEメールの自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 SendGrid 워크플로 통합이 필요한 이메일 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Automatización de Correo Electrónico que necesitan una integración avanzada de flujo de trabajo de SendGrid.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Automatisation de Courrier Électronique ayant besoin d''une intégration avancée du workflow SendGrid.","de":"Perfekt für E-Mail-Automatisierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte SendGrid-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação de E-mail que necessitam de integração avançada de fluxo de trabalho do SendGrid.","ru":"Идеально для агентов автоматизации электронной почты, требующих расширенной интеграции рабочего процесса SendGrid.","ar":"مثالي لعميل автомatisation البريد الإلكتروني الذي يحتاج إلى تكامل متقدم في SendGrid"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate SendGrid email delivery workflows, including marketing campaigns, contact and list management, sender identity setup, and email analytics through Composio''s SendGrid toolkit, utilizing RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS and RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","zh":"赋予代理人使用Composio的SendGrid工具包自动化SendGrid电子邮件投递工作流的能力，包括营销活动、联系人和列表管理、发件人身份设置以及电子邮件分析，利用RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS和RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS。","ja":"ComposioのSendGridツールキットを使用して、代理がSendGridのEメール配信ワークフローを自動化できるようにすることで、マーケティングキャンペーン、連絡先およびリスト管理、送信者IDの設定、およびEメール分析を含む機能を提供します。RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLSとRUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONSを利用しています。","ko":"Composio의 SendGrid 툴킷을 사용하여 에이전트가 SendGrid 이메일 전달 워크플로를 자동화할 수 있도록 강화하여, 마케팅 캠페인, 연락처 및 목록 관리, 발신자 ID 설정 및 이메일 분석을 포함한 기능을 제공하며, RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS와 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar flujos de trabajo de entrega de correo electrónico de SendGrid, incluyendo campañas de marketing, administración de contactos y listas, configuración de identidad de remitente y análisis de correo electrónico a través de la herramienta de SendGrid de Composio, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS y RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les flux de travail de livraison d''e-mail de SendGrid, y compris les campagnes de marketing, la gestion des contacts et des listes, la configuration de l''identité de l''expéditeur et l''analyse des e-mails via la boîte à outils SendGrid de Composio, en utilisant RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS et RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, SendGrid-E-Mail-Lieferungs-Workflows zu automatisieren, einschließlich Marketing-Kampagnen, Kontakt- und Listenverwaltung, Absender-Identitäts-Einrichtung und E-Mail-Analytics über Composios SendGrid-Toolkit, unter Verwendung von RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS und RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","pt":"Habilita agentes a automatizar fluxos de trabalho de entrega de e-mail do SendGrid, incluindo campanhas de marketing, gerenciamento de contatos e listas, configuração de identidade do remetente e análise de e-mail por meio da ferramenta SendGrid da Composio, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS e RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать рабочие процессы доставки электронной почты SendGrid, включая маркетинговые кампании, управление контактами и списками, настройку идентификатора отправителя и анализ электронной почты с помощью инструмента SendGrid от Composio, используя RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS и RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توفير أتمتة أنظمة تسليم البريد الإلكتروني في SendGrid، بما في ذلك حملات التسويق وإدارة الاتصالات والقوائم وإعداد هوية المرسل وتحليل البريد الإلكتروني من خلال أداة SendGrid من Composio، باستخدام RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS و RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Single Sends for marketing campaigns","Managing contacts and lists via SendGrid API","Setting up sender identities for improved email deliverability"],"zh":["自动化单次发送用于营销活动","通过SendGrid API管理联系人和列表","设置发件人身份以提高电子邮件投递率"],"ja":["マーケティングキャンペーン用の単一送信の自動化","SendGrid APIを介した連絡先およびリストの管理","Eメール配信の改善のための送信者IDの設定"],"ko":["마케팅 캠페인용 단일 발송 자동화","SendGrid API를 통해 연락처 및 목록 관리","이메일 전달률 개선을 위한 발신자 ID 설정"],"es":["Automatizar Envíos Únicos para campañas de marketing","Administrar contactos y listas a través de la API de SendGrid","Configurar identidades de remitente para una mejor entrega de correo electrónico"],"fr":["Automatiser les envois uniques pour les campagnes de marketing","Gérer les contacts et les listes via l''API SendGrid","Configurer les identités de l''expéditeur pour une meilleure livraison d''e-mail"],"de":["Automatisieren von Einzelversenden für Marketing-Kampagnen","Verwalten von Kontakten und Listen über die SendGrid-API","Einrichten von Absender-Identitäten für eine verbesserte E-Mail-Lieferung"],"pt":["Automatizar Envios Únicos para campanhas de marketing","Gerenciar contatos e listas via API do SendGrid","Configurar identidades de remetente para melhorar a entrega de e-mail"],"ru":["Автоматизировать одиночные отправки для маркетинговых кампаний","Управлять контактами и списками через API SendGrid","Настроить идентификаторы отправителей для улучшения доставки электронной почты"],"ar":["أتمتة إرسال مفرد ل حملات التسويق","إدارة الاتصالات والقوائم من خلال واجهة برمجة تطبيقات SendGrid","إعداد هوية المرسل لتحسين تسليم البريد الإلكتروني"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rube MCP connection with RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available","Active SendGrid connection via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS with toolkit sendgrid"],"zh":["需要Rube MCP连接且RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS可用","需要通过RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS的活动SendGrid连接以及工具包sendgrid"],"ja":["RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLSが利用可能なRube MCP接続が必要","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS経由でのアクティブなSendGrid接続とツールキットsendgridが必要"],"ko":["RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS가 사용 가능한 Rube MCP 연결이 필요합니다.","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 통한 활성 SendGrid 연결 및 툴킷 sendgrid가 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere conexión Rube MCP con RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponible","Conexión SendGrid activa a través de RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS con la herramienta de SendGrid"],"fr":["Nécessite une connexion Rube MCP avec RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponible","Connexion SendGrid active via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS avec la boîte à outils SendGrid"],"de":["Erfordert Rube-MCP-Verbindung mit verfügbarer RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","Aktive SendGrid-Verbindung über RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS mit dem SendGrid-Toolkit"],"pt":["Exige conexão Rube MCP com RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponível","Conexão ativa SendGrid via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS com toolkit sendgrid"],"ru":["Требует соединения Rube MCP с доступными RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","Активное соединение SendGrid через RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS с набором инструментов sendgrid"],"ar":["يتطلب اتصال Rube MCP مع RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS متاحة","اتصال نشط SendGrid من خلال RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS مع أداة sendgrid"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('vip32/TaskFlow/dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking', 'community', 'vip32', 'TaskFlow', 'vip32/TaskFlow', 'dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z', '2026-02-18T07:57:59.721Z', NULL, '{"id":"vip32/TaskFlow/dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking","name":"dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking","description":{"zh":"本技能关注于使用NSubstitute创建和管理测试双，涵盖测试双的五种类型、依赖隔离策略、行为设置和验证最佳实践","ja":"このスキルは、NSubstituteを使用してテストダブルを作成して管理することに焦点を当てており、テストダブルの5つのタイプ、依存関係の分離戦略、動作の設定、検証のベストプラクティスをカバーする","ko":"이 스킬은 NSubstitute를 사용하여 테스트 더블을 생성하고 관리하는 데 중점을 두며 테스트 더블의 5가지 유형, 의존성 분리 전략, 동작 설정 및 검증 최적화 방법을 다룹니다","es":"NSubstitute es una biblioteca de mocking para .NET que te permite crear y gestionar test doubles de manera eficiente.","fr":"NSubstitute est une bibliothèque de mocking pour .NET qui vous permet de créer et de gérer des test doubles de manière efficace.","de":"NSubstitute ist eine Mocking-Bibliothek für .NET, mit der Sie Test-Doubles effizient erstellen und verwalten können.","pt":"NSubstitute é uma biblioteca de mocking para .NET que ajuda a criar testes mais rápidos e confiáveis. Aprenda a usá-la para melhorar sua produtividade","ru":"NSubstitute — это библиотека мокинга для .NET, которая помогает создавать более быстрые и надежные тесты. Узнайте, как использовать ее для повышения производительности","ar":"NSubstitute هي مكتبة لموكينج .NET التي تساعد على إنشاء اختبارات أسرع وأكثر موثوقية. تعلم كيفية استخدامها لتحسين إنتاجيتك","en":"Task Flow is a focused personal productivity app built to help you do more than just collect tasks."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"使用NSubstitute进行测试双精通","ja":"NSubstituteを使用したテストダブルのマスター","ko":"NSubstitute를 사용한 테스트 더블 전문가","es":"Pruebas de .NET con NSubstitute","fr":"Test .NET avec NSubstitute","de":".NET-Tests mit NSubstitute","pt":"Testes .NET com NSubstitute: Melhores Práticas de Mocking","ru":"Тестирование .NET с NSubstitute: Лучшие практики мокинга","ar":"إختبار .NET مع NSubstitute: أفضل الممارسات لموكينج","en":"dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking"},"description":{"zh":"本技能关注于使用NSubstitute创建和管理测试双，涵盖测试双的五种类型、依赖隔离策略、行为设置和验证最佳实践","ja":"このスキルは、NSubstituteを使用してテストダブルを作成して管理することに焦点を当てており、テストダブルの5つのタイプ、依存関係の分離戦略、動作の設定、検証のベストプラクティスをカバーする","ko":"이 스킬은 NSubstitute를 사용하여 테스트 더블을 생성하고 관리하는 데 중점을 두며 테스트 더블의 5가지 유형, 의존성 분리 전략, 동작 설정 및 검증 최적화 방법을 다룹니다","es":"NSubstitute es una biblioteca de mocking para .NET que te permite crear y gestionar test doubles de manera eficiente.","fr":"NSubstitute est une bibliothèque de mocking pour .NET qui vous permet de créer et de gérer des test doubles de manière efficace.","de":"NSubstitute ist eine Mocking-Bibliothek für .NET, mit der Sie Test-Doubles effizient erstellen und verwalten können.","pt":"NSubstitute é uma biblioteca de mocking para .NET que ajuda a criar testes mais rápidos e confiáveis. Aprenda a usá-la para melhorar sua produtividade","ru":"NSubstitute — это библиотека мокинга для .NET, которая помогает создавать более быстрые и надежные тесты. Узнайте, как использовать ее для повышения производ...","ar":"NSubstitute هي مكتبة لموكينج .NET التي تساعد على إنشاء اختبارات أسرع وأكثر موثوقية. تعلم كيفية استخدامها لتحسين إنتاجيتك","en":"Task Flow is a focused personal productivity app built to help you do more than just collect tasks."},"definition":{"en":"Task Flow is a focused personal productivity app built to help you do more than just collect tasks."},"features":{"zh":["使用NSubstitute创建和管理测试双","支持测试双的五种类型","依赖隔离策略和行为设置","验证最佳实践","提高测试效率和稳定性"],"ja":["NSubstituteを使用してテストダブルを作成して管理する","テストダブルの5つのタイプをサポートする","依存関係の分離戦略と動作の設定","検証のベストプラクティス","テストの効率と安定性を高める"],"ko":["NSubstitute를 사용하여 테스트 더블을 생성하고 관리합니다","테스트 더블의 5가지 유형을 지원합니다","의존성 분리 전략 및 동작 설정","검증 최적화 방법","테스트 효율과 안정성을 향상합니다"],"es":["Creación de test doubles","Gestión de dependencias","Configuración de comportamiento","Verificación de resultados","Soporte para los cinco tipos de test doubles"],"fr":["Création de test doubles","Gestion des dépendances","Configuration du comportement","Vérification des résultats","Prise en charge des cinq types de test doubles"],"de":["Erstellung von Test-Doubles","Verwaltung von Abhängigkeiten","Konfiguration des Verhaltens","Überprüfung der Ergebnisse","Unterstützung für die fünf Arten von Test-Doubles"],"pt":["Criação de testes doubles para dependências externas","Isolamento de dependências para testes mais rápidos","Simulação de comportamentos para testes mais realistas","Verificação de comportamentos para garantir a correta funcionalidade","Suporte a todos os cinco tipos de testes doubles"],"ru":["Создание тестовых дубликатов для внешних зависимостей","Изоляция зависимостей для более быстрых тестов","Имитация поведения для более реалистичных тестов","Проверка поведения для обеспечения правильной функциональности","Поддержка всех пяти типов тестовых дубликатов"],"ar":["إنشاء مزدوجات اختبار للتبعيات الخارجية","عزل التبعيات لاختبارات أسرع","محاكاة السلوكيات لاختبارات أكثر واقعية","التحقق من السلوكيات لضمان الوظيفة الصحيحة","دعم جميع الأنواع الخمسة لمزدوجات الاختبار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NSubstitute","测试双",".NET测试","依赖隔离","行为设置","验证最佳实践"],"ja":["NSubstitute","テストダブル",".NETテスト","依存関係の分離","動作の設定","検証のベストプラクティス"],"ko":["NSubstitute","테스트 더블",".NET 테스트","의존성 분리","동작 설정","검증 최적화 방법"],"es":["NSubstitute","pruebas de .NET","test doubles","mocking","dependencias","comportamiento","verificación"],"fr":["NSubstitute","tests .NET","test doubles","mocking","dépendances","comportement","vérification"],"de":["NSubstitute",".NET-Tests","Test-Doubles","Mocking","Abhängigkeiten","Verhalten","Überprüfung"],"pt":["NSubstitute","mocking","testes doubles","dependências externas","isolamento de dependências","simulação de comportamentos","verificação de comportamentos","desenvolvimento de software","testes de unidade"],"ru":["NSubstitute","мокинг","тестовые дубликаты","внешние зависимости","изоляция зависимостей","имитация поведения","проверка поведения","разработка программного обеспечения","юнит-тесты"],"ar":["NSubstitute","موكينج","مزدوجات اختبار","التبعيات الخارجية","عزل التبعيات","محاكاة السلوكيات","التحقق من السلوكيات","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبارات الوحدة"]}},"owner":"vip32","repo":"TaskFlow","repoPath":"vip32/TaskFlow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dotnet-testing-nsubstitute-mocking","description":"Specialized skill for creating test doubles (Mock, Stub, Spy) using NSubstitute. Use when isolating external dependencies, simulating interface behavior, and verifying method calls. Covers complete guidance on Substitute.For, Returns, Received, Throws, etc.","bodyPreview":"# NSubstitute Mocking Skill\n\n## Skill Overview\n\nThis skill focuses on using NSubstitute to create and manage test doubles, covering all five Test Double types, dependency isolation strategies, behavior setup, and verification best practices.\n\n## Why Test Doubles?\n\nReal-world code typically depends on external resources, making tests:\n\n1. **Slow** - Requires actual database, file system, or network operations\n2. **Unstable** - External service failures cause test failures\n3. **Non-reproducible**","body":"# NSubstitute Mocking Skill\n\n## Skill Overview\n\nThis skill focuses on using NSubstitute to create and manage test doubles, covering all five Test Double types, dependency isolation strategies, behavior setup, and verification best practices.\n\n## Why Test Doubles?\n\nReal-world code typically depends on external resources, making tests:\n\n1. **Slow** - Requires actual database, file system, or network operations\n2. **Unstable** - External service failures cause test failures\n3. **Non-reproducible** - Time, random numbers cause inconsistent results\n4. **Environment-dependent** - Requires specific external environment setup\n5. **Development-blocking** - Must wait for external systems to be ready\n\nTest doubles enable us to isolate these dependencies and focus on testing business logic.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Package Installation\n\n```xml\n<PackageReference Include=\"NSubstitute\" Version=\"5.3.0\" />\n<PackageReference Include=\"xunit\" Version=\"2.9.3\" />\n<PackageReference Include=\"Microsoft.Extensions.Logging\" Version=\"9.0.0\" />\n<PackageReference Include=\"AwesomeAssertions\" Version=\"9.1.0\" />\n```\n\n### Basic using Statements\n\n```csharp\nusing NSubstitute;\nusing NSubstitute.ExceptionExtensions;\nusing Xunit;\nusing AwesomeAssertions;\nusing Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\n```\n\n## Five Test Double Types\n\nBased on Gerard Meszaros'' definitions in *xUnit Test Patterns*:\n\n### 1. Dummy - Filler Object\n\nUsed only to satisfy method signatures, never actually used.\n\n```csharp\npublic interface IEmailService\n{\n    void SendEmail(string to, string subject, string body, ILogger logger);\n}\n\n[Fact]\npublic void ProcessOrder_LoggerNotUsed_ShouldProcessOrderSuccessfully()\n{\n    // Dummy: Just to satisfy parameter requirements\n    var dummyLogger = Substitute.For<ILogger>();\n\n    var service = new OrderService();\n    var result = service.ProcessOrder(order, dummyLogger);\n\n    result.Success.Should().BeTrue();\n    // Don''t care if logger was called\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Stub - Predefined Return Values\n\nProvides predefined return values for testing specific scenarios.\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void GetUser_ValidUserId_ShouldReturnUserData()\n{\n    // Arrange - Stub: Predefined return value\n    var stubRepository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    stubRepository.GetById(123).Returns(new User { Id = 123, Name = \"John\" });\n\n    var service = new UserService(stubRepository);\n\n    // Act\n    var actual = service.GetUser(123);\n\n    // Assert\n    actual.Name.Should().Be(\"John\");\n    // Don''t care how many times GetById was called\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Fake - Simplified Implementation\n\nHas actual functionality but simplified, typically used for integration tests.\n\n```csharp\npublic class FakeUserRepository : IUserRepository\n{\n    private readonly Dictionary<int, User> _users = new();\n\n    public User GetById(int id) => _users.TryGetValue(id, out var user) ? user : null;\n    public void Save(User user) => _users[user.Id] = user;\n    public void Delete(int id) => _users.Remove(id);\n}\n\n[Fact]\npublic void CreateUser_CreateUser_ShouldSaveAndRetrieve()\n{\n    // Fake: Simplified implementation with real logic\n    var fakeRepository = new FakeUserRepository();\n    var service = new UserService(fakeRepository);\n\n    service.CreateUser(new User { Id = 1, Name = \"John\" });\n    var actual = service.GetUser(1);\n\n    actual.Name.Should().Be(\"John\");\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Spy - Call Recording\n\nRecords how it''s called, can verify calls afterward.\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void CreateUser_CreateUser_ShouldLogCreationInfo()\n{\n    // Arrange\n    var spyLogger = Substitute.For<ILogger<UserService>>();\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    var service = new UserService(repository, spyLogger);\n\n    // Act\n    service.CreateUser(new User { Name = \"John\" });\n\n    // Assert - Spy: Verify call records\n    spyLogger.Received(1).LogInformation(\"User created: {Name}\", \"John\");\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Mock - Behavior Verification\n\nExpects specific interaction behavior, test fails if expectations aren''t met.\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void RegisterUser_RegisterUser_ShouldSendWelcomeEmail()\n{\n    // Arrange\n    var mockEmailService = Substitute.For<IEmailService>();\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    var service = new UserService(repository, mockEmailService);\n\n    // Act\n    service.RegisterUser(\"john@example.com\", \"John\");\n\n    // Assert - Mock: Verify specific interaction behavior\n    mockEmailService.Received(1).SendWelcomeEmail(\"john@example.com\", \"John\");\n}\n```\n\n## NSubstitute Core Features\n\n### Basic Substitution Syntax\n\n```csharp\n// Create interface substitute\nvar substitute = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n\n// Create class substitute (needs virtual members)\nvar classSubstitute = Substitute.For<BaseService>();\n\n// Create multiple interface substitute\nvar multiSubstitute = Substitute.For<IService, IDisposable>();\n```\n\n### Return Value Setup\n\n#### Basic Return Values\n\n```csharp\n// Exact parameter matching\n_repository.GetById(1).Returns(new User { Id = 1, Name = \"John\" });\n\n// Any parameter matching\n_service.Process(Arg.Any<string>()).Returns(\"processed\");\n\n// Return sequence values\n_generator.GetNext().Returns(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);\n```\n\n#### Conditional Return Values\n\n```csharp\n// Use delegate to calculate return value\n_calculator.Add(Arg.Any<int>(), Arg.Any<int>())\n           .Returns(x => (int)x[0] + (int)x[1]);\n\n// Conditional matching\n_service.Process(Arg.Is<string>(x => x.StartsWith(\"test\")))\n        .Returns(\"test-result\");\n```\n\n#### Throw Exceptions\n\n```csharp\n// Synchronous method throws exception\n_service.RiskyOperation()\n        .Throws(new InvalidOperationException(\"Something went wrong\"));\n\n// Async method throws exception\n_service.RiskyOperationAsync()\n        .Throws(new InvalidOperationException(\"Async operation failed\"));\n```\n\n### Argument Matchers\n\n```csharp\n// Any value\n_service.Process(Arg.Any<string>()).Returns(\"result\");\n\n// Specific condition\n_service.Process(Arg.Is<string>(x => x.Length > 5)).Returns(\"long-result\");\n\n// Argument capture\nstring capturedArg = null;\n_service.Process(Arg.Do<string>(x => capturedArg = x)).Returns(\"result\");\n_service.Process(\"test\");\ncapturedArg.Should().Be(\"test\");\n\n// Argument validation\n_service.Process(Arg.Is<string>(x =>\n{\n    x.Should().StartWith(\"prefix\");\n    return true;\n})).Returns(\"result\");\n```\n\n### Call Verification\n\n```csharp\n// Verify called (at least once)\n_service.Received().Process(\"test\");\n\n// Verify call count\n_service.Received(2).Process(Arg.Any<string>());\n\n// Verify not called\n_service.DidNotReceive().Delete(Arg.Any<int>());\n\n// Verify called with any args\n_service.ReceivedWithAnyArgs().Process(default);\n\n// Verify call order\nReceived.InOrder(() =>\n{\n    _service.Start();\n    _service.Process();\n    _service.Stop();\n});\n```\n\n## Real-World Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Dependency Injection & Test Setup\n\n#### System Under Test\n\n```csharp\npublic class FileBackupService\n{\n    private readonly IFileSystem _fileSystem;\n    private readonly IDateTimeProvider _dateTimeProvider;\n    private readonly IBackupRepository _backupRepository;\n    private readonly ILogger<FileBackupService> _logger;\n\n    public FileBackupService(\n        IFileSystem fileSystem,\n        IDateTimeProvider dateTimeProvider,\n        IBackupRepository backupRepository,\n        ILogger<FileBackupService> logger)\n    {\n        _fileSystem = fileSystem;\n        _dateTimeProvider = dateTimeProvider;\n        _backupRepository = backupRepository;\n        _logger = logger;\n    }\n\n    public async Task<BackupResult> BackupFileAsync(string sourcePath, string destinationPath)\n    {\n        if (!_fileSystem.FileExists(sourcePath))\n        {\n            _logger.LogWarning(\"Source file not found: {Path}\", sourcePath);\n            return new BackupResult { Success = false, Message = \"Source file not found\" };\n        }\n\n        var fileInfo = _fileSystem.GetFileInfo(sourcePath);\n        if (fileInfo.Length > 100 * 1024 * 1024)\n        {\n            return new BackupResult { Success = false, Message = \"File too large\" };\n        }\n\n        var timestamp = _dateTimeProvider.Now.ToString(\"yyyyMMdd_HHmmss\");\n        var backupFileName = $\"{Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension(sourcePath)}_{timestamp}{Path.GetExtension(sourcePath)}\";\n        var fullBackupPath = Path.Combine(destinationPath, backupFileName);\n\n        _fileSystem.CopyFile(sourcePath, fullBackupPath);\n        await _backupRepository.SaveBackupHistory(sourcePath, fullBackupPath, _dateTimeProvider.Now);\n\n        _logger.LogInformation(\"Backup completed: {Path}\", fullBackupPath);\n\n        return new BackupResult { Success = true, BackupPath = fullBackupPath };\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Test Class Setup\n\n```csharp\npublic class FileBackupServiceTests\n{\n    private readonly IFileSystem _fileSystem;\n    private readonly IDateTimeProvider _dateTimeProvider;\n    private readonly IBackupRepository _backupRepository;\n    private readonly ILogger<FileBackupService> _logger;\n    private readonly FileBackupService _sut; // System Under Test\n\n    public FileBackupServiceTests()\n    {\n        _fileSystem = Substitute.For<IFileSystem>();\n        _dateTimeProvider = Substitute.For<IDateTimeProvider>();\n        _backupRepository = Substitute.For<IBackupRepository>();\n        _logger = Substitute.For<ILogger<FileBackupService>>();\n\n        _sut = new FileBackupService(_fileSystem, _dateTimeProvider, _backupRepository, _logger);\n    }\n\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task BackupFileAsync_FileExistsAndSizeReasonable_ShouldBackupSuccessfully()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        var sourcePath = @\"C:\\source\\test.txt\";\n        var destinationPath = @\"C:\\backup\";\n        var testTime = new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, 12, 0, 0);\n\n        _fileSystem.FileExists(sourcePath).Returns(true);\n        _fileSystem.GetFileInfo(sourcePath).Returns(new FileInfo { Length = 1024 });\n        _dateTimeProvider.Now.Returns(testTime);\n\n        // Act\n        var result = await _sut.BackupFileAsync(sourcePath, destinationPath);\n\n        // Assert\n        result.Success.Should().BeTrue();\n        result.BackupPath.Should().Be(@\"C:\\backup\\test_20240101_120000.txt\");\n\n        _fileSystem.Received(1).CopyFile(sourcePath, result.BackupPath);\n        await _backupRepository.Received(1).SaveBackupHistory(\n            sourcePath, result.BackupPath, testTime);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Mock vs Stub Real-World Differences\n\n#### Stub: Focus on State\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void CalculateDiscount_PremiumMember_ShouldReturn20Discount()\n{\n    // Stub: Only care about return value, used to set test scenario\n    var stubCustomerService = Substitute.For<ICustomerService>();\n    stubCustomerService.GetCustomerType(123).Returns(CustomerType.Premium);\n\n    var service = new PricingService(stubCustomerService);\n\n    // Act\n    var discount = service.CalculateDiscount(123, 1000);\n\n    // Assert - Only verify result state\n    discount.Should().Be(200); // 20% of 1000\n}\n```\n\n#### Mock: Focus on Behavior\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void ProcessPayment_SuccessfulPayment_ShouldLogTransactionInfo()\n{\n    // Mock: Care about correct interactions\n    var mockLogger = Substitute.For<ILogger<PaymentService>>();\n    var stubPaymentGateway = Substitute.For<IPaymentGateway>();\n    stubPaymentGateway.ProcessPayment(Arg.Any<decimal>()).Returns(PaymentResult.Success);\n\n    var service = new PaymentService(stubPaymentGateway, mockLogger);\n\n    // Act\n    service.ProcessPayment(100);\n\n    // Assert - Verify interaction behavior\n    mockLogger.Received(1).LogInformation(\n        \"Payment processed: {Amount} - Result: {Result}\",\n        100,\n        PaymentResult.Success);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Async Method Testing\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic async Task GetUserAsync_UserExists_ShouldReturnUserData()\n{\n    // Arrange\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    repository.GetByIdAsync(123).Returns(Task.FromResult(\n        new User { Id = 123, Name = \"John\" }));\n\n    var service = new UserService(repository);\n\n    // Act\n    var result = await service.GetUserAsync(123);\n\n    // Assert\n    result.Name.Should().Be(\"John\");\n    await repository.Received(1).GetByIdAsync(123);\n}\n\n[Fact]\npublic async Task SaveUserAsync_DatabaseError_ShouldThrowException()\n{\n    // Arrange\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    repository.SaveAsync(Arg.Any<User>())\n              .Throws(new InvalidOperationException(\"Database error\"));\n\n    var service = new UserService(repository);\n\n    // Act & Assert\n    await service.SaveUserAsync(new User { Name = \"John\" })\n                .Should().ThrowAsync<InvalidOperationException>()\n                .WithMessage(\"Database error\");\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: ILogger Verification\n\nDue to ILogger''s extension method nature, verify the underlying Log method:\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic async Task BackupFileAsync_FileNotExists_ShouldLogWarning()\n{\n    // Arrange\n    var sourcePath = @\"C:\\nonexistent\\test.txt\";\n    _fileSystem.FileExists(sourcePath).Returns(false);\n\n    // Act\n    var result = await _sut.BackupFileAsync(sourcePath, @\"C:\\backup\");\n\n    // Assert\n    result.Success.Should().BeFalse();\n\n    // Verify ILogger.Log method was called correctly\n    _logger.Received(1).Log(\n        LogLevel.Warning,\n        Arg.Any<EventId>(),\n        Arg.Is<object>(v => v.ToString().Contains(\"Source file not found\")),\n        null,\n        Arg.Any<Func<object, Exception, string>>());\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Complex Setup Management\n\nUse base test class to manage shared setup:\n\n```csharp\npublic class OrderServiceTestsBase\n{\n    protected readonly IOrderRepository Repository;\n    protected readonly IEmailService EmailService;\n    protected readonly ILogger<OrderService> Logger;\n    protected readonly OrderService Sut;\n\n    protected OrderServiceTestsBase()\n    {\n        Repository = Substitute.For<IOrderRepository>();\n        EmailService = Substitute.For<IEmailService>();\n        Logger = Substitute.For<ILogger<OrderService>>();\n        Sut = new OrderService(Repository, EmailService, Logger);\n    }\n\n    protected void SetupValidOrder(int orderId = 1)\n    {\n        Repository.GetById(orderId).Returns(\n            new Order { Id = orderId, Status = OrderStatus.Pending });\n    }\n\n    protected void SetupEmailServiceSuccess()\n    {\n        EmailService.SendConfirmation(Arg.Any<string>()).Returns(true);\n    }\n}\n\npublic class OrderServiceTests : OrderServiceTestsBase\n{\n    [Fact]\n    public void ProcessOrder_ValidOrder_ShouldProcessSuccessfully()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        SetupValidOrder();\n        SetupEmailServiceSuccess();\n\n        // Act\n        var result = Sut.ProcessOrder(1);\n\n        // Assert\n        result.Success.Should().BeTrue();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Argument Matching Techniques\n\n### Complex Object Matching\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void CreateOrder_CreateOrder_ShouldSaveCorrectOrderData()\n{\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IOrderRepository>();\n    var service = new OrderService(repository);\n\n    service.CreateOrder(\"Product A\", 5, 100);\n\n    // Verify object properties\n    repository.Received(1).Save(Arg.Is<Order>(o =>\n        o.ProductName == \"Product A\" &&\n        o.Quantity == 5 &&\n        o.Price == 100));\n}\n```\n\n### Argument Capture & Verification\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void RegisterUser_RegisterUser_ShouldGenerateCorrectPasswordHash()\n{\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n    var service = new UserService(repository);\n\n    User capturedUser = null;\n    repository.Save(Arg.Do<User>(u => capturedUser = u));\n\n    service.RegisterUser(\"john@example.com\", \"password123\");\n\n    capturedUser.Should().NotBeNull();\n    capturedUser.Email.Should().Be(\"john@example.com\");\n    capturedUser.PasswordHash.Should().NotBe(\"password123\"); // Should be hashed\n    capturedUser.PasswordHash.Length.Should().BeGreaterThan(20);\n}\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls & Best Practices\n\n### ✅ Recommended Practices\n\n1. **Create Substitute for Interfaces, Not Implementations**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ✅ Correct: Target interface\n    var repository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();\n\n    // ❌ Wrong: Target concrete class (unless virtual members)\n    var repository = Substitute.For<UserRepository>();\n    ```\n\n2. **Use Meaningful Test Data**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ✅ Correct: Clearly expresses intent\n    var user = new User { Id = 123, Name = \"John Doe\", Email = \"john@example.com\" };\n\n    // ❌ Wrong: Meaningless data\n    var user = new User { Id = 1, Name = \"test\", Email = \"a@b.c\" };\n    ```\n\n3. **Avoid Over-Verification**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ✅ Correct: Only verify important behavior\n    _emailService.Received(1).SendWelcomeEmail(Arg.Any<string>());\n\n    // ❌ Wrong: Verify all internal implementation details\n    _repository.Received(1).GetById(123);\n    _repository.Received(1).Update(Arg.Any<User>());\n    _validator.Received(1).Validate(Arg.Any<User>());\n    ```\n\n4. **Clear Distinction Between Mock and Stub**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ✅ Correct: Stub for setting scenario, Mock for verifying behavior\n    var stubRepository = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>(); // Stub\n    var mockLogger = Substitute.For<ILogger>(); // Mock\n\n    stubRepository.GetById(123).Returns(user);\n    service.ProcessUser(123);\n    mockLogger.Received(1).LogInformation(Arg.Any<string>());\n    ```\n\n### ❌ Practices to Avoid\n\n1. **Avoid Mocking Value Types**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ❌ Wrong: DateTime is value type\n    var badDate = Substitute.For<DateTime>();\n\n    // ✅ Correct: Abstract time provider\n    var dateTimeProvider = Substitute.For<IDateTimeProvider>();\n    dateTimeProvider.Now.Returns(new DateTime(2024, 1, 1));\n    ```\n\n2. **Avoid Tight Coupling Between Tests and Implementation**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ❌ Wrong: Test implementation details\n    _repository.Received(1).Query(Arg.Any<string>());\n    _repository.Received(1).Filter(Arg.Any<Expression<Func<User, bool>>>());\n\n    // ✅ Correct: Test behavior results\n    var users = service.GetActiveUsers();\n    users.Should().HaveCount(2);\n    ```\n\n3. **Avoid Overly Complex Setup**\n\n    ```csharp\n    // ❌ Wrong: Too many Substitutes (may violate SRP)\n    var sub1 = Substitute.For<IService1>();\n    var sub2 = Substitute.For<IService2>();\n    var sub3 = Substitute.For<IService3>();\n    var sub4 = Substitute.For<IService4>();\n\n    // ✅ Correct: Reconsider class responsibilities\n    // Consider if violating Single Responsibility Principle, needs refactoring\n    ```\n\n## Identifying Dependencies to Substitute\n\n### Should Substitute\n\n- ✅ External API calls (IHttpClient, IApiClient)\n- ✅ Database operations (IRepository, IDbContext)\n- ✅ File system operations (IFileSystem)\n- ✅ Network communication (IEmailService, IMessageQueue)\n- ✅ Time dependencies (IDateTimeProvider, TimeProvider)\n- ✅ Random number generation (IRandom)\n- ✅ Expensive calculations (IComplexCalculator)\n- ✅ Logging services (ILogger<T>)\n\n### Should Not Substitute\n\n- ❌ Value objects (DateTime, string, int)\n- ❌ Simple data transfer objects (DTO)\n- ❌ Pure function utilities (like AutoMapper''s IMapper, consider real instance)\n- ❌ Framework core classes (unless specific need)\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Q1: How to test classes without interfaces?\n\n**A:** Ensure members to mock are `virtual`:\n\n```csharp\npublic class BaseService\n{\n    public virtual string GetData() => \"real data\";\n}\n\nvar substitute = Substitute.For<BaseService>();\nsubstitute.GetData().Returns(\"test data\");\n```\n\n### Q2: How to verify method call order?\n\n**A:** Use `Received.InOrder()`:\n\n```csharp\nReceived.InOrder(() =>\n{\n    _service.Start();\n    _service.Process();\n    _service.Stop();\n});\n```\n\n### Q3: How to handle out parameters?\n\n**A:** Use `Returns()` with delegate:\n\n```csharp\n_service.TryGetValue(\"key\", out Arg.Any<string>())\n        .Returns(x =>\n        {\n            x[1] = \"value\";\n            return true;\n        });\n```\n\n### Q4: NSubstitute vs Moq - Which to choose?\n\n**A:** NSubstitute advantages:\n\n- More concise, intuitive syntax\n- Gentler learning curve\n- No privacy concerns\n- Sufficient for most testing scenarios\n\nChoose NSubstitute unless:\n\n- Project already uses Moq\n- Need Moq-specific advanced features\n- Team already familiar with Moq syntax\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\nThis skill can be combined with:\n\n- **unit-test-fundamentals**: Unit testing basics and 3A pattern\n- **dependency-injection-testing**: Dependency injection testing strategies\n- **test-naming-conventions**: Test naming conventions\n- **test-output-logging**: ITestOutputHelper and ILogger integration\n- **datetime-testing-timeprovider**: TimeProvider for abstracting time dependencies\n- **filesystem-testing-abstractions**: File system dependency abstraction\n\n## Template Files Reference\n\nThis skill provides these template files:\n\n- `templates/mock-patterns.cs`: Complete Mock/Stub/Spy pattern examples\n- `templates/verification-examples.cs`: Behavior verification and argument matching examples\n\n## Reference Resources\n\n### Original Articles\n\nContent distilled from \"Old-School Software Engineer''s Testing Practice - 30 Day Challenge\" series:\n\n- **Day 07 - Dependency Substitution Introduction: Using NSubstitute**\n  - Ironman article: https://ithelp.ithome.com.tw/articles/10374593\n  - Sample code: https://github.com/kevintsengtw/30Days_in_Testing_Samples/tree/main/day07\n\n### NSubstitute Official\n\n- [NSubstitute Official Website](https://nsubstitute.github.io/)\n- [NSubstitute GitHub](https://github.com/nsubstitute/NSubstitute)\n- [NSubstitute NuGet](https://www.nuget.org/packages/NSubstitute/)\n\n### Test Double Theory\n\n- [XUnit Test Patterns](http://xunitpatterns.com/Test%20Double.html)\n- [Martin Fowler - Test Double](https://martinfowler.com/bliki/TestDouble.html)"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:57:59.721Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for .NET Development Agents needing advanced unit testing and mocking capabilities with NSubstitute","zh":"非常适合需要使用NSubstitute进行高级单元测试和模拟功能的.NET开发代理","ja":"NSubstituteを使用した高度なユニットテストとモッキング機能を必要とする。NET開発エージェントに最適","ko":"NSubstitute를 사용한 고급 단위 테스트 및 모의 기능이 필요한 .NET 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de .NET que necesitan pruebas unitarias avanzadas y capacidades de mocking con NSubstitute","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement .NET ayant besoin de tests unitaires avancés et de capacités de mocking avec NSubstitute","de":"Perfekt für .NET-Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Einheitentests und Mocking-Funktionen mit NSubstitute benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento .NET que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de teste unitário e mocking com NSubstitute","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки .NET, которым необходимы расширенные возможности единичного тестирования и макетирования с помощью NSubstitute","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير .NET الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لاختبار الوحدة وموكنج مع NSubstitute"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage test doubles, isolate dependencies, and verify behavior using NSubstitute, covering all five Test Double types and best practices for dependency isolation and behavior setup","zh":"赋予代理创建和管理测试替身、隔离依赖并使用NSubstitute验证行为的能力，涵盖所有五种测试替身类型和依赖隔离以及行为设置的最佳实践","ja":"エージェントがNSubstituteを使用してテストダブルを作成および管理し、依存関係を分離し、動作を検証する能力を提供する。すべての5種類のテストダブルタイプと依存関係の分離および動作設定のベストプラクティスをカバーする","ko":"에이전트가 NSubstitute를 사용하여 테스트 더블을 생성하고 관리하며 의존성을 분리하고 동작을 검증하는 능력을 부여한다. 모든 5가지 테스트 더블 유형과 의존성 분리 및 동작 설정에 대한 모범 사례를 다룬다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y gestionar test doubles, aislar dependencias y verificar el comportamiento utilizando NSubstitute, cubriendo los cinco tipos de Test Double y las mejores prácticas para el aislamiento de dependencias y la configuración del comportamiento","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des test doubles, d''isoler les dépendances et de vérifier le comportement en utilisant NSubstitute, couvrant les cinq types de Test Double et les meilleures pratiques pour l''isolation des dépendances et la configuration du comportement","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Test-Doubles zu erstellen und zu verwalten, Abhängigkeiten zu isolieren und das Verhalten mit NSubstitute zu überprüfen, wobei alle fünf Test-Double-Typen und die besten Praktiken für Abhängigkeitsisolierung und Verhaltenskonfiguration abgedeckt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e gerenciar testes duplos, isolar dependências e verificar comportamento usando NSubstitute, cobrindo todos os cinco tipos de Test Double e as melhores práticas para isolamento de dependência e configuração de comportamento","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и управлять тестовыми дублерами, изолировать зависимости и проверять поведение с помощью NSubstitute, покрывая все пять типов тестовых дублеров и лучшие практики для изоляции зависимостей и настройки поведения","ar":"يمنح العملاء khảية إنشاء و إدارة اختبارات مزدوجة، عزل التبعيات و التحقق من السلوك باستخدام NSubstitute، و تغطية جميع أنواع اختبار مزدوج الخمسة و أفضل الممارسات لعزل التبعية و إعداد السلوك"},"useCases":{"en":["Isolating dependencies for unit testing using NSubstitute","Creating test doubles for external resources to improve test reliability","Verifying behavior of .NET applications using NSubstitute''s assertion capabilities"],"zh":["使用NSubstitute进行单元测试的依赖隔离","为外部资源创建测试替身以提高测试可靠性","使用NSubstitute的断言功能验证.NET应用程序的行为"],"ja":["NSubstituteを使用したユニットテストの依存関係の分離","外部リソースのテストダブルを作成してテストの信頼性を高める","NSubstituteのアサーション機能を使用して。NETアプリケーションの動作を検証する"],"ko":["NSubstitute를 사용한 단위 테스트의 의존성 분리","외부 리소스의 테스트 더블을 생성하여 테스트의 신뢰성을 높임","NSubstitute의 어서션 기능을 사용하여 .NET 애플리케이션의 동작을 검증"],"es":["Aislar dependencias para pruebas unitarias utilizando NSubstitute","Crear test doubles para recursos externos para mejorar la confiabilidad de las pruebas","Verificar el comportamiento de aplicaciones .NET utilizando las capacidades de afirmación de NSubstitute"],"fr":["Isoler les dépendances pour les tests unitaires en utilisant NSubstitute","Créer des test doubles pour les ressources externes pour améliorer la fiabilité des tests","Vérifier le comportement des applications .NET en utilisant les capacités d''affirmation de NSubstitute"],"de":["Abhängigkeiten für Einheitentests mit NSubstitute isolieren","Test-Doubles für externe Ressourcen erstellen, um die Testzuverlässigkeit zu verbessern","Das Verhalten von .NET-Anwendungen mit den Assert-Funktionen von NSubstitute überprüfen"],"pt":["Isolamento de dependências para teste unitário usando NSubstitute","Criação de testes duplos para recursos externos para melhorar a confiabilidade dos testes","Verificação do comportamento de aplicações .NET usando as capacidades de afirmação do NSubstitute"],"ru":["Изоляция зависимостей для единичного тестирования с помощью NSubstitute","Создание тестовых дублеров для внешних ресурсов для улучшения надежности тестов","Проверка поведения приложений .NET с помощью возможностей утверждения NSubstitute"],"ar":["عزل التبعيات لاختبار الوحدة باستخدام NSubstitute","إنشاء اختبارات مزدوجة للموارد الخارجية لتحسين موثوقية الاختبارات","التحقق من سلوك تطبيقات .NET باستخدام إمكانيات الإثبات من NSubstitute"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET environment","Specific to NSubstitute library","Focused on unit testing and mocking, not integration testing"],"zh":[".NET环境是必需的","特定于NSubstitute库","专注于单元测试和模拟，而不是集成测试"],"ja":[".NET環境が必要","NSubstituteライブラリに特有","ユニットテストとモッキングに焦点を当てており、統合テストではない"],"ko":[".NET 환경이 필요","NSubstitute 라이브러리에 특정","단위 테스트 및 모의에 중점을 두고 통합 테스트는 아님"],"es":["Requiere un entorno .NET","Específico de la biblioteca NSubstitute","Centrado en pruebas unitarias y mocking, no en pruebas de integración"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement .NET","Spécifique à la bibliothèque NSubstitute","Axé sur les tests unitaires et le mocking, et non sur les tests d''intégration"],"de":["Benötigt eine .NET-Umgebung","Spezifisch für die NSubstitute-Bibliothek","Konzentriert sich auf Einheitentests und Mocking, nicht auf Integrationstests"],"pt":["Exige ambiente .NET","Específico para a biblioteca NSubstitute","Focado em teste unitário e mocking, não em teste de integração"],"ru":["Требует среды .NET","Специфичен для библиотеки NSubstitute","Фокусируется на единичном тестировании и макетировании, а не на тестировании интеграции"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة .NET","محدد لمكتبة NSubstitute","مركز على اختبار الوحدة وموكنج، وليس على اختبار التكامل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
