to de perfil"],"ru":["Четкая информационная архитектура","Адаптивный дизайн","Персонализированная верхняя навигация","Компактный список важных ссылок","Место для фотографии профиля"],"ar":["هيكل معلومات واضح","تصميم مستجيب","تنقل 상위 مخصص","قائمة مدمجة من الروابط المهمة","مساحة لصورة الملف الشخصي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["学术主页","开发指南","顶级导航","研究摘要","个人资料照片","关键链接","博客","教学信息"],"ja":["アカデミックホームページ","開発ガイド","トップナビゲーション","研究サマリー","プロフィール写真","重要なリンク","ブログ","教学情報"],"ko":["학술 홈페이지","개발 가이드","상위 내비게이션","연구 요약","프로필 사진","중요한 링크","블로그","교학 정보"],"es":["página académica","investigación","publicaciones","enseñanza","desarrollo web","diseño de sitios web","experiencia del usuario","SEO para académicos","presencia en línea"],"fr":["page académique","recherche","publications","enseignement","développement web","conception de sites web","expérience utilisateur","SEO pour universitaires","présence en ligne"],"de":["akademische Seite","Forschung","Veröffentlichungen","Lehre","Webentwicklung","Webseitengestaltung","Benutzererfahrung","SEO für Wissenschaftler","Online-Präsenz"],"pt":["página de início acadêmica","desenvolvimento web","design responsivo","estrutura de informação","navegação personalizada","lista de links","foto de perfil"],"ru":["персонализированная академическая страница","веб-разработка","адаптивный дизайн","информационная архитектура","персонализированная навигация","список ссылок","фотография профиля"],"ar":["صفحة المنزل الأكاديمي","تطوير الويب","تصميم مستجيب","هيكل المعلومات","تنقل مخصص","قائمة الروابط","صورة الملف الشخصي"]}},"owner":"SBY7219","repo":"homepage","repoPath":"SBY7219/homepage","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.462Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"academic-homepage","description":"Design and maintain a minimal academic personal website using only static HTML and CSS, organizing notes and a static blog.","bodyPreview":"You are helping maintain my academic homepage in this repository.\n\nFollow these guidelines:\n\n1. Information architecture\n   - Provide top navigation with: Home, Research, Publications, Teaching, Notes, Blog, CV, Contact.\n   - The Home section should show:\n     - Name, current position and affiliation.\n     - One-paragraph research summary.\n     - A compact list of key links (email, CV, GitHub, Google Scholar if available).\n     - A visible placeholder for my profile photo (e.g., `/img/profile.jp","body":"You are helping maintain my academic homepage in this repository.\n\nFollow these guidelines:\n\n1. Information architecture\n   - Provide top navigation with: Home, Research, Publications, Teaching, Notes, Blog, CV, Contact.\n   - The Home section should show:\n     - Name, current position and affiliation.\n     - One-paragraph research summary.\n     - A compact list of key links (email, CV, GitHub, Google Scholar if available).\n     - A visible placeholder for my profile photo (e.g., `/img/profile.jpg` with good alt text).\n   - Research / Publications / Teaching can start as simple static pages, but they should have clear headings and room for future content.\n   - The Notes section should organize existing `*.html` notes (e.g., `calculus.html`, `linear_algebra.html`, `logic.html`) into themed groups like:\n     - Mathematics\n     - Programming languages and type theory\n     - Category theory and logic\n     - Miscellaneous\n     Use whatever structure you can infer from filenames and titles.\n\n2. Visual style\n   - Minimal light theme: white or very light background, dark text, and a single accent color used sparingly.\n   - Use a system font stack for body text (e.g., `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif`).\n   - Use consistent spacing scale (e.g., 1rem / 1.5rem / 2rem) for margins and paddings.\n   - Make the layout responsive:\n     - On mobile: stacked layout, navigation collapses into a vertical list.\n     - On larger screens: a centered content column with max width around 800–900px.\n\n3. Implementation rules\n   - Keep everything as static HTML + CSS. No build tools, no bundlers, no JS frameworks.\n   - Prefer semantic HTML5 tags. Use descriptive class names in CSS.\n   - Reuse the existing `styles.css` file; refactor or simplify it as needed.\n   - Keep fonts in the existing `fonts/` directory and only load fonts that are actually used.\n\n4. Notes and blog\n   - Treat `*.html` files whose names look like course or topic notes (for example `calculus.html`, `linear_algebra.html`, `logic.html`, `sicm.html`) as study notes.\n   - Create a `notes.html` (or similar) index page that groups and links to these notes.\n   - Create a `blog.html` index page for future static posts:\n     - Initially, you can add 1–2 sample posts as placeholders with title, date, and short summary.\n     - Link individual posts as separate HTML files under a `blog/` directory.\n\n5. Safety and cleanup\n   - Before deleting or moving any file, propose a cleanup plan:\n     - Category A: essential site assets (index, styles, fonts, key pages).\n     - Category B: intermediate or source files (for example Racket `.rkt` files under `source/`).\n     - Category C: clearly unused or obsolete files, if any.\n   - Ask for explicit confirmation before removing or moving Category B/C files.\n   - Always summarize changes and show high-level `git diff` summaries.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:59:06.049Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Knowledge Agents requiring structured academic information architecture and HTML/CSS templating for homepage maintenance.","zh":"适用于需要结构化学术信息架构和HTML/CSS模板化的知识代理，用于维护首页。","ja":"構造化された学術情報アーキテクチャとHTML/CSSテンプレーティングを必要とするナレッジエージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 학술 정보 아키텍처와 HTML/CSS 템플릿을 필요로 하는 지식 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Conocimiento que requieren una arquitectura de información académica estructurada y templating HTML/CSS para el mantenimiento de la página de inicio.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Connaissance nécessitant une architecture d''information académique structurée et un templating HTML/CSS pour la maintenance de la page d''accueil.","de":"Ideal für Wissensagenten, die eine strukturierte akademische Informationsarchitektur und HTML/CSS-Templating für die Wartung der Startseite benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Conhecimento que exigem arquitetura de informação acadêmica estruturada e modelagem de HTML/CSS para manutenção de página inicial.","ru":"Идеально для агентов знаний, требующих структурированной академической информации и шаблонов HTML/CSS для обслуживания домашней страницы.","ar":"مثالي لعميل المعرفة الذي يتطلب هيكلاً معلوماتياً أكاديمياً منظمًا وتصميمًا إطارًا للصفحة الرئيسية باستخدام HTML/CSS"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to organize academic profiles using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, providing top navigation, research summaries, and compact key links, including integration with GitHub and Google Scholar profiles via HTTPS protocols.","zh":"赋予代理组织学术资料的能力，使用HTML、CSS和JavaScript，提供顶部导航、研究摘要和紧凑的关键链接，包括通过HTTPS协议与GitHub和Google Scholar资料集成。","ja":"HTML、CSS、JavaScriptを使用して、エージェントが学術プロフィールを整理できるようにし、トップナビゲーション、研究サマリー、コンパクトなキーリンクを提供し、HTTPSプロトコル経由でGitHubおよびGoogle Scholarプロフィールと統合します。","ko":"에이전트가 학술 프로필을 조직할 수 있도록 HTML, CSS 및 JavaScript를 사용하여 상단 탐색, 연구 요약 및 컴팩트한 주요 링크를 제공하며 HTTPS 프로토콜을 통해 GitHub 및 Google Scholar 프로필과 통합합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes organizar perfiles académicos utilizando HTML, CSS y JavaScript, proporcionando navegación superior, resúmenes de investigación y enlaces clave compactos, incluyendo la integración con perfiles de GitHub y Google Scholar a través de protocolos HTTPS.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''organiser des profils académiques en utilisant HTML, CSS et JavaScript, en fournissant une navigation supérieure, des résumés de recherche et des liens clés compacts, y compris l''intégration avec des profils GitHub et Google Scholar via des protocoles HTTPS.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, akademische Profile mit HTML, CSS und JavaScript zu organisieren und bietet eine Top-Navigation, Forschungszusammenfassungen und kompakte Schlüssellinks, einschließlich der Integration mit GitHub- und Google-Scholar-Profilen über HTTPS-Protokolle.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a organizar perfis acadêmicos usando HTML, CSS e JavaScript, fornecendo navegação superior, resumos de pesquisa e links-chave compactos, incluindo integração com perfis do GitHub e Google Scholar via protocolos HTTPS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью организовывать академические профили с помощью HTML, CSS и JavaScript, обеспечивая верхнюю навигацию, сводки исследований и компактные ключевые ссылки, включая интеграцию с профилями GitHub и Google Scholar через протоколы HTTPS.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على تنظيم الملفات الشخصية الأكاديمية باستخدام HTML و CSS و JavaScript، وتقديم التنقل العلوي والملخصات البحثية والروابط الرئيسية المضغوطة، بما في ذلك التكامل مع ملفات تعريف GitHub و Google Scholar عبر بروتوكولات HTTPS"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating academic homepage templates with navigation menus","Populating research summaries and key links for faculty members","Integrating profile photos and CV links using HTTP requests"],"zh":["生成带有导航菜单的学术主页模板","为教师成员填充研究摘要和关键链接","使用HTTP请求集成个人资料照片和简历链接"],"ja":["ナビゲーションメニューを持つ学術ホームページテンプレートを生成する","教員メンバーの研究サマリーとキーリンクを埋める","HTTPリクエストを使用してプロファイル写真と履歴書リンクを統合する"],"ko":["탐색 메뉴가 있는 학술 홈페이지 템플릿 생성","교수 회원의 연구 요약 및 주요 링크填充","HTTP 요청을 사용하여 프로필 사진 및 이력서 링크 통합"],"es":["Generar plantillas de página de inicio académica con menús de navegación","Popular resúmenes de investigación y enlaces clave para miembros de la facultad","Integrar fotos de perfil y enlaces de CV utilizando solicitudes HTTP"],"fr":["Générer des modèles de page d''accueil académique avec des menus de navigation","Remplir des résumés de recherche et des liens clés pour les membres de la faculté","Intégrer des photos de profil et des liens de CV en utilisant des requêtes HTTP"],"de":["Erzeugen von Vorlagen für akademische Startseiten mit Navigationsmenüs","Auffüllen von Forschungszusammenfas