":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种高效的技术问题解决方法，强调找到问题的根源","ja":"体系的デバッグは、問題の根本原因を特定することで技術的な問題を解決する方法です","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 것을 강조하는 효율적인 기술 문제 해결 방법입니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para encontrar la causa raíz de los problemas técnicos. Evita soluciones temporales y busca la solución definitiva","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour trouver la cause profonde des problèmes techniques. Évitez les solutions temporaires et cherchez la solution d...","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um die Ursache von technischen Problemen zu finden. Vermeiden Sie temporäre Lösungen und suchen Sie nach der endg...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem eficaz para resolver problemas técnicos, encontrando a causa raiz antes de propor soluções","ru":"Системная отладка - это эффективный подход к решению технических проблем, находя коренную причину перед предложением решений","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو подход فعال لحل المشاكل الفنية، واعثر على السبب الجذري قبل اقتراح الحلول","en":"Electron+Svelte+Cagent brand asset management app"},"definition":{"en":"Electron+Svelte+Cagent brand asset management app"},"features":{"zh":["强调找到问题的根源","避免随机修复和掩盖问题","提高解决问题的效率","适用于任何技术问题","遵循铁律：没有根源调查就不提出修复方案"],"ja":["根本原因を特定することを強調","ランダムな修復と問題の隠蔽を避ける","問題解決の効率を向上させる","あらゆる技術的な問題に適用可能","鉄則：根本原因調査を行わない場合、修復提案はできない"],"ko":["문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 것을 강조","임의의 수정과 문제를 숨기는 것을 피함","문제를 해결하는 효율성을 향상","모든 기술적인 문제에 적용 가능","철칙：근본 원인 조사 없이 수정 제안은 할 수 없음"],"es":["Encontrar la causa raíz de los problemas","Evitar soluciones temporales","Mejorar la eficiencia en la resolución de problemas","Reducir el tiempo de depuración","Incrementar la calidad del código"],"fr":["Trouver la cause profonde des problèmes","Éviter les solutions temporaires","Améliorer l''efficacité dans la résolution de problèmes","Réduire le temps de débogage","Augmenter la qualité du code"],"de":["Die Ursache von Problemen finden","Temporäre Lösungen vermeiden","Die Effizienz bei der Fehlerbehebung verbessern","Die Debugging-Zeit reduzieren","Die Code-Qualität erhöhen"],"pt":["Encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos","Evitar soluções precipitadas","Propor soluções eficazes","Reduzir o tempo de depuração","Melhorar a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Найти коренную причину технических проблем","Избежать поспешных решений","Предложить эффективные решения","Сократить время отладки","Улучшить качество кода"],"ar":["اعثر على السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية","تجنب الحلول العرضية","اقتراح حلول فعالة","تقليل وقت التصحيح","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","根源分析","铁律","高效解决","技术调试","问题解决方法"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","技術的な問題解決","根本原因分析","鉄則","効率的な解決","技術的なデバッグ","問題解決方法"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","근본 원인 분석","철칙","효율적인 해결","기술적인 디버깅","문제 해결 방법"],"es":["depuración sistemática","encontrar la causa raíz","soluciones temporales","eficiencia en la resolución de problemas","tiempo de depuración","calidad del código","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software"],"fr":["débogage systématique","trouver la cause profonde","solutions temporaires","efficacité dans la résolution de problèmes","temps de débogage","qualité du code","développement de logiciels","tests de logiciels"],"de":["systematisches Debugging","die Ursache finden","temporäre Lösungen","Effizienz bei der Fehlerbehebung","Debugging-Zeit","Code-Qualität","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Tests"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","encontrar causa raiz","resolução de problemas","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de código","eficiência de depuração"],"ru":["системная отладка","найти коренную причину","решение проблем","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","эффективность отладки"],"ar":["التصحيح المنهجي","إيجاد السبب الجذري","حل المشاكل","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","فعالية التصحيح"]}},"owner":"alchimie-di-circe","repo":"Extractor-desktop-app","repoPath":"alchimie-di-circe/Extractor-desktop-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.463Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:04:03.206Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing a systematic approach to resolving technical issues in Electron, Svelte, and Cagent brand asset management apps","zh":"非常适合需要系统化方法来解决Electron、Svelte和Cagent品牌资产管理应用程序技术问题的调试代理","ja":"Electron、Svelte、Cagentブランドのアセット管理アプリケーションの技術的な問題を解決するための体系的なアプローチが必要なデバッグエージェントに最適","ko":"Electron, Svelte 및 Cagent 브랜드 자산 관리 애플리케이션의 기술적인 문제를 해결하는 데 체계적인 접근 방식이 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de depuración que necesitan un enfoque sistemático para resolver problemas técnicos en aplicaciones de gestión de activos de marca Electron, Svelte y Cagent.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de débogage ayant besoin d''une approche systématique pour résoudre les problèmes techniques dans les applications de gestion d''actifs de marque Electron, Svelte et Cagent.","de":"Ideal für Debugging-Agents, die einen systematischen Ansatz zur Lösung technischer Probleme in Electron-, Svelte- und Cagent-Brand-Asset-Management-Apps benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Depuração que necessitam de uma abordagem sistemática para resolver problemas técnicos em aplicativos de gestão de ativos de marca Electron, Svelte e Cagent","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов отладки, которым требуется системный подход к решению технических проблем в приложениях для управления брендами Electron, Svelte и Cagent","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التصحيح الذين يحتاجون إلى نهج منهجي لتحليل الأخطاء الفنية في تطبيقات إدارة الأصول التجارية لشركة Electron و Svelte و Cagent"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of bugs and test failures using a rigorous systematic-debugging methodology, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, and adhering to the Iron Law of debugging","zh":"赋予代理识别 Electron、Svelte 和 Cagent 品牌资产管理应用程序中 bug 和测试失败的根本原因的能力，使用严格的系统调试方法，确保在调查根本原因之前不进行修复，并遵守调试的铁律","ja":"Electron、Svelte、Cagentブランドのアセット管理アプリケーションにおけるバグやテストの失敗の根本原因を特定するエージェントをEmpowerするためのrigorousなsystematic-debugging方法論を使用し、根本原因を調査する前に修正をしないことを保証し、デバッグの鉄則に従う","ko":"전자, 스벨트 및 Cagent 브랜드 자산 관리 애플리케이션에서 버그 및 테스트 실패의 근본 원인을 식별할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하는 데 엄격한 체계적인 디버깅 방법론을 사용하며, 근본 원인을 조사하기 전에 수정을 하지 않도록 보장하며, 디버깅의 철칙을 준수","es":"Capacita a los agentes para identificar las causas principales de los errores y las fallas de prueba utilizando una metodología de depuración sistemática rigurosa, garantizando que NO HAY CORRECCIONES SIN UNA INVESTIGACIÓN PREVIA DE LA CAUSA PRINCIPAL, y adhiriéndose a la Ley de Hierro del depuración.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes racines des bogues et des échecs de test en utilisant une méthodologie rigoureuse de débogage systématique, garantissant AUCUNE RÉPARATION SANS ENQUÊTE PRÉALABLE SUR LA CAUSE RACINE, et en adhérant à la Loi de Fer du débogage.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, die Grundursachen von Bugs und Testfehlern mit einer rigorosen systematischen Debugging-Methodik zu identifizieren, stellt sicher, dass KEINE FIXES OHNE VORHERIGE GRUNDURSACHENANALYSE erfolgen, und hält sich an das Eiserne Gesetz des Debuggens.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz de bugs e falhas de teste usando uma metodologia rigorosa de depuração sistemática, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, e aderindo à Lei de Ferro da depuração","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины ошибок и сбоев тестирования с помощью строгой системной методологии отладки, гарантируя НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, и соблюдая Железный Закон отладки","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للأخطاء وFAILURES الاختبار باستخدام منهجية صارمة للتصحيح المنهجي، ويضمن عدم إصلاح بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، والامتثال لقانون الحديد للتصحيح"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures in Electron apps","Identifying root causes of bugs in Svelte components","Resolving technical issues in Cagent brand asset management apps"],"zh":["Electron 应用程序中的测试失败调试","Svelte 组件中的 bug 根本原因识别","Cagent 品牌资产管理应用程序中的技术问题解决"],"ja":["Electronアプリケーションのテスト失敗のデバッグ","Svelteコンポーネントのバグの根本原因の特定","Cagentブランドのアセット管理アプリケーションの技術的な問題の解決"],"ko":["Electron 애플리케이션의 테스트 실패 디버깅","Svelte 컴포넌트의 버그 근본 원인 식별","Cagent 브랜드 자산 관리 애플리케이션의 기술적인 문제 해결"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba en aplicaciones Electron","Identificación de causas principales de errores en componentes Svelte","Resolución de problemas técnicos en aplicaciones de gestión de activos de marca Cagent"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de test dans les applications Electron","Identification des causes racines des bogues dans les composants Svelte","Résolution des problèmes techniques dans les applications de gestion d''actifs de marque Cagent"],"de":["Debugging von Testfehlern in Electron-Apps","Identifizierung von Grundursachen für Fehler in Svelte-Komponenten","Behebung technischer Probleme in Cagent-Brand-Asset-Management-Apps"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste em aplicativos Electron","Identificação de causas raiz de bugs em componentes Svelte","Resolução de problemas técnicos em aplicativos de gestão de ativos de marca Cagent"],"ru":["Отладка сбоев тестирования в приложениях Electron","Выявление коренных причин ошибок в компонентах Svelte","Решение технических проблем в приложениях для управления брендами Cagent"],"ar":["تصحيح اخطاء الفشل في تطبيقات Electron","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للأخطاء في مكونات Svelte","حل المشاكل الفنية في تطبيقات إدارة الأصول التجارية لشركة Cagent"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the systematic-debugging methodology","Violating the letter of the process is considered a violation of the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守系统调试方法论","违反过程的字母被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["systematic-debugging方法論への従順が必要","プロセスの文字违反はデバッグの精神への違反とみなされる"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 방법론을 준수해야 함","프로세스의 문자 위반은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere adherencia a la metodología de depuración sistemática","Violar la letra del proceso se considera una violación del espíritu del depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la méthodologie de débogage systématique","Enfreindre la lettre du processus est considéré comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der systematischen Debugging-Methodik","Das Verletzen des Buchstabens des Prozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes des Debuggens"],"pt":["Exige adesão à metodologia de depuração sistemática","Violar a letra do processo é considerado violação do espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения системной методологии отладки","Нарушение буквы процесса считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمنهجية التصحيح المنهجي","الانتهاك حرفيًا للعملية يُعتبر انتهاكًا لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
