y convertir a los clientes en motores de crecimiento","fr":"Les programmes de parrainage et d''affiliation permettent aux entreprises de booster la croissance virale et de transformer les clients en moteurs de croissance","de":"Empfehlungs- und Affiliate-Programme ermöglichen es Unternehmen, das virale Wachstum zu fördern und Kunden in Wachstumsmotoren zu verwandeln","pt":"Desenvolva programas de recomendação para impulsionar o crescimento viral e transformar clientes em motores de crescimento","ru":"Разработайте программы рефералов для стимулирования вирусного роста и превращения клиентов в двигатели роста","ar":"طور برامج إحالة لتعزيز النمو الفيروسي وتحويل العملاء إلى محركات نمو","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["设计和优化推荐计划","将客户转变为增长引擎","推动业务发展","提高客户忠诚度","增加口碑营销","数据驱动的决策"],"ja":["リファラルプログラムの設計と最適化","顧客を成長エンジンに変える","ビジネスを成長させる","顧客忠誠度の向上","口コミマーケティングの増加","データドリブンの意思決定"],"ko":["리퍼럴 프로그램 설계 및 최적화","고객을 성장 엔진으로 바꾸는","비즈니스 성장에 기여","고객 충성도 향상","口碑 마케팅 증가","데이터 기반 의사 결정"],"es":["Diseño de programas de referidos personalizados","Optimización de la experiencia del cliente","Integración con plataformas de marketing existentes","Análisis y seguimiento de resultados","Incentivos y recompensas para los clientes","Automatización de procesos de referido"],"fr":["Conception de programmes de parrainage sur mesure","Optimisation de l''expérience client","Intégration avec les plateformes de marketing existantes","Analyse et suivi des résultats","Incitations et récompenses pour les clients","Automatisation des processus de parrainage"],"de":["Entwurf von maßgeschneiderten Empfehlungsprogrammen","Optimierung der Kundenerfahrung","Integration mit bestehenden Marketingplattformen","Analyse und Verfolgung von Ergebnissen","Anreize und Belohnungen für Kunden","Automatisierung von Empfehlungsprozessen"],"pt":["Otimização de crescimento viral","Transformação de clientes em motores de crescimento","Desenvolvimento de programas de recomendação personalizados","Análise de resultados e ajustes para melhorar o desempenho","Integração com estratégias de marketing existentes","Monitoramento e avaliação do sucesso do programa"],"ru":["Оптимизация вирусного роста","Превращение клиентов в двигатели роста","Разработка индивидуальных программ рефералов","Анализ результатов и корректировки для улучшения производительности","Интеграция с существующими маркетинговыми стратегиями","Мониторинг и оценка успеха программы"],"ar":["تحسين النمو الفيروسي","تحويل العملاء إلى محركات نمو","تطوير برامج إحالة مخصصة","تحليل النتائج وتعديلات لتحسين الأداء","التكامل مع الاستراتيجيات التسويقية الحالية","مراقبة وتقييم نجاح البرنامج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["推荐计划","增长黑客","营销策略","客户忠诚度","口碑营销","数据分析","业务增长","增长引擎"],"ja":["リファラルプログラム","成長ハック","マーケティング戦略","顧客忠誠度","口コミマーケティング","データ分析","ビジネス成長","成長エンジン"],"ko":["리퍼럴 프로그램","성장 해킹","마케팅 전략","고객 충성도","口碑 마케팅","데이터 분석","비즈니스 성장","성장 엔진"],"es":["programas de referidos","marketing de afiliados","crecimiento viral","estrategias de marketing","experiencia del cliente","automatización de marketing","análisis de resultados","incentivos para clientes","recompensas para clientes"],"fr":["programmes de parrainage","marketing d''affiliation","croissance virale","stratégies de marketing","expérience client","automatisation du marketing","analyse des résultats","incitations pour les clients","récompenses pour les clients"],"de":["Empfehlungsprogramme","Affiliate-Marketing","virales Wachstum","Marketingstrategien","Kundenerfahrung","Marketingautomatisierung","Ergebnisanalyse","Anreize für Kunden","Belohnungen für Kunden"],"pt":["programa de recomendação","crescimento viral","marketing de referência","desenvolvimento de programas de recomendação","otimização de crescimento","transformação de clientes","análise de resultados","integração com marketing"],"ru":["программа рефералов","вирусный рост","маркетинг рефералов","разработка программ рефералов","оптимизация роста","превращение клиентов","анализ результатов","интеграция с маркетингом"],"ar":["برنامج الإحالة","النمو الفيروسي","تسويق الإحالة","تطوير برامج الإحالة","تحسين النمو","تحويل العملاء","تحليل النتائج","التكامل مع التسويق"]}},"owner":"nadavyigal","repo":"Running-coach-","repoPath":"nadavyigal/Running-coach-","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"referral-program","description":"When the user wants to create, optimize, or analyze a referral program, affiliate program, or word-of-mouth strategy. Also use when the user mentions referral, affiliate, ambassador, word of mouth, viral loop, refer a friend, or partner program. This skill covers program design, incentive structure, and growth optimization.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Referral & Affiliate Programs\n\nYou are an expert in viral growth and referral marketing. Your goal is to help design and optimize programs that turn customers into growth engines.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Program Type\n- Customer","body":"# Referral & Affiliate Programs\n\nYou are an expert in viral growth and referral marketing. Your goal is to help design and optimize programs that turn customers into growth engines.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Program Type\n- Customer referral program, affiliate program, or both?\n- B2B or B2C?\n- What''s the average customer LTV?\n- What''s your current CAC from other channels?\n\n### 2. Current State\n- Existing referral/affiliate program?\n- Current referral rate (% who refer)?\n- What incentives have you tried?\n\n### 3. Product Fit\n- Is your product shareable?\n- Does it have network effects?\n- Do customers naturally talk about it?\n\n### 4. Resources\n- Tools/platforms you use or consider?\n- Budget for referral incentives?\n\n---\n\n## Referral vs. Affiliate\n\n### Customer Referral Programs\n\n**Best for:**\n- Existing customers recommending to their network\n- Products with natural word-of-mouth\n- Lower-ticket or self-serve products\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Referrer is an existing customer\n- One-time or limited rewards\n- Higher trust, lower volume\n\n### Affiliate Programs\n\n**Best for:**\n- Reaching audiences you don''t have access to\n- Content creators, influencers, bloggers\n- Higher-ticket products that justify commissions\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Affiliates may not be customers\n- Ongoing commission relationship\n- Higher volume, variable trust\n\n---\n\n## Referral Program Design\n\n### The Referral Loop\n\n```\nTrigger Moment → Share Action → Convert Referred → Reward → (Loop)\n```\n\n### Step 1: Identify Trigger Moments\n\n**High-intent moments:**\n- Right after first \"aha\" moment\n- After achieving a milestone\n- After exceptional support\n- After renewing or upgrading\n\n### Step 2: Design Share Mechanism\n\n**Ranked by effectiveness:**\n1. In-product sharing (highest conversion)\n2. Personalized link\n3. Email invitation\n4. Social sharing\n5. Referral code (works offline)\n\n### Step 3: Choose Incentive Structure\n\n**Single-sided rewards** (referrer only): Simpler, works for high-value products\n\n**Double-sided rewards** (both parties): Higher conversion, win-win framing\n\n**Tiered rewards**: Gamifies referral process, increases engagement\n\n**For examples and incentive sizing**: See [references/program-examples.md](references/program-examples.md)\n\n---\n\n## Program Optimization\n\n### Improving Referral Rate\n\n**If few customers are referring:**\n- Ask at better moments\n- Simplify sharing process\n- Test different incentive types\n- Make referral prominent in product\n\n**If referrals aren''t converting:**\n- Improve landing experience for referred users\n- Strengthen incentive for new users\n- Ensure referrer''s endorsement is visible\n\n### A/B Tests to Run\n\n**Incentive tests:** Amount, type, single vs. double-sided, timing\n\n**Messaging tests:** Program description, CTA copy, landing page copy\n\n**Placement tests:** Where and when the referral prompt appears\n\n### Common Problems & Fixes\n\n| Problem | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Low awareness | Add prominent in-app prompts |\n| Low share rate | Simplify to one click |\n| Low conversion | Optimize referred user experience |\n| Fraud/abuse | Add verification, limits |\n| One-time referrers | Add tiered/gamified rewards |\n\n---\n\n## Measuring Success\n\n### Key Metrics\n\n**Program health:**\n- Active referrers (referred someone in last 30 days)\n- Referral conversion rate\n- Rewards earned/paid\n\n**Business impact:**\n- % of new customers from referrals\n- CAC via referral vs. other channels\n- LTV of referred customers\n- Referral program ROI\n\n### Typical Findings\n\n- Referred customers have 16-25% higher LTV\n- Referred customers have 18-37% lower churn\n- Referred customers refer others at 2-3x rate\n\n---\n\n## Launch Checklist\n\n### Before Launch\n- [ ] Define program goals and success metrics\n- [ ] Design incentive structure\n- [ ] Build or configure referral tool\n- [ ] Create referral landing page\n- [ ] Set up tracking and attribution\n- [ ] Define fraud prevention rules\n- [ ] Create terms and conditions\n- [ ] Test complete referral flow\n\n### Launch\n- [ ] Announce to existing customers\n- [ ] Add in-app referral prompts\n- [ ] Update website with program details\n- [ ] Brief support team\n\n### Post-Launch (First 30 Days)\n- [ ] Review conversion funnel\n- [ ] Identify top referrers\n- [ ] Gather feedback\n- [ ] Fix friction points\n- [ ] Send reminder emails to non-referrers\n\n---\n\n## Email Sequences\n\n### Referral Program Launch\n\n```\nSubject: You can now earn [reward] for sharing [Product]\n\nWe just launched our referral program!\n\nShare [Product] with friends and earn [reward] for each signup.\nThey get [their reward] too.\n\n[Unique referral link]\n\n1. Share your link\n2. Friend signs up\n3. You both get [reward]\n```\n\n### Referral Nurture Sequence\n\n- Day 7: Remind about referral program\n- Day 30: \"Know anyone who''d benefit?\"\n- Day 60: Success story + referral prompt\n- After milestone: \"You achieved [X]—know others who''d want this?\"\n\n---\n\n## Affiliate Programs\n\n**For detailed affiliate program design, commission structures, recruitment, and tools**: See [references/affiliate-programs.md](references/affiliate-programs.md)\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What type of program (referral, affiliate, or both)?\n2. What''s your customer LTV and current CAC?\n3. Existing program or starting from scratch?\n4. What tools/platforms are you considering?\n5. What''s your budget for rewards/commissions?\n6. Is your product naturally shareable?\n\n---\n\n## Tool Integrations\n\nFor implementation, see the [tools registry](../../tools/REGISTRY.md). Key tools for referral programs:\n\n| Tool | Best For | Guide |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| **Rewardful** | Stripe-native affiliate programs | [rewardful.md](../../tools/integrations/rewardful.md) |\n| **Tolt** | SaaS affiliate programs | [tolt.md](../../tools/integrations/tolt.md) |\n| **Mention Me** | Enterprise referral programs | [mention-me.md](../../tools/integrations/mention-me.md) |\n| **Dub.co** | Link tracking and attribution | [dub-co.md](../../tools/integrations/dub-co.md) |\n| **Stripe** | Payment processing (for commission tracking) | [stripe.md](../../tools/integrations/stripe.md) |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **launch-strategy**: For launching referral program effectively\n- **email-sequence**: For referral nurture campaigns\n- **marketing-psychology**: For understanding referral motivation\n- **analytics-tracking**: For tracking referral attribution\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:17:32.188Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Growth-Hacking Agents specializing in viral marketing and customer acquisition strategies.","zh":"非常适合专注于病毒式营销和客户获取策略的增长黑客代理","ja":"ウイルスマーケティングと顧客獲得戦略を専門とする成長ハッキングエージェントに最適","ko":"바이러스 마케팅과 고객 확보 전략을 전문으로 하는 성장 해킹 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Growth-Hacking especializados en marketing viral y estrategias de adquisición de clientes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de Growth-Hacking spécialisés dans le marketing viral et les stratégies d''acquisition de clients.","de":"Perfekt für Growth-Hacking-Agenten, die sich auf virales Marketing und Kundenakquise-Strategien spezialisieren.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Growth-Hacking especializados em marketing viral e estratégias de aquisição de clientes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Growth-Hacking, специализирующихся на вирусном маркетинге и стратегиях приобретения клиентов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل Growth-Hacking المتخصص في التسويق الفيروسي و استراتيجيات الحصول على العملاء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and optimize referral programs using product marketing context, driving customer engagement and conversion through viral growth loops and affiliate marketing strategies.","zh":"赋予代理设计和优化推荐计划的能力，利用产品营销背景，通过病毒式增长环和联盟营销策略驱动客户参与和转化","ja":"プロダクトマーケティングのコンテキストを利用して、リファラルプログラムを設計・最適化し、ウイルス的な成長ループやアフィリエイトマーケティング戦略を通じてカスタマーエンゲージメントとコンバージョンを促進するエージェントの能力を高める","ko":"제품 마케팅.context를 활용하여 추천 프로그램을 설계하고 최적화하며, 바이러스 성장 루프와 아피리 에이트 마케팅 전략을 통해 고객 참여와 전환을 驅動하는 에이전트의 능력을 강화","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar y optimizar programas de referencia utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos, impulsando la participación y conversión del cliente a través de bucles de crecimiento viral y estrategias de marketing de afiliados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et d''optimiser des programmes de référence en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits, en stimulant l''engagement et la conversion client à travers des boucles de croissance virale et des stratégies de marketing d''affiliation.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Referenzprogramme unter Verwendung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts zu entwerfen und zu optimieren, die Kundenbeteiligung und -umwandlung durch virale Wachstumsschleifen und Affiliate-Marketing-Strategien antreiben.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar e otimizar programas de referência usando o contexto de marketing de produtos, impulsionando o engajamento e a conversão do cliente por meio de loops de crescimento viral e estratégias de marketing de afiliados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать и оптимизировать программы рекомендаций с использованием контекста маркетинга продукции, стимулируя вовлеченность и конверсию клиентов за счет вирусных циклов роста и стратегий партнерского маркетинга.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تصميم و تحسين برامج الإحالة باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتجات، مما يدفع التفاعل و التحويل للعملاء من خلال الحلقات النمو الفيروسي و استراتيجيات التسويق التابع."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing incentive structures for customer referrals","Optimizing program metrics for viral growth","Developing affiliate marketing campaigns"],"zh":["为客户推荐设计激励结构","优化程序指标以实现病毒式增长","开发联盟营销活动"],"ja":["カスタマーリファラルのインセンティブ構造を設計する","ウイルス的な成長を実現するためのプログラムメトリクスの最適化","アフィリエイトマーケティングキャンペーンの開発"],"ko":["고객 추천을 위한 인센티브 구조 설계","바이러스 성장 루프를 위한 프로그램 메트릭스 최적화","아피리 에이트 마케팅 캠페인 개발"],"es":["Diseñar estructuras de incentivos para referencias de clientes","Optimizar las métricas del programa para el crecimiento viral","Desarrollar campañas de marketing de afiliados"],"fr":["Concevoir des structures d''incitation pour les références client","Optimiser les métriques du programme pour la croissance virale","Développer des campagnes de marketing d''affiliation"],"de":["Entwerfen von Anreizstrukturen für Kundenreferenzen","Optimieren von Programm-Metriken für virales Wachstum","Entwickeln von Affiliate-Marketing-Kampagnen"],"pt":["Projeto de estruturas de incentivo para referências de clientes","Otimização de métricas de programa para crescimento viral","Desenvolvimento de campanhas de marketing de afiliados"],"ru":["Проектирование структур стимулирования для рекомендаций клиентов","Оптимизация метрик программы для вирусного роста","Разработка кампаний партнерского маркетинга"],"ar":["تصميم هياكل الحفーズ للعملاء المراجعين","تحسين معايير البرامج للنمو الفيروسي","تطوير حملات التسويق التابع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires product marketing context","Dependent on existing customer base"],"zh":["需要产品营销背景","依赖于现有的客户基础"],"ja":["プロダクトマーケティングのコンテキストが必要","既存のカスタマーベースに依存する"],"ko":["제품 마케팅.context가 필요","기존 고객 기반에 의존"],"es":["Requiere contexto de marketing de productos","Depende de la base de clientes existente"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte de marketing de produits","Dépend de la base de clients existante"],"de":["Benötigt Produktmarketing-Kontext","Hängt von der bestehenden Kundenbasis ab"],"pt":["Exige contexto de marketing de produtos","Depende da base de clientes existente"],"ru":["Требует контекста маркетинга продукции","Зависит от существующей базы клиентов"],"ar":["يتطلب سياق تسويق المنتجات","يعتمد على قاعدة العملاء الحالية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('a2f0/tearleads/preen-typescript', 'community', 'a2f0', 'tearleads', 'a2f0/tearleads', 'preen-typescript', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z', '2026-02-18T08:17:31.302Z', NULL, '{"id":"a2f0/tearleads/preen-typescript","name":"preen-typescript","description":{"zh":"TypeScript ","ja":"TypeScript ","ko":"TypeScript ","es":"Preen TypeScript es una herramienta que busca y corrige problemas de seguridad de tipos en el código, mejorando la calidad y la seguridad del mismo","fr":"Preen TypeScript est un outil qui recherche et corrige les problèmes de sécurité de types dans le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la sécurité du code","de":"Preen TypeScript ist ein Tool, das Sicherheitsprobleme von Typen im Code sucht und behebt, wodurch die Codequalität und -sicherheit verbessert werden","pt":"O Preen TypeScript é uma ferramenta que proativamente busca e fortalece tipagens fracas em monorepos, melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Preen TypeScript - это инструмент, который проactively ищет и укрепляет слабые типизации в монорепозиториях, улучшая качество кода","ar":"برين تايب سكريبت هو أداة تبحث بشكل نشط و تعزز التصنيفات الضعيفة في مونو ريبوزиторيز، مما يحسن جودة الكود","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TypeScript ","ja":"TypeScript ","ko":"TypeScript ","es":"Preen TypeScript: Mejora la calidad del código","fr":"Preen TypeScript: Améliorez la qualité du code","de":"Preen TypeScript: Verbessern Sie die Codequalität","pt":"Preen TypeScript: Otimização de Tipagens","ru":"Preen TypeScript: Улучшение Типизаций","ar":"برين تايب سكريبت: تحسين التصنيفات","en":"preen-typescript"},"description":{"zh":"TypeScript ","ja":"TypeScript ","ko":"TypeScript ","es":"Preen TypeScript es una herramienta que busca y corrige problemas de seguridad de tipos en el código, mejorando la calidad y la seguridad del mismo","fr":"Preen TypeScript est un outil qui recherche et corrige les problèmes de sécurité de types dans le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la sécurité du code","de":"Preen TypeScript ist ein Tool, das Sicherheitsprobleme von Typen im Code sucht und behebt, wodurch die Codequalität und -sicherheit verbessert werden","pt":"O Preen TypeScript é uma ferramenta que proativamente busca e fortalece tipagens fracas em monorepos, melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Preen TypeScript - это инструмент, который проactively ищет и укрепляет слабые типизации в монорепозиториях, улучшая качество кода","ar":"برين تايب سكريبت هو أداة تبحث بشكل نشط و تعزز التصنيفات الضعيفة في مونو ريبوزиторيز، مما يحسن جودة الكود","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore/@ts-expect-error"],"ja":["TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore/@ts-expect-error"],"ko":["TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore/@ts-expect-error"],"es":["Búsqueda de archivos con problemas de seguridad de tipos","Corrección de tipos `any` y `unknown`","Eliminación de comentarios `@ts-ignore` y `@ts-expect-error`","Mejora de la calidad y seguridad del código","Análisis de código en proyectos monorepo"],"fr":["Recherche de fichiers avec des problèmes de sécurité de types","Correction des types `any` et `unknown`","Élimination des commentaires `@ts-ignore` et `@ts-expect-error`","Amélioration de la qualité et de la sécurité du code","Analyse de code dans les projets monorepo"],"de":["Suche nach Dateien mit Sicherheitsproblemen von Typen","Korrektur von `any`- und `unknown`-Typen","Entfernung von Kommentaren `@ts-ignore` und `@ts-expect-error`","Verbesserung der Codequalität und -sicherheit","Code-Analyse in monorepo-Projekten"],"pt":["Proativamente busca tipagens fracas em monorepos","Substitui `any` por tipagens mais específicas","Reduz `unknown` para tipagens mais seguras","Remove casts `as` inseguros","Elimina comentários `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`"],"ru":["Проactively ищет слабые типизации в монорепозиториях","Заменяет `any` на более конкретные типизации","Уменьшает `unknown` до более безопасных типизаций","Удаляет небезопасные касты `as`","Удаляет комментарии `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`"],"ar":["تبحث بشكل نشط عن التصنيفات الضعيفة في مونو ريبوزиторيز","تحل محل `any` بالتصنيفات الأكثر تحديدا","تقلل من `unknown` إلى تصنيفات أكثر أمانا","تزيل التصنيفات غير الآمنة `as`","تزيل التعليقات `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TypeScript","TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore","@ts-expect-error"],"ja":["TypeScript","TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore","@ts-expect-error"],"ko":["TypeScript","TypeScript ","any","unknown","as ","@ts-ignore","@ts-expect-error"],"es":["Preen TypeScript","seguridad de tipos","análisis de código","TypeScript","monorepo","calidad del código","seguridad del código"],"fr":["Preen TypeScript","sécurité de types","analyse de code","TypeScript","monorepo","qualité du code","sécurité du code"],"de":["Preen TypeScript","Sicherheit von Typen","Code-Analyse","TypeScript","monorepo","Codequalität","Codesicherheit"],"pt":["Preen TypeScript","Otimização de tipagens","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Monorepos","TypeScript","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Preen TypeScript","Улучшение типизаций","Улучшение качества кода","Монорепозитории","TypeScript","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["برين تايب سكريبت","تحسين التصنيفات","تحسين جودة الكود","مونو ريبوزиторيز","تايب سكريبت","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"a2f0","repo":"tearleads","repoPath":"a2f0/tearleads","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"preen-typescript","description":"Proactively search the monorepo for weak TypeScript typings and strengthen them by replacing `any`, narrowing `unknown`, removing unsafe `as` casts, and eliminating `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error` comments. Use when maintaining code quality or during slack time.","bodyPreview":"# Preen TypeScript Types\n\nProactively search the monorepo for weak TypeScript typings and strengthen them by replacing `any`, narrowing `unknown`, removing unsafe `as` casts, and eliminating `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error` comments.\n\n## When to Run\n\nRun this skill when maintaining code quality or during slack time. It searches the entire codebase for type safety improvements.\n\n## Discovery Phase\n\nSearch all packages for files with type safety issues:\n\n```bash\n# Find files with `any` type annotat","body":"# Preen TypeScript Types\n\nProactively search the monorepo for weak TypeScript typings and strengthen them by replacing `any`, narrowing `unknown`, removing unsafe `as` casts, and eliminating `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error` comments.\n\n## When to Run\n\nRun this skill when maintaining code quality or during slack time. It searches the entire codebase for type safety improvements.\n\n## Discovery Phase\n\nSearch all packages for files with type safety issues:\n\n```bash\n# Find files with `any` type annotations\nrg -n --glob ''*.{ts,tsx}'' '': any|: any\\[\\]|<any>|as any'' . | wc -l\n\n# List specific files with `any`\nrg -l --glob ''*.{ts,tsx}'' '': any|: any\\[\\]|<any>|as any'' . | head -20\n\n# Find `as` type assertions (potential unsafe casts)\nrg -n --glob ''*.{ts,tsx}'' '' as [A-Z]'' . | rg -v ''\\.test\\.'' | head -20\n\n# Find ts-ignore and ts-expect-error comments\nrg -n --glob ''*.{ts,tsx}'' ''@ts-ignore|@ts-expect-error'' . | head -20\n\n# Find `unknown` that might need narrowing\nrg -n --glob ''*.{ts,tsx}'' '': unknown'' . | head -20\n```\n\n## Prioritization\n\nFix issues in this order (highest impact first):\n\n1. **`any` in function signatures** - Parameters and return types affect all callers\n2. **`any` in exported interfaces/types** - Affects consuming code across the codebase\n3. **`as` casts that bypass type checking** - Often hide real bugs\n4. **`@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`** - Usually indicate underlying issues\n5. **`any` in local variables** - Lower impact but still worth fixing\n6. **`unknown` that needs narrowing** - Usually safe but could be more precise\n\n## Replacement Strategies\n\n### Replacing `any`\n\n1. **Infer from usage**: Look at how the value is used to determine the correct type\n2. **Use generics**: Replace `any` with type parameters when the type varies\n3. **Use union types**: When a value can be one of several known types\n4. **Use `unknown`**: When the type is truly unknown at compile time (then narrow it)\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nfunction process(data: any): any { ... }\n\n// After - with proper types\nfunction process(data: UserInput): ProcessedResult { ... }\n\n// After - with generics\nfunction process<T extends BaseData>(data: T): ProcessedData<T> { ... }\n```\n\n### Replacing `as` Casts\n\n1. **Use type guards**: Write functions that narrow types safely\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nconst user = response.data as User;\n\n// After - with type guard\nfunction isUser(value: unknown): value is User {\n  if (typeof value !== ''object'' || value === null) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  const obj = value as Record<string, unknown>;\n  return (\n    typeof obj.id === ''string'' &&\n    typeof obj.email === ''string''\n  );\n}\n\nif (isUser(response.data)) {\n  const user = response.data; // Type is narrowed to User\n}\n```\n\n1. **Use assertion functions**: For cases where you want to throw on invalid data\n\n```typescript\nfunction assertIsUser(value: unknown): asserts value is User {\n  if (!isUser(value)) {\n    throw new Error(''Expected User object'');\n  }\n}\n```\n\n1. **Fix the source**: Often the upstream type is wrong and should be fixed there\n\n### Eliminating `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`\n\n1. **Fix the actual type error**: Usually the right solution\n2. **Update type definitions**: If the types are wrong\n3. **Add proper overloads**: If the function signature is incomplete\n4. **Use type assertions as last resort**: With a comment explaining why\n\n```typescript\n// Before\n// @ts-ignore - TODO fix this\nconst result = someFunction(data);\n\n// After - fix the root cause\nconst result = someFunction(data as ExpectedType); // Temporary: upstream types are incorrect, see issue #123\n```\n\n### Narrowing `unknown`\n\nUse type guards, `typeof`, `instanceof`, or discriminated unions:\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nfunction handle(error: unknown) {\n  console.log(error.message); // Error: ''unknown'' has no property ''message''\n}\n\n// After\nfunction handle(error: unknown) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.log(error.message);\n  } else if (typeof error === ''string'') {\n    console.log(error);\n  } else {\n    console.log(''Unknown error:'', String(error));\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Validating Network/Storage Data\n\nAlways validate data from external sources (SSE, WebSocket, Redis, localStorage):\n\n```typescript\n// Before - trusting external data\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(data) as StoredUser;\n\n// After - validate before use\ninterface StoredUser {\n  id: string;\n  email: string;\n}\n\nfunction isStoredUser(value: unknown): value is StoredUser {\n  return (\n    isRecord(value) &&\n    typeof value[''id''] === ''string'' &&\n    typeof value[''email''] === ''string''\n  );\n}\n\nconst parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(data);\nif (!isStoredUser(parsed)) {\n  return null; // or throw\n}\n// parsed is now safely typed as StoredUser\n```\n\n### Cleaner Global Type Access\n\nUse `globalThis` with a typed intersection instead of `window as unknown as {...}`:\n\n```typescript\n// Before - verbose and uses `unknown`\nconst handlers = (\n  window as unknown as {\n    __messageHandler?: Map<string, (msg: Message) => void>;\n  }\n).__messageHandler;\n\n// After - cleaner with globalThis\ntype MessageHandlerRegistry = Map<string, (msg: Message) => void>;\n\nconst handlers = (\n  globalThis as { __messageHandler?: MessageHandlerRegistry }\n).__messageHandler;\n```\n\n## Type Guard Patterns\n\nPlace type guards in a shared location when used across files:\n\n```text\npackages/shared/src/typeGuards/\n  user.ts          # isUser, assertIsUser\n  api.ts           # isApiResponse, isApiError\n  index.ts         # Re-exports\n```\n\n### Standard Type Guard Template\n\n```typescript\nexport function isTypeName(value: unknown): value is TypeName {\n  if (typeof value !== ''object'' || value === null) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const obj = value as Record<string, unknown>;\n\n  return (\n    typeof obj.requiredField === ''string'' &&\n    (obj.optionalField === undefined || typeof obj.optionalField === ''number'')\n  );\n}\n\nexport function assertIsTypeName(value: unknown): asserts value is TypeName {\n  if (!isTypeName(value)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`Expected TypeName, got: ${JSON.stringify(value)}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Discovery**: Run discovery commands to identify candidates across all packages.\n2. **Selection**: Choose a file or category with high-impact type issues.\n3. **Create branch**: `git checkout -b refactor/typescript-<area>`\n4. **Fix types**: Apply replacement strategies, starting with highest impact.\n5. **Add type guards**: Create reusable type guards for complex types.\n6. **Validate**: Run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` to ensure no regressions.\n7. **Run tests**: Ensure all tests still pass.\n8. **Commit and merge**: Run `$commit-and-push`, then `$enter-merge-queue`.\n\nIf no high-value fixes were found during discovery, do not create a branch or run commit/merge workflows.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not change runtime behavior unless fixing a bug\n- Do not introduce new `any`, `as`, or `@ts-ignore`\n- Prefer gradual improvement over big-bang rewrites\n- Keep PRs focused on one area or pattern\n- Add tests for new type guards\n- Document non-obvious type decisions with comments\n\n## Quality Bar\n\n- Zero new `any` types introduced\n- All type guards have corresponding tests\n- No regression in type coverage\n- All existing tests pass\n- Lint and typecheck pass\n\n## PR Strategy\n\nUse incremental PRs by category:\n\n- PR 1: Fix `any` in shared types/interfaces\n- PR 2: Add type guards for API responses\n- PR 3: Remove `as` casts in specific feature area\n- PR 4: Eliminate `@ts-ignore` comments\n\nIn each PR description, include:\n\n- What category of type issues were fixed\n- Files changed and why\n- Any new type guards added\n- Test evidence\n\n## Token Efficiency\n\nDiscovery commands can return many lines. Always limit output:\n\n```bash\n# Count first, then list limited results\nrg -l ... | wc -l                 # Get count\nrg -l ... | head -20              # Then sample\n\n# Suppress verbose validation output\npnpm typecheck >/dev/null\npnpm lint >/dev/null\npnpm test >/dev/null\ngit commit -S -m \"message\" >/dev/null\ngit push >/dev/null\n```\n\nOn failure, re-run without suppression to see errors.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:17:31.302Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Maintenance Agents needing advanced TypeScript type safety improvements.","zh":"非常适合需要高级TypeScript类型安全改进的代码维护代理。","ja":"TypeScriptの型安全性の強化が必要なコードメンテナンスエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 TypeScript 타입 안전성 개선을 필요로 하는 코드 유지 보수 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de mantenimiento de código que necesitan mejoras avanzadas de seguridad de tipos TypeScript.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de maintenance de code nécessitant des améliorations avancées de sécurité de types TypeScript.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Wartungsagenten, die erweiterte TypeScript-Typensicherheitsverbesserungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Manutenção de Código que precisam de melhorias avançadas de segurança de tipo TypeScript.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по техническому обслуживанию кода, которым необходимы продвинутые улучшения безопасности типов TypeScript.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات صيانة الشفرة التي تحتاج إلى تحسينات متقدمة لأمان أنواع TypeScript."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to proactively strengthen TypeScript typings by replacing ''any'' types, narrowing ''unknown'' types, removing unsafe ''as'' casts, and eliminating ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'' comments, ensuring robust code quality and type safety.","zh":"赋予代理主动加强TypeScript类型检查的能力，通过替换''any''类型，缩小''unknown''类型，移除不安全的''as''强制类型转换，并消除''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error''注释，确保代码质量和类型安全的强健性。","ja":"エージェントにTypeScriptの型チェックを強化する能力を与え、''any''型の置き換え、''unknown''型の狭義化、安全でない''as''キャストの削除、および''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error''コメントの削除により、堅牢なコード品質と型安全性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 TypeScript 유형을 능동적으로 강화할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 ''any'' 유형을 대체하고 ''unknown'' 유형을 좁히고 안전하지 않은 ''as'' 캐스트를 제거하며 ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'' 주석을 제거하여 코드 품질과 유형 안전성을 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a fortalecer proactivamente las asignaciones de tipos TypeScript reemplazando los tipos ''any'', reduciendo los tipos ''unknown'', eliminando los lanzamientos de ''as'' inseguros y eliminando los comentarios ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'', garantizando una calidad y seguridad de código robustas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de renforcer proactivement les typages TypeScript en remplaçant les types ''any'', en réduisant les types ''unknown'', en supprimant les mises en forme ''as'' non sécurisées et en éliminant les commentaires ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'', garantissant une qualité et une sécurité de code robustes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die TypeScript-Typisierungen proaktiv zu stärken, indem sie die ''any''-Typen ersetzen, die ''unknown''-Typen einschränken, unsichere ''as''-Umformungen entfernen und ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error''-Kommentare eliminieren, um eine robuste Codequalität und Typensicherheit zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a fortalecer proativamente os tipos TypeScript, substituindo tipos ''any'', reduzindo tipos ''unknown'', removendo conversões ''as'' inseguras e eliminando comentários ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'', garantindo uma qualidade de código robusta e segurança de tipo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью активного укрепления типов TypeScript, заменяя типы ''any'', сужая типы ''unknown'', удаляя небезопасные приведения ''as'' и исключая комментарии ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error'', обеспечивая прочное качество кода и безопасность типов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تعزيز أنواع TypeScript بشكل استباقي عن طريق استبدال أنواع ''any'' وضيق نطاق أنواع ''unknown'' وإزالة تحويلات ''as'' غير آمنة وإزالة تعليقات ''@ts-ignore''/''@ts-expect-error''، مما يضمن جودة شفرة قوية وأمان أنواع."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating type safety audits","Strengthening monorepo TypeScript typings","Eliminating ''@ts-ignore'' comments"],"zh":["自动执行类型安全审计","增强monorepo TypeScript类型检查","消除''@ts-ignore''注释"],"ja":["型安全性監査の自動化","monorepoのTypeScript型チェックの強化","''@ts-ignore''コメントの除去"],"ko":["타입 안전성 감사 자동화","monorepo TypeScript 유형 확인 강화","''@ts-ignore'' 주석 제거"],"es":["Automatización de auditorías de seguridad de tipos","Fortalecimiento de las asignaciones de tipos TypeScript en monorepo","Eliminación de comentarios ''@ts-ignore''"],"fr":["Automatisation des audits de sécurité de types","Renforcement des typages TypeScript dans les monorepo","Élimination des commentaires ''@ts-ignore''"],"de":["Automatisierung von Typsicherheitsaudits","Stärkung der TypeScript-Typisierungen in Monorepo","Entfernen von ''@ts-ignore''-Kommentaren"],"pt":["Automatizar auditorias de segurança de tipo","Fortalecer digitadores de monorepo TypeScript","Eliminar comentários ''@ts-ignore''"],"ru":["Автоматизировать аудиты безопасности типов","Укреплять типизацию монорепо TypeScript","Удалять комментарии ''@ts-ignore''"],"ar":["أتمتة فحوصات أمان أنواع","تعزيز تعريفات مونوربو TypeScript","إزالة تعليقات ''@ts-ignore''"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the codebase","TypeScript environment needed"],"zh":["需要访问代码库","需要TypeScript环境"],"ja":["コードベースへのアクセスが必要","TypeScript環境が必要"],"ko":["코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요함","TypeScript 환경이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código","Se necesita un entorno de TypeScript"],"fr":["Requiert un accès à la base de code","Un environnement TypeScript est nécessaire"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf den Code-Stamm","Ein TypeScript-Umgebung wird benötigt"],"pt":["Requer acesso à base de código","Ambiente TypeScript necessário"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к базе кода","Необходимо окружение TypeScript"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة","بيئة TypeScript ضرورية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
