 문서를 업데이트","지식과 경험을 보존","Epic Workflows（v5.0+）를 지원"],"es":["Cierre de workflows de características y épicos","Generación de documentación y preservación de conocimientos","Mejora de la calidad de los lanzamientos de producción","Integración con Spec-Driven Development","Generación de métricas de velocidad y resultados de sprint"],"fr":["Clôture des workflows de fonctionnalités et d''épics","Génération de documentation et préservation des connaissances","Amélioration de la qualité des lancements de production","Intégration avec Spec-Driven Development","Génération de métriques de vitesse et de résultats de sprint"],"de":["Schließung von Workflows für Funktionen und Epics","Generierung von Dokumentation und Bewahrung von Wissen","Verbesserung der Qualität von Produktionsstarts","Integration mit Spec-Driven Development","Generierung von Geschwindigkeitsmetriken und Sprint-Ergebnissen"],"pt":["Conclusão da fase de desenvolvimento com sucesso","Criação de lançamentos de produção com Spec-Driven Development","Geração de walkthrough com métricas de velocidade e resultados de sprint","Atualização da roadmap e arquivamento de artefatos","Preservação do conhecimento após o deploy"],"ru":["Завершение фазы разработки с успехом","Создание производственных запусков с Spec-Driven Development","Генерация walkthrough с метриками скорости и результатами спринта","Обновление дорожной карты и архивация артефактов","Сохранение знаний после деплоя"],"ar":["إنهاء مرحلة التطوير بنجاح","إنشاء إطلاق الإنتاج مع Spec-Driven Development","توليد walkthrough مع مقاييس السرعة ونتائج السباق","تحديث خريطة الطريق وتخزين الملفات","الحفاظ على المعرفة بعد النشر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","自动化工作流","产品发布","工作流闭合","开发效率","Epic Workflows"],"ja":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","ワークフロー自動化","プロダクト发布","ワークフローの終了","開発効率","Epic Workflows"],"ko":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","워크플로우 자동화","제품 출시","워크플로우 종료","개발 효율","Epic Workflows"],"es":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","desarrollo de software","cierre de workflows","generación de documentación","preservación de conocimientos","calidad de lanzamientos de producción"],"fr":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","développement de logiciels","clôture de workflows","génération de documentation","préservation des connaissances","qualité des lancements de production"],"de":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","Software-Entwicklung","Schließung von Workflows","Generierung von Dokumentation","Bewahrung von Wissen","Qualität von Produktionsstarts"],"pt":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","desenvolvimento de software","lançamento de produção","roadmap","artefatos","conhecimento","deploy"],"ru":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","разработка программного обеспечения","производственный запуск","дорожная карта","артефакты","знания","деплой"],"ar":["finalize-phase","Spec-Driven Development","تطوير البرمجيات","إطلاق الإنتاج","خريطة الطريق","الملفات","المعرفة","النشر"]}},"owner":"marcusgoll","repo":"Spec-Flow","repoPath":"marcusgoll/Spec-Flow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"finalize-phase","description":"Completes feature/epic workflows after deployment with comprehensive walkthrough generation for epics (v5.0+), roadmap updates, artifact archival, documentation, and branch cleanup. Use after /ship-prod, /deploy-prod, or /build-local completes, or when user asks to finalize. (project)","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nComplete feature/epic workflow, generate walkthrough (epics only), update roadmap, archive artifacts, and preserve knowledge after deployment. Ensures clean workflow closure with self-improving workflow system.\n\nThis skill orchestrates the /finalize phase, the final step after successful deployment to production, direct-prod, or local build.\n\n**For Epic Workflows (v5.0+)**:\n\n- Generate comprehensive walkthrough.md with velocity metrics, sprint results, lessons learned\n- Run post-mort","body":"<objective>\nComplete feature/epic workflow, generate walkthrough (epics only), update roadmap, archive artifacts, and preserve knowledge after deployment. Ensures clean workflow closure with self-improving workflow system.\n\nThis skill orchestrates the /finalize phase, the final step after successful deployment to production, direct-prod, or local build.\n\n**For Epic Workflows (v5.0+)**:\n\n- Generate comprehensive walkthrough.md with velocity metrics, sprint results, lessons learned\n- Run post-mortem audit with pattern detection (after 2-3 epics)\n- Offer workflow healing with improvement recommendations\n- Detect patterns for custom skills/commands generation\n\n**For Feature Workflows**:\n\n- Standard finalization (roadmap, artifacts, docs, branches)\n\nInputs: Deployed feature/epic, phase artifacts, ship report, state.yaml\nOutputs: walkthrough.md (epics only), updated roadmap, archived artifacts, updated documentation\nExpected duration: 10-15 minutes (features), 20-30 minutes (epics with walkthrough)\n</objective>\n\n<quick_start>\nAfter deployment completes, finalize the workflow:\n\n**Epic Workflows (NEW in v5.0)**: 0. Generate walkthrough - Comprehensive epic summary with velocity metrics, sprint results, lessons learned, pattern detection\n\n1. Run post-mortem audit - Final effectiveness analysis with improvement recommendations\n2. Offer workflow healing - Apply discovered improvements with user approval\n\n**All Workflows** (features + epics):\n\n1. Update roadmap - Move to \"Shipped\" with completion date, version, production URL\n2. Archive artifacts - Verify all phase artifacts in specs/NNN-slug/ or epics/NNN-slug/\n3. Update documentation - README, CHANGELOG, user guides (if applicable)\n4. Clean up branches - Delete feature branch locally and remotely\n5. Commit finalization - Small commit documenting workflow closure\n\nKey principles:\n\n- Clean closure preserves knowledge and enables learning\n- Epic walkthroughs enable self-improving workflow system\n- Pattern detection (after 2-3 epics) suggests custom automation\n  </quick_start>\n\n<prerequisites>\nBefore beginning finalization:\n- Deployment completed successfully (/ship-prod, /deploy-prod, or /build-local done)\n- Ship report generated (ship-summary.md exists)\n- All phase artifacts present in specs/NNN-slug/\n- Git working tree clean (all changes committed)\n\nIf deployment incomplete, return to /ship phase.\n</prerequisites>\n\n<workflow>\n<step number=\"0\">\n**Epic Walkthrough Generation** (Epic workflows only - NEW in v5.0)\n\nDetect epic vs feature workflow and generate comprehensive walkthrough for epics.\n\n**Detection**:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f \"epics/*/epic-spec.xml\" ]; then\n  WORKSPACE_TYPE=\"epic\"\n  EPIC_DIR=$(dirname \"epics/*/epic-spec.xml\")\nelse\n  WORKSPACE_TYPE=\"feature\"\n  # Skip to Step 1 (standard finalization)\n  continue\nfi\n```\n\n**If feature workflow**: Skip this step entirely, proceed to Step 1\n\n**If epic workflow**: Generate walkthrough before standard finalization\n\n**Walkthrough Generation Pipeline**:\n\n1. **Gather all epic artifacts**:\n\n   - epic-spec.xml (epic specification)\n   - research.xml (research phase output)\n   - plan.xml (plan phase output with meta-prompting)\n   - sprint-plan.xml (task breakdown with dependency graph)\n   - state.yaml (state tracking across phases)\n   - audit-report.xml (workflow effectiveness analysis)\n   - preview-report.xml (manual testing decision)\n   - Sprint results from epics/NNN-slug/sprints/\\*/\n\n2. **Calculate velocity metrics**:\n\n   - Expected parallelization multiplier (from sprint-plan.xml)\n   - Actual parallelization multiplier (from audit-report.xml)\n   - Time saved in hours (parallel vs sequential execution)\n   - Duration from start to completion\n\n3. **Extract key information**:\n\n   - Epic goal and success metrics\n   - Phases completed with timestamps\n   - Sprint execution results (status, tasks, duration, contracts, tests)\n   - Validation results (optimization, preview decision)\n   - Key files modified\n   - Next steps (enhancements, technical debt, monitoring needs)\n\n4. **Generate walkthrough.xml and walkthrough.md**:\n\n   - Use template: `.spec-flow/templates/walkthrough.xml`\n   - Populate with metrics, sprint results, lessons learned\n   - Write both machine-readable (XML) and human-readable (Markdown) versions\n\n5. **Run post-mortem audit**:\n\n   - Invoke `/audit-workflow --post-mortem`\n   - Analyze velocity accuracy (expected vs actual)\n   - Detect bottlenecks and inefficiencies\n   - Generate improvement recommendations\n\n6. **Pattern detection** (if 2+ epics completed):\n\n   - Analyze patterns across completed epics\n   - Detect code generation patterns (service boilerplate repeated 3x)\n   - Detect architectural patterns (all services use DI + Repository)\n   - Detect workflow patterns (always clarify auth approach)\n   - Suggest custom skills/commands if confidence ≥80%\n\n7. **Offer workflow healing**:\n\n   - Display immediate improvements from audit recommendations\n   - Categorize by priority (immediate vs deferred)\n   - Offer `/heal-workflow` to apply improvements\n   - Save deferred improvements for pattern-based optimization\n\n8. **Commit walkthrough**:\n\n```bash\ngit add epics/*/walkthrough.xml\ngit add epics/*/walkthrough.md\ngit add epics/*/audit-report.xml\n\ngit commit -m \"docs: generate epic walkthrough\n\n[EPIC SUMMARY]\nEpic: ${epic_slug}\nDuration: ${duration_hours}h\nVelocity: ${velocity_multiplier}x (saved ${time_saved}h)\n\n[SPRINTS COMPLETED]\nTotal: ${total_sprints}\nExecution: ${execution_strategy}\nTasks: ${tasks_completed}/${total_tasks}\n\n[QUALITY METRICS]\nAudit Score: ${audit_score}/100\nPhase Efficiency: ${phase_efficiency}/100\n\n[LESSONS LEARNED]\n- What worked: ${what_worked_summary}\n- What struggled: ${what_struggled_summary}\n\n{IF recommendations > 0}\nImprovement recommendations: ${recommendations_count}\nRun /heal-workflow to apply improvements\n{ENDIF}\n\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n9. **Present walkthrough summary** to user with:\n   - Velocity metrics (expected vs actual, time saved)\n   - Sprint results (status, tasks, duration, tests)\n   - Quality metrics (audit score, phase efficiency, parallelization score)\n   - What worked / what struggled / lessons learned\n   - Improvement recommendations (if any)\n   - Pattern detection results (if 2+ epics completed)\n\n**After walkthrough complete**: Proceed to Step 1 (standard finalization)\n\n**Validation**: For epics, walkthrough.xml and walkthrough.md exist in epics/NNN-slug/\n\nSee reference.md for epic walkthrough generation details.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"1\">\n**Update Roadmap**\n\nMove feature from \"In Progress\" to \"Shipped\" section in roadmap.\n\n**Actions**:\n\n1. Open `.spec-flow/memory/roadmap.md`\n2. Find feature in \"In Progress\" section\n3. Move to \"Shipped\" section with completion details\n\n**Required information**:\n\n- Completion date (deployment date)\n- Version number (from CHANGELOG or ship report)\n- Production URL (if applicable)\n- Links to ship report and release notes\n\n**Example**:\n\n```markdown\n## Shipped\n\n### Student Progress Dashboard (v1.3.0) - Shipped 2025-10-21\n\n- **Production URL**: https://app.example.com/students/progress\n- **Ship Report**: specs/042-student-progress-dashboard/ship-summary.md\n- **Release Notes**: CHANGELOG.md#v1.3.0\n- **Impact**: Teachers can now track student progress with completion rates and time spent\n```\n\n**Validation**: Feature appears in \"Shipped\" section with all required details.\n\nSee reference.md for roadmap update checklist.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"2\">\n**Archive Artifacts**\n\nVerify all workflow artifacts archived in `specs/NNN-slug/` directory.\n\n**Required artifacts checklist**:\n\n- [ ] spec.md (feature specification)\n- [ ] plan.md (implementation plan)\n- [ ] tasks.md (task breakdown)\n- [ ] optimization-report.md (quality gates results)\n- [ ] preview-checklist.md (manual testing checklist - if applicable)\n- [ ] ship-summary.md (deployment report)\n- [ ] release-notes.md (user-facing release notes)\n- [ ] state.yaml (workflow state tracking)\n\n**Optional artifacts**:\n\n- [ ] clarifications.md (if /clarify phase ran)\n- [ ] analysis-report.md (if /validate phase ran)\n- [ ] staging-ship-report.md (if staging deployment happened)\n\n**Validation steps**:\n\n```bash\n# List all artifacts in feature directory\nls -la specs/NNN-slug/\n\n# Should see all required files\n# No temporary files (.tmp, .bak, etc.)\n```\n\n**If artifacts missing**:\n\n- Check for artifacts in wrong locations (root directory, temp folders)\n- Regenerate missing artifacts if possible\n- Document missing artifacts in finalization commit message\n\nSee reference.md for complete artifact checklist.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"3\">\n**Update Documentation**\n\nUpdate user-facing documentation for shipped feature.\n\n**README.md updates** (if user-facing feature):\n\n```markdown\n## Features\n\n- **Student Progress Dashboard** - Track student completion rates and time spent\n  - View individual student progress\n  - Filter by class, subject, or time period\n  - Export progress reports to CSV\n```\n\n**CHANGELOG.md updates**:\n\n```markdown\n## [1.3.0] - 2025-10-21\n\n### Added\n\n- Student progress dashboard with completion tracking\n- CSV export for progress reports\n- Filtering by class, subject, and time period\n\n### Changed\n\n- Improved dashboard load time from 3s to 1.2s\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed timeout issue with large datasets (pagination added)\n```\n\n**User guides** (for complex features):\n\n- Create docs/features/student-progress-dashboard.md\n- Include screenshots, usage instructions, FAQs\n- Link from README.md\n\n**Validation**: Documentation accurately reflects shipped feature.\n\nSee reference.md for documentation standards.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"4\">\n**Clean Up Branches**\n\nDelete feature branch locally and remotely (if applicable).\n\n**Local branch deletion**:\n\n```bash\n# Verify branch is merged\ngit branch --merged main | grep feature/042-student-progress-dashboard\n\n# Delete local branch\ngit branch -d feature/042-student-progress-dashboard\n```\n\n**Remote branch deletion** (if pushed to remote):\n\n```bash\n# Delete remote branch\ngit push origin --delete feature/042-student-progress-dashboard\n\n# Verify deletion\ngit branch -r | grep feature/042-student-progress-dashboard  # Should return nothing\n```\n\n**If branch not merged**:\n\n- Verify feature deployed successfully\n- If deployed, force delete: `git branch -D feature/...`\n- Document why branch not merged in commit message\n\n**Validation**: Feature branch no longer exists locally or remotely.\n\nSee reference.md for branch cleanup guidelines.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"5\">\n**Commit Finalization**\n\nCreate small commit documenting workflow closure.\n\n**Commit format**:\n\n```bash\ngit add .spec-flow/memory/roadmap.md README.md CHANGELOG.md\ngit commit -m \"chore: finalize student-progress-dashboard (v1.3.0)\n\nUpdated roadmap, README, and CHANGELOG\nArchived artifacts in specs/042-student-progress-dashboard/\"\n```\n\n**Commit message format**:\n\n- Type: `chore` (finalization is housekeeping)\n- Subject: `finalize [feature-name] ([version])`\n- Body: List what was updated (roadmap, docs, etc.)\n\n**Update state.yaml**:\n\n```yaml\nfinalization:\n  status: completed\n  completion_date: 2025-10-21\n  version: v1.3.0\n  artifacts_archived: true\n  documentation_updated: true\n  branches_cleaned: true\n```\n\n**Validation**: Finalization commit pushed to main branch.\n\nSee reference.md for commit best practices.\n</step>\n</workflow>\n\n<validation>\nAfter finalization phase, verify:\n\n- Roadmap updated (feature in \"Shipped\" section with completion date, version, URL)\n- All artifacts archived (checklist 100% complete)\n- Documentation updated (README, CHANGELOG, user guides if applicable)\n- Branches cleaned up (feature branch deleted locally and remotely)\n- Finalization committed (chore commit with workflow closure details)\n- state.yaml updated (finalization.status = completed)\n\nWorkflow is now cleanly closed and ready for retrospective analysis.\n</validation>\n\n<anti_patterns>\n<pitfall name=\"roadmap_not_updated\">\n**❌ Don''t**: Skip roadmap update, leave feature in \"In Progress\"\n**✅ Do**: Always move to \"Shipped\" with completion date and links\n\n**Why**: Roadmap becomes stale and inaccurate. Team loses visibility into what shipped and when.\n\n**Impact**:\n\n- Historical tracking lost\n- Roadmap doesn''t reflect reality\n- Hard to analyze velocity over time\n\n**Example** (bad):\n\n```\nFeature deploys to production\n/finalize skips roadmap update\nRoadmap still shows feature \"In Progress\"\n6 months later: \"Did we ship this? When?\"\n```\n\n**Example** (good):\n\n```\nFeature deploys to production\n/finalize updates roadmap immediately\nRoadmap shows \"Shipped 2025-10-21, v1.3.0\"\n6 months later: Clear historical record\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"incomplete_documentation\">\n**❌ Don''t**: Skip README/CHANGELOG updates for \"small\" features\n**✅ Do**: Update all user-facing documentation for every shipped feature\n\n**Why**: Knowledge loss compounds over time. Users can''t discover features if not documented.\n\n**Impact**:\n\n- Feature discovery issues (users don''t know feature exists)\n- Onboarding friction (new team members confused)\n- Version history unclear (what changed when?)\n\n**Example** (bad):\n\n```\nShip feature, skip README update\n3 months later: User asks \"Do we have progress tracking?\"\nAnswer: \"Yes, we shipped that 3 months ago\" (not documented)\n```\n\n**Example** (good):\n\n```\nShip feature, update README immediately\nREADME: \"Student Progress Dashboard - Track completion\"\nUser discovers feature organically from README\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"branch_not_deleted\">\n**❌ Don''t**: Leave feature branches around \"just in case\"\n**✅ Do**: Delete merged feature branches immediately\n\n**Why**: Branch clutter makes it hard to find active work.\n\n**Impact**:\n\n- Git branch list becomes unusable (100+ stale branches)\n- Hard to identify active development\n- Wastes storage (remote branches)\n\n**Example** (bad):\n\n```\ngit branch -a\n# Shows 87 feature branches (only 3 active)\n# Which branches are safe to delete? Unknown.\n```\n\n**Example** (good):\n\n```\ngit branch -a\n# Shows 3 feature branches (all active)\n# Clear signal: current work only\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"no_finalization_commit\">\n**❌ Don''t**: Update files without committing finalization\n**✅ Do**: Create explicit finalization commit documenting closure\n\n**Why**: Finalization changes should be tracked in git history.\n\n**Impact**:\n\n- Changes not backed up\n- No clear signal when workflow closed\n- Hard to audit finalization process\n\n**Example** (bad):\n\n```\nUpdate roadmap, README, CHANGELOG\nGit status: 3 modified files\nNever commit (lose changes on machine wipe)\n```\n\n**Example** (good):\n\n```\nUpdate roadmap, README, CHANGELOG\ngit commit -m \"chore: finalize feature (v1.3.0)\"\nClear git history marker: finalization happened\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"artifacts_not_archived\">\n**❌ Don''t**: Delete or lose phase artifacts after deployment\n**✅ Do**: Archive all artifacts in specs/NNN-slug/ permanently\n\n**Why**: Artifacts contain valuable context for future maintenance.\n\n**Impact**:\n\n- Context loss (why was feature built this way?)\n- Hard to debug issues (no spec to reference)\n- Can''t analyze past decisions (no plan to review)\n\n**Example** (bad):\n\n```\nShip feature, delete spec.md and plan.md\n6 months later: \"Why did we implement it this way?\"\nAnswer: Unknown (artifacts deleted)\n```\n\n**Example** (good):\n\n```\nShip feature, archive all artifacts\n6 months later: \"Why did we implement it this way?\"\nAnswer: Check specs/042-.../spec.md (clear rationale)\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n</anti_patterns>\n\n<best_practices>\n<practice name=\"immediate_finalization\">\nRun /finalize immediately after deployment succeeds:\n\n- Don''t defer finalization \"for later\"\n- Don''t batch multiple finalizations\n- Run while deployment fresh in memory\n\nResult: Accurate documentation, fewer missed steps\n</practice>\n\n<practice name=\"complete_artifact_checklist\">\nUse complete artifact checklist from reference.md:\n\n- Verify each artifact present\n- Check for artifacts in wrong locations\n- Document missing artifacts if any\n\nResult: Complete archival, no lost context\n</practice>\n\n<practice name=\"user_facing_documentation\">\nAlways update README and CHANGELOG for user-facing features:\n\n- README: Feature list with one-line descriptions\n- CHANGELOG: Version entry with Added/Changed/Fixed\n- User guides: Detailed instructions for complex features\n\nResult: Feature discoverability, clear version history\n</practice>\n\n<practice name=\"clean_branch_hygiene\">\nDelete merged branches immediately:\n\n- Verify branch merged before deleting\n- Delete local and remote branches\n- Keep git branch list clean (active work only)\n\nResult: Clear signal of active development, reduced clutter\n</practice>\n\n<practice name=\"explicit_finalization_commit\">\nCreate explicit commit documenting workflow closure:\n\n- Type: chore\n- Subject: finalize [feature-name] ([version])\n- Body: List updates (roadmap, docs, artifacts)\n\nResult: Clear git history marker, auditable finalization\n</practice>\n</best_practices>\n\n<success_criteria>\nFinalization phase complete when:\n\n- [ ] Roadmap updated (feature moved to \"Shipped\" with date, version, URL, links)\n- [ ] All artifacts archived (100% checklist complete in specs/NNN-slug/)\n- [ ] Documentation updated (README, CHANGELOG, user guides if applicable)\n- [ ] Branches cleaned up (feature branch deleted locally and remotely)\n- [ ] Finalization committed (chore commit documenting closure)\n- [ ] state.yaml updated (finalization.status = completed)\n\nWorkflow is cleanly closed and ready for retrospective analysis.\n</success_criteria>\n\n<quality_standards>\n**Good finalization**:\n\n- Immediate (runs right after deployment)\n- Complete (all artifacts archived, all docs updated)\n- Clean (branches deleted, commit made)\n- Documented (roadmap + README + CHANGELOG updated)\n\n**Bad finalization**:\n\n- Deferred (runs days/weeks later, details forgotten)\n- Incomplete (missing artifacts, incomplete docs)\n- Messy (branches not deleted, no commit)\n- Undocumented (roadmap stale, README outdated)\n  </quality_standards>\n\n<troubleshooting>\n**Issue**: Can''t find feature in roadmap \"In Progress\" section\n**Solution**: Check \"Backlog\" or \"Planned\" sections, or search entire roadmap file with grep\n\n**Issue**: Missing artifacts (spec.md, plan.md, etc.)\n**Solution**: Check root directory, temp folders, or regenerate if possible. Document missing in commit.\n\n**Issue**: Feature branch won''t delete (not merged)\n**Solution**: Verify feature deployed successfully, then force delete with `git branch -D`. Document in commit.\n\n**Issue**: Unclear what version to use\n**Solution**: Check CHANGELOG for next version number, or use deployment date as version (v2025.10.21)\n\n**Issue**: Don''t know what to put in CHANGELOG\n**Solution**: Review ship-summary.md and release-notes.md for user-facing changes. Focus on Added/Changed/Fixed.\n</troubleshooting>\n\n<reference_guides>\nFinalization procedures:\n\n- Roadmap Update Checklist (reference.md#roadmap-updates) - Required information and format\n- Artifact Archival Guide (reference.md#artifact-archival) - Complete checklist and validation\n- Documentation Standards (reference.md#documentation-updates) - README, CHANGELOG, user guide formats\n\nExamples:\n\n- Complete Finalization (examples.md#complete-finalization) - All steps done correctly\n- Rushed Cleanup (examples.md#rushed-cleanup) - What happens when steps skipped\n\nWorkflow closure:\nAfter finalization completes, feature workflow is closed. Retrospective analysis can begin to learn from past work.\n</reference_guides>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:19:07.235Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents utilizing Spec-Driven Development and Claude Code workflows.","zh":"适用于采用规格驱动开发和 Claude Code 工作流的开发代理。","ja":"Spec-Driven Development と Claude Code ワークフローを使用する開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Spec-Driven Development와 Claude Code 워크플로를 사용하는 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que utilizan Desarrollo Dirigido por Especificaciones y flujos de trabajo de Claude Code.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement utilisant le développement piloté par spécifications et les flux de travail Claude Code.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die spezifikationsgesteuerte Entwicklung und Claude-Code-Workflows verwenden.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que utilizam Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações e fluxos de trabalho Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, использующих разработку, управляемую спецификациями, и рабочие процессы Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لعميلة التطوير الذين يستخدمون تطويرًا مدفوعًا بالمواصفات وأعمال تيار كلود كود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure clean workflow closure with self-improving workflow systems, utilizing quality gates, token budgets, and auditable artifacts, while generating comprehensive walkthrough.md files with velocity metrics and sprint results.","zh":"赋予代理确保清晰工作流关闭的能力，利用自我改进的工作流系统、质量门、令牌预算和可审计的工件，同时生成包含速度指标和冲刺结果的综合 walkthrough.md 文件。","ja":"エージェントがクリーンなワークフローのクロージャーを確保できるようにし、自己改善型のワークフローシステム、品質ゲート、トークン予算、および監査可能なアーティファクトを使用し、速度メトリクスとスプリント結果を含む包括的な walkthrough.md ファイルを生成します。","ko":"에이전트가 깨끗한 워크플로우 종료를 보장할 수 있도록 하며, 자기 개선형 워크플로우 시스템, 품질 게이트, 토큰 예산 및 감사 가능한 아티팩트를 사용하여, 속도 메트릭스와 스프린트 결과를 포함하는 포괄적인 walkthrough.md 파일을 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para garantizar el cierre limpio del flujo de trabajo con sistemas de flujo de trabajo auto-mejorables, utilizando puertas de calidad, presupuestos de tokens y artefactos auditables, mientras genera archivos walkthrough.md completos con métricas de velocidad y resultados de sprint.","fr":"Permet aux agents de s''assurer d''une fermeture de flux de travail propre avec des systèmes de flux de travail auto-améliorants, en utilisant des portes de qualité, des budgets de jetons et des artefacts auditable, tout en générant des fichiers walkthrough.md complets avec des métriques de vitesse et des résultats de sprint.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, eine saubere Arbeitsablaufschließung mit selbstverbessernden Arbeitsablaufsysteemen zu gewährleisten, indem Qualitäts gates, Token-Budgets und überprüfbare Artefakte verwendet werden, während umfassende walkthrough.md-Dateien mit Geschwindigkeitsmetriken und Sprint-Ergebnissen generiert werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes garantam o fechamento limpo do fluxo de trabalho com sistemas de fluxo de trabalho auto-aperfeiçoáveis, utilizando portas de qualidade, orçamentos de tokens e artefatos auditáveis, enquanto gera arquivos walkthrough.md abrangentes com métricas de velocidade e resultados de sprint.","ru":"Позволяет агентам обеспечить чистое закрытие рабочего процесса с помощью самоулучшающихся систем рабочего процесса, используя ворота качества, бюджет токенов и аудиторные артефакты, а также генерировать полные файлы walkthrough.md с метриками скорости и результатами спринта.","ar":"يُمكِّن العميل من ضمان إغلاق سير العمل النظيف مع أنظمة سير عمل تتحسن ذاتيًا، باستخدام بوابات الجودة وميزانيات الرموز والمنقولات القابلة للتدقيق، مع توليد ملفات walkthrough.md شاملة مع مقاييس السرعة ونتائج الركض."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating epic workflow completion","Generating walkthrough documents with velocity metrics","Updating roadmaps and archiving artifacts after deployment"],"zh":["自动完成史诗工作流","生成包含速度指标的走查文档","部署后更新路线图和存档工件"],"ja":["エピックワークフローの自動化","速度メトリクスを含むウォークスルー文書の生成","デプロイ後、ロードマップの更新とアーティファクトのアーカイブ"],"ko":["에픽 워크플로우 자동화","속도 메트릭스를 포함한 워크스루 문서 생성","배포 후 로드맵 업데이트 및 아티팩트 아카이브"],"es":["Automatización de la finalización del flujo de trabajo épico","Generación de documentos de instrucciones con métricas de velocidad","Actualización de hojas de ruta y archivo de artefactos después de la implementación"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''achèvement du flux de travail épique","Génération de documents de parcours avec des métriques de vitesse","Mise à jour des feuilles de route et archivage des artefacts après le déploiement"],"de":["Automatisierung der epic-Workflow-Vervollständigung","Generierung von Handbüchern mit Geschwindigkeitsmetriken","Aktualisierung von Roadmaps und Archivierung von Artefakten nach der Bereitstellung"],"pt":["Automatizar a conclusão do fluxo de trabalho épico","Gerar documentos de walkthrough com métricas de velocidade","Atualizar planos de estrada e arquivar artefatos após a implantação"],"ru":["Автоматизировать завершение эпического рабочего процесса","Генерировать документы walkthrough с метриками скорости","Обновлять дорожные карты и архивировать артефакты после развертывания"],"ar":["توسيع تلقائي لإكمال سير العمل الملحمي","توليد وثائق سير العمل مع مقاييس السرعة","تحديث خارطة الطريق وتأريخ المنقولات بعد النشر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code workflows","Limited to Epic Workflows (v5.0+)","Needs access to workflow and deployment data"],"zh":["需要 Claude Code 工作流","仅限于史诗工作流（v5.0+）","需要访问工作流和部署数据"],"ja":["Claude Code ワークフローが必要","エピックワークフロー（v5.0+）のみ","ワークフローおよびデプロイデータへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["Claude Code 워크플로우가 필요","에픽 워크플로우（v5.0+）のみ","워크플로우 및 배포 데이터에 대한 액세스가 필요"],"es":["Requiere flujos de trabajo de Claude Code","Limitado a flujos de trabajo épico (v5.0+)","Necesita acceso a datos de flujo de trabajo y de implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite des flux de travail Claude Code","Limité aux flux de travail épique (v5.0+)","Nécessite l''accès aux données de flux de travail et de déploiement"],"de":["Benötigt Claude-Code-Workflows","Begrenzt auf Epic-Workflows (v5.0+)","Benötigt Zugriff auf Workflow- und Bereitstellungsdaten"],"pt":["Exige fluxos de trabalho Claude Code","Limitado a Fluxos de Trabalho Épicos (v5.0+)","Necessita acesso a dados de fluxo de trabalho e implantação"],"ru":["Требует рабочих процессов Claude Code","Ограничен рабочими процессами Epic (v5.0+)","Требует доступа к данным рабочего процесса и развертывания"],"ar":["يتطلب سير عمل كلود كود","محدود بسير عمل الملحمة (الإصدار 5.0+)","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى بيانات سير العمل والنشر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rdfitted/Claude-Code-Setup/scout-plan-build-test', 'community', 'rdfitted', 'Claude-Code-Setup', 'rdfitted/Claude-Code-Setup', 'scout-plan-build-test', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z', '2026-02-18T08:19:49.092Z', NULL, '{"id":"rdfitted/Claude-Code-Setup/scout-plan-build-test","name":"scout-plan-build-test","description":{"es":"El flujo de trabajo Scout Plan Build Test es una metodología para desarrollar y probar características de software de manera estructurada","fr":"Le flux de travail Scout Plan Build Test est une méthodologie pour développer et tester des fonctionnalités de logiciel de manière structurée","de":"Der Entwicklungsworkflow Scout Plan Build Test ist eine Methode zur strukturierten Entwicklung und zum Testen von Softwarefunktionen","pt":"O Scout Plan Build Test é uma abordagem que envolve a execução de quatro etapas: Scout, Plan, Build e Test, para otimizar o fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","ru":"Скаут План Постройка Тест - это подход, который включает в себя выполнение четырех этапов: Скаут, План, Постройка и Тест, для оптимизации потока работы разработки","ar":"كشاف خطة بناء اختبار هو نهج ي涉ل تنفيذ أربع مراحل: كشاف، خطة، بناء واختبار، لتحسين تدفق العمل التطويري","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Scout Plan Build Test: Flujo de Trabajo de Desarrollo","fr":"Scout Plan Build Test: Flux de Travail de Développement","de":"Scout Plan Build Test: Entwicklungsworkflow","pt":"Scout Plan Build Test: Otimização de Fluxo de Trabalho","ru":"Скаут План Постройка Тест: Оптимизация Потока Работы","ar":"كشاف خطة بناء اختبار: تحسين تدفق العمل","en":"scout-plan-build-test"},"description":{"es":"El flujo de trabajo Scout Plan Build Test es una metodología para desarrollar y probar características de software de manera estructurada","fr":"Le flux de travail Scout Plan Build Test est une méthodologie pour développer et tester des fonctionnalités de logiciel de manière structurée","de":"Der Entwicklungsworkflow Scout Plan Build Test ist eine Methode zur strukturierten Entwicklung und zum Testen von Softwarefunktionen","pt":"O Scout Plan Build Test é uma abordagem que envolve a execução de quatro etapas: Scout, Plan, Build e Test, para otimizar o fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","ru":"Скаут План Постройка Тест - это подход, который включает в себя выполнение четырех этапов: Скаут, План, Постройка и Тест, для оптимизации потока работы разра...","ar":"كشاف خطة بناء اختبار هو نهج ي涉ل تنفيذ أربع مراحل: كشاف، خطة، بناء واختبار، لتحسين تدفق العمل التطويري","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Ejecución de Scout para el análisis de requisitos","Planificación de la implementación con Plan","Construcción de la función con Build","Pruebas de la función con Test","Generación de un resumen de implementación y resultados de pruebas"],"fr":["Exécution de Scout pour l''analyse des exigences","Planification de la mise en œuvre avec Plan","Construction de la fonction avec Build","Tests de la fonction avec Test","Génération d''un résumé de mise en œuvre et de résultats de tests"],"de":["Ausführen von Scout für die Anforderungsanalyse","Planung der Implementierung mit Plan","Bau der Funktion mit Build","Testen der Funktion mit Test","Erzeugung einer Implementierungsübersicht und Testergebnisse"],"pt":["Execução de quatro etapas: Scout, Plan, Build e Test","Otimização do fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","Melhoria da eficiência e produtividade","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Relatórios detalhados de testes e implementação"],"ru":["Выполнение четырех этапов: Скаут, План, Постройка и Тест","Оптимизация потока работы разработки","Улучшение эффективности и производительности","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Детальные отчеты о тестах и реализации"],"ar":["تنفيذ أربع مراحل: كشاف، خطة، بناء واختبار","تحسين تدفق العمل التطويري","تحسين الكفاءة والإنتاجية","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","تقارير مفصلة عن الاختبارات والتنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"es":["desarrollo de software","pruebas de software","metodologías de desarrollo","Scout Plan Build Test","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","desarrollo de características"],"fr":["développement de logiciel","tests de logiciel","méthodologies de développement","Scout Plan Build Test","flux de travail de développement","développement de fonctionnalités"],"de":["Softwareentwicklung","Softwaretests","Entwicklungsmethoden","Scout Plan Build Test","Entwicklungsworkflow","Funktionenentwicklung"],"pt":["scout plan build test","desenvolvimento de software","otimização de fluxo de trabalho","metodologia de desenvolvimento","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","testes de software","relatórios de testes"],"ru":["скаут план постройка тест","разработка программного обеспечения","оптимизация потока работы","методология разработки","инструменты разработки","тесты программного обеспечения","отчеты о тестах"],"ar":["كشاف خطة بناء اختبار","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين تدفق العمل","منهجية التطوير","أدوات التطوير","اختبارات البرمجيات","تقارير الاختبارات"]}},"owner":"rdfitted","repo":"Claude-Code-Setup","repoPath":"rdfitted/Claude-Code-Setup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"scout-plan-build-test","description":"Run scout, plan, build, and testing in one flow; use for end-to-end delivery with validation.","bodyPreview":"# Scout Plan Build Test\n\n## Overview\n\nRun Scout, Plan, Build, then Test Features.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Feature description\n- Optional URL for runtime testing\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Run Scout.\n2. Run Plan.\n3. Run Build.\n4. Run Test Features (or project tests).\n\n## Output\n\n- Plan file path, implementation summary, test results","body":"# Scout Plan Build Test\n\n## Overview\n\nRun Scout, Plan, Build, then Test Features.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Feature description\n- Optional URL for runtime testing\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Run Scout.\n2. Run Plan.\n3. Run Build.\n4. Run Test Features (or project tests).\n\n## Output\n\n- Plan file path, implementation summary, test results\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:19:49.092Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring streamlined feature development workflows with Scout, Plan, Build, and Test phases.","zh":"适合需要使用Scout、Plan、Build和Test阶段简化功能开发工作流的开发代理。","ja":"Scout、Plan、Build、Testの各段階で機能開発ワークフローを簡略化する必要がある開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Scout, Plan, Build 및 Test 단계를 사용하여 기능 개발 워크플ロー가 단순화된 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren flujos de trabajo de desarrollo de características simplificados con fases de Exploración, Planificación, Construcción y Pruebas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant des flux de travail de développement de fonctionnalités rationalisés avec des phases de reconnaissance, de planification, de construction et de test.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die optimierte Workflows für die Entwicklung von Funktionen mit den Phasen Aufklärung, Planung, Bau und Test erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento de recursos simplificados com as fases Scout, Planejamento, Construção e Teste.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих упрощенных рабочих процессов разработки функций с фазами Scout, планирования, разработки и тестирования.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات توكيل التطوير التي تتطلب سير عمل مبسط لتطوير الميزات مع مراحل الاستكشاف وال تخطيط والبناء والاختبار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to orchestrate feature development by running Scout, generating plans, building features, and testing implementations using runtime testing URLs and project tests, providing plan file paths, implementation summaries, and test results.","zh":"赋予代理编排功能开发的能力，通过运行Scout、生成计划、构建功能和使用运行时测试URL及项目测试测试实现，提供计划文件路径、实现摘要和测试结果。","ja":"エージェントに機能開発をオーケストレーションする能力を付与し、Scoutの実行、計画の生成、機能の構築、実装のテスト（実行時テストURLおよびプロジェクトテストを使用）を実行し、計画ファイルパス、実装の概要、テスト結果を提供します。","ko":"에이전트에 기능 개발을 오케스트레이션 할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Scout를 실행하고, 계획을 생성하고, 기능을 구축하고, 런타임 테스트 URL 및 프로젝트 테스트를 사용하여 구현을 테스트하며, 계획 파일 경로, 구현 요약 및 테스트 결과를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes orquestar el desarrollo de características ejecutando la exploración, generando planes, construyendo características y probando implementaciones utilizando URLs de prueba en tiempo de ejecución y pruebas de proyecto, proporcionando rutas de archivo de plan, resúmenes de implementación y resultados de pruebas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''orchestrer le développement de fonctionnalités en exécutant la reconnaissance, en générant des plans, en construisant des fonctionnalités et en testant les implémentations à l''aide d''URL de test en temps réel et de tests de projet, en fournissant des chemins de fichiers de plan, des résumés d''implémentation et des résultats de test.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Entwicklung von Funktionen zu orchestrieren, indem sie die Aufklärung durchführen, Pläne generieren, Funktionen erstellen und Implementierungen mit Laufzeit-Test-URLs und Projekttests testen, wobei Dateipfade, Implementierungszusammenfassungen und Testergebnisse bereitgestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orquestrar o desenvolvimento de recursos, executando o Scout, gerando planos, construindo recursos e testando implementações usando URLs de teste em tempo de execução e testes de projeto, fornecendo caminhos de arquivos de plano, resumos de implementação e resultados de teste.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять разработкой функций, выполняя Scout, генерируя планы, создавая функции и тестируя реализации с использованием URL-тестирования в режиме реального времени и проектных тестов, предоставляя пути файлов плана, сводки реализации и результаты тестирования.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تنسيق تطوير الميزات من خلال تشغيل الاستكشاف وتوليد الخطط وبناء الميزات واختبار التنفيذ باستخدام adres URL اختبار زمن التشغيل واختبارات المشروع وتوفير مسارات ملفات الخطة وملخصات التنفيذ ونَتائج الاختبار."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating feature testing with runtime URLs","Generating implementation plans for new features","Debugging feature builds using test results"],"zh":["使用运行时URL自动化功能测试","为新功能生成实现计划","使用测试结果调试功能构建"],"ja":["実行時URLを使用して機能テストを自動化する","新しい機能の実装計画を生成する","テスト結果を使用して機能ビルドをデバッグする"],"ko":["런타임 URL을 사용하여 기능 테스트를 자동화하는 것","새로운 기능에 대한 구현 계획을 생성하는 것","테스트 결과를 사용하여 기능 빌드를 디버깅하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas de características con URLs en tiempo de ejecución","Generación de planes de implementación para nuevas características","Depuración de compilaciones de características mediante resultados de pruebas"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests de fonctionnalités avec des URL en temps réel","Génération de plans d''implémentation pour de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Débogage des constructions de fonctionnalités à l''aide de résultats de test"],"de":["Automatisierung von Funktionsprüfungen mit Laufzeit-Test-URLs","Generierung von Implementierungsplänen für neue Funktionen","Fehlerbehebung bei der Erstellung von Funktionen mithilfe von Testergebnissen"],"pt":["Automatizar testes de recursos com URLs em tempo de execução","Gerar planos de implementação para novos recursos","Depurar compilações de recursos usando resultados de teste"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тестирование функций с помощью URL-тестирования в режиме реального времени","Генерировать планы реализации для новых функций","Отлаживать сборки функций с помощью результатов тестирования"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبار الميزات مع عناوين URL في وقت التشغيل","توليد خطط التنفيذ للميزات الجديدة","تصحيح أخطاء بناء الميزات باستخدام نتائج الاختبار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires feature description as input","Optional URL for runtime testing may be necessary"],"zh":["需要功能描述作为输入","可能需要运行时测试的可选URL"],"ja":["入力として機能説明が必要","実行時テストのオプションURLが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["입력으로 기능 설명이 필요","런타임 테스트에 대한 선택적 URL이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la descripción de la característica como entrada","URL opcional para pruebas en tiempo de ejecución puede ser necesario"],"fr":["Nécessite la description de la fonctionnalité comme entrée","URL facultatif pour les tests en temps réel peut être nécessaire"],"de":["Benötigt die Funktionsbeschreibung als Eingabe","Optionale URL für Laufzeit-Tests kann erforderlich sein"],"pt":["Exige descrição de recurso como entrada","URL opcional para teste em tempo de execução pode ser necessário"],"ru":["Требует описания функции в качестве входных данных","Необязательный URL для тестирования в режиме реального времени может быть необходим"],"ar":["يتطلب وصف الميزة كمدخل","يمكن أن يكون adress URL الاختبارات في وقت التشغيل اختياري ضروري"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/feature-implementation', 'community', 'CongDon1207', 'AGENTS.md', 'CongDon1207/AGENTS.md', 'feature-implementation', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z', '2026-02-18T08:19:11.749Z', NULL, '{"id":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/feature-implementation","name":"feature-implementation","description":{"zh":"作为专家全栈开发人员，实施新功能需要仔细规划和执行。todo列表是整个过程的关键","ja":"エキスパートフルスタック開発者として、新機能を実装するには、慎重な計画と実行が必要です。todoリストはプロセス全体の重要な要素です","ko":"전문가 전체 스택 개발자로서 새로운 기능을 구현하려면慎重한 계획과 실행이 필요합니다. todo 목록은 전체 프로세스의 중요한 요소입니다","es":"Implementa nuevas características en tu proyecto de manera efectiva. Aprende a planificar y ejecutar tareas de manera estructurada.","fr":"Mettez en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités dans votre projet de manière efficace. Apprenez à planifier et à exécuter des tâches de manière structurée.","de":"Implementieren Sie neue Funktionen in Ihrem Projekt effektiv. Lernen Sie, Aufgaben strukturiert zu planen und auszuführen.","pt":"A habilidade feature-implementation permite que você implemente novos recursos em seu projeto de forma eficiente. Ela envolve a cópia de pastas e arquivos para o diretório raiz do projeto.","ru":"Навык feature-implementation позволяет вам реализовать новые функции в вашем проекте эффективно. Он включает в себя копирование папок и файлов в корневой каталог проекта.","ar":"مهارة feature-implementation تمكنك من تنفيذ الميزات الجديدة في مشروعك بفعالية. وهي تتضمن نسخ المجلدات والملفات إلى الدليل الجذر للمشروع.","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"实现新功能和增强","ja":"新機能の実装","ko":"새 기능 및 강화 구현","es":"Implementación de Características","fr":"Mise en Œuvre de Fonctionnalités","de":"Funktion Implementierung","pt":"Implementação de Recursos com feature-implementation","ru":"Реализация функций с помощью feature-implementation","ar":"تنفيذ الميزات باستخدام feature-implementation","en":"feature-implementation"},"description":{"zh":"作为专家全栈开发人员，实施新功能需要仔细规划和执行。todo列表是整个过程的关键","ja":"エキスパートフルスタック開発者として、新機能を実装するには、慎重な計画と実行が必要です。todoリストはプロセス全体の重要な要素です","ko":"전문가 전체 스택 개발자로서 새로운 기능을 구현하려면慎重한 계획과 실행이 필요합니다. todo 목록은 전체 프로세스의 중요한 요소입니다","es":"Implementa nuevas características en tu proyecto de manera efectiva. Aprende a planificar y ejecutar tareas de manera estructurada.","fr":"Mettez en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités dans votre projet de manière efficace. Apprenez à planifier et à exécuter des tâches de manière structurée.","de":"Implementieren Sie neue Funktionen in Ihrem Projekt effektiv. Lernen Sie, Aufgaben strukturiert zu planen und auszuführen.","pt":"A habilidade feature-implementation permite que você implemente novos recursos em seu projeto de forma eficiente. Ela envolve a cópia de pastas e arquivos pa...","ru":"Навык feature-implementation позволяет вам реализовать новые функции в вашем проекте эффективно. Он включает в себя копирование папок и файлов в корневой кат...","ar":"مهارة feature-implementation تمكنك من تنفيذ الميزات الجديدة في مشروعك بفعالية. وهي تتضمن نسخ المجلدات والملفات إلى الدليل الجذر للمشروع.","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"definition":{"en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"features":{"zh":["todo列表规划","项目结构设计","全栈开发","新功能实现","增强功能开发","软件架构设计"],"ja":["todoリストの計画","プロジェクト構造設計","フルスタック開発","新機能の実装","強化機能の開発","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ設計"],"ko":["todo 목록 계획","프로젝트 구조 설계","전체 스택 개발","새 기능 구현","강화 기능 개발","소프트웨어 아키텍처 설계"],"es":["Planificación estructurada","Ejecución de tareas paso a paso","Integración de nuevas funcionalidades","Desarrollo full-stack","Arquitectura de software"],"fr":["Planification structurée","Exécution de tâches étape par étape","Intégration de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Développement full-stack","Architecture de logiciel"],"de":["Strukturierte Planung","Schritt-für-Schritt-Ausführung von Aufgaben","Integration neuer Funktionalitäten","Full-Stack-Entwicklung","Softwarearchitektur"],"pt":["Cópia de pastas e arquivos para o diretório raiz do projeto","Implementação de novos recursos de forma eficiente","Planejamento e execução de tarefas de forma organizada","Preservação do contexto de memória durante a execução","Cobertura de todas as fases do projeto, incluindo tarefas secundárias"],"ru":["Копирование папок и файлов в корневой каталог проекта","Реализация новых функций эффективно","Планирование и выполнение задач в организованном порядке","Сохранение контекста памяти во время выполнения","Покрытие всех фаз проекта, включая второстепенные задачи"],"ar":["نسخ المجلدات والملفات إلى الدليل الجذر للمشروع","تنفيذ الميزات الجديدة بفعالية","التخطيط والتنفيذ المهام بطريقة منظمة","الحفاظ على سياق الذاكرة أثناء التنفيذ","التغطية لجميع مراحل المشروع، بما في ذلك المهام الثانوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["新功能实现","全栈开发","todo列表","项目结构","软件架构","增强功能","dotnet","angular"],"ja":["新機能の実装","フルスタック開発","todoリスト","プロジェクト構造","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","強化機能","dotnet","angular"],"ko":["새 기능 구현","전체 스택 개발","todo 목록","프로젝트 구조","소프트웨어 아키텍처","강화 기능","dotnet","angular"],"es":["implementación de características","desarrollo full-stack","arquitectura de software","planificación de proyectos","integración de funcionalidades","desarrollo de software","programación","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["mise en œuvre de fonctionnalités","développement full-stack","architecture de logiciel","planification de projets","intégration de fonctionnalités","développement de logiciel","programmation","ingénierie de logiciel"],"de":["Funktion Implementierung","Full-Stack-Entwicklung","Softwarearchitektur","Projektplanung","Integration von Funktionalitäten","Softwareentwicklung","Programmierung","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["feature-implementation","implementação de recursos","desenvolvimento de software","full-stack","dotnet","angular","arquitetura de software"],"ru":["feature-implementation","реализация функций","разработка программного обеспечения","full-stack","dotnet","angular","архитектура программного обеспечения"],"ar":["feature-implementation","تنفيذ الميزات","تطوير البرمجيات","full-stack","dotnet","angular","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"CongDon1207","repo":"AGENTS.md","repoPath":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"feature-implementation","description":"Use when the user asks to implement a new feature, enhancement, add functionality, build something new, or create new capabilities. Triggers on keywords like implement, add feature, build, create new, develop, enhancement.","bodyPreview":"# Implementing a New Feature or Enhancement\n\nYou are to operate as an expert full-stack dotnet angular principle developer, software architecture to implement new requirements.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Always think hard, plan step-by-step todo list first before execute. Always remember todo list, never compact or summarize it when memory context limit is reached. Always preserve and carry your todo list through every operation. Todo list must cover all phases, from start to end, including child tasks in","body":"# Implementing a New Feature or Enhancement\n\nYou are to operate as an expert full-stack dotnet angular principle developer, software architecture to implement new requirements.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Always think hard, plan step-by-step todo list first before execute. Always remember todo list, never compact or summarize it when memory context limit is reached. Always preserve and carry your todo list through every operation. Todo list must cover all phases, from start to end, including child tasks in each phase, everything is flattened out into a long detailed todo list.\n\n---\n\n## Core Anti-Hallucination Protocols\n\n### ASSUMPTION_VALIDATION_CHECKPOINT\n\nBefore every major operation:\n\n1. \"What assumptions am I making about [X]?\"\n2. \"Have I verified this with actual code evidence?\"\n3. \"Could I be wrong about [specific pattern/relationship]?\"\n\n### EVIDENCE_CHAIN_VALIDATION\n\nBefore claiming any relationship:\n\n- \"I believe X calls Y because...\" → show actual code\n- \"This follows pattern Z because...\" → cite specific examples\n- \"Service A owns B because...\" → grep for actual boundaries\n\n### TOOL_EFFICIENCY_PROTOCOL\n\n- Batch multiple Grep searches into single calls with OR patterns\n- Use parallel Read operations for related files\n- Combine semantic searches with related keywords\n- Batch Write operations when creating multiple files\n\n### CONTEXT_ANCHOR_SYSTEM\n\nEvery 10 operations:\n\n1. Re-read the original task description from the `## Metadata` section\n2. Verify the current operation aligns with original goals\n3. Check if we''re solving the right problem\n4. Update the `Current Focus` bullet point within the `## Progress` section\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference Checklist\n\nBefore any major operation:\n\n- [ ] ASSUMPTION_VALIDATION_CHECKPOINT\n- [ ] EVIDENCE_CHAIN_VALIDATION\n- [ ] TOOL_EFFICIENCY_PROTOCOL\n\nEvery 10 operations:\n\n- [ ] CONTEXT_ANCHOR_CHECK\n- [ ] Update ''Current Focus'' in `## Progress` section\n\nEmergency:\n\n- **Context Drift** → Re-read `## Metadata` section\n- **Assumption Creep** → Halt, validate with code\n- **Evidence Gap** → Mark as \"inferred\"\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: EXTERNAL MEMORY-DRIVEN KNOWLEDGE MODEL CONSTRUCTION\n\nYour sole objective is to build a structured knowledge model in a Markdown analysis file at `ai_task_analysis_notes/[semantic-name].ai_task_analysis_notes_temp.md` with systematic external memory management.\n\n### PHASE 1A: INITIALIZATION AND DISCOVERY\n\n1. **Initialize** the analysis file with a `## Metadata` heading. Under it, add the full original prompt in a markdown box using 5 backticks:\n\n   ```markdown\n   [Full original prompt here]\n   ```\n\n2. **Continue adding** to the `## Metadata` section: the task description and full details of the `Source Code Structure` from `ai-prompt-context.md`. Use 6 backticks for this nested markdown:\n\n   ```markdown\n   ## Task Description\n\n   [Task description here]\n\n   ## Source Code Structure\n\n   [Full details from ai-prompt-context.md]\n   ```\n\n3. **Create all required headings**:\n   - `## Progress`\n   - `## Errors`\n   - `## Assumption Validations`\n   - `## Performance Metrics`\n   - `## Memory Management`\n   - `## Processed Files`\n   - `## File List`\n   - `## Knowledge Graph`\n\n4. **Populate `## Progress`** with:\n   - **Phase**: 1\n   - **Items Processed**: 0\n   - **Total Items**: 0\n   - **Current Operation**: \"initialization\"\n   - **Current Focus**: \"[original task summary]\"\n\n5. **Discovery searches** - Semantic search and grep search all keywords to find:\n   - **Domain Entities, Commands, Queries, Event Handlers, Controllers, Background Jobs, Consumers, front-end Components .ts**\n\n6. **Additional targeted searches to ensure no critical infrastructure is missed**:\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*EventHandler.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*EventHandler`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*BackgroundJob.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*BackgroundJob`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Consumer.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Consumer`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Service.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Service`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Helper.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Helper`\n   - Include pattern: `**/*.{cs,ts,html}`\n\n**CRITICAL:** Save ALL file paths immediately as a numbered list under `## File List`. Update the `Total Items` count in `## Progress`.\n\n### PHASE 1B: KNOWLEDGE GRAPH CONSTRUCTION\n\n**IMPORTANT: MUST DO WITH TODO LIST**\n\nCount total files in file list, split it into many batches of 10 files in priority order. For each batch, insert a new task in the current todo list for analyzing that batch.\n\n**File Analysis Order (by priority)**:\n\n1. Domain Entities\n2. Commands\n3. Queries\n4. Event Handlers\n5. Controllers\n6. Background Jobs\n7. Consumers\n8. Frontend Components .ts\n\n**CRITICAL:** You must analyze ALL files in the file list identified as belonging to the highest priority categories.\n\nFor each file, add results into `## Knowledge Graph` section. **The heading of each analyzed file must have the item order number in the heading.**\n\n**Core fields** for each file:\n\n- `filePath`: Full path to the file\n- `type`: Component classification\n- `architecturalPattern`: Design pattern used\n- `content`: Purpose and logic summary\n- `symbols`: Classes, interfaces, methods\n- `dependencies`: Imports/using statements\n- `businessContext`: Comprehensive detail of all business logic, how it contributes to requirements\n- `referenceFiles`: Files using this file''s symbols\n- `relevanceScore`: 1-10\n- `evidenceLevel`: \"verified\" or \"inferred\"\n- `uncertainties`: Unclear aspects\n- `platformAbstractions`: Platform base classes used\n- `serviceContext`: Microservice ownership\n- `dependencyInjection`: DI registrations\n- `genericTypeParameters`: Generic type relationships\n\n**Message Bus Analysis** (CRITICAL FOR CONSUMERS):\n\n- `messageBusAnalysis`: When analyzing Consumer files (`*Consumer.cs` extending `PlatformApplicationMessageBusConsumer<T>`):\n  1. Identify the `*BusMessage` type used\n  2. Grep search ALL services to find files that send/publish this message\n  3. List all producer files and their service locations in `messageBusProducers`\n\n**Targeted Aspect Analysis** (`targetedAspectAnalysis`):\n\nFor **Front-End items**:\n\n- `componentHierarchy`, `routeConfig`, `routeGuards`\n- `stateManagementStores`, `dataBindingPatterns`, `validationStrategies`\n\nFor **Back-End items**:\n\n- `authorizationPolicies`, `commands`, `queries`\n- `domainEntities`, `repositoryPatterns`, `businessRuleImplementations`\n\nFor **Consumer items**:\n\n- `messageBusMessage`, `messageBusProducers`\n- `crossServiceIntegration`, `handleLogicWorkflow`\n\n**MANDATORY PROGRESS TRACKING**: After processing every 10 files, you **MUST** update `Items Processed` in `## Progress`, run a `CONTEXT_ANCHOR_CHECK`, and explicitly state your progress. After each file, add its path to the `## Processed Files` list.\n\n### PHASE 1C: OVERALL ANALYSIS\n\nWrite comprehensive `overallAnalysis:` summary showing:\n\n- Complete end-to-end workflows discovered\n- Key architectural patterns and relationships\n- All business logic workflows: From front-end to back-end\n  - Example: Front-end Component => Controller Api Service => Command/Query => EventHandler => Others (Send email, producer bus message)\n  - Example: Background Job => Event Handler => Others\n- Integration points and dependencies\n- Cross-service dependencies identified\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: PLAN GENERATION\n\n**Prerequisites**: Ensure ALL files are analyzed. Read the ENTIRE analysis notes file.\n\nGenerate detailed implementation plan under `## Plan` heading:\n\n- Follow coding conventions from platform documentation\n- Think step-by-step with todo list\n- Reference patterns for each step\n\n### PHASE 2.1: VERIFY AND REFACTOR\n\nFirst, verify and ensure your implementation plan follows code patterns and conventions from these files:\n\n- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` - Platform patterns\n- `.github/instructions/frontend-angular.instructions.md` - Frontend patterns\n- `.github/instructions/backend-dotnet.instructions.md` - Backend patterns\n- `.github/instructions/clean-code.instructions.md` - Clean code rules\n\nThen verify and ensure your implementation plan satisfies clean code rules.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: APPROVAL GATE\n\n**CRITICAL**: Present the plan for explicit user approval. **DO NOT** proceed without it.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: EXECUTION\n\nOnce approved:\n\n1. Before creating or modifying **ANY** file, you **MUST** first load its relevant entry from your `## Knowledge Graph`\n2. Use all **EXECUTION_SAFEGUARDS**\n3. If any step fails, **HALT**, report the failure, and return to the APPROVAL GATE\n\n---\n\n## SUCCESS VALIDATION\n\nBefore completion:\n\n1. Verify implementation against all requirements\n2. Document under `## Success Validation` heading\n3. Summarize changes in `changelog.md`\n\n---\n\n## Coding Guidelines\n\n- **Evidence-based approach**: Use grep and semantic search to verify assumptions\n- **Service boundary discovery**: Find endpoints before assuming responsibilities\n- **Never assume service ownership**: Verify patterns with code evidence\n- **Platform-first approach**: Use established templates\n- **Cross-service sync**: Use event bus, not direct database access\n- **CQRS adherence**: Follow established Command/Query patterns\n- **Clean architecture respect**: Maintain proper layer dependencies\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:19:11.749Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Full-Stack Agents requiring structured feature implementation in dotnet and angular environments.","zh":"适合需要在dotnet和angular环境中实现结构化功能的全栈代理。","ja":"dotnetおよびangular環境で構造化された機能を実装する必要があるフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"dotnet 및 angular 환경에서 구조화된 기능을 구현해야 하는 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Full-Stack que requieren implementación de características estructuradas en entornos dotnet y angular.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Full-Stack nécessitant une mise en œuvre de fonctionnalités structurées dans des environnements dotnet et angular.","de":"Ideal für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine strukturierte Implementierung von Funktionen in dotnet- und angular-Umgebungen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes Full-Stack que requerem implementação de recursos estruturados em ambientes dotnet e angular.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Full-Stack, требующих структурированной реализации функций в средах dotnet и angular.","ar":"مثالي لعميل كامل الحزمة الذي يتطلب تنفيذ ميزات منظم في بيئات dotnet و angular."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement new features by copying and pasting specific folders and files, such as the .* folder and AGENTS.md, to the root of a project, utilizing todo lists for step-by-step planning and execution, covering all phases from start to end, including child tasks, and preserving context through every operation.","zh":"使代理能够通过复制和粘贴特定文件夹和文件（例如 .* 文件夹和AGENTS.md）到项目根目录，利用待办事项列表进行分步规划和执行，涵盖从开始到结束的所有阶段，包括子任务，并在每个操作中保持上下文。","ja":"エージェントが特定のフォルダやファイル（たとえば、.* フォルダやAGENTS.md）をプロジェクトのルートにコピーして貼り付けることで、新しい機能を実装できるようにし、ステップごとの計画と実行のためのtodoリストを利用し、開始から終了までのすべての段階をカバーし、子タスクを含み、すべての操作でコンテキストを保持します。","ko":"에이전트가 특정 폴더 및 파일(예: .* 폴더 및 AGENTS.md)을 프로젝트 루트에 복사하여 붙여 넣음으로써 새로운 기능을 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 단계별 계획 및 실행을 위한 todo 목록을 활용하며, 시작부터 종료까지 모든 단계를 커버하며, 하위 작업을 포함하며, 모든 작업에서 컨텍스트를 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar nuevas características copiando y pegando carpetas y archivos específicos, como la carpeta .* y AGENTS.md, en la raíz de un proyecto, utilizando listas de tareas para la planificación y ejecución paso a paso, cubriendo todas las fases desde el inicio hasta el final, incluyendo tareas secundarias, y preservando el contexto a través de cada operación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités en copiant et en collant des dossiers et des fichiers spécifiques, tels que le dossier .* et AGENTS.md, à la racine d''un projet, en utilisant des listes de tâches pour la planification et l''exécution étape par étape, couvrant toutes les phases de début à fin, y compris les tâches secondaires, et en préservant le contexte à travers chaque opération.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, neue Funktionen durch Kopieren und Einfügen spezifischer Ordner und Dateien, wie den Ordner .* und AGENTS.md, in die Wurzel eines Projekts zu implementieren, unter Verwendung von Todo-Listen für die schrittweise Planung und Ausführung, die alle Phasen von Anfang bis Ende abdecken, einschließlich Kindertasks, und den Kontext durch jeden Vorgang hindurch erhalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar novos recursos copiando e colando pastas e arquivos específicos, como a pasta .* e AGENTS.md, para a raiz de um projeto, utilizando listas de tarefas para planejamento e execução passo a passo, cobrindo todas as fases desde o início até o fim, incluindo tarefas secundárias, e preservando o contexto por meio de cada operação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать новые функции путем копирования и вставки определенных папок и файлов, таких как папка .* и AGENTS.md, в корень проекта, используя списки дел для пошагового планирования и выполнения, покрывая все фазы от начала до конца, включая дочерние задачи, и сохраняя контекст при каждой операции.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تنفيذ ميزات جديدة عن طريق نسخ ولصق مجلدات وملفات محددة ، مثل المجلد .* و AGENTS.md ، إلى الجذر لمشروع ، باستخدام قوائم المهام لتخطيط التنفيذ خطوة بخطوة ، وتغطية جميع المراحل من البداية إلى النهاية ، بما في ذلك المهام الفرعية ، وحفظ السياق من خلال كل عملية."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing new requirements in dotnet projects","Enhancing angular applications with structured feature additions","Managing and planning feature implementation using detailed todo lists"],"zh":["在dotnet项目中实现新的要求","使用结构化的功能增强来增强angular应用程序","使用详细的todo列表来管理和计划功能实现"],"ja":["dotnetプロジェクトで新しい要求を実装する","構造化された機能の追加を使用してangularアプリケーションを強化する","詳細なtodoリストを使用して機能の実装を管理および計画する"],"ko":["dotnet 프로젝트에서 새로운 요구 사항을 구현하는 것","구조화된 기능 추가를 사용하여 angular 애플리케이션을 강화하는 것","详细한 todo 목록을 사용하여 기능 구현을 관리 및 계획하는 것"],"es":["Implementar nuevos requisitos en proyectos dotnet","Mejorar aplicaciones angular con adiciones de características estructuradas","Gestionar y planificar la implementación de características utilizando listas de tareas detalladas"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre de nouveaux exigences dans les projets dotnet","Améliorer les applications angular avec des ajouts de fonctionnalités structurées","Gérer et planifier la mise en œuvre de fonctionnalités en utilisant des listes de tâches détaillées"],"de":["Implementierung neuer Anforderungen in dotnet-Projekten","Verbesserung von angular-Anwendungen mit strukturierten Funktionsadditionen","Verwaltung und Planung der Funktionsimplementierung unter Verwendung detaillierter Todo-Listen"],"pt":["Implementação de novos requisitos em projetos dotnet","Melhoria de aplicações angular com adições de recursos estruturados","Gerenciamento e planejamento da implementação de recursos usando listas de tarefas detalhadas"],"ru":["Реализация новых требований в проектах dotnet","Улучшение приложений angular с помощью структурированных добавлений функций","Управление и планирование реализации функций с помощью подробных списков дел"],"ar":["تنفيذ متطلبات جديدة في مشاريع dotnet","تحسين التطبيقات angular بإضافة ميزات منسقة","إدارة وتخطيط تنفيذ الميزات باستخدام قوائم مهام مفصلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires expertise in dotnet and angular","Demands meticulous planning and step-by-step execution","Limited to full-stack development environments"],"zh":["需要dotnet和angular的专业知识","需要详细的规划和分步执行","仅限于全栈开发环境"],"ja":["dotnetおよびangularの専門知識が必要","詳細な計画とステップごとの実行が必要","フルスタック開発環境のみに限定される"],"ko":["dotnet 및 angular의 전문 지식이 필요","상세한 계획 및 단계별 실행이 필요","풀스택 개발 환경에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en dotnet y angular","Exige una planificación y ejecución meticulosas y paso a paso","Limitado a entornos de desarrollo full-stack"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise en dotnet et angular","Exige une planification et une exécution méticuleuses et étape par étape","Limité aux environnements de développement full-stack"],"de":["Erfordert Expertenwissen in dotnet und angular","Fordert eine sorgfältige Planung und schrittweise Ausführung","Begrenzt auf Full-Stack-Entwicklungsumgebungen"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento especializado em dotnet e angular","Exige planejamento meticuloso e execução passo a passo","Limitado a ambientes de desenvolvimento full-stack"],"ru":["Требует специализированных знаний в области dotnet и angular","Требует тщательного планирования и пошагового выполнения","Ограничен средами разработки full-stack"],"ar":["يتطلب خبرة في dotnet و angular","يطالب بالتخطيط الدقيق والتنفيذ خطوة بخطوة","محدود بالبيئات التطويرية الكاملة الحزمة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('WILLOSCAR/research-units-pipeline-skills/argument-selfloop', 'community', 'WILLOSCAR', 'research-units-pipeline-skills', 'WILLOSCAR/research-units-pipeline-skills', 'argument-selfloop', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z', '2026-02-18T08:19:07.040Z', NULL, '{"id":"WILLOSCAR/research-units-pipeline-skills/argument-selfloop","name":"argument-selfloop","description":{"zh":"Argument Self-loop 技术是一种通过结构化的中间文物来实现显式约束下的论证操作的方法，用于升级文本生成能力","ja":"論理的自己ループは、明示的な制約の下で論理的操作を実行するために、構造化された中間アーティファクトを使用する方法です","ko":"인자 셀프 루프는 명시적인 제약조건 하에서 논리적 동작을 수행하기 위해 구조화된 중간 아티팩트를 사용하는 방법입니다","es":"Argument Self-loop es un mecanismo que mejora la generación de texto mediante la ejecución de acciones de argumentación bajo restricciones explícitas. Permite escribir, auto-revisar y mejorar la coherencia del texto","fr":"Argument Self-loop est un mécanisme qui améliore la génération de texte en exécutant des actions d''argumentation sous contraintes explicites. Il permet d''écrire, de réviser et d''améliorer la cohérence du texte","de":"Argument Self-loop ist ein Mechanismus, der die Textgenerierung durch die Ausführung von Argumentationshandlungen unter expliziten Einschränkungen verbessert. Er ermöglicht es, zu schreiben, selbst zu überprüfen und die Kohärenz des Textes zu verbessern","pt":"O Argument Self-loop é uma habilidade que opera como uma unidade de execução semântica, permitindo a melhoria da geração de texto.","ru":"Argument Self-loop — это навык, который работает как семантическая единица выполнения, позволяющая улучшить генерацию текста.","ar":"argument self-loop هو مهارة تعمل كوحدة تنفيذ семантиكية، مما يسمح بتحسين توليد النص.","en":"Research pipelines as semantic execution units: each skill declares inputs/outputs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails. Evidence-first methodology prevents hollow writing through structured intermediate artifacts."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Argument Self-loop 技术","ja":"論理的自己ループ","ko":"인자 셀프 루프","es":"Argument Self-loop: Mejora de la Generación de Texto","fr":"Argument Self-loop : Amélioration de la Génération de Texte","de":"Argument Self-loop: Verbesserung der Textgenerierung","pt":"Argument Self-loop: Otimização de Pipelines de Pesquisa","ru":"Argument Self-loop: Улучшение исследовательских трубопров...","ar":"argument self-loop: تحسين أنابيب البحث","en":"argument-selfloop"},"description":{"zh":"Argument Self-loop 技术是一种通过结构化的中间文物来实现显式约束下的论证操作的方法，用于升级文本生成能力","ja":"論理的自己ループは、明示的な制約の下で論理的操作を実行するために、構造化された中間アーティファクトを使用する方法です","ko":"인자 셀프 루프는 명시적인 제약조건 하에서 논리적 동작을 수행하기 위해 구조화된 중간 아티팩트를 사용하는 방법입니다","es":"Argument Self-loop es un mecanismo que mejora la generación de texto mediante la ejecución de acciones de argumentación bajo restricciones explícitas. Permit...","fr":"Argument Self-loop est un mécanisme qui améliore la génération de texte en exécutant des actions d''argumentation sous contraintes explicites. Il permet d''écr...","de":"Argument Self-loop ist ein Mechanismus, der die Textgenerierung durch die Ausführung von Argumentationshandlungen unter expliziten Einschränkungen verbessert...","pt":"O Argument Self-loop é uma habilidade que opera como uma unidade de execução semântica, permitindo a melhoria da geração de texto.","ru":"Argument Self-loop — это навык, который работает как семантическая единица выполнения, позволяющая улучшить генерацию текста.","ar":"argument self-loop هو مهارة تعمل كوحدة تنفيذ семантиكية، مما يسمح بتحسين توليد النص.","en":"Research pipelines as semantic execution units: each skill declares inputs/outputs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails. Evidence-first methodology prevents ..."},"definition":{"en":"Research pipelines as semantic execution units: each skill declares inputs/outputs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails. Evidence-first methodology prevents hollow writing through structured intermediate artifacts."},"features":{"zh":["结构化的中间文物","显式约束下的论证操作","升级文本生成能力","pipeline-native 组件","自我检查和修订功能"],"ja":["構造化された中間アーティファクト","明示的な制約の下での論理的操作","テキスト生成能力の向上","パイプラインネイティブコンポーネント","自己チェックと修正機能"],"ko":["구조화된 중간 아티팩트","명시적인 제약조건 하での 논리적 동작","텍스트 생성 능력의 업그레이드","파이프라인 네이티브 컴포넌트","자기 체크 및 수정 기능"],"es":["Ejecución de acciones de argumentación bajo restricciones explícitas","Escritura y auto-revisión de textos","Mantenimiento de un registro de argumentos para garantizar la coherencia","Revisión y mejora del texto hasta lograr la coherencia deseada","Integración con otros mecanismos de auto-revisión"],"fr":["Exécution d''actions d''argumentation sous contraintes explicites","Écriture et révision automatique de textes","Maintenance d''un registre d''arguments pour assurer la cohérence","Révision et amélioration du texte jusqu''à atteindre la cohérence désirée","Intégration avec d''autres mécanismes de révision automatique"],"de":["Ausführung von Argumentationshandlungen unter expliziten Einschränkungen","Schreiben und Selbstüberprüfung von Texten","Aufrechterhaltung eines Registers von Argumenten, um die Kohärenz zu gewährleisten","Überprüfung und Verbesserung des Textes, bis die gewünschte Kohärenz erreicht ist","Integration mit anderen Mechanismen der Selbstüberprüfung"],"pt":["Escrita seção a seção","Verificação automática parágrafo a parágrafo","Manutenção de um registro de argumentos","Revisão de apenas o que falha","Melhoria da geração de texto"],"ru":["Написание раздела за разделом","Автоматическая проверка абзаца за абзацем","Ведение реестра аргументов","Правка только того, что не проходит","Улучшение генерации текста"],"ar":["كتابة القسم بعد القسم","التحقق التلقائي من الفقرة إلى الفقرة","صيانة سجل للحجج","مراجعة ما فشل فقط","تحسين توليد النص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Argument Self-loop","结构化中间文物","显式约束","论证操作","文本生成","pipeline-native","自我检查"],"ja":["論理的自己ループ","構造化された中間アーティファクト","明示的な制約","論理的操作","テキスト生成","パイプラインネイティブ","自己チェック"],"ko":["인자 셀프 루프","구조화된 중간 아티팩트","명시적인 제약조건","논리적 동작","텍스트 생성","파이프라인 네이티브","자기 체크"],"es":["generación de texto","acción de argumentación","restricciones explícitas","auto-revisión","coherencia del texto","mecanismos de revisión","textos coherentes","generación de contenido"],"fr":["génération de texte","action d''argumentation","contraintes explicites","révision automatique","cohérence du texte","mécanismes de révision","textes cohérents","génération de contenu"],"de":["Textgenerierung","Argumentationshandlung","explizite Einschränkungen","Selbstüberprüfung","Kohärenz des Textes","Mechanismen der Selbstüberprüfung","kohärente Texte","Inhaltsgenerierung"],"pt":["argument self-loop","pipelines de pesquisa","execução de ações de argumentação","restrições explícitas","geração de texto","otimização de pipelines"],"ru":["argument self-loop","исследовательские трубопроводы","выполнение аргументативных действий","явные ограничения","генерация текста","улучшение трубопроводов"],"ar":["argument self-loop","أنابيب البحث","تنفيذ إجراءات الحجة","قيود صريحة","توليد النص","تحسين الأنابيب"]}},"owner":"WILLOSCAR","repo":"research-units-pipeline-skills","repoPath":"WILLOSCAR/research-units-pipeline-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.465Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"argument-selfloop","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Argument Self-loop (write -> self-check -> ledger -> revise)\n\nPurpose: upgrade C5 from “generate text” to “execute argument actions under explicit constraints”.\n\nThis skill operationalizes the mechanism you described as a reusable, pipeline-native component:\n- write section-by-section\n- self-check paragraph-by-paragraph\n- maintain a small argument ledger that makes dependencies explicit\n- revise only what fails until the chain is continuous\n\nIt complements (not replaces) the other self-loops:","body":"# Argument Self-loop (write -> self-check -> ledger -> revise)\n\nPurpose: upgrade C5 from “generate text” to “execute argument actions under explicit constraints”.\n\nThis skill operationalizes the mechanism you described as a reusable, pipeline-native component:\n- write section-by-section\n- self-check paragraph-by-paragraph\n- maintain a small argument ledger that makes dependencies explicit\n- revise only what fails until the chain is continuous\n\nIt complements (not replaces) the other self-loops:\n- `evidence-selfloop`: blocks writing when packs are not writeable (do not pad)\n- `writer-selfloop`: blocks template voice, missing sections/leads, scope/citation violations\n- `argument-selfloop` (this skill): blocks *argument discontinuity* and *premise drift* (even when prose is fluent)\n\n\n## Core idea: two intermediate artifacts (never in the paper)\n\nThis skill treats “argument structure” as a first-class intermediate artifact, like evidence packs.\n\nOutputs:\n- `output/SECTION_ARGUMENT_SUMMARIES.jsonl` (structured; per-section/per-paragraph argument moves)\n- `output/ARGUMENT_SKELETON.md` (compact narrative + dependency map; not a prose restatement)\n- `output/ARGUMENT_SELFLOOP_TODO.md` (PASS/FAIL + actionable edits)\n\nThese files are *not* reader-facing and must never be merged into `output/DRAFT.md`.\n\nDownstream:\n- `paragraph-curator` uses `output/SECTION_ARGUMENT_SUMMARIES.jsonl` (moves/outputs) + the `## Consistency Contract` to run a controlled select->evaluate->subset->fuse pass without changing citation keys.\n\n\n\n## What this self-loop enforces (your 3 invariants)\n\nAfter you complete a section (H3 or key front matter), the section must satisfy:\n\n1) **Correct narrative linkage (paragraph-to-paragraph)**\n- the relation between adjacent paragraphs is explicit (cause/contrast/refinement/boundary)\n- no silent topic-switch; no “jump cut”\n\n2) **Closed argument loop (section-level)**\nThe section answers, in its own text (not in a hidden outline):\n- what question is it resolving?\n- what argument path does it take?\n- what is the conclusion?\n- what premises does the conclusion rely on?\n\n3) **Premises + definitions are explicit and stable**\n- new terms / protocol assumptions are defined at first use\n- the definition matches global usage (no drift)\n- task/metric/constraint assumptions do not silently change across sections\n\nThe self-check must result in concrete edits: add a missing definition, add a bridge sentence, add an explicit contrast, add a scope boundary, delete/reorder a paragraph, or strengthen the local conclusion.\n\n\n## Paragraph contract (argument actions)\n\nEvery paragraph must execute at least one argument action and be locally self-consistent.\nUse this action set (can be combined, but never empty):\n\n- `Claim`: a testable judgement/conclusion (avoid generic background)\n- `Definition/Setup`: introduce a concept, assumption, task definition, protocol, comparison set\n- `Justification`: reasoning chain or evidence support (including citations)\n- `Contrast/Differentiation`: clarify differences, remove ambiguity\n- `Boundary/Failure`: applicability limits, failure modes, threats to validity\n- `Local Conclusion`: a reusable takeaway / constraint that downstream paragraphs can rely on\n\nOne-sentence self-check (per paragraph):\n- \"This paragraph’s action(s) are: <…>. Its output is: <…>.\"\n\nIf you cannot answer, the paragraph must be rewritten/merged/split until the action and output are clear.\n\n\n## How to run it (LLM-first workflow)\n\n1) Pick the scope of this pass\n- default: run it after `writer-selfloop` PASS, before merge\n- incremental: run it after finishing 1-2 H3s, so you catch drift early\n\n2) For each target section file (start with H3 bodies)\n- read the section\n- do a paragraph-by-paragraph action labeling *in the ledger*, not in the prose\n- identify failures (missing definition, missing bridge, missing conclusion, implicit premise)\n- apply the fix to the *section file* (`sections/S<sub_id>.md`) without changing citation keys\n\n3) Update the two-level ledger\n- write/update the record for that section in `output/SECTION_ARGUMENT_SUMMARIES.jsonl`\n- update `output/ARGUMENT_SKELETON.md` so it reflects:\n  - the section’s functional role in the paper\n  - what premises it consumes\n  - what conclusions/definitions it produces for downstream sections\n\n4) Write `output/ARGUMENT_SELFLOOP_TODO.md`\n- `- Status: FAIL` + a list of concrete edits when any section fails\n- `- Status: PASS` only when all required sections are coherent and premises are stable\n\n5) Rerun until PASS\n\n\n## Output contract\n\n### `output/ARGUMENT_SELFLOOP_TODO.md`\n\nMust exist and start with:\n- `- Status: PASS|FAIL`\n\nRecommended structure (keep it short and debuggable):\n- `## Failures (blocking)`\n- `## Fix plan (actionable edits)` (per file)\n- `## Premise drift watchlist (non-blocking)`\n\n\n### `output/SECTION_ARGUMENT_SUMMARIES.jsonl`\n\nJSONL (one record per section/subsection).\n\nRequired fields per record:\n- `kind`: `h3` | `front_matter` | `discussion` | `conclusion` (minimal set)\n- `id`: for H3 use the subsection id (e.g., `\"3.2\"`)\n- `title`\n- `section_id`, `section_title` (for H3)\n- `section_role`: what this unit does in the paper (e.g., `mechanism`, `evaluation_lens`, `risk_lens`, `synthesis`)\n- `depends_on`: list of premises/definitions it assumes\n- `adds`: list of premises/definitions/conclusions it introduces\n- `paragraphs`: list of objects, each with:\n  - `i` (1-based paragraph index)\n  - `moves` (non-empty list; pick from: `claim`, `definition_setup`, `justification`, `contrast`, `boundary_failure`, `local_conclusion`)\n  - `output` (one sentence: what this paragraph produces)\n\nNotes:\n- This is an intermediate ledger: short, structural, no prose restatement.\n- Do not paste long sentences from the draft. Use short summaries.\n\n\n### `output/ARGUMENT_SKELETON.md`\n\nA compact narrative/dependency map (not a retelling of the paper).\n\nIt should include:\n- each H2/H3''s **necessity** (what gap it fills)\n- explicit **dependencies** (premises consumed, outputs produced)\n- a global **Consistency Contract** section (single source of truth) that must not drift across edits:\n  - canonical terminology + synonym policy (what to call the same thing)\n  - task/environment/threat-model boundary (what counts as in-scope)\n  - evaluation protocol fields that make numbers interpretable (task + metric + constraint/budget/tool access)\n  - comparison set naming policy (baseline families; avoid drifting labels)\n\nMinimum format requirement:\n- `output/ARGUMENT_SKELETON.md` must contain a heading line: `## Consistency Contract`\n\nChange rule (regression trigger):\n- If you change any definition/protocol assumption/term naming, update the Consistency Contract first, then revise the affected `sections/*.md` to match, and rerun this self-loop until PASS.\n\nKeep it \"writer-facing\": no reader signposting, no “in this section we…”.\n\n\n## Routing rules (avoid polishing around missing substance)\n\n- If a section cannot produce a justified claim without new evidence: STOP and route to `evidence-selfloop`.\n- If a section fails due to template voice / missing citations / out-of-scope keys: route to `writer-selfloop` / `citation-*` first.\n- This skill is for argument continuity and premise hygiene, not for adding new facts.\n\n\n## Script (validator-only)\n\nThis skill includes a validator script so the pipeline can block on missing ledgers.\nIt does not write prose; it only checks that the required artifacts exist and that the ledger covers all H3s.\n\n### Quick Start\n\n- `python .codex/skills/argument-selfloop/scripts/run.py --workspace workspaces/<ws>`\n\n### All Options\n\n- `--workspace <dir>`\n- `--unit-id <U###>`\n- `--inputs <semicolon-separated>`\n- `--outputs <semicolon-separated>`\n- `--checkpoint <C#>`\n\n### Examples\n\n- Validate the ledgers exist + are PASS + cover all H3:\n  - `python .codex/skills/argument-selfloop/scripts/run.py --workspace workspaces/<ws>`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:19:07.040Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Language Agents requiring structured argumentation and semantic execution capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要结构化论证和语义执行能力的高级语言代理。","ja":"高度な言語エージェントが構造化された議論とセマンティック実行機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"구조화된 논증과 의미적 실행 기능이 필요한 고급 언어 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que requieren argumentación estructurada y capacidades de ejecución semántica.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Langage Avancés nécessitant une argumentation structurée et des capacités d''exécution sémantique.","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche Sprachagenten, die eine strukturierte Argumentation und semantische Ausführungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que requerem argumentação estruturada e capacidades de execução semântica.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых языковых агентов, требующих структурированного аргументирования и возможностей семантического выполнения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة متقدم يتطلب حجة منظمة وقدرات تنفيذ دلالية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute argument actions under explicit constraints using evidence-first methodology, maintaining a ledger of dependencies and revising content through a self-check mechanism, leveraging pipeline-native components for efficient text generation and validation.","zh":"赋予代理执行明确约束下的论证动作的能力，使用证据优先的方法，维护依赖关系的账本，并通过自我检查机制修订内容，利用管道原生组件实现高效的文本生成和验证。","ja":"エージェントが明示的な制約の下で議論アクションを実行する能力を付与し、証拠優先の方法を使用して依存関係の台帳を維持し、自己チェックメカニズムを通じてコンテンツを修正し、パイプラインネイティブコンポーネントを利用して効率的なテキスト生成と検証を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 명시적인 제약조건 하에서 논증 행동을 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 증거 우선 방식을 사용하여 의존성 레저를 유지하고, 자기 검사 메커니즘을 통해 콘텐츠를 수정하며, 파이프라인 네이티브 구성 요소를 활용하여 효율적인 텍스트 생성 및 검증을 수행합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar acciones de argumentación bajo restricciones explícitas utilizando la metodología de evidencia en primer lugar, manteniendo un registro de dependencias y revisando el contenido a través de un mecanismo de autoverificación, aprovechando componentes nativos de la canalización para una generación y validación de texto eficientes.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des actions d''argumentation sous des contraintes explicites en utilisant la méthodologie de preuve en premier lieu, en maintenant un registre des dépendances et en révisant le contenu à travers un mécanisme d''auto-vérification, en exploitant les composants natifs du pipeline pour une génération et une validation de texte efficaces.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Argumentationsaktionen unter expliziten Einschränkungen auszuführen, indem sie die evidenzbasierte Methodik verwenden, ein Register der Abhängigkeiten führen und den Inhalt durch einen Selbstprüfmechanismus überprüfen, wobei pipeline-eigene Komponenten für eine effiziente Textgenerierung und -validierung genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar ações de argumentação sob restrições explícitas, utilizando metodologia de evidência em primeiro lugar, mantendo um registro de dependências e revisando o conteúdo por meio de um mecanismo de autoverificação, aproveitando componentes nativos do pipeline para geração e validação de texto eficientes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять действия аргументации под явными ограничениями, используя методологию, основанную на доказательствах, поддерживая реестр зависимостей и пересматривая содержание через механизм само-проверки, используя компоненты, родные для конвейера, для эффективной генерации и проверки текста.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تنفيذ إجراءات الحجة تحت قيود صريحة باستخدام منهجية الأولوية للأدلة، مع الحفاظ على سجل للاتكاليات ومراجعة المحتوى من خلال آلية التحقق الذاتي، واستخدام مكونات.pipeline الأصلية للتحليل النصي والتحقق الفعال."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating coherent and continuous argument chains","Validating paragraph-level consistency and logical flow","Maintaining explicit dependencies through a small argument ledger"],"zh":["生成连贯且连续的论证链","验证段落级的一致性和逻辑流程","通过小型论证账本维护明确的依赖关系"],"ja":["一貫性と連続性のある議論チェーンを生成する","段落レベルの整合性と論理的流れを検証する","小規模な議論台帳を通じて明示的な依存関係を維持する"],"ko":["일관성과 연속성이 있는 논증 체인을 생성하는 것","단락 수준의 일치성과 논리적 흐름을 검증하는 것","소규모 논증 장부를 통해 명시적인 의존성을 유지하는 것"],"es":["Generar cadenas de argumentos coherentes y continuas","Validar la consistencia y el flujo lógico a nivel de párrafo","Mantener dependencias explícitas a través de un pequeño registro de argumentos"],"fr":["Générer des chaînes d''arguments cohérentes et continues","Valider la cohérence et le flux logique au niveau du paragraphe","Maintenir des dépendances explicites à travers un petit registre d''arguments"],"de":["Erzeugen kohärenter und kontinuierlicher Argumentationsketten","Überprüfen der Konsistenz und des logischen Flusses auf Absatzebene","Beibehalten expliziter Abhängigkeiten durch ein kleines Argumentationsregister"],"pt":["Gerar cadeias de argumentação coerentes e contínuas","Validar a consistência e o fluxo lógico a nível de parágrafo","Manter dependências explícitas por meio de um pequeno registro de argumentos"],"ru":["Генерировать связные и непрерывные цепочки аргументации","Проверять последовательность и логический поток на уровне абзаца","Поддерживать явные зависимости посредством небольшого реестра аргументов"],"ar":["توليد سلاسل حجة متسقة ومستمرة","التحقق من الاتساق والتدفق المنطقي على مستوى الفقرة","الحفاظ على التبعيات الصريحة من خلال سجل صغير للحجج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit declaration of inputs, outputs, and acceptance criteria","Complements other self-loops but does not replace them"],"zh":["需要明确声明输入、输出和接受标准","补充其他自环但不能替代它们"],"ja":["入力、出力、および受け入れ基準を明示的に宣言する必要がある","他の自己ループを補完するが、それらを置き換えるものではない"],"ko":["입력, 출력 및 수락 기준을 명시적으로 선언해야 함","他の 자기 루프를 보완하지만, 대체하지는 않음"],"es":["Requiere la declaración explícita de entradas, salidas y criterios de aceptación","Complementa otros bucles de retroalimentación, pero no los reemplaza"],"fr":["Nécessite la déclaration explicite des entrées, des sorties et des critères d''acceptation","Complète d''autres boucles de rétroaction, mais ne les remplace pas"],"de":["Erfordert die explizite Deklaration von Eingaben, Ausgaben und Akzeptanzkriterien","Ergänzt andere Rückkopplungsschleifen, ersetzt sie jedoch nicht"],"pt":["Requer declaração explícita de entradas, saídas e critérios de aceitação","Complementa outros loops auto-referenciais, mas não os substitui"],"ru":["Требует явного объявления входных, выходных данных и критериев принятия","Дополнит другие самопетли, но не заменяет их"],"ar":["يتطلب الإعلان الصريح للمدخلات والمخرجات ومعيار القبول","يكمل الحلقات الذاتية الأخرى، ولكنه لا يحل محلها"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
