fehler und die Bewahrung bestehender Modelle","pt":"O xlsx é uma ferramenta para modelagem financeira que exige precisão e atenção ao detalhe.","ru":"xlsx - это инструмент для финансового моделирования, который требует точности и внимания к деталям.","ar":"xlsx هو أداة لنمذجة مالية تتطلب دقة واهتمام بالتفاصيل.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["零公式错误","保留现有模板","金融模型的颜色编码","电子表格数据存储","Excel 文件格式兼容性","模板样式和约定匹配"],"ja":["ゼロフォーミュラエラー","既存テンプレートの保存","金融モデルのカラーコーディング","電子表計算データの保存","Excel ファイル形式の互換性","テンプレートスタイルと約束のマッチング"],"ko":["0개의 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 보존","금융 모델의 색상 코드","전자 스프레드시트 데이터 저장","Excel 파일 형식 호환성","템플릿 스타일과 약속 일치"],"es":["Cero errores de fórmula","Conservación de los modelos existentes","Respeto a las convenciones de formato y estilo","No imposición de formatos estandarizados","Análisis y reproducción exacta de los modelos existentes","Color codificación para modelos financieros"],"fr":["Zéro erreur de formule","Conservation des modèles existants","Respect des conventions de format et de style","Pas d''imposition de formats standardisés","Analyse et reproduction exacte des modèles existants","Codage de couleur pour les modèles financiers"],"de":["Null Formel-fehler","Bewahrung bestehender Modelle","Respekt für Format- und Stilkonventionen","Keine Auferlegung standardisierter Formate","Analyse und exakte Reproduktion bestehender Modelle","Farbcodierung für Finanzmodelle"],"pt":["Zero erros de fórmula","Preservação de templates existentes","Modelagem financeira precisa","Evite erros de fórmula como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Estudo e reprodução exata de formatos, estilos e convenções existentes"],"ru":["Отсутствие ошибок формул","Сохранение существующих шаблонов","Точное финансовое моделирование","Избегайте ошибок формул, таких как #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Изучение и точное воспроизведение существующих форматов, стилей и конвенций"],"ar":["لا أخطاء صيغ","الحفاظ على القوالب الحالية","نمذجة مالية دقيقة","تجنب أخطاء الصيغ مثل #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","دراسة وتمثيل دقيق لتنسيقات وأساليب وتقاليد موجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["xlsx","Excel 文件","电子表格","零公式错误","保留现有模板","金融模型","颜色编码","Excel 文件格式"],"ja":["xlsx","Excel ファイル","電子表計算","ゼロフォーミュラエラー","既存テンプレートの保存","金融モデル","カラーコーディング","Excel ファイル形式"],"ko":["xlsx","Excel 파일","전자 스프레드시트","0개의 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 보존","금융 모델","색상 코드","Excel 파일 형식"],"es":["xlsx","errores de fórmula","modelos existentes","convenciones de formato","color codificación","modelos financieros","creación de archivos xlsx","precisión y atención al detalle"],"fr":["xlsx","erreurs de formule","modèles existants","conventions de format","codage de couleur","modèles financiers","création de fichiers xlsx","précision et attention aux détails"],"de":["xlsx","Formel-fehler","bestehende Modelle","Format- und Stilkonventionen","Farbcodierung","Finanzmodelle","Erstellung von xlsx-Dateien","Präzision und Aufmerksamkeit für Details"],"pt":["xlsx","modelagem financeira","ferramentas de modelagem","erros de fórmula","templates existentes","precisão financeira"],"ru":["xlsx","финансовое моделирование","инструменты моделирования","ошибки формул","существующие шаблоны","финансовая точность"],"ar":["xlsx","نمذجة مالية","أدوات نمذجة","أخطاء صيغ","قوالب حالية","دقة مالية"]}},"owner":"nadavyigal","repo":"Running-coach-","repoPath":"nadavyigal/Running-coach-","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.466Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Comprehensive spreadsheet creation, editing, and analysis with support for formulas, formatting, data analysis, and visualization. When Claude needs to work with spreadsheets (.xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv, etc) for: (1) Creating new spreadsheets with formulas and formatting, (2) Reading or analyzing data, (3) Modify existing spreadsheets while preserving formulas, (4) Data analysis and visualization in spreadsheets, or (5) Recalculating formulas","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding S","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:19:44.639Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced Excel file manipulation capabilities with zero formula errors","zh":"非常适合需要高级Excel文件操作能力的数据分析代理，且无公式错误","ja":"データ分析エージェントが高度なExcelファイル操作機能を必要とする場合に最適で、ゼロのフォーミュラエラー","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트가 고급 Excel 파일 조작 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합하며, 잔여 수식 오류가 없음","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de manipulación de archivos de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant des capacités avancées de manipulation de fichiers Excel avec zéro erreur de formule","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte Excel-Dateimanipulationsfunktionen mit null Formel-fehlern benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de manipulação de arquivos do Excel com zero erros de fórmula","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности манипулирования файлами Excel с нулевым количеством ошибок формул","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل البيانات الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتعديل ملفات إكسل مع عدم وجود أي أخطاء في الصيغ"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and modify Excel files with precise formatting and style matching, while avoiding formula errors like #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, and #NAME?, utilizing Excel templates and color coding conventions","zh":"赋予代理生成和修改Excel文件的能力，具有精确的格式和样式匹配，同时避免#REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A和#NAME?等公式错误，利用Excel模板和颜色编码约定","ja":"エージェントがExcelファイルを生成および変更する能力を与え、正確なフォーマットとスタイルのマッチングを実現し、#REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A、#NAME?などのフォーミュラエラーを回避し、Excelテンプレートと色コード規約を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 Excel 파일을 생성 및 수정할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 정확한 서식과 스타일을 일치시키고, #REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A、#NAME? 등의 수식 오류를 피하며, Excel 템플릿과 색상 코드 규칙을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar y modificar archivos de Excel con formato y estilo precisos, mientras evita errores de fórmula como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A y #NAME?, utilizando plantillas de Excel y convenciones de codificación de colores","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de modifier des fichiers Excel avec un formatage et un style précis, tout en évitant les erreurs de formule comme #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A et #NAME?, en utilisant des modèles Excel et des conventions de codage de couleurs","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Excel-Dateien mit präziser Formatierung und Stilübereinstimmung zu generieren und zu modifizieren, während Formel-fehler wie #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A und #NAME? vermieden werden, unter Verwendung von Excel-Vorlagen und Farbcodierungs-konventionen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e modificar arquivos do Excel com formatação precisa e estilo de correspondência, evitando erros de fórmula como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A e #NAME?, utilizando modelos do Excel e convenções de codificação de cores","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и изменять файлы Excel с точной форматировкой и стилевым соответствием, избегая ошибок формул, таких как #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A и #NAME?, используя шаблоны Excel и конвенции цветового кодирования","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء وتعديل ملفات إكسل بدقة الصياغة والتنسيق، وتجنب أخطاء الصيغ مثل #REF! و #DIV/0! و #VALUE! و #N/A و #NAME?، عن طريق استخدام قوالب إكسل وأساليب الترميز بالألوان"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating financial model updates with exact format preservation","Generating Excel reports with zero formula errors","Debugging #REF! and #DIV/0! errors in existing Excel files","Modifying existing templates while maintaining established conventions"],"zh":["自动更新财务模型，保留确切的格式","生成Excel报告，且无公式错误","调试现有Excel文件中的#REF!和#DIV/0!错误","修改现有模板，同时保持既定的约定"],"ja":["財務モデルの自動更新、正確なフォーマットの保存","Excelレポートの生成、フォーミュラエラーのゼロ化","既存のExcelファイルの#REF!および#DIV/0!エラーのデバッグ","既存テンプレートの変更、既存の規約の維持"],"ko":["재무 모델의 자동 업데이트와 정확한 형식 보존","Excel 보고서 생성 및 수식 오류 제거","기존 Excel 파일의 #REF! 및 #DIV/0! 오류 디버깅","기존 템플릿 수정 및既存 규약 유지"],"es":["Automatizar actualizaciones de modelos financieros con preservación exacta de formato","Generar informes de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas","Depurar errores #REF! y #DIV/0! en archivos de Excel existentes","Modificar plantillas existentes mientras se mantienen las convenciones establecidas"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de modèles financiers avec préservation exacte du format","Générer des rapports Excel avec zéro erreur de formule","Déboguer les erreurs #REF! et #DIV/0! dans les fichiers Excel existants","Modifier les modèles existants tout en maintenant les conventions établies"],"de":["Automatisierung von Finanzmodell-Updates mit exakter Format-Erhaltung","Generierung von Excel-Berichten mit null Formel-fehlern","Fehlerbehebung von #REF!- und #DIV/0!-Fehlern in bestehenden Excel-Dateien","Modifizierung von bestehenden Vorlagen unter Beibehaltung etablierter Konventionen"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de modelos financeiros com preservação exata do formato","Gerar relatórios do Excel com zero erros de fórmula","Depurar erros #REF! e #DIV/0! em arquivos do Excel existentes","Modificar modelos existentes mantendo as convenções estabelecidas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обновления финансовых моделей с точным сохранением формата","Генерировать отчеты Excel с нулевым количеством ошибок формул","Отладить ошибки #REF! и #DIV/0! в существующих файлах Excel","Изменять существующие шаблоны, сохраняя установленные конвенции"],"ar":["تأتمتة تحديث النماذج المالية مع الحفاظ على التنسيق بدقة","إنشاء تقارير إكسل مع عدم وجود أخطاء في الصيغ","تصحيح أخطاء #REF! و #DIV/0! في ملفات إكسل الحالية","تعديل القوالب الحالية مع الحفاظ على الأساليب المتبعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires precise template analysis to match existing format and style","May not impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns"],"zh":["需要对模板进行精确分析以匹配现有格式和样式","可能无法对具有既定模式的文件施加标准化格式"],"ja":["既存のフォーマットとスタイルにマッチするために、テンプレートの正確な分析が必要","既存のパターンを持つファイルに対して、標準化されたフォーマットを課すことができない可能性"],"ko":["既存의 형식과 스타일을 일치시키기 위해 템플릿에 대한 정확한 분석이 필요","既存의 패턴을 가진 파일에 대해 표준화된 형식을 강제할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere un análisis preciso de plantillas para coincidir con el formato y estilo existente","Puede no imponer un formato estandarizado en archivos con patrones establecidos"],"fr":["Nécessite une analyse précise de modèles pour correspondre au format et au style existant","Peut ne pas imposer un formatage standardisé sur les fichiers avec des modèles établis"],"de":["Erfordert eine präzise Vorlagenanalyse, um mit dem bestehenden Format und Stil übereinzustimmen","Kann auf Dateien mit etablierten Mustern kein standardisiertes Format aufzwingen"],"pt":["Exige análise precisa de modelos para corresponder ao formato e estilo existentes","Pode não impor formatação padronizada em arquivos com padrões estabelecidos"],"ru":["Требует точного анализа шаблонов для соответствия существующему формату и стилю","Может не навязывать стандартизированную форматировку файлам с установленными шаблонами"],"ar":["يتطلب تحليلًا دقيقًا للقوالب ليتوافق مع التنسيق والنمط الحاليين"," قد لا يفرض تنسيقًا معياريًا على الملفات التي تحتوي على أنماط محددة مسبقًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('alexey1312/swift-index/openspec-apply-change', 'community', 'alexey1312', 'swift-index', 'alexey1312/swift-index', 'openspec-apply-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.466Z', '2026-02-18T08:20:10.106Z', NULL, '{"id":"alexey1312/swift-index/openspec-apply-change","name":"openspec-apply-change","description":{"zh":"Openspec 应用更改实现 SwiftIndex 语义代码搜索，自动化代码变更管理","ja":"Openspec 変更の適用で SwiftIndex 语義コード検索を実現し、コードの変更管理を自動化する","ko":"Openspec 변경 적용을 통해 SwiftIndex 의미 코드 검색을 구현하고 코드 변경 관리를 자동화합니다","es":"OpenSpec-apply-change es una habilidad que implementa tareas desde un cambio de OpenSpec con SwiftIndex","fr":"OpenSpec-apply-change est une compétence qui met en œuvre des tâches à partir d''un changement OpenSpec avec SwiftIndex","de":"OpenSpec-apply-change ist eine Fähigkeit, die Aufgaben aus einer OpenSpec-Änderung mit SwiftIndex implementiert","en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Openspec 应用更改 - SwiftIndex 语义代码搜索","ja":"Openspec 変更の適用 - SwiftIndex 语義コード検索","ko":"Openspec 변경 적용 - SwiftIndex 의미 코드 검색","es":"Aplicar cambios con OpenSpec","fr":"Appliquer des modifications avec OpenSpec","de":"Änderungen mit OpenSpec anwenden","en":"openspec-apply-change"},"description":{"zh":"Openspec 应用更改实现 SwiftIndex 语义代码搜索，自动化代码变更管理","ja":"Openspec 変更の適用で SwiftIndex 语義コード検索を実現し、コードの変更管理を自動化する","ko":"Openspec 변경 적용을 통해 SwiftIndex 의미 코드 검색을 구현하고 코드 변경 관리를 자동화합니다","es":"OpenSpec-apply-change es una habilidad que implementa tareas desde un cambio de OpenSpec con SwiftIndex","fr":"OpenSpec-apply-change est une compétence qui met en œuvre des tâches à partir d''un changement OpenSpec avec SwiftIndex","de":"OpenSpec-apply-change ist eine Fähigkeit, die Aufgaben aus einer OpenSpec-Änderung mit SwiftIndex implementiert","en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"definition":{"en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"features":{"zh":["自动化代码变更管理","支持 SwiftIndex 语义代码搜索","提高开发效率","简化代码变更流程","实现代码搜索和变更的集成"],"ja":["コードの変更管理の自動化","SwiftIndex 语義コード検索のサポート","開発効率の向上","コード変更のワークフローを簡素化","コード検索と変更の統合を実現"],"ko":["코드 변경 관리 자동화","SwiftIndex 의미 코드 검색 지원","개발 효율성 향상","코드 변경 워크플ロー简化","코드 검색과 변경의 통합 구현"],"es":["Implementación de tareas desde un cambio de OpenSpec","Búsqueda de código semántico nativa de Swift con SwiftIndex","Selección automática de cambios","Inferencia de cambios a partir del contexto de conversación","Compatibilidad con varios cambios"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de tâches à partir d''un changement OpenSpec","Recherche de code sémantique native Swift avec SwiftIndex","Sélection automatique de modifications","Inférence de modifications à partir du contexte de conversation","Compatibilité avec plusieurs modifications"],"de":["Implementierung von Aufgaben aus einer OpenSpec-Änderung","Native semantische Code-Suche von Swift mit SwiftIndex","Automatische Auswahl von Änderungen","Ableitung von Änderungen aus dem Konversationskontext","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Änderungen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Openspec","SwiftIndex","语义代码搜索","代码变更管理","自动化","开发效率","代码搜索","代码变更"],"ja":["Openspec","SwiftIndex","语義コード検索","コードの変更管理","自動化","開発効率","コード検索","コード変更"],"ko":["Openspec","SwiftIndex","의미 코드 검색","코드 변경 관리","자동화","개발 효율성","코드 검색","코드 변경"],"es":["OpenSpec","SwiftIndex","búsqueda de código semántico","implementación de tareas","cambios de OpenSpec","desarrollo de software","IA para desarrolladores"],"fr":["OpenSpec","SwiftIndex","recherche de code sémantique","mise en œuvre de tâches","modifications OpenSpec","développement de logiciels","IA pour les développeurs"],"de":["OpenSpec","SwiftIndex","semantische Code-Suche","Implementierung von Aufgaben","OpenSpec-Änderungen","Software-Entwicklung","KI für Entwickler"]}},"owner":"alexey1312","repo":"swift-index","repoPath":"alexey1312/swift-index","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.466Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-apply-change","description":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change. Use when the user wants to start implementing, continue implementation, or work through tasks.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the *","body":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select\n\n   Always announce: \"Using change: <name>\" and how to override (e.g., `/opsx:apply <other>`).\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifact contains the tasks (typically \"tasks\" for spec-driven, check status for others)\n\n3. **Get apply instructions**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns:\n   - Context file paths (varies by schema - could be proposal/specs/design/tasks or spec/tests/implementation/docs)\n   - Progress (total, complete, remaining)\n   - Task list with status\n   - Dynamic instruction based on current state\n\n   **Handle states:**\n   - If `state: \"blocked\"` (missing artifacts): show message, suggest using openspec-continue-change\n   - If `state: \"all_done\"`: congratulate, suggest archive\n   - Otherwise: proceed to implementation\n\n4. **Read context files**\n\n   Read the files listed in `contextFiles` from the apply instructions output.\n   The files depend on the schema being used:\n   - **spec-driven**: proposal, specs, design, tasks\n   - Other schemas: follow the contextFiles from CLI output\n\n5. **Show current progress**\n\n   Display:\n   - Schema being used\n   - Progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - Remaining tasks overview\n   - Dynamic instruction from CLI\n\n6. **Implement tasks (loop until done or blocked)**\n\n   For each pending task:\n   - Show which task is being worked on\n   - Make the code changes required\n   - Keep changes minimal and focused\n   - Mark task complete in the tasks file: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n   - Continue to next task\n\n   **Pause if:**\n   - Task is unclear → ask for clarification\n   - Implementation reveals a design issue → suggest updating artifacts\n   - Error or blocker encountered → report and wait for guidance\n   - User interrupts\n\n7. **On completion or pause, show status**\n\n   Display:\n   - Tasks completed this session\n   - Overall progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - If all done: suggest archive\n   - If paused: explain why and wait for guidance\n\n**Output During Implementation**\n\n```\n## Implementing: <change-name> (schema: <schema-name>)\n\nWorking on task 3/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n\nWorking on task 4/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n```\n\n**Output On Completion**\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 7/7 tasks complete ✓\n\n### Completed This Session\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n...\n\nAll tasks complete! Ready to archive this change.\n```\n\n**Output On Pause (Issue Encountered)**\n\n```\n## Implementation Paused\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 4/7 tasks complete\n\n### Issue Encountered\n<description of the issue>\n\n**Options:**\n1. <option 1>\n2. <option 2>\n3. Other approach\n\nWhat would you like to do?\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n\n- Keep going through tasks until done or blocked\n- Always read context files before starting (from the apply instructions output)\n- If task is ambiguous, pause and ask before implementing\n- If implementation reveals issues, pause and suggest artifact updates\n- Keep code changes minimal and scoped to each task\n- Update task checkbox immediately after completing each task\n- Pause on errors, blockers, or unclear requirements - don''t guess\n- Use contextFiles from CLI output, don''t assume specific file names\n\n**Fluid Workflow Integration**\n\nThis skill supports the \"actions on a change\" model:\n\n- **Can be invoked anytime**: Before all artifacts are done (if tasks exist), after partial implementation, interleaved with other actions\n- **Allows artifact updates**: If implementation reveals design issues, suggest updating artifacts - not phase-locked, work fluidly\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:20:10.106Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring semantic code search and OpenSpec integration","zh":"适合需要语义代码搜索和OpenSpec集成的代码分析代理","ja":"セマンティックコード検索とOpenSpec統合を必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適","ko":"시멘틱 코드 검색 및 OpenSpec 통합이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren búsqueda de código semántica y integración con OpenSpec","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une recherche de code sémantique et une intégration OpenSpec","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die semantische Code-Suche und OpenSpec-Integration erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que requerem busca de código semântica e integração com OpenSpec","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих семантического поиска кода и интеграции с OpenSpec","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يتطلب بحث شفرة دلالية وتكامل مع OpenSpec"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement tasks from OpenSpec changes using SwiftIndex for Swift-native semantic code search, leveraging JSON output from `openspec list` commands and seamlessly integrating with conversation context to infer change names","zh":"赋予代理实现从OpenSpec更改中使用SwiftIndex的Swift本地语义代码搜索任务的能力，利用来自`openspec list`命令的JSON输出，并无缝地与对话上下文集成以推断更改名称","ja":"SwiftIndexを使用したSwiftネイティブのセマンティックコード検索により、OpenSpecの変更からタスクを実装できるようにエージェントをEmpowerし、`openspec list`コマンドからのJSON出力を利用し、会話のコンテキストとシームレスに統合して変更名を推測する","ko":"SwiftIndex를 사용하는 Swift 네이티브 시멘틱 코드 검색을 통해 OpenSpec 변경에서 태스크를 구현할 수 있는 에이전트를 배포하고, `openspec list` 명령어로부터의 JSON 출력을 활용하며, 대화 문脈과 무심하게 통합하여 변경 이름을 추론","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar tareas desde los cambios de OpenSpec utilizando SwiftIndex para la búsqueda de código semántico nativa de Swift, aprovechando la salida JSON de los comandos `openspec list` y integrándose de forma transparente con el contexto de conversación para inferir nombres de cambios","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des tâches à partir des modifications OpenSpec en utilisant SwiftIndex pour la recherche de code sémantique native Swift, en exploitant la sortie JSON des commandes `openspec list` et en s''intégrant de manière transparente avec le contexte de conversation pour déduire les noms de modifications","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Aufgaben aus OpenSpec-Änderungen umzusetzen, indem SwiftIndex für die native Swift-Semantikcode-Suche verwendet wird, die JSON-Ausgabe von `openspec list`-Befehlen nutzt und nahtlos in den Konversationskontext integriert wird, um Änderungsnamen abzuleiten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar tarefas a partir de alterações do OpenSpec usando SwiftIndex para busca de código semântica nativa em Swift, aproveitando a saída JSON dos comandos `openspec list` e integrando-se perfeitamente com o contexto da conversa para inferir nomes de alterações","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать задачи на основе изменений OpenSpec, используя SwiftIndex для семантического поиска кода на Swift, используя выходные данные JSON из команд `openspec list` и бесшовно интегрируясь с контекстом разговора для вывода имен изменений","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من تنفيذ مهام من التغييرات في OpenSpec باستخدام SwiftIndex للبحث الدلالي الشفرة الأصلي في Swift، و利用 الإخراج JSON من أوامر `openspec list` والتركيب السلس مع سياق المحادثة لاستنتاج أسماء التغييرات"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing OpenSpec changes","Inferring change names from conversation context","Automating task selection from available changes"],"zh":["实现OpenSpec更改","从对话上下文中推断更改名称","自动从可用更改中选择任务"],"ja":["OpenSpecの変更を実装する","会話のコンテキストから変更名を推測する","利用可能な変更からタスクを自動的に選択する"],"ko":["OpenSpec 변경 사항 구현","대화 문脈에서 변경 이름 추론","사용 가능한 변경 사항에서 태스크 자동 선택"],"es":["Implementar cambios de OpenSpec","Inferir nombres de cambios desde el contexto de conversación","Automatizar la selección de tareas desde los cambios disponibles"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des modifications OpenSpec","Déduire les noms de modifications à partir du contexte de conversation","Automatiser la sélection de tâches à partir des modifications disponibles"],"de":["OpenSpec-Änderungen umsetzen","Änderungsnamen aus dem Konversationskontext ableiten","Aufgaben-Auswahl aus verfügbaren Änderungen automatisieren"],"pt":["Implementar alterações do OpenSpec","Inferir nomes de alterações do contexto da conversa","Automatizar a seleção de tarefas a partir de alterações disponíveis"],"ru":["Реализация изменений OpenSpec","Вывод имен изменений из контекста разговора","Автоматизация выбора задач из доступных изменений"],"ar":["تنفيذ التغييرات في OpenSpec","استنتاج أسماء التغييرات من سياق المحادثة","تأتمة اختيار المهام من التغييرات المتاحة"]},